{"raw": {"https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Clinical-Research-Coordinator-I-II-III_R0088021": {"title": "Clinical Research Coordinator I/II/III", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 10/03/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: TRI | Rural Research Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Clinical Research Coordinator I/II/III position will be directly responsible for facilitating and coordinating the daily clinical research activities for multiple research studies, working closely with investigators, research sponsors, contract research organization representatives, research staff, and UAMS institutional oversight offices. Position must be able to organize complex projects, provide attention to detail, and communicate effectively. The position will be responsible for participant recruitment, screening, consent, data collection, including administration of survey instruments and collection of biometrics, management of records, generation of reports, and management of the day-to-day operations of the research projects, including scheduling and appointment reminder calls. He/She will maintain and manage study files and research databases within established quality control and security protocols. Will apply knowledge of local policies, federal regulations, and guidelines in support of an assigned clinical trial portfolio and the objectives of the Rural Research Network. Contributes information and ideas related to areas of responsibility as part of a cross-functional team. Ensures effective and efficient workflow and adherence to quality standards for staff/program, and self. Position maintains a working knowledge of the Code of Federal Regulations and the Code of Conduct for human research. Qualifications: Level I: Bachelor's degree plus three (3) years of general research experience, or High School diploma/GED plus seven (7) years of general research experience required. Obtain CRS Certification within 2 years of hire. Level II: Bachelor's degree plus three (3) years of clinical research experience w/demonstrated proficiency in study planning/development, study coordination/management, and/or data collection required. Obtain CRS Certification within 2 years of hire. Level III: Bachelor's degree plus three (3) years of clinical research experience w/demonstrated proficiency in study planning/development, study coordination/management, and/or data collection required. CCRP, CCRC, or equivalent professional certification required at hire. Obtain CRS Certification within 2 years of hire. Responsibilities: Organizes for data collection events, including ensuring study-related supplies are ordered. Screens potentially eligible participants, coordinates data collection appointments for study visits with participants, prepares data collection packets, conducts enrollment and obtains consent, organizes and conducts data collection events (collection of surveys and biometrics), and delivers and/or transports study-related items to eligible participants as needed. Supports and serves as back-up support to regional study sites across the State (i.e., requires travel). Maintains and manages project/research databases within established quality control and security protocols. Enters data consistently and accurately and ensures quality control. Creates and manages study files (electronic and hard files) and generates reports as requested. Develops and maintains study timelines to ensure the individual and collective study goals are met. Follows standard operating procedures and provides recommendations for quality improvement to successfully execute research activities. Maintains a working knowledge of the Code of Federal Regulations and the code of conduct for human research and adheres to strict regulatory requirements. Fosters relationships with patients, study participants and family members, study personnel, site leads, collaborators, local patient and family advisory committee and regional coordinators. May collaborate with faith-based organizations, community organizations, and other community leaders and agencies to co-facilitate workshops and conduct outreach and community-based recruitment. Participates and contributes to routine staff and organizational meetings. Performs other duties as assigned. Additional Information: Physical Demands: Constant: Hearing, Finger dexterity, including keyboarding, Sitting, Standing, Talking Frequent: \u00a0Driving, Walking Occasional \u00a0Crouching, Grasping, Lifting, Reaching, Stooping Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Clinical-Services-Manager---Primary-Care-Clinics---Central-Arkansas_R0091089-1": {"title": "Clinical Services Manager - Primary Care Clinics - Central Arkansas", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 10/04/2026 Type of Position: Clinical Staff - Medical Services Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | PCPHSL Primary Care Clinics #2 Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: This position is for Central Arkansas Outpatient Primary Care Clinics. The Clinical Services Manager (CSM) plays a vital role in the UAMS Family Medical Clinics above. Their primary responsibility is to oversee the daily operations of the nursing department and ensure that all essential functions are running smoothly. This includes staffing, development, budgeting, patient satisfaction, professional growth, and quality outcomes. The CSM will also collaborate with the Medical Director, Residency Director, physicians, and leadership within the organization to ensure that quality patient care and exceptional customer service are delivered while adhering to regulations and requirements set by UAMS, insurance companies, government agencies, and internal goals/strategies. Clinical Service Managers (CSMs) are responsible for implementing the organizational vision, mission, philosophy, core values, evidence-based practices, and standards, as well as nursing support services in their areas of responsibility. The CSM practices in accordance with the scope and standards of practice of the UAMS, the American Nurses Association, and the Nursing Social Policy Statement. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor of Science in Nursing (BSN) degree\u00a0 Five (5) or more years of clinical experience in the field of Nursing At least three (3) years of experience in a leadership capacity Current Registered Nurse License in the State of Arkansas.\u00a0 Current BLS certification or must successfully obtain certification within the first 30 days of employment. \u00a0 \u200b Preferred Qualifications: Master of Science in Nursing (MSN) degree Two Years of Pediatric Experience Ambulatory clinic experience National Nursing Certification Knowledge, Skills & Abilities: Strong organizational and leadership skills Excellent communication and interpersonal skills Ability to adapt to changing priorities and handle multiple tasks simultaneously Knowledge of healthcare regulations and compliance Proficient in using healthcare software and databases Desire to foster a culture of continuous learning and professional development Demonstrates empathy, compassion, and a commitment to delivering quality patient care Additional Information: Responsibilities: Responsible for recruiting, hiring, and onboarding qualified nursing staff for the department. This includes conducting interviews, evaluating candidates, and ensuring proper training and orientation are provided to new hires. Coordinate and monitor the workload of nursing staff to ensure adequate coverage and efficient operations. Contributes to the development of the nursing department by staying updated on industry trends, best practices, and advancements in healthcare. Identify opportunities for improvement and implement strategies to enhance the quality of care provided. This may include conducting training seminars or workshops, implementing new protocols or technologies, and collaborating with other departments for interdisciplinary collaboration. Responsible for developing and managing the nursing department's budget. Collaborate with leadership to identify cost-saving opportunities while maintaining adequate staffing levels and ensuring the highest quality patient care. Continuously monitors patient satisfaction levels and works to address any concerns or issues promptly. Actively engage with patients, their families, and healthcare providers to gather feedback, identify areas of improvement, and implement strategies to enhance the overall patient experience. Fosters a culture of continuous learning and professional development within the nursing department. Mentor and guide individual staff members, conduct performance evaluations, and assist with career advancement opportunities. Promote a culture of teamwork, collaboration, and open communication among nursing staff. Responsible for monitoring and maintaining the highest level of quality in the nursing department. Collaborate with the Medical Director, Residency Director, and other leadership to establish quality metrics, measure performance, and identify areas for improvement. Ensure that nursing practices adhere to UAMS, regulatory, and internal standards, and that patient outcomes are consistently exceptional. Serves as a liaison between the nursing department and other departments within the organization, including the Medical Director, Residency Director, physicians, and leadership. Facilitate effective communication, coordinate efforts, and ensure that nursing department activities are aligned with the overall goals and objectives of the organization. Ensures that all regulations and requirements set by UAMS, insurance companies, government agencies, and internal goals/strategies are adhered to. May perform other duties as assigned. Salary Information: commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Criminal Background Check, Substance Abuse Testing This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Feeling, Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Repetitive Motion, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Reaching, Sharps, Standing, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Lifting, Pulling, Pushing, Sitting Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Medical-Assistant-PRN---IMSL-PRN-Float-Pool--Outpatient-Clinics-M-F-_R0091131-1": {"title": "Medical Assistant PRN - IMSL PRN Float Pool (Outpatient Clinics M-F)", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted Today\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 10/04/2026 Type of Position: Clinical Staff - Nursing Job Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | PCPHSL | PCSL PRN Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Medical Assistant, (MA), works under the direct supervision of the clinic physician by assisting in the examination and treatment of patients. The MA will conduct patient interviews and all required screenings, measure vital signs (i.e., pulse rate, temperature, blood pressure, weight, and height), and records information in patients' Electronic Medical Record (EMR). The MA will also draw and collect blood samples from patients and prepare specimens for laboratory analysis. May also perform EKGs. Also prepares treatment rooms for examination of patients and ensures exam rooms are stocked with supplies needed for patient care activities. The MA may also perform administrative tasks by registering and scheduling patients for appointments, procedures, etc. using the various registrations and scheduling systems. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: High School Diploma or GED PLUS Successful completion of an accredited Medical Assistant program Preferred Qualifications: Registered or Certified in Medical Assistant One (1) year of Medical Assistant experience BLS (CPR) Certification.\u00a0 Ability to perform point of care testing, draw and collect blood specimens and prepare for laboratory processing. Additional Information: Responsibilities: Collects/records patients\u2019 medical history and acquires patient vital signs. Advises patients regarding treatment, medication, and specific physician instructions. Collects lab samples and complete necessitated documentation for submission to lab. Manages the patient appointment schedule by balancing medical needs with patients\u2019 timetable. Greets all patients/customers in professional and courteous manner upon arrival at clinic. Registers and check-out patients, collect payments, issue receipts, and verify insurance coverage. Interacts with and assists the public in a professional and friendly manner as needed. Demonstrates effective communication skills; communicates accurate and complete information; maintains strict confidentiality when necessary. Demonstrates positive working relationships with co-workers, management team, and ancillary departments; follows the Core Concepts of Patient and Family Centered Care and the Basic Code of Conduct Guidelines. Assists internal and external stakeholders as needed with exceptional customer service. May perform other duties as assigned. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Criminal Background Check, Substance Abuse Testing This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Balancing, Feeling, Hearing, Repetitive Motion, Sharps, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Lifting, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching Occasional Physical Activity: Crouching, Grasping Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Pharmacy-Technician-IV---Procurement_R0091115-1": {"title": "Pharmacy Technician IV - Procurement", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/24/2026 Type of Position: Clinical Staff - Medical Ancillary Support Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | PTSL Pharmacy Stores Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Pharmacy Technician IV will supervise, direct, coordinate and provide first line administrative and technical functions for our technicians, volunteers, students, and other personnel as directed. This position is an upper-level technician position in the Department of Pharmacy. The employee in this position must demonstrate special skills and knowledge not required by the other pharmacy technicians. The technician in this position will assist department leadership to support the goals and vision of the service line. The pharmacy technician IV works in partnership with the pharmacist manager to develop and streamline pharmacy improvement initiative, including project aimed at meeting departmental goals. The individual participates as an essential member of the pharmacy leadership team to address and resolve broad management/administrative issues such as planning for future programs and services, patient and staff safety, regulatory compliance, and operational monitoring. Pharmacy Technician IVs may work online based on department need to help with day-to-day dispensing functions, tasks and job duties to provide timely and efficient patient services. They will help with maintaining, changing, and implementing new workflows, technology/automation, and process improvement projects. They provide leadership and assistance for developing appropriate training, education, and competencies for employees and rotation students. This position will promote staff engagement and great customer service. They will also represent the department by serving on committees and attending meetings as assigned. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: HS/GED plus 4 yrs Pharmacy Tech Experience ( i.e. retail, hospital, etc. ) \u00a0 or Bachelors Degree in Pharmaceutical Sciences; Competent in all areas and technician roles \u00a0 1 year to obtain ASHP/ACPE accredited technician training or certificate program; National Technician Certification (PTCB); Pharmacy Technician License by the Arkansas State Board of Pharmacy \u00a0 Preferred Qualifications: Advanced Degree \u00a0 Good/Strong Math Skills \u00a0 2+ years of UAMS pharmacy experience \u00a0 Additional Information: Responsiblities: Ordering, stocking, and managing inventory for UAMS Health hospitals and clinics\u00a0 Orient new hires on job requirements, policies, and work procedures\u00a0 Counsel employees on unsatisfactory performance and work behaviors\u00a0 Administer formal disciplinary actions, up to and including termination\u00a0 Help implement changes to the medication specialized computer systems within the Department of Pharmacy\u00a0 Assist with technology\u00a0upgrades including testing and training\u00a0 Communicate with other departments, healthcare professionals, and services in accordance with established policies and procedures.\u00a0\u00a0 Assist with managing accreditation body activities including Joint Commission, State Board, etc.\u00a0 Communicate information effectively on updates to the pharmacy policies and procedures\u00a0 Assist Pharmacy Manager(s) with special projects\u00a0 Cover shifts when needed\u00a0 Ensure proper training for technicians\u00a0 Assist with student training and programs\u00a0 Assist P&T committee with the add and removal of formulary and non-formulary drugs\u00a0 Monitor temperature, humidity, and pressure logs Expedites delivery of all STAT/NOW orders\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Delivers medication carts accurately and promptly\u00a0\u00a0 Rotates medications appropriately\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Delivers Pyxis accurately and promptly\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Restock assigned areas daily\u00a0 Maintain Pyxis Stock Out on units\u00a0\u00a0 Maintains security of controlled substances\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Monitor the Removal of expired drugs from assigned areas monthly\u00a0 Inspection and maintenance of drug storage area\u00a0 May perform other duties as assigned. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience. Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry, Substance Abuse Testing This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Hearing Frequent Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Crouching, Lifting, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Sharps Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Pharmacy-Technician-IV---Procurement_R0091118-1": {"title": "Pharmacy Technician IV - Procurement", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/24/2026 Type of Position: Clinical Staff - Medical Ancillary Support Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | PTSL Pharmacy Stores Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: A Pharmacy Technician IV will supervise, direct, coordinate and provide first line administrative and technical functions for our technicians, volunteers, students, and other personnel as directed. This position is an upper-level technician position in the Department of Pharmacy responsible for procuring and stocking medications for UAMS Health. The employee in this position must demonstrate special skills and knowledge not required by the other pharmacy technician. The technician in this position will assist department leadership to support the goals and vision of the service line. The pharmacy technician IV works in partnership with the pharmacist manager to develop and streamline pharmacy improvement initiative, including project aimed at meeting departmental goals. The individual participates as an essential member of the pharmacy leadership team to address and resolve broad management/administrative issues such as planning for future programs and services, patient and staff safety, regulatory compliance, and operational monitoring. Pharmacy Technician IV may work online based on department need to help with day-to-day dispensing functions, tasks and job duties to provide timely and efficient patient services. They will help with maintaining, changing, and implementing new workflows, technology/automation, and process improvement projects. They provide leadership and assistance for developing appropriate training, education, and competencies for employees and rotation students. This position will promote staff engagement and great customer service. They will also represent the department by serving on committees and attending meetings as assigned. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: HS/GED plus 4 yrs Pharmacy Tech Experience ( i.e. retail, hospital, etc. ) \u00a0 or Bachelors Degree in Pharmaceutical Sciences; Competent in all areas and technician roles \u00a0 1 year to obtain ASHP/ACPE accredited technician training or certificate program; National Technician Certification (PTCB); Pharmacy Technician License by the Arkansas State Board of Pharmacy \u00a0 Preferred Qualifications: Advanced Degree \u00a0 Good/Strong Math Skills \u00a0 2+ years of UAMS pharmacy experience \u00a0 Additional Information: Responsiblities: Ordering, stocking, and managing inventory for UAMS Health hospitals and clinics\u00a0 Orient new hires on job requirements, policies, and work procedures\u00a0 Counsel employees on unsatisfactory performance and work behaviors\u00a0 Administer formal disciplinary actions, up to and including termination\u00a0 Help implement changes to the medication specialized computer systems within the Department of Pharmacy\u00a0 Assist with technology\u00a0upgrades including testing and training\u00a0 Communicate with other departments, healthcare professionals, and services in accordance with established policies and procedures.\u00a0\u00a0 Assist with managing accreditation body activities including Joint Commission, State Board, etc.\u00a0 Communicate information effectively on updates to the pharmacy policies and procedures\u00a0 Assist Pharmacy Manager(s) with special projects\u00a0 Cover shifts when needed\u00a0 Ensure proper training for technicians\u00a0 Assist with student training and programs\u00a0 Assist P&T committee with the add and removal of formulary and non-formulary drugs\u00a0 Monitor temperature, humidity, and pressure logs Expedites delivery of all STAT/NOW orders\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Delivers medication carts accurately and promptly\u00a0\u00a0 Rotates medications appropriately\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Delivers Pyxis accurately and promptly\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Restock assigned areas daily\u00a0 Maintain Pyxis Stock Out on units\u00a0\u00a0 Maintains security of controlled substances\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Monitor the Removal of expired drugs from assigned areas monthly\u00a0 Inspection and maintenance of drug storage area\u00a0 May perform other duties as assigned. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience. Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry, Substance Abuse Testing This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Hearing Frequent Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Crouching, Lifting, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Sharps Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Benton/Licensed-Social-Worker---UAMS-Health-Benton-Bryant_R0091139": {"title": "Licensed Social Worker - UAMS Health Benton/Bryant", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/17/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Shift Vary (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: INA | Institutional Admin Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Licensed Social Worker is a member of the care management team and responsible for assisting in the management of the continuum of patient care on the inpatient medical setting from admission through discharge at the UAMS Health Benton/Bryant location. The role reflects appropriate knowledge of Social Work scope of practice, current state requirements, CMS Conditions of Participation, EMTALA, Patient Bill of Rights, AB 1203 and other Federal or State regulatory agency requirements specific to the Social Work role. The Social Work team members will partner with the multi-disciplinary team utilizing best practices, relevant data and compliance with the mission/philosophy, standards, goals and core values of UAMS: Comfort, Hope, and Healing. The primary elements of the social work role include assessment of the psychological, financial, and discharge planning needs of the patients and families, providing information, support, counseling, and referrals to other levels of care and appropriate resources for a variety of diagnoses for the adult population. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Master\u2019s degree in social work. Must be a licensed by an Arkansas Professional Board as a Licensed Masters Social Worker or Licensed Certified Social Worker (LMSW or LCSW). Preferred Qualifications: Two (2) years of experience in an Acute Care Hospital Setting. Experience in Case Management. Certified Case Manager (CCM) or American Case Management (ACM) certification. Additional Information: Responsibilities: Psychosocial Assessment/Services: Completes assessment for patients admitted to the hospital. Performs discharge planning and aftercare coordination, community referrals and linkages. Provides patient and family education and adjustment to illness counseling, grief counseling and crisis intervention. Promotes patient and family centered care and documents the patient choices in the medical record as required. Recommends care and services that are appropriate to the specified chronological age, developmental age, social maturity, and cultural background of the patient being treated.\u00a0\u00a0 Communication/Collaboration: Documents and communicates with all treatment teams, patients, and family pertaining to the coordination of care and services. Serves as a consultant for processing guardianship, power of attorney, health care proxy, and advanced directives. Collaborates with other UAMS Departments and actively participates in hospital wide performance improvement metrics and regulatory compliance initiatives. Reports and reviews department specific data metrics on a monthly basis. Implements, monitors, and evaluates the Care Management quality improvement initiatives.\u00a0\u00a0 Leadership - Acts as a resource to others in the performance of duties. Demonstrates a commitment to the personal and professional development of other UAMS employees. Participates in recruitment/retention of staff. Other duties as assigned in order to meet the UAMS Core Values and the business needs of the Department Physical Requirements: Light Work | Exerting up to 20 pounds of force occasionally, and/or up to 10 pounds of force frequently, and/or a negligible amount of force constantly to move objects. If the use of force is greater than that for sedentary work and the worker sits most of the time, the job is rated for light work. The employee is not substantially exposed to adverse environmental conditions (such as in typical office or administrative work). Constant physical activities: Hearing: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding Frequent physical activities: Sitting; Talking; Walking Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/APRN---Myeloma-Clinic_R0089874-1": {"title": "APRN - Myeloma Clinic", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 10/03/2026 Type of Position: Clinical Staff - Nursing Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | CASL MY AdvancedPracticeProviders CL Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: **Shift: 4 -10's a week** The APRN will extend the patient care and administrative services for UAMS physicians in the outpatient settings. APP will be expected provide comprehensive health assessments, determine diagnoses, implement treatment plans, perform procedures, and prescribe medicines and treatments. The APP will also manage health issues for patients, independently or in collaboration with the designated physicians. The APRN will work autonomously as well as in collaboration with a variety of individuals to diagnose and manage patient's health care problems; and will serve as a health care resource, interdisciplinary consultant, and patient advocate. The APRN will also coordinate the multidisciplinary care of patients, facilitating all necessary consults, assuring that care is timely and appropriate. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Master\u2019s Degree Plus Two (2) years nursing experience with Licensed Registered Nurse in Arkansas and APRN/CPN License Current BLS certification or must successfully obtain certification within the first 30 days of employment.\u00a0 Must be able to operate all typical nursing equipment essential to performing the job (i.e., scales, procedure equipment, needles, blood pressure equipment, and EKG machines). \u00a0\u00a0 Must have normal communication sensory requirement. \u00a0 Ability to comply with CDC Universal Precautions when indicated. \u00a0 Preferred Qualifications: Prescriptive authority and DEA license must be obtained after hire Additional Information: Responsibilities: Conducts comprehensive assessments of patients (history, physical exam, risk factors) and establish baseline and ongoing status. Orders and interprets diagnostic tests (labs, imaging, other studies) as appropriate for the patient population and condition. Develops, implements, and evaluates treatment plans \u2014 including prescribing medications (as authorized), non-pharmacologic interventions, and monitoring response to therapy. Coordinates multidisciplinary care: collaborate with physicians, specialists, nursing staff, allied health professionals, referrals, and ensure continuity and appropriateness of care. Educates patients and their families about diagnoses, treatments, preventive health, self-care, expected side-effects, and when/how to seek escalation of care. Documents all patient encounters, treatments, outcomes in the electronic health record, ensure compliance with institutional and regulatory standards, and engage in quality improvement initiatives. Serves as a resource/consultant in the healthcare team: work autonomously as well as collaboratively to diagnose/manage complex issues, advocate for patients, and support program development. May perform other duties as assigned. Salary Information: commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Criminal Background Check, Substance Abuse Testing This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, N/A Frequent Physical Activity: N/A, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Crouching, Feeling, Kneeling, Lifting, N/A, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/APRN-PA---Urology-Clinic_R0091098-1": {"title": "APRN/PA - Urology Clinic", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 10/03/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | SUSL Urology Mid-L Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: *This position will select either an APRN or PA* The Advanced Practice Nurse/Physician Assistant (APRN/PA) will be a vital member of the Urology Team at the University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS). This provider will assist physicians with clinic operations, organize patient visits, and perform clinic procedures. They will also serve as a high-level clinical extender, working both independently and collaboratively with supervising physicians to manage patient care across inpatient and outpatient settings. The APRN/PA will perform clinical assessments, assist with care coordination, answer MyChart and in-basket messages, respond to patient questions and phone calls, and manage prescriptions. In the outpatient clinic, they will see new and follow up patients and follow up on pathology and imaging, and ensure patients receive comprehensive education and appropriate follow-up. The provider must possess a high level of clinical expertise to assess, diagnose, and treat actual and potential problems in patients. The APRN/PA will serve as a key communicator between the care team and patients, ensuring timely, complete, and accurate information sharing. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: APRN Master\u2019s Degree in Nursing Three years of nursing experience Licensed Registered Nurse in Arkansas APRN License Minimum Qualifications:\u00a0 PA Master's Education PA Licensure Additional Information: Responsibilities: Coordinates specialized, multidisciplinary care and facilitates consults of patients to ensure timely and appropriate treatment. Provides comprehensive health assessments, determines diagnoses, implements treatment plans, prescribes medical treatments, and manages health issues for patients in collaboration with the designated physician. Collaborates with a variety of health care professionals to diagnose and manage patients' health care problems, serving as a resource, interdisciplinary consultant, and patient advocate. Manages post procedure immunosuppression and labs of the patient in coordination with the physician and pharmacist. Participates in institutional initiatives and encourages the participation of others. Collaborates in policy and program development, implementation, and evaluation using best practices in delivering quality service. Edits and documents results in various critical care systems Performs other duties as assigned. Constant Physical Activity : Hear, Read, Concentrate, Think Analytically, Frequent Physical Activity : Stand Occasional Physical Activity : Bend, sit, crawl, crouch, kneel, stoop or reach overhead Lift/Carry Weight: 11 - 25 Lbs. or more Push/Pull Weight: 100 Lbs. or more Physical Environment : Inside medical Facility Noise Level: Moderate Visual Requirements: Color discrimination, Depth perception, Far visual acuity Near visual acuity Hazards : Biological, Dust, Fumes/Gases/Odors, Radiation, Sharp objects/tools Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Benton/Manager--Patient-Food-Services---UAMS-Health-Benton-Bryant_R0091077-1": {"title": "Manager, Patient Food Services \u2013 UAMS Health Benton/Bryant", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/16/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Shift Vary (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: INA | Institutional Admin Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Manager, Patient Food Services is responsible for the direction and guidance of all aspects of patient food service and tray line at the UAMS Health Benton/Bryant location. This position works closely with all managers to ensure high standards for patients. This position coordinates planning, implementation and evaluation of menus in conjunction with other managers. The Manager, Patient Food Services, is responsible for all food handling safety and sanitation concerns along as well as making sure all equipment is being used properly and maintained in proper working order. This position is also responsible for the orientation and in-servicing of staff as well as making sure all competencies are met and that employees are current on all annual requirements; along with maintaining standards in accordance to all regulatory agencies. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor\u2019s degree plus 4 years of experience in foodservice management, catering management, hospitality industry management, or equivalent experience including 2 years supervisory experience. OR High School diploma and 8 years of experience in foodservice management, catering management, hospitality industry management, or equivalent experience including 2 years supervisory experience. Additional Information: Responsibilities: Inspects patient food area for cleanliness, safety, maintenance needs, and coordinates repairs as needed. Handles customer complaints by meeting and talking with special groups or other departments. Monitors food preparation, service, storage and cleaning activities to ensure compliance with health, safety, and department operating standards by: sampling food, examining serving sizes, identifying and controlling food waste, inspecting kitchen and service areas, and adjusting work assignments as needed Checks the quality of the food products that are served, as well as, the products that are received to ensure proper standards are met. Ensures temperature logs are up to date. Modifies items as needed to meet specific diet orders as prescribed by physicians. Ensures that patients, families, and medical staff are satisfied with service Provides leadership and directly supervises all staff within the patient food service area, including, all supervisors, dietetic technicians I and II, room service ambassadors, lead room service ambassadors, cooks, and institutional services assistants. Responsible for scheduling the interviews, completing reference checks, interviewing, hiring, and terminating employees. Complete all duties/tasks assigned. Physical Requirements: Medium Work | Exerting up to 50 pounds of force occasionally, and/or up to 30 pounds of force frequently, and/or up to 10 pounds of force constantly to move objects. The Employee is required to have visual acuity to determine the accuracy, neatness, and thoroughness of the work assigned (i.e., custodial, general laborer, lab personnel, etc.) or to make general observations of facilities or structures (i.e., security guard). The employee is not substantially exposed to adverse environmental conditions (such as in typical office or administrative work). Constant physical activities: Standing; Talking; Walking Frequent physical activities: Crawling; Crouching; Stooping Occasional physical activities: Sitting Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Benton/Surgical-Technician---UAMS-Health-Benton-Bryant_R0091074-1": {"title": "Surgical Technician \u2013 UAMS Health Benton/Bryant", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/16/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Shift Vary (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: INA | Institutional Admin Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: As individuals dedicated to ensuring the safety and quick recovery of our patients, surgical technicians are integral members of a team dedicated to providing the best care for patients through collaboration, communication and patient safety. As part of the UAMS Health Benton/Bryant team, operating room surgical technicians define their practice through attention to detail with excellence and outstanding patient care, are driven by their expertise, compassion and dedication to evidence-based practice, and operate at a higher level of practice. If you are a Surgical Technician who has current Operating Room experience, we invite you to consider a career with UAMS Health Benton/Bryant. The Surgical Technician assembles supplies for surgical procedures, sets up and maintains the sterile field, passes surgical instruments, and assists in room preparation. This professional role will require the ability to coordinate care and anticipate the needs for the surgical case; assisting the surgeon, nurses, other members of the team to provide an optimal outcome for the patient and work collaboratively with clinic providers, fellows, and staff. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: High School Diploma or GED Graduate of NBSTSA-accredited Surgical Technology program OR graduate of NCCT-approved Surgical Technology program OR completed military surgical/scrub tech training OR have two or more years of on-the-job surgical/scrub experience in an acute care facility or ambulatory surgery center. Additional Information: Responsibilities: Assessment of the surgical procedure. Ensures availability of appropriate instrumentation, supplies and equipment for assigned cases. Preparation of the OR. Ensures that the room has been prepared for the upcoming cases, with appropriate equipment available and ready for surgical use. Ensures that the instruments are cleaned arranged and transported to the soiled workroom according to department policy. Independently assists with instrument reprocessing tasks when assigned cases are completed and time permits. Ensures that the operating rooms are ready for the following day\u2019s cases. Exhibits practical knowledge of OR equipment including maintenance and safety aspects. Utilizes available communication tools. Demonstrates teamwork by offering assistance to other team members. Shares knowledge of information and expertise with other staff. Attends departmental in-services and other educational offerings. Consistently demonstrates new knowledge and skills through incorporation into actual clinical practice. Willing to learn new techniques. Other duties assigned Physical Requirements : Very Heavy Work | Exerting in excess of 100 pounds of force occasionally, and/or in excess of 50 pounds of force frequently, and/or in excess of 20 pounds of force constantly to move objects. The Employee is required to have close visual acuity to perform an activity such as: preparing and analyzing data and figures; transcribing; viewing a computer terminal; extensive reading; and/or visual inspection at distances close to the eyes. The Employee is subject to inside environmental conditions. Protection from weather conditions but not necessarily from temperature changes. Constant physical activities: Hearing; Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding Frequent physical activities: Balancing; Feeling; Grasping; Kneeling; Lifting; Pulling; Pushing; Reaching; Repetitive Motion; Sharps; Standing; Stooping; Talking; Walking Occasional physical activities: Climbing; Sitting Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Benton/Cardiac-Catheterization-Lab-Registered-Nurse--RN----UAMS-Health-Benton-Bryant_R0091054-1": {"title": "Cardiac Catheterization Lab Registered Nurse (RN) \u2013 UAMS Health Benton/Bryant", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/16/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Shift Vary (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: INA | Institutional Admin Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: This position is located at the UAMS Health Benton/Bryant location and may be used to fill multiple positions. The Cardiac Catheterization Lab Registered Nurse (RN) provides specialized nursing care to patients undergoing diagnostic and interventional cardiovascular procedures within a heart hospital setting. This position assesses and prepares patients for procedures, monitors cardiac and hemodynamic status, administers medications and sedation as appropriate, and provides nursing interventions throughout the procedural and recovery phases. The RN works collaboratively with cardiologists and the interdisciplinary cardiovascular team to provide safe, efficient, and high-quality care to patients with complex cardiovascular conditions. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Baccalaureate Degree, ADN Degree, or Diploma RN.\u00a0 Major: Registered Nurse RN with a minimum of 1 year of RN experience Valid Arkansas Registered Nursing License Special knowledge, abilities and skills: Ability to perform point of care testing, draw and collect blood specimens and prepare for laboratory processing. Preferred Qualifications: Pediatric experience a plus. BLS (CPR) Certification. A minimum of 1 year phlebotomy and RN experience Two years of experience in an ambulatory care setting Additional Information: Responsibilities: Provides specialized nursing care before, during, and after cardiac catheterization and other cardiovascular procedures, including patient assessment, preparation, monitoring, and recovery. Monitors cardiac rhythm, hemodynamic status, vital signs, oxygenation, and overall patient condition and promptly recognizes and responds to changes, complications, or cardiovascular emergencies. Administers medications, IV therapies, and moderate sedation as appropriate and monitors patient response in accordance with provider orders, established protocols, and nursing standards. Assists cardiologists and other members of the cardiovascular team during diagnostic and interventional procedures , supporting patient safety and efficient procedural workflow. Responds to emergency situations and changes in patient condition , initiating appropriate nursing interventions and participating in resuscitative measures as necessary. Provides education to patients and families regarding cardiovascular procedures, medications, recovery expectations, activity restrictions, risk-factor modification, and follow-up care. Documents assessments, medications, interventions, procedural care, and patient outcomes and collaborates with the interdisciplinary care team to support continuity, quality, and safety of patient care. Physical Requirements: Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sharps, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Feeling, Grasping, Reaching, Repetitive Motion Occasional Physical Activity: Balancing, Climbing, Crawling, Crouching, Driving, Lifting, Pulling, Pushing, Stooping Lifting to 100lbs. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Benton/Insurance-Verification-Specialist-II---UAMS-Health-Benton-Bryant_R0091013-1": {"title": "Insurance Verification Specialist II \u2013 UAMS Health Benton/Bryant", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/15/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Shift Vary (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: INA | Institutional Admin Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Insurance Verification Specialist II is responsible for verifying insurance benefits, processing authorizations and pre-certifications, and working appropriate registration and billing work queues at the UAMS Health Benton/Bryant location. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: High School Diploma/GED Two (2) years of experience in customer service and two (2) years of insurance, billing, scheduling experience in a healthcare environment. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Must have excellent organizational and interpersonal skills in order to successfully interact with individuals of diverse backgrounds. Well-developed decision-making skills are required. Must maintain confidentiality and HIPAA compliance. Highly motivated and self-directed individual that establishes plans of action. Highly proficient in computer and keyboard skills. Additional Information: Responsibilities: Conducts verification of eligibility and benefits for patient insurance. Completes authorizations and pre-certifications, tracks pre-authorizations and maintains referrals. Enters benefit and authorization information into EPIC. Initiates peer-to-peer submissions and works closely with clinical counterparts to collect requested information. Obtains and coordinates completion of out of network waivers. Coordinates with UAMS Office of Financial Clearance when appropriate Work effectively in a team environment, coordinating workflows with other team members and ensuring a productive and efficient environment. Deals with conflicts in a positive and professional manner using careful listening and negotiation skills to resolve disagreements. Comply with safety principles, laws, regulations, and standards associated with, but not limited to CMS, Joint Commission, EMTALA, and OSHA. Demonstrates a high level of integrity and innovative thinking and actively contributes to the success of the organization. May perform other duties as assigned. Physical Requirements: Constant Activities: Sit; Use hands to touch, handle or feel; Talk; Hear; Read Concentrate, or Think Analytically Occasional Activities: Stand, Walk, Bend, Crawl, Crouch, Kneel, Stoop, Reach Lift/Carry: 10-25lbs. Push/Pull: 10-25lbs. Physical Environment: Inside Office Environment Noise Level: Moderate Visual Requirements: Near Visual Acuity; Far Visual Acquity; Color Discrimination; Depth Perception; Peripheral Vision Hazards: None Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Benton/Medical-Assistant---UAMS-Health-Benton-Bryant_R0091007-1": {"title": "Medical Assistant \u2013 UAMS Health Benton/Bryant", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/15/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Shift Vary (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: INA | Institutional Admin Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Medical Assistant (MA) provides direct patient care to assigned patients at the UAMS Health Benton/Bryant location. The MA works under the direct supervision of the clinic nurse(s) by assisting in the examination and treatment of patients. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: High School, GED or formal educational equivalent Current BLS Completion of Accredited Medical Assistant training program Excellent communication skills, basic computer skills, strong work ethics and accountability. Preferred Qualifications: Experience in an ambulatory care setting One (1) or more years of MA experience Additional Information: Responsibilities: Prepares treatment rooms for examination. Assists with medical procedures and examinations Conducts patient interviews, measures vital signs (i.e., pulse rate, temperature, blood pressure, weight, and height), and phlebotomy. Performs EKG\u2019s, dressing changes. Administers approved medications. Researches and scribes physicians\u2019. Orders/accession orders for clinical laboratory or appropriate processing center. Performs administrative tasks by registering and scheduling patients for appointments, procedures, etc. using the various registration and scheduling systems. Perform other duties as needed. \u00a0 PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS Stand: Frequently Sit: Frequently Walk: Occasionally Bend, crawl, crouch, kneel, stoop or reach overhead: Frequently Lift and carry weight: 25 lbs Push and pull weight: 25 lbs Use hands to touch, handle or feel: Frequently Talk: Continuously Hear: Continuously Taste or smell: Occasionally Read, concentrate, think analytically: Continuously Physical Environment : Inside Medical Facility Environment Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Benton/Financial-Counseling-Specialist---UAMS-Health-Benton-Bryant_R0091006-1": {"title": "Financial Counseling Specialist - UAMS Health Benton/Bryant", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/15/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Shift Vary (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: INA | Institutional Admin Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Financial Counseling Specialist works with patients who have scheduled specific clinical services to promote financial clearance prior to the day of care. In addition to contacting payers and providers to secure authorizations as needed, this staff member provides information regarding hospital payment requirements, alternative financing and charity care programs during pre-service. This individual will relay relevant financial information in a clear and patient-friendly manner per UAMS\u2019 customer service and price transparency initiatives at the UAMS Health Benton/Bryant location. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: High School, GED or formal educational equivalent\u00a0plus 6 years\u2019 experience in healthcare in a revenue cycle related function.\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Bachelor\u2019s degree in finance, business or related 2\u00a0years of experience in healthcare revenue cycle or revenue cycle related function\u00a0 Knowledge in basic medical terminology preferred, medical terminology competent within 3 months of hire, Must be able to perform basic operations on a computer, Able to follow oral and written instructions and communicate with others effectively, Problem solving skills, critical thinking skills, and ability to multi-task, Excellent customer relations skills, Must possess the required level of skills and abilities to read, write, speak, and apply mathematical concepts and sounds reasoning to successfully perform the essential duties and responsibilities of this job.\u00a0 Additional Information: Responsibilities: Meet with all self-pay\u00a0and under insured and\u00a0patients to explain benefits, financial obligation, payment options and assistance programs.\u00a0 Assure that a payment methodology is in place prior to discharge.\u00a0 Screen\u00a0scheduled non-urgent self-pay\u00a0and under insured\u00a0surgical and diagnostic study patients (in and outpatient) prior to service, collect payment prior to service and assure plan for financial coverage is in place before service is performed.\u00a0 Process a deposit and establish a payment plan for large out of pocket obligations.\u00a0Screen\u00a0referred clinic patients prior to service, collect minimum payment prior to visit and assure plan for financial coverage is in place before clinic visit.\u00a0\u00a0 Screen all patients for eligibility for\u00a0Social Security, COBRA, Crime Victims,\u00a0Health Insurance Marketplace, Medicaid\u00a0and other programs when appropriate.\u00a0 Assure that lifetime reserve letter signatures are obtained as needed.\u00a0\u00a0 Screen all patients applying or deemed eligible for the Financial Assistance Plan for any additional programs they may be eligible for to assure the hospital discount is the second option in place.\u00a0\u00a0 Processes applications for charity discounts.\u00a0 This involves review of\u00a0patient financial information, determination that all required information is received and determines eligibility for the program.\u00a0\u00a0 Assist with financial screening and program explanation in the Emergency Department when requested.\u00a0\u00a0Discuss alternative payment options with patients who present as self-pay but are deemed ineligible for assistance programs and also with patients having a high deductible or a limited benefit plan.\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Perform other duties as needed PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS: Stand: Frequently Sit: Continuously Walk: Occasionally Bend, crawl, crouch, kneel, stoop or reach overhead: Frequently Lift and carry weight: 25 lbs Push and pull weight: 25 lbs Use hands to touch, handle or feel: Frequently Talk: Continuously Hear: Continuously Taste or smell: Occasionally Read, concentrate, think analytically: Continuously Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Benton/Diagnostic-Medical-Sonographer---UAMS-Health-Benton-Bryant_R0091005-1": {"title": "Diagnostic Medical Sonographer \u2013 UAMS Health Benton/Bryant", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/15/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Shift Vary (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: INA | Institutional Admin Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The General Diagnostic Medical Sonographer is responsible for performing quality ultrasound images for medical interpretation within the UAMS Health Benton/Bryant location. The sonographer will perform a wide variety of ultrasound studies in collaboration with the ordering provider and reading Radiologists requests. This position requires rotational after hour/weekend and holiday call coverage. The sonographer will work closely with Radiologists to provide needed information to make an accurate diagnosis. The Sonographer will assist physicians in such procedures as renal biopsies, sonohysterograms and Lumason enhancement studies. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: High School Diploma/GED. Graduate from an accredited Diagnostic Medical Sonography program. Registered with the American Registry for Diagnostic Medical Sonography (ARDMS) or registry eligible. First Advanced Certification by the ARDMS must be obtained within 12 months from date of hire. Second Advanced Certification by the ARDMS must be obtained within 24 months from date of hire. Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor's degree One (1) or more years of experience working as a sonographer Advanced Certification by the ARDMS Additional Information: Responsibilities: Performs quality ultrasound imaging including Abdomen, Abdomen Doppler, Elastography, Renal, Pelvic (transabdominal and transvaginal), Neonatal (head, abdomen and spine), Ist, 2nd and 3rd Trimester Inhouse ob, Scrotal and Thyroid ultrasounds. Assists in procedures including biopsies, sonohysterograms and Lumason enhancement studies. Obtains, reviews, and integrates pertinent patient history and supporting clinical data to facilitate optimal diagnostic results. Explains procedures while being compassionate towards patients. Performs advanced tests with portable equipment in patients' rooms when necessary. Maintains sonographic and other equipment in efficient operating order; assists with preventative maintenance on a regularly scheduled basis. Participates in various teaching and/or learning opportunities to further his/her own personal knowledge and to assist in expanding the knowledge of others. Performs additional manager or supervisor assigned duties. Other duties may be assigned to this position. Physical Requirements: Constant Activity: Seeing, Hearing, Manipulating things with fingers (including keyboarding) Frequent Activity: Speaking, Standing, Walking, Repetitive motion Occasional Activity: Bending, Stooping, Reaching, Grasping Lift up to 150lbs. Lift to waist: 100lbs. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Benton/Supervisory--Access-Services---UAMS-Health-Benton-Bryant_R0091003-1": {"title": "Supervisor, Access Services \u2013 UAMS Health Benton/Bryant", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/15/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Shift Vary (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: INA | Institutional Admin Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Access Services Supervisor will oversee daily operations of access services, including front-line customer support, scheduling, registration, admissions, and staff coordination at the UAMS Health Benton/Bryant location. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: High School Diploma plus 7 years of registration and/or billing experience including three (3) years of experience in a healthcare environment. Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in business, healthcare, or related field Leadership or supervisory experience CHAA Certification Additional Information: Requirements: Supervises department staff by monitoring activities and productivity daily and takes appropriate action to ensure staff consistently meets performance standards Responsible for ensuring the team meets expectations for work queue productivity, quality, and customer service Seeks continuing education of regulatory changes and industry standards; ensures information is provided to staff timely and based on workload Documents personnel issues and promotes a balanced a conducive work environment Ensures all department, CABC, ICE, and UAMS policies are followed Establishes and maintains performance standards for productivity, quality, and compliance Implements process improvement and reports results Ensures staff is educated and conducts themselves in the performance of all duties Knowledge of individual responsibility and ensures staff preparedness following Joint Commission standards and facility safety and emergency preparedness standards Maintains current knowledge of the profession and all state and federal regulatory mandates. Maintains required job skills competencies and completes skills assessments annually Completes and maintains documentation of continuing education hours annually Supervises the day-to-day operations of the assigned Access Coordinators, and Patient Representatives. Responsible for knowing and understanding clinic policies/procedures and is able to act on these policies/procedures Schedules, reschedules, coordinates, and cancels appointments using the hospital systems Works closely with management to develop, implement, and maintain formalized training plans Responsible for annual training facilitation staff development and providing employee coaching. Responsible for employee evaluations. Works with CABC Support for timekeeping and other HR items. Promotes teamwork and models the core concepts of Patient Family-Centered Care (PFCC). Conducts and assists with crucial conversations with staff when disagreements occur and when necessary progressive discipline. Perform other duties as needed. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS Stand: Frequently Sit: Frequently Walk: Occasionally Bend, crawl, crouch, kneel, stoop or reach overhead: Frequently Lift and carry weight: 25 lbs Push and pull weight: 25 lbs Use hands to touch, handle or feel: Frequently Talk: Continuously Hear: Continuously Taste or smell: Occasionally Read, concentrate, think analytically: Continuously Physical Environment : Inside Medical Facility Environment Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Benton/Access-Coordinator-III---UAMS-Health-Benton-Bryant_R0090993-1": {"title": "Access Coordinator III - 