to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | NRSL Med Oncology H7 IP C Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: This posting will be used to fill multiple positions Shift: Nights The Registered Nurse provides direct patient care to assigned patients in Medical Oncology/Family Medicine (H7).\u00a0 This unit has 30 private rooms and provides state of the art therapies to a wide range of medical oncology patients and family medicine patients. Practicing in this environment allows the RN to develop skills in chemotherapy and biotherapy administration, management of a range of IV central access devices, management of a variety of symptoms associated with the disease process and/or treatment, and development of skills in emotional support and palliative care. This area also provides learning opportunities in all areas of medical-surgical nursing. A strong interdisciplinary team including physicians, nurses, pharmacists, nutritionists, and social workers support the patient in their various therapies. Qualifications: Required: Graduate of an accredited Nursing Program with Associates Degree, Nursing Diploma, Bachelors in Nursing, or Master's in Nursing.\u00a0 Valid RN License. 1 year of Registered Nursing experience. Excellent communication skills. Basic computer skills. Strong work ethics and accountability. \u00a0 Preferred: \u00a0BSN or MSN 2 or more years of nursing experience with a minimum of 1 year in an acute care setting such as a teaching hospital. 1 year or more of Oncology RN experience.\u00a0 National Certification Additional Information: Responsibilities: The Registered Nurse delivers nursing care for patients in within the limits of the Nurse Practice Act of the State of Arkansas and adheres to institutional policies, procedures and standards. \u00a0 The RN is responsible for the following: Adhere to the standard of care defined by UAMS, ANA, and Standards for specialty patient population with support and mentoring by other team members.\u00a0 Collects and documents assessment data. Develops a Plan of Care (POC) per standard.\u00a0 Implements POC including medical order and interdisciplinary approach. Evaluates the progress of patient toward attainment of desired outcomes.\u00a0 Provides effective patient/family education/discharge planning. Administers medication per standard including drug information to patients/families.\u00a0 Acts as a resource/supports others.\u00a0 Delivers patient care using the principles of the defined nursing modality.\u00a0 Delegates care based on UAMS standards, legal and regulatory requirements, specific job description and individual level of education and training.\u00a0 Contributes to a positive work environment that is conducive to clinical education while serving as a resource for student nurses and staff. Perform any other duties assigned. Constant Physical Activity : Hear, Read, Concentrate, Think Analytically, Frequent Physical Activity : Stand, Walk, Talk, Use hands to touch, handle or feel, Occasional Physical Activity : Sit, Bend, crawl, crouch, kneel, stoop, reach overhead, Taste or Smell, Lift/Carry Weight: 100 Lbs. or more Push/Pull Weight: 100 Lbs. or more Physical Environment : Inside Medical Facility Environment Noise Level: Moderate Visual Requirements: Near Visual Acuity, Far Visual Acuity, Color Discrimination, Depth Perception Hazards : Biological, Chemical, Sharp Objects/Tools, Dust, Fumes/Gases/Odors Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Physical-Therapist---Acute-Care_R0090331-1": {"title": "Physical Therapist - Acute Care", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-24\nPosted: Posted 11 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/24/2026 Type of Position: Clinical Staff - Rehabilitation Therapy Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | MUSL Physical Therapy Inpatient Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Physical Therapist performs examinations, evaluations, and establishes plans of care including goals and recommendations for discharge. The PT provides daily treatment to promote functional independence and modifies treatment programs. Performs documentation in EHR. Coordinates/communicates with interdisciplinary team. Participates in program improvement, clinical education, and customer service standards. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor\u2019s degree in Physical Therapy if graduated prior to 2002 OR Master\u2019s degree in Physical Therapy if graduated prior to 2016 OR Doctorate degree in Physical Therapy; Licensed as a Physical Therapist by the Arkansas State Board of Physical Therapy or eligible for licensure. Additional Information: Responsibilities: Performs comprehensive examination of patients using appropriate tests/measures, completes the evaluation, and formulates an individualized plan of care. Provides evidence based quality patient treatment and education and monitors patient for physiological status during sessions. Responsive to needs/requests outside of direct patient care. May include serving as a Clinical Instructor, providing presentations, serving on committees/teams, performing program development//projects, developing educational materials, providing education to coworkers after attending continuing education that was supported by travel or educational leave, etc Consistently meets departmental productivity target. Completes accurate and thorough documentation in a timely manner following regulatory policies. Submits accurate and complete charges and daily summary sheets. Adheres to UAMS/Department policy for attendance; reports for all scheduled shifts on time and completes shift duties. Performs other duties as assigned. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Criminal Background Check, Substance Abuse Testing This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Feeling, Hearing, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Grasping, Lifting, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Repetitive Motion, Standing, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Balancing, Kneeling, Sitting, Stooping Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/RN---Solid-Organ-Transplant-Nephrology---H9_R0090517-1": {"title": "RN - Solid Organ Transplant/Nephrology - H9", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-24\nPosted: Posted 11 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 11/28/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | NRSL Nephrology H9 IP C Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: This posting will be used to fill multiple positions. The Registered Nurse provides direct patient care to assigned patients in Medical/Surgical Unit (H9) Specializing in Solid Organ Transplantation and Nephrology. This unit is a 30 bed medical/surgical adult inpatient unit serving general medical and surgical patients from adolescent age to geriatrics. The unit specializes in the care of the adult renal and liver failure patients, solid organ transplant patients, hemodialysis and peritoneal dialysis patients, general surgery patients, colorectal and urology patients. H9 also cares for moderate to high acuity and progressive care patients. Through an interdisciplinary approach, quality care is delivered to our patients using a customized primary nursing modality to meet the physical, emotional, and educational needs of both the patient and their family. Qualifications: \u200b Minimum: Bachelor\u2019s degree in Nursing, Associate\u2019s degree in Nursing, Diploma RN, or Master\u2019s degree in Nursing. Must be a graduate of an accredited RN nursing program. Minimum of 1 year of Registered Nursing experience; Valid Registered Nursing License Additional Information: Key Responsibilities: The Registered Nurse (RN) delivers nursing care for patients within the limits of the Nurse Practice Act of the State of Arkansas and adheres to institutional policies, procedures and standards.\u00a0The\u00a0RN is responsible to adhere to the standard of care defined by UAMS, ANA, and Standards for specialty patient population with support and mentoring by other team members.\u00a0 Collects and documents assessment data. Develops a Plan of Care (POC) per standard.\u00a0 Implements POC including medical order and interdisciplinary approach.\u00a0 Evaluates the progress of patient toward attainment of desired outcomes.\u00a0 Provides effective patient/family education/discharge planning.\u00a0 Administers medication per standard including drug information to patients/families.\u00a0 Acts as a resource/supports others.\u00a0 Delivers patient care using the principles of the defined nursing modality.\u00a0 Delegates care based on UAMS standards, legal and regulatory requirements, specific job description and individual level of education and training.\u00a0 Contributes to a positive work environment that is conducive to clinical education while serving as a resource for student nurses and staff. Physical Requirements: Stand: Frequently Sit: Occasionally Walk: Frequently Bend, crawl, crouch, kneel, stoop or reach overhead: Occasionally Lift and carry weight: 100+ lbs. Push and pull weight: 100+ lbs. Use hands to touch, handle or feel: Frequently Talk: Frequently Hear: Continuously Taste or smell: Occasionally Read, concentrate, and think analytically: Continuously Physical Environment : Inside Medical Facility Environment Noise Level: Moderate Visual Requirements: Color discrimination, Depth perception, Far visual acuity, Near visual acuity Hazards: Biological, Chemical, Dust, Electrical, Fumes/Gases/Odors, Radiation, Sharp objects/tools #UAMSNurses Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of five Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/RN---Medical-Oncology-Transplant---E7_R0090513-1": {"title": "RN - Medical Oncology/Transplant - E7", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-24\nPosted: Posted 11 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 11/25/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | NRSL Med Onco Trans E7 IP C Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: This posting will be used to fill multiple positions Full-time and part-time positions available. Varied shifts available. The Registered Nurse provides direct patient care to assigned patients in Medical Oncology/Transplant (E7).\u00a0 This unit has 28 private rooms and provides state of the art therapies, including stem cell transplant, to a wide range of medical oncology patients. Practicing in this environment allows the registered nurse to develop skills in chemotherapy and biotherapy administration, management of a range of IV central access devices and a variety of symptoms associated with the disease and/or treatment, and the development of skills in emotional support and palliative care. A strong interdisciplinary team including physicians, nurses, pharmacists, nutritionists, and social workers who support the patient in their various therapies. Qualifications: Required: Graduate of an accredited Nursing Program with Associates Degree, Nursing Diploma, Bachelors in Nursing, or Master's in Nursing Valid RN License One (1) year of Registered Nursing experience Excellent communication skills Basic computer skills Strong work ethics and accountability Preferred: Two (2) years or more nursing experience with current BLS Med/Surg or Oncology experience Chemotherapy Certified Employees in this role must be fitted for, capable of donning and performing routine tasks in personal protective equipment to include N95 masks, Powered Air Purifying Respirators (PAPR) or Controlled Air Purifying Respirators (CAPR). Responsibilities : Delivers nursing care for patients in within the limits of the Nurse Practice Act of the State of Arkansas and adheres to institutional policies, procedures and standards. Adheres to the standard of care defined by UAMS, ANA, and Standards for specialty patient population with support and mentoring by other team members. Collects and documents assessment data. Develops a Plan of Care (POC) per standard.\u00a0 Implements POC including medical order and interdisciplinary approach.\u00a0 Evaluates the progress of patient toward attainment of desired outcomes. Provides effective patient/family education/discharge planning. Administers medication per standard including drug information to patients/families. Acts as a resource/supports others. Delivers patient care using the principles of the defined nursing modality. Delegates care based on UAMS standards, legal and regulatory requirements, specific job description and individual level of education and training. Contributes to a positive work environment that is conducive to clinical education while serving as a resource for student nurses and staff. Additional Information: Constant Physical Activity : Hear, Read, Concentrate, Think Analytically, Frequent Physical Activity : Stand, Walk, Talk, Use hands to touch, handle or feel, Occasional Physical Activity : Sit, Bend, crawl, crouch, kneel, stoop, reach overhead, Taste or Smell, Lift/Carry Weight: 100 Lbs. or more Push/Pull Weight: 100 Lbs. or more Physical Environment : Inside Medical Facility Environment Noise Level: Moderate Visual Requirements: Near Visual Acuity, Far Visual Acuity, Color Discrimination, Depth Perception Hazards : Biological, Chemical, Sharp Objects/Tools, Dust, Fumes/Gases/Odors #UAMSNurses Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/RN---Medical-Specialties--F6-_R0090499-1": {"title": "RN - Medical Specialties (F6)", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-24\nPosted: Posted 11 Days Ago\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 11/30/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Shift Vary (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | NRSL Medical Spec F6 IP C Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Schedule:\u00a0Full-time & Part-time available, 7A-7P or 7P-7A or alternate 12 hour shifts, must work three shifts during the week plus rotate weekends. Available shifts based on unit needs and to be discussed with unit hiring manager. ****This posting will be utilized to fill multiple positions**** The Registered Nurse provides direct patient care to assigned patients in Medical Specialties (F6).\u00a0 This unit has an inpatient capacity of 30 beds. Patients receive comprehensive medical care which spans diagnosis and periodic re-admissions for treatment. Specialty nursing skills utilized on these units include provision of support to families and patients related to the psychosocial and emotional issues encountered with the diagnoses. A multidisciplinary approach to care is utilized and includes a social worker, pharmacist, clinical nurse specialist, and dietitian.\u00a0 The Patient Education Department provides assistance to staff in the development of education materials and provides ongoing patient education classes for patients and their families. Care is provided to a broad spectrum of patients including general medicine, pulmonary, gastrointestinal illness and infectious diseases. We strongly believe in patient and family centered care and plan our care with the patient as the primary focus. The partnership between healthcare providers and the patient and families are designed to meet individual spiritual, emotional, social and medical needs. Qualifications: Required Experience : Graduate of an accredited Nursing Program with Associates Degree, Nursing Diploma, Bachelors in Nursing, or Master's in Nursing.\u00a0 Valid RN License. One (1) year of Nursing Experience (direct patient care) similar to or related to the position applied for Basic computer skills. \u00a0 Preferred Experience : Two (2) or more years of registered nursing experience. Additional Information: Responsibilities: Delivers nursing care for patients in within the limits of the Nurse Practice Act of the State of Arkansas and adheres to institutional policies, procedures and standards. \u00a0 Responsible to adhere to the standard of care defined by UAMS, ANA, and Standards for specialty patient population with support and mentoring by other team members.\u00a0 Collects and documents assessment data. Develops a Plan of Care (POC) per standard.\u00a0 Implements POC including medical order and interdisciplinary approach.\u00a0 Evaluates the progress of patient toward attainment of desired outcomes.\u00a0 Provides effective patient/family education/discharge planning.\u00a0 Administers medication per standard including drug information to patients/families.\u00a0 Acts as a resource/supports others.\u00a0 Delivers patient care using the principles of the defined nursing modality.\u00a0 Delegates care based on UAMS standards, legal and regulatory requirements, specific job description and individual level of education and training.\u00a0 Contributes to a positive work environment that is conducive to clinical education while serving as a resource for student nurses and staff. Constant Physical Activity : Hear, Read, Concentrate, Think Analytically, Frequent Physical Activity : Stand Occasional Physical Activity : Bend, sit, crawl, crouch, kneel, stoop or reach overhead Lift/Carry Weight: 100 Lbs. or more Push/Pull Weight: 100 Lbs. or more Physical Environment : Inside medical Facility Noise Level: Moderate Visual Requirements: Color discrimination, Depth perception, Far visual acuity Near visual acuity Hazards : Biological, Dust, Fumes/Gases/Odors, Radiation, Sharp objects/tools #UAMSNurses Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/RN---Trauma-Surgical-Cardiovascular-Intensive-Care-Unit--CVICU----H4_R0090489-1": {"title": "RN - Trauma Surgical Cardiovascular Intensive Care Unit (CVICU) - H4", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-24\nPosted: Posted 11 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 11/27/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Shift Vary (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | NRSL CVICU H4 IP C Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: This posting will be used to fill multiple positions full-time and part-time positions available. Varied shifts available. The Registered Nurse (RN) will provide direct patient care as an RN. This professional nursing role will require the ability to coordinate care for patients, triage patients, and work collaboratively with clinic providers, fellows, and staff. Requires the ability to effectively work with patient referral sources, facilitate appointments, coordinate transitions of care, and provide patient education on complex conditions. The RN will work with the individual patient, their families, and providers of care to develop and implement individual health plans. Qualifications: Minimum: Bachelor\u2019s degree in Nursing, Associate\u2019s degree in Nursing, Diploma RN, or Master\u2019s degree in Nursing. Must be a graduate of an accredited RN nursing program. Minimum of 1 year of Registered Nursing experience. Valid Registered Nursing License Additional Information: Responsibilities: The Registered Nurse (RN) delivers nursing care for patients within the limits of the Nurse Practice Act of the State of Arkansas and adheres to institutional policies, procedures and standards.\u00a0The\u00a0RN is responsible to adhere to the standard of care defined by UAMS, ANA, and Standards for specialty patient population with support and mentoring by other team members.\u00a0 Collects and documents assessment data. Develops a Plan of Care (POC) per standard.\u00a0 Implements POC including medical order and interdisciplinary approach.\u00a0 Evaluates the progress of patients toward attainment of desired outcomes.\u00a0 Provides effective patient/family education/discharge planning.\u00a0 Administers medication per standard including drug information to patients/families.\u00a0 Acts as a resource/supports others.\u00a0 Delivers patient care using the principles of the defined nursing modality.\u00a0 Delegates care based on UAMS standards, legal and regulatory requirements, specific job descriptions and individual levels of education and training.\u00a0 Contributes to a positive work environment that is conducive to clinical education while serving as a resource for student nurses and staff. Perform other duties assigned. Physical Requirements: Stand: Frequently Sit: Occasionally Walk: Frequently Bend, crawl, crouch, kneel, stoop or reach overhead: Occasionally Lift and carry weight: 100+ lbs. Push and pull weight: 100+ lbs. Use hands to touch, handle or feel: Frequently Talk: Frequently Hear: Continuously Taste or smell: Occasionally Read, concentrate, and think analytically: Continuously Physical Environment : Inside Medical Facility Environment Noise Level: Moderate Visual Requirements: Color discrimination, Depth perception, Far visual acuity, Near visual acuity Hazards: Biological, Chemical, Dust, Electrical, Fumes/Gases/Odors, Radiation, Sharp objects/tools #UAMSNurses Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/RN---ENT-Ortho-Surgical-Specialties---F9_R0090485-1": {"title": "RN - ENT/Ortho Surgical Specialties - F9", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-24\nPosted: Posted 11 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 11/27/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Shift Vary (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | NRSL ENT/Ortho Surg Spec F9 IP C Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: This posting will be used to fill multiple positions. Full time/part time positions available - all shifts. The Registered Nurse (RN) delivers nursing care for patients in within the limits of the Nurse Practice Act of the State of Arkansas and adheres to institutional policies, procedures and standards.\u00a0The\u00a0RN is responsible to adhere to the standard of care defined by UAMS, ANA, and Standards for specialty patient population with support and mentoring by other team members.\u00a0 Collects and documents assessment data. Develops a Plan of Care (POC) per standard.\u00a0 Implements POC including medical order and interdisciplinary approach.\u00a0 Evaluates the progress of patient toward attainment of desired outcomes.\u00a0 Provides effective patient/family education/discharge planning.\u00a0 Administers medication per standard including drug information to patients/families.\u00a0 Acts as a resource/supports others.\u00a0 Delivers patient care using the principles of the defined nursing modality.\u00a0 Delegates care based on UAMS standards, legal and regulatory requirements, specific job description and individual level of education and training.\u00a0 Contributes to a positive work environment that is conducive to clinical education while serving as a resource for student nurses and staff. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Graduate of an accredited Nursing Program with Associates Degree, Nursing Diploma, Bachelors in Nursing, or Master's in Nursing.\u00a0 Valid RN License. One (1) year of Registered Nursing experience by date of hire. Additional Requirements/Competencies: Excellent communication skills. Basic computer skills. Strong work ethics and accountability. \u200b Preferred Qualifications: Two (2) or more years of nursing experience with current BLS. Responsibilities: The Registered Nurse provides direct patient care to assigned patients in ENT/Ortho Surgical Specialties (F9) .\u00a0 This 30-bed Medical Surgical unit provides care to adult patients with post-operative conditions. Orthopedic procedures include digit and limb re-implantation, joint replacement, re-constructive surgery and the latest in internal and external fixation of fractures. In addition, nurses care for Head and Neck (ENT) as well as Plastic surgery patients including microvascular free flaps. The needs of the surgical patient bring together the physician, nurse, social worker, rehabilitation specialists, respiratory therapist, patient educator, case manager and dietician for a multidisciplinary approach to care. Additional Information: Employees in this role must be fitted for, capable of donning and performing routine tasks in personal protective equipment to include N95 masks, Powered Air Purifying Respirators (PAPR) or Controlled Air Purifying Respirators (CAPR). Constant Physical Activity: See, Hear, Read, Concentrate, Think Analytically Frequent Physical Activity: Talk, Touch, Stand, Sit, Walk, Use hands to touch, handle or Feel Occasional Physical Activity: Taste, Smell, Bend, Crouch, Kneel, Stoop, or Reach Overhead Lift/Carry Weight: 0 to 65 lbs Push/Pull Weight: 65 lbs or more Physical Environment: Inside Medical Facility; Inside Office Environment Noise Level: Moderate Visual Requirements: \u00a0Near Visual Acuity, Far Visual Acuity, Color Discrimination, Depth Perception, Peripheral Vision Potential Hazards: Biological, Chemical, Electrical, Radiation, Sharp Objects/Tools #UAMSNurses Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/RN---Hospital-Medicine--H6-_R0090484-1": {"title": "RN - Hospital Medicine (H6)", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-24\nPosted: Posted 11 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 11/25/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Shift Vary (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | NRSL Hospital Med H6 IP C Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Schedule:\u00a0Full-time, 7A-7P or 7P-7A or alternate 12 hour shifts, must work three shifts during the week plus rotate weekends. Available shifts based on unit needs and to be discussed with unit hiring manager. This requisition will be used to fill multiple positions. Registered Nurse delivers nursing care for patients in within the limits of the Nurse Practice Act of the State of Arkansas and adheres to institutional policies, procedures and standards.\u00a0The\u00a0RN is responsible to adhere to the standard of care defined by UAMS, ANA, and Standards for specialty patient population with support and mentoring by other team members.\u00a0 Collects and documents assessment data. Develops a Plan of Care (POC) per standard.\u00a0 Implements POC including medical order and interdisciplinary approach.\u00a0 Evaluates the progress of patient toward attainment of desired outcomes.\u00a0 Provides effective patient/family education/discharge planning.\u00a0 Administers medication per standard including drug information to patients/families.\u00a0 Acts as a resource/supports others.\u00a0 Delivers patient care using the principles of the defined nursing modality.\u00a0 Delegates care based on UAMS standards, legal and regulatory requirements, specific job description and individual level of education and training.\u00a0 Contributes to a positive work environment that is conducive to clinical education while serving as a resource for student nurses and staff. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Graduate of an accredited Nursing Program with Associates Degree, Nursing Diploma, Bachelors in Nursing, or Master's in Nursing.\u00a0 Valid RN License, 1 year of Registered Nursing experience excellent communication skills, basic computer skills, strong work ethics and accountability. Preferred Qualifications: \u00a0 Previous hospital med/surg certification a plus 2 years or more nursing experience with current BLS. Additional Information: Responsibilities: The Registered Nurse provides direct patient care to assigned patients in Hospital Medicine Unit (H6) .\u00a0 This area is a 30-bed medical/surgical patient care unit that provides 24 hour care to acutely ill patients as well as palliative care for specialty patients and hospice patients.\u00a0 H6 provides care to a wide variety of patients such as Liver Disease, End-Stage Renal Disease, Respiratory Conditions, Immune Systems Diseases, Gastro-Intestinal Disease, and Musculoskeletal/Integumentary Diseases. Remote telemetry is available for patients who are presenting with clinical cardiac concerns who present with a history of cardiac disease.\u00a0 \u00a0We also provide pre/postoperative care as well. The patient population ranges from young adult to geriatric. Employees in this role must be fitted for, capable of donning and performing routine tasks in personal protective equipment to include N95 masks, Powered Air Purifying Respirators (PAPR) or Controlled Air Purifying Respirators (CAPR). Constant Physical Activity : Hear, Read, Concentrate, Think Analytically, Frequent Physical Activity : Stand, Walk, Talk, Use hands to touch, handle or feel, Occasional Physical Activity : Sit, Bend, crawl, crouch, kneel, stoop, reach overhead Lift/Carry Weight: 11 - 25 lbs Push/Pull Weight: 100 Lbs. or more Physical Environment : Inside Medical Facility Environment Noise Level: Moderate Visual Requirements: Near Visual Acuity Hazards : Biological, Sharp Objects/Tools #UAMSNurses Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/RN---ICU-Trauma-Progressive-Care---F4_R0090482": {"title": "RN - ICU/Trauma Progressive Care - F4", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-24\nPosted: Posted 11 Days Ago\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 11/27/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | NRSL Trauma Surg Spec F4 IP C Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Schedule: Full-Time, Shifts Vary This position will be used to fill multiple positions\u00a0 The Registered Nurse provides direct patient care to assigned patients in the ICU /Trauma Progressive Care Unit (F4).\u00a0 F4 is a 30-bed blended ICU and Intermediate care unit providing care for a wide variety of patient populations, primarily focused on trauma and acute care surgery. Common diagnoses include traumatic brain injuries, spinal cord injuries, blunt, penetrating, and orthopedic trauma, as well as geriatric falls. Care is also provided for surgical patients following abdominal surgeries and patients requiring long term mechanical ventilation. Education is provided to staff that includes the basic critical care course, dysrhythmia course, advanced cardiac life support certification, and trauma nursing core certification. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Graduate of an accredited Nursing Program with Associates Degree, Nursing Diploma, Bachelors in Nursing, or Master's in Nursing.\u00a0 Valid RN License. One (1) year Registered Nursing experience. Excellent communication skills. Basic computer skills. Strong work ethics and accountability. Preferred Qualifications: National Certification BSN or MSN 2 or more years of nursing experience A minimum of 1 year in an acute care setting such as a teaching hospital Cardiac experience Additional Information: Responsibilities Collects and documents assessment data Develops a Plan of Care (POC) per standard Implements POC including medical order and interdisciplinary approach Evaluates the progress of patient toward attainment of desired outcomes Provides effective patient/family education/discharge planning Administers medication per standard including drug information to patients/families Acts as a resource/supports others; Delivers patient care using the principles of the defined nursing modality Delegates care based on UAMS standards, legal and regulatory requirements, specific job description and individual level of education and training Contributes to a positive work environment that is conducive to clinical education while serving as a resource for student nurses and staff. Other duties as assigned\u00a0 Employees in this role must be fitted for, capable of donning and performing routine tasks in personal protective equipment to include N95 masks, Powered Air Purifying Respirators (PAPR) or Controlled Air Purifying Respirators (CAPR). PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS Stand: Frequently Sit: Occasionally Walk: Frequently Bend, crawl, crouch, kneel, stoop or reach overhead: Occasionally Lift and carry weight: 100+ lbs Push and pull weight :100+ lbs Use hands to touch, handle or feel: Frequently Talk: Frequently Hear: Continuously Taste or smell: Occasionally Read, concentrate, think analytically: Continuously Physical Environment : Inside Medical Facility Environment Noise Level : Moderate Visual Requirements: Color discrimination, Depth perception, Far visual acuity, Near visual acuity Hazards: Biological, Chemical, Dust, Electrical, Fumes/Gases/Odors, Radiation, Sharp objects/tools #UAMSNurses Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/RN---Medical-Neurology-ICU--E4-_R0090480-1": {"title": "RN - Medical Neurology ICU (E4)", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-24\nPosted: Posted 11 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 11/25/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | NRSL Med/Neuro ICU E4 IP C Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Schedule: full-time & part-time available Shift: day shift and night shift available This posting will be utilized to fill multiple positions. The Registered Nurse provides direct patient care to assigned patients in the Intensive Care Unit (E4). Our 28-bed ICU unit located in the Harry P. & Betty Jo Ward Towers provides care for a wide variety of Medical, Neurology, Neuro-Surgical and Bone Marrow Transplant patients. The unit is equipped with state-of-the-art technology and a highly-trained all RN staff. Comprehensive orientation and educational courses are provided, based on individual need. The exposure to educational enhancements combined with the opportunity to participate in research is unmatched. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Graduate of an accredited Nursing Program with Associates Degree, Nursing Diploma, Bachelors in Nursing, or Master's in Nursing.\u00a0 Valid RN License. One (1) year Registered Nursing experience. Excellent communication skills. Basic computer skills. Strong work ethics and accountability. Preferred Qualifications: BSN or MSN 2 or more years of nursing experience with a minimum of 1 year in an acute care setting such as a teaching hospital. 1 year or more of Oncology RN experience.\u00a0 National Certification Additional Information: Responsibilities Collects and documents assessment data Develops a Plan of Care (POC) per standard Implements POC including medical order and interdisciplinary approach Evaluates the progress of patient toward attainment of desired outcomes Provides effective patient/family education/discharge planning Administers medication per standard including drug information to patients/families Acts as a resource/supports others; Delivers patient care using the principles of the defined nursing modality Delegates care based on UAMS standards, legal and regulatory requirements, specific job description and individual level of education and training Contributes to a positive work environment that is conducive to clinical education while serving as a resource for student nurses and staff. Other duties as assigned\u00a0 Employees in this role must be fitted for, capable of donning and performing routine tasks in personal protective equipment to include N95 masks, Powered Air Purifying Respirators (PAPR) or Controlled Air Purifying Respirators (CAPR). PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS Stand: Frequently Sit: Occasionally Walk: Frequently Bend, crawl, crouch, kneel, stoop or reach overhead: Occasionally Lift and carry weight: 100+ lbs Push and pull weight :100+ lbs Use hands to touch, handle or feel: Frequently Talk: Frequently Hear: Continuously Taste or smell: Occasionally Read, concentrate, think analytically: Continuously Physical Environment : Inside Medical Facility Environment Noise Level : Moderate Visual Requirements: Color discrimination, Depth perception, Far visual acuity, Near visual acuity Hazards: Biological, Chemical, Dust, Electrical, Fumes/Gases/Odors, Radiation, Sharp objects/tools #UAMSNurses Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/RN---Stem-Cell-Transplant---F7_R0090478-1": {"title": "RN - Stem Cell Transplant - F7", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-24\nPosted: Posted 11 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 11/24/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | NRSL Stem Cell Transplant F7 IP C Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Schedule: full-time & part-time available Shift: day shift and night shift available This posting will be utilized to fill multiple positions. The Registered Nurse provides direct patient care to assigned patients in the Stem Cell Transplant Unit (F7).\u00a0 This is a 30 private bed unit which specializes in the care of Multiple Myeloma patients.\u00a0 Team members include physicians, registered nurses, APRN\u2019s, clinical pharmacists, dietitians, social workers, chaplains, physical and occupational therapists, and psychologists. This team provides continuity of care for all patients receiving stem cell transplants, both autologous and allogeneic.\u00a0 Nurses are an integral part of the multidisciplinary team providing care to these patients, administering chemotherapy and supportive care treatments throughout the inpatient stay. Qualifications: Required Qualifications: Graduate of an accredited Nursing Program with Associates Degree, Nursing Diploma, Bachelors in Nursing, or Master's in Nursing.\u00a0 Valid RN License. One (1) year of Registered Nursing experience. Excellent communication skills. Basic computer skills. Strong work ethics and accountability. Preferred Qualifications: Two (2) years or more nursing experience with current BLS. Responsibilities: Registered Nurse delivers nursing care for patients in within the limits of the Nurse Practice Act of the State of Arkansas and adheres to institutional policies, procedures and standards. \u00a0 The\u00a0RN is responsible to adhere to the standard of care defined by UAMS, ANA, and Standards for specialty patient population with support and mentoring by other team members.\u00a0 Collects and documents assessment data. Develops a Plan of Care (POC) per standard.\u00a0 Implements POC including medical order and interdisciplinary approach.\u00a0 Evaluates the progress of patient toward attainment of desired outcomes.\u00a0 Provides effective patient/family education/discharge planning.\u00a0 Administers medication per standard including drug information to patients/families.\u00a0 Acts as a resource/supports others.\u00a0 Delivers patient care using the principles of the defined nursing modality.\u00a0 Delegates care based on UAMS standards, legal and regulatory requirements, specific job description and individual level of education and training.\u00a0 Contributes to a positive work environment that is conducive to clinical education while serving as a resource for student nurses and staff. Additional Information: Constant Physical Activity : Hear, Read, Concentrate, Think Analytically, Frequent Physical Activity : Stand, Walk, Talk, Use hands to touch, handle or feel, Occasional Physical Activity : Sit, Bend, crawl, crouch, kneel, stoop, reach overhead, Taste or Smell, Lift/Carry Weight: 100 Lbs. or more Push/Pull Weight: 100 Lbs. or more Physical Environment : Inside Medical Facility Environment Noise Level: Moderate Visual Requirements: Near Visual Acuity, Far Visual Acuity, Color Discrimination, Depth Perception Hazards : Biological, Chemical, Sharp Objects/Tools, Dust, Fumes/Gases/Odors #UAMSNurses Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/RN---Cardiovascular-Medical-Specialties--F8-_R0090476-1": {"title": "RN - Cardiovascular/Medical Specialties (F8)", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-24\nPosted: Posted 11 Days Ago\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 11/30/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Shift Vary (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | NRSL Cardiac Med Spec F8 IP C Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Schedule: full-time & part-time available Shift: day shift and night shift available This posting will be utilized to fill multiple positions. The Registered Nurse provides direct patient care to assigned patients in Cardiovascular/Medical Specialties (F8). This 30-bed adult inpatient unit specializing in the care and treatment of patients belonging to the Cardiology, Cardiothoracic (CT) Surgery, and Vascular Surgery teams, as well as Medicine teams. Our inter-professional team works together to meet the needs of patients with heart and/or vascular conditions including patients recovering from open heart surgery transferred from the CVICU, lung surgery, angioplasty, pacemaker insertion, vascular surgery, aneurysm repair, amputations, heart attack, arrhythmias, heart failure, and wide variety of other conditions. Patients on telemetry are remotely monitored, and portable bedside monitors are available for patients requiring closer observation. F8 embraces the mission and values of the UAMS Integrated Clinical Enterprise philosophy of patient care delivery. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Graduate of an accredited Nursing Program Valid RN License One (1) year of Registered Nursing experience Excellent communication skills, basic computer skills, strong work ethics and accountability. Preferred Qualifications: National Certification BSN or MSN Two (2) or more years of nursing experience with a minimum of one (1) year in an acute care setting such as a teaching hospital Cardiac experience Additional Information: Responsibilities: Delivers nursing care for patients in within the limits of the Nurse Practice Act of the State of Arkansas and adheres to institutional policies, procedures and standards. \u00a0 Responsible to adhere to the standard of care defined by UAMS, ANA, and Standards for specialty patient population with support and mentoring by other team members.\u00a0 Collects and documents assessment data. Develops a Plan of Care (POC) per standard.\u00a0 Implements POC including medical order and interdisciplinary approach.\u00a0 Evaluates the progress of patient toward attainment of desired outcomes.\u00a0 Provides effective patient/family education/discharge planning.\u00a0 Administers medication per standard including drug information to patients/families.\u00a0 Acts as a resource/supports others.\u00a0 Delivers patient care using the principles of the defined nursing modality.\u00a0 Delegates care based on UAMS standards, legal and regulatory requirements, specific job description and individual level of education and training.\u00a0 Contributes to a positive work environment that is conducive to clinical education while serving as a resource for student nurses and staff. May perform other duties as assigned. Constant Physical Activity : Hear, Read, Concentrate, Think Analytically, Frequent Physical Activity : Stand Occasional Physical Activity : Bend, sit, crawl, crouch, kneel, stoop or reach overhead Lift/Carry Weight: 100 Lbs. or more Push/Pull Weight: 100 Lbs. or more Physical Environment : Inside medical Facility Noise Level: Moderate Visual Requirements: Color discrimination, Depth perception, Far visual acuity Near visual acuity Hazards : Biological, Dust, Fumes/Gases/Odors, Radiation, Sharp objects/tools #UAMSNurses Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Fort-Smith/RN-Outpatient-Clinic-M-F---Ft-Smith--AR-_R0090172-1": {"title": "RN-Outpatient Clinic M-F  (Ft. Smith, AR)", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-20\nPosted: Posted 15 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/30/2026 Type of Position: Clinical Staff - Nursing Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: REP | PCPHSL CS West Fort Smith Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: We are seeking a dedicated and experienced Registered Nurse (RN) to join our team at our Fort Smith Family Medical Center. You will be responsible for ensuring the delivery of the highest quality Patient and Family-Centered Care within the clinic. Manage the patient flow processes, and promote wellness, improved outcomes, and self-care among a defined patient population. Additionally, you will play a crucial role in providing support, education, and assistance to patients who have chronic conditions, helping them prevent and maintain their health. Join us at UAMS and enjoy a fulfilling career where your skills help transform lives. Grow professionally in a team that values collaboration, innovation, and compassionate care. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Graduate of an accredited Nursing Program with Associates Degree, Nursing Diploma, Bachelors in Nursing, or Master's in Nursing Valid RN License Minimum of one (1) year Registered Nursing experience.Will consider RN with two (2) years of LPN clinical experience. Preferred Qualifications: Clinic or Ambulatory Setting experience. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: The ability to work independently and maintain high-quality care, and the application of policies will be required. Good communication skills (written and oral). Excellent customer service skills. Problem-solving skills. Leadership and collaborative skills. Strong patient advocacy and patient education skills. Strong organizational skills and computer knowledge. Professional and courteous telephone etiquette. General knowledge of office machines, including printers, fax machines, and scanners. Understanding basic medical terminology is necessary. Additional Information: Key Responsibilities : Triage, assessment, planning, implementation, and evaluation of nursing care and patient education either by telephone or within the UAMS Clinic.\u00a0 Delivers nursing care according to standards as defined by UAMS, American Nurses Association (ANA), AR State Board of Nursing (ASBN), and those set forth by nursing specialty organizations. Coordinates care and/or follow-up for patients who receive care in inpatient and outpatient facilities.\u00a0 Implements patient care using an approach that is interdisciplinary and Patient and Family-Centered Care. Effectively collaborates and communicates with nursing staff at all levels, interdisciplinary teams, executive leaders, and other stakeholders. May perform other duties as assigned to support the mission of UAMS. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience. Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), Resume Optional Documents: List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Criminal Background Check, Substance Abuse Testing This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Repetitive Motion, Sharps, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Feeling, Grasping, Lifting, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Standing Occasional Physical Activity: Balancing, Kneeling, Sitting, Stooping Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/RN---Neurology-Neurosurgery--H8-_R0090200-1": {"title": "RN - Neurology/Neurosurgery (H8)", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-18\nPosted: Posted 17 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 11/30/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | NRSL Neuro/Neuro Surg H8 IP C Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Schedule: Full-Time, Shift Varies This posting will be used to fill multiple positions.\u00a0 The Registered Nurse provides patient care to assigned patients in the H8 Neuroscience Progressive Care Unit (NPCU). The NPCU is a 30-bed unit specializing in neurological and neurosurgical diagnoses. Neuroscience nursing at UAMS is part of the Critical Care Division. Our nurses receive focused education and competency assessment for common neuroscience concepts, monitoring, procedures, and devices. The NPCU works closely with the Neurocritical Care area and can facilitate transfer for the right candidate. UAMS is designated as a Comprehensive Stroke Certified Center, providing the highest level of acute stroke care, Comprehensive Level 4 Epilepsy Center, providing the highest level of epilepsy monitoring and treatment, and recognized by Healthgrades with the 2022 Cranial Neurosurgery Excellence Award. Neurosurgical services include: \u2022 Pre and post-op care for procedures \u2022 Craniotomy \u2022 Spinal decompression \u2022 Deep brain stimulation (DBS) \u2022 Surgical EEG \u2022 Care of TBI Neurological services consist of care for: \u2022 Stroke \u2022 Epilepsy \u2022 Parkinson\u2019s and movement disorders \u2022 Multiple Sclerosis \u2022 ALS & Neuromuscular disease We strongly support achieving national certification, including specialty certifications, i.e., Stroke Certified Registered Nurse (SCRN) and Certified Neuroscience Registered Nurse (CNRN), and offer preparatory resources, as well as compensation. Qualifications: Minimum: Graduate of an accredited Nursing Program with Associates Degree, Nursing Diploma, Bachelors in Nursing, or Master's in Nursing.\u00a0 Valid RN License. One (1) year Registered Nursing experience. Excellent communication skills. Basic computer skills. Strong work ethics and accountability. Preferred: National Certification BSN or MSN 2 or more years of nursing experience\u00a0 A minimum of 1 year in an acute care setting such as a teaching hospital Cardiac experience a plus Employees in this role must be fitted for, capable of donning and performing routine tasks in personal protective equipment to include N95 masks, Powered Air Purifying Respirators (PAPR) or Controlled Air Purifying Respirators (CAPR). Responsibilities Collects and documents assessment data Develops a Plan of Care (POC) per standard Implements POC including medical order and interdisciplinary approach Evaluates the progress of patient toward attainment of desired outcomes Provides effective patient/family education/discharge planning Administers medication per standard including drug information to patients/families Acts as a resource/supports others; Delivers patient care using the principles of the defined nursing modality Delegates care based on UAMS standards, legal and regulatory requirements, specific job description and individual level of education and training Contributes to a positive work environment that is conducive to clinical education while serving as a resource for student nurses and staff. Other duties as assigned\u00a0 Additional Information: PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS Constant Physical Activity : Hear, Read, Concentrate, Think Analytically, Frequent Physical Activity : Stand, Walk, Talk, Use hands to touch, handle or feel, Occasional Physical Activity : Sit, Bend, crawl, crouch, kneel, stoop, reach overhead, Taste or Smell, Lift/Carry Weight: 100 Lbs. or more Push/Pull Weight: 100 Lbs. or more Physical Environment : Inside Medical Facility Environment Noise Level: Moderate Visual Requirements: Near Visual Acuity, Far Visual Acuity, Color Discrimination, Depth Perception Hazards : Biological, Chemical, Sharp Objects/Tools, Dust, Fumes/Gases/Odors #UAMSNurses Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Pharmacy-Technician-III---Distribution_R0090125-1": {"title": "Pharmacy Technician III - Distribution", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-18\nPosted: Posted 17 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 10/18/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Shift Vary (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | PTSL Pharmacy Stores Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: ** This job posting will fill two positions** The Distribution Technician is responsible for supporting the centralized pharmacy distribution operations of the health system through accurate medication receiving, inventory management, replenishment, picking, packing, delivery, and distribution activities across inpatient, ambulatory, clinic, and infusion service lines. This position works closely with pharmacy procurement, warehouse, and operational leadership to ensure timely and compliant medication movement throughout the organization while maintaining appropriate inventory control standards, medication security, and regulatory compliance. The Distribution Technician assists with daily operations involving pharmaceutical wholesaler orders, internal stock transfers, automated dispensing cabinet replenishment support, controlled workflow processes, cold-chain product handling, expiration date monitoring, shortage mitigation support, and management of pharmaceutical supplies and packaging materials. The technician is expected to maintain a high level of accuracy, organization, and customer service while supporting efficient medication distribution and minimizing waste and drug spend. The Distribution Technician operates within established pharmacy policies, health system procedures, and applicable regulatory standards including state board of pharmacy requirements, USP standards, and health system safety protocols. Responsibilities may include operation of inventory technology systems, barcode scanning platforms, automated storage systems, and distribution software to document medication movement and maintain inventory integrity. This role collaborates with pharmacists, buyers, clinic staff, couriers, and supply chain personnel to resolve distribution issues, support emergency medication requests, coordinate backorder or shortage substitutions, and maintain continuity of patient care services across multiple sites of care. Qualifications: Minimum Quallifications: Three (3) years relevant pharmacy technician work experience (i.e. retail, hospital, etc.) Pharmacy Technician License by the Arkansas State Board of Pharmacy National Technician Certification (PTCB) Computer Skills (i.e. Microsoft Office and EMR experience) Preferred Qualifications: Undergraduate degree Good/Strong Math Skills Prior experience in a specialized role - Automation, Controlled Substances, Pharmacy Buyer, Investigational Drugs, Medication Reconciliation, IV Compounding Specialist, WAM Orders Entry ASHP/ACPE accredited technician training or certified program (i.e. PTCB Certified Compounded Sterile Preparation Technician, ASHP Sterile Compounding Certificate, etc.) Relevant pharmacy technician experience (i.e. retail, hospital, etc.) Additional Information: Responsibilities: Receives, verifies, and stocks pharmaceutical inventory from wholesalers, manufacturers, 340B accounts, and internal transfers Maintains accurate inventory levels and replenishment processes for inpatient pharmacies, ambulatory clinics, infusion centers, procedural areas, and automated dispensing systems Picks, packs, stages, and coordinates medication deliveries accurately and efficiently across multiple sites of care Performs barcode scanning, inventory tracking, cycle counts, expiration date monitoring, and discrepancy resolution activities Supports management of pharmaceutical inventory across GPO, WAC, and 340B purchasing accounts while maintaining inventory integrity and segregation requirements Maintains cold-chain handling and storage requirements for refrigerated and frozen medications Assists with medication shortage mitigation strategies, substitution workflows, and emergency inventory requests Processes returns, recalls, expired medications, damaged product documentation, and reverse distribution activities in accordance with policy Maintains organization, cleanliness, and security of warehouse, storage, and distribution areas Operates and troubleshoots pharmacy inventory technology systems, barcode systems, automated storage equipment, and distribution software platforms Assists with controlled substance inventory workflows and maintains appropriate security and documentation standards Coordinates replenishment and delivery priorities based on operational urgency and patient care needs Responds promptly and professionally to medication distribution requests from inpatient units, clinics, infusion centers, and procedural areas Communicates effectively with pharmacists, buyers, technicians, nursing staff, and operational leaders regarding inventory issues, backorders, and delivery status Supports timely resolution of stock-outs, missing medication requests, and urgent distribution needs Maintains strong customer service standards while ensuring accuracy, professionalism, and confidentiality Assists with delivery documentation, routing workflows, and courier coordination activities Maintains compliance with state board of pharmacy regulations, USP standards, health system policies, and accreditation requirements Adheres to medication handling procedures for hazardous drugs and other high-risk medications Maintains active Arkansas Pharmacy Technician registration and national technician certification as required Demonstrates flexibility to support multiple operational areas and changing distribution priorities Other duties as assigned Physical Demands: Medium Work | Exerting up to 50 pounds of force occasionally, and/or up to 30 pounds of force frequently, and/or up to 10 pounds of force constantly to move objects. Visual Requirements: close visual acuity to perform an activity such as: preparing and analyzing data and figures; transcribing; viewing a computer terminal; extensive reading; and/or visual inspection at distances close to the eyes. Constant Physical Demands: Repetitive Movements Think Analytically, Read, Concentrate Frequent Physical Demands: Standing Sitting Stooping Walking Talking Hearing Occasional Physical Demands: Lifting Taste Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Access-Coordinator-III---Cancer-Institute_R0090026-1": {"title": "Access Coordinator III - Cancer Institute", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-17\nPosted: Posted 18 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 10/17/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | CORE PA Float Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Access Coordinator III works under supervision to function as a patient resource for all scheduling and billing questions and to facilitate comprehensive patient data collections, timely and accurate billing, prompt collections of payment for services rendered, facilitates scheduling coordination and conflicts. This position must be able to perform all duties of the Access Coordinator I & II level and performs other duties to support the patient care activities as needed. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: High School Diploma or GED PLUS Three (3) years experience in registration, billing, or scheduling in a healthcare environment . Good communication skills, computer/basic keyboard skills, telephone etiquette skills, and general knowledge of office machines including printers and scanners. Excellent customer service skills. Knowledge in basic medical terminology. Preferred Qualifications: CHAA Certification Additional Information: Responsibilities: Records daily and monthly statistics and communicates any medical records issues Schedules and coordinates appointments and surgeries or tests using hospital systems by processing visit notifications of patients Ensures adequate stock of supplies, and cleans and maintains equipment and waiting rooms Conducts pre-registration, inputs and/or updates patient information, processes walk-ins, creates new patient charts, and accesses systems for orders Conducts insurance verification and benefits explanation by running eligibility on patients, requesting outside records and gathering outside medical records from referrals and files patient charts as needed. Conducts authorizations and pre-certifications, tracks pre-authorizations, and maintains referrals Collects and posts payments and issues receipts. Reconciles daily deposit and batch dollars and counsels patients on any and all related financial information Performs other duties as assigned All UAMS employees will treat others with Dignity and Respect. \u00a0We communicate and share complete and unbiased information, assuring our colleagues receive timely, complete, and accurate information in order make informed decisions. \u00a0We participate in institutional initiatives and encourage the participation of others. \u00a0We collaborate in policy and program development, implementation, and evaluation using best practices in delivering quality service. All duties will be performed in accordance with the UAMS Core Concepts of Patient and Family Centered Care set forth by UAMS. \u00a0These core concepts allow for an approach to health care that shapes policies, programs, facility design and staff day-to-day interactions. It leads to better health outcomes and wiser allocation of resources, and greater patient and family satisfaction. \u00a0The core concepts of patient and family centered care consist of Dignity & Respect, Information Sharing, Participation, and Collaboration. Salary Information: $17.72 - hr Required Documents to Apply: List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Pharmacy-Technician-IV---Specialty-Pharmacy_R0090071-2": {"title": "Pharmacy Technician IV - Specialty Pharmacy", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-17\nPosted: Posted 18 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 11/17/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Shift Vary (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | PTSL Specialty Coordinators Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: ** This posting will fill multiple positions** The Pharmacy Technician IV will work under the supervision of the pharmacist to provide excellent customer service to patients receiving specialty medications. This technician will be responsible for the management for the dispensing functions for specialty medications and monthly outreach calls to assess the need for refills on medications and check on the overall wellbeing of the assigned patients. The Pharmacy Technician IV will also be responsible for managing prior authorizations and financial assistance for assigned specialty patients as well as serve as a role model and assist in the training of staff. All clinical issues will be referred to the pharmacist. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: High School Diploma or GED Plus 4 years relevant pharmacy technician experience OR Undergraduate degree and relevant pharmacy technician experience Licensed pharmacy technician by the Arkansas State Board of Pharmacy 1 year to obtain ASHP/ACPE Accredited Technician Training or certificate program (such as Advanced Certified) PTCB National Certification Preferred Qualifications: Master's Degree 2+ years of UAMS Pharmacy experience Additional Information: Responsibilities: Monitors prior authorizations for timely submission and processing as outlined in the policies and procedures.\u00a0 Ability to identify pertinent literature for appeals and help/teach others this process.\u00a0 Possesses a good understanding of all disease states. Ensures outstanding prior authorizations are monitored daily.\u00a0 Audit documentation for presence and accuracy. Monitors outstanding financial assistance to streamline timely patient access. Promotes continuous patient communication throughout the patient journey.\u00a0 Refers all clinical issues to the pharmacist, always working within the pharmacy technician's scope of practice. Participates in the training of staff.\u00a0 Works in any disease state as needed.\u00a0 Monitors the ACD and addresses gaps.\u00a0 Uses appropriate walk-away codes.\u00a0 Reports all gaps to the Assistant Director of Pharmacy. Possesses advanced knowledge of the adjudication process and mitigates billing problems as they arise.\u00a0 Assists others with adjudication issues and can teach the adjudication process.\u00a0 Audits each specialty prescription for accuracy to ensure proper billing.\u00a0 Ensures prescription processing is promptly done with a focus on patient safety and clean claims.\u00a0 Assists others once work is completed every day.\u00a0 Ensures that prescriptions are accurately filled and all necessary information is in the work basket, including payment. Works to enhance the workflow. Is responsible for improving documentation to enhance patient safety and outcomes.\u00a0 Models professional communication with patients, providers, payers, and PBMs.\u00a0 Works in any disease state as needed.\u00a0 Reports all gaps to the Assistant Director of Pharmacy. Other duties as assigned. Physical Demands: Medium Work | Exerting up to 50 pounds of force occasionally, and/or up to 30 pounds of force frequently, and/or up to 10 pounds of force constantly to move objects. Visual Requirements: close visual acuity to perform an activity such as: preparing and analyzing data and figures; transcribing; viewing a computer terminal; extensive reading; and/or visual inspection at distances close to the eyes. Constant Physical Demands: Hearing Repetitive Movements Standing Talking Walking Frequent Physical Demands: Sitting Stooping Occasional Physical Demands: Lifting Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/RN-Part-Time---Capitol-Mall-Clinic--M-F-Outpatient-_R0089984-1": {"title": "RN Part Time - Capitol Mall Clinic (M-F Outpatient)", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-14\nPosted: Posted 21 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/14/2026 Type of Position: Clinical Staff - Nursing Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | PCPHSL | Capitol Mall Clinic Department's Website: https://uamshealth.com/location/neighborhood-capitol-mall/ Summary of Job Duties: This part-time Registered Nurse (RN) position averages between 20 and 30 hours per week and is benefits-eligible. This position is ideal for a nurse seeking consistent part-time hours and a supportive team environment. The Registered Nurse will promote wellness; improve outcomes, and self-care within a defined population of patients. The RN will provide patients who have chronic conditions the support, education, and assistance in the prevention and/or maintenance of their disease and/or health and wellness state. Will work with the individual patient, their families, and providers of care to develop and implement individual health plans and provide support to the patient in self-management. Coordinate care and/or follow-up for patients who receive care in outpatient facilities. Coordination of prescription refill requests and patient education coordination in collaboration with physician staff. Commitment to patient outcomes results in high levels of performance despite workload changes. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Graduate of an accredited Nursing Program with an Associate's Degree, Nursing Diploma, Bachelor's in Nursing, or Master's in Nursing ; Valid RN License; Minimum of 1 year Registered Nursing experience. Preferred Qualifications: 3 years of RN experience with current BLS certification. Knowledge or experience in PCMH ACLS certification or obtain certification within one year of hire date. Additional Information: BENEFITS ELIGIBLE - This position offers part-time hours ranging from 20 to 30 hours per week, with a schedule that includes daytime shifts. There are no night, weekend, or most State holiday commitments associated with this role. Responsibilities: Collects and documents assessment data from patients and/or others per UAMS standard.\u00a0 Develops patient's Plan of Care (POC) per department/unit standards utilizing assessment data.\u00a0 Evaluates the progress of patients toward attainment of desired outcomes. Administers medication following department/unit standards and the Nurse Practice Act.\u00a0 Verifies and evaluates care delivered to ensure it is consistent with patient and family-centered care principles, practice standards, and regulatory requirements. Supports the integration of current evidence into nursing practices.\u00a0 Promotes an environment conducive to positive educational experience for all students and staff.\u00a0 Provides effective patient/family education/discharge planning. Effectively collaborates and communicates with nursing staff at all levels, interdisciplinary teams, executive leaders, and other stakeholders.\u00a0 Communicates care appropriately through documentation in the medical record. Reports variances in care/ systems/ processes through the appropriate means.\u00a0 Participates in the recruitment/retention of staff.\u00a0 Facilitates the development and implementation of nursing practice standards that are evidence-based and in compliance with ANA standards. May perform other duties as assigned. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Criminal Background Check, Substance Abuse Testing This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Feeling, Grasping, Hearing, Repetitive Motion, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Standing Occasional Physical Activity: Crouching, Driving, Kneeling, Lifting, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Sitting, Stooping Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/APRN-PA---Electrophysiology_R0089960-1": {"title": "APRN/PA - Electrophysiology", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-14\nPosted: Posted 21 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/30/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | CVSL Mid-Levels IP C Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: This posting will fill with either an APRN or PA. The Advanced Practice Nurse/Physician Assistant works collaboratively with a physician and multidisciplinary health team to provide comprehensive care to outpatients. The APRN/PA is responsible for assessment, diagnosis, treatment, management, education, health promotion, and care coordination for patients and families with acute and chronic health needs. As an integral part of the UAMS Cardiovascular Electrophysiology (EP) Team, the APRN or PA works collaboratively with the attending physicians and residents to ensure continuity of care to the EP patients. The APRNs or PAs help plan, implement, and evaluate health care treatments. This position requires both inpatient and outpatient practice areas. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: APRNs: Master\u2019s Degree in nursing Adult-Gerontology Acute Care Certification 3 years nursing experience Licensed Registered Nurse in Arkansas; APRN License Prescriptive authority and DEA license must be obtained after hire. \u00a0 PAs: Master's Degree Graduate of an accredited Physician Assistant program Certification through NCCPA Prescriptive authority and DEA license must be obtained after hire \u00a0 Preferred Qualifications: At least 1 year APP experience in cardiology specialty Prior EP experience Additional Information: Responsibilities: Extend the patient care and administrative services of the University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences physicians. \u00a0 Provide comprehensive health assessments, determine diagnoses, implement treatment plans, prescribe medical treatments, and manage health issues for patients in collaboration with the designated physician(s). \u00a0 Work autonomously, as well as, in collaboration with a variety of individuals to diagnose and manage patients' health care problems; and will serve as a health care resource, interdisciplinary consultant, and patient advocate. \u00a0 Coordinate the multidisciplinary care of patients, facilitating all necessary consults, and assuring that care is timely and appropriate. \u00a0 Interacts with and assists the public in a professional and friendly manner as needed. Demonstrates effective communication skills; communicates accurate and complete information; maintains strict confidentiality when necessary. Demonstrates positive working relationships with co-workers, management team, and ancillary departments; follows the Core Concepts of Patient and Family Centered Care and the Basic Code of Conduct Guidelines. Assist internal and external stakeholders as needed with exceptional customer service.\u00a0 Extend the patient care and administrative services of the University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences physicians. Other duties as assigned. Constant Physical Activity : Hear, Read, Concentrate, Think Analytically, Frequent Physical Activity : Stand Occasional Physical Activity : Bend, sit, crawl, crouch, kneel, stoop or reach overhead Lift/Carry Weight: 11 - 25 Lbs. or more Push/Pull Weight: 100 Lbs. or more Physical Environment : Inside medical Facility Noise Level: Moderate Visual Requirements: Color discrimination, Depth perception, Far visual acuity Near visual acuity Hazards : Biological, Dust, Fumes/Gases/Odors, Radiation, Sharp objects/tools Salary Information: \"Commensurate with Education and Experience\" Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Medical-Assistant---Rahling-Rd-Neighborhood-Clinic_R0089955-1": {"title": "Medical Assistant - Rahling Rd Neighborhood Clinic", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-14\nPosted: Posted 21 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/14/2026 Type of Position: Clinical Staff - Nursing Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | PCPHSL Rahling Road Clinic Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Medical Assistant, (MA), works under the direct supervision of the clinic physician by assisting in the examination and treatment of patients. The MA will conduct patient interviews and all required screenings, measure vital signs (i.e., pulse rate, temperature, blood pressure, weight, and height), and records information in patients' Electronic Medical Record (EMR). The MA will also draw and collect blood samples from patients and prepare specimens for laboratory analysis. May also perform EKGs. Also prepares treatment rooms for examination of patients and ensures exam rooms are stocked with supplies needed for patient care activities. The MA may also perform administrative tasks by registering and scheduling patients for appointments, procedures, etc. using the various registrations and scheduling systems. This position will float to other PCPHSL Clinics as needed. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: High School Diploma or GED Plus Successful completion of an accredited Medical Assistant program. Current, Active Basic Life Support (BLS) certificate Preferred Qualifications: 1 year of Medical Assistant experience Previous experience in ambulatory care setting Pediatric experience Additional Information: Responsibilities: Provides direct patient care by acquiring medical history, vital signs, and lab samples. Communicates with nursing staff regarding changes in patient's condition and maintains adequate level of supplies required for patient care. Greets patients upon arrival to clinic. Schedules, registers, and checks out patients. Collects payments, issues receipts, and verifies insurance coverage. Transports patients to other areas of the hospital. Provides appropriate grooming/oral hygiene and comfort measures and assists patients with physical activities. Documents all patient care activities. Adheres to UAMS safety plan. Complies with safety instructions and observes safe work practices. Provides input on safety issues. Serves as resource to support department members in performance of duties. Notifies appropriate staff members of problems requiring prompt intervention. Participates in continuing education and professional/ institutional advancement opportunities. Performs other duties as assigned. Salary Information: Commensurate with Education and Experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Criminal Background Check, Substance Abuse Testing This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Sharps, Standing, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Feeling, Grasping, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Reaching, Repetitive Motion, Sitting Occasional Physical Activity: Balancing, Climbing, Crawling, Crouching, Driving, Kneeling, Pulling, Pushing, Stooping Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/APRN-PA---IMSL-Endocrine-Clinic_R0089959-1": {"title": "APRN/PA - IMSL Endocrine Clinic", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-13\nPosted: Posted 22 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/30/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | IMSL MS APRN Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: This posting will fill with either an APRN or PA. The Advanced Practice Nurse/Physician Assistant works collaboratively with a physician and multidisciplinary health team to provide comprehensive care to outpatients. The APRN/PA is responsible for assessment, diagnosis, treatment, management, education, health promotion, and care coordination for patients and families with acute and chronic health needs. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: APRN: Master\u2019s Degree in Nursing \u2013 Family Medicine Three (3) years of nursing experience.\u00a0 Licensed Registered Nurse in Arkansas APRN License 1 year of APRN experience in a Family Medicine or Internal Medicine Clinic or Endocrine Clinic preferred PA: Master\u2019s Degree \u2013 Physician Assistant 1 year of PA experience in a Family Medicine or Internal Medicine Clinic or Endocrine clinic PA Preferred Qualifications: APRN: DNP 3 years of nursing experience 3 years of APRN experience in a Family Medicine or Internal Medicine Clinic, or Endocrine clinic PA: 3 years of PA experience in a Family Medicine or Internal Medicine Clinic, or Endocrine clinic Additional Information: Responsibilities: Extend the patient care and administrative services of the University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences physicians. \u00a0 Provide comprehensive health assessments, determine diagnoses, implement treatment plans, prescribe medical treatments, and manage health issues for patients in collaboration with the designated physician(s). \u00a0 Work autonomously, as well as, in collaboration with a variety of individuals to diagnose and manage patients' health care problems; and will serve as a health care resource, interdisciplinary consultant, and patient advocate. \u00a0 Coordinate the multidisciplinary care of patients, facilitating all necessary consults, and assuring that care is timely and appropriate. \u00a0 Interacts with and assists the public in a professional and friendly manner as needed. Demonstrates effective communication skills; communicates accurate and complete information; maintains strict confidentiality when necessary. Demonstrates positive working relationships with co-workers, management team, and ancillary departments; follows the Core Concepts of Patient and Family Centered Care and the Basic Code of Conduct Guidelines. Assist internal and external stakeholders as needed with exceptional customer service.\u00a0 Extend the patient care and administrative services of the University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences physicians. Other duties as assigned. Constant Physical Activity : Hear, Read, Concentrate, Think Analytically, Frequent Physical Activity : Stand Occasional Physical Activity : Bend, sit, crawl, crouch, kneel, stoop or reach overhead Lift/Carry Weight: 11 - 25 Lbs. or more Push/Pull Weight: 100 Lbs. or more Physical Environment : Inside medical Facility Noise Level: Moderate Visual Requirements: Color discrimination, Depth perception, Far visual acuity Near visual acuity Hazards : Biological, Dust, Fumes/Gases/Odors, Radiation, Sharp objects/tools Salary Information: \"Commensurate with Education and Experience\" Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Clinical-Interpreter_R0087533-1": {"title": "Clinical Interpreter", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-12\nPosted: Posted 23 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/12/2026 Type of Position: Clinical Staff - Medical Services Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | CORE PA Medicaid Enrollment Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Clinical Interpreter (Bilingual) will assist English and Spanish speaking patients with Medicaid applications. Major responsibility is processing Medicaid applications for our Spanish speaking patients who need financial assistance. Proficiency in verification of Medicaid application. Increases knowledge of Medicaid categories; DHS programs and UAMS internal programs. Beginning understanding of Medicaid policies and procedures. Other duties as assigned. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor\u2019s degree or High School diploma plus 4 years formal interpreting experience Able to follow oral and written instructions and communicate with others effectively. Strong computer/basic keyboard skills, telephone skills, and general knowledge of office machines including printers. Excellent customer relations skills. Preferred Qualifications: Two years of experience interpreting and translating, preferably in a medical setting, including one year medical, Medicaid, and clerical experience Experience in healthcare insurance and billing. Knowledge in advanced medical terminology and medical coding. Oral and written fluency in English and Spanish. Additional Information: Job Requirements: Specializes in assisting our Spanish speaking patients. \u00a0 Analyze patient\u2019s responsibility by understanding verification of\u00a0assets, family size, citizenship status and FPL. Keys Medicaid cases into DHS eligibility system.\u00a0 Retrieves eligibility information from different data bases. Submits weekly spreadsheets of\u00a0cases in need of additional review. Knowledge of complete Medicaid interview process. \u00a0 Performs other duties as assigned with a positive team attitude. Develops and maintains knowledge-base of Medicaid policies and procedures,\u00a0maintains current knowledge of all federal and state regulatory mandates and requirements\u00a0including but not limited to Medicare, EMTALA, and JCAHO; successfully completes annual\u00a0competency test and any additional competency testing and training required to validate\u00a0required skills. Determines eligibility for Spanish and English speaking\u00a0patients for Medicaid, EMA and financial assistance programs available. This position provides\u00a0assistance in obtaining coverage for patients who are underinsured and uninsured.\u00a0 \u00a0Performs other duties as assigned. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS Stand: Frequently Sit: Frequently Walk: Occasionally Bend, crawl, crouch, kneel, stoop or reach overhead: Frequently Lift and carry weight: 25 lbs Push and pull weight: 25 lbs Use hands to touch, handle or feel: Frequently Talk: Continuously Hear: Continuously Taste or smell: Occasionally Read, concentrate, think analytically: Continuously Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Criminal Background Check This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Sitting, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Crouching, Feeling, Grasping, Lifting, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Reaching, Repetitive Motion, Sitting, Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Climbing, Crawling, Feeling, Kneeling, Pulling, Pushing, Standing, Stooping Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/APRN-PA---Cancer-Service-Line---Clinic-and-Infusion-Areas_R0089849-1": {"title": "APRN/PA - Cancer Service Line - Clinic and Infusion Areas", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-12\nPosted: Posted 23 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 11/12/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Shift Vary (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | CASL MY AdvancedPracticeProviders I4 Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: This posting will cover multiple positions with various shifts and schedules. The APP will extend the patient care and administrative services for UAMS physicians in both inpatient and outpatient settings at the Cancer Institute Outpatient Clinic and Infusion areas. APP will be expected provide comprehensive health assessments, determine diagnoses, implement treatment plans, perform procedures, and prescribe medicines and treatments. The APP will also manage health issues for patients, independently or in collaboration with the designated physicians. The APP will work autonomously as well as in collaboration with a variety of individuals to diagnose and manage patient's health care problems; and will serve as a health care resource, interdisciplinary consultant, and patient advocate. The APP will also coordinate the multidisciplinary care of patients, facilitating all necessary consults, assuring that care is timely and appropriate. This posting interviews for multiple positions including, but not limited to: Infusion B - Transplant APP Myeloma Clinic APP Hematology Oncology Clinic APP Thoracic Oncology/Surgery Clinic APP Head and Neck Oncology APP Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications : APRN: Master\u2019s Degree in nursing\u00a0PLUS 2 years nursing experience, preferably in Acute Care APRN Licensed Registered Nurse in Arkansas and APRN/CPN License Current BLS certification or must successfully obtain certification within the first 30 days of employment. Must be able to operate all typical medical equipment essential to performing the job (i.e., scales, procedure equipment, needles, blood pressure equipment, and EKG machines).\u00a0 Must have normal communication sensory requirements. Ability to comply with CDC Universal Precautions when indicated.\u00a0 \u00a0 PA: Master's Degree as a Physician Assistant (PA). Licensed Registered Physician Assistant (PA) Current BLS certification or must successfully obtain certification within the first 30 days of employment. Must be able to operate all typical medical equipment essential to performing the job (i.e., scales, procedure equipment, needles, blood pressure equipment, and EKG machines).\u00a0 Must have normal communication sensory requirements. Ability to comply with CDC Universal Precautions when indicated.\u00a0 \u00a0 Preferred Qualifications : Prescriptive authority and DEA license must be obtained after hire for both APRN and PA roles. Additional Information: Responsibilities: Manage health issues for patients, independently or in collaboration with the designated physicians. Work autonomously as well as in collaboration with a variety of medical professional individuals. Extend the patient care and administrative services of the University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences physicians in both inpatient and outpatient settings. Provide comprehensive health assessments, determine diagnoses, implement treatment plans, perform procedures, and prescribe medicines and treatments. APRN provides daily care until last patient is seen for the day. Work autonomously as well as in collaboration with a variety of individuals to diagnose and manage patient's health care problems; and will serve as a health care resource, interdisciplinary consultant, and patient advocate. Coordinate the multidisciplinary care of patients, facilitating all necessary consults, assuring that care is timely and appropriate. Interacts with and assists the public in a professional and friendly manner as needed. Demonstrates effective communication skills; communicates accurate and complete information; maintains strict confidentiality when necessary. Demonstrates positive working relationships with co-workers, management team, and ancillary departments; follows the Core Concepts of Patient and Family Centered Care and the Basic Code of Conduct Guidelines. Assist internal and external stakeholders as needed with exceptional customer service. Other duties may be assigned. Physical Demands: Constant Physical Activity : Hear, Read, Concentrate, Think Analytically, Frequent Physical Activity : Stand Occasional Physical Activity : Bend, sit, crawl, crouch, kneel, stoop or reach overhead Lift/Carry Weight: 11 - 25 Lbs. or more Push/Pull Weight: 100 Lbs. or more Physical Environment : Inside medical Facility Noise Level: Moderate Visual Requirements: Color discrimination, Depth perception, Far visual acuity Near visual acuity Hazards : Biological, Dust, Fumes/Gases/Odors, Radiation, Sharp objects/tools Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/APRN-PA---Hospital-Medicine_R0089769-1": {"title": "APRN/PA - Hospital Medicine", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-11\nPosted: Posted 24 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 10/11/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Shift Vary (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | IMSL MS APRN Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: **This position will hire for either APRN or PA** As an integral part of the UAMS Hospitalist Care Team, the APRN works collaboratively with the attending physicians and residents to ensure continuity of care to inpatient patients. The APRN help plan, implement, and evaluate health care treatments. Daily rounds, a variety of procedures, monitoring patient progress, and providing patient and family education, are part of the wide scope of practice. ` Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: APRN: Master\u2019s Degree in Nursing \u2013 Acue Care Three (3) years of nursing experience.\u00a0 Licensed Registered Nurse in Arkansas APRN License 1 year of APRN experience in Acute Care National certification in Acute Care Nurse Practitioner, Adult Gero Acute Care Nurse Practitioner, and Family Nurse Practitioner if an APRN PA: Master\u2019s Degree \u2013 Physician Assistant 1 year of PA experience in Acute Care PA License Preferred Qualifications: APRN: DNP 3 years of APRN experience in a Acute Previous experience in infectious diseases, internal medicine, primary care, hospital medicine, or related specialty preferred. Experience managing chronic infectious diseases Experience working in an academic medical center environment. Interest in antimicrobial stewardship, quality improvement, or clinical education. Strong communication, organizational, and interdisciplinary collaboration skills. Previous experience in obesity medicine, endocrinology, primary care, family medicine, internal medicine, bariatrics, or lifestyle medicine. Experience managing chronic metabolic diseases and anti-obesity pharmacotherapy. PA: 3 years of PA experience in Acute Care Previous experience in infectious diseases, internal medicine, primary care, hospital medicine, or related specialty preferred. Experience managing chronic infectious diseases Experience working in an academic medical center environment. Interest in antimicrobial stewardship, quality improvement, or clinical education. Strong communication, organizational, and interdisciplinary collaboration skills. Previous experience in obesity medicine, endocrinology, primary care, family medicine, internal medicine, bariatrics, or lifestyle medicine. Experience managing chronic metabolic diseases and anti-obesity pharmacotherapy. Additional Information: Employees in this role must be fitted for, capable of donning and performing routine tasks in personal protective equipment to include N95 masks, Powered Air Purifying Respirators (PAPR) or Controlled Air Purifying Respirators (CAPR). Responsibilities: Maintains required audits for credentialing. Engages in appropriate continuing education programs, maintains mandatory competencies, medical center computer-based learning modules, and health monitoring services. Participates in institutional initiatives and encourages the participation of others.\u00a0 Collaborates in policy and program development, implementation, and evaluation using best practices in delivering quality service. Coordinates the multidisciplinary care of patients, facilitating all necessary consults, assuring that care is timely and appropriate.\u00a0 Actively engage in service line meetings and take an approach to health care that shapes policies, programs, facility design, and day-to-day interactions. Provides healthcare services to patients, which may include: comprehensive care during acute and chronic episodes of injury and illness, follow-up care during post-hospital clinic appointments, education and counseling of families, health promotion and prevention, and referral to other healthcare providers and community resources when appropriate. Works autonomously, as well as, in collaboration with a variety of disciplines to diagnose and manage health care problems; will serve as a health care resource, interdisciplinary consultant, and patient advocate. Communicates and shares complete and unbiased information, assuring their colleagues receive timely, complete, and accurate information in order to make informed decisions. May perform other duties as assigned. Constant Physical Activity : Hear, Read, Concentrate, Think Analytically Frequent Physical Activity : Stand Occasional Physical Activity : Bend, sit, crawl, crouch, kneel, stoop or reach overhead Lift/Carry Weight: 11 - 25 Lbs. or more Push/Pull Weight: 100 Lbs. or more Physical Environment : Inside medical Facility Noise Level: Moderate Visual Requirements: Color discrimination, Depth perception, Far visual acuity Near visual acuity Hazards : Biological, Dust, Fumes/Gases/Odors, Radiation, Sharp objects/tools Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Pharmacist-II---Inpatient-Pharmacy_R0089613-1": {"title": "Pharmacist II - Inpatient Pharmacy", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-10\nPosted: Posted 25 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/10/2026 Type of Position: Clinical Staff - Medical Ancillary Support Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Shift Vary (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | PTSL Inpat Pharm EveningShift IP C Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: A Pharmacist II operates independently to manage pharmacy dispensing functions, ensuring accurate medication therapy and safety. They oversee workflow, supervise technicians, and provide educational support to healthcare teams. Additionally, they lead process improvement initiatives, offer training to new staff, and may serve as a liaison between pharmacy services and specific practice areas. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in Pharmacy plus 3 years of experience working as a pharmacist in a retail or hospital setting, o r PGY-1 residency Certification as a licensed Pharmacist by the State of Arkansas or eligible for licensure by the State of Arkansas Preferred Qualifications: Graduate of an ACPE-accredited School of Pharmacy with a Pharm.D. Advanced degree \u2013 (MS, MBA, MHA, MPA, etc.) AND/OR Completion of a general or administrative ASHP-accredited residency Additional Information: Responsibilities: Reviews and interprets prescriber's orders and detects appropriateness of therapy Prepares and dispenses medications. Prepares sterile admixtures using proper aseptic technique. Prepares chemotherapy according to departmental policies and procedures. Answers questions from physicians and nurses. Serves as a primary or co-preceptor for College of Pharmacy rotational students. Provides formal, in-depth training of students and new staff. Serves as primary trainer for newly onboarded employees. Assists with development of educational materials and in-services for staff development. Directs, advises, and instructs staff in assigned area in all activities pertaining to job duties and functions. Assists leadership in all aspects of pharmacy operations in area of assigned responsibility. Serves as a liaison between the pharmacy service line and the assigned practice area. Works well as part of a team and with all shifts. Displays a positive attitude that contributes to the overall morale of the inpatient pharmacy team. Corrects, rather than ignores, problems involving any issues within the medication use process or normal operation of the pharmacy. Promotes a safe working environment by adhering to UAMS patient safety plan and ensuring compliance with policies. Adheres to pharmacy laws, regulations, and policies. Ensures equipment and facilities are used, calibrated, and maintained properly (Baxa, KitCheck, Pyxis). Completes assigned cleaning duties and documents appropriately. Works with leadership on quality improvement projects. Provides input on new initiatives. First to learn new processes to help train other staff. Other duties as assigned. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience. Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Criminal Background Check, Substance Abuse Testing This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Crawling, Sharps Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/North-Little-Rock/Sociology-Pool--Evergreen-_R0044509": {"title": "Adjunct Instructor - Sociology Pool", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-07\nPosted: Posted 28 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Less than Annual Appointment (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas Pulaski Technical College University of Arkansas - Pulaski Technical College at North Little Rock is an integral part of the Arkansas Technical and Community College System maintained by the State of Arkansas. The college is governed by the University of Arkansas System Board of Trustees and a seven-member Board of Visitors and derives its support largely from student tuition and fees and legislative appropriations. UA - Pulaski Tech, a comprehensive two-year college, offers associate degree and certificate programs for students who plan to transfer to four-year colleges and universities and/or for career preparation and advancement. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply link/button. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at (501) 812-2839. Department: Social Science Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Teach one or more classes as needed in Sociology. Classes include but are not limited to Intro to Sociology and Social Problems. Classes may be offered online, virtual (at anytime), or evenings as noted on the schedule. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications : 18 graduate hours in Sociology. Preferred Qualifications: PhD in Sociology. Additional Information: Salary Information: Commensurate with education Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Curriculum Vitae, License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants Recruitment Contact Information: Human Resources Humanresources@uaptc.edu 501-812-2839 All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: University of Arkansas - Pulaski Technical College is committed to providing a safe campus community. Title IX protects the college community from sexual harassment in a school's education programs and activities. This means that Title IX protects the college community in connection with all academic, educational, extracurricular, athletic, and other programs of the school, whether those programs take place in a school's facilities, in college transportation, at a class or training program sponsored by the school at another location, or elsewhere. \u00a0 We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Dental-Assistant-PRN----Oral-Health-Clinic_R0086093-1": {"title": "Dental Assistant PRN  - Oral Health Clinic", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-06\nPosted: Posted 29 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/06/2026 Type of Position: Clinical Staff - Medical Ancillary Support Job Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Shift Vary (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | PCPHSL Oral Health Clinical Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Dental Assistant will support dentists during procedures, prepare treatment rooms, sterilize instruments, and provide excellent patient care. The ideal candidate should be organized, have strong communication skills, and be committed to ensuring a comfortable and positive experience for every patient. This position will work in the operating room as well as the clinic. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: High school diploma/GED PLUS completion of a dental assisting training program AND a minimum of 1 year of experience as a dental assistant. Must be currently licensed/certified in the State of Arkansas as a registered dental assistant Candidates must meet the training and experience qualifications in order to be considered, and are advised to contact the training facility/source to verify accreditation status. Must be trained in four-handed dentistry; Must possess a thorough working knowledge of Current Dental Terminology (CDT) codes, OSHA regulations, and the Arkansas Dental Practice Act. Must possess a permit for the following expanded functions: 1) radiography, 2) coronal polishing, and 3) nitrous oxide administration. Additional Information: Responsibilities: Organize and assist dental hygienists in the delivery of dental procedures in the Oral Health Clinic Guide patients through dental processes before treatment, Educate patients in oral hygiene instruction and provide postoperative instructions Perform assessments that include obtaining and reviewing patient health histories Taking/recording blood pressure and other vital signs Perform appropriate dental charting and treatment documentation in the electronic record Expose and process dental radiographs of diagnostic quality Administer nitrous oxide/oxygen analgesia and monitor sedation cases Perform coronal polishing Perform in-office whitening Perform daily and routine maintenance of dental hygiene equipment as assigned Clean and sterilize dental instruments, supplies, and dental assist units, and maintain Organization and supply ofthe sterilization area Establish and maintain an organized, efficient, cost-effective inventory control system Continually monitoring supply levels and re-ordering by working with athe ssigned purchaser Maintain a stock of daily supplies in all hygiene clinic rooms Review daily schedules and resolve conflicts as necessary Perform a variety of clerical and administrative duties (answer telephones. Make appointments, and other duties as assigned Assist with front desk/business administration duties as assigned Perform duties as assigned. Salary Information: \"Commensurate with education and experience\" Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Other (see special instructions for details), Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Nitrous Certification required Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Criminal Background Check, Substance Abuse Testing This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sharps, Sitting, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Feeling, Reaching, Repetitive Motion Occasional Physical Activity: Grasping Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Supervisor--Access-Services---Ortho-and-HSC_R0089475-1": {"title": "Supervisor, Access Services - Ortho and HSC", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-05\nPosted: Posted 30 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/05/2026 Type of Position: Professional Staff - Fiscal Affairs Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | CORE PA HSC & Ortho Clinics Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: This Access Supervisor manages the day-to-day Patient Access outpatient operations of The Orthopedic North Little Rock and HSC locations Rodney Parham. This position is responsible for the team\u2019s performance meeting and/or exceeding the department standards as developed by the Access Manager and the CABC Director. This position reports directly to the Access Manager. This position will comply with all CABC, Patient Access, Integrated Clinical Enterprise, and UAMS policies and will ensure that direct and indirect reports comply as well. This position will serve as an advocate for enhanced patient access performance within the team. The position is responsible for ensuring the team provides the highest level of customer service and creates an atmosphere that motivates employees to work at optimal efficiency. Qualifications: Min imum Qualifications: Bachelor\u2019s degree in Business or related field plus three (3) years of registration and/or billing experience, or \u00a0High School diploma/GED plus seven (7) years of registration and/or billing experience, including three (3) years of experience in a healthcare environment. Must have excellent organizational and interpersonal skills in order to successfully interact with individuals of diverse backgrounds Well-developed decision-making skills Highly motivated and self-directed individual to establish plans of action Preferred Qualifications:\u00a0 Advanced knowledge of Epic system and third-party payer requirements. Additional Information: Responsibilities: Supervises department staff by monitoring activities and productivity daily and takes appropriate action to ensure staff consistently meets performance standards. Ensures the team meets expectations for work queue productivity, quality, and customer service. Ensures staff is educated and conducts themselves in the performance of all duties. Seeks out continuing education of regulatory changes and industry standards Ensures information is provided to staff timely and based on workload. Documents personnel issues and promotes a balanced a conducive work environment. Assists with and contributes to employee evaluations. Supervises the day-to-day operations of the assigned Access Coordinators, and Patient Representatives. Responsible for knowing and understanding clinic policies/procedures and is able to act on these policies/procedures. Schedules, reschedules, coordinates, and cancels appointments using the hospital systems. Collects co-pays, deductible, and/or payments for patient account and other cash handling responsibilities. Promotes teamwork and models the core concepts of Patient Family-Centered Care (PFCC). Conducts and assists with crucial conversations with staff when disagreements occur and when necessary progressive discipline. Ensures all department, CABC, ICE, and UAMS policies are followed. Knowledge of individual responsibility and ensures staff preparedness following Joint Commission standards and facility safety and emergency preparedness standards, Maintains current knowledge of the profession and all state and federal regulatory mandates. Establishes and maintains performance standards for productivity, quality, and compliance. Conducts team meetings and one-on-one meetings with direct reports. Participates in new employee onboarding, training, and development of staff. Works closely with management to develop, implement, and maintain formalized training. Other duties as assigned. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Criminal Background Check This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Sitting, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Crouching, Feeling, Grasping, Lifting, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Reaching, Sitting, Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Climbing, Crawling, Feeling, Kneeling, Pulling, Pushing, Standing, Stooping Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/APRN-PA---IMSL-Renal-Clinic_R0089491-1": {"title": "APRN/PA - IMSL Renal Clinic", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-05\nPosted: Posted 30 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 10/05/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | IMSL MS APRN Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: This posting will fill with either an APRN or PA. The Advanced Practice Nurse/Physician Assistant works collaboratively with a physician and multidisciplinary health team to provide comprehensive care to outpatients. The APRN/PA is responsible for assessment, diagnosis, treatment, management, education, health promotion, and care coordination for patients and families with acute and chronic health needs. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: APRN: Master\u2019s Degree in Nursing \u2013 Family Medicine Three (3) years of nursing experience.\u00a0 Licensed Registered Nurse in Arkansas APRN License 1 year of APRN experience in a Family Medicine or Internal Medicine Clinic or Nephrology preferred PA: Master\u2019s Degree \u2013 Physician Assistant 1 year of PA experience in a Family Medicine or Internal Medicine Clinic or Nephrology clinic PA Preferred Qualifications: APRN: DNP 3 years of nursing experience 3 years of APRN experience in a Family Medicine or Internal Medicine Clinic, or Nephrology clinic PA: 3 years of PA experience in a Family Medicine or Internal Medicine Clinic, or Nephrology clinic Additional Information: Responsibilities: Extend the patient care and administrative services of the University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences physicians. \u00a0 Provide comprehensive health assessments, determine diagnoses, implement treatment plans, prescribe medical treatments, and manage health issues for patients in collaboration with the designated physician(s). \u00a0 Work autonomously, as well as, in collaboration with a variety of individuals to diagnose and manage patients' health care problems; and will serve as a health care resource, interdisciplinary consultant, and patient advocate. \u00a0 Coordinate the multidisciplinary care of patients, facilitating all necessary consults, and assuring that care is timely and appropriate. \u00a0 Interacts with and assists the public in a professional and friendly manner as needed. Demonstrates effective communication skills; communicates accurate and complete information; maintains strict confidentiality when necessary. Demonstrates positive working relationships with co-workers, management team, and ancillary departments; follows the Core Concepts of Patient and Family Centered Care and the Basic Code of Conduct Guidelines. Assist internal and external stakeholders as needed with exceptional customer service.\u00a0 Extend the patient care and administrative services of the University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences physicians. Other duties as assigned. Constant Physical Activity : Hear, Read, Concentrate, Think Analytically, Frequent Physical Activity : Stand Occasional Physical Activity : Bend, sit, crawl, crouch, kneel, stoop or reach overhead Lift/Carry Weight: 11 - 25 Lbs. or more Push/Pull Weight: 100 Lbs. or more Physical Environment : Inside medical Facility Noise Level: Moderate Visual Requirements: Color discrimination, Depth perception, Far visual acuity Near visual acuity Hazards : Biological, Dust, Fumes/Gases/Odors, Radiation, Sharp objects/tools Salary Information: \"Commensurate with Education and Experience\" Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/APRN-PA---Peds-Cardiology---CVICU_R0089408-1": {"title": "APRN/PA - Peds Cardiology - CVICU", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-04\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 10/04/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: COM | Peds Cardiology APP's Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The APRN/PA is a skilled healthcare provider who has completed an educational program that provides specialized certification and is regulated by either the Arkansas State Board of Nursing or the Arkansas State Medical Board. An APRN/PA manifests a high level of expertise in assessing, diagnosing, and treating actual and potential health problems of pediatric patients and their families. An APRN/PA possesses an advanced knowledge level, skill, and competence in the provision of care to specific patient and family populations and serves across the care continuum as a clinical resource for patients, families, staff, and the community. Qualifications: APRN: Graduate from an accredited nursing program with at least a Master\u2019s in Nursing. National Certification as an Advanced Practice Registered Nurse. May have a certification as a Pediatric Nurse practitioner in either acute or primary care. PA: Graduate from an accredited physician assistant program defined by the Arkansas State Medical Board. Current Arkansas Physician Assistant license. \u00a0 Preferred Qualifications : Basic Life Support (BLS). Pediatric Advanced Life Support (PALS). \u00a0 Responsibilities: Provide direct clinical services for patients according to established protocols and utilizing evidence-based clinical practice standards in collaboration with a physician. Obtain patient health histories, complete physical examinations, and interpret hemodynamic data. Document pertinent normal and abnormal findings. Order and interpret appropriate diagnostic and laboratory tests. Formulate and implement a treatment plan for the management of acute and chronic\u00a0 illnesses in collaboration with the physician. Document in medical records appropriately.\u00a0 Provide family-centered care to meet the child\u2019s health care needs. Utilize current research and evidence-based decision-making in all clinical practice. Participate in staff education, and educate other APRN/PA students, residents, and/or fellows. Provide leadership and professional interaction within your team or to team members. Coordinate with families the care and progress of their child in person, by telephone, or by email as\u00a0 appropriate. Communicate with others with mutual respect and professional demeanor. Adhere to all standard policies and procedures. Participate in QI or research projects as deemed necessary by your department. Perform other duties as assigned. Additional Information: Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/APRN-PA---Outpatient-Medical-Weight-Management-Clinic_R0089352-1": {"title": "APRN/PA - Outpatient Medical Weight Management Clinic", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-03\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 08/03/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Shift Vary (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | IMSL MS APRN Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: **This position will hire for either APRN or PA** The APRN/PA for the Outpatient Medical Weight Management Clinic provides comprehensive, evidence-based care for patients seeking medical management of obesity and related metabolic conditions within an academic medical center environment. The APP collaborates with physicians, dietitians, behavioral health professionals, exercise specialists, pharmacists, and interdisciplinary teams to develop individualized treatment plans focused on sustainable weight management and improvement of overall health outcomes. This position supports the missions of patient care, education, research, and clinical excellence while promoting compassionate, patient-centered obesity care. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: APRN: Master\u2019s Degree in Nursing \u2013 Family Medicine or Adult Gero Primary Care Three (3) years of nursing experience.\u00a0 Licensed Registered Nurse in Arkansas APRN License 1 year of APRN experience in a Family Medicine or Internal Medicine Clinic National certification in Acute Care Nurse Practitioner, Adult Gero Acute Care Nurse Practitioner, and Family Nurse Practitioner if an APRN PA: Master\u2019s Degree \u2013 Physician Assistant 1 year of PA experience in a Family Medicine or Adult Gero Primary Care PA License Preferred Qualifications: APRN: DNP 3 years of nursing experience 3 years of APRN experience in a Family Medicine or Adult Gero Primary Care Previous experience in infectious diseases, internal medicine, primary care, hospital medicine, or related specialty preferred. Experience managing chronic infectious diseases Experience working in an academic medical center environment. Interest in antimicrobial stewardship, quality improvement, or clinical education. Strong communication, organizational, and interdisciplinary collaboration skills. Previous experience in obesity medicine, endocrinology, primary care, family medicine, internal medicine, bariatrics, or lifestyle medicine. Experience managing chronic metabolic diseases and anti-obesity pharmacotherapy. PA: 3 years of PA experience in Family Medicine or Adult Gero Primary Care Previous experience in infectious diseases, internal medicine, primary care, hospital medicine, or related specialty preferred. Experience managing chronic infectious diseases Experience working in an academic medical center environment. Interest in antimicrobial stewardship, quality improvement, or clinical education. Strong communication, organizational, and interdisciplinary collaboration skills. Previous experience in obesity medicine, endocrinology, primary care, family medicine, internal medicine, bariatrics, or lifestyle medicine. Experience managing chronic metabolic diseases and anti-obesity pharmacotherapy. Additional Information: Responsibilities: Provide comprehensive outpatient evaluation and management for patients with obesity, who are overweight, and/or have associated metabolic conditions. Perform detailed patient assessments including medical history, physical examination, obesity-related risk assessment, and evaluation of contributing factors to weight gain. Develop individualized treatment plans incorporating: o\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Lifestyle modification o\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Nutrition counseling reinforcement o\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Physical activity recommendations o\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Behavioral modification strategies o\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Pharmacologic weight management therapies Prescribe and manage FDA-approved anti-obesity medications as appropriate. Monitor treatment effectiveness, medication tolerance, and patient progress toward individualized goals. Evaluate and manage obesity-related comorbidities including: o\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Type 2 diabetes o\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Hypertension o\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Hyperlipidemia o\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Obstructive sleep apnea o\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Fatty liver disease o\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Metabolic syndrome o\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Polycystic ovarian syndrome (PCOS) Order and interpret diagnostic testing and laboratory studies relevant to obesity and metabolic health. Provide longitudinal follow-up care and ongoing patient education regarding nutrition, exercise, medication adherence, and behavior change. Collaborate with bariatric surgery teams for patient referral, preoperative optimization, and postoperative follow-up when appropriate. Coordinate care with primary care providers and specialty services. Document patient encounters accurately and efficiently within the electronic medical record. Participate in telehealth services as appropriate. Participate in the academic mission of the institution through collaboration with medical students, residents, fellows, APP students, and allied health learners. Assist with education related to obesity medicine, lifestyle interventions, pharmacologic therapies, and chronic disease prevention. Participate in departmental conferences, continuing education activities, and multidisciplinary meetings. May assist with quality improvement initiatives, clinical research, presentations, publications, or program development. Participate in quality improvement and patient outcome initiatives related to obesity and metabolic health. Maintain current knowledge of evidence-based obesity medicine guidelines and emerging therapies. Promote patient-centered, culturally competent, and stigma-free obesity care. Participate in departmental meetings, committees, and institutional initiatives as assigned. \u00a0Maintain professional licensure, certifications, and credentialing requirements. May perform other duties as assigned. Constant Physical Activity : Hear, Read, Concentrate, Think Analytically Frequent Physical Activity : Stand Occasional Physical Activity : Bend, sit, crawl, crouch, kneel, stoop or reach overhead Lift/Carry Weight: 11 - 25 Lbs. or more Push/Pull Weight: 100 Lbs. or more Physical Environment : Inside medical Facility Noise Level: Moderate Visual Requirements: Color discrimination, Depth perception, Far visual acuity Near visual acuity Hazards : Biological, Dust, Fumes/Gases/Odors, Radiation, Sharp objects/tools Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Supervisor----Access-Services-IMSL-Primary-Care_R0089247-1": {"title": "Supervisor -  Access Services IMSL/Primary Care", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-30\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 10/30/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | CORE PA Float Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: **This posting will fill positions at various clinics, including Cardiovascular, Internal Medicine, and Primary Care. Final clinic assignment will be determined by the department manager based on operational needs and position availability.** Supervises the operations of assigned workflows including patient check-in/check-out, scheduling, registration, patient portals, on-line/e-requests, EPIC work queues, and physician referrals. Assists with the testing, managing, and/or monitoring of workflows within UAMS electronic systems to ensure maximum productivity. This position assumes responsibility of the manager during the absence of the manager, educates staff on scheduling requirements, physician templates, payer requirements, and government rules and regulations required for compliance, registration, and customer service. They will also perform regular audits to ensure productivity, quality, and compliance. Provides report of findings and works with administrative team to develop corrective action plans. Displays exceptional leadership, supervisory, communication, and interpersonal skills. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: High School diploma, GED, or formal educational equivalent Seven (7) years of experience in registration, billing, or scheduling in a healthcare environment \u00a0 Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor's Degree in Business, Healthcare, or a related field Three (3) years of experience in registration, billing, or scheduling in a healthcare environment Leadership or supervisory experience Additional Information: Responsibilities: Supervises department staff by monitoring activities and productivity daily and takes appropriate action to ensure staff consistently meet performance standards Responsible for ensuring the team meets expectations for work queue productivity, quality, and customer service\u00a0 Seeks out continuing education on regulatory changes and industry standards; ensures information is provided to staff in a timely manner and based on workload\u00a0 Documents personnel issues and promotes a balanced and conducive work environment Ensures all department, CABC, ICE, and UAMS policies are followed Establishes and maintains performance standards for productivity, quality, and compliance Implements process improvement and reports results\u00a0 Ensures staff is educated and conducts themselves in the performance of all duties\u00a0 Knowledge of individual responsibility and ensures staff preparedness following Joint Commission standards and facility safety and emergency preparedness standards Maintains current knowledge of the profession and all state and federal regulatory mandates. Maintains required job skills competencies and completes skills assessments annually\u00a0 Completes and maintains documentation of continuing education hours annually Supervises the day-to-day operations of the assigned Access Coordinators and Patient Representatives. Responsible for knowing and understanding clinic policies/procedures and is able to act on these policies/procedures Schedules, reschedules, coordinates, and cancels appointments using the hospital systems Works closely with management to develop, implement, and maintain formalized training plans\u00a0 Responsible for annual training facilitation of staff development and providing employee coaching. Responsible for employee evaluations. Works with CABC Support for timekeeping and other HR items. Promotes teamwork and models the core concepts of Patient Family-Centered Care (PFCC). Conducts and assists with crucial conversations with staff when disagreements occur and when necessary progressive discipline. Conducts team meetings and one-on-one meetings with direct reports. Participates in new employee onboarding, training, and development of staff Provides proper transfer of information as necessary using communication skills and tools. Ensures staff is collecting all front-end payments during the check-in process. Performs other duties as needed. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAMS/Epic-ASAP----Clinical-Applicication-Analyst----Intermediate_R0086766-1": {"title": "Epic ASAP  - Clinical Applicication Analyst  - Intermediate", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-29\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 07/29/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: IT | EMR Systems Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: We are seeking a Clinical Application Systems Analyst - Intermediate to support IT EMR Services with a primary focus on Epic ASAP and related clinical applications. This role is responsible for application support, system maintenance, troubleshooting, upgrades, and workflow optimization while ensuring system integrity and reliability. The ideal candidate will collaborate with operational and IT teams to resolve complex issues, implement system enhancements, and support continuous improvement initiatives that advance clinical and business operations. This position offers the opportunity to work in a dynamic healthcare technology environment, contribute to innovative solutions that support patient care, and play a key role in advancing operational excellence across UAMS. Join our team and help enhance the technology and workflows that empower clinicians, improve patient experiences, and support our mission of delivering exceptional healthcare. Qualifications: High School diploma/GED plus seven (7) years of experience supporting and maintaining computer systems , or Associate's degree in Computer Sciences, Nursing, or related healthcare field, plus five (5) years of experience supporting and maintaining computer systems or Bachelor's degree in Computer Sciences, Nursing, or related healthcare field, plus three (3) years of experience supporting and maintaining computer systems , or Post Graduate degree in Computer Sciences, Nursing, or related healthcare field, plus one (1) year of experience supporting and maintaining computer systems required. Epic ASAP certification required. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities: Proficiency in Epic ASAP and related applications. Knowledge of drug formulary, dispensing and ordering methods & products, processes and procedures used in a pharmacy is required to develop, configure, test, document, and implement a Pharmacy system. The ability to lead meetings, resolve conflicts, maintain issue lists, and manage a project plan. The ability to probe for information about the underlying needs of the organization and user community, which directly influences how the system will be utilized. Strong communication and follow-up skills. Key Responsibilities: System Build and Configuration: Configure, maintain, test, and optimize Epic ASAP and related clinical applications to support operational needs, system integrity, and regulatory compliance. Workflow Analysis and Collaboration: Partner with end users, operational stakeholders, vendors, and IT teams to analyze business processes, define system requirements, and implement effective workflow solutions. Problem Solving: Troubleshoot complex application issues, perform root cause analysis, and implement timely resolutions in accordance with established service level agreements. Application Management: Monitor application performance, integrations, and security to ensure system reliability, data integrity, and compliance with organizational and regulatory standards. Project Management: Lead or support application implementations, upgrades, enhancements, testing activities, and documentation while ensuring project objectives and timelines are met. Professional Performance: Provide mentorship and technical guidance to team members, maintain required certifications, and contribute to continuous process improvement initiatives. May perform additional tasks as assigned to support departmental goals. Additional Information: Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Pharmacist-I---Inpatient-Pharmacy_R0088926-1": {"title": "Pharmacist I - Inpatient Pharmacy", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-24\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 10/24/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | PTSL Inpat Pharm EveningShift IP C Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The job posting will fill multiple positions. A Pharmacist I works under minimal supervision to assess, prepare, dispense and assist in coordinating all day-to-day dispensing functions of the pharmacy in a timely and accurate manner. The pharmacist will use their knowledge, skills and clinical judgment through reviewing orders to ensure safe and effective medication therapy. They will evaluate appropriateness of dose, route and formulation, allergies, medication interactions, monitoring, etc. The pharmacist will have frequent communication with other healthcare professionals as a drug information resource and provide educational information to ensure great patient care. They will report adverse drug events and medication safety events. They will document interventions in the medical record. The pharmacist will work as a team member to efficiently and accurately perform day-to-day work along with any additional tasks or projects to help achieve departmental goals. A Pharmacist I will assist with technician and student supervision/direction as it relates to day-to-day dispensing functions, tasks and job duties to provide timely and efficient patient services. They will assist with prioritizing day-to-day workflow based on immediate need and a rapidly changing workload. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in Pharmacy plus 1 year of experience working as a pharmacist (or pharmacy intern) \u00a0in a retail or hospital setting. Certification as a licensed Registered Pharmacist by the State of Arkansas or eligibility for licensure by the State of Arkansas. Preferred Qualifications: Graduate of an ACPE-accredited School of Pharmacy with a Pharm.D. 2 years of applicable pharmacy experience Additional Information: Responsibilities: Reviews and interprets prescriber's orders and detects appropriateness of therapy; prepares and dispenses medications. Prepares sterile admixtures using proper aseptic technique. Prepares chemotherapy according to departmental policies and procedures. Answers client questions regarding prescription renewal, dosage, and side effects. Serves as a primary or co-preceptor for rotational students; provides formal, in-depth training of students and new staff. Assists with development of educational materials and in-services for staff development. Directs, advises, and instructs staff in assigned area in all activities pertaining to job duties and functions. Assists leadership in all aspects of pharmacy operations in area of assigned responsibility. Serves as a liaison between the pharmacy service line and the assigned practice area. Promotes a safe working environment by adhering to UAMS patient safety plan. Ensures equipment and facilities are used, calibrated, and maintained properly. Other duties as assigned. Physical Demands: Constant : Standing, Talking, Walking, Hearing, Sitting, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding Frequent : Crawling, Crouching, Stooping Occasional : n/a Physical Requirements : Medium Work, Exerting up to 50 lbs of force occasionally and/or up to 30 lbs of force frequently, and/or up to 10 lbs of farce constantly ro move objects. Visual Acuity : Employee is required to have acuity to determine the accuracy, neatness, and thoroughness of work assigned.\u00a0 Working Conditions : The employee is subject to hazards. Includes a variety of physical conditions, such as proximity to moving mechanical parts or vehicles, electrical current, working in high places, exposure to chemicals, biological, radiological or hazardous materials. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/RN----Adult-ICU--Med-Surg--Oncology---PRN_R0085357-1": {"title": "RN -  Adult ICU, Med/Surg, Oncology - PRN", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-23\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 10/23/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | NRSL PRN Pool IP C Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Schedule: PRN, As Needed Basis Shifts Vary,\u00a0Equivalent of 24 hours on a regularly scheduled basis (monthly). The 24 hours is typically 2-12 hours or 3-8 hour shifts, but the shifts could change based on the need of the unit/clinic. This posting will be used to fill multiple positions The Registered Nurse will require the ability to coordinate care for patients, triage patients, and work collaboratively with clinic\u00a0 providers, fellows, and staff.\u00a0 Requires the ability to effectively work with patient referral sources, facilitate appointments, coordinate transitions of care, and provide patient education on complex conditions. The RN I will work with the individual patient, their families, and providers of care to develop and implement individual health plans within the ICU's, Medical/Surgical and\u00a0 Oncology units.\u00a0 PRN staff are not eligible to receive benefits, but may contribute to pre-tax supplemental Retirement. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Graduate of an accredited Nursing Program with Associates Degree, Nursing Diploma, Bachelors in Nursing, or Master's in Nursing.\u00a0 Valid RN License. Nursing Experience One (1) year patient care experience similar to or related to the position applied for Excellent communication skills. Basic computer skills. Strong work ethics and accountability. Specialty areas, i.e.., Intensive Care, F4 Surgical Trauma are required to pass a pre-screening testing\u00a0with a minimum score of 80% Chemotherapy certification may be required to work Oncology units Work one major holiday (Thanksgiving, Christmas, Christmas Eve or New Year ) and one additional holiday, in addition to two weekend shifts. PRN staff are only allowed to work 1000 hours in a 12 month rolling year, which begins at orientation and includes any education hours. Preferred Qualifications:\u00a0 Two (2) or more years of RN experience \u00a0 Transfers Into PRN: Must Follow Transfer Requirements Prior To Last Working Day As Posted On Website\u00a0 Http://nurses.uams.edu/ . Select 'Employment Info' Drop Down Tab Prior To Submitting An Application. Additional Information: Responsibilities: Provides direct patient care\u00a0 to assigned patients within the\u00a0 Adult\u00a0 ICU's, Medical/Surgical, and Oncology units.\u00a0 Provides triage, assessment, planning, implementation, and evaluation of nursing care and patient education either by telephone or within the UAMS Clinic. Delivers nursing care according to standards as defined by UAMS, American Nurses Association (ANA), AR State Board of Nursing, (ASBN), and those set forth by nursing specialty organizations. Helps develop patient\u2019s Plan of Care (POC) per clinic standards utilizing assessment data. Evaluates the progress of patients\u2019 toward attainment of desired outcomes. Administers medication following clinic standards and Nurse Practice Act. Verifies and evaluates care delivered to ensure care is consistent with standards and regulatory requirements. Coordinates care and/or follow-up for patients who receive care in inpatient and outpatient facilities. Coordinates patients\u2019 prescription refill requests and patient education coordination in collaboration with physician staff. May perform other duties as assigned. Employees in this role must be fitted for, capable of donning and performing routine tasks in personal protective equipment to include N95 masks, Powered Air Purifying Respirators (PAPR) or Controlled Air Purifying Respirators (CAPR). Constant Physical Activity : Hear, Read, Concentrate, Think Analytically, Frequent Physical Activity : Stand, Walk, Talk, Use hands to touch, handle or feel, Occasional Physical Activity : Sit, Bend, crawl, crouch, kneel, stoop, reach overhead, Taste or Smell, Lift/Carry Weight: 100 Lbs. or more Push/Pull Weight: 100 Lbs. or more Physical Environment : Inside medical Facility Noise Level: Moderate Visual Requirements: Near Visual Acuity, Far Visual Acuity, Color Discrimination, Depth Perception, Peripheral Vision Hazards : Biological, Chemical, Electrical, Radiation, Sharp Objects/Tools, Dust #UAMSNurses Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAMS/Epic-Cadence---Clinical-Application-Analyst----Intermediate_R0086763-1": {"title": "Epic Cadence - Clinical Application Analyst", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-23\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/30/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: IT | EMR Systems Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: We are seeking a skilled Epic Cadence Clinical Application Analyst - Intermediate to support IT Patient Systems with a focus on Epic Cadence, Prelude, Referrals, and Authorizations. This role requires acting independently under general supervision, demonstrating expertise in system functionality, integration, and maintenance. The ideal candidate will ensure system integrity, support process improvement, and collaborate with cross-functional teams to meet operational and business needs. This position provides the chance to engage in a fast-paced healthcare IT setting, enhance processes, and support vital patient systems while furthering your professional development. Join our team today and make a meaningful difference! Qualifications: High School diploma/GED plus seven (7) years of IT experience or clinical/operational experience, or any combination of the two, or Associate degree in a Clinical, Healthcare, Business, IT, or related field plus five (5) years of IT experience or clinical/operational experience, or any combination of the two, or Bachelor\u2019s degree in a Clinical, Healthcare, Business, IT, or related field plus three (3) years of IT experience or clinical/operational experience, or any combination of the two, or Post Graduate degree in a Clinical, Healthcare, Business, IT, or related field, plus one (1) year of IT experience or clinical/operational experience, or any combination of the two required. Cadence certification required. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities: Proficiency in Epic Cadence and related applications. Strong analytical, troubleshooting, and communication skills. Ability to document and implement system changes while guiding operational users. Experience in project management and cross-team collaboration. Must have an aptitude for technical tasks and project management. Working knowledge of Microsoft Office Suite. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Key Responsibilities System Build and Configuration: Interpret, analyze, and design system data to maintain and enhance application functionality while ensuring compliance with regulatory requirements. Problem Solving: Proactively resolve system issues, identify root causes, and implement solutions within IT Service Level Agreements (SLAs). Professional Performance: Mentor junior analysts, maintain certifications, and contribute to quality improvement initiatives. Integrated Application Management: Monitor system integration, participate in cross-functional testing, and ensure application security aligns with organizational and regulatory standards. Project Management: Lead or support IT projects, including system upgrades, testing, and implementation, while adhering to project management methodologies. May perform additional tasks as assigned to support departmental goals. Additional Information: Required to rotate 24/7 on-call duties and respond immediately to trouble calls outside of general work hours. Work occasionally may require an excess of eight hours per day, plus weekend work. Workload and deadline pressure will regularly subject the incumbent to moderate to high job-related stress. Occasional overnight travel may be required for training, evaluating vendor systems at other customer sites, or industry conferences. This position will primarily work remotely from home, but must be able to travel to campus and/or University Towers to attend meetings and support application analyst staff to meet our Service Level Agreements. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/RN---Freeway-Endoscopy_R0088686-1": {"title": "RN - Freeway Endoscopy", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-22\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 10/20/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | PeriopSvc Endoscopy Lab Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: ** This posting will fill multiple positions** The Endoscopy Registered Nurse (RN) will provide specialized care for patients undergoing diagnostic and therapeutic endoscopic procedures in a high-acuity academic medical center. This professional nursing role will require the ability to coordinate care for patients, triage patients, and work collaboratively with clinic providers, fellows, and staff. Requires the ability to effectively work with patient referral sources, facilitate appointments, coordinate transitions of care, and provide patient education on complex conditions. The RN will work with the individual patient, their families, and providers of care to develop and implement individual health plans. Provides direct patient care in the Endoscopy lab, serving in the roles in the procedural space, Preop, and PACU Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Graduate of an accredited Nursing Program with an Associate's Degree, Nursing Diploma, Bachelor's in Nursing, or Master's in Nursing.\u00a0 Valid RN License. Minimum of one (1) year Registered Nursing experience. Preferred Qualifications: Two (2) or more years of nursing experience. Current BLS Excellent communication skills. Basic computer skills. Strong work ethic and accountability. Additional Information: Employees in this role must be fitted for, capable of donning and performing routine tasks in personal protective equipment to include N95 masks, Powered Air Purifying Respirators (PAPR) or Controlled Air Purifying Respirators (CAPR). Responsibilities: Collects and documents assessment data from patients and/or others per UAMS standard.\u00a0 Develops patient's Plan of Care (POC) per department/unit standards utilizing assessment data.\u00a0 Evaluates the progress of patients toward attainment of desired outcomes. Administers medication following department/unit standards and Nurse Practice Act.\u00a0 Verifies and evaluates care delivered to ensure it is consistent with patient and family centered care principles, practice standards and regulatory requirements. Supports the integration of current evidence into nursing practices.\u00a0 Promotes an environment conducive to positive educational experience for all students and staff.\u00a0 Provides effective patient/family education/discharge planning. Effectively collaborates and communicates with nursing staff at all levels, interdisciplinary teams, executive leaders, and other stakeholders.\u00a0 Communicates care appropriately through documentation in the medical record. Reports variances in care/ systems/ processes through the appropriate means.\u00a0 Participates in recruitment/retention of staff.\u00a0 Facilitates development and implementation of nursing practice standards that are evidence-based and in compliance with ANA standards. May perform other duties as assigned. Constant Physical Activity : Hear, Read, Concentrate, Think Analytically, Frequent Physical Activity : Stand Occasional Physical Activity : Bend, sit, crawl, crouch, kneel, stoop or reach overhead Lift/Carry Weight: 11 - 25 Lbs. or more Push/Pull Weight: 100 Lbs. or more Physical Environment : Inside medical Facility Noise Level: Moderate Visual Requirements: Color discrimination, Depth perception, Far visual acuity Near visual acuity Hazards : Biological, Dust, Fumes/Gases/Odors, Radiation, Sharp objects/tools Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Endoscopy-Technician---Freeway-Endoscopy_R0088691-1": {"title": "Endoscopy Technician - Freeway Endoscopy", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-21\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 10/20/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | PeriopSvc Endoscopy Lab Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: **This posting will fill multiple positions** Under the general supervision of a Registered Nurse (RN and Medical Doctors), the Endoscopy Technician assists physicians or other providers with procedures performed in the gastroenterology endoscopy setting. Patient populations range from adolescents to older adults and an understanding of the age-specific needs of these patients is required. Outpatients who present with a wide range of illnesses and complaints are cared for in this endoscopy setting. Some duties may be performed independently with intermittent supervision by the Registered Nurse. The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: High School Diploma/GED Must have\u00a0excellent communication skills, ability to follow oral instructions, basic computer skills, strong work ethics, and accountability. Must be able to lift 100 lbs. to waist height. Preferred Qualifications: Successful completion of Endoscopy Technician course within 3 months of hire into this role. Previous\u00a0Endoscopic Technician or Patient Care Technician experience. Patient care experience in acute care setting. Additional Information: Employees in this role must be fitted for, capable of donning and performing routine tasks in personal protective equipment to include N95 masks, Powered Air Purifying Respirators (PAPR) or Controlled Air Purifying Respirators (CAPR). Responsibilities: Participates in educating the patient about the procedure being performed including preparation, rationale, and expectations.\u00a0 Demonstrates understanding of the plan of care. Demonstrates knowledge of aseptic techniques and infection prevention procedures.\u00a0 Assists RN with transport of sedated patients to the recovery area. Communicates accurate patient observations, interventions, and outcomes of care to the Registered Nurse.\u00a0 Informs the RN of the equipment and accessories used during procedures including quantity, size, and equipment settings to be documented in the medical record.\u00a0 Participates in specimen collection and handling. Correctly labels specimens according to hospital policy.\u00a0 May assist the Registered Nurse with patient monitoring (vs. observation) during and following procedures, when appropriate.\u00a0 Provides emergency care to patients when necessary, using basic life support protocols (CPR certified) until Registered Nurse and/or physician staff arrives.\u00a0 Participates in supporting the patient during the procedure. May offer coaching and relaxation techniques.\u00a0 Demonstrates proper handling and use of various types and sizes of video endoscopes, including colonoscopes, upper endoscopes, flexible sigmoidoscopes, duodenoscopies, ultrasound endoscopes, bronchoscopes, and enteroscopies\u00a0 Inspects all equipment and accessories for defects prior to use to ensure highest level of infection prevention.\u00a0 Understands theory and safety when using cautery modalities including monopolar, bipolar, and argon plasma coagulation and their various probes.\u00a0 Performs procedures in OR setting or at patient bedside including ICU, ED, or Radiology.\u00a0 Assists with pulmonary procedures such as bronchoscopy and chest tube placements.\u00a0 Assists with therapeutic interventions such as balloon dilations, polypectomy, sphincterotomy, stent placement, and gastrostomy tube placement. Demonstrates recognition of patient\u2019s emotional and physical needs and the ability to provide a supportive environment.\u00a0 Understands that the stress of illness may alter patient behavior and the ability to follow through on the plan of health car e.\u00a0 Assists with the application of monitoring equipment and the setting of parameters and alarms (NIBP, ECG, and pulse oximetry).\u00a0 Initiates start-up of endoscopy network and photo documentation procedures.\u00a0 Properly pre-cleans/disinfects endoscopic equipment and accessories prior to sterile processing.\u00a0 Stocks procedure rooms. Initiates the reorder of supplies as needed.\u00a0 Performs telephone reminder calls for procedures and provides limited procedure information under RN supervision.\u00a0 May perform other duties as assigned Constant Physical Activity : Hear, Read, Concentrate, Think Analytically, Frequent Physical Activity : Stand Occasional Physical Activity : Bend, sit, crawl, crouch, kneel, stoop or reach overhead Lift/Carry Weight:\u00a0 11 - 25 Lbs. or more Push/Pull Weight:\u00a0 100 Lbs. or more Physical Environment : Inside medical Facility Noise Level:\u00a0 Moderate Visual Requirements:\u00a0 Color discrimination, Depth perception, Far visual acuity Near visual acuity Hazards : Biological, Dust, Fumes/Gases/Odors, Radiation, Sharp objects/tools Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Registered-Dietitian---Hospitality_R0088425": {"title": "Registered Dietitian - Hospitality", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-21\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 12/31/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: OPS | NUTRI Inpatient Nutrition Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Registered Dietitian is responsible for providing nutritional care individually and as part of an interdisciplinary outpatient care team. The Registered Dietitian is responsible for educating patients, family, professional staff and students/interns. The Registered Dietitian works under the general direction and is responsible to the Nutrition Department Outpatient Team Lead position. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications - Registered Dietitian\u00a0 Bachelor of Science Degree in Nutrition/Dietetics Registered Dietitian (RD) Licensed Dietitian (LD) in the State of Arkansas Completion of a dietetic internship Strong oral and written communication skills Basic computer skills Interviewing candidates with all levels of experience - Nutrition, LD & RD Preferred Qualifications: Clinical experience Registered Dietitian and Licensed by the State of Arkansas preferred Registered Dietitian II RD, LD 1-year clinical experience Registered Dietitian III Master\u2019s degree required or Specialty Certification required Precepts dietetic interns in the UAMS internship program 2+ years\u2019 experience Registered Dietitian IV 4 + years\u2019 experience Masters required Specialty Certification required \u200b \u00a0 Additional Information: Responsibilities: \u2022 Assessing the nutritional needs of the patient and making recommendations to meet those needs. \u2022 Documentation in the electronic medical record. \u2022 Education of family, students and other professional staff. \u2022 Teaching, discussing with medical staff and other caregivers the patient needs. \u2022 Clerical and office duties. \u2022 Presentations outside the hospital as required. \u2022 Other duties as assigned. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Fort-Smith/RN-Charge-Nurse--Ft-Smith--AR-_R0088152-1": {"title": "RN-Charge Nurse (Ft. Smith, AR)", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-16\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/05/2026 Type of Position: Clinical Staff - Nursing Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: REP | PCPHSL CS West Fort Smith Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: We are seeking a dedicated and experienced Registered Nurse (RN) to join our team as a Charge Nurse at our Fort Smith Family Medical Center. As the Charge Nurse, you will be responsible for ensuring the delivery of the highest quality Patient and Family-Centered Care within the clinic. You will oversee the nursing and clinical team, manage the patient flow processes, and promote wellness, improved outcomes, and self-care among a defined patient population. Additionally, you will play a crucial role in providing support, education, and assistance to patients who have chronic conditions, helping them prevent and maintain their health. As the Charge Nurse the individual will work with the CSM in the daily operations and supervision of the clinic and staff. Join us at UAMS and enjoy a fulfilling career where your skills help transform lives. Grow professionally in a team that values collaboration, innovation, and compassionate care. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Graduate of an accredited Nursing Program with Associates Degree, Nursing Diploma, Bachelors in Nursing, or Master's in Nursing Valid RN License Minimum of one (1) year Registered Nursing experience.Will consider RN with two (2) years of LPN clinical experience. Preferred Qualifications: Charge RN or Leadership experience. Clinic or Ambulatory Setting experience. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: The ability to work independently and maintain high-quality care, and the application of policies will be required. Good communication skills (written and oral). Excellent customer service skills. Problem-solving skills. Leadership and collaborative skills. Strong patient advocacy and patient education skills. Strong organizational skills and computer knowledge. Professional and courteous telephone etiquette. General knowledge of office machines, including printers, fax machines, and scanners. Understanding basic medical terminology is necessary. Additional Information: Key Responsibilities : Assist with scheduling, payroll, staffing issues, communication between staff and providers, clinical/nursing staff education and training, policy compliance and maintaining quality measures. Triage, assessment, planning, implementation, and evaluation of nursing care and patient education either by telephone or within the UAMS Clinic.\u00a0 Delivers nursing care according to standards as defined by UAMS, American Nurses Association (ANA), AR State Board of Nursing (ASBN), and those set forth by nursing specialty organizations. Coordinates care and/or follow-up for patients who receive care in inpatient and outpatient facilities.\u00a0 Implements patient care using an approach that is interdisciplinary and Patient and Family-Centered Care. Effectively collaborates and communicates with nursing staff at all levels, interdisciplinary teams, executive leaders, and other stakeholders. May perform other duties as assigned to support the mission of UAMS. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience. Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), Resume Optional Documents: List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Criminal Background Check, Motor Vehicle Reports Check, Substance Abuse Testing This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Feeling, Grasping, Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Pulling, Reaching, Repetitive Motion, Sharps, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Balancing, Crouching, Kneeling, Pushing, Stooping Occasional Physical Activity: Crawling, Crouching Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Access-Coordinator-II---Admissions-HOD-Emergency-Department_R0088371-1": {"title": "Access Coordinator II \u2013 Admissions/HOD/Emergency Department", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-14\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Shift Vary (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | CORE PA Float Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: **This posting will fill positions at various areas, including Admissions, One Day Surgery, HOD or Emergency Department. Final clinic assignment will be determined by the department manager based on operational needs and position availability** ***shifts vary including days, evening, nights, and weekends*** Access Coordinator II works under supervision and provides comprehensive support for patient care activities. This position may meet, greet, and assist the public, answer telephones and/or may coordinate appointments, referrals, consults, tests and/or procedures, check-in and registers patients, check-out patients, and collects payments and issues receipts, verifies insurance coverage and responds appropriately to the requirements of third- party payers. Assists with coordinating hospital admissions and surgery scheduling. This position must be able to perform all duties of the Access Coordinator I level and perform other duties to support the patient care activities as needed. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: High school diploma/GED\u00a0 Two (2) years of customer service or healthcare experience Basic proficiency with computers (preferably\u00a0MS Office) Excellent telephone etiquette skills General knowledge of office machines including printers and scanners. Preferred Qualifications: Call center experience Experience in registration, billing, or scheduling in a healthcare environment Knowledge of basic medical terminology Additional Information: Job Requirements: Schedules, reschedules, coordinates and cancels appointments using the hospital system; conducts pre-registration as needed Inputs and/or updates accurate patient information Creates new patient charts and accesses systems for orders as appropriate Conducts insurance verification and benefit explanation by running eligibility on patients, requests outside records, and gathers outside medical records from referrals as needed Meets, greets, and assists the public, answers telephones in a professional and friendly manner Deals with conflicts in a positive and professional manner using careful listening and negotiation skills to resolve disagreements Consistently utilizes communication devices and keeps accurate records as required Demonstrates effective service recovery skills Attends required hours of training and/or in-services Participates in annual educational needs and assessment Maintains required job skill competencies and completes skill assessment annually \u00a0Completes and maintains documentation of continuing education hours annually Performs other duties as assigned PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS Stand: Frequently Sit: Continuously Walk: Occasionally Bend, crawl, crouch, kneel, stoop or reach overhead: Frequently Lift and carry weight: 25 lbs Push and pull weight: 25 lbs Use hands to touch, handle or feel: Frequently Talk: Continuously Hear: Continuously Taste or smell: Occasionally Read, concentrate, think analytically: Continuously Physical Environment : Inside Medical Facility Environment Salary Information: $17.23/hr. Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Appointment-Business-Center-Scheduler-I-II_R0087571": {"title": "Appointment Business Center Scheduler I/II", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-14\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/14/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | CORE PA Float Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Appointment Business Center Scheduler (Access Coordinator) answers telephones and coordinates appointments in a call center environment. The Appointment Business Center Scheduler plays a crucial role in our organization by supporting patient care activities. If you have strong communication skills and a passion for providing excellent customer service, we invite you to apply for this exciting opportunity to join our team. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: High school diploma/GED Basic proficiency with computers (preferably MS Office) Excellent telephone etiquette skills General knowledge of office machines including printers and scanners Level I : One (1) year of customer service experience Level II : Two (2) years of customer service experience Preferred Qualifications: Call center experience Experience in registration, billing, or scheduling in a healthcare environment Knowledge of basic medical terminology Additional Information: Job Responsibilities: Schedules, reschedules, coordinates, and cancels appointments Inputs and/or updates accurate patient information Communications accurate and complete information Must maintain strict confidentiality Performs other duties as assigned This position is in a call center and remote work is not an option. Salary Information: Level I: $16.00 - hr Level II: $16.88 - hr Required Documents to Apply: List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/APRN-PA---Infectious-Disease_R0088272-1": {"title": "APRN/PA - Infectious Disease", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-13\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/13/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Shift Vary (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | IMSL MS APRN Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: **This position will hire for either APRN or PA** The Advanced Practice Nurse/Physician Assistant works collaboratively with a physician and multidisciplinary health team to provide comprehensive care to outpatients. The APRN/PA is responsible for assessment, diagnosis, treatment, management, education, health promotion, and care coordination for patients and families with acute and chronic health needs. Provide comprehensive outpatient infectious disease care under established collaborative practice agreements and institutional policies.\u00a0Perform detailed patient assessments including history, physical examination, diagnostic interpretation, and formulation of treatment plans. \u00a0Evaluate and manage patients with: o\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0HIV/AIDS o\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Hepatitis and other chronic viral infections o\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Osteomyelitis and chronic bone/joint infections o\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Recurrent or multidrug-resistant infections o\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Complex wound and soft tissue infections o\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Fungal and parasitic infections o\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Fever of unknown origin o\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Immunocompromised host infections o\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Post-hospitalization infectious disease follow-up o\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Patients requiring long-term antimicrobial therapy Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: APRN: Master\u2019s Degree in Nursing \u2013 Family Medicine Three (3) years of nursing experience.\u00a0 Licensed Registered Nurse in Arkansas APRN License 1 year of APRN experience in a Family Medicine or Internal Medicine Clinic National certification in Acute Care Nurse Practitioner, Adult Gero Acute Care Nurse Practitioner, and Family Nurse Practitioner if an APRN PA: Master\u2019s Degree \u2013 Physician Assistant 1 year of PA experience in a Family Medicine or Internal Medicine Clinic PA License Preferred Qualifications: APRN: DNP 3 years of nursing experience 3 years of APRN experience in a Family Medicine or Internal Medicine Clinic Previous experience in infectious diseases, internal medicine, primary care, hospital medicine, or related specialty preferred. Experience managing chronic infectious diseases Experience working in an academic medical center environment. Interest in antimicrobial stewardship, quality improvement, or clinical education. Strong communication, organizational, and interdisciplinary collaboration skills. PA: 3 years of PA experience in a Family Medicine or Internal Medicine Clinic Previous experience in infectious diseases, internal medicine, primary care, hospital medicine, or related specialty preferred. Experience managing chronic infectious diseases Experience working in an academic medical center environment. Interest in antimicrobial stewardship, quality improvement, or clinical education. Strong communication, organizational, and interdisciplinary collaboration skills. Additional Information: Responsibilities: Initiate, adjust, and monitor antimicrobial therapies, including oral and intravenous antibiotic regimens. Manage and monitor patients enrolled in Outpatient Parenteral Antimicrobial Therapy (OPAT) programs. Review laboratory, microbiology, pathology, and radiologic data to guide clinical management. Coordinate care with primary care providers, specialists, infusion centers, home health agencies, pharmacies, and case management teams. Provide patient and family education regarding disease processes, medications, infection prevention, and treatment adherence. Document patient encounters accurately and efficiently within the electronic medical record. Participate in telehealth services as appropriate. Academic & Educational Responsibilities Participate in the academic mission of the institution through collaboration with medical students, residents, fellows, APP students, and nursing staff. Assist with education related to infectious diseases, antimicrobial stewardship, HIV care, infection prevention, and evidence-based practice. Participate in departmental conferences, continuing education activities, and multidisciplinary meetings. May assist with clinical research initiatives, quality improvement projects, presentations, publications, or protocol development. May perform other duties as assigned. Constant Physical Activity : Hear, Read, Concentrate, Think Analytically, Frequent Physical Activity : Stand Occasional Physical Activity : Bend, sit, crawl, crouch, kneel, stoop or reach overhead Lift/Carry Weight: 11 - 25 Lbs. or more Push/Pull Weight: 100 Lbs. or more Physical Environment : Inside medical Facility Noise Level: Moderate Visual Requirements: Color discrimination, Depth perception, Far visual acuity Near visual acuity Hazards : Biological, Dust, Fumes/Gases/Odors, Radiation, Sharp objects/tools Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/RN-Neonatal-Intensive-Care-Unit--NICU-_R0085497-2": {"title": "RN Neonatal Intensive Care Unit (NICU)", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-07\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/07/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | WISL Neonatal ICU IP C Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Schedule: Full Time, 12 HR Shifts - Multiple Shifts Available, Shifts will vary This position used to fill multiple positions. The Registered Nurse is responsible for providing direct patient care and the provision of other patient services in a clinical setting. This position is governed by state and federal laws, and agency policy. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Graduate of an accredited Nursing Program with Associates Degree, Nursing Diploma, Bachelors in Nursing, or Master's in Nursing.\u00a0 Valid RN License. One (1) year Registered Nursing experience. Excellent communication skills. Basic computer skills. Strong work ethics and accountability. Preferred Qualifications: 2 or more years nursing experience with current BLS\u00a0 Previous experience in NICU Additional Information: Employees in this role must be fitted for, capable of donning and performing routine tasks in personal protective equipment to include N95 masks, Powered Air Purifying Respirators (PAPR) or Controlled Air Purifying Respirators (CAPR). Responsibilities: Collects and documents assessment data Develops a Plan of Care (POC) per standard Implements POC including medical order and interdisciplinary approach Evaluates the progress of patient toward attainment of desired outcomes Provides effective patient/family education/discharge planning Administers medication per standard including drug information to patients/families Acts as a resource/supports others; Delivers patient care using the principles of the defined nursing modality Delegates care based on UAMS standards, legal and regulatory requirements, specific job description and individual level of education and training Contributes to a positive work environment that is conducive to clinical education while serving as a resource for student nurses and staff. Other duties as assigned\u00a0 PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS Stand: Frequently Sit: Occasionally Walk: Frequently Bend, crawl, crouch, kneel, stoop or reach overhead: Occasionally Lift and carry weight: 100+ lbs Push and pull weight :100+ lbs Use hands to touch, handle or feel: Frequently Talk: Frequently Hear: Continuously Taste or smell: Occasionally Read, concentrate, think analytically: Continuously Physical Environment : Inside Medical Facility Environment Noise Level : Moderate Visual Requirements: Color discrimination, Depth perception, Far visual acuity, Near visual acuity Hazards: Biological, Chemical, Dust, Electrical, Fumes/Gases/Odors, Radiation, Sharp objects/tools Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/APRN-PA---Shoulder-APP_R0088047-1": {"title": "APRN/PA - Shoulder APP", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-07\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 10/07/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | MUSL APP Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Advanced Practice Nurse/Physician Assistant rotates with attending physicians and rotates through all the orthopedic subspecialties. They will assist the surgeon with clinic, organize visits, and perform clinic procedures; assist in the operating room; answer pages; and round on post-operative patients on a daily and PRN basis. The APRN/PA will be responsible for managing postoperative outpatient care, answering telephone inquiries, and filling prescriptions. APRN/PA must have a high level of expertise to perform assessments/diagnosis/treatment of actual/potential patients problems. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: APRN: Graduate of an accredited Nursing Program with a Master's in Nursing Valid Licenses as a Registered Nurse and APRN by the State of Arkansas PA: Graduate of an accredited Physician Assistant program Valid license as a PA by the State of Arkansas\u200b PLUS: Must be able to operate all typical nursing equipment essential to performing the job (i.e., scales, procedure equipment, needles, blood pressure equipment, and EKG machines). Must have normal communication and sensory requirements. Ability to comply with CDC Universal Precautions when indicated. Preferred Qualifications: Experience as PA or Acute Care APRN Prescriptive authority and a DEA license must be obtained after hire. Additional Information: Responsibilities: Extend the patient care and administrative services of the University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences physicians. Work autonomously, as well as, in collaboration with a variety of individuals to diagnose and manage patients' health care problems; and will serve as a health care resource, interdisciplinary consultant, and patient advocate. Coordinate the multidisciplinary care of patients, facilitating all necessary consults, assuring that care is timely and appropriate. Other duties may be assigned to this position. Physical Demands: Frequently: Seeing, Hearing Constantly: Standing, Walking Occasionally: Bending Lift weight: 100lbs Lifting to the waist, chest, and above the head Salary Information: Commensurate with Education and Experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/North-Little-Rock/Adjunct-Instructor---Political-Science_R0042302": {"title": "Adjunct Instructor - Political Science (Pool)", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-06\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Less than Annual Appointment (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas Pulaski Technical College University of Arkansas - Pulaski Technical College at North Little Rock is an integral part of the Arkansas Technical and Community College System maintained by the State of Arkansas. The college is governed by the University of Arkansas System Board of Trustees and a seven-member Board of Visitors and derives its support largely from student tuition and fees and legislative appropriations. UA - Pulaski Tech, a comprehensive two-year college, offers associate degree and certificate programs for students who plan to transfer to four-year colleges and universities and/or for career preparation and advancement. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply link/button. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at (501) 812-2839. Department: Social Science Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Teach one or more classes as needed in Political Science. Classes include but are not limited to Introduction to Political Science. Classes may be offered online, virtual (at anytime), or evenings as noted on the schedule. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications : 18 Graduate hours in Political Science or Law. Preferred Qualifications : PhD or JD in Political Science or Law. Additional Information: Salary Information: Commensurate with education Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Curriculum Vitae, Resume, Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants Recruitment Contact Information: Human Resources Humanresources@uaptc.edu 501-812-2839 All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: University of Arkansas - Pulaski Technical College is committed to providing a safe campus community. Title IX protects the college community from sexual harassment in a school's education programs and activities. This means that Title IX protects the college community in connection with all academic, educational, extracurricular, athletic, and other programs of the school, whether those programs take place in a school's facilities, in college transportation, at a class or training program sponsored by the school at another location, or elsewhere. \u00a0 We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Instrument-Technician-I_R0088001": {"title": "Instrument Technician I", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-06\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 10/06/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Shift Vary (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: Yes Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | PeriopSvc Instrument Processing Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: This position will fill multiple positions. The Instrument Tech will be responsible for decontamination, assembling and inspecting, packaging, testing and sterilizing instruments and/or sets. Maintain records of loads and items being removed from department for processing, transports loads to and from SSD and prepare proper storage for equipment. Performs routine testing including biological test for steam autoclaves, Sterrad and System 1E. Assist Operating Room (OR) staff with needed supplies and equipment. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: High School Diploma/GED. \u200b Preferred Qualifications: Certified Instrument Tech. Work experience as an Instrument Tech. Experience fulfilling orders/requests (packing, assembling & stocking items). Additional Information: \u200bResponsibilities: Decontaminate (dis-assemble, clean by hand and/or machine) medical instruments/materials. Assemble and package,\u00a0 inspect and test instruments, re-assemble sets, place sets in proper containers and/or wrapping and load/transport loaded carts with prepared sets. Maintain record of loads and items being removed from department for processing. Transport loads to and from CSS and prepare proper storage of instruments and equipment. Use and test sterilizing equipment; perform dart and biological tests for autoclaves; perform diagnostic and biological tests for Steris sterilizer. Record and accurately interpret results of tests; assist OR staff; help locate needed supplies and equipment. Communicate professionally even when under pressure/fulfilling demanding and/or stressful requests. Position revolves around serving the Operating Room's (OR\u2019s) sterile instrument and equipment needs. Must understand the URGENCY of the OR staff\u2019s requests. Answer directly to the Sterile Processing Supervisor. Other related duties as assigned. Constant Physical Activity : Hear, Read, Concentrate, Think Analytically, Frequent Physical Activity : Stand Occasional Physical Activity : Bend, sit, crawl, crouch, kneel, stoop or reach overhead Lift/Carry Weight: \u00a0 11 - 25 Lbs. or more Push/Pull Weight: \u00a0 100 Lbs. or more Physical Environment : Inside medical Facility Noise Level: \u00a0 Moderate Visual Requirements: \u00a0 Color discrimination, Depth perception, Far visual acuity Near visual acuity Hazards : Biological, Dust, Fumes/Gases/Odors, Radiation, Sharp objects/tools Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience. Required Documents to Apply: List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/APRN-PA---Orthopedic-Residency_R0088000-2": {"title": "APRN/PA - Orthopedic Residency", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-06\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 10/06/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | MUSL APP Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Advanced Practice Nurse/Physician Assistant rotates with attending physicians in the OR clinic and rotates through all the orthopedic subspecialties. They will assist the surgeon with clinic, organize visits, and perform clinic procedures; assist in the operating room; answer pages; and round on post-operative patients on a daily and PRN basis. The APRN/PA will be responsible for managing postoperative outpatient care, answering telephone inquiries, and filling prescriptions. APRN/PA must have a high level of expertise to perform assessments/diagnosis/treatment of actual/potential problems of patients. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: APRN: Graduate of an accredited Nursing Program with a Master's in Nursing Valid Licenses as a Registered Nurse and APRN by the State of Arkansas PA: Graduate of an accredited Physician Assistant program Valid license as a PA by the State of Arkansas\u200b PLUS: Must be able to operate all typical nursing equipment essential to performing the job (i.e., scales, procedure equipment, needles, blood pressure equipment, and EKG machines). Must have normal communication and sensory requirements. Ability to comply with CDC Universal Precautions when indicated. Preferred Qualifications: Experience in a surgical setting Prescriptive authority and a DEA license must be obtained after hire. Additional Information: Responsibilities: Extend the patient care and administrative services of the University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences physicians. Work autonomously, as well as, in collaboration with a variety of individuals to diagnose and manage patients' health care problems; and will serve as a health care resource, interdisciplinary consultant, and patient advocate. Coordinate the multidisciplinary care of patients, facilitating all necessary consults, assuring that care is timely and appropriate. Other duties may be assigned to this position. Physical Demands: Frequently: Seeing, Hearing Constantly: Standing, Walking Occasionally: Bending Lift weight: 100lbs Lifting to the waist, chest, and above the head Salary Information: Commensurate with Education and Experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/RN---In-House-Agency_R0086011-1": {"title": "RN - In-House Agency", "description": "Start date: 2026-06-24\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 08/24/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Shift Vary (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | NRSL | In-House Agency Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: This posting will be used to fill multiple positions. Temporary Part-Time PRN (as needed) / Shifts vary The In-House Agency RN Program offers PRN employment for 13-week intervals. Participants are required to work 36 hours/week for 13 weeks and will be paid a competitive hourly rate plus weekend differentials. To qualify, applicants must have a valid RN license issued by the State of Arkansas and 12 months experience in an acute care hospital. Experience in the past 12 months must include 6 months in a direct patient care role in an acute care hospital. Applicants cannot be currently employed by UAMS, and previous UAMS employees must have terminated more than 180 days prior. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Graduate of an accredited Nursing Program with an Associate Degree, Nursing Diploma, Bachelor\u2019s in Nursing, or Master's in Nursing Valid RN License Nursing Experience: minimum of 12 months of experience as an RN in an acute care hospital Experience in the last 12 months may include up to 6 months in a management position, but must include at least 6 months in a direct patient care role in an acute care hospital Excellent communication skills Basic computer skills Strong work ethics and accountability Specialty areas, i.e.., Intensive Care, F4 Surgical Trauma are required to pass a pre-screening testing\u00a0with a minimum score of 80% Chemotherapy certification may be required to work Oncology units Work one major holiday and one additional holiday if applicable, in addition to every other weekend throughout the duration of the 13-week RN Internal Contract agreement period. Preferred Qualifications:\u00a0 2 or more years of RN experience Employees in this role must be fitted for, capable of donning and performing routine tasks in personal protective equipment to include N95 masks, Powered Air Purifying Respirators (PAPR) or Controlled Air Purifying Respirators (CAPR). Additional Information: Responsibilities: The Registered Nurse (RN) will provide direct patient care as an RN. This professional nursing role will require the ability to coordinate care for patients, triage patients, and work collaboratively with clinic providers, fellows, and staff. Requires the ability to effectively work with patient referral sources, facilitate appointments, coordinate transitions of care, and provide patient education on complex conditions. The RN will work with the individual patient, their families, and providers of care to develop and implement individual health plans. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS: Stand: Frequently Sit: Occasionally Walk: Frequently Bend, crawl, crouch, kneel, stoop or reach overhead: Occasionally Lift and carry weight: 100+ lbs Push and pull weight :100+ lbs Use hands to touch, handle or feel: Frequently Talk: Frequently Hear: Continuously Taste or smell: Occasionally Read, concentrate, think analytically: Continuously Physical Environment : Inside Medical Facility Environment Noise Level : Moderate Visual Requirements: Color discrimination, Depth perception, Far visual acuity, Near visual acuity Hazards: Biological, Chemical, Dust, Electrical, Fumes/Gases/Odors, Radiation, Sharp objects/tools #UAMSNurses Salary Information: Competitive Hourly Rate Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/APRN-PA---Pediatrics_R0082371-2": {"title": "Pediatric Emergency Medicine - APRN/PA", "description": "Start date: 2026-06-23\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/23/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: COM | Peds Emergency Medicine APP's Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: **This position will fill multiple vacancies** The APRN/PA is a skilled healthcare provider who has completed an educational program that provides specialized certification and is regulated by either the Arkansas State Board of Nursing or the Arkansas State Medical Board. An APRN/PA manifests a high level of expertise in assessing, diagnosing, and treating actual and potential health problems of pediatric patients and their families. An APRN/PA possesses an advanced knowledge level, skill, and competence in the provision of care to specific patient and family populations and serves across the care continuum as a clinical resource for patients, families, staff, and the community. Qualifications: APRN: Graduate from an accredited nursing program with at least a Master\u2019s in Nursing. National Certification as an Advanced Practice Registered Nurse. May have a certification as a Pediatric Nurse practitioner in either acute or primary care. PA: Graduate from an accredited physician assistant program defined by the Arkansas State Medical Board. Current Arkansas Physician Assistant license. \u00a0 Preferred Qualifications : Basic Life Support (BLS). Pediatric Advanced Life Support (PALS). Responsibilities: Provide direct clinical services for patients according to established protocols and utilizing evidence-based clinical practice standards in collaboration with a physician. Obtain patient health histories, complete physical examinations, and interpret hemodynamic data. Document pertinent normal and abnormal findings. Order and interpret appropriate diagnostic and laboratory tests. Formulate and implement a treatment plan for the management of acute and chronic\u00a0 illnesses in collaboration with the physician. Document in medical records appropriately.\u00a0 Provide family-centered care to meet the child\u2019s health care needs. Utilize current research and evidence-based decision-making in all clinical practice. Participate in staff education, and educate other APRN/PA students, residents, and/or fellows. Provide leadership and professional interaction within your team or to team members. Coordinate with families the care and progress of their child in person, by telephone, or by email as\u00a0 appropriate. Communicate with others with mutual respect and professional demeanor. Adhere to all standard policies and procedures. Participate in QI or research projects as deemed necessary by your department. Perform other duties as assigned. Additional Information: Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Assistant-Professor--Associate-Professor--or-Professor_R0082870-1": {"title": "Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Professor", "description": "Start date: 2026-06-05\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 08/06/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: COP | Pharmacy Practice Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Professor faculty position is a 12-month, tenure-track or non-tenure track, full-time faculty position in the Department of Pharmacy Practice in the University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) College of Pharmacy. The faculty member serves as a key member of the faculty to advance the teaching, scholarly, and service missions of the Department of Pharmacy Practice. The faculty member will participate in a wide variety of didactic and/or experiential teaching of pharmacy students, pharmacy residents, and/or graduate students. The faculty member is expected to disseminate scholarly work through peer-reviewed publications and professional/scientific meeting presentations. Research-focused faculty are expected to develop an independent research program in an area complementary to others in the College. Service contributions to the Department, College, University, and profession are also expected. Specific expectations for performance in each area of responsibility will be set according to the faculty member\u2019s distribution of effort in each area. Academic rank will be commensurate with education and experience. Qualifications: Ph.D in an area relevant to the mission of the department or a PharmD plus completion of 1 year residency training. For those with clinical responsibilities, at least 3 years of clinical practice experience in a relevant practice setting. For those holding a PharmD degree - Must hold an active Arkansas pharmacist license or be eligible for Arkansas Pharmacist licensure. Must have excellent verbal and written communication, interpersonal, and patient care skills. Preferred Qualifications: For those with clinical responsibilities: completion of a PGY2 residency in a relevant area. Previous faculty experience, post-doctoral fellowship in an area of expertise relevant to the mission of the department. For those with clinical responsibilities: Board certification in a relevant area (eg, BCPS, BCACP, etc). Responsibilities: Provides functions in teaching, research/scholarly activities, academic service, academic citizenship, and professional development. Additional Information: Salary Information: Salary is commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/RN-New-Grad-Resident-Program-Winter-2027_R0082948-1": {"title": "RN New Grad Resident Program Winter 2027", "description": "Start date: 2026-03-04\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 12/01/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual orientation, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | NRSL RN Residency Program IP C Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: December Graduates Start dates: January 2027 Schedule: Full-time, 7A-7P or 7P-7A or alternate 12-hour shifts, must work three shifts during the week plus rotate weekends. Available shifts based on unit needs and to be discussed with the unit hiring manager. The UAMS Transition to Practice- RN New Graduate Residency Program is designed with a specialized and focused platform to include lectures, simulation, case studies, online modules, etc., and clinical experience with designated preceptors. Support and training continue throughout the first year through continued education and mentorship. All RN New Graduates must actively participate in the Transition to Practice Program. New Graduate RN Residents must complete 1 year of experience and meet the Transition to Practice program requirements to be considered RN I. Qualifications: Required: Only accepting RN New Graduates with less than 12 months of RN experience at this time Must obtain temporary or permanent RN license by start/hire date (Offers will be contingent upon meeting this requirement by start/hire date) Basic computer skills Strong work ethic Preferred: Previous Patient Care experience New Graduate RN Residents must complete 1 year of experience and meet the program requirements to be considered RN I.\u00a0 Please refer to New Graduate RN Resident Info Webpage \u00a0for program details and FAQs. Additional Information: Selected applicants will receive an email requesting a minimum of three (3) references to be submitted.\u00a0 The reference checking process is a requirement for all applicants and must be completed within 72 hours of request to be considered. Responsibilities: The New Graduate RN Resident will provide direct patient care in one of the following specialty areas: Acute Care Critical Care Division NICU Labor & Delivery Perinatal Oncology Surgical Services Emergency Department Psychiatric Research Institute Cardiac Catheterization Lab Orthopaedic and Spine Hospital (TOSH) - Surgical Services Physical Requirements: Stand: Frequently Sit: Occasionally Walk: Frequently Bend, crawl, crouch, kneel, stoop or reach overhead: Occasionally Lift and carry weight: 100+ lbs. Push and pull weight: 100+ lbs. Use hands to touch, handle or feel: Frequently Talk: Frequently Hear: Continuously Taste or smell: Occasionally Read, concentrate, and think analytically: Continuously Physical Environment: Inside Medical Facility Environment Noise Level: Moderate Visual Requirements: Color discrimination, Depth perception, Far visual acuity, Near visual acuity Hazards: Biological, Chemical, Dust, Electrical, Fumes/Gases/Odors, Radiation, Sharp objects/tools Potential for violence/physical altercations Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Curriculum Vitae, Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Social-Work---Oncology_R0089497-1": {"title": "Social Work - Oncology", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/30/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | CASL CA Social Work Team B Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: \"This posting can fill a LMSW or LCSW position\" LMSW - The Licensed Master Social Worker (LMSW) provides clinical psychosocial services and case management for the WPRCI patients and families in our outpatient clinical areas. Services include but are not limited to: initial psychosocial assessment with new patients; ongoing psychosocial assessment as needed during treatment process; development of treatment plans/interventions; coordination with inpatient Care Management/medical staff; advocacy for patient/family with healthcare providers and community resources; patient/family education, information and referrals; assistance with financial/social needs related to housing, transportation, food, medications, and access to treatment/clinical trials; interdisciplinary team coordination/communication; and assistance with mental health issues and emotional adjustment to illness, including emotional support, psychotherapy (individual, group, family, couples, children), crisis intervention, and grief counseling. Participates in program development under the supervision of LCSW staff. Participates in supervision process with LCSW toward obtaining LCSW. LCSW - Serves within multidisciplinary team to provide clinical psychosocial services for patients in the UAMS Cancer Service Line to include: initial psychosocial assessment with new patients; ongoing psychosocial assessment as needed during treatment process and beyond; development of treatment plans/interventions that are documented in the EMR; response to emotional components of illness, including adjustment to illness and grief counseling, psychotherapy (individual, couples, family, children), and crisis intervention. Provides direct counseling and education to patients/families regarding financial/social support to insure completion of treatment and access to clinical trials. Develops programs that offer specialty care to support them through the continuum of cancer treatment. Supervises graduate interns through their field experience and final requirements for graduation. Serves as liaison with other departments/agencies, both internal and external. Models positive collaboration/interaction with colleagues, management team, and other UAMS departments. Periodic travel and evening work may be required Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: LMSW: Masters Degree - Social Work PLUS Professional License / Certificate - LMSW; Excellent oral and written communication skills and decision-making skills. Ability to think independently, multi-task, make quick, decisive choices, all while fostering team interactions. Excellent customer service skills. Must have thorough knowledge of Microsoft Office Suite. LCSW: Masters Degree in Social Work; PLUS Zero (0) to Two (2) years working in administration, nonprofit organization, or health care environment with supervisory experience Current LCSW license from Arkansas Social Work Licensing Board. Excellent oral and written communication skills and decision-making skills. Ability to think independently, multi-task, make quick, decisive choices, all while fostering team interactions. Excellent customer service skills. Must have thorough knowledge of Microsoft Office Suite. Additional Information: Responsibilities: Serves as a member of the multidisciplinary health care team by preparing individualized treatment plans based on diagnostic assessments. Liaisons with other departments and agencies to ensure proper allocation of resources to administer treatment plans. Administers direct clinical services including individual therapy, family therapy, and group therapy. Completes mandatory reporting in compliance with legal and professional standards and guidelines. Supports and provides therapy and intervention for families dealing with disease, grief, crisis, and acute or chronic mental health issues. Organizes patient support groups and serves as an advocate for patients within the community. Interviews clients and performs psychosocial assessments to determine the needs of the patient or family. Documents interview information and assessment results into medical records and initiates intervention plan. Offers coping strategies and assists patients and families in securing needed resources for financial and other services to ensure continuity of care. Participates with quality improvement, student supervision, obtaining resources, and departmental projects. Maintains professional skills and credentialing as required by professional licensing organization. Represents the department as needed on campus committees. May perform other duties. Physical Requirements: Stand: Constantly Sit: Constantly Walk: Constantly Bend, crawl, crouch, kneel, stoop or reach overhead: Occasionally Lift and carry weight: 20+ lbs. Push and pull weight: 20+ lbs. Use hands to touch, handle or feel: Frequently Talk: Constantly Hear: Continuously Taste or smell: Never Read, concentrate, and think analytically: Continuously Physical Environment: Inside Medical Facility Environment Noise Level: Moderate Visual Requirements: Color discrimination, Depth perception, Far visual acuity, Near visual acuity Hazards: None Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAMS/Executive-Assistant-I_R0091109-1": {"title": "Executive Assistant I", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/19/2026 Type of Position: Professional Staff - Operations Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: COM | Emergency Medicine Administration Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Executive Assistant provides senior-level administrative support to the Chair of the Department of Emergency Medicine, Department Administrator, faculty, and resident physicians. This position coordinates departmental activities, manages calendars, meetings, travel, purchasing, timekeeping, communications, and financial records. The role requires independent judgment, strong organizational skills, and discretion when handling sensitive or confidential information. Qualifications: Education, general: Bachelor's degree in business administration, finance, or related field, plus two (2) years of administrative support experience OR High School Diploma/GED, plus six (6) years of administrative support experience. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Must also be proficient in Microsoft Office, Word, Excel, and PowerPoint. Preference given to the applicant with cutting edge skills utilizing organizational software such as Box, Adobe Suite,\u00a0 RedCap database development and management skills, Workday experience, and professional caliber social media communications and experience with SharePoint. Additional Information: Responsibilities Manage the Chair\u2019s calendar, travel arrangements, meetings, correspondence, and departmental activities. Coordinate communication with faculty, staff, and other departments across campus. Prepare presentations, reports, correspondence, meeting materials, and minutes. Maintain departmental spreadsheets, databases, files, and records. Process and reconcile faculty and staff travel expenses and the department\u2019s BTA card account. Procure departmental supplies and services and process purchase requisitions in Workday. Identify and apply the appropriate cost centers for departmental expenses. Serve as the departmental timekeeper and assist with screening applicant resumes. Provide administrative support to the Department Administrator, faculty, and resident physicians. Track faculty and resident expenditures from designated fund accounts. Manage general office operations, including phone calls, visitors, mail, faxes, office supplies, and housekeeping requests. Protect sensitive and confidential information. Perform other duties as assigned. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Substance Abuse Testing This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Institutional-Services-Assistant_R0088775-1": {"title": "Institutional Services Assistant", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 10/03/2026 Type of Position: Skilled Labor Job Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: OPS | NUTRI Production Team Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Institutional Services Assistant, in conjunction with other assistants and under the direction of a supervisor, cleans dishes, the kitchen area, food preparation equipment, and utensils. The Institutional Services Assistant also removes trash while maintaining a clean, safe, and sanitary environment. Qualifications: Minimum: High School Diploma or GED Able to exert up to 50 pounds of force occasionally and/or up to 20 pounds of force frequently or constantly to lift, carry, push, pull, or otherwise move objects. Washes dishes, glassware, flatware, pots, or pans using a dishwasher or manually then places the equipment in designated storage areas. Maintains kitchen work areas, floors, equipment, or utensils. Uses and stores chemical and cleaning supplies. Sorts and removes trash, placing it in designated pickup areas and clean/line garbage containers. May perform other duties as assigned. Additional Information: Salary Information: $16 hourly. Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Criminal Background Check This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Standing, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Crawling, Crouching, Stooping Occasional Physical Activity: Sitting Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Fayetteville-AR/Engineering-Research-Coordinator_R0090698-2": {"title": "Engineering Research Coordinator", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com, then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at all University of Arkansas institutions will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students.\u201d University of Arkansas, Fayetteville students will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Student Jobs at UAF.\u201d All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. Closing Date: 09/14/2026 Type of Position: Project Management Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas, Fayetteville Founded in 1871, the University of Arkansas is a land grant institution, classified by the Carnegie Foundation among the nation\u2019s top 2 percent of universities with the highest level of research activity. The University of Arkansas works to advance the state and build a better world through education, research, and outreach by providing transformational opportunities and skills, fostering a welcoming climate, and nurturing creativity, discovery, and the spread of new ideas and innovations. The University of Arkansas campus is located in Fayetteville, a welcoming community ranked as one of the best places to live in the U.S. The growing region surrounding Fayetteville is home to numerous Fortune 500 companies and one of the nation\u2019s strongest economies. Northwest Arkansas is also quickly gaining a national reputation for its focus on the arts and overall quality of life. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10% of employee salary. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions, you should review before applying for the opening. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process, please submit a request via the Disability Accommodations | OEOC | University of Arkansas (uark.edu) : Request an Accommodation. Appli\u00adcants are required to submit a request for each position of which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 479.575.5351. Department: Associate Dean of Research Reports Department's Website: https://engineering.uark.edu/ Summary of Job Duties: The Engineering Research Coordinator supports the College of Engineering\u2019s research enterprise by coordinating proposal development, contract and industry-related activities, sponsored project administration, and research operations. The coordinator also provides program and financial support, develops and maintains research administration resources and reporting tools, assists with team workload and proposal intake, and leads or supports research-related events and collaborative initiatives that strengthen faculty and industry engagement. Regular, reliable, and non-disruptive attendance is an essential job duty, as is the ability to create and maintain collegial, harmonious working relationships with others. Qualifications: Minimum qualifications: Bachelor\u2019s degree from an accredited institution of higher education At least two years of professional experience in research administration, sponsored programs, grants and contracts administration, project coordination, higher education administration, or a related field Applicable equivalencies may be considered on the above qualifications. Preferred qualifications: Master\u2019s degree or higher from an accredited institution of higher education Experience coordinating industry-sponsored research activities or working with corporate and foundation partners. At least three years in a position working in higher education At least three years of experience in pre-award research administration, including preparing proposals, developing budgets, coordinating proposal submissions to federal, state, foundation, industry, and/or other private sponsors Certified Research Administrator certification or other relevant certifications Additional Information: Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Recruitment Contact Information: Shannon Davis, Director of Research Operations, College of Engineering, sgdavis@uark.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Special Instructions to Applicants: Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas seeks to attract, develop and retain high quality faculty, staff and administrators that consistently display practices and behaviors to advance a culture that embeds equal opportunity, educational excellence and unparalleled access for all. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All Application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAMS/Student-Employee_R0088658-1": {"title": "Student Employee", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted Today\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/19/2026 Type of Position: Other Health Care - Medical Ancillary Support Job Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: CHP | Student Employees and Trainees Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Student Employee provides administrative and operational support to the department by assisting with front office activities, completing routine administrative tasks, and maintaining organized department materials and supplies. This position offers students the opportunity to develop professional skills while contributing to the efficient daily operations of the department and providing excellent customer service to faculty, staff, students, and visitors. Qualifications: Bachelor's degree required. Student must be in good academic standing with the CHP Department of Physical Therapy. Requirements are between 5-10 hours per week, depending on department needs and student\u2019s academic schedule.. Responsibilities: Assist with department events. Assist faculty with gathering research information and literature reviews. Assist faculty with data collection and organization. Assist faculty with preparation of grant and/or research materials. Perform other tasks as assigned by either faculty or staff. Additional Information: Salary Information: $16.00/hr Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Lifting, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Reaching, Repetitive Motion, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Fayetteville-AR/Social-Media-and-Design-Specialist_R0090796": {"title": "Social Media and Design Specialist", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/21/2026 Type of Position: Professional Staff - Project/Program Administration Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: Division of Agriculture of the University of Arkansas The University of Arkansas System Division of Agriculture is a state wide campus, with faculty based on University campuses, at Research and Extension Centers and in every Arkansas county. It consists of the Arkansas Agricultural Experiment Station (AES) and the Arkansas Cooperative Extension Service (CES), and is home to more than 1400 employees.\u00a0 The Division was established in 1959 and is headed by the Vice-President for Agriculture.\u00a0 The Division headquarters is located in Little Rock with the rest of the University of Arkansas System Administration.\u00a0 As an employer, the University of Arkansas System Division of Agriculture offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance.\u00a0 Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process and require reasonable accommodations, please contact the Division's Office of Program & Employment Compliance at compliance@uada.edu . For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-671-2219 or 479-502-9820. Department: AGCS | Agricultural Communication Services Department's Website: https://aaes.uada.edu/communications/ Summary of Job Duties: The Arkansas Agricultural Experiment Station (AAES) is seeking a creative and strategic Social Media and Design Specialist to join our Communications team. This full time position is ideal for someone with a passion for social media storytelling and who has strong writing and editing skills and the ability to create high-quality, engaging graphics for social media, web and print. The Social Media and Design Specialist plays a key role in communicating the mission, research, and impact of AAES to a wide range of audiences. This role works closely with the Research Communications team to promote news, web, publications and video content across social media, and reports to the Director of Research Communications. The Social Media and Design Specialist will: \u2022 Write, edit, design, and publish engaging and accessible content daily (e.g., original text, photos, videos and graphics) that meets platform-specific requirements on all AAES social media platforms. \u2022 Coordinate with communications team members to promote news releases, web content, events, and ongoing campaigns. \u2022 Ensure social media content amplifies the broader research communications mission. \u2022 Oversee social media strategy and execution by following updated best practices and trends, including content planning, execution, collaboration with team members, and day-to-day engagement with followers. \u2022 Oversee design of social media accounts (e.g., Facebook timeline cover, profile pictures and branded images). \u2022 Analyze performance metrics, using insights to refine strategy and improve engagement and reach. \u2022 Schedule content in advance to ensure consistent posting. \u2022 Provide technical and strategic social media support to departmental and other official, AAES-affiliated social media accounts (troubleshooting, strategic advisement, account registry, analytics, etc.). \u2022 Maintain social media governance process and recommend best practices for AAES-affiliated social media accounts. \u2022 Plan and conduct regular social media training for employees. \u2022 As needed, attend AAES events for social media coverage, which may include infrequent in-state travel. \u2022 Create on-brand visual assets to support AAES communications, including graphics for social media, basic web visuals, event promotions, presentations, and limited print materials. \u2022 Maintain visual consistency and brand standards across AAES social media platforms and select communications materials, ensuring graphics align with established brand guidelines. \u2022 Support design needs for campaigns and initiatives, including adapting existing templates or assets and making minor design updates to meet platform or audience needs Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor\u2019s degree in communications, public relations, journalism, or a related field. Degree must be obtained prior to the start date. Must submit a portfolio and/or links to previously produced social media content and design work. Candidates should include a brief description of their role in creating submitted materials. Preferred Qualifications: 2+ years\u2019 experience in social media management 2+ years\u2019 design experience Excellent verbal and written communication skills Strong photography skills Experience creating videos (shooting and editing using smartphone) for social media Knowledge/awareness of WCAG accessibility standards Experience with paid ads and boosted posts in all social media platforms Experience managing Facebook, Instagram, Reels, X, LinkedIn, and Threads, as well as scheduling tools (e.g., SocialPilot) Proficiency with design tools (Cana, Adobe Creative Suite) Positive and collaborative work ethic Experience managing Facebook, Instagram, Reels, X, LinkedIn, and Threads, as well as scheduling tools (e.g., SocialPilot) Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Excellent interpersonal and communication skills, with the ability to write, edit, and proofread content for a variety of audiences; strong attention to detail required Ability to balance multiple priorities Project management skills, including planning, organization, and prioritization of social media content and design projects Analytical skills, with the ability to interpret social media metrics and make informed decisions to refine content strategy Knowledge of social media platforms and best practices, including platform specific content requirements, emerging trends, and accessibility considerations. Design skills, including the ability to create and edit visually engaging, on brand graphics for social media, web, presentations, and limited print materials. Ability to use graphic design tools (e.g., Canva, Adobe Creative Suite) to adapt templates, resize assets and make basic design updates as needed. Ability to master AAES brand standards and visual consistency, with the ability to apply established guidelines across digital and print communications. Collaborative skills, with the ability to work effectively with colleagues, subject matter experts, and stakeholders to develop content and visual materials. Basic familiarity with AI as it relates to communications and design tools, with the ability to use them responsibly to improve workflow efficiency while maintaining human judgment and final editorial control. \u00a0 \u00a0 Additional Information: Salary Information: Starting at $50,000, commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Other (see special instructions for details), Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Candidates must submit a portfolio and/or links to previously produced social media content and design work. Candidates should include a brief description of their role in creating submitted materials. Recruitment Contact Information: Mollie Pratt, Director of Research Communications mcpratt@uark.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Motor Vehicle Reports Check The University of Arkansas System Division of Agriculture may conduct pre-employment background checks on certain positions for applicants being considered for employment. \u00a0 The background checks may include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. \u00a0 Required checks are identified in the position listing. \u00a0 A criminal background check or arrest pending adjudication information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absences of a relationship to the requirements of the position. \u00a0 Background check information will be used in a consistent, non-discriminatory manner consistent with the state and federal law. \u00a0 The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting Frequent Physical Activity: Hearing, Talking Occasional Physical Activity: Driving, Standing Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Fayetteville-AR/ARE-ON-Associate-Network-Engineer_R0091112-1": {"title": "ARE-ON Associate Network Engineer", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com, then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at all University of Arkansas institutions will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students.\u201d University of Arkansas, Fayetteville students will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Student Jobs at UAF.\u201d All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. Closing Date: 10/01/2026 Type of Position: Professional Staff - Information Technology Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: Arkansas Research and Education Optical Network (ARE-ON) Founded in 1871, the University of Arkansas is a land grant institution, classified by the Carnegie Foundation among the nation\u2019s top 2 percent of universities with the highest level of research activity. The University of Arkansas works to advance the state and build a better world through education, research, and outreach by providing transformational opportunities and skills, fostering a welcoming climate, and nurturing creativity, discovery, and the spread of new ideas and innovations. The University of Arkansas campus is located in Fayetteville, a welcoming community ranked as one of the best places to live in the U.S. The growing region surrounding Fayetteville is home to numerous Fortune 500 companies and one of the nation\u2019s strongest economies. Northwest Arkansas is also quickly gaining a national reputation for its focus on the arts and overall quality of life. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10% of employee salary. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions, you should review before applying for the opening. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process, please submit a request via the Disability Accommodations | OEOC | University of Arkansas (uark.edu) : Request an Accommodation. Appli\u00adcants are required to submit a request for each position of which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 479.575.5351. Department: Network and Technical Support Department's Website: https://www.areon.net Summary of Job Duties: The ARE-ON Associate Network Engineer's role is to ensure the operations and service delivery of the ARE-ON state-wide backbone network and subscribed network services for our member organizations. About ARE-ON ARE-ON provides and supports WAN and select networking services for 45 institutions of higher-ed and healthcare delivery in Arkansas, including internet delivery, managed WAN router service, and project consulting. The ARE-ON associate network engineer is directly responsible for supporting technology services that drive the healthcare, research, and education missions of some of the largest public organizations in the state. ARE-ON is a unit of the University of Arkansas System, and all our employees are eligible for the same benefits package as the University of Arkansas, Fayetteville campus. Day-to-Day Work The Associate Network Engineer for ARE-ON reports to the Director of Network Services and provides hands-on installation, maintenance, and support for ARE-ON's state-wide network infrastructure. This role installs fiber cabling and networking equipment at ARE-ON facilities and performs basic troubleshooting of network switching and routing systems, their operating systems, and associated components. The Associate Network Engineer documents equipment and connections as they map to ARE-ON's services, maintaining accurate and current network records. This role participates in on-call rotation, triaging and resolving network service incidents and tickets, and supports the broader network team with project execution, systems support, and infrastructure management. This role is on the ARE-ON network operations team of 5 that shares the support of the state-wide telecommunications shelters, more than 2,200 miles of leased and owned fiber optic cables and strands, optical transmission systems, installed network router and switch hardware, and a myriad of other network support hardware and software that encompass ARE-ON\u2019s Network and member services. This position reports directly to the ARE-ON Director of Network Services. Work Conditions \u2022 Network maintenance activities, including both planned and emergency work, frequently occur during off-peak hours, including evenings, overnight, and weekends, to minimize disruption to member institutions' operations \u2022 Regular in-state travel and occasional interstate travel to ARE-ON network facilities, points of presence, and member institutions is required, up to 50% of working time \u2022 Participation in an on-call rotation to support incident response outside of standard business hours \u2022 Remote work for this position is allowed under the University of Arkansas Fayetteville Policies and Procedures 412.3. The employee must be a resident of Arkansas but does not have to work out of the Fayetteville ARE-ON offices or reside in the Northwest Arkansas area. \u2022 Regular, reliable, and non-disruptive attendance is an essential job duty, as is the ability to create and maintain collegial, harmonious working relationships with others. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications Associates Degree from an accredited institution of higher education \u00a0 At least three (3) years of experience in network engineering as a primary job function, Demonstrated experience with interior routing protocols (e.g., OSPF or similar) and network switching. At least one (1) year of experience with exterior routing protocols, including the use of BGP and autonomous systems Valid Drivers License (driving is required for this position) Preferred Qualifications Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, or a related field from an accredited institution of higher education At least five (5) years of experience in network engineering as a primary job function, including at least two (2) year of experience with exterior routing protocols Entry-level certification from a major data networking vendor in network routing and switching (e.g., CCNA, JNCIA, or equivalent) Working exposure to network monitoring and management tools and practices Experience working with DC-based power systems in data center or telecommunications environments Proven knowledge and experience with supporting Internet networks, including specific experience with the use of autonomous systems, BGP routing protocols and policy, IP multicast, IPv4 and IPv6, SNMP network monitoring and management KSA's Working technical knowledge of current network hardware, protocols, and Internet standards Knowledge of working with Juniper, Cisco, or other carrier-grade routing and switching hardware, including network operating systems/firmware, network management software, and firewalls Proven customer service skills Experience working in a team-oriented, collaborative environment Strong interpersonal, written, and oral communication skills Highly self-motivated and directed, with keen attention to detail Able to effectively prioritize tasks in a high-pressure environment Proven analytical and problem-solving abilities Additional Information: Salary Information: $98,800 - $114,200 commensurate with education and experience) Required Documents to Apply: List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Proof of Veteran Status Recruitment Contact Information: Contact University HR All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Special Instructions to Applicants: Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Motor Vehicle Reports Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas seeks to attract, develop and retain high quality faculty, staff and administrators that consistently display practices and behaviors to advance a culture that embeds equal opportunity, educational excellence and unparalleled access for all. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All Application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding Frequent Physical Activity: Driving, Lifting Occasional Physical Activity: Climbing Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Cossatot-Community-College-of-the-University-of-Arkansas/Administrative-Specialist-III-Receptionist_R0091196-1": {"title": "Administrative Specialist III-Receptionist", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/19/2026 Type of Position: Staff - Clerical Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: Cossatot Community College of the University of Arkansas Cossatot Community College of the University of Arkansas (UA Cossatot) began in DeQueen, Arkansas in 1975 as an Arkansas Vocational-Technical School, designed to provide relevant workforce training for four counties in southwest Arkansas. Fast forward to now where UA Cossatot has four vibrant campuses and over 1500 students learning in a variety of for-credit disciplines plus a host of area industry employees sharpening their skills through our workforce training programs. UA Cossatot prides itself on a safe work environment, where all employees undergo rigorous background checks and are welcomed to the college with an abundance of hands-on orientations to their positions. UA Cossatot also embraces Continuous Quality Improvement (CQI) where everything we do is measured and analyzed to ensure we are giving students the very best we have to offer. CQI involves all employees and completes a cycle that starts with the strategic plan and ends with an Institutional Effectiveness Evaluation. It's okay to brag a little when you work for UA Cossatot!Cossatot Community College of the University o Arkansas is an NCA-accredited two-year institution affiliated with the University of Arkansas System with Campuses in De Queen, Nashville, Ashdown, and Lockesburg Arkansas. The Colleges designated service area includes Sevier, Little River, Howard and Pike counties.\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please submit a request via the OEOC website: \u00a0Applicants are required to submit a request for each position to which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at (870) 584-1104. Department: Student Services Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Administrative Assistant III/Receptionist serves as the initial point of contact for the De Queen campus and provides administrative support to Admissions and Enrollment Services. The position assists students, prospective students, employees, and visitors while supporting admissions, enrollment, communication, and general office operations. DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES \u2022 Greets and assists students, employees, visitors, and prospective students, providing information or directing inquiries as appropriate. \u2022 Answers and transfers incoming calls, maintains the campus phone directory, and updates phone messages during college closures. \u2022 Provides information regarding college operations, academic programs, and admissions processes. \u2022 Maintains the De Queen campus mailroom and assists with office machines and related functions. \u2022 Supports recruitment and admissions activities, including mail campaigns, prospective student outreach, and submission of admissions applications. \u2022 Follows up with enrolled students to assist with completion of required onboarding tasks. \u2022 Maintains student records and performs data entry and record maintenance for Admissions, Registrar, Institutional Research and Reporting, Financial Aid, and the Business Office. \u2022 Performs other duties as assigned. Qualifications: High school diploma or GED required; associate degree preferred. Strong customer service and communication skills. Strong organizational skills and attention to detail. Self-motivated with the ability to take initiative, think critically, and work independently or as part of a team. Proficiency in Microsoft Office, particularly Word, Excel, and Outlook. Must successfully complete required criminal background and Child Maltreatment Central Registry checks as a condition of employment. Additional Information: Salary Information: $25,773 annual salary; plus an excellent benefits package Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Other (see special instructions for details), Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: All applications must include a cover letter, an updated r\u00e9sum\u00e9, and a copy of high school diploma or GED, or college transcripts. Applications received without the required documents will be considered incomplete and will not be reviewed. Recruitment Contact Information: Kelly Plunk, Director of Human Resources, (870) 584-1104 or kplunk@cccua.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check Cossatot Community College of the University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Fayetteville/Member-Engagement-Manager_R0090840-1": {"title": "Member Engagement Manager", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com, then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at all University of Arkansas institutions will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students.\u201d University of Arkansas, Fayetteville students will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Student Jobs at UAF.\u201d All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. Closing Date: 09/21/2026 Type of Position: Professional Staff - Project/Program Administration Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: Arkansas Research and Education Optical Network (ARE-ON) Founded in 1871, the University of Arkansas is a land grant institution, classified by the Carnegie Foundation among the nation\u2019s top 2 percent of universities with the highest level of research activity. The University of Arkansas works to advance the state and build a better world through education, research, and outreach by providing transformational opportunities and skills, fostering a welcoming climate, and nurturing creativity, discovery, and the spread of new ideas and innovations. The University of Arkansas campus is located in Fayetteville, a welcoming community ranked as one of the best places to live in the U.S. The growing region surrounding Fayetteville is home to numerous Fortune 500 companies and one of the nation\u2019s strongest economies. Northwest Arkansas is also quickly gaining a national reputation for its focus on the arts and overall quality of life. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10% of employee salary. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions, you should review before applying for the opening. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process, please submit a request via the Disability Accommodations | OEOC | University of Arkansas (uark.edu) : Request an Accommodation. Appli\u00adcants are required to submit a request for each position of which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 479.575.5351. Department: Arkansas Research Education Optical Network Department's Website: https://www.areon.net Summary of Job Duties: About ARE-ON ARE-ON provides and supports WAN and select networking services for 45 institutions of higher-ed and healthcare delivery in Arkansas, including internet delivery, managed WAN router service, and project consulting. The ARE-ON associate network engineer is directly responsible for supporting technology services that drive the healthcare, research, and education missions of some of the largest public organizations in the state. ARE-ON is a unit of the University of Arkansas System, and all our employees are eligible for the same benefits package as the University of Arkansas, Fayetteville campus. Day to Day The Member Engagement Manager reports to the Executive Director and serves as ARE-ON's primary relationship-builder with information technology departments, research offices, and applied users of ARE-ON's services across the member community, spanning the academy and healthcare delivery. This role identifies where members' institutional strategy and technology goals should inform ARE-ON's investment in services and capabilities, and surfaces shared investment and partnership opportunities across the membership. The Member Engagement Manager facilitates member education on ARE-ON's services and benefits to help institutions realize the full value of their existing investment, leads onboarding for new member institutions, and owns ARE-ON's total engagement strategy, including in-person conferences, meetings, online seminars, and working groups. This role also establishes and maintains ARE-ON's overall member engagement program and associated metrics, including tracking applied engagement work carried out across ARE-ON's technical and support teams in response to member needs. This is an individual contributor position with no direct reports. Working Conditions -This position requires that the successful candidate reside within the state of Arkansas as defined in University of Arkansas Policies and Procedures #412.3. Remote work within the state of Arkansas is an option, but travel for on-site meetings to meet the job functions is required. -This position requires regular in-state travel to ARE-ON member campuses for in-person relationship building and initiative development, estimated at 25% to 50% of working time. -Regular, reliable, and non-disruptive attendance is an essential job duty, as is the ability to create and maintain collegial, harmonious working relationships with others. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications Bachelor's degree in a relevant field from an accredited institution of higher education, or equivalent combination of education and experience At least four years of experience building and managing professional relationships with senior leadership or decision-makers across multiple organizations, departments, or business units Demonstrated experience operating in a complex, multi-stakeholder environment, coordinating across functions or organizational boundaries rather than within a single team Preferred Qualifications Demonstrated understanding of higher education's operating environment at an institutional or system level, extending beyond a single department or unit, such as through experience within a research and education network or broader higher education setting Ability to communicate credibly across a range of technology domains, including academic technology, healthcare technology, research cyberinfrastructure, and enterprise IT service delivery, without requiring deep technical expertise in any single area Excellent interpersonal and communication skills, with demonstrated ability to listen, translate, and build rapport across varied institutional audiences Demonstrated executive presence and public-speaking ability, with comfort engaging senior institutional leadership in both small and large group settings, including conferences and working groups Experience in a higher education technology environment Familiarity with the funding landscape for multi-institutional and regional technology or research initiatives Experience facilitating cross-institutional collaboration, shared governance, or shared-services initiatives Experience coordinating conferences, working groups, or member- or community-engagement programs Experience with CRM or member-database platforms (e.g., Salesforce) to manage relationship and engagement records Experience defining and reporting on member engagement metrics or program KPIs Additional Information: Salary Information: $85,000 \u2013 $109,000 (Commensurate with education and experience) Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Proof of Veteran Status Recruitment Contact Information: Leslie Pounds, HR Recruiter, pounds@uark.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Special Instructions to Applicants: Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Motor Vehicle Reports Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas seeks to attract, develop and retain high quality faculty, staff and administrators that consistently display practices and behaviors to advance a culture that embeds equal opportunity, educational excellence and unparalleled access for all. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All Application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding Frequent Physical Activity: Driving, Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Extra-Help-ESPN-Camera-Operator-2_R0053876": {"title": "Extra Help/ESPN Camera Operator (Multiple Open Positions)", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted Today\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Staff - Clerical Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Little Rock The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is a metropolitan research university that provides an accessible, quality education through flexible learning and unparalleled internship opportunities. At UA Little Rock, we prepare our more than 8,900 students to be innovators and responsible leaders in their fields. Committed to its metropolitan research university mission, UA Little Rock is a driving force in Little Rock's thriving cultural community and a major component of the city and state's growing profile as a regional leader in research, technology transfer, economic development, and job creation. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . Department: Sports Information Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Extra Help/ ESPN Camera Operator will assist with operating the camera and other duties as assigned. This position is governed by state and federal laws and agency policy. Qualifications: REQUIRED EDUCATION AND/OR EXPERIENCE: High School diploma. JOB DUTIES & RESPONSIBILITIES: Responsible for operating the camera equipment; Collaborate and work closely with the producer and the team; Responsible for operating various camera support equipment. Monitor technical aspects of the camera equipment during shoots; Must follow safety protocols to ensure the well-being of the team and themselves; Responsible for the maintenance and organization of camera equipment; Collaborating with the technical crews; Ensure that all equipment is tested and maintained before filming begins; Resolve technical and practical problems. KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS & ABILITIES: Must be able to work home events as needed; Must be able to work weekend and late nights; Must be professional and punctual; Must respond quickly to directions; Need strong communication and collaboration skills to work effectively with other crew members; Able to coordinate with camera assistants, grips, and other departments to ensure smooth camera movements and efficient workflow. Additional Information: Salary Information: $50 stipend per game Required Documents to Apply: None Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Brandy Dixon, Assistant AD of Communications (MBB, XC, TF), bmsweeden@ualr.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: No Background Check Required The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Standing, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Hearing, Standing, Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Hearing, Standing, Talking, Walking Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Anesthesia-Technician---Perioperative-Services_R0091179-1": {"title": "Anesthesia Technician - Perioperative Services", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/11/2026 Type of Position: Clinical Staff - Medical Ancillary Support Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Shift Vary (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | PeriopSvc Anesthesia Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: **Schedule: Full-Time, Shift Varies** The Anesthesia Technician assists anesthesia staff before, during, and after procedures requiring anesthesia and answers directly to the SPS/Anesthesia Tech Supervisor. Anesthesia Technicians will work in the UAMS Main and One Day Surgery (ODS) Operating Rooms. The Main OR is a 20-room suite, operational 24/7, and located on the 2nd floor of the Central Hospital. There are 10 endoscopic rooms, 2 laminar flow rooms, 2 DaVinci Robotic rooms and a dedicated endovascular room. It is a fast-paced environment performing state of the art procedures with state-of-the-art equipment. Specialties include: Gynecology, Urology, Orthopedic (total and trauma), Vascular, Cardiovascular (open heart), E.N.T., Plastic/Reconstructive, and General (Kidney and Liver transplant) and Neurosurgery. ODS is an 8-room suite, M-F 0630-1900 and located on the 4th floor of the Outpatient Center. It services primarily outpatient procedures in all services listed above excluding Heart, Vascular and Transplants. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: High School/GED, Plus 1 year of patient care experience Preferred Qualifications: Previous Anesthesia Tech experience 2 years patient care experience \u00a0 Additional Information: Employees in this role must be fitted for, capable of donning and performing routine tasks in personal protective equipment to include N95 masks, Powered Air Purifying Respirators (PAPR) or Controlled Air Purifying Respirators (CAPR). Responsibilites: Assembly of set-ups and preparing machines and equipment for use Performing basic tests of machines and trouble-shooting problems with machines Cleaning, replacing tubing, stocking carts and general turn-over of rooms between and after cases Performing blood tests Taking care of residents and staff needs as a member of the operating room team Follows directions and instructions from the Anesthesia staff and the OR coordinator Models the Core Values of UAMS \u2013 Integrity, Respect, Diversity, Teamwork, Creativity, and Excellence in compliance with company guidelines. Performs related responsibilities as required or assigned Salary Information: commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Criminal Background Check, Substance Abuse Testing This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Standing, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Sitting, Stooping Occasional Physical Activity: Grasping, Kneeling, Repetitive Motion, Sharps Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAMS/Child-Development-Technician--Kids-First--Fort-Smith--AR-_R0083210-1": {"title": "Child Development Technician (Kids First, Fort Smith, AR)", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 10/03/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: COM | Peds Kids First Fort Smith Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: KIDS FIRST serves children with special healthcare needs ranging in age from six weeks to five years. In our pediatric day healthcare clinics, children diagnosed as having a medical condition known to place them at risk for developmental delays and disabilities receive intensive intervention. The Child Development Technician assists the Early Childhood Development Specialist in providing care and intervention to a group of young children birth to age 5 with developmental delays and special medical needs. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: \u00a0 High School Diploma or GED PLUS 6 months experience working in the care of children Additional education including CCOT, CDA, AA, or Bachelor\u2019s Degree in Early Childhood Education, Child Development, or a related filed may be substituted for the experience requirement. Additional Information: Responsibilities:\u00a0 Provides quality direct patient care for a group of young children including serving mealtimes, assisting with feeding, diapering, and dressing.\u00a0 Provides developmentally appropriate behavioral guidance within daily scheduled activities. Follows the direction of the ECDS to provide individualized developmental services of their assigned treatment rooms in a manner that is child-centered, family focused, and demonstrates evidence-based or best practice.\u00a0 Establishes exciting learning environments for young children and apply curriculum to address the objectives contained in each child\u2019s treatment plan. Constant Physical Activity: Feeling, Hearing Frequent Physical Activity: Crawling, Crouching, Kneeling, Lifting, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Standing, Stooping, Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Sitting Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Proof of Veteran Status, Resume, Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Cossatot-Community-College-of-the-University-of-Arkansas/Institutional-Services-Assistant-De-Queen-Campus_R0091186": {"title": "Institutional Services Assistant-De Queen Campus", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/19/2026 Type of Position: Skilled Labor Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: Cossatot Community College of the University of Arkansas Cossatot Community College of the University of Arkansas (UA Cossatot) began in DeQueen, Arkansas in 1975 as an Arkansas Vocational-Technical School, designed to provide relevant workforce training for four counties in southwest Arkansas. Fast forward to now where UA Cossatot has four vibrant campuses and over 1500 students learning in a variety of for-credit disciplines plus a host of area industry employees sharpening their skills through our workforce training programs. UA Cossatot prides itself on a safe work environment, where all employees undergo rigorous background checks and are welcomed to the college with an abundance of hands-on orientations to their positions. UA Cossatot also embraces Continuous Quality Improvement (CQI) where everything we do is measured and analyzed to ensure we are giving students the very best we have to offer. CQI involves all employees and completes a cycle that starts with the strategic plan and ends with an Institutional Effectiveness Evaluation. It's okay to brag a little when you work for UA Cossatot!Cossatot Community College of the University o Arkansas is an NCA-accredited two-year institution affiliated with the University of Arkansas System with Campuses in De Queen, Nashville, Ashdown, and Lockesburg Arkansas. The Colleges designated service area includes Sevier, Little River, Howard and Pike counties.\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please submit a request via the OEOC website: \u00a0Applicants are required to submit a request for each position to which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at (870) 584-1104. Department: Buildings and Grounds Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Institutional Services Assistant is responsible for maintaining clean, safe, and orderly facilities and assisting with the general care of campus buildings and surrounding areas. RESPONSIBILITIES INCLUDE \u2022 Performs general cleaning and custodial duties in classrooms, offices, hallways, restrooms, common areas, and other campus facilities. \u2022 Sweeps and mops; vacuums and shampoos carpets; and cleans baseboards and other floor surfaces as needed. \u2022 Cleans and sanitizes restrooms, fixtures, furniture, desks, tables, cabinets, appliances, whiteboards, windows, walls, stairways, entrances, and other surfaces; replenishes restroom and cleaning supplies. \u2022 Remove trash and replace liners. \u2022 Safely uses appropriate cleaning products, equipment, and procedures, including specialized cleaning methods, and performs scheduled or periodic cleaning activities. \u2022 Assists with campus event setup and cleanup and monitors assigned areas for cleanliness, maintenance, and safety concerns. \u2022 Performs other duties as assigned. Qualifications: High school diploma, GED, or equivalent. Ability to read, write, communicate effectively, follow oral and written instructions, have basic computer knowledge, and work independently with limited supervision. Ability to bend, stoop, stand, stretch, and perform other physical activities associated with custodial work, including lifting and carrying up to 50 pounds. Valid driver\u2019s license required. Ability to pass required background and Child Maltreatment Registry checks. Additional Information: All applications must include a cover letter, resume, and copy of high school diploma or GED.\u00a0 Applications received without the required documents will be incomplete and will not be considered for the position. Salary Information: $24,413 annual salary; plus an excellent benefits package Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Other (see special instructions for details), Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: All applications must include a cover letter, resume, and copy of high school diploma or GED. Applications received without the required documents will be incomplete and will not be considered for the position. Recruitment Contact Information: Kelly Plunk, Director of Human Resources, (870) 584-1104 or kplunk@cccua.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check Cossatot Community College of the University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Talking Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: Driving, Kneeling, Lifting, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Standing Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/RN---Gynecology-Oncology-Clinic_R0091121-1": {"title": "RN - Gynecology Oncology Clinic", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/11/2026 Type of Position: Clinical Staff - Nursing Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | CASL CA Gynecologic Oncology Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Registered Nurse (RN) will provide direct patient care as a Clinic RN. This professional nursing role will require the ability to coordinate care for patients, triage patients, and work collaboratively with clinic providers, fellows, and staff. Requires the ability to effectively work with patient referral sources, facilitate appointments, coordinate transitions of care, and provide patient education on complex conditions. The RN will work with the individual patient, their families, and providers of care to develop and implement individual health plans. This position is posted as a Monday - Friday 8:00 am - 4:30 pm. Come work with our wonderful group of Physician's at the UAMS Cancer Institute. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor\u2019s degree in Nursing, Associate\u2019s degree in Nursing, Diploma RN, or Master\u2019s degree in Nursing. Must be a graduate of an accredited RN nursing program Minimum of 1 year of Registered Nursing experience Valid Registered Nursing License Excellent communication skills. Strong work ethics and accountability Basic computer skills. Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor\u2019s degree in Nursing Oncology Nursing Experience\u00a0 Current BLS, National Nursi ng Certification Additional Information: Responsibilities: Collects and documents assessment data from patients and/or others per UAMS standard.\u00a0 Develops patient's Plan of Care (POC) per department/unit standards utilizing assessment data.\u00a0 Evaluates the progress of patients toward attainment of desired outcomes. Administers medication following department/unit standards and Nurse Practice Act.\u00a0 Verifies and evaluates care delivered to ensure it is consistent with patient and family centered care principles, practice standards and regulatory requirements. Supports the integration of current evidence into nursing practices.\u00a0 Promotes an environment conducive to positive educational experience for all students and staff.\u00a0 Provides effective patient/family education/discharge planning. Effectively collaborates and communicates with nursing staff at all levels, interdisciplinary teams, executive leaders, and other stakeholders.\u00a0 Communicates care appropriately through documentation in the medical record. Reports variances in care/ systems/ processes through the appropriate means.\u00a0 Participates in recruitment/retention of staff.\u00a0 Facilitates development and implementation of nursing practice standards that are evidence-based and in compliance with ANA standards. May perform other duties as assigned. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Criminal Background Check, Substance Abuse Testing This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Feeling, Grasping, Hearing, Lifting, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Repetitive Motion, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Balancing, Climbing, Sharps Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Cossatot-Community-College-of-the-University-of-Arkansas/Adult-Education-Paraprofessional-De-Queen-Campus--Part-Time-_R0089375": {"title": "Adult Education Paraprofessional/De Queen Campus (Part-Time)", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted Today\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/19/2026 Type of Position: Adjunct Faculty Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Less than Annual Appointment (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: Cossatot Community College of the University of Arkansas Cossatot Community College of the University of Arkansas (UA Cossatot) began in DeQueen, Arkansas in 1975 as an Arkansas Vocational-Technical School, designed to provide relevant workforce training for four counties in southwest Arkansas. Fast forward to now where UA Cossatot has four vibrant campuses and over 1500 students learning in a variety of for-credit disciplines plus a host of area industry employees sharpening their skills through our workforce training programs. UA Cossatot prides itself on a safe work environment, where all employees undergo rigorous background checks and are welcomed to the college with an abundance of hands-on orientations to their positions. UA Cossatot also embraces Continuous Quality Improvement (CQI) where everything we do is measured and analyzed to ensure we are giving students the very best we have to offer. CQI involves all employees and completes a cycle that starts with the strategic plan and ends with an Institutional Effectiveness Evaluation. It's okay to brag a little when you work for UA Cossatot!Cossatot Community College of the University o Arkansas is an NCA-accredited two-year institution affiliated with the University of Arkansas System with Campuses in De Queen, Nashville, Ashdown, and Lockesburg Arkansas. The Colleges designated service area includes Sevier, Little River, Howard and Pike counties.\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please submit a request via the OEOC website: \u00a0Applicants are required to submit a request for each position to which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at (870) 584-1104. Department: Adult Education Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The part-time Paraprofessional assists in carrying out daily activities for the Adult Education program, will greet visitors and students, provide accurate information to the public, complete intake/registration on new students, administer Locator and Test of Adult Basic Education (TABE) Tests for placement and for progress, maintain student files and enter updated information or scores as necessary, monitor student sign-in sheets and calculate totals, assist students in computer lab with educational programs and job related activities, provide assistance to Adult Education instructors and staff, answer questions, assist with individualized tutoring as needed, schedule Official General Educational Development (GED) Ready Tests and the official GED Tests, attend required trainings and meetings, and other departmental duties as assigned/needed. Qualifications: High School Diploma or GED Must be proficient with computers and pay close attention to detail Possess excellent written and oral communication skills; bilingual preferred Must be friendly and approachable Must pass Criminal Background and Child Maltreatment Registry checks Additional Information: All applications must include a cover letter, resume, and copy of High School Diploma or GED.\u00a0 Applications received without the required documents will be incomplete and will not be considered for the position. Salary Information: $11.50 per hour; up to 28 hours per week Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Other (see special instructions for details), Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: All applications must include a cover letter, resume, and copy of High School Diploma or GED. Applications received without the required documents will be incomplete and will not be considered for the position. Recruitment Contact Information: Kelly Plunk, Director of Human Resources, (870) 584-1104 or kplunk@cccua.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Child Maltreatment, Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry Cossatot Community College of the University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAG--University-of-Arkansas-Grantham/Associate-Vice-Chancellor--Academic-Operations_R0091158-1": {"title": "Associate Vice Chancellor, Academic Operations", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Professional Staff - Project/Program Administration Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas Grantham As an employer, the University of Arkansas Grantham offers a remote work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 - 10% of employee salary. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions, you should review before applying for the opening. If you need assistance with the application process, or if you are a person with a disability who would like to request a reasonable accommodation related to the application process, please contact the Department of Human Resources at hr@uagrantham.edu. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at recruiting@uagrantham.edu. Department: General Academics Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The University of Arkansas Grantham is looking for a REMOTE Associate Vice Chancellor, Academic Operations in the following states: AL, AR, AZ, DE, FL, GA, KS, IA, ID, IN, KY, LA, MD, MI, MO, MS, NC, NE, NJ, OH, OK, SC, TN, TX, UT, VA, VT, WI and WY. Please only apply if you are able to live and work full-time in one of the states listed above. State locations and specifics are subject to change as our hiring requirements shift. POSITION DESCRIPTION: The Associate Vice Chancellor, Academic Operations provides leadership for the operational infrastructure of the academic division. This position oversees Academic Operations, Faculty Managers and the Education Technology areas. This role translates strategic academic vision into scalable operational systems, administrative compliance, and academic technology. This position ensures UA Grantham maintains and further develops processes that enable efficiency and effectiveness. The Associate Vice Chancellor, Academic Operations is responsible for the execution of innovative, impactful processes and moving forward projects. KEY JOB RESPONSIBILITIES: 60% - Operational Management \u2022 Establish and oversee academic operations to establish consistency, scalability, and operational efficiency \u2022 Ensure the execution of strategic academic projects and educational technology initiatives in a compliant and timely manner \u2022 Ensure operational integrity, workflow optimization, and high-quality service delivery across the Academic Operations, Faculty Management, and Education Technology teams \u2022 Develop and maintain academic operational workflows and continuous process improvements to support institutional growth. \u2022 Other duties as assigned 20% - People Management \u2022 Define team priorities, deliverables, timelines, and performance standards \u2022 Ensure direct reports have well-defined responsibilities, documented procedures, and required resources \u2022 Manage performance using metrics, clear expectations, and standardized policy application \u2022 Provide training, tools, and clear processes while monitoring progress and adjusting resources as needed 15% - Stakeholder Engagement \u2022 Coordinate with the academic team and other stakeholders to ensure efficient faculty management and operational alignment across academics \u2022 Collaborate effectively with university leadership and cross-functional administrative units to streamline operational workflows, eliminate process bottlenecks, and advance strategic academic priorities \u2022 Maintain relationships and interact with higher education partners to drive technological innovation and operational excellence. 5% - Continuous Learning and Development \u2022 Continuously update skills and knowledge through required training \u2022 Seek feedback and opportunities for growth to enhance expertise and effectiveness Qualifications: EDUCATION: Master\u2019s degree required; Doctorate in Education, Higher Education Administration or a related field preferred \u00a0 WORK EXPERIENCE: Minimum of 7 \u2013 10 years of experience in higher education; at least 7 years in a leadership role Experience managing a team in a remote environment preferred \u00a0 \u00a0SKILLS: Demonstrated experience in higher education academic operations, instructional design strategies, and faculty development frameworks. Strong understanding of online education, including best practices in online teaching and learning. Ability to analyze operational metrics to drive efficiency and optimize resource allocation. Demonstrated skill in managing complex, multi-phase academic projects and guiding teams through organizational changes. Basic operational budget management, resource forecasting, and risk-mitigation skills within an academic environment. Excellent oral, written, and interpersonal communication skills, with the ability to articulate operational strategies across all institutional levels. Proven collaborative track record of leading, mentoring, and building consensus within diverse, geographically distributed teams. Strong talent development skills with the proven ability to train staff, drive high performance toward shared goals, and directly address difficult performance conversations. Familiarity with accreditation processes and regulatory requirements in higher education. High emotional intelligence (EQ) paired with a resourceful, analytical approach to conflict resolution and operational decision-making. Ability to interact and effectively communicate with all levels of staff and leadership. Computer skills, including Microsoft Office Suite, required Research skills required\u00a0 Excellent verbal and written communication skills. Language Skills : Able to read, analyze, and interpret common journals and legal documents. Able to respond to common inquiries or complaints from customers, regulatory agencies, or members of the business community. Able to effectively present information to executive management, faculty, staff, and/or students. Mathematical Skill : Able to apply concepts such as fractions, percentages, ratios, and proportions to practical situations. Reasoning Ability: Able to define problems, collect data, establish facts, and draw valid conclusions. Ability to present facts to faculty for departmental response. Able to deal with a variety of information presented in oral or written formats. Able to deal with non-verbal behavior in assisting with problem resolution. Physical Demands: The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Frequently required to use hand to finger, handle, or feel (including the use of computer keyboards) and talk or hear (including the use of a telephone and computer). Occasionally required to walk, stand, and make presentations This position may involve sitting at a desk for extended periods of time Specific vision abilities include close vision and distance vision \u00a0 University of Arkansas Grantham will seek to reasonably accommodate qualified individuals with a disability. Such reasonable accommodation may take the form of making existing facilities readily accessible to or usable by individuals with a disability, restructuring jobs, modifying schedules, acquiring, or modifying equipment, adjusting training materials, adjusting employment policies, and the like. \u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Additional Information: Salary Information: $100,000 Required Documents to Apply: Proof of Veteran Status, Resume, Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: recruiting@uagrantham.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Warren/Speech-Language-Pathologist--Warren-_R0090957-1": {"title": "Speech Language Pathologist (Warren)", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 10/04/2026 Type of Position: Clinical Staff - Rehabilitation Therapy Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: COM | Peds Kids First Warren Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: This Position is in Warren, AR. Speech Therapist, provides speech-language assessments and treatment using evidence-based techniques in a naturalistic, developmentally appropriate manner. Works collaborative and communicates effectively within the team; engages families as members of the treatment team. KIDS FIRST serves children with special healthcare needs ranging in age from six weeks to five years. In our pediatric day healthcare clinics, children diagnosed as having a medical condition known to place them at risk for developmental delays and disabilities receive intensive intervention. Qualifications: Master's degree in Speech Language Pathology required.\u00a0 Must have Arkansas license and American Speech-Language-Hearing Association (ASHA) Certificate of Clinical Competence or be eligible pending completion of Clinical Fellowship Year. Additional Information: Responsibilities: Participates in multi-disciplinary and department communication, which may include patient care discussion and/or meetings, unit/department clinic/hospital meetings. Provides education which may include serving as a clinical instructor, serving as a mentor for a clinical observer, providing education to other disciplines within UAMS and/or community. Documents patient evaluation/treatment/education and submits accurate and timely charges according to regulatory policies. Provides comprehensive evaluations of patients using appropriate tests/measures based on populations. Formulates an individualized plan of care. This includes an assessment of speech/language skills and vision/hearing screenings appropriate for the age of the client. Performs other duties as assigned Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), Proof of Veteran Status, Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Adult Maltreatment, Child Maltreatment, Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Feeling, Hearing, Standing, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Balancing, Climbing, Crawling, Crouching, Kneeling, Lifting, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Repetitive Motion Occasional Physical Activity: Sitting Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Cossatot-Community-College-of-the-University-of-Arkansas/Adult-Education-Instructor-De-Queen-Campus--Part-Time-_R0091178": {"title": "Adult Education Instructor/De Queen Campus (Part-Time)", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted Today\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Adjunct Faculty Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Less than Annual Appointment (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: Cossatot Community College of the University of Arkansas Cossatot Community College of the University of Arkansas (UA Cossatot) began in DeQueen, Arkansas in 1975 as an Arkansas Vocational-Technical School, designed to provide relevant workforce training for four counties in southwest Arkansas. Fast forward to now where UA Cossatot has four vibrant campuses and over 1500 students learning in a variety of for-credit disciplines plus a host of area industry employees sharpening their skills through our workforce training programs. UA Cossatot prides itself on a safe work environment, where all employees undergo rigorous background checks and are welcomed to the college with an abundance of hands-on orientations to their positions. UA Cossatot also embraces Continuous Quality Improvement (CQI) where everything we do is measured and analyzed to ensure we are giving students the very best we have to offer. CQI involves all employees and completes a cycle that starts with the strategic plan and ends with an Institutional Effectiveness Evaluation. It's okay to brag a little when you work for UA Cossatot!Cossatot Community College of the University o Arkansas is an NCA-accredited two-year institution affiliated with the University of Arkansas System with Campuses in De Queen, Nashville, Ashdown, and Lockesburg Arkansas. The Colleges designated service area includes Sevier, Little River, Howard and Pike counties.\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please submit a request via the OEOC website: \u00a0Applicants are required to submit a request for each position to which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at (870) 584-1104. Department: Adult Education Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The instructor will be responsible for teaching courses in an educational setting and developing and updating individual learning plans for students. Responsibilities include conducting structured classes or one-on-one instruction, organizing and leading student events, incorporating instructional aids and educational media, and coordinating guest speakers or special demonstrations to enhance the curriculum. The instructor will provide individualized instruction as needed, maintain accurate student records (including attendance, assessments, progression, and achievements), and advise students on both short- and long-term educational goals. Additional duties include student recruitment and retention, as well as participation in annual professional development activities. Classes are held three-four days per week. Qualifications: Bachelor\u2019s degree Valid Arkansas Teaching License Must be friendly, approachable, and possess a strong desire to teach Ability to successfully pass Criminal Background check and Child Maltreatment Registry checks Additional Information: All applications must include a cover letter, resume, unofficial transcripts, and copy of current teaching license.\u00a0 Applications received without the required documents will be incomplete and will not be considered for the position. Salary Information: $22.00 per hour; working approximately 24 hours per week Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), Resume, Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: All applications must include a cover letter, resume, unofficial transcripts, and copy of current teaching license. Applications received without the required documents will be incomplete and will not be considered for the position. Recruitment Contact Information: Kelly Plunk, Director of Human Resources, (870) 584-1104 or kplunk@cccua.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Child Maltreatment Cossatot Community College of the University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding Frequent Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding Occasional Physical Activity: Lifting Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAMS/Speech-Therapist_R0091030-1": {"title": "Speech Therapist", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 10/05/2026 Type of Position: Clinical Staff - Medical Ancillary Support Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: COM | Peds Dennis Development Center Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Speech Language Pathologist evaluates children from birth through adolescence in a multidisciplinary team setting. The evaluation may be independent, with a psychological examiner or with a multidisciplinary team. The evaluation is conducted to make initial and ongoing diagnoses, provide second opinions regarding diagnosis, and to provide clinical observations regarding the presence or absence of a developmental disability. This position is governed by speech/language certification regulations, state and federal laws, and agency/institution policy. Qualifications: Master's degree in Speech-Language Pathology required. Must have a\u00a0Certificate of Clinical Competence in Speech-Language Pathology (CCC-SLP) from the American Speech-Language-Hearing Association (ASLHA). Experience with Microsoft Office. Preferred Qualifications: Two (2) years of experience working with a pediatric population. EPIC experience. Additional Information: Responsibilities: Provide speech/language and other developmentally related evaluations or screenings using a variety of standardized instruments and behavioral observations to determine appropriate diagnoses and make recommendations for treatment. Conduct chart review, interview of caregivers, consultation with current or previous service providers; as well as clinical observation in structured and unstructured settings in order to facilitate clinical decision making. Conduct pure-tone audiometric screenings and/or distortion product otoacoustic emission screenings for the purpose of identifying possible hearing loss and to make appropriate referrals when necessary. Consult with other disciplines (i.e., physicians: nurses, clinical social workers, .psychological examiners, psychologists) to discuss evaluation findings and formulate diagnosis and appropriate recommendations for treatment (when applicable). As appropriate, compile resource material for families including handouts, website addresses, names and numbers of local providers, and referrals to community agencies. Participate in parent and professional staffing to share evaluation results. Listen and respond empathetically to the parent\u2019s concerns or questions. Offer options as appropriate. Document services provided by billing on the date the patient received the evaluation. Complete comprehensive evaluation report in a timely manner in accordance with current DDC policy, with appropriate impressions and recommendations for treatment:\u00a0 \u00a0 Serve as a clinical resource to the other disciplines. Select and prioritize services based on individual patient needs and referral concerns. Provide ongoing consultation to families upon request. Serve as a clinical supervisor for student clinicians. Participate in ongoing continuing education to maintain clinical competence and professional certification/licensure. Participate in work-related task forces to ensure the effective and efficient operation of the clinic and to promote patient safety. May perform other duties as assigned. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience. Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Adult Maltreatment, Child Maltreatment, Criminal Background Check, FBI Background Check This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: Hearing, Talking Occasional Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Access-Coordinator-II_R0091035-1": {"title": "Access Coordinator II", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/19/2026 Type of Position: Clinical Staff - Medical Ancillary Support Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: COM | Peds DDC Access Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Access Coordinator II works under supervision and provides comprehensive support for the patient care activities. This position may meet, greet, and assists the public, answer telephones and/or may coordinate appointments, referrals, consults, tests and/or procedures, check-in and registers patients, check-out patients, and collects payments and issues receipts, verifies insurance coverage and responds appropriately to the requirements of third- party payers. This position must be able to perform all duties of the Access Coordinator I level and performs other duties to support the patient care activities as needed. Qualifications: \u00a0 High School diploma/GED plus two (2) years of customer service or healthcare experience required. Additional Information: Responsibilities: Interacts with and assists the public in a professional and friendly manner as needed. Demonstrates effective communication skills; communicates accurate and complete information; maintains strict confidentiality when necessary. Demonstrates positive working relationships with co-workers, management team, and ancillary departments. Deals with conflicts in a positive and professional manner using careful listening and negotiation skills to resolve disagreements.\u00a0 Consistently utilizes communication devices and keeps accurate records as required. Demonstrates effective service recovery skills; follows the Core Concepts of Patient and Family Centered Care and the Basic Code of Conduct Guidelines. Assists internal and external stakeholders as needed with exceptional customer service. Schedules, reschedules, and coordinates appointments using the hospital systems by performing visit notifications of patients, conducts pre-registration as needed, and inputs and/or updates accurate patient information.\u00a0 Process walk-ins, create new patient charts, access systems for orders as appropriate.\u00a0 Conducts insurance verification and benefit explanation by running eligibility on patients, requesting outside records, and gathering outside medical records from referrals and files patient charts as needed. Pick up and deliver mail to mailroom, ensure the waiting room is clean, stocked with educational information and coffee. Perform ABN completion, schedule surgeries and/or tests. Issues school/work excuses, send out no show letters, take patient photos. Responsible for blocking schedules as appropriate, canceling and rescheduling appointments as requested.\u00a0 Collects and posts payments and issues receipts. Responsible for reconciliation/management change fund. Responsible for reconciliation of daily deposit & batch dollars and must complete deposit agreement. Maintain initial plan of care (signatures, etc.), and is responsible for recording daily and monthly statistics and communication of any medical records issues.\u00a0 Attends required training and/or in-services. Attends staff meetings and participates in the orientation and/or training of new staff.\u00a0 Participates in annual educational needs assessment. Maintains required job skill competencies and completes skill assessments annually. Completes and maintains documentation of continuing education hours annually. May perform other duties as assigned. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Crouching, Feeling, Grasping, Hearing, Lifting, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Pulling, Reaching, Repetitive Motion, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Hearing, Lifting, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Pulling, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Balancing, Crouching, Kneeling Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Diagnostic-Radiology-Technologist-PRN---MUSL-Ambulatory_R0091040-1": {"title": "Diagnostic Radiology Technologist PRN - MUSL Ambulatory", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted Today\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 10/04/2026 Type of Position: Clinical Staff - Medical Ancillary Support Job Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | MUSL Ambulatory Clinic PRN Staff (Jacob Allen Mitchell) Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Diagnostic Radiology Technologist produces radiographic images for medical interpretation, interacts with all healthcare staff, many clerical staff members, all patient care departments and with patient\u2019s families and visitors. This position is held accountable for performing the correct radiologic exams and producing high quality images. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Graduate of an approved Radiology program, Registered or eligible by the American Registry of Radiologic Technologists (ARRT) Licensed by the State of Arkansas in Radiology Technology \u200b Preferred Qualifications: BS Degree CPR Certification More than one (1) year of experience in diagnostic radiology or a related field Additional Information: Responsibilities: Operates and positions radiologic equipment to produce images of the body for diagnostic purposes and according to exam specifications, following established radiologic requirements and regulations to ensure patient care and safety. Prepares patients for radiologic procedures by escorting patients to rooms, providing verbal instructions, and assisting patients in positioning body parts to be radiographed. Explains procedures and observes patients to ensure patient care, safety and comfort during scan. Serves as a back-up for clinical team members, as needed, by controlling patient flow and triaging. Maintains working order of radiologic equipment including reporting equipment malfunctions and scheduling regular maintenance. Reviews patient records and imports external images into the systems. Performs other duties as assigned. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Criminal Background Check, Substance Abuse Testing This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Sitting, Standing, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Reaching, Repetitive Motion Occasional Physical Activity: Crouching, Kneeling, Lifting Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Data-and-Reporting-Specialist_R0091120": {"title": "Data and Reporting Specialist", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 12/31/2026 Type of Position: Professional Staff - Project/Program Administration Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas Pulaski Technical College University of Arkansas - Pulaski Technical College at North Little Rock is an integral part of the Arkansas Technical and Community College System maintained by the State of Arkansas. The college is governed by the University of Arkansas System Board of Trustees and a seven-member Board of Visitors and derives its support largely from student tuition and fees and legislative appropriations. UA - Pulaski Tech, a comprehensive two-year college, offers associate degree and certificate programs for students who plan to transfer to four-year colleges and universities and/or for career preparation and advancement. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply link/button. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at (501) 812-2839. Department: Institutional Research Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The University of Arkansas \u2013 Pulaski Technical College in North Little Rock, Arkansas, is accepting applications for a Data and Reporting Specialist. University of Arkansas \u2013 Pulaski Technical College provides access to high-quality education that promotes student learning and enables individuals to develop to their fullest potential. Position Summary: This is a two-year grant-funded position that will work with a variety of applications to produce reliable, accurate, and dependable information to assist the college in making data-informed recommendations on matters including student success and program viability. General Responsibilities: \u2022 Utilize Excel to extract, compile, analyze, interpret, and communicate complex data-related issues clearly and succinctly to various audiences \u2022 Performs data extraction, analysis and reporting \u2022 Collaborates with stakeholders on data and technical needs \u2022 Assures the confidentiality of data, including sensitive information related to students, faculty, and staff \u2022 Other duties as assigned Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor\u2019s degree required in an appropriate area of specialization, with emphasis in data analytics and/or information management Advanced experience working with large datasets in Excel Strong written and verbal communication skills Strong organizational skills and analytical capabilities Meticulous attention to detail Ability to work independently with minimal guidance and as part of a team toward common goals, and to coordinate efforts and collaborate with a variety of individuals Preferred Qualifications Demonstrated track record of compiling and presenting data for grants Experience working with State or Federal Workforce agencies \u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0 Additional Information: Salary Information: $44,500 Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume, Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants Recruitment Contact Information: Human Resources humanresources@uaptc.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Motor Vehicle Reports Check, Sex Offender Registry University of Arkansas - Pulaski Technical College is committed to providing a safe campus community. Title IX protects the college community from sexual harassment in a school's education programs and activities. This means that Title IX protects the college community in connection with all academic, educational, extracurricular, athletic, and other programs of the school, whether those programs take place in a school's facilities, in college transportation, at a class or training program sponsored by the school at another location, or elsewhere. \u00a0 We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Reaching, Repetitive Motion, Standing, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Feeling, Grasping, Hearing Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Fayetteville/Cleanroom-Process-and-Operations-Engineer_R0090877-1": {"title": "Cleanroom Process and Operations Engineer", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com, then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at all University of Arkansas institutions will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students.\u201d University of Arkansas, Fayetteville students will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Student Jobs at UAF.\u201d All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. Closing Date: 09/15/2026 Type of Position: Technical Research Support Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas, Fayetteville Founded in 1871, the University of Arkansas is a land grant institution, classified by the Carnegie Foundation among the nation\u2019s top 2 percent of universities with the highest level of research activity. The University of Arkansas works to advance the state and build a better world through education, research, and outreach by providing transformational opportunities and skills, fostering a welcoming climate, and nurturing creativity, discovery, and the spread of new ideas and innovations. The University of Arkansas campus is located in Fayetteville, a welcoming community ranked as one of the best places to live in the U.S. The growing region surrounding Fayetteville is home to numerous Fortune 500 companies and one of the nation\u2019s strongest economies. Northwest Arkansas is also quickly gaining a national reputation for its focus on the arts and overall quality of life. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10% of employee salary. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions, you should review before applying for the opening. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process, please submit a request via the Disability Accommodations | OEOC | University of Arkansas (uark.edu) : Request an Accommodation. Appli\u00adcants are required to submit a request for each position of which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 479.575.5351. Department: Department of Physics Research Assistants 01 Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Cleanroom Process and Operations Engineer will be providing technical and scientific support for the Materials Institute Cleanroom User Facility, which serves a diverse user base of faculty, researchers, and students conducting cutting-edge research in materials science, engineering, physics, chemistry, and related disciplines. We are searching for a talented individual with strong analytical skills and hands-on expertise in nanofabrication processes to work as a senior research associate. Key responsibilities include operating and supporting day-to-day operations of a wide range of nanofabrication processes such as physical and chemical vapor deposition systems, wet and dry-etching, photolithography, and related processes. The individual will provide training to students and faculty on these and other instrumentations, assist researchers with process development and experimental design, manage user access, scheduling systems, ensure safe and efficient facility usage, troubleshoot and repair equipment issues. The individual must have a background in Materials Science, Physics, Chemistry or Engineering and at least some experience working on Nanofabrication equipment. More specifically, the individual must be able to work with compressed gases, acids and other chemicals and will be expected to fulfill the following tasks: \u2022 Train and certify users on nanofabrication tools, processes, and cleanroom protocols. \u2022 Develop and implement effective training strategies for students and researchers. \u2022 Assist researchers with process development and experimental design related to micro- and nanofabrication techniques. \u2022 Perform preventative maintenance and maintain detailed equipment service records. \u2022 Troubleshoot and resolve minor equipment issues and coordinate vendor-supported repairs. \u2022 Manage user access, equipment reservations, and facility utilization systems. \u2022 Ensure facility operations remain compliant with University policies and Environmental Health and Safety (EHS) regulations. \u2022 Assist with facility tours, outreach activities, and demonstrations for faculty, staff, students, industrial partners, and visitors. \u2022 Promote facility capabilities and services to potential users across the University and external research community. \u2022 Contribute to continuous improvement of facility operations and user experience. Regular, reliable, and non-disruptive attendance is an essential job duty, as is the ability to establish and maintain collegial and effective working relationships with faculty, staff, students, and external collaborators. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: A BS degree in Materials Science, Engineering, Physics or related fields from an accredited institution of higher education At least two years experience working in nanofabrication and clean room facilities Preferred Qualifications: An MS or PhD degree in Materials Sciences, Engineering, Physics or related fields from an accredited institution of higher education Knowledge, Skills, & Abilities (KSAs): Candidates must have strong problem-solving Analytical skills Excellent interpersonal and communication skills for successful inter and intra-group interactions Additional Information: This position is a Designated Research Position \u00a0and is regulated by the Arkansas Research Education Protection Act of 2025 .\u00a0 Prior to issuance of an offer of employment, the University is required to request and obtain additional information about an applicant\u2019s background and, if required, conduct an additional review of that background information. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience. Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Recruitment Contact Information: Emily Ebbing, Project Program Specialist, eebbing@uark.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Special Instructions to Applicants: Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas seeks to attract, develop and retain high quality faculty, staff and administrators that consistently display practices and behaviors to advance a culture that embeds equal opportunity, educational excellence and unparalleled access for all. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All Application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Benton/Medical-Laboratory-Scientist--MLS--I--II----III--PRN---UAMS-Health-Benton-Bryant_R0091169-1": {"title": "Medical Laboratory Scientist (MLS) I, II, & III  PRN \u2013 UAMS Health Benton/Bryant", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/17/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Shift Vary (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: INA | Institutional Admin Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: This is a temporary/PRN Part-Time (as needed) position (not benefits eligible) located at the UAMS Health Benton/Bryant location. The MLS I is responsible for processing, evaluating and performing tests to identify microorganisms or antigens according to written procedures and performs susceptibilities. This person will also record and evaluate daily, weekly, and monthly QC in their assigned areas for further review by the supervisor. This position requires one to maintain safe work practices, follow all regulatory requirements and engage supervisor, manager, or director as appropriate. The MLS II performs a variety of technical procedures including HLA typing by rSSO and next generation sequencing methods, Luminex based HLA Antibody identification, and donor/recipient flow cytometric cross-matching. They are expected to keep all instrumentation in good working order and identify and notify the supervisor or lead tech of instrument malfunctions. The MLS II fulfills all the responsibilities and tasks of a MLS I as well as performing quality assurance metric studies, and training/competency assessments. The MLS III performs complex medical laboratory tests and procedures in a clinical laboratory setting. Analyzes and interprets results, troubleshoots issues, and ensures accuracy and quality control. Provides guidance and training to less experienced staff, assists in developing new laboratory protocols, and may participate in research projects. The MLS III fulfills all the responsibilities and tasks of a MLS I & II as well as performing quality assurance metric studies, and training/competency assessments. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: MLS I Bachelor\u2019s Degree in Medical Technology or Medical Laboratory Sciences OR an approved ASCP discipline (30 semester hours in biology and chemistry, which may be obtained within, or in addition to, the Bachelor's). ASCP or another accrediting agency certified or eligible (Certification must be obtained within one year of employment). MLS II Bachelor's degree in a chemistry, biology, or medical laboratory science 2 years of experience in a clinical laboratory CHT (ABHI) certification within 1 year of eligibility. If eligible at time of hire then within 1 year of hire date. Must be able to identify and report abnormal test results as well as communicate and interact with reviewing Pathologists and submitting clinicians. Must be able to work independently, multi-task, and make subjective decisions. Must be able to communicate effectively both orally and in writing. MLS III Bachelor of Science in Medical Technology (BSMT) / Medical Laboratory Scientist (BSMLS) or Bachelor of Science or higher degree, including sufficient biology and chemistry course credits in an ASCP approved discipline 3 years of clinical laboratory experience. ASCP or equivalent certification as a Medical Laboratory Scientist/Medical Technologist or have been grandfathered in before ASCP requirement. All staff, including BS/BA employees, must have Cytogenetics (ASCP), certification within 24 months of hire. MLS III Preferred Qualifications: BSMT or BSMLS degree or degree in Cytogenetics 5 years of Cytogenetics experience Previous MLS(ASCP) certification and/or related specialty such as MB(ASCP), in addition to required CG(ASCP) Evidence of excellent knowledge of clinical laboratory quality control practices such as having previous experience as a CAP inspector. Additional Information: Responsibilities: MLS I Conducts inventory counts on assigned areas, restocks supplies as needed, reports supplies to be ordered, and stores received supplies per storage requirements and regulations. Interacts with staff from various departments to coordinate the proper acquisition, testing, and reporting of patient test results. Performs function checks on analyzers, lab equipment and automation equipment. Completes machine maintenance, calibrations, and troubleshoots problems as required. Works with service representatives as needed to facilitate instrument repairs. Perform other duties as needed. MLS II Assists Medical Director and supervisor with analyzing and implementing new tests. Performs additional studies as required for quality assurance initiatives, research support or verification/validation of new equipment or methods. Completes validation and verification of new instrumentation and testing. Ensures the accuracy of instrument calibration and that preventative maintenance is performed. Leads training for new employees, students, and residents and performs employee competencies as assigned. Serves as a resource to assist other technologists in the Microbiology Laboratory. Maintains all aspects of quality control and quality assurance, assesses for acceptability, and takes corrective action as required. Performs testing of patient samples, interprets, reviews, and prepares patient test results for review by the Supervisor and/or Medical Director. Interacts with staff from various departments to coordinate the proper acquisition, testing, and reporting of patient test results. Performs other duties as assigned. MLS III Oversees daily operations in area of responsibility, ensuring adequate staff of demonstrated competency is available to meet the workload. Adjusts staff and testing priorities as required. Supervises and provides general oversight to staff. Contributes to the development of job descriptions, screens and interviews potential hires, trains staff, and engages in ongoing disciplinary actions as needed. Implements projects, establishes schedules, and assigns staff as needed to meet project requirements as it relates to quality initiatives, research, or validation studies. Adheres to department budget goals by overseeing the purchasing of supplies, ensuring adequate inventory is on hand to meet operational needs. Oversees compliance with regulatory requirements of accrediting agencies such as the College of American Pathologists (CAP), Joint Commission on Accreditation of Healthcare Organizations (JCAHO), Food and Drug Administration (FDA), and Clinical Laboratory Improvement Amendments (CLIA). Participates in CAP inspections both as a direct contact for inspections and as an inspector for other facilities. Completes required testing on the bench including maintenance, quality control, and function checks as needed. Performs other duties as assigned. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS: Stand: Frequently Sit: Frequently Walk: Occasionally Bend, crawl, crouch, kneel, stoop or reach overhead: Frequently Lift and carry weight: 25 lbs Push and pull weight: 25 lbs Use hands to touch, handle or feel: Frequently Talk: Continuously Hear: Continuously Taste or smell: Occasionally Read, concentrate, think analytically: Continuously Physical Environment : Inside Medical Facility Environment Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Benton/Manager--Supply-Chain---UAMS-Health-Benton-Bryant_R0091164-1": {"title": "Manager, Supply Chain \u2013 UAMS Health Benton/Bryant", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/17/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Shift Vary (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: INA | Institutional Admin Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Manager, Supply Chain oversees supply chain operations to ensure the efficient availability, management, and distribution of supplies throughout the UAMS Health Benton/Bryant location. This position is responsible for inventory management, purchasing coordination, product standardization, cost containment, and supply availability while supporting clinical and operational needs. The Manager partners with department leadership, vendors, and other stakeholders to optimize inventory levels, maintain appropriate controls, identify cost-saving opportunities, and ensure supply chain practices support quality patient care. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's Degree Plus 4 years' experience in supply management, preferably healthcare related, including a minimum two years in a supervisory capacity OR High School Diploma plus 8 years of experience in supply management, preferably healthcare related, including 2 years in a supervisory capacity. \u200b Knowledge of medical supplies and inventory control is required. Preferred Qualifications: Five (5) or more years of experience in healthcare supply management. Additional Information: Responsibilities: Manages daily supply chain and inventory operations , including ordering, receiving, stocking, replenishment, distribution and management of stock supplies. Establishes and maintains appropriate inventory and PAR levels based on utilization, operational needs, lead times, and other relevant factors to ensure adequate supply availability while minimizing excess inventory and waste. Monitors and improves inventory performance , including inventory accuracy, product utilization, stock rotation, expiration management, cycle counts, and physical inventory processes. Partners with clinical and operational leaders to evaluate supply needs, coordinate non-standard product requests, support product standardization, and identify cost-effective and contract-compliant alternatives without compromising patient care. Provides leadership and supervision to assigned staff , including hiring, training, performance management, scheduling, coaching, and addressing employee performance or operational concerns. Coordinates with vendors, purchasing, clinical departments, and other stakeholders to resolve supply and logistical issues, maintain product availability, and support effective supply chain operations. Identifies and implements opportunities for operational improvement and cost containment by evaluating processes, utilization, inventory practices, service levels, and supply chain performance metrics. Physical Requirements: Medium Work | Exerting up to 50 pounds of force occasionally, and/or up to 30 pounds of force frequently, and/or up to 10 pounds of force constantly to move objects. The Employee is required to have visual acuity to determine the accuracy, neatness, and thoroughness of the work assigned (i.e., custodial, general laborer, lab personnel, etc.) or to make general observations of facilities or structures (i.e., security guard). The employee is not substantially exposed to adverse environmental conditions (such as in typical office or administrative work). Constant physical activities: Standing; Talking; Walking Frequent physical activities: Crawling; Crouching; Stooping Occasional physical activities: Sitting Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience. Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Fire-Alarm-System-Technician_R0087275-1": {"title": "Fire Alarm System Technician", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 10/03/2026 Type of Position: Professional Staff - Facilities Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: OPS | Campus Operation EO Fire Alarms Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: This position is responsible for the maintenance and repair of the fire alarm systems and pneumatic tube system that serve the medical, educational, and research facilities on the UAMS Campus. These systems are vital to the safety, comfort, and general wellbeing of patients, students and employees. This position is also responsible for assisting with all problems and/or emergencies relating to facility issues on the UAMS Campus. The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. All UAMS employees will treat others with Dignity and Respect. We communicate and share complete and unbiased information, assuring our colleagues receive timely, complete, and accurate information in order make informed decisions. We participate in institutional initiatives and encourage the participation of others. We collaborate in policy and program development, implementation, and evaluation using best practices in delivering quality service. All duties will be performed in accordance with the UAMS Core Concepts of Patient and Family Centered Care set forth by UAMS. These core concepts allow for an approach to health care that shapes policies, programs, facility design and staff day-to-day interactions. It leads to better health outcomes and wiser allocation of resources, and greater patient and family satisfaction. The core concepts of patient and family centered care consist of Dignity & Respect, Information Sharing, Participation, and Collaboration. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: HS diploma/GED Technical degree in electronics or similar may be accepted in lieu of experience 5 years of fire alarm maintenance experience Valid driver\u2019s license with fewer than 12 points on their Motor Vehicle Record NICET Level 1 Certification State of Arkansas Alarm Systems Technician License Computer program proficiency level: Intermediate Thorough understanding of NFPA and experience with various fire alarm manufacturers Preferred Qualifications: Technical degree in electronics or similar 10 plus years of fire alarm maintenance experience NICET Level 2, 3, or 4 Certification Arkansas Journeyman Electrical License Swisslog Certificate of Training for Pneumatic Tube Systems Additional Information: Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Criminal Background Check This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: Crawling, Crouching, Feeling, Hearing, Kneeling, Reaching, Standing, Stooping, Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Sitting Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Hot-Springs/Horticulture-Assistant---Garvan-Woodland-Gardens_R0090941-1": {"title": "Horticulture Assistant \u2013 Garvan Woodland Gardens", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com, then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at all University of Arkansas institutions will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students.\u201d University of Arkansas, Fayetteville students will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Student Jobs at UAF.\u201d All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. Closing Date: 11/06/2026 Type of Position: Staff - Clerical Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas, Fayetteville Founded in 1871, the University of Arkansas is a land grant institution, classified by the Carnegie Foundation among the nation\u2019s top 2 percent of universities with the highest level of research activity. The University of Arkansas works to advance the state and build a better world through education, research, and outreach by providing transformational opportunities and skills, fostering a welcoming climate, and nurturing creativity, discovery, and the spread of new ideas and innovations. The University of Arkansas campus is located in Fayetteville, a welcoming community ranked as one of the best places to live in the U.S. The growing region surrounding Fayetteville is home to numerous Fortune 500 companies and one of the nation\u2019s strongest economies. Northwest Arkansas is also quickly gaining a national reputation for its focus on the arts and overall quality of life. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10% of employee salary. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions, you should review before applying for the opening. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process, please submit a request via the Disability Accommodations | OEOC | University of Arkansas (uark.edu) : Request an Accommodation. Appli\u00adcants are required to submit a request for each position of which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 479.575.5351. Department: Horticulture Operations Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Garvan Woodland Gardens, one of the top attractions in Arkansas is hiring! We are looking for positive, motivated, personable new team members to join our crew. Work outdoors in a setting voted in the top 10 most colorful places on the planet by Trip Advisor. We would love for you to come grow with us! Garvan Woodland Gardens, a 210-acre botanical garden situated on a peninsula surrounded by scenic Lake Hamilton located in Hot Springs, AR is seeking a skilled and dedicated Horticulture Assistant. The Horticulture Assistant will be responsible for weeding, watering, mulching, tilling, raking, planting, removing plantings, and other duties as assigned. This position requires physical work outside year-round. This team member will be expected to work well with others and under the supervision of an experienced staff member. Pay $13-15 per hour based on experience and skill level. Landscape Maintenance Technician is a part-time, temporary position limited to the 1250-hour University of Arkansas policy. The campus is a non-smoking facility. This position requires a valid driver\u2019s license. Some night and weekend work will be required seasonally. Regular, reliable, and non-disruptive attendance is an essential job duty, as is the ability to create and maintain collegial, harmonious working relationships with others. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: High School Diploma or equivalent Valid Driver\u2019s License Background Checks Required: Criminal Background Check, Motor Vehicle Reports Check, Sex Offender Registry Must be able to lift 30 pounds No previous experience required as individuals will be trained on site Preferred Qualifications: Experience working in a public garden Experience with planting, gardening, landscaping, etc. is preferred Formal education in horticulture or a related field Additional Information: Graduate students are subject to background check. Salary Information: $13 - 16 per hour Required Documents to Apply: None Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Recruitment Contact Information: Leslie Pounds, HR Partner, pounds@uark.edu; Minnie Hahn, Sr Manager, minnie@uark.edu; Heather Boyett, Business Coordinator, hd024@uark.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Special Instructions to Applicants: Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas seeks to attract, develop and retain high quality faculty, staff and administrators that consistently display practices and behaviors to advance a culture that embeds equal opportunity, educational excellence and unparalleled access for all. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All Application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Crouching, Kneeling, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Repetitive Motion, Standing, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Balancing, Feeling, Grasping, Hearing, Lifting, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Stooping, Talking Occasional Physical Activity: Climbing, Crawling, Sitting Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAM--McGehee-Campus/Workforce-Ed-Part-Time-Faculty_R0091099-1": {"title": "Workforce Ed Part-Time Faculty", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Faculty - Non-Tenure (Workforce Ed) Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Monticello UAM, one of twenty campuses of the University of Arkansas System, is located in southeastern Arkansas in the beautiful timberlands, rich in outdoor recreation activities, and approximately 100 miles south of Little Rock. UAM is a comprehensive, residential and commuter, undergraduate institution also offering selected master\u2019s degree programs. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please submit a request via the OEOC website: \u00a0Applicants are required to submit a request for each position to which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 870-460-1422 . Department: Instruction Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Primary duties include teaching a variety of technical courses. In addition to teaching, the employee will be responsible for developing instructional and lab activities; maintaining program and student records; coordinating and supervising internship/practicum assignments, assisting with maintaining program approval and other duties as assigned. Evening and/or summer hours may be required. Qualifications: Formal education of master\u2019s degree in the discipline or bachelor\u2019s degree plus two years of experience in higher education. \u00a0 Additional Information: Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience. Required Documents to Apply: List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume, Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Elaine Hargraves, Assistant Vice Chancellor, hargravese@uamont.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Child Maltreatment, Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Feeling, Grasping, Hearing, Kneeling, Reaching, Standing, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Hearing, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Pulling, Pushing, Stooping Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Diagnostic-Radiology-Technologist-Part-Time---Rodney-Parham-Orthopedic-Clinic_R0091036-1": {"title": "Diagnostic Radiology Technologist Part-Time - Rodney Parham Orthopedic Clinic", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 10/03/2026 Type of Position: Clinical Staff - Medical Ancillary Support Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | MUSL Ambulatory Clinic PRN Staff (Jacob Allen Mitchell) Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Radiology Technician is responsible for maintaining and using equipment and supplies that image portions of the human body on x-ray film or fluoroscopic screens. This position is governed by state and federal law and agency policy. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Associate's Degree Plus Graduate from a 2-year certificate program certified by the ASRT in Radiology Technology Registered or eligible by the American Registry of Radiologic Technologists Licensed or eligible for license by the State of Arkansas in Radiology Technology \u200b Preferred Qualifications: CPR certified Additional Information: Responsibilities: Operates and positions radiologic equipment to produce images of the body for diagnostic purposes and according to exam specifications, following established radiologic requirements and regulations to ensure patient care and safety. Prepares patients for radiologic procedures by escorting patients to x-ray rooms, providing verbal instructions, and assisting patients in positioning body parts to be radiographed; explains procedures and observes patients to ensure patient care, safety and comfort during scan. Serves as a back-up for clinical team members, as needed, by controlling patient flow and triaging. Maintains working order of radiologic equipment including reporting equipment malfunctions and scheduling regular maintenance. Reviews patient records and imports external images into the picture archiving and communication system (PACS). Performs other duties as assigned. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Criminal Background Check, Motor Vehicle Reports Check This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Grasping, Lifting, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching Occasional Physical Activity: Stooping Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Project-Coordinator---Perioperative-Care-Services_R0090981-1": {"title": "Project Coordinator - Perioperative Care Services", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/17/2026 Type of Position: Professional Staff - Project/Program Administration Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | PERIOP PROJECT ADMIN Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Within the Perioperative Care Services Division, the Clinical and Operational Performance Project Coordinator provides support and coordination of all clinical and operational analytics as well as performance improvement projects. The Periop Project Coordinator has experience in data management and analysis, performance improvement, creation of actionable reports and management of complex projects in diverse clinical and operational realms. This team member utilizes data in problem identification and resolution. Effective communication techniques are a necessity as well as the ability to effectively translate information to team members inclusive of all levels of education, background and disciplines. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelors degree in health, business or related field or HS plus four (4) years of project coordination or administrative support experience. Preferrred Qualifications: 3 year of project management experience Effective communication and interpersonal skills; ability to present to large audiences effectively Strong skills in MS Office, database software and analytics software Upon request, must be able to provide samples demonstrating proficiency in areas indicated above as well as technical writing and presentations Additional Information: Responsibilities: Ensures organizational data requirements are captured, reported, and managed according to UAMS regulations Responsible for coordinating improvement initiatives as outlined by the organization, regulatory bodies, and Perioperative Care Services Coordinates tracking and resolution of safety submissions Coordinates and standing audits and subsequent findings/actions Operational Processes and Performance Provides operational reporting, inclusive of all daily, weekly, monthly, quarterly, and annual analyses of efficiency and productivity metrics Identifies and disseminates evidence for performance improvement activities Conducts on-site and front-line studies to gather objective and subjective information to support projects involving operational change and improvement Serves as a resource to all Perioperative team members and stakeholders Provides performance improvement consultative support to the leadership team, physicians, residents, and all Perioperative Care Services employees Is visible and accessible in the patient care setting Supports the financial and administrative team in the management of productivity, revenue, and budgetary metrics. May perform other duties as assigned. Salary Information: commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Criminal Background Check, Substance Abuse Testing This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Standing, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Sitting, Stooping Occasional Physical Activity: Grasping, Kneeling, Repetitive Motion, Sharps Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Surgical-Scrub-Technician---Main-OR_R0090948-1": {"title": "Surgical/Scrub Technician - Main OR", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/17/2026 Type of Position: Clinical Staff - Medical Ancillary Support Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | PeriopSvc Main Operating Room Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Summary Of Job Duties The Surgical/Scrub Technician will assemble supplies for surgical procedures, set up and maintain the sterile field, pass surgical instruments, and assist in room preparation. This professional nursing role will require the ability to coordinate care for the needs of the surgical case, the surgeon, nurses, and other members of the team to provide an optimal outcome for the patient and work collaboratively with clinic providers, fellows, and staff. Requires the ability to effectively communicate. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: High School Diploma or GED Plus\u00a0Graduate of an NBSTSA-accredited Surgical Technology program OR NCCT-approved Surgical Technology program\u00a0OR Completed military surgical/scrub tech training OR Have two or more years of on-the-job surgical/scrub experience in an acute care facility or ambulatory surgery center Preferred Qualifications: 1 year of operating room experience Scrub Tech Certification Additional Information: Employees in this role must be fitted for, capable of donning, and performing routine tasks in personal protective equipment, to include N95 masks, Powered Air Purifying Respirators (PAPR), or Controlled Air Purifying Respirators (CAPR). Responsibilities: Ensures availability of appropriate instrumentation, supplies and equipment for assigned cases.\u00a0 Ensures that the room has been prepared for the upcoming cases, with appropriate equipment available and ready for surgical use.\u00a0 Ensures that the instruments are cleaned arranged and transported to the soiled workroom according to department policy; independently assists with instrument reprocessing tasks when assigned cases are completed and time permits; Ensures that the operating rooms are case-ready for the following day\u2019s cases;\u00a0 Exhibits practical knowledge of OR equipment including maintenance and safety aspects.\u00a0 Utilizes available communication tools; Demonstrates teamwork by offering assistance to other team members;\u00a0 Shares knowledge information and expertise with other staff; attends departmental in-services and other educational offerings; Consistently demonstrates new knowledge and skills through incorporation into actual clinical practice. Willing to learn new techniques. With any other duties assigned Salary Information: commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Criminal Background Check, Substance Abuse Testing This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Standing, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Sitting, Stooping Occasional Physical Activity: Grasping, Kneeling, Repetitive Motion, Sharps Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Medical-Laboratory-Scientist-II---HLA_R0091068-1": {"title": "Medical Laboratory Scientist II - HLA", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/17/2026 Type of Position: Clinical Staff - Medical Ancillary Support Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | LPSL CPATH Human Lympho Antibodies Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: This position will work under the supervision and direction of the HLA laboratory supervisor. MLS II in the HLA laboratory performs a variety of technical procedures including HLA typing by rSSO and next generation sequencing methods, Luminex based HLA Antibody identification, and donor/recipient flow cytometric cross-matching. They are expected to keep all instrumentation in good working order and identify and notify the supervisor or lead tech of instrument malfunctions. The MLS II also performs quality assurance metric studies, and training/competency assessments. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor of Science degree in Medical Laboratory Science, Medical Technology, Chemistry, or Biology Valid ASCP (or equivalent) certification 2 years of clinical laboratory experience Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor of Science degree in Medical Laboratory Science Previous HLA lab experience Additional Information: Job Requirements: Perform complex HLA and histocompatibility testing on patient and donor specimens. Perform HLA typing using molecular and serologic methodologies as applicable. Conduct antibody screening, identification, and other transplant-related immunologic testing. Perform crossmatching and compatibility testing for organ and tissue transplantation. Process and evaluate specimens according to established laboratory procedures. Operate, calibrate, troubleshoot, and maintain specialized laboratory equipment. Analyze and interpret complex test results and recognize clinically significant findings. Review, validate, and accurately report laboratory results within established turnaround times. Perform quality control and quality assurance activities and investigate unacceptable results. Assist with validation, verification, and implementation of new testing methodologies. Maintain accurate documentation, worksheets, test records, and quality-control records. Participate in proficiency testing and regulatory compliance activities. Follow CAP, CLIA, laboratory, and applicable transplant/histocompatibility standards. Communicate critical or complex findings appropriately to pathologists, transplant teams, physicians, and other healthcare professionals. Assist with training, mentoring, and competency assessment of laboratory staff. Monitor inventory and ensure appropriate availability of reagents and supplies. Participate in process-improvement initiatives to improve accuracy, efficiency, and patient outcomes. Maintain patient confidentiality and adhere to all laboratory safety and infection-control procedures. Perform other duties as needed. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS Stand: Frequently Sit: Frequently Walk: Occasionally Bend, crawl, crouch, kneel, stoop or reach overhead: Frequently Lift and carry weight: 25 lbs Push and pull weight: 25 lbs Use hands to touch, handle or feel: Frequently Talk: Continuously Hear: Continuously Taste or smell: Occasionally Read, concentrate, think analytically: Continuously Physical Environment : Inside Medical Facility Environment Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), Proof of Veteran Status, Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Criminal Background Check, Substance Abuse Testing This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Feeling, Grasping, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Repetitive Motion, Sharps, Sitting, Standing Frequent Physical Activity: Hearing, Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Kneeling, Lifting, Pulling, Pushing, Stooping Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-Arkansas-at-Pine-Bluff/Extra-Help-Research-Assistant---Horticulture---Nutraceuticals-Lab_R0091071": {"title": "Extra Help Research Assistant - Horticulture & Nutraceuticals Lab", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Research Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff The University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff is an 1890 Land-Grant HBCU with a diverse student population, competitive degree offerings and stellar faculty. For more than 140 years, the University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff has worked to create an environment that inculcates learning, growth and productivity while affording a basic need to its students \u2013 a chance to advance. The 15:1 student to teacher ratio makes it possible to maintain a learning environment with close interaction between students and faculty while challenging curricula encourage our students to seek and fulfill their potential. You can excel in your chosen field of study through a curriculum of \u00a0 Certificate and Associates degree programs,\u00a0 more than thirty\u00a0 Undergraduate programs, Master\u2019s degree programs and a Doctorate program in Aquaculture/Fisheries. You can also develop workplace readiness through internships, co-ops and fellowships in the U.S. and abroad. Out-of-class experiences and student involvement include more than 90 student organizations, an internationally renowned Vesper Choir, Marching Band, Concert Bands, Wind Symphony, nationally recognized debate team, award-winning theater department and accomplished athletic program. Though the main campus is in Pine Bluff, its reach is worldwide. UAPB has an extended campus in North Little Rock and offers as well as online courses. With the addition of the Arkansas Research and Education Optical Network (ARE-ON), students can engage in information exchange with others anywhere in the world. There are also Research and Extension offices in Lonoke, Newport and Lake Village and collaborations with other colleges and universities in the State through the National Science Foundation funded STEM (Science, Technology, Engineering and Mathematics) Academy. As the second oldest land-grant institution in the state of Arkansas, the mission of this No Excuse University remains the same \u2013 to provide a high quality, affordable education with a personal touch. We invite you to Become a Part of the Pride at the University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process and require reasonable accommodations, please contact Human Resources at 870.575.8400 . Department: Plant Science Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: We are seeking an energetic, motivated, and dependable Research Assistant (part-time) to join our research team. Responsibilities: The successful candidate will assist with field, greenhouse, and laboratory research involving horticultural crops, plant production, sample collection, nutritional and phytochemical analyses, data collection, and other research-related activities as assigned by the supervisor. Position: Research Assistant (Part-Time) Qualifications: Qualifications: \u2022 B.S. or M.S. degree in Horticulture, Plant Science, Food Science, Nutrition, Biology, Chemistry, Biotechnology, or a related field \u2022 Strong interest in horticulture and nutraceutical research \u2022 Willingness to work actively in field, greenhouse, and laboratory environments \u2022 Energetic, hardworking, responsible, and willing to learn \u2022 Ability to work independently and as part of a research team Additional Information: Salary Information: $14.00 hourly Required Documents to Apply: Resume, Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants (Please upload all required documents in the \"Resume\" attachment section of your application to be considered for this position) : Recruitment Contact Information: Sharron Williams All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Motor Vehicle Reports Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff may conduct pre-employment background checks on certain positions for applicants being considered for employment. \u00a0 The background checks may include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. \u00a0 Required checks are identified in the position listing. \u00a0 A criminal background check or arrest pending adjudication information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absences of a relationship to the requirements of the position. \u00a0 Background check information will be used in a consistent, non-discriminatory manner consistent with the state and federal law. \u00a0 The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-Arkansas-at-Pine-Bluff/Instructor-Counselor_R0090250": {"title": "Instructor/Counselor", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Faculty - Non-Tenure Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff The University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff is an 1890 Land-Grant HBCU with a diverse student population, competitive degree offerings and stellar faculty. For more than 140 years, the University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff has worked to create an environment that inculcates learning, growth and productivity while affording a basic need to its students \u2013 a chance to advance. The 15:1 student to teacher ratio makes it possible to maintain a learning environment with close interaction between students and faculty while challenging curricula encourage our students to seek and fulfill their potential. You can excel in your chosen field of study through a curriculum of \u00a0 Certificate and Associates degree programs,\u00a0 more than thirty\u00a0 Undergraduate programs, Master\u2019s degree programs and a Doctorate program in Aquaculture/Fisheries. You can also develop workplace readiness through internships, co-ops and fellowships in the U.S. and abroad. Out-of-class experiences and student involvement include more than 90 student organizations, an internationally renowned Vesper Choir, Marching Band, Concert Bands, Wind Symphony, nationally recognized debate team, award-winning theater department and accomplished athletic program. Though the main campus is in Pine Bluff, its reach is worldwide. UAPB has an extended campus in North Little Rock and offers as well as online courses. With the addition of the Arkansas Research and Education Optical Network (ARE-ON), students can engage in information exchange with others anywhere in the world. There are also Research and Extension offices in Lonoke, Newport and Lake Village and collaborations with other colleges and universities in the State through the National Science Foundation funded STEM (Science, Technology, Engineering and Mathematics) Academy. As the second oldest land-grant institution in the state of Arkansas, the mission of this No Excuse University remains the same \u2013 to provide a high quality, affordable education with a personal touch. We invite you to Become a Part of the Pride at the University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process and require reasonable accommodations, please contact Human Resources at 870.575.8400 . Department: Center for Student Success and Academic Excellence | Undergraduate Academic Advising | Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The responsibilities of the Instructor/Counselor include: *Providing developmental and intrusive advising; *Determining placement and registering freshman students for courses; *Maintaining files and tracking first-year students; *Consulting with faculty and staff on behalf of individual students; *Making referrals for support services as needed; *Assisting in the planning and implementation of new student orientation; *Providing classroom instruction and student-development workshops; *Performing classroom and related research deemed necessary for the area; *Serving as advisor to student organizations; *Serving on University committees; *Assisting in departmental recruitment and retention programs; and *Assisting in developing and expanding innovative programs to improve student transition, achievement, and persistence in college. Qualifications: The candidate must hold a Master's degree in guidance counseling, education, or related field. It is preferred that the candidate have two or more years of experience in teaching or advising students. It is also preferred that the Instructor/Counselor have knowledge and skills in Microsoft, serve as a team player, promote excellent written and oral communication skills, promote interpersonal skills, and organizational skills. Additional Information: N/A Salary Information: 35,000.00 Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Letters of Recommendation, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume, Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants (Please upload all required documents in the \"Resume\" attachment section of your application to be considered for this position) : Recruitment Contact Information: Sharron Williams Employment Manager 870-575-8403 williamssm@uapb.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Child Maltreatment, Criminal Background Check, Motor Vehicle Reports Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff may conduct pre-employment background checks on certain positions for applicants being considered for employment. \u00a0 The background checks may include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. \u00a0 Required checks are identified in the position listing. \u00a0 A criminal background check or arrest pending adjudication information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absences of a relationship to the requirements of the position. \u00a0 Background check information will be used in a consistent, non-discriminatory manner consistent with the state and federal law. \u00a0 The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Hearing, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Hearing, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAPBSIMMONSSimmons-Bank-Field/Academic-Counselor_R0090666": {"title": "Academic Counselor", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Education Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff The University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff is an 1890 Land-Grant HBCU with a diverse student population, competitive degree offerings and stellar faculty. For more than 140 years, the University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff has worked to create an environment that inculcates learning, growth and productivity while affording a basic need to its students \u2013 a chance to advance. The 15:1 student to teacher ratio makes it possible to maintain a learning environment with close interaction between students and faculty while challenging curricula encourage our students to seek and fulfill their potential. You can excel in your chosen field of study through a curriculum of \u00a0 Certificate and Associates degree programs,\u00a0 more than thirty\u00a0 Undergraduate programs, Master\u2019s degree programs and a Doctorate program in Aquaculture/Fisheries. You can also develop workplace readiness through internships, co-ops and fellowships in the U.S. and abroad. Out-of-class experiences and student involvement include more than 90 student organizations, an internationally renowned Vesper Choir, Marching Band, Concert Bands, Wind Symphony, nationally recognized debate team, award-winning theater department and accomplished athletic program. Though the main campus is in Pine Bluff, its reach is worldwide. UAPB has an extended campus in North Little Rock and offers as well as online courses. With the addition of the Arkansas Research and Education Optical Network (ARE-ON), students can engage in information exchange with others anywhere in the world. There are also Research and Extension offices in Lonoke, Newport and Lake Village and collaborations with other colleges and universities in the State through the National Science Foundation funded STEM (Science, Technology, Engineering and Mathematics) Academy. As the second oldest land-grant institution in the state of Arkansas, the mission of this No Excuse University remains the same \u2013 to provide a high quality, affordable education with a personal touch. We invite you to Become a Part of the Pride at the University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process and require reasonable accommodations, please contact Human Resources at 870.575.8400 . Department: ATHL | Athletics Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: ) Implementing academic support to include: academic and career counseling for student-athletes, individual and team study sessions; tutoring services 30% Qualifications: (l) Managing the academic eligibility and progress towards degree requirements of student-athletes (Men & Women Track, Baseball, & Golf) 30% (2) Implementing academic support to include: academic and career counseling for student-athletes, individual and team study sessions; tutoring services 30% (3) Academic learning center oversight 20% (4) Developing and implementing successful student-athlete leadership and welfare programming 5% (5) Responsible for the University\u2019s, NCAA and conference reporting 10% (6) Assist coaches in evaluating prospects for NCAA academic eligibility and other duties as assigned 5% Additional Information: Salary Information: $40,000 - $45,000 Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume, Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants (Please upload all required documents in the \"Resume\" attachment section of your application to be considered for this position) : Recruitment Contact Information: Sharron Williams, Human Resources williamss@uapb.edu (870) 575-8403 All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check The University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff may conduct pre-employment background checks on certain positions for applicants being considered for employment. \u00a0 The background checks may include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. \u00a0 Required checks are identified in the position listing. \u00a0 A criminal background check or arrest pending adjudication information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absences of a relationship to the requirements of the position. \u00a0 Background check information will be used in a consistent, non-discriminatory manner consistent with the state and federal law. \u00a0 The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Talking Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAPBSIMMONSSimmons-Bank-Field/Assistant-Coach_R0090667": {"title": "Assistant Coach", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Professional Staff - Coach Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff The University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff is an 1890 Land-Grant HBCU with a diverse student population, competitive degree offerings and stellar faculty. For more than 140 years, the University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff has worked to create an environment that inculcates learning, growth and productivity while affording a basic need to its students \u2013 a chance to advance. The 15:1 student to teacher ratio makes it possible to maintain a learning environment with close interaction between students and faculty while challenging curricula encourage our students to seek and fulfill their potential. You can excel in your chosen field of study through a curriculum of \u00a0 Certificate and Associates degree programs,\u00a0 more than thirty\u00a0 Undergraduate programs, Master\u2019s degree programs and a Doctorate program in Aquaculture/Fisheries. You can also develop workplace readiness through internships, co-ops and fellowships in the U.S. and abroad. Out-of-class experiences and student involvement include more than 90 student organizations, an internationally renowned Vesper Choir, Marching Band, Concert Bands, Wind Symphony, nationally recognized debate team, award-winning theater department and accomplished athletic program. Though the main campus is in Pine Bluff, its reach is worldwide. UAPB has an extended campus in North Little Rock and offers as well as online courses. With the addition of the Arkansas Research and Education Optical Network (ARE-ON), students can engage in information exchange with others anywhere in the world. There are also Research and Extension offices in Lonoke, Newport and Lake Village and collaborations with other colleges and universities in the State through the National Science Foundation funded STEM (Science, Technology, Engineering and Mathematics) Academy. As the second oldest land-grant institution in the state of Arkansas, the mission of this No Excuse University remains the same \u2013 to provide a high quality, affordable education with a personal touch. We invite you to Become a Part of the Pride at the University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process and require reasonable accommodations, please contact Human Resources at 870.575.8400 . Department: ATHL | Athletics Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Assist head coach with practices, game planning. recruiting, scheduling and day to day game operations. Qualifications: Bachelor's degree Additional Information: Salary Information: $28,000 - $30,000 Required Documents to Apply: List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume, Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants (Please upload all required documents in the \"Resume\" attachment section of your application to be considered for this position) : Recruitment Contact Information: Sharron Williams, Human Resources williamssm@uapb.edu (870) 575-8403 All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check The University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff may conduct pre-employment background checks on certain positions for applicants being considered for employment. \u00a0 The background checks may include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. \u00a0 Required checks are identified in the position listing. \u00a0 A criminal background check or arrest pending adjudication information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absences of a relationship to the requirements of the position. \u00a0 Background check information will be used in a consistent, non-discriminatory manner consistent with the state and federal law. \u00a0 The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Kneeling, Reaching, Repetitive Motion, Standing, Stooping, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Orthopedic-Tech---Rodney-Parham-Orthopedic-Clinic_R0091051-1": {"title": "Orthopedic Tech - Rodney Parham Orthopedic Clinic", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/10/2026 Type of Position: Clinical Staff - Medical Ancillary Support Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | MUSL Autumn Clinic Nursing Staff (Jacob Allen Mitchell) Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Orthopedic Technician assists physicians in the application and management of casts and braces, provides instruction and assistance to resident physicians in cast, splint, and brace application, gives instruction on proper care of casts, braces, etc., to patients. Also provides instructions to rotating medical students, and assists with orders and maintains an adequate stock of orthopedic supplies. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: High School Diploma, GED PLUS\u00a0One (1) year direct patient care experience Preferred Qualifications: Medical Assistant or Orthopedic Tech experience Additional Information: Responsibilities: Educates patients regarding casts, splints, or braces following application Collects and records patients' medical history and acquires patient vital signs. Advises patients regarding treatment, medication, and specific physician instructions Collects lab samples and completes documentation for submission to lab Monitors inventory of and obtains necessary supplies and/or equipment for patient care in orthopedic unit Performs other duties as assigned Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Criminal Background Check, Substance Abuse Testing This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Feeling, Grasping, Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: Pulling, Pushing, Reaching Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Medical-Laboratory-Scientist-II--Flow-Cytometry_R0091058": {"title": "Medical Laboratory Scientist II- Flow Cytometry", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/17/2026 Type of Position: Clinical Staff - Medical Ancillary Support Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | LPSL CPATH Flow Cytometry Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Medical Laboratory Scientist II \u2013 Flow Cytometry performs complex laboratory testing and analysis of blood, bone marrow, tissue, and other clinical specimens using flow cytometry methodologies. This position is responsible for specimen processing, instrument operation, quality control, data analysis, and accurate reporting of results to support the diagnosis and monitoring of hematologic, immunologic, and other diseases Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor of Science Degree in Medical Laboratory Sciences, Medical Technology , Chemistry, or Biology Valid ASCP Certification Two or more years of experience working in a clinical laboratory Preferred Qualifications: Previous flow cytometry lab experience Additional Information: Job Requirements: This person will work under the supervision and direction of the Flow Cytometry supervisor. Duties include processing, staining and analyzing routine specimens. They will be expected to keep all instrumentation in good working order and identify and notify the supervisor of instrument malfunctions. They should be able to aid in instrument repair. They should be able to identify abnormal or discrepancy results. They will have limited participation in student teaching and assisting of other personnel rotating through the section. They will have limited administrative duties. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS Stand: Frequently Sit: Frequently Walk: Occasionally Bend, crawl, crouch, kneel, stoop or reach overhead: Frequently Lift and carry weight: 25 lbs Push and pull weight: 25 lbs Use hands to touch, handle or feel: Frequently Talk: Continuously Hear: Continuously Taste or smell: Occasionally Read, concentrate, think analytically: Continuously Physical Environment : Inside Medical Facility Environment Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), Proof of Veteran Status, Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Criminal Background Check, Substance Abuse Testing This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding Frequent Physical Activity: Feeling, Grasping, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Repetitive Motion, Sharps, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Crouching, Kneeling, Lifting, Stooping Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Orthopedic-Tech-PRN---Ambulatory_R0091039-1": {"title": "Orthopedic Tech PRN - Ambulatory", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/10/2026 Type of Position: Clinical Staff - Medical Ancillary Support Job Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | MUSL Ambulatory Clinic PRN Staff (Jacob Allen Mitchell) Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Orthopedic Tech assists physicians in the application and management of casts and braces, provides instruction and assistance to resident physicians in cast, splint, and brace application, gives instruction on proper care of casts, braces, etc to patients. Also provides instructions to rotating medical students, and assists with orders and maintains an adequate stock of orthopaedic supplies. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: High School Diploma or GED, Plus One (1) year of direct patient care experience. BLS required within 90 days of hire date. Preferred Qualifications: Experience as an Orthopedic Technician Orthopedic Technician certification Additional Information: Responsibilities: Provides professional and competent assistance to physicians with the application and management of casts for patients with orthopaedic problems.\u00a0 Provides technical instruction to resident physicians and medical students in the area of application of orthopaedic devices. \u00a0 Ensures that casts, splints, and other devices are properly fitted and educates patients on proper healthcare practices. \u00a0 \u00a0Provides patient instructions and teaching on their casts, splint, and/or brace following application. \u00a0 Administrative Care Provides coverage for the Orthopaedic Clinic, patient care floors, operating room, and emergency room as requested. \u00a0 Will be required to work in an on-call capacity as needed. \u00a0 Obtains necessary supplies and/or equipment for patient care in the orthopedic clinic. Attends mandatory in-services and clinic staff meetings. \u00a0Participates in orientation with new staff.\u00a0 Performs other duties as assigned. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Criminal Background Check, Substance Abuse Testing This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Crouching, Feeling, Grasping, Kneeling, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding Frequent Physical Activity: Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAPBFACILITIESFacilities-Management/Administrative-Specialist-III_R0090126": {"title": "Administrative Specialist III", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Clerical Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff The University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff is an 1890 Land-Grant HBCU with a diverse student population, competitive degree offerings and stellar faculty. For more than 140 years, the University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff has worked to create an environment that inculcates learning, growth and productivity while affording a basic need to its students \u2013 a chance to advance. The 15:1 student to teacher ratio makes it possible to maintain a learning environment with close interaction between students and faculty while challenging curricula encourage our students to seek and fulfill their potential. You can excel in your chosen field of study through a curriculum of \u00a0 Certificate and Associates degree programs,\u00a0 more than thirty\u00a0 Undergraduate programs, Master\u2019s degree programs and a Doctorate program in Aquaculture/Fisheries. You can also develop workplace readiness through internships, co-ops and fellowships in the U.S. and abroad. Out-of-class experiences and student involvement include more than 90 student organizations, an internationally renowned Vesper Choir, Marching Band, Concert Bands, Wind Symphony, nationally recognized debate team, award-winning theater department and accomplished athletic program. Though the main campus is in Pine Bluff, its reach is worldwide. UAPB has an extended campus in North Little Rock and offers as well as online courses. With the addition of the Arkansas Research and Education Optical Network (ARE-ON), students can engage in information exchange with others anywhere in the world. There are also Research and Extension offices in Lonoke, Newport and Lake Village and collaborations with other colleges and universities in the State through the National Science Foundation funded STEM (Science, Technology, Engineering and Mathematics) Academy. As the second oldest land-grant institution in the state of Arkansas, the mission of this No Excuse University remains the same \u2013 to provide a high quality, affordable education with a personal touch. We invite you to Become a Part of the Pride at the University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process and require reasonable accommodations, please contact Human Resources at 870.575.8400 . Department: Motor Pool Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Researches and analyzes data pertinent to work programs and/or agency/institution goals and objectives and prepares reports explaining findings and recommendations. Assists in developing or revising policies, procedures, and directives based on research findings; submits to supervisor for approval. Compiles financial information used by supervisor to formulate budget proposals and monitors expenditures to ensure optimum operating efficiency. Reviews and answers or prepares correspondence relating to agency/institution programs. Interprets agency administrative directives, policies, and procedures to ensure consistent application. Provides information, assistance, and clarifications to interested parties concerning agency/institution programs, policies, and procedures. Assists supervisor by maintaining leave records, appointment calendar, and prioritizing incoming correspondence. May supervise a small to medium-sized administrative support staff and evaluate the work performance of incumbents. Performs other duties as assigned. Qualifications: Qualifications The formal education equivalent of a high school diploma; plus one year of specialized training in business management, business education, or a related field; plus two years of experience in a specialized or a related field applicable to work performed. Additional Information: Salary Information: 27,803 to 30,000 Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants (Please upload all required documents in the \"Resume\" attachment section of your application to be considered for this position) : Recruitment Contact Information: Sharron Williams, Employment Manager, Human Resources williamssm@uapb.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Motor Vehicle Reports Check The University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff may conduct pre-employment background checks on certain positions for applicants being considered for employment. \u00a0 The background checks may include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. \u00a0 Required checks are identified in the position listing. \u00a0 A criminal background check or arrest pending adjudication information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absences of a relationship to the requirements of the position. \u00a0 Background check information will be used in a consistent, non-discriminatory manner consistent with the state and federal law. \u00a0 The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Feeling, Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting, Talking Occasional Physical Activity: Driving, Lifting, Pulling, Pushing Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/HR-Business-Partner_R0091042": {"title": "HR Business Partner", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Human Resources Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Little Rock The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is a metropolitan research university that provides an accessible, quality education through flexible learning and unparalleled internship opportunities. At UA Little Rock, we prepare our more than 8,900 students to be innovators and responsible leaders in their fields. Committed to its metropolitan research university mission, UA Little Rock is a driving force in Little Rock's thriving cultural community and a major component of the city and state's growing profile as a regional leader in research, technology transfer, economic development, and job creation. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . Department: HCM Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The HR Business Partner works proactively with designated department and college administrators, faculty and staff to provide guidance and advice on most HR-related issues. This position will assist in addressing a variety of HR services including, but not limited to, recruitment, onboarding, compensation, performance management, job analysis, benefits, employee relations, disciplinary process, employee leave, and Workday processes. This position will act as the initial point of contact for all HR matters for the designated departments and colleges. This position is governed by state and federal laws and agency/institution policy. Qualifications: Required Education and/or Experience: Bachelor\u2019s Degree with at least 3 years of human resources experience. Preferred Education and/or Experience: Master\u2019s Degree with 5 years of human resources experience; experience working with Workday; university experience preferred. Job Duties and Responsibilities: Advise designated departments and colleges on the administration of human resources policies and procedures; Advise appropriate HR personnel of any recurring issues or problems within the designated departments and colleges; Establish and build rapport with designated department and college administrators, faculty, and staff; Provide advice and make recommendations for the resolution of daily issues for assigned departments and colleges; Ensure business practices are in accordance with human resources policies and labor laws; Act as an internal consultant by analyzing and recommending solutions to human resource issues within the assigned departments and colleges; Ensure departments and colleges follow established policies and procedures and are in compliance with any relevant federal, state, or local legislation; Prepare and maintain special internal and external reports as requested; Assist with developing, coordinating, and recommending changes for the improvement of HR workflow and procedures in the assigned departments and colleges; Develop procedures for compiling and analyzing data for reports and special projects; Participate in professional development sessions or seminars; Present training sessions related to the assigned departments and colleges; Keep abreast of new trends and advancements in the human resources field; Perform other related duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Knowledge of personnel, payroll, and budget processes, policies, and procedures; Superior planning and organizational skills; Knowledge of the principles and legal requirements in human resource management, recruitment, and hiring in higher education; Knowledge of all university benefits plans; Excellent communication skills to include the ability to prepare, present, and review oral and written information, reports, and programs; Excellent critical thinking and reasoning skills; Excellent interpersonal skills; Ability to maintain professionalism at all times; Ability to address sensitive employee issues; Ability to determine the most appropriate approach in employee relations matters; Must maintain the confidentiality of company documents and information; Ability to work independently, be self-motivated, and demonstrate a \u201ccan-do\u201d attitude; Ability to manage multiple tasks and priorities; Willingness to convert to a schedule which will include early morning, evening, and possibly weekend work, if needed; Thrive in a work environment that has periods of high demand; Ability to sustain intentional superior customer service; Ability to be flexible with frequent changes of state, federal, and university policies, and procedures; Ability to promote diversity, inclusiveness & cultural awareness. Additional Information: Salary Information: $55,000 Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Michele Curd Director of Human Capital Management & HR Business Partners rmcurd@ualr.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Kneeling, Lifting, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Repetitive Motion, Sitting, Standing, Stooping, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Repetitive Motion, Sitting, Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Crouching, Grasping, Kneeling, Lifting, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Stooping Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Certified-Nurse-Midwife--CNM---APRN_R0091057-1": {"title": "Certified Nurse-Midwife (CNM), APRN", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/17/2026 Type of Position: Clinical Staff - Nursing Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Shift Vary (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | WISL CNM IP C Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Certified Nurse-Midwife (CNM), APRN provides antepartum, intrapartum and postpartum and women\u2019s health patient care services. The CNM will be expected to provide women\u2019s health, prenatal and postpartum care to women in selected clinic settings, triage women who present to Labor and Delivery, and to manage the care of essentially healthy women admitted in labor, delivery and postpartum. CNMs provide comprehensive health assessments, determine diagnoses, implement treatment plans, prescribe medical treatments and manage health issues for patients independently or in collaboration with the designated physicians. The CNM will work autonomously as well as in collaboration with a variety of individuals to diagnose and manage patients' health care problems, and will serve as a health care resource interdisciplinary consultant, and patient advocate. The CNM coordinates the multidisciplinary care of patients, facilitating all necessary consults, assuring that care is timely and appropriate. The CNM teaches aspects of midwifery and obstetric care and services to medical, nursing and midwifery students and participates in research initiatives led by the Women and Infants Service Line. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Valid License as an APRN by the State of Arkansas Required and National Board Certification for Nurse-Midwifery, Prescriptive authority and DEA license is required but may be obtained after hire.\u00a0 Will consider a new CNM graduate.\u00a0 The in-person response time requirement is 1 hour.\u00a0 Demonstrated communication (written and oral) problem-solving, leadership and collaborative skills, strong patient advocacy and patient education skills.\u00a0 This position is subject to a pre-employment criminal background and registry check and drug screen.\u00a0 A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Additional Information: Job Responsibilities: Provides antepartum, intrapartum, postpartum, and women\u2019s health care services. Performs comprehensive health assessments and establishing diagnoses. Develops and implementing treatment and care plans. Prescribes medications, therapies, and diagnostic tests within APRN scope. Triages patients presenting to Labor & Delivery. Manages laboring patients independently or collaboratively with OB/GYN physicians. Monitors fetal and maternal well-being during pregnancy and birth. Collaborates with interdisciplinary teams including physicians, nurses, and specialists Supports evidence-based, low-intervention, patient-centered maternity care. Consults or referring to physicians when complications arise. Documents patient care and maintaining compliance with APRN and hospital standards. May perform other duties as assigned. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS Stand: Frequently Sit: Frequently Walk: Occasionally Bend, crawl, crouch, kneel, stoop or reach overhead: Frequently Lift and carry weight: 25 lbs Push and pull weight: 25 lbs Use hands to touch, handle or feel: Frequently Talk: Continuously Hear: Continuously Taste or smell: Occasionally Read, concentrate, think analytically: Continuously Physical Environment : Inside Medical Facility Environment Salary Information: 104,475-140,805 Required Documents to Apply: Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Adult Maltreatment, Annual TB Screening, Child Maltreatment, Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry, Substance Abuse Testing This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Hearing Frequent Physical Activity: Feeling, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Reaching, Repetitive Motion, Sharps, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Crouching, Kneeling, Lifting, Pulling Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Fayetteville/RazorTemps--Housing-Service-Center-Dispatcher-1_R0090758": {"title": "RazorTemps- Housing Service Center Dispatcher-1", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com, then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at all University of Arkansas institutions will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students.\u201d University of Arkansas, Fayetteville students will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Student Jobs at UAF.\u201d All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. Closing Date: 09/10/2026 Type of Position: Staff - Clerical Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas, Fayetteville Founded in 1871, the University of Arkansas is a land grant institution, classified by the Carnegie Foundation among the nation\u2019s top 2 percent of universities with the highest level of research activity. The University of Arkansas works to advance the state and build a better world through education, research, and outreach by providing transformational opportunities and skills, fostering a welcoming climate, and nurturing creativity, discovery, and the spread of new ideas and innovations. The University of Arkansas campus is located in Fayetteville, a welcoming community ranked as one of the best places to live in the U.S. The growing region surrounding Fayetteville is home to numerous Fortune 500 companies and one of the nation\u2019s strongest economies. Northwest Arkansas is also quickly gaining a national reputation for its focus on the arts and overall quality of life. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10% of employee salary. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions, you should review before applying for the opening. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process, please submit a request via the Disability Accommodations | OEOC | University of Arkansas (uark.edu) : Request an Accommodation. Appli\u00adcants are required to submit a request for each position of which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 479.575.5351. Department: RazorTemps Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Answering phone calls directing them to what is needed. Observing our DSX Door system. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: High School Diploma 18 years of age Preferred Qualifications: Clerical experience Dispatching experience Additional Information: Salary Information: $13.00 per hour Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Recruitment Contact Information: RazorTemps rzrtemps@uark.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Special Instructions to Applicants: Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry, Substance Abuse Testing The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas seeks to attract, develop and retain high quality faculty, staff and administrators that consistently display practices and behaviors to advance a culture that embeds equal opportunity, educational excellence and unparalleled access for all. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All Application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: Feeling, Grasping, Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Reaching, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/RN-PRN---Orthopedic-Clinics_R0091027-1": {"title": "RN PRN - Orthopedic Clinics", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 10/03/2026 Type of Position: Clinical Staff - Nursing Job Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Shift Vary (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | MUSL Ambulatory Clinic PRN Staff (Jacob Allen Mitchell) Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: \"This is a PRN position\" Registered Nurse (RN) that will provide direct patient care. This professional nursing role will require the ability to coordinate care for patients, triage patients, and work collaboratively with clinic providers, fellows, and staff. Requires the ability to effectively work with patient referral sources, facilitate appointments, coordinate transitions of care, and provide patient education on complex conditions. The RN will work with the individual patient, their families, and providers of care to develop and implement individual health plans. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Graduate of an accredited Nursing Program with Associate Degree in Nursing, Nursing Diploma, Bachelor\u2019s in Nursing, or Master's in Nursing.\u00a0 Valid RN License. One (1) year of direct Registered Nursing experience. Excellent communication skills. Basic computer skills. Strong work ethics and accountability. Additional Information: Responsibilities: Collects and documents assessment data from patients and/or others per UAMS standard.\u00a0 Develops patient's Plan of Care (POC) per department/unit standards utilizing assessment data.\u00a0 Evaluates the progress of patients toward attainment of desired outcomes. Administers medication following department/unit standards and the Nurse Practice Act.\u00a0 Verifies and evaluates care delivered to ensure it is consistent with patient and family-centered care principles, practice standards, and regulatory requirements. Supports the integration of current evidence into nursing practices.\u00a0 Promotes an environment conducive to positive educational experience for all students and staff.\u00a0 Provides effective patient/family education/discharge planning. Effectively collaborates and communicates with nursing staff at all levels, interdisciplinary teams, executive leaders, and other stakeholders.\u00a0 Communicates care appropriately through documentation in the medical record. Reports variances in care/ systems/ processes through the appropriate means. Participates in the recruitment/retention of staff.\u00a0 Facilitates the development and implementation of nursing practice standards that are evidence-based and in compliance with ANA standards. May perform other duties as assigned. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Criminal Background Check, Substance Abuse Testing This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Repetitive Motion, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Hearing, Kneeling, Lifting, Pulling, Pushing Occasional Physical Activity: Reaching Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/RN-PRN---Orthopedic-Clinics_R0091018-1": {"title": "RN PRN - Orthopedic Clinics", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 10/03/2026 Type of Position: Clinical Staff - Nursing Job Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Shift Vary (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | MUSL Ambulatory Clinic PRN Staff (Jacob Allen Mitchell) Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: \"This is a PRN position\" Registered Nurse (RN) that will provide direct patient care. This professional nursing role will require the ability to coordinate care for patients, triage patients, and work collaboratively with clinic providers, fellows, and staff. Requires the ability to effectively work with patient referral sources, facilitate appointments, coordinate transitions of care, and provide patient education on complex conditions. The RN will work with the individual patient, their families, and providers of care to develop and implement individual health plans. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Graduate of an accredited Nursing Program with Associate Degree in Nursing, Nursing Diploma, Bachelor\u2019s in Nursing, or Master's in Nursing.\u00a0 Valid RN License. One (1) year of direct Registered Nursing experience. Excellent communication skills. Basic computer skills. Strong work ethics and accountability. Additional Information: Responsibilities: Collects and documents assessment data from patients and/or others per UAMS standard.\u00a0 Develops patient's Plan of Care (POC) per department/unit standards utilizing assessment data.\u00a0 Evaluates the progress of patients toward attainment of desired outcomes. Administers medication following department/unit standards and the Nurse Practice Act.\u00a0 Verifies and evaluates care delivered to ensure it is consistent with patient and family-centered care principles, practice standards, and regulatory requirements. Supports the integration of current evidence into nursing practices.\u00a0 Promotes an environment conducive to positive educational experience for all students and staff.\u00a0 Provides effective patient/family education/discharge planning. Effectively collaborates and communicates with nursing staff at all levels, interdisciplinary teams, executive leaders, and other stakeholders.\u00a0 Communicates care appropriately through documentation in the medical record. Reports variances in care/ systems/ processes through the appropriate means. Participates in the recruitment/retention of staff.\u00a0 Facilitates the development and implementation of nursing practice standards that are evidence-based and in compliance with ANA standards. May perform other duties as assigned. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Criminal Background Check, Substance Abuse Testing This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Feeling, Grasping, Lifting, Pulling, Pushing Occasional Physical Activity: Sharps, Stooping Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/APRN-Neurosurgery-Clinic_R0091053-1": {"title": "APRN Neurosurgery Clinic", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/17/2026 Type of Position: Clinical Staff - Nursing Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | NUSL Mid-Level Outpatient OP C Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Advanced Practice Nurse will assist surgeon with clinic, organizing visits and performing clinic procedures, assist in the operating room, answer pages and round on post-operative patients on a daily and PRN basis. The APRN will be responsible for managing care of outpatients post-operatively, answering telephone inquiries and filling prescriptions. The APRN must have a high level of expertise to perform assessments/diagnosis/treatment of actual/potential problems of patients. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Master's Degree in Nursing Licensed RN in Arkansas, Current APRN License 4 years of Nursing experience Additional Information: Job Requirements: Schedule and coordinate new and established patient appointments, follow-ups, procedures, and diagnostic testing. Coordinate referrals and ensure required documentation and authorizations are obtained prior to appointments. Register patients and accurately update demographic, insurance, and medical information. Verify insurance eligibility, benefits, and referral requirements. Respond to patient phone calls and portal messages and provide timely assistance with scheduling and clinic-related questions. Coordinate communication between patients, neurosurgeons, advanced practice providers, nurses, and other clinical staff. Assist with coordinating pre-operative and post-operative appointments and testing. Ensure medical records, imaging, referrals, and other clinical documentation are available for scheduled visits. Obtain and track prior authorizations for procedures, imaging, and specialty services as required. Reschedule appointments and manage provider schedules while minimizing delays in patient care. Assist with identifying and resolving complex patient access and scheduling issues. Provide patients with instructions regarding appointments, testing, referrals, and follow-up care. Maintain patient confidentiality and comply with HIPAA and organizational policies. Document patient interactions and scheduling activities accurately in the electronic medical record. Provide compassionate, professional customer service to patients and families dealing with complex neurological and neurosurgical conditions Perform other job duties as needed. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS Stand: Frequently Sit: Frequently Walk: Occasionally Bend, crawl, crouch, kneel, stoop or reach overhead: Frequently Lift and carry weight: 25 lbs Push and pull weight: 25 lbs Use hands to touch, handle or feel: Frequently Talk: Continuously Hear: Continuously Taste or smell: Occasionally Read, concentrate, think analytically: Continuously Physical Environment : Inside Medical Facility Environment Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Adult Maltreatment, Annual TB Screening, Child Maltreatment, Criminal Background Check, Substance Abuse Testing This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Feeling, Grasping, Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Repetitive Motion, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Kneeling, Reaching, Sharps Occasional Physical Activity: Crouching, Kneeling, Lifting, Pulling, Pushing, Stooping Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Credentialing-Coordinator_R0090446-1": {"title": "Credentialing Coordinator", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/10/2026 Type of Position: Professional Staff - Fiscal Affairs Job Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | CORE Medical Staffing Organization Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Credentialing Coordinator supports the Professional Staff Office functions, including: primary source verifications of expirables, outpatient ordering provider processing, practitioner status requests and terminations of credentialed and managed care practitioners; Credentials Committee agenda support; credentialing file maintenance; scanning of practitioner files; project management tasks; administrative functions related to the Bylaws, Rules and Regulations, and Departmental Policies and Procedures; and regulatory compliance. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor\u2019s Degree\u00a0 OR High School Diploma/GED + 4 years of general administrative experience. Experience in medical staff services, credentialing office, physician\u2019s office practice, hospital admissions, medical records, or other health care related fields is preferred. Additional Information: Job Requirements: Coordinate the credentialing and re-credentialing process for physicians, advanced practice providers, and other clinical practitioners. Collect, verify, and maintain provider credentials, including licenses, certifications, education, training, work history, and professional references. Process initial appointments, reappointments, privileging, and credentialing applications in accordance with organizational policies and regulatory requirements. Conduct primary-source verification of licenses, certifications, DEA registrations, malpractice coverage, education, training, and other required credentials. Prepare credentialing files and applications for review by medical staff leadership, credentialing committees, and governing bodies. Monitor expiration dates and ensure timely renewal of licenses, certifications, registrations, and other provider credentials. Maintain accurate and confidential provider credentialing records in electronic databases and credentialing systems. Communicate with providers, medical staff offices, licensing boards, hospitals, insurance companies, and other external organizations to obtain required documentation. Identify incomplete or discrepant information and follow up with providers and appropriate departments for resolution. Assist with provider privileging by ensuring requested clinical privileges are supported by appropriate education, training, experience, and documentation. Track credentialing applications and provide status updates to providers and leadership. Ensure credentialing activities comply with applicable regulatory, accreditation, and organizational standards. Assist with audits and surveys by preparing credentialing documentation and reports. Maintain confidentiality of sensitive provider and organizational information. Collaborate with Medical Staff Services, Human Resources, Provider Enrollment, Compliance, Legal, and clinical departments. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS Stand: Frequently Sit: Frequently Walk: Occasionally Bend, crawl, crouch, kneel, stoop or reach overhead: Frequently Lift and carry weight: 25 lbs Push and pull weight: 25 lbs Use hands to touch, handle or feel: Frequently Talk: Continuously Hear: Continuously Taste or smell: Occasionally Read, concentrate, think analytically: Continuously Physical Environment : Inside Medical Facility Environment Noise Level : Moderate Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: No Background Check Required This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Sitting Frequent Physical Activity: Talking Occasional Physical Activity: Standing Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Benton/Clinical-Engineering-Technician-I--UAMS-Health-Benton-Bryant-_R0090201-1": {"title": "Clinical Engineering Technician (UAMS Health Benton/Bryant)", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/17/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Shift Vary (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: INA | Institutional Admin Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Clinical Engineering Technician plays a vital role in the safe and effective operation of medical equipment throughout the healthcare system. This position is responsible for the inspection, preventive maintenance, calibration, troubleshooting, and repair of a broad range of biomedical, electronic, and electromechanical devices used in patient diagnosis, treatment, and monitoring. The technician ensures that all clinical equipment meets manufacturer specifications, regulatory requirements, and hospital safety standards, while minimizing equipment downtime and supporting uninterrupted patient care. Working closely with clinical staff, nursing, and other departments, the Clinical Engineering Technician contributes directly to patient safety and the overall efficiency of healthcare delivery by maintaining high standards of equipment reliability and performance. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Associate\u2019s degree in biomedical Instrumentation Technology, Biomedical Equipment Technology, Biomedical Engineering Technology Electronics, Information Technology or related field or completion of U.S. military biomedical equipment technology program and 1 year of experience in biomed, electronic repairs, IT or related fields; hospital experience preferred OR HS Diploma and 3 years of experience in biomed, electronic repairs, IT or related fields; hospital experience preferred Additional Information: Responsibilities: Performs repairs on all facets of medical, diagnostic, and therapeutic equipment used in the treatment of patients at UAMS, its clinics, and health education centers, working with minimal supervision on even the most sophisticated devices. Conducts scheduled preventive maintenance (PM) and electrical safety inspections on all medical, diagnostic, and therapeutic equipment, completing PMs and work orders on time as scheduled. Performs software and networking-related updates and repairs on clinical equipment with minimal supervision required for advanced systems. Provides clinical support and troubleshooting assistance to end-users of medical, diagnostic, and therapeutic equipment. Delivers in-service training to clinical staff and hands-on training to Biomedical Instrumentation Technology students on the proper use and maintenance of medical equipment. Initiates purchases for parts and materials required to complete repairs and preventive maintenance activities. Performs incident investigations related to safety violations or failures involving risk-classified equipment. Conducts initial inspections, acceptance testing, and performance verification on all new, rental, and loaned medical equipment entering UAMS facilities. May perform other duties as assigned. Physical Requirements Constant: Sitting, Standing, Stooping, Talking, Walking Frequent: Crouching, Feeling, Hearing, Kneeling, Manipulate items with fingers (keyboarding), Reaching Occasion: Crawling, Repetitive Motion Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/RN---TOSH-OR_R0091028-1": {"title": "RN - TOSH OR", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 10/03/2026 Type of Position: Clinical Staff - Nursing Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | MUSL | TOSH Operating Room Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: As individuals dedicated to ensuring the safety and quick recovery of our patients, nurses are integral members of a team dedicated to providing the best care for patients through collaboration, communication and patient safety. As part of the TOSH teams, operating room nurses define their practice through attention to nursing excellence and outstanding patient care, driven by their expertise, compassion and dedication to evidence-based practice, and operate at a higher level of practice. If you are an RN who has current Operating Room experience, we invite you to consider a career with The Orthopaedic & Spine Hospital at UAMS Health. The operating room registered nurse (OR RN) provides direct patient care throughout the perioperative process, including the preoperative, intraoperative, and immediate postoperative phases. This role requires the ability to assess, plan, implement, and evaluate care for surgical patients while maintaining a safe and sterile environment. OR RN collaborates closely with surgeons, anesthesiologists, surgical technologists, and other perioperative team members to coordinate care before, during, and after surgical procedures. Key responsibilities include conducting patient assessments and verifications, confirming the surgical site, preparing the operating room, maintaining sterile technique, and continuously monitoring the patient\u2019s condition throughout surgery. Acting as a patient advocate, the OR RN ensures that safety standards are upheld and responds promptly to any changes in patient status. The role also involves effective communication with patients, families, and the interdisciplinary team to provide education on surgical procedures, recovery expectations, and postoperative care instructions. Additional duties include documenting intraoperative care, managing surgical instruments and equipment, adhering to infection prevention protocols, facilitating smooth transitions to recovery staff, and participating in quality improvement and patient safety initiatives. The OR RN works collaboratively with patients, families, surgeons, anesthesia providers, and perioperative staff to deliver comprehensive, individualized surgical care. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Associate\u2019s degree in nursing, Diploma RN. Preferred bachelor's degree in nursing Must be a graduate of an accredited RN nursing program Minimum of 1 year of Registered Nursing experience Valid Registered Nursing License BLS (Or obtain within 30 days of hire) Ability to follow oral instruction, read and write Basic computer skills Excellent communication skills Strong work ethics and accountability Preferred Qualifications: Orthopaedic experience 1-year Operating Room experience (preferred in Orthopaedics) Scrubbing experience Current BLS EPIC Additional Information: Responsibilities: The Registered Nurse (RN) delivers nursing care for patients within the limits of the Nurse Practice Act of the State of Arkansas and adheres to institutional policies, procedures and standards. The RN is responsible to adhere to the standard of care defined by UAMS, ANA, and Standards for specialty patient population with support and mentoring by other team members. Conduct preoperative assessments and verify patient identity, procedure, consent, and surgical site. Develop and implement individualized perioperative plans of care. Collaborate with surgeons, anesthesia providers, and the surgical team to ensure safe, efficient procedures. Monitor patient status throughout the intraoperative phase and respond to clinical changes. Maintain a sterile surgical environment, including surgical counts, specimen handling, and proper patient positioning. Administer medications, IV fluids, and blood products according to established protocols. Serve as the patient advocate and ensure adherence to patient safety standards. Provide patient and family education related to surgical care and recovery. Delegate tasks appropriately and support a collaborative, perioperative team environment. Other duties as assigned Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry, Substance Abuse Testing This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Balancing, Feeling, Grasping, Lifting, Pulling, Pushing, Repetitive Motion, Sharps, Standing, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Grasping, Hearing, Lifting, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching Occasional Physical Activity: Climbing, Crawling, Crouching, Kneeling, Sitting, Stooping Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Laboratory-Procedure-Technician---Gross-Room_R0090955-1": {"title": "Laboratory Procedure Technician - Gross Room", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/17/2026 Type of Position: Other Health Care - Clinical Support Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Shift Vary (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | LPSL APATH Gross Room Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The UAMS Department of Pathology is seeking a motivated individual to join our team! Are you looking for an exciting career in a hospital setting that explores human anatomy daily? Our team works closely with Pathology residents and Pathologists to aid in tissue processing in the lab. We handle specimens as tiny as a mustard seed to full size limbs! This position is also responsible for ensuring correct documentation for patients entering and leaving our morgue along with basic assistance with postmortem examinations. If these things excite you, this job is for you! Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Associates degree in laboratory science, medical laboratory technology degree - OR - 60 credit hours obtained from an accredited institution that\u00a0must include 24 credit hours in Medical Technology or Science Courses which include 6 credit hours of Biology & 6 credit\u00a0hours of Chemistry.\u00a0 Ability to\u00a0work on occasional weekends and rotate on-call duties. Preferred Qualifications: One (1) year experience as a grossing tech or assistant. Professional License/Certification (Certified by ASCP or equivalent). Experience in a hospital setting. EPIC training Additional Information: Job Requirements: Assesses specimen and order acceptability according to departmental policies and procedures.\u00a0 Accession all specimen received indicated for Surgical Pathology. Label specimen correctly and adding formalin to all specimen that do not require special attention.\u00a0 Responsible for dictating gross descriptions of GI, GYN, prostate, kidney, liver, bone marrows, as well as surgical devices. Inks and cuts breasts in accordance with appropriate breast protocols. Performs and assists with specimen and frozen section preparation.\u00a0 Receives and releases bodies in the morgue to ARORA, Coroner\u2019s office, Crime lab, and funeral homes, assuring all paperwork is complete and correct. Maintaining cleanliness and set up of autopsies in morgue. Daily cleaning of cryostats with appropriate reagents.\u00a0 Maintaining a positive attitude and correctly performs all duties during strenuous work hours. Performs preventative maintenance on machines and equipment. Performs troubleshooting on laboratory equipment.\u00a0 Ensures all cassettes are added to Histology processors with appropriate date and end time. \u00a0General lab duties, including but not limited to, recording room and equipment temperatures in appropriate logbook, restock supplies and maintain a safe and organized work environment. Perform other duties as needed. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS Stand: Frequently Sit: Frequently Walk: Occasionally Bend, crawl, crouch, kneel, stoop or reach overhead: Frequently Lift and carry weight: 25 lbs Push and pull weight: 25 lbs Use hands to touch, handle or feel: Frequently Talk: Continuously Hear: Continuously Taste or smell: Occasionally Read, concentrate, think analytically: Continuously Physical Environment : Inside Medical Facility Environment Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), Proof of Veteran Status, Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Criminal Background Check, Substance Abuse Testing This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Grasping, Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Reaching, Sharps, Standing, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Feeling, Kneeling, Pulling, Pushing, Repetitive Motion, Sitting, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Lifting Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Fayetteville/Teaching-Assistant-Professor-of-Film-Studies_R0090791-1": {"title": "Teaching Assistant Professor of Film Studies", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com, then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at all University of Arkansas institutions will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students.\u201d University of Arkansas, Fayetteville students will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Student Jobs at UAF.\u201d All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. Closing Date: Type of Position: Faculty - Non-Tenure Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Academic Term (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: Yes Institution Name: University of Arkansas, Fayetteville Founded in 1871, the University of Arkansas is a land grant institution, classified by the Carnegie Foundation among the nation\u2019s top 2 percent of universities with the highest level of research activity. The University of Arkansas works to advance the state and build a better world through education, research, and outreach by providing transformational opportunities and skills, fostering a welcoming climate, and nurturing creativity, discovery, and the spread of new ideas and innovations. The University of Arkansas campus is located in Fayetteville, a welcoming community ranked as one of the best places to live in the U.S. The growing region surrounding Fayetteville is home to numerous Fortune 500 companies and one of the nation\u2019s strongest economies. Northwest Arkansas is also quickly gaining a national reputation for its focus on the arts and overall quality of life. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10% of employee salary. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions, you should review before applying for the opening. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process, please submit a request via the Disability Accommodations | OEOC | University of Arkansas (uark.edu) : Request an Accommodation. Appli\u00adcants are required to submit a request for each position of which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 479.575.5351. Department: Department of Communication Department's Website: https://communication.uark.edu/ Summary of Job Duties: The Department of Communication in the Fulbright College of Arts and Sciences at the University of Arkansas invites applications for a Teaching Assistant Professor in the area of Film Studies. The successful candidate should have experience teaching introductory film studies courses, in addition to upper level courses in film criticism. Candidates should have experience teaching courses in-person as well as online. The position will start in August 2027. This is a standard nine-month faculty appointment. Duties will include developing classes and teaching effectively at both the undergraduate and graduate levels, and providing service to the Department, University, and discipline. This is an in-person position. Most University classes are offered face-to-face and this role requires regular on-campus presence to support high-quality instruction and student learning. Participation in selected departmental or programmatic activities that advance teaching quality and student success is also expected, consistent with the responsibilities of non-tenure track faculty as defined by the academic department. Regular, reliable, and non-disruptive attendance is an essential job duty, as is the ability to create and maintain collegial, harmonious working relationships with others. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Ph.D. in Communication, Film or Media Studies, or terminal degree in a related field from an accredited institution of higher education conferred by the start of appointment Demonstrated competency in the classroom as evidenced in the CV and evidence of teaching effectiveness Experience and competency teaching introductory and upper-level courses in film studies Preferred Qualifications: Experience teaching film courses in large lecture sections Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities (KSAs): Experience teaching lower and upper-level in-person courses in film studies Experience teaching lower and upper-level courses in online formats Experience with service at the departmental, university, or disciplinary level Additional Information: About the Department: The Department of Communication is committed to excellence in scholarship, instruction, and expression of human communication. We nurture a thriving intellectual community by bridging the humanities and social sciences. Discovery, learning and engagement are the hallmarks of this community. Visit https://communication.uark.edu/ \u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 About the Department: The Department hosts the Center for Communication Research (CCR) which facilitates collaborative, interdisciplinary social research within the University of Arkansas, Northwest Arkansas region, and broader intellectual community. The CCR seeks to stimulate and support interdisciplinary collaborations; provide opportunities for undergraduate and graduate participation; engage regional, state, and national funding agencies; and acquire and maintain the equipment necessary to support research endeavors. The CCR manages a research lab space that includes state-of-the-art technology for studying all facets of communication. Salary Information: Salary is commensurate with experience and qualifications. Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Curriculum Vitae, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Statement of Teaching Philosophy Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Recruitment Contact Information: Jake Dionne, search committee chair, dionne@uark.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Special Instructions to Applicants: Completed applications received by September 30, 2026, will be assured full consideration. Late applications will be reviewed as necessary to fill the position. For additional inquiries, please contact the search committee chair, Jake Dionne, at dionne@uark.edu. Applicants must submit: \u2022 Curriculum vitae, \u2022 Cover letter/letter of application, \u2022 Teaching philosophy statement that has evidence of teaching effectiveness including a list of courses taught and up to three years of quantitative and qualitative evaluations, \u2022 List of three professional references (name, title, email address, and phone number) willing to provide letters of recommendation if requested during the application process. Letters of recommendation will be requested only for candidates selected for interviews. Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas seeks to attract, develop and retain high quality faculty, staff and administrators that consistently display practices and behaviors to advance a culture that embeds equal opportunity, educational excellence and unparalleled access for all. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All Application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Fayetteville/Supply-Chain-Management-Events-Coordinator_R0090519-1": {"title": "Supply Chain Management Events Coordinator", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com, then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at all University of Arkansas institutions will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students.\u201d University of Arkansas, Fayetteville students will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Student Jobs at UAF.\u201d All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. Closing Date: 09/03/2026 Type of Position: Conference and Events Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Fixed Duration of Project/Grant (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas, Fayetteville Founded in 1871, the University of Arkansas is a land grant institution, classified by the Carnegie Foundation among the nation\u2019s top 2 percent of universities with the highest level of research activity. The University of Arkansas works to advance the state and build a better world through education, research, and outreach by providing transformational opportunities and skills, fostering a welcoming climate, and nurturing creativity, discovery, and the spread of new ideas and innovations. The University of Arkansas campus is located in Fayetteville, a welcoming community ranked as one of the best places to live in the U.S. The growing region surrounding Fayetteville is home to numerous Fortune 500 companies and one of the nation\u2019s strongest economies. Northwest Arkansas is also quickly gaining a national reputation for its focus on the arts and overall quality of life. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10% of employee salary. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions, you should review before applying for the opening. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process, please submit a request via the Disability Accommodations | OEOC | University of Arkansas (uark.edu) : Request an Accommodation. Appli\u00adcants are required to submit a request for each position of which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 479.575.5351. Department: Conference Hub Hourly Support Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Sam M. Walton College of Business at the University of Arkansas in Fayetteville invites applications for the position of Supply Chain Management Events Coordinator. This position is responsible for planning, coordinating, and executing events hosted by the Department of Supply Chain Management and the Supply Chain Management Research Center (SCMRC). The Events Coordinator oversees logistical planning for department events, coordinates vendors and campus partners, manages event timelines and operational details, and ensures exceptional experiences for students, faculty, alumni, industry partners, and guests. The position supports networking events, case competitions, Shadow Days, the annual Supply Chain Trends Expo, graduate program weekends in Dallas, faculty events, and other supply chain management programming. Working closely with faculty, program directors, the SCMRC, and the Walton marketing team, this position ensures events are executed efficiently while aligning with departmental goals and university policies. Regular, reliable, and non-disruptive attendance is an essential job duty, as is the ability to create and maintain collegial, harmonious working relationships with others. This position requires flexibility to work occasional evenings and weekends in support of departmental events. There is occasional travel, including overnight travel, to support off-campus programs and events. This is a fully in-person position. This is appointment is renewable based on the need for the position, availability of funding, and continued satisfactory level of performance in the role. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor\u2019s degree in Hospitality Management, Business, Event Management, Communications, Marketing, or a related field from an accredited institution of higher education At least three years of professional experience coordinating events or managing projects Applicable equivalencies may be considered for the above qualifications. Preferred Qualifications: Experience planning conferences, networking events, or educational events Experience coordinating vendors and event logistics Experience coordinating travel, lodging, and logistical arrangements for speakers, guests, or program participants Experience managing event budgets and reconciling event-related expenses Experience administering event registration software Experience working in higher education Additional Information: This position is renewable annually based on continued need for the position, availability of funding, and satisfactory job performance. Salary Information: $51,021 - $55,000 Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Recruitment Contact Information: Shannon Bullock, Associate Director of Walton Conferencing and Events, shstewar@uark.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Special Instructions to Applicants: Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas seeks to attract, develop and retain high quality faculty, staff and administrators that consistently display practices and behaviors to advance a culture that embeds equal opportunity, educational excellence and unparalleled access for all. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All Application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Fayetteville/Assistant-Professor---9-MONTH_R0090240-1": {"title": "Assistant Professor - 9 MONTH", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com, then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at all University of Arkansas institutions will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students.\u201d University of Arkansas, Fayetteville students will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Student Jobs at UAF.\u201d All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. Closing Date: Type of Position: Faculty - Tenure/Tenure Track Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: Yes Institution Name: University of Arkansas, Fayetteville Founded in 1871, the University of Arkansas is a land grant institution, classified by the Carnegie Foundation among the nation\u2019s top 2 percent of universities with the highest level of research activity. The University of Arkansas works to advance the state and build a better world through education, research, and outreach by providing transformational opportunities and skills, fostering a welcoming climate, and nurturing creativity, discovery, and the spread of new ideas and innovations. The University of Arkansas campus is located in Fayetteville, a welcoming community ranked as one of the best places to live in the U.S. The growing region surrounding Fayetteville is home to numerous Fortune 500 companies and one of the nation\u2019s strongest economies. Northwest Arkansas is also quickly gaining a national reputation for its focus on the arts and overall quality of life. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10% of employee salary. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions, you should review before applying for the opening. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process, please submit a request via the Disability Accommodations | OEOC | University of Arkansas (uark.edu) : Request an Accommodation. Appli\u00adcants are required to submit a request for each position of which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 479.575.5351. Department: Department of Sociology and Criminology Department's Website: https://sociology.uark.edu/ Summary of Job Duties: The Department of Sociology & Criminology in the Fulbright College of Arts and Sciences at the University of Arkansas invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor of Sociology & Criminology to start in August 2027. This is a standard nine-month faculty appointment with a competitive startup package. The successful candidate will have the opportunity to contribute to the Public Policy Ph.D. and Data Science / Analytics B.A. programs. We prefer candidates who have demonstrated potential to secure external research funding commensurate with career stage. Additionally, candidates with a demonstrated ability to teach graduate and undergraduate courses in criminology and sociology, or both, are highly desirable. This is an in-person position. Most university classes are offered face-to-face, and extensive in-person engagement in such activities as office hours, student advising, and departmental, college, and university committee meetings\u202fis essential to advancing\u202fstudent success and departmental effectiveness. Regular, reliable, and non-disruptive attendance is an essential job duty, as is the ability to create and maintain collegial, harmonious working relationships with others. About the Department: The Department is a dynamic, productive, collegial, and student success-oriented unit in Fulbright College of Arts and Sciences. The Department offers undergraduate degrees in Sociology and Criminology, and an M.A. in Sociology, and affiliation with three research units: the Center for Social Research, Community and Family Institute, and the Terrorism Research Center. The Department participates in African and African American Studies, Asian Studies, Latin American & Latino Studies, and other interdisciplinary area studies programs. The department contributes to the larger university strategic missions outlined in detail in the Chancellor\u2019s guiding priorities. For more information about the department, please visit https://fulbright.uark.edu/departments/sociology/. Duties will include: \u2022 40% Teaching or Professional Performance \u2022 40% Research/Scholarly and/or Creative Activities \u2022 20% Academic Service Activities Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: With submitted materials, the candidate must demonstrate Ph.D. in Sociology, Criminology, or related social science field from an accredited institution of higher education conferred by the start of appointment An active research agenda and evidence of scholarly productivity Evidence that expertise contributes to one or more departmental strengths in the research areas of criminology, community, social inequality\u00a0and/or\u00a0stratification,\u00a0and\u00a0health Evidence\u00a0of\u00a0contributing\u00a0to\u00a0a\u00a0scholarly\u00a0environment\u00a0for\u00a0all through teaching, mentoring, research, outreach, and/or service\u00a0commensurate\u00a0with rank Preferred Qualifications: Candidates who have\u00a0demonstrated \u00a0potential to secure external research funding\u00a0commensurate\u00a0with career stage Candidates with a demonstrated ability to teach graduate and undergraduate courses in criminology and sociology, or both, are highly desirable Additional Information: This position is a Designated Research Position \u00a0and is regulated by the Arkansas Research Education Protection Act of 2025 .\u00a0 Prior to issuance of an offer of employment, the University is required to request and obtain additional information about an applicant\u2019s background and, if required, conduct an additional review of that background information. Salary Information: Salary is commensurate with experience and qualifications. Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Curriculum Vitae, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Statement of Research Philosophy Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Recruitment Contact Information: Michael Nino, search committee chair, mnino@uark.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Special Instructions to Applicants: Completed applications received by September 30, 2026, will be assured full consideration. Late applications will be reviewed as necessary to fill the position. For additional inquiries, please contact the search committee chair, Dr. Michael Ni\u00f1o, at mnino@uark.edu. Applicants must submit: \u2022 a curriculum vitae, \u2022 a cover letter/letter of application, \u2022 a research statement (no more than two pages), and \u2022 a list of three professional references (name, title, email address, and phone number) willing to provide letters of recommendation if requested during the application process. Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas seeks to attract, develop and retain high quality faculty, staff and administrators that consistently display practices and behaviors to advance a culture that embeds equal opportunity, educational excellence and unparalleled access for all. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All Application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Police-Officer---UAMS-Health-Benton-Bryant_R0091088-1": {"title": "Police Officer", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/17/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Shift Vary (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: INA | Institutional Admin Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Works under the general supervision of the Chief of Police and the direct supervision of the Sergeant. Responsible for enforcement of traffic control, criminal laws, and parking regulations. This position is governed by the Law Enforcement Standards of Arkansas and UAMS Policies. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: High School Diploma / GED required. Be certified by the Arkansas Law Enforcement Standards Training Academy as a Police Officer or become certified within one (1) year of employment.\u00a0 (Possibility of a one-year extension). Be at least 21 years of age. Current and valid Arkansas driver\u2019s license. Ability to communicate and maintain a good rapport with the campus population.\u00a0 Engages in and maintains control of situations/persons through use of minimal force needed in required situations. Able to pass a medical physical examination. Able to pass a psychological examination. Ability to walk 8 to 12 miles in an 8-to-12-hour shift. Ability to climb stairwells. Preferred Qualifications: Associates degree or higher. Basic knowledge of computers. General knowledge of Microsoft Office software. Critical Competencies and Skills: Knowledge of law enforcement practices, methods, and techniques Knowledge of traffic and criminal laws, and departmental regulations and procedures Maintains control of persons by use of minimal force needed in required situations Skill in the operations of fire arms Possesses basic computer skills with a general knowledge of Microsoft Office software Ability to properly prepare and write police reports Communicates and maintains a good rapport with the campus population Practices appropriate enforcement of parking regulations Ability to operate motor vehicles used in work activities Additional Information: Responsibilities: Manages stressful situations courteously, tactfully and calmly in a professional manner Exercises good judgment in evaluating situations and making decisions Responds quickly to emergency situations and calls for service without unnecessarily jeopardizing the safety of oneself, other members of the police department or the public Utilizes common-sense understanding in order to execute written, oral or diagrammed instructions Proficient in the use of firearms and the operation of police vehicles Observes situations objectively and analytically, record and report them clearly and concisely both orally in writing Ability and willingness to perform moderately physical work Ability and willingness to perform work indoors, outdoors and in a vehicle Exhibits good character (i.e. courteous, friendly and empathetic) as determined by a detailed background investigation Attends related training classes and schools as needed UAMS is a very diverse campus therefore officers must be at ease with members of other ethnic, cultural, and social groups May perform other duties as assigned by superior officers or administration Physical Requirements: Heavy Work | Exerting up to 100 pounds of force occasionally, and/or up to 50 pounds of force frequently, and/or up to 20 pounds of force constantly to move objects. The e mployee is required to have close visual acuity to perform an activity such as: preparing and analyzing data and figures; transcribing; viewing a computer terminal; extensive reading; and/or visual inspection at distances close to the eyes. The employee is not substantially exposed to adverse environmental conditions (such as in typical office or administrative work) The employee is subject to both environmental conditions. Activities occur inside and outside. Constant physical activities: Driving; Hearing; Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding; Sitting; Standing; Talking; Walking F requent physical activities: Feeling; Grasping; Pulling; Pushing; Reaching; Repetitive Motion Occasional physical activities: Climbing; Crawling; Crouching Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience. Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Fayetteville/Instructor_R0090862-1": {"title": "Instructor", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com, then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at all University of Arkansas institutions will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students.\u201d University of Arkansas, Fayetteville students will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Student Jobs at UAF.\u201d All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. Closing Date: 09/11/2026 Type of Position: Faculty - Non-Tenure Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Academic Term (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas, Fayetteville Founded in 1871, the University of Arkansas is a land grant institution, classified by the Carnegie Foundation among the nation\u2019s top 2 percent of universities with the highest level of research activity. The University of Arkansas works to advance the state and build a better world through education, research, and outreach by providing transformational opportunities and skills, fostering a welcoming climate, and nurturing creativity, discovery, and the spread of new ideas and innovations. The University of Arkansas campus is located in Fayetteville, a welcoming community ranked as one of the best places to live in the U.S. The growing region surrounding Fayetteville is home to numerous Fortune 500 companies and one of the nation\u2019s strongest economies. Northwest Arkansas is also quickly gaining a national reputation for its focus on the arts and overall quality of life. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10% of employee salary. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions, you should review before applying for the opening. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process, please submit a request via the Disability Accommodations | OEOC | University of Arkansas (uark.edu) : Request an Accommodation. Appli\u00adcants are required to submit a request for each position of which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 479.575.5351. Department: Accounting Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The William Dillard Department of Accounting in the Sam M. Walton College of Business at the University of Arkansas seeks applications from interested candidates to fill a non-tenure track Instructor position effective August 2027. The Instructor position is a non-tenure-track, teaching-focused position with a four-course (12 credit hour) teaching load each semester with a mix of face-to-face and online courses, as needed. Duties include discipline-specific intellectual engagement activities to maintain currency in their teaching disciplines, consistent with AACSB Instructional Practitioner status. Teaching duties include holding regular office hours, providing timely grading feedback for students, and conducting the class to facilitate learning for all students, consistent with good teaching practices. \u202f All full-time faculty are responsible for participating in program curriculum development and reviewing and maintaining program currency, viability, and quality along with activities linked to department course assignments. Departmental service activities are expected. Reduced teaching loads may be included dependent upon assigned service and administrative roles. Instructors can expect to devote 40 or more hours a week to the position. The amount of time spent on campus will vary. Salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience; benefits are competitive. Regular on-campus availability, in-person teaching, and active contribution to the life of the department, including exhibiting respect and cooperation in shared academic and administrative tasks are essential duties. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: \u00a0 Master's degree from an AACSB (or equivalent) accredited university in accounting or a closely related field conferred by the start of employment In the absence of a graduate degree, qualified experience is considered. Experience should be equivalent to the degree it would otherwise require for the faculty position. Experience should include breadth and depth of experience outside of the classroom in real-world situations relevant to accounting Must meet Instructional Practitioner status under AACSB guidelines, including two or more years of industry work experience and a demonstrated record of engagement with industry professionals \u00a0 Preferred Qualifications: Experience and/or an interest in teaching courses in financial accounting and/or managerial accounting At least five years of teaching experience in the Walton College of Business or a similar business school Evidence of high-quality teaching in undergraduate and/or graduate accounting courses \u00a0 \u00a0 At least five years of professional work experience in accounting or a closely related field Additional Information: Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Recruitment Contact Information: Caleb Rawson Associate Professor Sam M. Walton College of Business CRawson@walton.uark.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Special Instructions to Applicants: Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas seeks to attract, develop and retain high quality faculty, staff and administrators that consistently display practices and behaviors to advance a culture that embeds equal opportunity, educational excellence and unparalleled access for all. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All Application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Helena-Campus/Adjunct--Construction-Manufacturing-Instructor_R0091100": {"title": "Adjunct, Construction/Manufacturing Instructor", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Adjunct Faculty Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Less than Annual Appointment (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: Phillips Community College of the University of Arkansas The first community college established in Arkansas, Phillips Community College of the University of Arkansas (PCCUA) is a multi-campus, two-year college serving Eastern Arkansas. PCCUA has academic, occupational/technical and continuing education programs and offers over 25 associate degree programs with campuses in DeWitt, Helena-W. Helena and Stuttgart. Thank you for your interest, and we hope you\u2019ll be joining our Ridge Runner family soon! Below you will find the details for the position as well as any specific application requirements you should review before applying for this opening. To apply for this position, please click the Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process, please call Human Resources at (870) 338-6474, ext. 1271. Department: Workforce Training Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Teach, develop and update construction and manufacturing courses. Teach all applicable regulation for health and safety and environmental compliance. Instruct and prepare students for full time and part time employment. Assist with program recruiting. Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in a construction / manufacturing related field preferred. 3 years experience in manufacturing and or construction. Computer skills including Word, Excel, Power Point. Auto CAD/ blue print reading or equivalent is necessary. Other skills including but not limited to CNC, HVAC/R, Sheet metal fabrication, machine shop technology, PLC programing. Basic carpentry skills including table saws, band saws, shapers, routers and other power and hand tools. other qualifications include forklift operation, heavy equipment, safety and sanitation. Additional Information: Salary Information: commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Joe St. Columbia All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check For general application assistance, or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at (870) 338-6474, ext. 1271. PCCUA is committed to providing a safe campus community. We will conduct criminal background checks and a sex offender registry check for applicants seeking employment. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Climbing, Crouching, Grasping, Hearing, Kneeling, Lifting, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Pulling, Pushing, Sharps, Standing, Stooping, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Security-Officer_R0090507-1": {"title": "Security Officer", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 10/03/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: POL | Police Nght Shift B Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Security Officer works under the direct supervision of the Shift Sergeant or Administrative Sergeant. This position is responsible for conducting interior patrols, providing public assistance, monitoring campus facilities, and supporting a safe and secure environment for patients, visitors, students, faculty, and staff. Qualifications: High School Diploma / GED. At least 19 years of age. Current and Valid driver's license. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities: Ability to walk a minimum of 8 to 12 miles in an 8-to-12-hour shift. Ability to climb stairwells. Ability to maintain and communicate a good rapport with the campus population. Additional Information: Responsibilities: Conducts routine interior patrols of assigned buildings and campus areas to help maintain a safe and secure environment. Monitors entrances, hallways, stairwells, parking areas, and other designated locations for suspicious activity or safety concerns. Provides directions, escorts, and general assistance to patients, visitors, students, faculty, and staff. Responds promptly to calls for service, alarms, disturbances, and emergency situations. Reports safety hazards, security concerns, suspicious activity, and policy violations to the appropriate personnel. Documents incidents and daily activities accurately and completes required reports. Assists with access control, including securing and unlocking designated buildings and areas. Supports law enforcement officers and emergency personnel as directed. Maintains professional and courteous communication with members of the campus community. Performs other duties as assigned. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Licensed-Master-Social-Worker---Emergency-Department_R0090876-1": {"title": "Licensed Master Social Worker - Emergency Department", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/17/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | CORE PA Lead Social Worker Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: This posting will be used to fill multiple positions located in the Emergency Room department for Care Management, with cross coverage in other areas. The Licensed Social Worker is a member of the care management team and responsible for assisting in the management of the continuum of care from admission through discharge for assigned patients. The role reflects appropriate knowledge of Social Work scope of practice, current state requirements, CMS Conditions of Participation, EMTALA, Patient Bill of Rights, AB 1203 and other Federal or State regulatory agency requirements specific to the Social Work role. The Social Work team member will partner with the multi-disciplinary team utilizing best practices, relevant data and compliance with the mission/philosophy, standards, goals and core values of UAMS: Comfort, Hope, and Healing. Primary elements of the social work role include: assessment of the psychological, financial, and discharge planning needs of the patients and families, providing information, support, counseling, and referrals to other levels of care and appropriate resources for a variety of age-specific populations, including neonatal, pediatric, adolescents, adults, and geriatric. There are two different shifts: Sunday - Wednesday: 12 pm (noon) - 10:30 pm Thursday - Saturday: 10:00 AM - 10:30 pm Qualifications: Minimum: Qualifications: Masters' degree in Social Work Must be licensed by an Arkansas Professional Board as a Licensed Master Social Worker (LMSW) or Licensed Certified Social Worker (LCSW) by date of hire Preferred Qualifications: Certified Case Manager (CCM) or American Case Management (ACM) certification. 2 years experience in an Acute Care Hospital Setting Experience in Case Management Additional Information: Job Requirements: Completes assessment for patients admitted to the Emergency Department that maybe admitted to the hospital. Performs discharge planning and aftercare coordination, community referrals and linkages. Provides patient and family education and adjustment to illness counseling, grief counseling and crisis intervention. Promotes patient and family centered care and documents the patient choices in the medical record as required. Recommends care and services that are appropriate to the specified chronological age, developmental age, social maturity, and cultural background of the patient being treated. Documents and communicates with all team, physicians, and patient family concerns pertaining to the coordination of care and services. Serves as a consultant for processing guardianship, power of attorney, health care proxy, and advance directives. Collaborates with other UAMS Departments and actively participates in hospital wide performance improvement metrics and regulatory compliance initiatives. Reports and reviews department specific data metrics on a monthly basis. Implements, monitors, and evaluates the Care Management quality improvement initiatives.\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Interacts with and assists the public in a professional and friendly manner as needed. Demonstrates effective communication skills; communicates accurate and complete information; maintains strict confidentiality when necessary. Demonstrates positive working relationships with co-workers, management team, and ancillary departments; follows the Core Concepts of Patient and Family Centered Care and the Basic Code of Conduct Guidelines. Assist internal and external stakeholders as needed with exceptional customer service. Other duties as assigned in order to meet the UAMS Core Values and the business needs of the Department PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS Stand: Frequently Sit: Frequently Walk: Occasionally Bend, crawl, crouch, kneel, stoop or reach overhead: Frequently Lift and carry weight: 25 lbs Push and pull weight: 25 lbs Use hands to touch, handle or feel: Frequently Talk: Continuously Hear: Continuously Taste or smell: Occasionally Read, concentrate, think analytically: Continuously Physical Environment : Inside Medical Facility Environment Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: UAMS Licensed Master Social Worker 2 Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAMS/LPN-Outpatient-M-F--Fayetteville--AR_R0091095-1": {"title": "LPN-Outpatient(M-F)-Fayetteville, AR", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 10/31/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: REP | PCPHSL CS NWA Fayetteville Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: We are seeking a skilled Licensed Practical Nurse (LPN) to join our team at UAMS Fayetteville Family Medical Center. This position plays a vital role in providing direct patient care under the supervision of a Registered Nurse, contributing to the assessment, planning, implementation, and evaluation of nursing care for a select group of patients. This role is ideal for individuals who are compassionate, detail-oriented, and committed to delivering exceptional patient care in a dynamic healthcare environment. If you are eager to contribute to a team dedicated to excellence in family medicine, we encourage you to apply. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications High School, GED, or formal educational equivalent. Graduate of an accredited Licensed Practical Nurse program. Associates Degree in Nursing. One (1) year of work experience in clinical nursing Current Arkansas Licensed Practical Nurse license Current CPR certification Knowledge, Abilities, and Skills: Strong clinical knowledge and technique. Knowledge of basic medical terminology required Strong patient advocacy and patient education skills.\u00a0 Attention to communication, oral, written, and persuasive. Must be able to build collaborative relationships. Possess personal credibility. Ability to make independent judgments that have highly significant impacts on the organization. Ability to provide motivational support to the area of responsibility. Strong customer service orientation. Intermediate computer skills. Professional and courteous telephone etiquette. General knowledge of office machines, including printers, fax machines, and scanners. Preferred Qualifications Two (2) years of work experience in a clinical environment with direct patient care. Good working knowledge of the state immunization registry, care manager. PCMH experience and care management experience. Additional Information: Key Responsibilities: Direct patient care within the limits of the Nurse Practice Act of the State of Arkansas, UAMS policies, procedures, and standards. Accountable for adhering to UAMS care guidelines. Observe patients, charting, and reporting changes in patients\u2019 conditions. Provide basic care and treatment of patients. Administer prescribed medications and start intravenous fluids. Measure and record the patient\u2019s vital signs. Assist patients in standing, walking, bathing, dressing, and moving in bed. Supervise nurses\u2019 aides and assistants. Answer the patient\u2019s call and determine how to assist them. Collect samples such as blood, urine, and sputum from patients and perform routine laboratory tests on samples. Clean rooms and make beds. Inventory and requisition supplies and instruments. Record food and fluid intake and output. Models the Core Values of UAMS \u2013 Integrity, Respect, Diversity, Teamwork, Creativity, and Excellence in compliance with company guidelines. Performs related responsibilities as required or assigned. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), Resume Optional Documents: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of five Professional References (name, email, business title), Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Please upload a copy of your nursing license. Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Benton/Supply-Technician---UAMS-Health-Benton-Bryant_R0091094-1": {"title": "Supply Technician - UAMS Health Benton/Bryant", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/16/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Shift Vary (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: INA | Institutional Admin Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Supply Technician is responsible for proper handling and dispensing of medical/surgical supplies in clinical areas, supply par and inventory at the UAMS Health Benton/Bryant location. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: High School Diploma/GED. Six (6) months of experience in supply distribution preferably in a healthcare environment. Additional Information: Responsibilities: Responsible for accurately ordering and completely filling par levels of medical/surgical supplies in automated supply cabinets and manually controlled bulk par rooms.\u00a0 Checks par areas on a daily basis and as assigned; breaks down pallets and delivers supplies on carts; refills central supply inventory locations and adjust inventory counts.\u00a0 Counts, manages and places replenishment orders as needed.\u00a0 Rotates supplies into Sterile and non-sterile area's on shelves, specialty carts, floors on the FIFO (first in, first out) basis when restocking; daily checks supplies for package integrity and outdates and removes damaged or outdated supplies.\u00a0 Performs cycle counts and corrects on a daily basis and as needed to ensure accurate inventory counts.\u00a0 Maintains cabinets and carts in assigned areas in a neat and orderly basis; organizes shelves, bins and labels and keeps the supply areas clean; follows through on needed repairs to cabinets and carts; removes unauthorized/excessive/damaged/outdated supplies.\u00a0 Staffs the Central Supply dispatch window and tube system as assigned; issues and records, supplies that are sent via pick up, delivery or tube system.\u00a0 Issues out procedural trays and carts and records the issuance.\u00a0 Responsible for after hour delivery of isolation cart. Physical Requirements: Stand: Frequently Sit: Occasionally Walk: Frequently Bend, crawl, crouch, kneel, stoop or reach overhead: Frequently Lift and carry weight: 50+ lbs. Push and pull weight: 50+ lbs. Use hands to touch, handle or feel: Frequently Talk: Frequently Hear: Continuously Taste or smell: None Read, concentrate, and think analytically: Continuously Physical Environment : Inside Medical Facility Environment Noise Level: Moderate Visual Requirements: Color discrimination, Near visual acuity Hazards: Dust Salary Information: \"Commensurate with education and experience\" Required Documents to Apply: List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Benton/Program-Administrator---UAMS-Health-Benton-Bryant_R0091084-1": {"title": "Program Administrator - UAMS Health Benton/Bryant", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/16/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Shift Vary (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: HBB | UMH Benton/Bryant Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Program Administrator supports the administrative needs of the UAMS Health Benton/Bryant location and is responsible for developing & maintaining scheduling templates in Epic & coordinating schedule changes. The Program Administrator will be assigned various projects; will prepare & analyze reports; and will assist in coordinating the daily operations at this location. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelors Degree in a directly related field plus 4 years program/project administration or related experience OR High School Diploma plus 8 years program/project administration or related experience. Experience in a medical office setting and Epic Cadence experience preferred. Required to attend Epic training and pass required exams within one year of hire. Preferred Qualifications: Clinical chart review and abstraction experience Experience in bariatric surgery, weight\u2011management programs, or chronic disease management Familiarity with insurance authorization processes Experience in an academic medical center or research\u2011oriented environment Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Knowledge of medical terminology, basic anatomy, physiology, and disease process is required. Knowledge and comfort with Microsoft Office products is essential for success in this position (Word and Excel experience is required; PowerPoint experience strongly preferred). Strong communication, organizational, and interpersonal skills. Ability to work effectively with diverse patient populations and multidisciplinary teams. Ability to work effectively with diverse patient populations and multidisciplinary teams. Additional Information: Responsibilities: Template Administration: \u00a0Develops & maintains clinic scheduling templates, decision trees, diagnosis matrices, and scheduling criteria for all providers in the service line. \u00a0Builds & updates templates directly in Epic as needed. \u00a0Works closely with IT to maintain accurate decision trees in Epic. \u00a0Manages clinic block processes Provides technical and customer support for providers and access staff utilizing Epic scheduling templates. \u00a0Meets regularly with providers & access staff to review scheduling templates, making recommendations to optimize schedules and ensuring compliance with Access Committee guidelines Monitors clinic schedules and works closely with clinic and appointment center access staff to ensure accurate and efficient use of provider time Develops formal written documentation of policies & processes Develops & designs reports. \u00a0Collects, compiles & analyzes data from a variety of sources. \u00a0Identifies outliers or variances. \u00a0Develops & implements action plan to address outliers or variances Maintains departmental organizational charts & distribution lists Manages, consults and advises on projects or programs and provides general support as necessary. Responsible for the overall direction of assigned specialized projects Cross trained to provide coverage on various administrative functions Performs related responsibilities as required or assigned Physical Requirements: Exerting up to 10 pounds of force occasionally and/or negligible amount of force frequently or constantly. Sedentary work involves sitting most of the time. The Employee is required to have close visual acuity to perform an activity such as: preparing and analyzing data and figures; transcribing; viewing a computer terminal; extensive reading; and/or visual inspection at distances close to the eyes. The Employee is not substantially exposed to adverse environmental conditions (such as in typical office or administrative work). F requent physical activities: Feeling; Grasping; Hearing; Kneeling; Lifting; Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding; Pulling; Pushing; Reaching; Repetitive Motion; Sharps; Sitting; Standing; Stooping; Talking; Walking Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Inpatient-Certified-Procedural-Coding-Specialist_R0091015-1": {"title": "Inpatient Certified Procedural Coding Specialist", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/17/2026 Type of Position: Other Health Care - Clinical Support Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: FIN | CORE Coding - Inpatient Review Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: **This is a remote coding position** The Certified Procedural Coding Specialist \u2013 Inpatient reviews and interprets inpatient health records to identify diagnoses and procedures that impact the current hospital encounter. This position ensures documentation supports all assigned diagnoses and procedures and selects the appropriate ICD-10 and CPT codes within established deadlines. The specialist also reviews documentation for medical necessity, assigns working diagnoses and DRGs, identifies expected length of stay and Core Measure cases as applicable, and conducts periodic reviews throughout the patient\u2019s hospitalization. Additionally, the specialist collaborates with Clinical Documentation Specialists II to identify and address documentation deficiencies to support accurate and complete coding. Qualifications: High School diploma/GED with one of the following certifications: CCA, CCS, CPC, RHIT, or RHIA, with two (2) years of coding experience\u00a0required. Must be self-directed with critical thinking and collaborative abilities. Preferred Qualification: Degree in Health Information Management or related field. Two years of inpatient coding experience in an acute care facility, in a multi-service/specialty setting. Current CCS certification preferred. Responsibilities: Complete final review of medical record and select appropriate ICD-10 and \u00a0CPT codes within 4 \u00a0days of patient discharge as assigned. Review documentation to match appropriate codes with documentation for medical necessity. Review records upon admission and periodically throughout hospitalization to assign working diagnosis and DRG, expected length of stay, and identification of Core Measures cases as assigned.\u00a0 Work collaboratively with the Clinical Documentation Specialists II to identify and address documentation deficiencies.\u00a0 Performs other duties as assigned. Additional Information: Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience. Required Documents to Apply: List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Repetitive Motion, Sitting Frequent Physical Activity: Grasping, Hearing, Reaching, Talking Occasional Physical Activity: Crouching, Feeling, Kneeling, Lifting, Pulling, Pushing, Standing, Stooping Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Locksmith_R0090767-1": {"title": "Locksmith", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/24/2026 Type of Position: Professional Staff - Facilities Job Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ISS | TSS Services & Keys Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: *This is a temporary position* Under direct supervision, the Locksmith provides accurate and timely troubleshooting of electronic and mechanical lock hardware and systems. This position participates in a group 24 hours a day, 7 days a week 365 days a year on-call rotation where each member of the group takes call for 1 week at a time. Qualifications: High School Diploma/GED plus five (5) years of Cabling, low-voltage systems, carpentry/building maint., and mechanical/electronic lock systems required. Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in Information Technology, Computer Science, or related field. Customer Service experience. Responsibilities: Perform installations of mechanical and electronic control systems, which may include door access control, mechanical locks, keypads, electronic locks, Wi-Fi locks, and associated hardware. Respond to situations where lock hardware or systems have failed and action must be taken to isolate or repair problem equipment or software, or make configuration changes to return locking systems to full functionality. Process key requests and issue keys, and ensure that the Simple K platform is kept up to date.\u00a0 Perform other duties as assigned. Additional Information: Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Criminal Background Check This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: Crawling, Crouching, Feeling, Hearing, Kneeling, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Reaching, Sitting, Standing, Stooping, Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Computer-Tomography-Technologist_R0088234-1": {"title": "Computer Tomography Technologist", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 10/02/2026 Type of Position: Other Health Care - Clinical Support Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | IGSL Computed Tomography IOP C Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The CT Technologist will be responsible for providing quality diagnostic imaging for medical interpretation. Duties will include: operating CT equipment, handling patients, venipuncture, post-processing of images, patient transport, working with electronic medical records, and communication with physicians, and other services. This position also includes call and holidays. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: High School Diploma or GED PLUS Graduate of an approved Radiology program New graduate or less than one (1) year of CT experience Registry eligible or Registered by the American Registry of Radiologic Technologists. An Arkansas Radiologic Technologist License must be obtained before the start date. CT Advanced Certification by the American Registry of Radiologic Technologists must be obtained within 12 months of the date of hire Ability to Follow Oral Instruction, Read, and Write Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor\u2019s Degree in Radiological Sciences 1 or more years of experience as a CT technologist Advanced Registry by the American Registry of Radiologic Technologists in Computed Tomography Additional Information: Responsibilities: Operation of CT imaging equipment and post-processing of data Handling patients Venipuncture Use of EPIC Call and holiday coverage Communicate with patients, physicians, clinics, and other services in the hospital in an effective, professional, and courteous manner. Responsible for maintaining their professional license(s), National Registry, and all annual competencies. Other duties may be assigned to this position Salary Information: commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry, Substance Abuse Testing This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Feeling, Grasping, Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Repetitive Motion, Sharps, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Feeling, Grasping, Hearing, Lifting, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Repetitive Motion, Sharps, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Crouching, Kneeling, Stooping Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-Arkansas-at-Pine-Bluff/Research-Specialist-Farm-technician_R0090030": {"title": "Research Specialist/Farm technician", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Research Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff The University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff is an 1890 Land-Grant HBCU with a diverse student population, competitive degree offerings and stellar faculty. For more than 140 years, the University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff has worked to create an environment that inculcates learning, growth and productivity while affording a basic need to its students \u2013 a chance to advance. The 15:1 student to teacher ratio makes it possible to maintain a learning environment with close interaction between students and faculty while challenging curricula encourage our students to seek and fulfill their potential. You can excel in your chosen field of study through a curriculum of \u00a0 Certificate and Associates degree programs,\u00a0 more than thirty\u00a0 Undergraduate programs, Master\u2019s degree programs and a Doctorate program in Aquaculture/Fisheries. You can also develop workplace readiness through internships, co-ops and fellowships in the U.S. and abroad. Out-of-class experiences and student involvement include more than 90 student organizations, an internationally renowned Vesper Choir, Marching Band, Concert Bands, Wind Symphony, nationally recognized debate team, award-winning theater department and accomplished athletic program. Though the main campus is in Pine Bluff, its reach is worldwide. UAPB has an extended campus in North Little Rock and offers as well as online courses. With the addition of the Arkansas Research and Education Optical Network (ARE-ON), students can engage in information exchange with others anywhere in the world. There are also Research and Extension offices in Lonoke, Newport and Lake Village and collaborations with other colleges and universities in the State through the National Science Foundation funded STEM (Science, Technology, Engineering and Mathematics) Academy. As the second oldest land-grant institution in the state of Arkansas, the mission of this No Excuse University remains the same \u2013 to provide a high quality, affordable education with a personal touch. We invite you to Become a Part of the Pride at the University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process and require reasonable accommodations, please contact Human Resources at 870.575.8400 . Department: SAFHS Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The prospective candidate will be responsible for assisting the Livestock Technician in the management of the UAPB Livestock Farm, which includes managing livestock animals (E.g., Cows, goats, sheep, chickens, rabbits, etc.). The candidate will assist the Livestock Technician and the UAPB farm manager. The candidate will also oversee the cleanliness, well-maintained, and/or working animal facilities, including cattle handling facility, goat barn, farrowing house, pig fattening and weaning units, rabbit hutches, and poultry facility. This individual will also assist and facilitate student outreach activities during laboratory sessions and on and off-campus farm demonstrations. May have to work on some weekends. Qualifications: A minimum of a high school diploma with 3-5+ years of experience working on a livestock farm, with 2+ years of experience. Individuals must have experience in farm maintenance and general animal husbandry. Additional Information: Salary Information: $39,000 Required Documents to Apply: Letters of Recommendation, Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants (Please upload all required documents in the \"Resume\" attachment section of your application to be considered for this position) : Please submit 2 letters of recommendation and upload in the Resume portion of the application. Recruitment Contact Information: Sharron M. Williams Employment Manager University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff 1200 N. University Drive Mail Slot 4942 Pine Bluff, AR 71601 Phone: (870) 575-8403 williamssm@uapb.edu www.uapb.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Motor Vehicle Reports Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff may conduct pre-employment background checks on certain positions for applicants being considered for employment. \u00a0 The background checks may include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. \u00a0 Required checks are identified in the position listing. \u00a0 A criminal background check or arrest pending adjudication information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absences of a relationship to the requirements of the position. \u00a0 Background check information will be used in a consistent, non-discriminatory manner consistent with the state and federal law. \u00a0 The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: Climbing, Crawling, Crouching, Kneeling, Lifting, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Standing, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Driving, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting, Talking Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAMS/Patient-Representative--Northwest--AR-_R0090824-1": {"title": "Patient Representative (Northwest, AR)", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/16/2026 Type of Position: Clinical Staff - Nursing Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | MUSL NWA Van Asche Access Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: We are looking for a proactive, detail-oriented individual to join our Ortho Clinical Administration team as a Patient Representative. The Patient Representative at UAMS Ortho Clinic plays a vital role in patient scheduling, financial counseling, and revenue cycle management, operating under general supervision. Key responsibilities include advising patients on their financial obligations, connecting them with sponsoring agencies, and ensuring adherence to financial policies. The role also involves managing high-risk pre-certifications, developing strategies to prevent denials, and generating reports to maintain financial accuracy. Additionally, the Patient Representative ensures precise record-keeping, collaborates with insurance providers, and handles billing inquiries. This position contributes to improving the clinic's operational efficiency and enhances patient satisfaction. If you are experienced in financial counseling and revenue cycle management, we encourage you to apply and help us deliver exceptional care to our patients. This position will support UAMS Ortho Clinic locations in Northwest Arkansas, including Fayetteville and Bentonville. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: High School Diploma/GED plus four (4) years of experience in customer service, call center, business office administration, registration, billing, insurance, or scheduling. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities: Ability to follow oral instructions, read, and write. Computer/basic keyboard skills, telephone etiquette skills, General knowledge of office machines, including printers and scanners. Excellent customer service skills. Understanding of financial counseling and revenue cycle management. Ability to manage high-risk pre-certifications and develop denial avoidance strategies. Proficiency in producing and analyzing financial reports to ensure accuracy. Detail-oriented and patient-focused, with experience in financial counseling and revenue cycle functions. Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in Business, Healthcare, or related OR Associates Degree plus two (2) years of experience in customer service, call center, business office administration, medical office registration, billing, or scheduling. Additional Information: Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Repetitive Motion, Sitting Frequent Physical Activity: Standing, Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Grasping, Kneeling, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Stooping Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Fayetteville-AR/Director-of-Executive-Education_R0089650": {"title": "Director of Executive Education", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com, then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at all University of Arkansas institutions will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students.\u201d University of Arkansas, Fayetteville students will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Student Jobs at UAF.\u201d All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. Closing Date: 09/20/2026 Type of Position: Outreach Programs Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas, Fayetteville Founded in 1871, the University of Arkansas is a land grant institution, classified by the Carnegie Foundation among the nation\u2019s top 2 percent of universities with the highest level of research activity. The University of Arkansas works to advance the state and build a better world through education, research, and outreach by providing transformational opportunities and skills, fostering a welcoming climate, and nurturing creativity, discovery, and the spread of new ideas and innovations. The University of Arkansas campus is located in Fayetteville, a welcoming community ranked as one of the best places to live in the U.S. The growing region surrounding Fayetteville is home to numerous Fortune 500 companies and one of the nation\u2019s strongest economies. Northwest Arkansas is also quickly gaining a national reputation for its focus on the arts and overall quality of life. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10% of employee salary. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions, you should review before applying for the opening. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process, please submit a request via the Disability Accommodations | OEOC | University of Arkansas (uark.edu) : Request an Accommodation. Appli\u00adcants are required to submit a request for each position of which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 479.575.5351. Department: Executive Education Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Director of Executive Education is responsible for leading business development and revenue generation efforts for the Walton College Executive Education unit. This position develops and implements strategies to expand the client base, increase program revenue, and support the financial sustainability of executive education initiatives. The Director builds and manages relationships with external organizations, identifies professional workforce development needs, and collaborates with faculty and internal partners to design and deliver executive education programs. The position is accountable for revenue performance, client acquisition, account growth, long-term partnership development, and supervision of the Executive Education staff. Regular, reliable, and non-disruptive attendance is an essential job duty, as is the ability to create and maintain collegial, harmonious working relationships with others. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor\u2019s degree from an accredited institution in business, communications, adult education, or other related field Experience in business development, corporate sales, executive education, professional learning, or a related field, including direct responsibility for revenue generation, client acquisition, and closing complex service or program agreements Experience developing and executing revenue growth strategies, forecasting, and performance reporting. Experience negotiating contracts, pricing structures, and service agreements Experience leading consultative sales engagements and translating organizational needs into structured service or program solutions. Experience collaborating with senior leaders within complex organizations Experience supervising professional staff or leading cross-functional teams Preferred Qualifications : Master\u2019s degree or MBA in Business, Organizational Leadership, Higher Education, or other related field from an accredited institution Experience in executive education or university-based professional development Experience managing long-term client partnerships that result in sustained revenue growth Additional Information: Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Recruitment Contact Information: Blythe Eggleston Executive Director, Executive Education and Strategic Engagement Beggleston@walton.uark.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Special Instructions to Applicants: Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas seeks to attract, develop and retain high quality faculty, staff and administrators that consistently display practices and behaviors to advance a culture that embeds equal opportunity, educational excellence and unparalleled access for all. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All Application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAMS---NWA/NWA-Charge-RN_R0087868-1": {"title": "NWA Charge RN (Outpatient M-F)", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/30/2026 Type of Position: Clinical Staff - Nursing Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: REP | PCPHSL CS NWA Fayetteville Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: We are seeking a dedicated and experienced Registered Nurse (RN) to join our team as a Charge Nurse in our designated clinic. As the Charge Nurse, you will be responsible for ensuring the delivery of the highest quality Patient and Family-Centered Care within the clinic. You will oversee the nursing and clinical team, manage the patient flow processes, and promote wellness, improved outcomes, and self-care among a defined patient population. Additionally, you will play a crucial role in providing support, education, and assistance to patients who have chronic conditions, helping them prevent and maintain their health. As the Charge Nurse the individual will work with the CSM in the daily operations and supervision of the clinic and staff. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Graduate of accredited nursing program.\u00a0Baccalaureate Degree, ADN Degree, or Diploma RN.\u202f Minimum of one (1) year of RN clinical experience. Valid Arkansas Registered Nursing License. American Heart Association Basic Life Support Certification.\u00a0 Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: The ability to work independently, maintain high-quality care, and the application of policies will be required. Good communication skills (written and oral). Excellent customer service skills. Problem-solving skills. Leadership and collaborative skills. Strong patient advocacy and patient education skills. Strong organizational skills and computer knowledge. Professional and courteous telephone etiquette. General knowledge of office machines, including printers, fax machines, and scanners. Understanding basic medical terminology is necessary. Preferred Qualifications: Three (3) years of RN experience. Will consider RN with one (1) year of RN clinical experience and two (2) years LPN clinical experience. One (1) year clinic/ambulatory setting experience. Charge nurse and/or leadership experience. Additional Information: Key Responsibilities : Assist with scheduling, payroll, staffing issues, communication between staff and providers, clinical/nursing staff education and training, policy compliance and maintaining quality measures. Triage, assessment, planning, implementation, and evaluation of nursing care and patient education either by telephone or within the UAMS Clinic.\u00a0 Delivers nursing care according to standards as defined by UAMS, American Nurses Association (ANA), AR State Board of Nursing (ASBN), and those set forth by nursing specialty organizations. Coordinates care and/or follow-up for patients who receive care in inpatient and outpatient facilities.\u00a0 Implements patient care using an approach that is interdisciplinary and Patient and Family-Centered Care. Effectively collaborates and communicates with nursing staff at all levels, interdisciplinary teams, executive leaders, and other stakeholders. May perform other duties as assigned to support the mission of UAMS. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of five Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Criminal Background Check, Substance Abuse Testing This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sharps, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Feeling, Grasping, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Lifting, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Sharps, Stooping Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Medical-Laboratory-Scientist-I---Hematology_R0090898-1": {"title": "Medical Laboratory Scientist I - Hematology Night Shift", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/16/2026 Type of Position: Other Health Care - Clinical Support Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Shift Vary (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | LPSL CPATH Hematology-General Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Medical Laboratory Scientist I \u2013 Hematology performs a variety of routine and specialized laboratory testing in the hematology department to support accurate diagnosis, treatment, and monitoring of patients. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor of Science degree in Medical Laboratory Sciences, Medical Laboratory Technology, Biology, or Chemistry Must have or be eligible for ASCP certification. Certification must be obtained within 12 months of hire. \u200b Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor of Science degree in Medical Laboratory Sciences Active ASCP certification Previous clinical laboratory experience, preferably in hematology Additional Information: Job Requirements: Conduct analysis of blood, urine, spinal fluid, body fluids and other biological samples to determine presence of normal and abnormal components in assigned section(s). \u00a0Perform quality controls or quality check materials and perform corrective action as required.\u00a0 Enter test results and other data related to analysis and communication of results into relevant computer information systems or other document archival systems. Provide technical information about specimen collection, sample transport, sample identification, required documents, test methods and other related technical information to RN\u2019s, physicians or laboratory clients.\u00a0 Use laboratory computer systems to order tests, generate results, generate reports, document results and communications, interpret results, and other lab duties related to inventory, testing method verifications and quality control. The core laboratory uses multiple information systems including Microsoft Office software programs, instrument specific programs, automation line software and middleware, programs for test interpretation, server databases, laboratory information system, quality control programs, inventory control software, document control and online programs related to employee continuing education and training. \u00a0 Set-up, maintain and operate lab automation systems used to process samples.\u00a0 Operate, calibrate and maintain equipment used in analysis such as spectrophotometers, analyzers, microscopes, slide stainers, diluters, and computer controlled high volume analyzers, mixers, rotators, pipettes.\u00a0 Perform basic troubleshooting on equipment used to perform testing. Maintain equipment used for personal protection and safety such as eyewashes, safety showers, biohazard containers, hoods, chemical cabinets and personal protective equipment. Maintain temperature dependent equipment such as refrigerators, freezers, incubators, water baths, heat blocks. Daily quality control review. Organize and clean workspaces. Ensure adequate supplies required for daily operations are available by restocking inventory, preparing reagents, rotating stock as required. Communicate with clinics, physicians and external staff regarding sample integrity issues and/or critical values. Other duties as assigned PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS Stand: Frequently Sit: Frequently Walk: Occasionally Bend, crawl, crouch, kneel, stoop or reach overhead: Frequently Lift and carry weight: 25 lbs Push and pull weight: 25 lbs Use hands to touch, handle or feel: Frequently Talk: Continuously Hear: Continuously Taste or smell: Occasionally Read, concentrate, think analytically: Continuously Physical Environment : Inside Medical Facility Environment Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), Proof of Veteran Status, Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting, Standing, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting, Standing, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Kneeling, Lifting, Pulling, Pushing Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Lab-Support-Technician-I---Blood-Bank_R0090949-1": {"title": "Lab Support Technician I - Blood Bank", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/16/2026 Type of Position: Clinical Staff - Medical Ancillary Support Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Shift Vary (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | LPSL CPATH Transfusion Service Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The purpose of this position is to organize and coordinate the actives of the front desk from receiving patient samples, ordering the tests, preparing aliquots of blood for the neonate population to issuing blood and blood components. The position requires a lot of interaction between the clients of the UAMS blood bank. The person at the front desk is the first voice the clients hear. The position will assist in blood inventory management in order to ensure the amount of available inventory is acceptable at all times. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: High School Diploma/GED Preferred Qualifications: Previous clinical laboratory or medical office experience Additional Information: Job Requirements: Modifies blood and blood components suitable for each patient's need Interact with Blood Bank staff and hospital staff in order to facilitate patient care. Receives patient samples, orders tests, issues blood products, and centrifuge samples Manages available blood component inventory to ensure appropriate levels are maintained. Perform other duties as needed. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS Stand: Frequently Sit: Frequently Walk: Occasionally Bend, crawl, crouch, kneel, stoop or reach overhead: Frequently Lift and carry weight: 25 lbs Push and pull weight: 25 lbs Use hands to touch, handle or feel: Frequently Talk: Continuously Hear: Continuously Taste or smell: Occasionally Read, concentrate, think analytically: Continuously Physical Environment : Inside Medical Facility Environment Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Criminal Background Check, Substance Abuse Testing This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding Frequent Physical Activity: Feeling, Grasping, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Repetitive Motion, Sharps, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Crouching, Kneeling, Lifting, Stooping Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Medical-Laboratory-Scientist-I---Microbiology-PRN_R0090953-1": {"title": "Medical Laboratory Scientist I - Microbiology PRN", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/16/2026 Type of Position: Clinical Staff - Medical Ancillary Support Job Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Shift Vary (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | LPSL CPATH Microbiology Staff Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: As a bench technologist in Microbiology, this person is responsible for processing, evaluating patient specimens, performing tests to identify microorganisms or antigens according to written procedures and perform susceptibilities. This person will also record and evaluate daily, weekly, and monthly QC in their assigned areas for further review by the supervisor. This position requires one to maintain safe work practices, follow all regulatory requirements and engage supervisor, manager, or director as appropriate. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelors degree in medical laboratory sciences, Medical Technology or an ASCP approved discipline (chemistry or biology) CHT (ABHI) certification within 1 year of eligibility. If eligible at time of hire, certification must be obtained within 1 year of hire date. Additional Information: Job Requirements: Processing patient specimens such as blood, urine, sputum, stool, wound cultures, and body fluids Performing microbial cultures to grow and isolate organisms Identifying microorganisms using biochemical tests, microscopy, automated analyzers, and molecular methods Conducting Gram stains and other differential staining procedures Performing antimicrobial susceptibility testing to determine effective antibiotics Operating and maintaining laboratory instruments and analyzers Reviewing and verifying test results for accuracy before reporting Following strict quality control and quality assurance procedures Maintaining compliance with Clinical Laboratory Improvement Amendments (CLIA), College of American Pathologists (CAP), and safety standards Using aseptic technique and biosafety precautions when handling infectious materials Communicating critical test results to physicians, nurses, and infection prevention teams Assisting with outbreak investigations and infection control monitoring Training students, new employees, or laboratory assistants Documenting laboratory findings in electronic medical record and laboratory information systems Perform other duties as needed. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS Stand: Frequently Sit: Frequently Walk: Occasionally Bend, crawl, crouch, kneel, stoop or reach overhead: Frequently Lift and carry weight: 25 lbs Push and pull weight: 25 lbs Use hands to touch, handle or feel: Frequently Talk: Continuously Hear: Continuously Taste or smell: Occasionally Read, concentrate, think analytically: Continuously Physical Environment : Inside Medical Facility Environment Noise Level : Moderate Visual Requirements: Color discrimination, Depth perception, Far visual acuity, Near visual acuity Hazards: Biological, Chemical, Dust, Electrical, Fumes/Gases/Odors, Radiation, Sharp objects/tools Salary Information: $33.76 per hour Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), Proof of Veteran Status, Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Criminal Background Check, Substance Abuse Testing This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding Frequent Physical Activity: Feeling, Grasping, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Repetitive Motion, Sharps, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Crouching, Kneeling, Lifting, Stooping Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Medical-Lab-Technician---Chemistry---PRN_R0090952-1": {"title": "Medical Lab Technician - Chemistry - PRN", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/16/2026 Type of Position: Other Health Care - Medical Ancillary Support Job Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Shift Vary (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | LPSL CPATH Chemistry Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: A Medical Laboratory Technician performs laboratory tests and conducts analysis of blood, urine, spinal fluid, body fluids and other biological samples to determine presence of normal and abnormal components. Enters results in electronic medical record and performs quality controls to verify accurate test results. Maintains and operates laboratory equipment and instruments. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Associate of Science in Medical Laboratory Technician from a regionally accredited school or program that is recognized by ASCP. Eligible to take the ASCP or equivalent certification board exam as a Medical Laboratory Technician. Must pass the exam within 1 year of hire or eligible date. Preferred Qualifications: Previous clinical laboratory experience ASCP certification Additional Information: Job Requirements: Set-up, maintain and operate lab automation systems used to process samples. Operate, calibrate and maintain equipment used in analysis such as spectrophotometers, analyzers, microscopes, slide stainers, diluters, and computer controlled high volume analyzers, mixers, rotators, pipettes. Perform basic troubleshooting on equipment used to perform testing. Maintain equipment used for personal protection and safety such as eyewashes, safety showers, biohazard containers, hoods, chemical cabinets and personal protective equipment. Maintain temperature dependent equipment such as refrigerators, freezers, incubators, water baths, heat blocks. Conduct analysis of blood, urine, spinal fluid, body fluids and other biological samples to determine presence of normal and abnormal components in assigned section(s). Perform quality controls or quality check materials and perform corrective action as required. Enter test results and other data related to analysis and communication of results into relevant computer information systems or other document archival systems. Provide technical information about specimen collection, sample transport, sample identification, required documents, test methods and other related technical information to RN, physicians or laboratory clients. Use laboratory computer systems to order tests, generate results, generate reports, document results and communications, interpret results, and other lab duties related to inventory, testing method verifications and quality control. Perform other duties as needed. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS Stand: Frequently Sit: Frequently Walk: Occasionally Bend, crawl, crouch, kneel, stoop or reach overhead: Frequently Lift and carry weight: 25 lbs Push and pull weight: 25 lbs Use hands to touch, handle or feel: Frequently Talk: Continuously Hear: Continuously Taste or smell: Occasionally Read, concentrate, think analytically: Continuously Physical Environment : Inside Medical Facility Environment Noise Level : Moderate Visual Requirements: Color discrimination, Depth perception, Far visual acuity, Near visual acuity Hazards: Biological, Chemical, Dust, Electrical, Fumes/Gases/Odors, Radiation, Sharp objects/tools Salary Information: $24.57 per hour Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), Proof of Veteran Status, Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Criminal Background Check, Substance Abuse Testing This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding Frequent Physical Activity: Feeling, Grasping, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Repetitive Motion, Sharps, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Crouching, Kneeling, Lifting, Stooping Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Intermediate-Contracts-Analyst_R0089739-1": {"title": "Intermediate Contracts Analyst", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/17/2026 Type of Position: Professional Staff - Project/Program Administration Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: FIN | Finance SC Contracts Clinical Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Intermediate Contracts Analyst reports to the Manager, Contracts and is responsible for the effective maintenance of contract data files and the integrity of contract pricing. The role includes coordinating and preforming analyses of product usage and pricing to optimize Group Purchasing Organization (\u201cGPO\u201d), GPO Enhanced, State, and Local Contracts with an emphasis on identifying cost-saving and expense reduction. The individual will ensure the adherence to best practices in contract management, analysis, and reporting, ensuring all contracts and databases remain accurate and current. The position is also responsible for verifying contract compliance with Arkansas State Procurement Law, DFA Policies, relevant Board of Trustees and U of A Systemwide Policies, and Procedures and UAMS Administrative Guide Policies and Procedures, as applicable. Assists with financial analysis, contract negotiations, and the execution of purchase agreements/contracts for the procurement of goods, services, and equipment for clinical and non-clinical areas, while proactively identifying opportunities for cost savings, cost avoidance, standardization and enhanced utilization. Qualifications: Minimum: Bachelor\u2019s degree in supply chain management, business administration or related field plus three (3) years of experience in healthcare supply chain contracting, procurement or relevant work experience or Associates' degree in related field plus (5) five years of healthcare supply chain contracting, procurement or relevant work experience or high school diploma plus (7) seven years of healthcare supply chain contracting, procurement or relevant work experience Strong knowledge of contract negotiation, contract management, and procurement best practices Ability to analyze and interpret contract data and spend analysis Excellent communication skills, both written and verbal Proficient in Microsoft Office Suite and contract management software (e.g., Ntracts, Ariba) Strong attention to detail and ability to manage multiple tasks and deadlines Ability to work on a computer for eight hours in an office setting and perform office related tasks such as filing, record storage, etc Preferred: Clinical Experience (Surgical Technologist, RN, LPN) Experience in healthcare contracts management or financial analytics/auditing CPSM (Certified Professional in Supply Management) or CPCM (Certified Professional Contracts Manager) Additional Information: Responsibilities: \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Manages a portfolio of contracts ensuring that all documentation is current, complete, accurate and maintained in the appropriate databases. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Recognized as Subject Matter Expert (SME) in assigned contract portfolio.\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Manages the entire lifecycle of contracts from initiation to renewal, and or termination.\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Independently evaluates contract language under the review and guidance of legal counsel.\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Communicates changes as appropriate, in accordance with UAMS policies, guidelines and state laws. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Performs audits and provides reports on contract status, contract spending and identifies opportunities for savings and improving contract penetration.\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Negotiates terms and best price on all supplies, services and equipment as directed.\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Attends and presents for regular meetings with stakeholders and vendor partners to review quarterly performance.\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Works collaboratively with various internal departments, external resources, and/or finance and department leaders to resolve issues, while keeping leadership informed of progress and resolutions. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Meets with suppliers to coordinate efforts for improved services and pricing.\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Evaluates supplier performance through quarterly reviews, performance KPIs and customer feedback. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Resolves issues and implements solutions to address negative supplier performance.\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Communicates performance issues with suppliers and provides a schedule for resolution. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Collaborate with leadership to identify long-term contracting and procurement strategies to maximize cost efficiency and operational effectiveness. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Maintains abreast of all industry trends, market conditions, technological innovation and ethical standards in the contracting profession.\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Reacts and adapts to changes in contracting strategies to be aware that research findings have the potential to significantly impact UAMS operations.\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Attends educational events to increase knowledge of all state procurement, accounting regulations, and the University of Arkansas System\u2019s procedures and regulations. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Performs other duties as assigned. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Repetitive Motion, Sitting Frequent Physical Activity: Hearing, Talking Occasional Physical Activity: Reaching, Standing, Stooping, Walking Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Proton-Dosimetrist-PRN_R0091014-1": {"title": "Proton Dosimetrist PRN", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/09/2026 Type of Position: Clinical Staff - Clinical Support Job Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Shift Vary (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | CASL Proton Dosimetry Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: This position is responsible for providing physicians and therapists with treatment planning, calculations, quality assurance planning, constructing custom blocks as needed for patient treatment, taking required measurements on patients, consulting with physicians and other therapists in planning and delivering patient treatments and maintaining quality control. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree plus certification as a Medical Dosimetrist by the Medical Dosimetry Certification Board (MDCB) or eligible after completion of a JRCERT-accredited program in Medical Dosimetry Certification as a Medical Dosimetrist by the Medical Dosimetry Certification Board (MDCB) within 18 months of hire Preferred Qualifications: MDCB certification Technical skill in mathematics and physics as normally acquired in freshman and sophomore college level coursework for science majors or in completing an accredited dosimetry dosimetry program. Math coursework should include 2 semesters of algebra, one semester of pre-ca pre-calculus and one semester of calculus. Math coursework requirements may be for waived for appropriate amount of amount of workplace experience obtained by working in the medical dosimetry field. Knowledge of\u00a0 treatment planning techniques,\u00a0 record and verify techniques, scheduling, physician protocols or (prerogatives), equipment and/or software operation, safety and quality control guidelines as acquired through clinical rotation of all treatment areas (machines) for a period of one year. Additional Information: Responsibilities: Designs patient treatment plans and prepares dose calculations by using computers, calculators, and manual techniques for external beam treatment planning. Consults with physicians and therapists to ensure accurate patient information and dose calculations. Collaborates with radiation therapy staff to assess and improve patient treatments and/or set-up techniques. Shares results and recommendations with their supervisor, as appropriate. Assists radiation therapists with patient set-up procedures at the treatment machine and/or simulator as needed. Completes proper records, patient data forms, planning documents, and billing information logs. Checks patient charts for accuracy and proper documentation according to established procedures. Monitors and adheres to general radiation safety guidelines. Participates in clinical research and quality improvement processes, as necessary. Performs other duties as assigned. Salary Information: PRN Rate $100/hour Required Documents to Apply: List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Criminal Background Check, Substance Abuse Testing This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting Frequent Physical Activity: Talking Occasional Physical Activity: Standing, Walking Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Police-Sergeant_R0090611-1": {"title": "Police Sergeant", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/18/2026 Type of Position: Professional Staff - Public Safety Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: POL | Police 2nd Shift Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Police Sergeant works under the general supervision of the Chief of Police and the direct supervision of the Patrol Lieutenant. This position supervises assigned Patrol Officers and Dispatchers and is responsible for enforcing traffic laws, criminal laws, parking regulations, and departmental policies. The Police Sergeant supports a safe and secure environment for patients, employees, students, visitors, and the broader campus community. This position is governed by UAMS policies and the standards established by the Arkansas Commission on Law Enforcement Standards and Training. Qualifications: High school diploma or GED and at least two years of certified law enforcement experience. Candidates must be at least 21 years old, possess a valid Arkansas driver\u2019s license, and hold current Police Officer certification and a General Certificate from the Arkansas Commission on Law Enforcement Standards and Training (CLEST). Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Have basic computer skills with a general knowledge of Microsoft Office software. Ability to properly prepare and write police reports. Ability to communicate and maintain a good rapport with the campus population. Ability to engage in and maintain control of persons by use of minimal force needed in required situations. Knowledge of law enforcement practices, methods, and techniques. Knowledge of law enforcement traffic, criminal laws, and departmental regulations and procedures. Ability to enforce parking regulations. Ability to operate motor vehicles used in work activities Skill in the operations of firearms. Ability to walk a minimum of 8 to 12 miles in a 12-hour shift. Ability to climb stairwells. Additional Information: Responsibilities Supervises Patrol Officers and Dispatchers assigned to the shift. Manages work schedules, evaluates performance, provides training and development, and ensures compliance with departmental policies and procedures. Escalates employee grievances and significant performance concerns to the appropriate supervisor. Provides safety and security services for the campus community through foot and vehicle patrols, traffic control, building access assistance, patient transportation, and monitoring emergency response activities. Investigates campus accidents and incidents. Collects statements, evidence, and other relevant information and prepares detailed reports. May make arrests and provide court testimony as required. Performs other duties as assigned. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Fayetteville/Associate-Professor_R0090744-1": {"title": "Associate Professor of Exercise Science", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com, then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at all University of Arkansas institutions will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students.\u201d University of Arkansas, Fayetteville students will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Student Jobs at UAF.\u201d All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. Closing Date: Type of Position: Faculty - Tenure/Tenure Track Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: Yes Institution Name: University of Arkansas, Fayetteville Founded in 1871, the University of Arkansas is a land grant institution, classified by the Carnegie Foundation among the nation\u2019s top 2 percent of universities with the highest level of research activity. The University of Arkansas works to advance the state and build a better world through education, research, and outreach by providing transformational opportunities and skills, fostering a welcoming climate, and nurturing creativity, discovery, and the spread of new ideas and innovations. The University of Arkansas campus is located in Fayetteville, a welcoming community ranked as one of the best places to live in the U.S. The growing region surrounding Fayetteville is home to numerous Fortune 500 companies and one of the nation\u2019s strongest economies. Northwest Arkansas is also quickly gaining a national reputation for its focus on the arts and overall quality of life. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10% of employee salary. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions, you should review before applying for the opening. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process, please submit a request via the Disability Accommodations | OEOC | University of Arkansas (uark.edu) : Request an Accommodation. Appli\u00adcants are required to submit a request for each position of which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 479.575.5351. Department: Department of Health, Human Performance & Recreation Department's Website: https://hhpr.uark.edu/ Summary of Job Duties: The Position: The College of Education and Health Professions at the University of Arkansas, Fayetteville, invites nominations and applications for an Associate Professor of Exercise Science in the Department of Health, Human Performance, and Recreation. The Associate Professor of Exercise Science is a 9-month, tenured, full-time faculty position. The successful candidate will complement or add to existing strengths within the Exercise Science Program and the College of Education and Health Professions. We are seeking candidates who demonstrate both synergy with existing teaching strengths and a commitment to promoting a culture of research excellence. Primary Duties and Responsibilities of the tenured Associate Professor of Exercise Science include pursuing their established research agenda, securing external funding, mentoring and assisting early-career faculty in pursuing external funding opportunities, publishing in peer-reviewed journals, and presenting at professional conferences; teaching graduate and undergraduate courses in Exercise Science; supervising theses, dissertations, and honors projects; mentoring/advising both undergraduate and graduate students; and providing service to the department, college, university, community, and profession. The faculty member is responsible for fulfilling the core academic functions of teaching, scholarship/research/ creative activity, and service in support of the University\u2019s mission. This is an in-person position. On-campus presence is an essential function of this position. Extensive in-person engagement in activities such as office hours, student advising, collaborative work, and departmental, college, and university committee meetings is required to advance student success, departmental effectiveness, and the mission of the college and the university. Through teaching, research, and service, this position supports the University\u2019s 150 Forward priorities of student success, research excellence, and an employer-of-choice environment. Regular, reliable, and non-disruptive attendance is an essential job duty, as is the ability to create and maintain collegial, harmonious working relationships with others. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Earned doctorate from an accredited institution in Exercise Science or related field An established research agenda. The area of research inquiry is open, but focal areas include the following: metabolic health, cardiac physiology, respiratory physiology, molecular signaling, female-specific physiology, or multi-omics Evidence of sustained and ongoing exemplary research as evidenced by external funding, refereed peer-reviewed publications, and presentations Dedicated commitment and competence in teaching and instruction, as evidenced by effective teaching and student mentorship Evidence of participation in productive service to the department, college, university, and profession Preferred Qualifications: Evidence of interdisciplinary research bridging exercise science, health, and education Strong desire to mentor early-career faculty in developing strategies for external funding Additional Information: This position is a Designated Research Position \u00a0and is regulated by the Arkansas Research Education Protection Act of 2025 .\u00a0 Prior to issuance of an offer of employment, the University is required to request and obtain additional information about an applicant\u2019s background and, if required, conduct an additional review of that background information. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Curriculum Vitae, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title) Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Recruitment Contact Information: Dr. Brendon McDermott Department Head of Health, Human Performance, and Recreation brendonm@uark.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Special Instructions to Applicants: Completed applications received by October 1, 2026, will be assured full consideration. Late applications will be reviewed as necessary to fill the position. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas seeks to attract, develop and retain high quality faculty, staff and administrators that consistently display practices and behaviors to advance a culture that embeds equal opportunity, educational excellence and unparalleled access for all. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All Application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAG--University-of-Arkansas-Grantham/PT-Faculty---English_R0091001-2": {"title": "PT Faculty - English", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Adjunct Faculty Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Less than Annual Appointment (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas Grantham As an employer, the University of Arkansas Grantham offers a remote work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 - 10% of employee salary. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions, you should review before applying for the opening. If you need assistance with the application process, or if you are a person with a disability who would like to request a reasonable accommodation related to the application process, please contact the Department of Human Resources at hr@uagrantham.edu. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at recruiting@uagrantham.edu. Department: General Academics Team Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The University of Arkansas Grantham is looking for REMOTE Part Time Faculty in the following states: AL, AR, AZ, DE, FL, GA, KS, IA, ID, IN, KY, LA, MD, MI, MO, MS, NC, NE, NJ, OH, OK, SC, TN, TX, UT, VA, VT, WI and WY. Please only apply if you are able to live and work full-time in one of the states listed above. State locations and specifics are subject to change as our hiring requirements shift. POSITION DESCRIPTION: Part-time Faculty for University of Arkansas Grantham (UAG) have primary responsibility for online instruction and corresponding outreach to an approximate maximum load of 70 students at a given time. Part-time faculty serve in a remote capacity at the University. This position is for the designated college and will report to the Faculty Manager. Part-time faculty teach courses that may begin monthly or quarterly depending on the course and program. Courses are eight weeks in length and utilize the Blackboard Learning Management System. Each course week runs Wednesday through Tuesday midnight of the following week. Faculty are given access one week prior to the course start date to set up the course. KEY JOB RESPONSIBILITIES: \u25cf Follow all University policies as provided in the University Catalog and Faculty Handbook. \u25cf Provide instruction in accordance with the University and within the scope of departmentally-defined courses, programs of study, and degrees. \u25cf Responsibility includes timely interaction with students and quality assessment of student work with substantive feedback. \u25cf Provide weekly \u201coffice hours\u201d support and communicate (e.g., email, posting, live-chat, etc.) in a timely manner with students, other faculty and staff regarding student concerns or issues. \u25cf Faculty may take part in shared governance of curriculum, in some instances participating in curriculum development. \u25cf Participate in training on necessary technologies to facilitate courses. \u25cf Assume responsibility to keep current in the field of study/area of expertise and continue to develop professionally in content, methodologies, and distance-learning strategies. \u25cf Able to make decisions and work independently with exceptional problem solving and analytical skills. \u25cf Maintain accurate electronic records for both the learning management system maintenance as well as the University records system and submit all records when required. \u25cf Participate actively in faculty development opportunities (internally and externally). \u25cf Provide feedback concerning student and faculty issues. \u25cf Utilize the philosophy and objectives of University of Arkansas Grantham to create a positive growth environment for learning. Follow principles of good educational practice: provide ongoing contact between students, develop reciprocity/cooperation among students, use active learning techniques, give prompt feedback, emphasize time on task, communicate high expectations, and respect diverse talents and ways of learning. \u25cf Proactively participate with students within programs through teaching, welcome forums, recorded videos, etc. \u25cf Notify the appropriate University administrator of any course or course administration issues in a timely manner. \u25cf Other duties as assigned Qualifications: EDUCATION/WORK EXPERIENCE REQUIREMENTS AND DESIRED SKILLS: Part-time faculty teaching undergraduate courses are required to hold a Master\u2019s degree in English Composition or Technical Writing or hold a PhD in English with a minimum of 18 graduate credit hours in English Composition or Technical Writing. Required qualifications for graduate teaching include a PhD in relevant field required Five years of professional experience Prospective faculty must enroll in and successfully complete the Faculty Orientation Training Course Online teaching experience is preferred All degrees must be conferred from an institution accredited by an accreditation agency recognized by the United States Department of Education or the Council for Higher Education Accreditation (CHEA).\u00a0 For faculty holding degrees awarded by non-U.S. institutions, the institutions must be approved by the appropriate governmental or accreditation agency. A student-centered instructional philosophy is required Curriculum development experience a plus Proficiency in MS Office Suite Products and leveraging the Internet Knowledge of, and use of Blackboard Learning Management System is preferred Able to make decisions and work independently with effective problem solving and analytical skills Strong interpersonal skills and ability to collaborate with technicians and faculty Knowledge of distance learning educational model required Able to gather, analyze, evaluate, and integrate information electronically In-depth knowledge of distance learning educational models, adult learning styles, and technology-assisted instruction. In-depth knowledge of developing curriculum design required Excellent analytical, interpersonal, oral, and written communication skills required High speed Internet and a webcam are required for this role. Able to effectively communicate orally and in writing. A flexible work schedule is required. Able to multi-task yet maintain close attention to detail and timeliness of work production. Able to work in a positive team-oriented manner with a variety of people (students, faculty, staff, administrators, vendors, and members of the general public) Language Skills : Able to read, analyze, and interpret common journals and legal documents. Able to respond to common inquiries or complaints from customers, regulatory agencies, or members of the business community. Able to effectively present information to executive management, faculty, staff, and/or students. Mathematical Skill : Able to apply concepts such as fractions, percentages, ratios, and proportions to practical situations. Reasoning Ability: Able to define problems, collect data, establish facts, and draw valid conclusions. Ability to present facts to faculty for departmental response. Able to deal with a variety of information presented in oral or written formats. Able to deal with non-verbal behavior in assisting with problem resolution. Physical Demands: The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Frequently required to use hand to finger, handle, or feel (including the use of computer keyboards) and talk or hear (including the use of a telephone and computer). Occasionally required to walk, stand, and make presentations. This position may involve sitting at a desk for extended periods of time. Specific vision abilities include close vision and distance vision. \u00a0 University of Arkansas Grantham will seek to reasonably accommodate qualified individuals with a disability. Such reasonable accommodation may take the form of making existing facilities readily accessible to or usable by individuals with a disability, restructuring jobs, modifying schedules, acquiring, or modifying equipment, adjusting training materials, adjusting employment policies, and the like. \u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0 Additional Information: Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Proof of Veteran Status, Resume, Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: recruiting@uagrantham.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Occupational-Safety-Coordinator_R0087624-1": {"title": "Occupational Safety Coordinator", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/17/2026 Type of Position: Investigations, Inspections Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: OPS | Campus Ops Environmental Programs Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: A safety specialist performs worksite assessments to determine what kinds of risks and hazards exist and whether the site meets all regulatory compliance standards. The duties and responsibilities in this field include investigating occupational or worksite accidents or issues, writing reports based on your findings, and communicating with managers and employees about specific issues that need attention, such as unsafe work practices and failure to comply with health and safety standards. Some safety specialists also conduct training and safety education sessions for workers, such as how to properly use safety equipment or avoid accidents. The Chemical/Environmental Hygiene Specialist (CEHS) works under the general direction of Chemical Hygiene Officer (CHO). The CEHS is responsible for monitoring campus programs designed to identify, evaluate and control occupational hazards to UAMS employees including but are not limited to, acceptance, processing, packing, documentation and tracking of hazardous chemicals waste for storage, shipment, and disposal. Provides assistance in environmental compliance. Member of the Emergency Spill Response Team. Stay up to date with regulatory changes and update SOPs as needed. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications:\u00a0 High School Diploma/GED with 4 years of experience in occupational health and safety\u00a0related field Computer competency Must be able to perform physical activities such as, but not limited to, lifting items up to 50 lbs. unassisted; maneuvering 55 gallon drums using a hand truck or drum dolly.\u00a0 Must medically qualify to wear a respirator and other protective equipment, as needed.\u00a0 Position requires frequent exposure to hazardous chemical and radioactive wastes. Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor's Degree in environmental sciences, chemistry, safety, industrial hygiene, biology or a related field, plus 2 years' experience in occupational health and safety or in related field. Other job-related education and/or experience may be substituted for all or part of these basic requirements. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities: OSHA\u2019s Hazardous Waste and Emergency Response standard (HAZWOPER); 40 Hour initial training with eight (8) hours annual refresher. Will be provided within the first year if candidate does not have it. Additional Information: Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Criminal Background Check This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: Crawling, Crouching, Feeling, Hearing, Kneeling, Reaching, Sitting, Standing, Stooping, Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAFS--University-of-Arkansas-Fort-Smith/Assistant-Professor--Management_R0088134": {"title": "Assistant Professor, Management", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Faculty - Non-Tenure Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Fort Smith University of Arkansas \u2013 Fort Smith The University of Arkansas - Fort Smith is a dynamic, mid-sized public university that\u2019s redefining higher education. We\u2019re on a mission to provide transformative, hands-on learning experiences for students of all backgrounds and aspirations. Our multi-faceted approach to education offers a wealth of opportunities, with over 70 academic programs, including certificates, associate, bachelor\u2019s, and master\u2019s degrees. We\u2019re committed to building a diverse community that mirrors Arkansas\u2019s rich tapestry, reflecting our dedication to serving the state\u2019s varied population while enhancing the quality of our institution. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life, and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10 percent of employee salary. \u00a0 Fort Smith, Arkansas Nestled along the Arkansas River, this vibrant city offers a perfect blend of history, culture, and natural beauty. Immerse yourself in the rich heritage of the Old West at the Fort Smith National Historic Site, explore the eclectic local art scene, or take a scenic stroll along the picturesque riverfront trails. With a welcoming community, diverse dining options, and a thriving downtown, Fort Smith is the ideal destination for history enthusiasts and those seeking modern amenities. Thank you for your interest in joining our university. Below you will find details for the position including any supplementary documentation and/or questions you should review before submitting your application. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at (479) 788-7080. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 479-788-7080. Applicants are required to submit a request for each position to which they have applied. Department: CBI Business Administration Department's Website: https://uafs.edu/programs/bachelors/bba.php Summary of Job Duties: Responsibilities at this AACSB-accredited college include developing and teaching undergraduate courses in General Business and Management (Foundations of Business, Organizational Behavior, Business Analytics, Social Responsibility and Ethics, Project Management, Leadership, Operations Management, Entrepreneurship, and/or Supply Chain) as well as sustained interaction with business and industry. Other duties will include assessment/evaluation of instruction; career advisement, recruitment, and retention activities; and participation in college and University committees. The position reports to the department head of Business in the College of Business and Industry. Qualifications: Required Education and/or Work Experience: Ph.D. in Management or appropriately related field from an accredited institution (ABD with completion date no later than December 2026 considered) Preferred Education and/or Work Experience: Previous teaching experience across multiple delivery modes including full online; extensive knowledge of current and emerging technologies relevant to the profession Essential Job Duties and Responsibilities: Classroom and online instruction Scholarly activity sufficient to maintain faculty appointment including a consistent record of publishing in high-quality and impactful journals Service to college and University, including career advising and committees Curriculum planning, implementation, and evaluation Assessment and evaluation of instruction Engagement with the business community Other Job Duties and Responsibilities: Activities in support of the recruitment and retention of students Attendance and participation in all faculty and administrative meetings, Student Research Symposium, commencement ceremonies, and other meetings/events as required Other duties as assigned. Responsible for maintaining a positive work atmosphere by acting and communicating in a manner to foster teamwork and by providing leadership to subordinates. Requires consistent on-time attendance. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: To perform the job successfully, the following competencies are required for the essential functions of this position: Ability to effectively work with a diverse body of students, staff, and faculty Commitment to excellence in teaching, including the utilization of technology Maintenance of an active applied research or professional development agenda Willingness to engage with external stakeholders Well-developed communication and teamwork skills Strong organization and prioritization skills Additional Information: Working Relationships: NA List Employees Supervised: NA Special Job Dimensions: Work performed primarily in an office/classroom setting. Occasional travel and extended hours required. While performing the duties of this job, the employee regularly exhibits digital dexterity when entering data into computer. Required abilities include walking, standing, and sitting for extended periods. Visual demands include close, relatively detailed vision when focusing on a computer screen. Employee regularly talks and hears. Employee occasionally lifts items up to 10 pounds. Background Check Requirements. Criminal Background Check and Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) Check This job description is not designed to contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties, and/or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time with or without notice. Salary Information: $100,000 - $110,000/9 months commensurate with education and experience This position is for Spring 2027 or Fall 2027. Applicants are encouraged to apply by September 30, 2026 for best consideration Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Curriculum Vitae, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: HR 479-788-7080 All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position may be subject to a pre-employment criminal background check, sex offender registry check, financial history background check, and/or drug screening. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication and/or adverse financial history alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background checks and drug screening information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAMS/Groundskeeper_R0090626-2": {"title": "Groundskeeper", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/17/2026 Type of Position: Professional Staff - Facilities Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: OPS | Campus Operation Landscape Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Groundskeeper, under the direction of the UAMS Landscape Manager, performs landscaping and grounds maintenance for healthcare, education, and research facilities throughout the UAMS campus. This position maintains safe, clean, and attractive outdoor spaces and assists in responding to campus facility-related issues and emergencies as needed. Qualifications: High School Diploma/GED, PLUS\u00a0one (1) year of experience in landscaping and/or schooling in the trade. Valid AR Driver's license with fewer than 12 points on their Motor Vehicle Record Basic computer experience required Preferred Qualifications: High School Diploma PLUS five to ten (5-10) years of landscaping and grounds experience Additional Information: Responsibilities Maintains campus turf by mowing, trimming, edging, watering, seeding, and fertilizing grass areas using appropriate landscaping equipment. Assists Landscape Technicians with preparing, installing, and maintaining decorative landscaping features, including flowers, plants, shrubs, ornamental grasses, trees, planters, and borders. Applies approved insecticides and weed-control products and assists with maintaining sprinkler systems and fountains in accordance with safety procedures. Maintains roads, building entrances and exits, sidewalks, and parking lots during inclement weather to support safe access and continued facility operations. Completes required documentation for the Engineering and Operations work-order system and preventive maintenance program. Performs other duties as assigned. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Criminal Background Check This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Feeling, Hearing, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Crawling, Crouching, Kneeling, Reaching, Sitting, Standing, Stooping, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Fayetteville-AR/Computer-Lab-Technician-Hourly_R0090856-1": {"title": "Computer Lab Technician-Hourly", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com, then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at all University of Arkansas institutions will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students.\u201d University of Arkansas, Fayetteville students will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Student Jobs at UAF.\u201d All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. Closing Date: 09/08/2026 Type of Position: Staff - Clerical Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas, Fayetteville Founded in 1871, the University of Arkansas is a land grant institution, classified by the Carnegie Foundation among the nation\u2019s top 2 percent of universities with the highest level of research activity. The University of Arkansas works to advance the state and build a better world through education, research, and outreach by providing transformational opportunities and skills, fostering a welcoming climate, and nurturing creativity, discovery, and the spread of new ideas and innovations. The University of Arkansas campus is located in Fayetteville, a welcoming community ranked as one of the best places to live in the U.S. The growing region surrounding Fayetteville is home to numerous Fortune 500 companies and one of the nation\u2019s strongest economies. Northwest Arkansas is also quickly gaining a national reputation for its focus on the arts and overall quality of life. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10% of employee salary. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions, you should review before applying for the opening. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process, please submit a request via the Disability Accommodations | OEOC | University of Arkansas (uark.edu) : Request an Accommodation. Appli\u00adcants are required to submit a request for each position of which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 479.575.5351. Department: Computer Lab Technicians Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Computer Lab Technician assists students, using hardware/software. This position will be working closely with students, staff, and faculty. You will be expected to have great customer service. You will be asked technical questions, as well as be expected to troubleshoot printing issues. There will also be equipment that is checked out to Students, Staff, and Faculty. Regular, reliable, and non-disruptive attendance is an essential job duty, as is the ability to create and maintain collegial, harmonious working relationships with others. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: High school diploma or equivalent Customer service experience Working knowledge of Microsoft Office applications Working Hours: Saturday\u2013Tuesday: 7:00 PM\u2013midnight, Wednesday\u2013Friday: 7:00 PM\u2013midnight Preferred Qualifications: Prior experience in customer service role Demonstrated knowledge of the operations of personal computers and the functions of various software Additional Information: Salary Information: $11.00/hr Required Documents to Apply: Availability to Work and/or Class Schedule Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status, Resume Recruitment Contact Information: Dawn Hefley, Human Resources Partner, dawn@uark.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Special Instructions to Applicants: Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas seeks to attract, develop and retain high quality faculty, staff and administrators that consistently display practices and behaviors to advance a culture that embeds equal opportunity, educational excellence and unparalleled access for all. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All Application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Sitting, Standing, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Crouching, Lifting, Pulling, Pushing Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAM--Monticello-Campus/Academic-Advisor--Student-Success-Initiative-_R0090887-2": {"title": "Academic Advisor (Student Success Initiative)", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Professional Staff - Academic Affairs Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Monticello UAM, one of twenty campuses of the University of Arkansas System, is located in southeastern Arkansas in the beautiful timberlands, rich in outdoor recreation activities, and approximately 100 miles south of Little Rock. UAM is a comprehensive, residential and commuter, undergraduate institution also offering selected master\u2019s degree programs. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please submit a request via the OEOC website: \u00a0Applicants are required to submit a request for each position to which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 870-460-1422 . Department: Academic Advising Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Academic Advisor plays a key role in student success and retention. Responsibilities include: \u2022 Assist the Assistant Vice Chancellor for Academic Success in the development of student success and retention goals for specific populations. \u2022 Assist in the implementation of student success initiatives. \u2022 Monitor and track student retention and other success benchmarks as needed and assigned. \u2022 Advise, monitor, track and provide academic support to students in specific populations as assigned. This may include, but is not limited to, students close to completion, developmental students, student athletes or certain student demographics who need additional support. \u2022 Assist in developing academic success and advising resources. \u2022 Develop and conduct workshops, classroom presentations and coordinate events to support student academic and personal success. \u2022 Assist students in understanding and adjusting to the demands and culture of higher education, including the development of realistic academic plans. \u2022 Assist students in maintaining good academic standing, informing them of relevant policies, procedures and campus resources. \u2022 Based on education and/or qualifications, provide instruction for up to three 1-hour sections of UNIV 11171 \u201cPathway to Success\u201d per academic year. \u2022 Maintain positive and productive working relationships with all faculty and staff to ensure that students receive accurate and reliable information. \u2022 Refer students to appropriate campus resources for assistance with disability services, academic and personal issues and other college-related concerns. \u2022 Perform other related duties as assigned. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications : Baccalaureate degree is required. Must have strong interpersonal and excellent written communication skills; ability to work collaboratively with staff, faculty, and students; proficient computer skills; and availability for evening and weekend work as needed. Preferred Qualifications : A master\u2019s degree with two years of related experience. Additional Information: Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience. Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Caroline Johnson, Assistant Vice Chancellor for Academic Success Email: johnsonc@uamont.edu Phone: 870-460-1233 All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Repetitive Motion, Sitting, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Lifting, Standing Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Nursing-Programs-Clinical-and-Simulation-Coordinator_R0084438": {"title": "Nursing Programs Clinical and Simulation Coordinator", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 12/31/2026 Type of Position: Clinical Staff - Nursing Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas Pulaski Technical College University of Arkansas - Pulaski Technical College at North Little Rock is an integral part of the Arkansas Technical and Community College System maintained by the State of Arkansas. The college is governed by the University of Arkansas System Board of Trustees and a seven-member Board of Visitors and derives its support largely from student tuition and fees and legislative appropriations. UA - Pulaski Tech, a comprehensive two-year college, offers associate degree and certificate programs for students who plan to transfer to four-year colleges and universities and/or for career preparation and advancement. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply link/button. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at (501) 812-2839. Department: Math, Natural Sciences, and Allied Health Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The steepest healthcare workforce shortages in the State of Arkansas, especially in lower-income urban and rural areas, directly impact the delivery of essential health services to high-need communities. To address this dire healthcare workforce need, a statewide consortium of six of Arkansas\u2019 public two-year institutions has been awarded $5.7 million for the Bridging Healthcare Workforce Shortages in Arkansas (BRIDGE-AR) initiative. The institutions are as follows: \u2022 University of Arkansas Pulaski Technical College \u2022 Arkansas State University Mid-South \u2022 Southeast Arkansas College \u2022 Phillips Community College of the University of Arkansas \u2022 University of Arkansas East Arkansas Community College \u2022 Northwest Arkansas Community College BRIDGE-AR assembles a collaboration of employers, workforce organizations, and training providers to address essential local labor needs. The initiative\u2019s strategies are designed to impact rural and underserved communities in the Nursing and Emergency Medical Technician (EMT) pathways. These occupations are primary labor needs in the state and provide career progression and family-sustaining wages in local communities. Position Summary Reporting to the Dean of Sciences, Mathematics, and Allied Health, the Clinical and Simulation Coordinator will provide clinical and administrative support for the Allied Health programs, including maintenance of inventory, completion of student clinical rotation requirements, maintenance of clinical agreements, scheduling rooms, preparing simulation sessions, developing simulation scenarios, and delivery of simulation experiences. The Clinical and Simulation Coordinator will also be responsible for monitoring data on simulation center usage and other areas to enhance usage. *This position is funded 100% by the BRIDGE AR DOL Grant. As such, the Clinical and Simulation Coordinator assists the Director of the BRIDGE-AR grant and the Dean of the School of Science, Math, and Allied Health with implementing the objectives established in the grant for this federally-funded activity. Essential Functions: \u2022 Assists program directors, faculty, and students in the lab setting with integration of simulation into the curriculum. \u2022 Supervises and evaluates students\u2019 progress in meeting designated program student learning outcomes (PSLOs) and course student learning outcomes (CSLOs) and reports progress to course faculty and program directors through end of term reports. \u2022 Coordinates and schedules use of labs for all functions, including: regular classes, special class sections, open lab, advanced clinical skills, and clinical skills evaluation. \u2022 Collaborates with the Director of Nursing to establish, review, and research policies, standard practices, and procedures related to the skills and simulation lab with a focus on continuous quality improvement. \u2022 Collaborates with course faculty in planning, designing, organizing, and delivering lab and simulation activities to meet the needs and schedule of the course. \u2022 Collaborates with the nursing faculty to coordinate the complementary blending of lab practice, simulation, virtual simulation and the clinical experience. \u2022 Researches, develops, updates, collaborates, and refines lab and clinical scenarios for the nursing programs based on student and faculty needs and reflective of current practice standards. \u2022 Ensures safety and maintains OSHA standards within the simulation lab; to include appropriate disposal of hazardous waste and sharps \u2022 Keeps current with safety standards and informs the Director of Nursing Programs of changes in standards. \u2022 Monitors inventory and orders necessary supplies for the skills and simulation lab, including performing the annual inventory. \u2022 Ensures maintenance of simulation manikins and other equipment in the skills and simulation lab; initiates repair and maintains appropriate warranties. \u2022 Provides orientation to instructors regarding the policies, procedures and use of the simulation lab. \u2022 Collaborates with the nursing faculty to coordinate the complementary blending of lab practice, simulation, virtual simulation and the clinical experience. \u2022 Assists students and faculty in meeting course objectives through the utilization of the skills and simulation lab activities. \u2022 Oversees utilization of the skills and simulation lab and equipment. \u2022 Serves as a resource and support for all Allied Health faculty in utilizing the simulation lab. \u2022 Collaborates with Nursing faculty to provide student remediation in the lab setting. \u2022 Utilizes and emphasizes instructional methods that promote the development of critical thinking, problem solving, decision-making, and clinical competency for real life application. \u2022 Conducts tours for internal/external stakeholders. \u2022 Provides and develops all training for clinical learning lab faculty regarding the administration of at the beginning of each term to include lab equipment, changes to curriculum, software, and/or supplies to be used. \u2022 Orders, prepares, and organizes equipment and supplies to be utilized in the clinical learning lab. \u2022 Manages all aspects of the clinical placement process and ensures effective operation of clinical practicums by organizing, supervising, and evaluating clinical sites, preceptors & students. Responsibilities include but are not limited to the following: \u2022 Ensuring effective operation of clinical practicums by organizing, supervising & evaluating clinical sites, preceptors & students. \u2022 Monitoring student placements and clinical records. \u2022 Maintaining and obtaining contracts, mandatory legal documentation (license verification, liability insurance, qualifications of preceptors and preceptor orientation etc.). \u2022 Securing and coordinating clinical placement for all assigned programs for incoming and continuing students. \u2022 Meet all clinical and other scheduled responsibilities such as office hours and meetings at the designated time. \u2022 Creates and manages assigned databases to ensure complete and accurate information. Compiles reports and communicates data to appropriate stakeholders. Databases may include: \u2022 Tracking of clinical placements \u2022 Contracts/Agreements \u2022 Documentation \u2022 Legal verification (for students, preceptors, and clinical sites) \u2022 The successful candidate must be a team player with the ability to problem-solve, share creative solutions, and implement best practices. S/He will possess critical thinking skills and the ability to balance multiple tasks simultaneously, accurately setting priorities that make sense for the College and its partners. The role requires excellent organizational skills and the ability to work in a fast-paced environment. The Clinical and Simulation Coordinator will have superb interpersonal and communication skills, the ability to deal with all levels of faculty, staff and students, and exemplary customer service skills. \u2022 This position will require moderate lifting and carrying of simulation equipment up to 25lbs. Proficiency in Microsoft applications including Word, Excel and Power Point, is also required. \u2022 Flexibility and adaptability to work varying schedules and hours including evenings is necessary. \u2022 Demonstrate sensitivity to and understanding of college students that come from a variety of academic and social backgrounds. \u2022 Develop positive rapport with colleagues and other members of the campus community to develop a sense of teamwork. \u2022 Strong analytical, observational, and problem-solving skills. \u2022 Effective verbal and written communication skills \u2022 Ability to be self-directed and solve problems effectively and efficiently \u2022 Strong organizational skills \u2022 Positive and professional demeanor \u2022 Other duties as assigned Qualifications: MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS: Associate of Science in Nursing Minimum of two (two) years of nursing practice PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS: Three (3) to five (5) years of instructional experience Bachelor or Science in Nursing Additional Information: Special Instructions to Applicants Salary Salary Information: $50,000-$65,000 Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of five Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants Recruitment Contact Information: Human Resources humanresources@uaptc.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Motor Vehicle Reports Check, Sex Offender Registry University of Arkansas - Pulaski Technical College is committed to providing a safe campus community. Title IX protects the college community from sexual harassment in a school's education programs and activities. This means that Title IX protects the college community in connection with all academic, educational, extracurricular, athletic, and other programs of the school, whether those programs take place in a school's facilities, in college transportation, at a class or training program sponsored by the school at another location, or elsewhere. \u00a0 We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Repetitive Motion, Sharps, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Crouching, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching Occasional Physical Activity: Kneeling, Lifting, Reaching Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Fayetteville-AR/Director-of-Operations---Anthony-Timberland-Center_R0090002-1": {"title": "Director of Operations - Anthony Timberland Center", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com, then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at all University of Arkansas institutions will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students.\u201d University of Arkansas, Fayetteville students will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Student Jobs at UAF.\u201d All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. Closing Date: 09/09/2026 Type of Position: Researchers and Scientists Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas, Fayetteville Founded in 1871, the University of Arkansas is a land grant institution, classified by the Carnegie Foundation among the nation\u2019s top 2 percent of universities with the highest level of research activity. The University of Arkansas works to advance the state and build a better world through education, research, and outreach by providing transformational opportunities and skills, fostering a welcoming climate, and nurturing creativity, discovery, and the spread of new ideas and innovations. The University of Arkansas campus is located in Fayetteville, a welcoming community ranked as one of the best places to live in the U.S. The growing region surrounding Fayetteville is home to numerous Fortune 500 companies and one of the nation\u2019s strongest economies. Northwest Arkansas is also quickly gaining a national reputation for its focus on the arts and overall quality of life. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10% of employee salary. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions, you should review before applying for the opening. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process, please submit a request via the Disability Accommodations | OEOC | University of Arkansas (uark.edu) : Request an Accommodation. Appli\u00adcants are required to submit a request for each position of which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 479.575.5351. Department: Dean's Suite Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Anthony Timberlands Director of Operations manages daily operations and business planning, and collaborates with the Fay Jones School of Architecture and Design (FJSAD) faculty and administration to develop a long-term strategy for the newly built, state-of-the-art Anthony Timberlands research and teaching facility. This leader ensures high efficiency, strict regulatory compliance, financial budget control, and proper team supervision to advance the research and teaching agenda of the University of Arkansas and the Fay Jones School of Architecture and Design. This is an in-person position, not a remote position. Extensive in-person engagement in both supervisory activities and formal and informal interactions with colleagues contributes to successful leadership, coordination, and collaboration and is essential to the expectations for this position. Regular, reliable, and non-disruptive attendance is an essential job function of this job, as is the ability to create and maintain collegial, harmonious working relationships with others. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor\u2019s degree in relevant science, engineering, or design discipline from an accredited institution of higher education At least five years of professional lab experience At least two years two years in a leadership role in a professional lab setting Experience with software related to digital technology and fabrication (CAM, 3D Modeling, Arduino) Experience with traditional fabrication assemblies and techniques (woodworking, metalworking) Experience with contemporary fabrication (CNC router, CNC lathe, CNC mill, 3D printing, Robotics) Preferred Qualifications: Master\u2019s degree in a relevant science, engineering, or design discipline from an accredited institution of higher education Experience working in an educational environment Experience in the design and fabrication of custom robotic end effectors Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Strong business acumen and process optimization skills Exceptional communication skills Deep knowledge of safety and regulatory guidelines Ability to support faculty research and grants Exceptional communication skills Additional Information: Salary Information: $100,000; commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Recruitment Contact Information: Amy Shell, Chief of Staff shell@uark.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Special Instructions to Applicants: Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas seeks to attract, develop and retain high quality faculty, staff and administrators that consistently display practices and behaviors to advance a culture that embeds equal opportunity, educational excellence and unparalleled access for all. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All Application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Talking Occasional Physical Activity: Talking Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAMS/Assistant-Professor_R0090549-1": {"title": "Assistant Professor", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/19/2026 Type of Position: Faculty - Tenure/Tenure Track Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: COM | Biomedical Informatics Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The UAMS Department of Biomedical Informatics is a vibrant environment for research. It hosts multiple National Institutes of Health and National Cancer Institute (NIH/NCI) funded projects and provides biomedical informatics insights to the entire UAMS community. The expertise and research interests of the Department of Biomedical Informatics (DBMI) faculty cover multiple key disciplines of Biomedical Informatics, including Imaging Informatics, Bioinformatics, Clinical Research Informatics, and Semantic Web technologies in the life sciences. The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourage and support teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving the health, health care, and wellbeing of Arkansans. The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) maintains high performance computing facilities for research use by faculty and staff, as well as collaborators across the UA system. The UAMS Department of Biomedical Informatics (DBMI) provides all system administration and operations support functions for HPC on the UAMS campus. UAMS is collaborating to build statewide capacity for high-performance computing and the advanced digital infrastructure needed to support AI research. The long-term goal is to establish sustainable, powerful computing resources designed for AI workloads to support research and analytics. The ideal candidate will assist with the installation, configuration, and maintenance of the HPC software and hardware, provide technical support and troubleshooting for the users and work with research faculty, staff, and students to provide specialized expertise in new fields such as ML/AI, data manipulation and analysis, and visualization. As a faculty member in Biomedical Informatics the successful candidate will be expected to acquire grant funding to support their independent research agenda and to assist or lead applications for funding to support and expand the Center for High Performance computing. Qualifications: Terminal degree in Biomedical Informatics, Computer Science, Data Science, or a comparable scientific or technical discipline. Experience with system administration in a Linux environment. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities: Knowledge of Linux server configuration, including RHEL, CentOS, or an equivalent operating system. Knowledge of system scripting, security practices, and network protocols. Demonstrated analytical, troubleshooting, and problem-solving skills. Ability to work collaboratively as part of a multidisciplinary team. Ability to work independently, take initiative, and learn emerging technologies. Preferred Qualifications Experience working in an HPC environment. Experience with cluster file systems, job scheduling, workflow management, and resource management tools. Experience with tools such as Moab, Maui, or TORQUE. Experience with Singularity, Docker, or other container technologies. Knowledge of parallel computing techniques, including multithreading and Message Passing Interface (MPI). Experience with GPU computing and optimizing software for high-performance computing environments. Experience supporting machine learning, artificial intelligence, data-intensive research, or scientific visualization. Demonstrated experience developing or contributing to grant-funded research. Additional Information: Responsibilities Install, configure, maintain, and support HPC hardware, software, and related infrastructure. Provide Linux system administration and operational support for research computing environments. Troubleshoot technical issues and provide support to faculty, staff, students, and research collaborators. Collaborate with researchers on machine learning, artificial intelligence, data analysis, data management, and visualization projects. Assist researchers with optimizing applications and workflows for parallel and GPU-based computing environments. Evaluate and implement emerging technologies that support advanced computing and research needs. Develop and maintain an independent research program. Pursue external grant funding and contribute to collaborative research proposals. Assist with or lead funding applications supporting the growth and sustainability of the Center for High Performance Computing. Participate in departmental, institutional, and professional service activities consistent with a faculty appointment. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Fayetteville-AR/Diesel-Technician-II_R0090870-1": {"title": "Diesel Technician II", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com, then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at all University of Arkansas institutions will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students.\u201d University of Arkansas, Fayetteville students will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Student Jobs at UAF.\u201d All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. Closing Date: 09/01/2026 Type of Position: Skilled Crafts and Trades Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Shift Vary (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas, Fayetteville Founded in 1871, the University of Arkansas is a land grant institution, classified by the Carnegie Foundation among the nation\u2019s top 2 percent of universities with the highest level of research activity. The University of Arkansas works to advance the state and build a better world through education, research, and outreach by providing transformational opportunities and skills, fostering a welcoming climate, and nurturing creativity, discovery, and the spread of new ideas and innovations. The University of Arkansas campus is located in Fayetteville, a welcoming community ranked as one of the best places to live in the U.S. The growing region surrounding Fayetteville is home to numerous Fortune 500 companies and one of the nation\u2019s strongest economies. Northwest Arkansas is also quickly gaining a national reputation for its focus on the arts and overall quality of life. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10% of employee salary. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions, you should review before applying for the opening. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process, please submit a request via the Disability Accommodations | OEOC | University of Arkansas (uark.edu) : Request an Accommodation. Appli\u00adcants are required to submit a request for each position of which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 479.575.5351. Department: Skilled Trade Operations Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Transit Bus Mechanic is responsible for the safe, timely repair, and maintenance of heavy-duty transit vehicles, passenger vehicles, and other fleet vehicles used in transporting passengers to specific destinations within the City of Fayetteville Arkansas. Regular, reliable, and non-disruptive attendance is an essential job duty, as is the ability to create and maintain collegial, harmonious working relationships with others. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: The formal education equivalent of a high school diploma PLUS Completion of required education or training along with the required license or certification (appropriate military service training or Diesel Truck Technician certification) OR At least five years of experience in vehicle maintenance or a related field Preferred Qualifications: Associate\u2019s degree or advanced specialized or technical training Commercial Driver\u2019s License ASE\u00a0Certification At least one year of heavy truck/ transit maintenance experience Additional Information: Salary Information: $61,735.00 - $77,169.00 Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Recruitment Contact Information: Razorback Transit Career Center, rtcareer@uark.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Special Instructions to Applicants: Please upload a copy of U.S Driver's License. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Motor Vehicle Reports Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas seeks to attract, develop and retain high quality faculty, staff and administrators that consistently display practices and behaviors to advance a culture that embeds equal opportunity, educational excellence and unparalleled access for all. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All Application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Grasping, Hearing, Standing, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Fayetteville/Director-of-Eligibility---Certification_R0090680-1": {"title": "Director of Eligibility & Certification", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com, then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at all University of Arkansas institutions will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students.\u201d University of Arkansas, Fayetteville students will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Student Jobs at UAF.\u201d All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. Closing Date: 09/09/2026 Type of Position: Athletics Compliance Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas, Fayetteville Founded in 1871, the University of Arkansas is a land grant institution, classified by the Carnegie Foundation among the nation\u2019s top 2 percent of universities with the highest level of research activity. The University of Arkansas works to advance the state and build a better world through education, research, and outreach by providing transformational opportunities and skills, fostering a welcoming climate, and nurturing creativity, discovery, and the spread of new ideas and innovations. The University of Arkansas campus is located in Fayetteville, a welcoming community ranked as one of the best places to live in the U.S. The growing region surrounding Fayetteville is home to numerous Fortune 500 companies and one of the nation\u2019s strongest economies. Northwest Arkansas is also quickly gaining a national reputation for its focus on the arts and overall quality of life. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10% of employee salary. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions, you should review before applying for the opening. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process, please submit a request via the Disability Accommodations | OEOC | University of Arkansas (uark.edu) : Request an Accommodation. Appli\u00adcants are required to submit a request for each position of which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 479.575.5351. Department: Compliance Department's Website: https://arkansasrazorbacks.com/ https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=j9ihImu88OQ&t=9s Summary of Job Duties: The Director of Athletics Eligibility & Certification serves as the University of Arkansas Athletics Department's primary authority and final campus certifying official for student-athlete academic eligibility. This position provides strategic leadership and oversight of all NCAA, Southeastern Conference (SEC), and University eligibility certification processes, ensuring institutional compliance while supporting student-athlete academic success. Responsibilities include administering initial, transfer, and continuing eligibility certification; monitoring progress-toward-degree requirements; preparing NCAA, SEC, institutional, and state reports; interpreting NCAA and SEC legislation; and collaborating with Student-Athlete Academic Services, the Office of the Registrar, Admissions, Financial Aid, academic colleges, coaches, faculty, and external governing bodies. The Director ensures the integrity of all eligibility certification processes through accurate monitoring, documentation, reporting, and legislative interpretation. Regular, reliable, and non-disruptive attendance is an essential job duty, as is the ability to create and maintain collegial, harmonious working relationships with others. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree from an accredited institution At least two (2) years of NCAA Division I experience in athletics compliance, eligibility certification, student-athlete academic services, or a related field Experience interpreting and applying NCAA eligibility, transfer, and progress-toward-degree legislation Demonstrated analytical, organizational, problem-solving, and communication skills \u00a0 Preferred Qualifications: Master's degree from an accredited institution At least three (3) or more years of NCAA Division I experience administering eligibility certification Experience serving as a campus certifying official or primary eligibility administrator Experience with Teamworks Compliance + Recruiting, Compliance Assistant, NCAA Academic Portal, NCAA Eligibility Center, Transfer Portal, LSDBi, RSRO, Workday, and other NCAA and institutional student information systems Experience preparing NCAA Academic Progress Rate (APR), Graduation Success Rate (GSR), Equity in Athletics Disclosure Act (EADA), IPEDS, revenue distribution, sports sponsorship, participation, and other NCAA or conference reports \u00a0 Knowledge, Skills & Abilities: Comprehensive knowledge of NCAA, SEC, and University academic eligibility legislation, policies, and procedures Knowledge of NCAA initial eligibility, transfer eligibility, continuing eligibility, and progress-toward-degree requirements Strong organizational and project management skills with the ability to prioritize multiple deadlines Strong analytical and critical thinking skills with exceptional attention to detail and accuracy Excellent written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills with the ability to collaborate effectively across multiple departments Ability to interpret complex legislation, academic transcripts, degree audits, and institutional policies Ability to maintain confidential information while exercising sound judgment and discretion Proficiency with NCAA compliance platforms, student information systems, Microsoft Office Suite, and database management systems Commitment to integrity, institutional control, compliance, and student-athlete academic success Additional Information: Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Recruitment Contact Information: Krista Hoover, Senior HR Partner - Athletics, kristah@uark.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Special Instructions to Applicants: Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas seeks to attract, develop and retain high quality faculty, staff and administrators that consistently display practices and behaviors to advance a culture that embeds equal opportunity, educational excellence and unparalleled access for all. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All Application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Fayetteville/Clinical-Assistant-Professor-of-Nursing_R0090820-1": {"title": "Clinical Assistant Professor of Nursing", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com, then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at all University of Arkansas institutions will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students.\u201d University of Arkansas, Fayetteville students will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Student Jobs at UAF.\u201d All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. Closing Date: Type of Position: Faculty - Non-Tenure Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Academic Term (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: Yes Institution Name: University of Arkansas, Fayetteville Founded in 1871, the University of Arkansas is a land grant institution, classified by the Carnegie Foundation among the nation\u2019s top 2 percent of universities with the highest level of research activity. The University of Arkansas works to advance the state and build a better world through education, research, and outreach by providing transformational opportunities and skills, fostering a welcoming climate, and nurturing creativity, discovery, and the spread of new ideas and innovations. The University of Arkansas campus is located in Fayetteville, a welcoming community ranked as one of the best places to live in the U.S. The growing region surrounding Fayetteville is home to numerous Fortune 500 companies and one of the nation\u2019s strongest economies. Northwest Arkansas is also quickly gaining a national reputation for its focus on the arts and overall quality of life. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10% of employee salary. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions, you should review before applying for the opening. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process, please submit a request via the Disability Accommodations | OEOC | University of Arkansas (uark.edu) : Request an Accommodation. Appli\u00adcants are required to submit a request for each position of which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 479.575.5351. Department: Department of Nursing Department's Website: https://nursing.uark.edu/ Summary of Job Duties: The Clinical Assistant Professor of Nursing, a 9-month non-tenure-track position, teaches graduate and undergraduate level courses, participates in student advisement and mentoring, engages in service activities in the department, university, and profession, and contributes to departmental efforts towards maintaining accreditation. The Clinical Assistant Professor of Nursing also participates in curriculum development, assessment, and continuous improvement activities to support the quality and effectiveness of academic programs. The position also contributes to the effective operation of academic programs and academic governance by participating in departmental, college, and university service activities, as appropriate to their appointment. This is an in-person position. On-campus presence is an essential function of this position. Extensive in-person engagement in activities such as office hours, student advising, collaborative work, and departmental, college, and university committee meetings is required to advance student success, departmental effectiveness, and the mission of the college and the university. Through teaching, research, and service, this position supports the University\u2019s 150 Forward priorities of student success, research excellence, and an employer-of-choice environment. Regular, reliable, and non-disruptive attendance is an essential job duty, as is the ability to create and maintain collegial, harmonious working relationships with others. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: An earned doctorate from a nationally recognized and accredited institution of higher education conferred by the start of employment Commitment to high-quality teaching at the undergraduate and/or graduate levels Commitment to preparation of effective professionals Eligible to hold an unencumbered RN license with the Arkansas State Board of Nursing and secured by the first date of employment Preferred Qualifications: Documented teaching experience at the college/university level Experience in student advising at the college/university level Experience or interest in the scholarship of teaching and learning Additional Information: Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Curriculum Vitae, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Statement of Teaching Philosophy Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Recruitment Contact Information: Dr. Carrie McDermott Executive Director of the Eleanor Mann School of Nursing carriem@uark.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Special Instructions to Applicants: Completed applications received by October 1, 2026, will be assured full consideration. Late applications will be reviewed as necessary to fill the position. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas seeks to attract, develop and retain high quality faculty, staff and administrators that consistently display practices and behaviors to advance a culture that embeds equal opportunity, educational excellence and unparalleled access for all. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All Application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Reaching, Repetitive Motion, Sitting, Standing, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Repetitive Motion Occasional Physical Activity: Grasping, Walking Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/RN-PRN---Cardiac-Cath-Lab_R0087973": {"title": "RN PRN - Cardiac Cath Lab", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 10/01/2026 Type of Position: Clinical Staff - Nursing Job Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Shift Vary (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | CVSL Cardiac Cath Lab IP C Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Cardiac Cath Lab and Electrophysiology Lab RN will provide direct patient care as a RN in Cardiac Cath Lab/EP Lab. In this role physical care will be provided in the prep, intra procedure and post procedure care of patients. Intra procedure care includes administering moderate sedation and patient monitoring. This professional nursing role will require the ability to coordinate care for patients, triage patients, and work collaboratively with clinic providers, fellows, and staff. Requires the ability to effectively work with patient referral sources, facilitate appointments, coordinate transitions of care, and provide patient education on complex conditions. The Nurse will work with the individual patient, their families, and providers of care to develop and implement individual health plans within Cath Lab/Electrophysiology Lab. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Graduate of an accredited Nursing Program with an Associate's Degree, Nursing Diploma, Bachelor's in Nursing, or Master's in Nursing Valid RN License Minimum of 1 year Registered Nursing experience. Preferred Qualifications: 2 or more years of Cath Lab Experience Additional Information: Responsibilities: Collects and documents assessment data from patients and/or others per UAMS standard.\u00a0 Develops the patient's Plan of Care (POC) per department/unit standards utilizing assessment data.\u00a0 Evaluates the progress of patients toward attainment of desired outcomes. Administers medication following department/unit standards and Nurse Practice Act.\u00a0 Verifies and evaluates care delivered to ensure it is consistent with patient and family-centered care principles, practice standards, and regulatory requirements. Supports the integration of current evidence into nursing practices.\u00a0 Promotes an environment conducive to a positive educational experience for all students and staff.\u00a0 Provides effective patient/family education/discharge planning. Effectively collaborates and communicates with nursing staff at all levels, interdisciplinary teams, executive leaders, and other stakeholders.\u00a0 Communicates care appropriately through documentation in the medical record. Reports variances in care/ systems/ processes through the appropriate means.\u00a0 Participates in recruitment/retention of staff.\u00a0 Facilitates development and implementation of nursing practice standards that are evidence-based and in compliance with ANA standards. May perform other duties as assigned. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Criminal Background Check, Substance Abuse Testing This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Feeling, Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sharps, Standing, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Lifting, Pulling, Pushing, Sharps, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Grasping, Reaching, Sitting Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Fayetteville/Razorback-Analytic-Fellow-2_R0090769-1": {"title": "Razorback Analytic Fellow-2", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com, then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at all University of Arkansas institutions will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students.\u201d University of Arkansas, Fayetteville students will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Student Jobs at UAF.\u201d All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. Closing Date: 09/18/2026 Type of Position: Staff - Clerical Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas, Fayetteville Founded in 1871, the University of Arkansas is a land grant institution, classified by the Carnegie Foundation among the nation\u2019s top 2 percent of universities with the highest level of research activity. The University of Arkansas works to advance the state and build a better world through education, research, and outreach by providing transformational opportunities and skills, fostering a welcoming climate, and nurturing creativity, discovery, and the spread of new ideas and innovations. The University of Arkansas campus is located in Fayetteville, a welcoming community ranked as one of the best places to live in the U.S. The growing region surrounding Fayetteville is home to numerous Fortune 500 companies and one of the nation\u2019s strongest economies. Northwest Arkansas is also quickly gaining a national reputation for its focus on the arts and overall quality of life. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10% of employee salary. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions, you should review before applying for the opening. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process, please submit a request via the Disability Accommodations | OEOC | University of Arkansas (uark.edu) : Request an Accommodation. Appli\u00adcants are required to submit a request for each position of which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 479.575.5351. Department: Razorback Analytic Fellowships Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Razorback Analytics Fellowship provides University of Arkansas students with hands-on, part-time experience in applied data analytics through real-world projects that support University operations. Fellows partner with campus stakeholders to understand business needs and translate them into analytics solutions, including interactive dashboards and reports built in Power BI and related tools. They analyze and transform data to support operational and strategic decision-making, and communicate findings through presentations, visualizations, and written summaries. Fellows also contribute to project teams, manage assigned tasks collaboratively, and apply best practices in data quality, documentation, and reporting. The Fellowship is designed to prepare students for careers in data analytics through practical experience, mentorship, and exposure to complex organizational data challenges. Work Environment Razorback Analytics Fellows work within the Department of Strategic Data and Process Innovation and collaborate with a variety of campus partners. This is an in-person, part-time position, and Fellows are provided with a designated workstation. Fellows work 10 to 20 hours per week, with flexibility to accommodate academic schedules. The Fellowship runs for the full academic year, from September through May, ending at the conclusion of the spring semester. Regular, reliable, and non-disruptive attendance is an essential job duty, as is the ability to create and maintain collegial, harmonious working relationships with others. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications Current UA junior or senior student enrolled in an analytics-related degree program, such as Data Science, Information Systems, Statistics, Economics, Engineering, or a similar field, with at least a 3.0 cumulative GPA Proficient with concepts covered in Calculus I and introductory statistics coursework Familiarity with data analysis concepts and techniques\u00a0such as data representation, retrieval, manipulation, storage, and governance Foundational experience with at least one programming language (Python, R, SQL, etc.) Strong interest in pursuing a career in data analytics or a related field\u00a0 Preferred Qualifications Completion of at least one programming focused course with a grade of B or higher, such as DASC 10201, DASC 12004, DASC 16003, CSCE 20004, CSCE 20104, or a similar course Completion of at least one analytics focused course with a grade of B or higher, such as DASC 22103, DASC 22003, ISYS 20303, ISYS 31903, or a similar course Proficient with concepts covered in Calculus II and/or advanced statistics coursework Intermediate experience with one or more programming languages Experience with data visualization tools, such as Python/R packages, Tableau, Power BI, or similar Applicants do not need to meet all preferred qualifications to be competitive. Applications will be reviewed holistically based on preparation, interest, communication skills, and potential for growth. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Critical thinking and analytical skills Strong written and verbal communication skills\u00a0 Strong organizational and prioritization skills Ability to work both independently and collaboratively Additional Information: Salary Information: $15.00 Required Documents to Apply: List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume, Unofficial/Official Transcript(s), Writing Sample Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Recruitment Contact Information: Salim Yahaya, HR Coordinator, salimy@uark.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Special Instructions to Applicants: Personal Statement, no more than one page, describing your interest in the program, how you meet the qualifications, and how the Fellowship aligns with your future goals List of two Professional References from UA Faculty or Staff, including each reference\u2019s name, title, contact information, and relationship to you. References outside of UA will be considered only if they can speak to experiences relevant to data analytics. Resume/CV, no more than two pages Unofficial transcript showing GPA and relevant coursework Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas seeks to attract, develop and retain high quality faculty, staff and administrators that consistently display practices and behaviors to advance a culture that embeds equal opportunity, educational excellence and unparalleled access for all. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All Application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Hot-Springs/ASMSA-Residential-Life-Weekend-Desk_R0090689": {"title": "ASMSA Residential Life Weekend Desk", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Professional Staff - ASMSA Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: Arkansas School for Mathematics, Sciences and the Arts Arkansas\u2019 Premier Public High School The Arkansas School for Mathematics, Sciences, and the Arts is a specific investment by the General Assembly in many of the state\u02bcs most talented and promising young minds. Each year, students from counties across Arkansas come to ASMSA to live and learn within a community of 230 intellectual peers. The residential experience combines college-level coursework, dynamic faculty, advanced research opportunities, diverse experiences within the arts, study abroad trips, and more to create an educational community unlike any other in Arkansas. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.\u00a0 To apply for the position, please click the Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 501-622-5131. Applicants are required to submit a request for each position of which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-662-5131. Department: Office - Residential Life Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: POSITION: Residential Life Weekend Desk REPORTS TO: Assistant Dean of Students CLASSIFICATION: Non-Exempt PURPOSE OF THE POSITION: To support all aspects of the Residential Life Office (RLO) operations on the weekend. Qualifications: RESPONSIBILITIES AND PERFORMANCE STANDARD: Duties include, but are not limited to: \u2022 Maintains a log of all incoming calls received in the RLO and distributes phone messages. \u2022 Checks emails and responds as needed for the RLO \u2022 Maintains student check-in/check-out and visitor\u2019s permission logs via the Reach student life management system. \u2022 Performs other duties as assigned. POSITION QUALIFICATIONS: \u2022 High school diploma or equivalent. \u2022 Experience in a clerical or related field preferred. \u2022 Demonstrated ability in verbal and written communication. \u2022 Working knowledge of the Microsoft Office and Google suites. \u2022 Strong interpersonal skills to communicate and relate to students, parents, and school officials in a positive and professional manner. \u2022 Organization and time management skills. Additional Information: Salary Information: $15.00/hour Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Brandi Brazil, SHRM-SCP Director Human Resources and Campus Culture brazilb@asmsa.org All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Child Maltreatment, Criminal Background Check, FBI Background Check, Motor Vehicle Reports Check, Sex Offender Registry Arkansas School for Mathematics, Sciences, and the Arts is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Hearing, Sitting, Standing Occasional Physical Activity: Walking Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Fayetteville/Academic-Advisor-III_R0090873-1": {"title": "Academic Advisor III", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com, then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at all University of Arkansas institutions will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students.\u201d University of Arkansas, Fayetteville students will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Student Jobs at UAF.\u201d All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. Closing Date: 09/15/2026 Type of Position: Academic Advising Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas, Fayetteville Founded in 1871, the University of Arkansas is a land grant institution, classified by the Carnegie Foundation among the nation\u2019s top 2 percent of universities with the highest level of research activity. The University of Arkansas works to advance the state and build a better world through education, research, and outreach by providing transformational opportunities and skills, fostering a welcoming climate, and nurturing creativity, discovery, and the spread of new ideas and innovations. The University of Arkansas campus is located in Fayetteville, a welcoming community ranked as one of the best places to live in the U.S. The growing region surrounding Fayetteville is home to numerous Fortune 500 companies and one of the nation\u2019s strongest economies. Northwest Arkansas is also quickly gaining a national reputation for its focus on the arts and overall quality of life. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10% of employee salary. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions, you should review before applying for the opening. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process, please submit a request via the Disability Accommodations | OEOC | University of Arkansas (uark.edu) : Request an Accommodation. Appli\u00adcants are required to submit a request for each position of which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 479.575.5351. Department: Fulbright College Advising Center Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Reporting to the Director of the College Advising in the Fulbright College of Arts and Sciences, the Academic Advisor will be responsible for providing traditional academic advising support for an assigned caseload of up to 550 undergraduate students. The Academic Advisor will assist students as they work to clarify educational and career goals, develop and implement plans to achieve those goals, make decisions that align with academic policy, and utilize campus resources/processes. In addition to traditional academic advising, this position will be responsible for a number of related duties. The advisor will participate in a small number of coordinated proactive advising programs aimed at aggressively supporting targeted cohorts of advisees (for example, students who have applied for graduation or students that did not enroll as expected). The advisor will engage in a variety of activities related to New Student Orientation through the year and especially in the month of June and, to a lesser degree, other college events. Finally, the advisor will be expected to engage (both proactively and as assigned) in service activities that facilitate the day-to-day operation of the center and/or contribute to the profession of academic advising. Regular, reliable, and non-disruptive attendance is an essential job duty, as is the ability to create and maintain collegial, harmonious working relationships with others. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree with a major in the arts and sciences from an accredited institution of higher education conferred by the time of the appointment \u00a0 OR \u00a0 Bachelor's degree from an accredited institution of higher education conferred by the time of the appointment \u00a0 and \u00a0 At least one year of full-time employment in a field that commonly employs art and sciences graduates \u00a0 Preferred Qualifications: Master's degree completed or completed within six months of start date from an accredited institution of higher education \u00a0 OR \u00a0 At least two years of full-time employment in a field that commonly employs arts and science graduate \u00a0 \u00a0 At least one year of full-time experience in one (or a combination) of the following fields: \u00a0 \u00a0 1. Academic advising or student conduct \u00a0 2. Career advising or coaching \u00a0 3. College, high school, or middle school teaching or counseling \u00a0 4. Social \u00a0 worker \u00a0 or other mental health care \u00a0 professional \u00a0 working directly with clients \u00a0 5. Related higher education experience working directly with students (two years of work as a graduate assistant or adjunct teacher is equivalent to one year full-time) \u00a0 Knowledge, Skills & Abilities (KSAs): Ability to create trust through communication\u00a0 \u00a0 Ability to have adaptability of communication strategies to varying stakeholders \u00a0 Ability to convey the purpose of a liberal arts education to varying stake holders \u00a0 Ability to assess own professional development and \u00a0 identify \u00a0 desired areas of growth \u00a0 Additional Information: Salary Information: $46,383 Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Recruitment Contact Information: Shane Barker Assistant Dean for Academics Fulbright College of Arts and Sciences Sxb028@uark.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Special Instructions to Applicants: Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas seeks to attract, develop and retain high quality faculty, staff and administrators that consistently display practices and behaviors to advance a culture that embeds equal opportunity, educational excellence and unparalleled access for all. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All Application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Fayetteville/Assistant-Professor-of-Childhood-Education_R0090736": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Childhood Education", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com, then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at all University of Arkansas institutions will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students.\u201d University of Arkansas, Fayetteville students will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Student Jobs at UAF.\u201d All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. Closing Date: Type of Position: Faculty - Tenure/Tenure Track Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: Yes Institution Name: University of Arkansas, Fayetteville Founded in 1871, the University of Arkansas is a land grant institution, classified by the Carnegie Foundation among the nation\u2019s top 2 percent of universities with the highest level of research activity. The University of Arkansas works to advance the state and build a better world through education, research, and outreach by providing transformational opportunities and skills, fostering a welcoming climate, and nurturing creativity, discovery, and the spread of new ideas and innovations. The University of Arkansas campus is located in Fayetteville, a welcoming community ranked as one of the best places to live in the U.S. The growing region surrounding Fayetteville is home to numerous Fortune 500 companies and one of the nation\u2019s strongest economies. Northwest Arkansas is also quickly gaining a national reputation for its focus on the arts and overall quality of life. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10% of employee salary. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions, you should review before applying for the opening. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process, please submit a request via the Disability Accommodations | OEOC | University of Arkansas (uark.edu) : Request an Accommodation. Appli\u00adcants are required to submit a request for each position of which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 479.575.5351. Department: Department of Curriculum and Instruction Department's Website: https://cied.uark.edu/ Summary of Job Duties: The Department of Curriculum and Instruction in the College of Education and Health Professions at the University of Arkansas is seeking candidates for a nine-month tenure-track Assistant Professor of Childhood Education faculty position with a specialization in teaching emergent bilingual students and/or bilingual and dual language education. The Assistant Professor of Childhood Education is a full-time, nine-month position to begin August 16, 2027. The successful candidate will join a vibrant team of faculty in a department growing in stature and recognized for excellence in teaching, research, faculty development, and student success. The Assistant Professor of Childhood Education will be expected to teach courses preparing teacher candidates to teach students from all linguistic and cultural backgrounds, including multilingual learners and students in bilingual or dual language programs; conduct research that results in peer-reviewed publications and professional presentations; pursue external funding through grant proposal submissions; participate in student advising and mentoring, including service on dissertation committees; collaborate with colleagues across departmental programs in teaching and service; and collaborate with PK-6 educators and schools related to clinical experiences for preservice teachers. Providing service to the university, college, department, program, profession, and community is a foundational expectation. Through teaching, research, and service, this position supports the University\u2019s 150 Forward priorities of student success, research excellence, and an employer-of-choice environment. This is an in-person position. On-campus presence is an essential function of this position. Extensive in-person engagement in activities such as office hours, student advising, collaborative work, and departmental, college, and university committee meetings is required to advance student success, departmental effectiveness, and the mission of the college and the university. Regular, reliable, and non-disruptive attendance is an essential job duty, as is the ability to create and maintain collegial, harmonious working relationships with others. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: An earned doctorate from a nationally recognized and accredited institution of higher education in Literacy, Elementary Education, Teaching English to Speakers of Other Languages (TESOL), Bilingual and Dual Language Education or a closely related field conferred by the start of employment Evidence and/or promise of effective teaching at the higher education level Evidence of research interest in literacy and TESOL or bilingual and dual language education Evidence of relevant, productive service or potential to actively contribute to the program, department, university, and profession related to bilingual program development and teacher preparation Preferred Qualifications: Evidence of successful in-person and/or online teaching at the higher education level Evidence of teaching and/or preparation of teachers for primary/elementary settings, including bilingual or dual language programs Evidence of scholarly productivity (e.g., publications, presentations, grants) related to literacy and TESOL or bilingual and dual language education Experience in grant writing, managing grants, and/or grant evaluation Evidence and/or promise of advising graduate students, including doctoral candidates Evidence of primary/elementary classroom experience (3 years) in the United States Familiarity with clinical models of teacher preparation (such as immersive field placements, Professional Development Schools, and teaching residencies) Spanish language proficiency Additional Information: This position is a Designated Research Position \u00a0and is regulated by the Arkansas Research Education Protection Act of 2025 .\u00a0 Prior to issuance of an offer of employment, the University is required to request and obtain additional information about an applicant\u2019s background and, if required, conduct an additional review of that background information. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Curriculum Vitae, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title) Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Recruitment Contact Information: Dr. Alissa Blair Assistant Professor ab139@uark.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Special Instructions to Applicants: Completed applications received by October 1, 2026, will be assured full consideration. Late applications will be reviewed as necessary to fill the position. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas seeks to attract, develop and retain high quality faculty, staff and administrators that consistently display practices and behaviors to advance a culture that embeds equal opportunity, educational excellence and unparalleled access for all. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All Application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding Occasional Physical Activity: Hearing Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Fayetteville/Case-Manager_R0090866-1": {"title": "Case Manager", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com, then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at all University of Arkansas institutions will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students.\u201d University of Arkansas, Fayetteville students will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Student Jobs at UAF.\u201d All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. Closing Date: 09/12/2026 Type of Position: Student Support Services Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas, Fayetteville Founded in 1871, the University of Arkansas is a land grant institution, classified by the Carnegie Foundation among the nation\u2019s top 2 percent of universities with the highest level of research activity. The University of Arkansas works to advance the state and build a better world through education, research, and outreach by providing transformational opportunities and skills, fostering a welcoming climate, and nurturing creativity, discovery, and the spread of new ideas and innovations. The University of Arkansas campus is located in Fayetteville, a welcoming community ranked as one of the best places to live in the U.S. The growing region surrounding Fayetteville is home to numerous Fortune 500 companies and one of the nation\u2019s strongest economies. Northwest Arkansas is also quickly gaining a national reputation for its focus on the arts and overall quality of life. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10% of employee salary. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions, you should review before applying for the opening. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process, please submit a request via the Disability Accommodations | OEOC | University of Arkansas (uark.edu) : Request an Accommodation. Appli\u00adcants are required to submit a request for each position of which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 479.575.5351. Department: Fulbright College Advising Center Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Case Manager in the Fulbright College will serve as advisor and point of contact for students navigating a variety of processes related to records, registration, petitions, and academic integrity. They will apply foundational student support competencies to specific student situations as assigned. The Case Manager will work closely with both the Assistant Dean for Academics and the Director of Academic Operations and may be assigned other operational responsibilities as needed. Caseloads will be unpredictable and, at times, extremely high volume. Regular, reliable, and non-disruptive attendance is an essential job duty, as is the ability to create and maintain collegial, harmonious working relationships with others. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree with a major in the arts and sciences from an accredited institution of higher education conferred by the time of the appointment \u00a0 OR \u00a0 Bachelor's degree from an accredited institution of higher education conferred by the time of the appointment \u00a0 AND At least one year of full-time employment in a field that commonly employs art and sciences graduates \u00a0 Preferred Qualifications: Master's degree completed or completed within six months of start date from an accredited institution of higher education \u00a0 OR \u00a0 At least two years of full-time employment in a field that commonly employs arts and science graduate \u00a0 At least one year of full-time experience in one (or a combination) of the following fields: \u00a0 Academic advising or student conduct \u00a0 Career advising or coaching \u00a0 College, high school, or middle school teaching or counseling \u00a0 Social \u00a0 worker \u00a0 or other mental health care \u00a0 professional \u00a0 working directly with clients \u00a0 Related higher education experience working directly with students (two years of work as a graduate assistant or adjunct teacher is equivalent to one year full-time) \u00a0 Knowledge, Skills & Abilities (KSAs): Ability to create trust through communication\u00a0 \u00a0 Ability to have adaptability of communication strategies to varying stakeholders \u00a0 Ability to convey the purpose of a liberal arts education to varying stake holders \u00a0 Ability to assess own professional development and \u00a0 identify \u00a0 desired areas of growth \u00a0 Additional Information: Salary Information: $46,383 Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Recruitment Contact Information: Shane Barker Assistant Dean for Academics Fulbright College of Arts and Sciences Sxb028@uark.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Special Instructions to Applicants: Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas seeks to attract, develop and retain high quality faculty, staff and administrators that consistently display practices and behaviors to advance a culture that embeds equal opportunity, educational excellence and unparalleled access for all. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All Application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Fayetteville/Assistant-Professor-of-Higher-Education_R0090741-1": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Higher Education", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com, then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at all University of Arkansas institutions will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students.\u201d University of Arkansas, Fayetteville students will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Student Jobs at UAF.\u201d All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. Closing Date: Type of Position: Faculty - Tenure/Tenure Track Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: Yes Institution Name: University of Arkansas, Fayetteville Founded in 1871, the University of Arkansas is a land grant institution, classified by the Carnegie Foundation among the nation\u2019s top 2 percent of universities with the highest level of research activity. The University of Arkansas works to advance the state and build a better world through education, research, and outreach by providing transformational opportunities and skills, fostering a welcoming climate, and nurturing creativity, discovery, and the spread of new ideas and innovations. The University of Arkansas campus is located in Fayetteville, a welcoming community ranked as one of the best places to live in the U.S. The growing region surrounding Fayetteville is home to numerous Fortune 500 companies and one of the nation\u2019s strongest economies. Northwest Arkansas is also quickly gaining a national reputation for its focus on the arts and overall quality of life. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10% of employee salary. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions, you should review before applying for the opening. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process, please submit a request via the Disability Accommodations | OEOC | University of Arkansas (uark.edu) : Request an Accommodation. Appli\u00adcants are required to submit a request for each position of which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 479.575.5351. Department: Counseling, Leadership, and Research Methods Department's Website: https://clrm.uark.edu/ Summary of Job Duties: The Assistant Professor of Higher Education is a 9-month tenure-track faculty position in the Department of Counseling, Leadership, and Research Methods in the College of Education and Health Professions at the University of Arkansas. The duties and responsibilities of this faculty position include: teaching graduate courses in the Higher Education Program; conducting research that results in refereed publications and professional presentations; pursuing external funding through grant proposal submissions; mentoring graduate students and chairing/serving on doctoral advisory and dissertation committees; participating in public service and professional organizations; and engaging in service activities at the program, department, college, and university levels. This is an in-person position. Most university classes are offered face-to-face, and extensive in-person engagement in such activities as office hours, student advising, and departmental, college, and university committee meetings is essential to advancing student success and departmental effectiveness. Regular, reliable, and non-disruptive attendance is an essential job duty, as is the ability to create and maintain collegial, harmonious working relationships with others. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: An earned doctorate from a nationally recognized and accredited institution in higher education or a closely related field conferred by the start of employment Demonstrated record of an active research agenda related to higher education as evidenced by publications, presentations, and/or funding activity Ability to teach a variety of graduate courses in higher education Evidence\u00a0and/or\u00a0promise\u00a0of\u00a0productive\u00a0service\u00a0to\u00a0the\u00a0program,\u00a0department, institution, and profession Preferred Qualifications: Research and teaching interests related to higher education leadership, college access, student success, legal issues, student affairs, and/or teaching and learning\u00a0 Expertise in qualitative, quantitative, or mixed methods research Professional experience in higher education Graduate teaching experience Experience submitting and/or securing grant funds Participation in higher education professional/scholarly associations such as ACPA, AERA, ASHE, NASPA, etc. Additional Information: This position is a Designated Research Position \u00a0and is regulated by the Arkansas Research Education Protection Act of 2025 .\u00a0 Prior to issuance of an offer of employment, the University is required to request and obtain additional information about an applicant\u2019s background and, if required, conduct an additional review of that background information. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Curriculum Vitae, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title) Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Recruitment Contact Information: Dr. Becca S. Bassett Assistant Professor of Higher Education bassett@uark.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Special Instructions to Applicants: Completed applications received by October 1, 2026, will be assured full consideration. Late applications will be reviewed as necessary to fill the position. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas seeks to attract, develop and retain high quality faculty, staff and administrators that consistently display practices and behaviors to advance a culture that embeds equal opportunity, educational excellence and unparalleled access for all. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All Application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Fayetteville/Assistant-Professor-of-Public-Health_R0090780-1": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Public Health", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com, then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at all University of Arkansas institutions will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students.\u201d University of Arkansas, Fayetteville students will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Student Jobs at UAF.\u201d All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. Closing Date: Type of Position: Faculty - Tenure/Tenure Track Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: Yes Institution Name: University of Arkansas, Fayetteville Founded in 1871, the University of Arkansas is a land grant institution, classified by the Carnegie Foundation among the nation\u2019s top 2 percent of universities with the highest level of research activity. The University of Arkansas works to advance the state and build a better world through education, research, and outreach by providing transformational opportunities and skills, fostering a welcoming climate, and nurturing creativity, discovery, and the spread of new ideas and innovations. The University of Arkansas campus is located in Fayetteville, a welcoming community ranked as one of the best places to live in the U.S. The growing region surrounding Fayetteville is home to numerous Fortune 500 companies and one of the nation\u2019s strongest economies. Northwest Arkansas is also quickly gaining a national reputation for its focus on the arts and overall quality of life. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10% of employee salary. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions, you should review before applying for the opening. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process, please submit a request via the Disability Accommodations | OEOC | University of Arkansas (uark.edu) : Request an Accommodation. Appli\u00adcants are required to submit a request for each position of which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 479.575.5351. Department: Department of Health, Human Performance & Recreation Department's Website: https://hhpr.uark.edu/ Summary of Job Duties: The College of Education and Health Professions at the University of Arkansas, Fayetteville, invites nominations and applications for an Assistant Professor of Public Health in the Department of Health, Human Performance, and Recreation. The Assistant Professor of Public Health is a 9-month, tenure-track, full-time faculty position. The successful candidate will complement existing strengths within the Public Health Program and the College of Education and Health Professions. Primary Duties and Responsibilities of the Assistant Professor of Public Health include maintaining an ongoing record of research, seeking external funding to support research endeavors, and disseminating research through peer-reviewed publications and presentations; teaching graduate and undergraduate courses in Public Health; supervising Integrative Learning Experiences for MPH students, dissertations, and honors projects; mentor/advise both undergraduate and graduate students; and provide service to the department, college, university, community, and profession. This faculty position is part of the Arkansas Health Research and Solutions cluster hire at the University of Arkansas. Driven by three Fortune 500 companies, booming steel and lithium sectors, world-class museums, and rich natural beauty, Arkansas is transforming into a vibrant hub of opportunity and innovation. Yet Arkansas also faces significant health challenges. Too many Arkansans experience chronic disease, high rates of infant and maternal mortality, mental health crises, and limited healthcare access. Through this cluster hire initiative, the University will advance its land-grant mission by expanding capacity to address our state\u2019s most pressing challenges. Building on existing campus expertise, these new faculty members will advance their research agendas through collaborative research\u2014both with other scholars and with communities in the state\u2014that results in peer-reviewed publications, external funding, and new approaches to healthcare. The successful candidate for this position will join a multidisciplinary community of scholars committed to confronting major issues, generating new knowledge, and providing research-based solutions that improve health outcomes for people living in Arkansas and beyond. This is an in-person position. On-campus presence is an essential function of this position. Extensive in-person engagement in activities such as office hours, student advising, collaborative work, and departmental, college, and university committee meetings is required to advance student success, departmental effectiveness, and the mission of the college and the university. Through teaching, research, and service, this position supports the University\u2019s 150 Forward priorities of student success, research excellence, and an employer-of-choice environment. Regular, reliable, and non-disruptive attendance is an essential job duty, as is the ability to create and maintain collegial, harmonious working relationships with others. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications Earned doctorate from an accredited institution in Public Health or a related field, conferred by the start of employment An established or emerging research agenda with a clear trajectory toward external funding. The area of research inquiry is open, but focal areas include the following areas: implementation science and behavioral health; community-based participatory research, alcohol, tobacco and other drugs; prevention and early intervention in behavioral health; translational health research; big data analytics in public health Record of refereed peer-reviewed publications and presentations Preferred Qualifications: MPH degree from an accredited institution conferred by the start of employment Postdoctoral experience Evidence of or strong potential to obtain external funding Evidence of effective teaching and student mentorship Evidence of or strong potential to engage in interdisciplinary collaborative research.\u00a0 Additional Information: This position is a Designated Research Position \u00a0and is regulated by the Arkansas Research Education Protection Act of 2025 .\u00a0 Prior to issuance of an offer of employment, the University is required to request and obtain additional information about an applicant\u2019s background and, if required, conduct an additional review of that background information. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Curriculum Vitae, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Statement of Research Philosophy Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Recruitment Contact Information: Dr. Bart Hammig Professor bhammig@uark.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Special Instructions to Applicants: Completed applications received by October 1, 2026, will be assured full consideration. Late applications will be reviewed as necessary to fill the position. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas seeks to attract, develop and retain high quality faculty, staff and administrators that consistently display practices and behaviors to advance a culture that embeds equal opportunity, educational excellence and unparalleled access for all. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All Application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Talking Occasional Physical Activity: Talking Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Fayetteville/Assistant-Professor-of-Exercise-Science_R0090779-1": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Exercise Science", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com, then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at all University of Arkansas institutions will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students.\u201d University of Arkansas, Fayetteville students will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Student Jobs at UAF.\u201d All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. Closing Date: Type of Position: Faculty - Tenure/Tenure Track Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: Yes Institution Name: University of Arkansas, Fayetteville Founded in 1871, the University of Arkansas is a land grant institution, classified by the Carnegie Foundation among the nation\u2019s top 2 percent of universities with the highest level of research activity. The University of Arkansas works to advance the state and build a better world through education, research, and outreach by providing transformational opportunities and skills, fostering a welcoming climate, and nurturing creativity, discovery, and the spread of new ideas and innovations. The University of Arkansas campus is located in Fayetteville, a welcoming community ranked as one of the best places to live in the U.S. The growing region surrounding Fayetteville is home to numerous Fortune 500 companies and one of the nation\u2019s strongest economies. Northwest Arkansas is also quickly gaining a national reputation for its focus on the arts and overall quality of life. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10% of employee salary. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions, you should review before applying for the opening. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process, please submit a request via the Disability Accommodations | OEOC | University of Arkansas (uark.edu) : Request an Accommodation. Appli\u00adcants are required to submit a request for each position of which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 479.575.5351. Department: Department of Health, Human Performance & Recreation Department's Website: https://hhpr.uark.edu/ Summary of Job Duties: The Position: The College of Education and Health Professions at the University of Arkansas, Fayetteville, invites nominations and applications for an Assistant Professor of Exercise Science in the Department of Health, Human Performance, and Recreation. The Assistant Professor of Exercise Science is a 9-month, tenure-track, full-time faculty position. The successful candidate will complement or add to existing strengths within the Exercise Science Program and the College of Education and Health Professions. We are seeking candidates who demonstrate both synergy with existing teaching strengths and a commitment to promoting a culture of research excellence. Primary Duties and Responsibilities of the Assistant Professor of Exercise Science include establishing a research agenda capable of securing external funding, publishing in peer-reviewed journals, and presenting at professional conferences; teaching graduate and undergraduate courses in Exercise Science; supervising theses, dissertations, and honors projects; mentor/advise both undergraduate and graduate students; and providing service to the department, college, university, community, and profession. This is an in-person position. On-campus presence is an essential function of this position. Extensive in-person engagement in activities such as office hours, student advising, collaborative work, and departmental, college, and university committee meetings is required to advance student success, departmental effectiveness, and the mission of the college and the university. Through teaching, research, and service, this position supports the University\u2019s 150 Forward priorities of student success, research excellence, and an employer-of-choice environment. Regular, reliable, and non-disruptive attendance is an essential job duty, as is the ability to create and maintain collegial, harmonious working relationships with others. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications Earned doctorate from an accredited institution in Exercise Science or related field conferred by the start of employment An established or emerging research agenda with clear trajectory toward external funding. The area of research inquiry is open, but focal areas include the following: metabolic health, cardiac physiology, respiratory physiology, molecular signaling, female-specific physiology, or multi-omics Record of refereed peer-reviewed publications and presentations Preferred Qualifications Evidence of interdisciplinary research bridging exercise science, health, and education Postdoctoral experience Strong potential for, or history of securing external funding Evidence of effective teaching and student mentorship Additional Information: This position is a Designated Research Position \u00a0and is regulated by the Arkansas Research Education Protection Act of 2025 .\u00a0 Prior to issuance of an offer of employment, the University is required to request and obtain additional information about an applicant\u2019s background and, if required, conduct an additional review of that background information. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Curriculum Vitae, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Statement of Research Philosophy Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Recruitment Contact Information: Dr. Abigail Schmitt Assistant Professor acs063@uark.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Special Instructions to Applicants: Completed applications received by October 1, 2026, will be assured full consideration. Late applications will be reviewed as necessary to fill the position. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas seeks to attract, develop and retain high quality faculty, staff and administrators that consistently display practices and behaviors to advance a culture that embeds equal opportunity, educational excellence and unparalleled access for all. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All Application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Talking Occasional Physical Activity: Talking Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Fayetteville/RazorTemp---Razorback-Raffle-Sellers-1_R0090763-1": {"title": "RazorTemp - Razorback Raffle Sellers-1", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com, then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at all University of Arkansas institutions will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students.\u201d University of Arkansas, Fayetteville students will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Student Jobs at UAF.\u201d All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. Closing Date: 09/08/2026 Type of Position: Staff - Press, Journalism Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas, Fayetteville Founded in 1871, the University of Arkansas is a land grant institution, classified by the Carnegie Foundation among the nation\u2019s top 2 percent of universities with the highest level of research activity. The University of Arkansas works to advance the state and build a better world through education, research, and outreach by providing transformational opportunities and skills, fostering a welcoming climate, and nurturing creativity, discovery, and the spread of new ideas and innovations. The University of Arkansas campus is located in Fayetteville, a welcoming community ranked as one of the best places to live in the U.S. The growing region surrounding Fayetteville is home to numerous Fortune 500 companies and one of the nation\u2019s strongest economies. Northwest Arkansas is also quickly gaining a national reputation for its focus on the arts and overall quality of life. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10% of employee salary. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions, you should review before applying for the opening. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process, please submit a request via the Disability Accommodations | OEOC | University of Arkansas (uark.edu) : Request an Accommodation. Appli\u00adcants are required to submit a request for each position of which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 479.575.5351. Department: RazorTemps Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Responsibilities include, but not limited to: \u2022 Facilitate and process \"50/50\" raffle ticket sales via electronic devices at stationary and / or mobile locations at scheduled University of Arkansas Athletics home games / events \u2022 Proactively approach, engage, and invite fans to participate in Athletics' \"50/50\" raffle (Razorback Raffle) at each game / event, to include education of raffle details / rules and selling of tickets \u2022 Accurately handle transactions from raffle ticket sales \u2022 Serve as a brand ambassador, representing the Razorback Foundation and University of Arkansas Athletics in a positive manner as brand ambassadors, while providing exceptional service to fans. \u2022 Position requires standing, walking and navigation of stairs during the duration of an athletics event; i.e. Football, Basketball, Baseball and others \u2022 Selected candidate will be outgoing, willing to engage with fans in a loud, crowded environment and be comfortable with selling and fundraising Regular, reliable, and non-disruptive attendance is an essential job duty, as is the ability to create and maintain collegial, harmonious working relationships with others. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications 18 years of age or older May not be an immediate family member of employees of the Razorback Foundation or Razorback Athletics Preferred Qualifications Due to the nature/scope of Athletics and Athletics events, position requires attendance at all scheduled home games / matches, which may require work during evenings, weekends, and holidays, as well as the ability to stand / walk for extended periods of time. Additional Information: Salary Information: $20 per hour Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Recruitment Contact Information: RazorTemps rzrtemps@uark.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Special Instructions to Applicants: Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas seeks to attract, develop and retain high quality faculty, staff and administrators that consistently display practices and behaviors to advance a culture that embeds equal opportunity, educational excellence and unparalleled access for all. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All Application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: Grasping, Hearing, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Fayetteville-AR/Admissions-Customer-Service-Manager_R0089708-2": {"title": "Admissions Customer Service Manager", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com, then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at all University of Arkansas institutions will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students.\u201d University of Arkansas, Fayetteville students will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Student Jobs at UAF.\u201d All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. Closing Date: 09/09/2026 Type of Position: Recruitment and Admissions Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas, Fayetteville Founded in 1871, the University of Arkansas is a land grant institution, classified by the Carnegie Foundation among the nation\u2019s top 2 percent of universities with the highest level of research activity. The University of Arkansas works to advance the state and build a better world through education, research, and outreach by providing transformational opportunities and skills, fostering a welcoming climate, and nurturing creativity, discovery, and the spread of new ideas and innovations. The University of Arkansas campus is located in Fayetteville, a welcoming community ranked as one of the best places to live in the U.S. The growing region surrounding Fayetteville is home to numerous Fortune 500 companies and one of the nation\u2019s strongest economies. Northwest Arkansas is also quickly gaining a national reputation for its focus on the arts and overall quality of life. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10% of employee salary. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions, you should review before applying for the opening. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process, please submit a request via the Disability Accommodations | OEOC | University of Arkansas (uark.edu) : Request an Accommodation. Appli\u00adcants are required to submit a request for each position of which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 479.575.5351. Department: Graduate Admissions & Enrollment Management Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Admissions Customer Service Manager is responsible for managing the customer service center. The Admissions Customer Service Manager should be current and well informed on admissions and enrollment related policies and procedures ensuring that student staff consistently provide the highest level of customer service to students, faculty, and staff. This position supervises work-study positions, trains staff, creates and maintains training materials, evaluates workflow needs and reassigns staff and workloads as appropriate. This position serves as the front line, central point of contact for students, staff, and faculty within and outside the GSIE unit on graduate and international admission processes, workflows, and the admission and enrollment status of applicants. Regular, reliable, and non-disruptive attendance is an essential job duty, as is the ability to create and maintain collegial, harmonious working relationships with others. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree from an accredited institution of higher education At least one year of experience in implementing customer service and/or business process solutions Preferred Qualifications: At least two years customer service experience At least one year of related higher education admissions experience Proficient in Microsoft Office Suite (particularly MS Word and Excel) and ability to learn other software as required Knowledge, Skills & Abilities: Knowledge of and the ability to learn university policies and procedures Excellent communication and relationship building skills Skilled\u00a0in identifying complex problems and reviewing related information to develop and evaluate options and implement solutions Organizational skills in managing projects simultaneously while maintaining a satisfactory work product Ability to understand and comply with the Family Educational Rights and Privacy Act (FERPA) Ability to demonstrate and explain how to navigate and view the Slate admissions process to external audiences The ability to receive and follow directions, while maintaining the ability to question current practices and policies Ability to accurately prepare and maintain records, files, and reports Ability to communicate effectively in both verbal and written form Ability to handle difficult and stressful situations with professional composure Ability to establish and maintain a good rapport with university faculty and staff, students, and the\u00a0general public Ability to work successfully as a member of a team and independently with moderate supervision Ability to plan, assign,\u00a0train,\u00a0and\u00a0supervise the work of others Additional Information: Salary Information: $44,000.00 Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Recruitment Contact Information: Miriam Burns, miriamb@uark.edu, Human Resources Business Partner GSIE All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Special Instructions to Applicants: Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas seeks to attract, develop and retain high quality faculty, staff and administrators that consistently display practices and behaviors to advance a culture that embeds equal opportunity, educational excellence and unparalleled access for all. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All Application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Reaching, Repetitive Motion, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Scheduling-Coordinator---Cath-Lab_R0090927-2": {"title": "Scheduling Coordinator - Cath Lab", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/22/2026 Type of Position: Clinical Staff - Nursing Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | CVSL Cardiac Cath Lab IP C Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Scheduling Coordinator is responsible for supporting all department/clinic staff and providers who utilize the schedule for Endoscopy procedural areas. Ensures the procedural schedules are managed according to policies and procedures in a manner that yields maximum utilization and accuracy. Scheduling Coordinators have an in-depth understanding of the operational areas to effectively meet the patient and provider needs. Highly focused on customer service and achievement of perioperative utilization metrics. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree plus three (3) years of experience in patient registration, scheduling, or billing in a healthcare environment OR High school graduate, GED, or formal education equivalent plus (7) seven years of training and/or experience in business office administration, customer service, or related work of which three years\u2019 experience is in patient registration, scheduling, or billing in a healthcare environment Additional Information: Responsibilities: Responsible for managing case requests ensuring accuracy and the completion of all required pre-authorizations and clinical screenings prior to placing on the schedule. Schedulers monitor requested times for alignment with case time averaging and scheduling policies/procedures. Collaborates with procedural area leadership in determining appropriateness of placement and alignment with staffing and targeted rooms in operation at specified times. Schedulers are integral players in ensuring all capacity, access and utilization targets are met resulting in achievement of budgetary/revenue expectations. Schedulers will be assigned primary specialties and services they support while having the ability to meet the need for any service/specialty/department. High level of skill and understanding of Epic Optime required. Acts as the point of contact for procedural scheduling for all UAMS departments/clinics staff and providers. Other duties as assigned. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience\") Required Documents to Apply: List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Criminal Background Check, Substance Abuse Testing This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Crawling, Crouching, Feeling, Grasping, Hearing, Kneeling, Lifting, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Repetitive Motion, Sitting, Standing, Stooping, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Crawling, Crouching, Driving, Feeling, Grasping, Hearing, Kneeling, Lifting, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Repetitive Motion, Sitting, Standing, Stooping, Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Crawling, Crouching, Driving, Feeling, Grasping, Hearing, Kneeling, Lifting, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Repetitive Motion, Sitting, Standing, Stooping, Talking, Walking Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Scheduling-Coordinator---Cath-Lab_R0090931-1": {"title": "Scheduling C