review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | CVSL Cardiac Cath Lab IP C Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Scheduling Coordinator is responsible for supporting all department/clinic staff and providers who utilize the schedule for Cath Lab procedural areas. Ensures the procedural schedules are managed according to policies and procedures in a manner that yields maximum utilization and accuracy. Scheduling Coordinators have an in-depth understanding of the operational areas to effectively meet the patient and provider needs. Highly focused on customer service and achievement of perioperative utilization metrics. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree plus three (3) years of experience in patient registration, scheduling, or billing in a healthcare environment OR High school graduate, GED, or formal education equivalent plus (7) seven years of training and/or experience in business office administration, customer service, or related work of which three years\u2019 experience is in patient registration, scheduling, or billing in a healthcare environment Additional Information: Responsibilities: Responsible for managing case requests ensuring accuracy and the completion of all required pre-authorizations and clinical screenings prior to placing on the schedule. Schedulers monitor requested times for alignment with case time averaging and scheduling policies/procedures. Collaborates with procedural area leadership in determining appropriateness of placement and alignment with staffing and targeted rooms in operation at specified times. Schedulers are integral players in ensuring all capacity, access and utilization targets are met resulting in achievement of budgetary/revenue expectations. Schedulers will be assigned primary specialties and services they support while having the ability to meet the need for any service/specialty/department. High level of skill and understanding of Epic Optime required. Acts as the point of contact for procedural scheduling for all UAMS departments/clinics staff and providers. Other duties as assigned. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Criminal Background Check, Substance Abuse Testing This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Climbing, Crouching, Driving, Feeling, Grasping, Hearing, Kneeling, Lifting, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Repetitive Motion, Sitting, Standing, Stooping, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Crawling, Crouching, Driving, Feeling, Grasping, Hearing, Kneeling, Lifting, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Repetitive Motion, Sitting, Standing, Stooping, Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Crawling, Crouching, Feeling, Grasping, Hearing, Kneeling, Lifting, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Repetitive Motion, Sitting, Standing, Stooping, Talking, Walking Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/RN---Healthy-Heart_R0090923-1": {"title": "RN - Healthy Heart", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 10/01/2026 Type of Position: Clinical Staff - Nursing Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | CVSL Healthy Heart Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Heart Healthy Screening Nurse conducts comprehensive cardiovascular risk assessments for clients during the organization's screening events. The nurse's primary role is to perform a series of health screenings and educate clients on their results and heart disease prevention. This position requires strong clinical skills, excellent communication, and the ability to manage and be self directed. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications:\u00a0 Graduate of an accredited Nursing Program with Associates Degree, Nursing Diploma, Bachelors in Nursing, or Master's in Nursing\u00a0; Valid RN License; Minimum of 1 year Registered Nursing experience. Preferred Qualifications: Previous experience in a cardiac, outpatient clinic, or public health screening setting. Additional Information: Responsibilities: Perform direct, one-on-one screenings with clients, which may include: Taking medical histories related to cardiac risk factors. Measuring and recording vital signs such as blood pressure and heart rate. Collecting blood samples for lab work, such as cholesterol and glucose testing. Performing electrocardiograms (EKGs)\u00a0 Performing urine dip sticks test Provide health education based on screening results to help clients understand their current health status and risks for heart disease. Educate clients on preventative care, lifestyle modifications, and how to improve their heart health. Refer and coordinate follow-up with a provider, such as a cardiologist or primary care physician, when screening results indicate a need for further evaluation. Maintain accurate and confidential client records, documenting all screening results and educational interventions. Ensure a smooth patient flow during screening events by efficiently managing appointments . Adhere to all health protocols and safety procedures, including maintaining a sterile environment. Collaborate with a multidisciplinary team to deliver comprehensive care and a positive client experience.\u00a0 May perform other duties as assigned. Salary Information: \"Commensurate with education and experience\" Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Criminal Background Check, Substance Abuse Testing This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Crouching, Grasping, Hearing, Lifting, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Lifting Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Fayetteville/Foundry-Engineer_R0090585": {"title": "Foundry Engineer", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com, then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at all University of Arkansas institutions will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students.\u201d University of Arkansas, Fayetteville students will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Student Jobs at UAF.\u201d All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. Closing Date: 10/01/2026 Type of Position: Researchers and Scientists Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Fixed Duration of Project/Grant (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas, Fayetteville Founded in 1871, the University of Arkansas is a land grant institution, classified by the Carnegie Foundation among the nation\u2019s top 2 percent of universities with the highest level of research activity. The University of Arkansas works to advance the state and build a better world through education, research, and outreach by providing transformational opportunities and skills, fostering a welcoming climate, and nurturing creativity, discovery, and the spread of new ideas and innovations. The University of Arkansas campus is located in Fayetteville, a welcoming community ranked as one of the best places to live in the U.S. The growing region surrounding Fayetteville is home to numerous Fortune 500 companies and one of the nation\u2019s strongest economies. Northwest Arkansas is also quickly gaining a national reputation for its focus on the arts and overall quality of life. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10% of employee salary. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions, you should review before applying for the opening. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process, please submit a request via the Disability Accommodations | OEOC | University of Arkansas (uark.edu) : Request an Accommodation. Appli\u00adcants are required to submit a request for each position of which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 479.575.5351. Department: Department of Physics Research Assistants 02 Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: MonArk NSF Quantum Foundry (a consortium between Montana State University, University of Utah, University of Arkansas) is seeking to fill a position of Foundry Engineer to support its Arkansas site. The Foundry operates as a shared user facility supporting researchers across multiple institutions. This role requires balancing hands-on engineering work with user support, system reliability, and collaborative development. The Foundry Engineer will work closely with multidisciplinary teams to design, build, integrate, and maintain automated fabrication systems, focusing on developing software for existing systems supporting the ongoing integration of new automation capabilities. This role combines hands-on engineering, system integration, and software control development to enable reliable, production-grade quantum device fabrication workflows. This role will play a critical part in finalizing and operationalizing robotic automation systems, enabling reproducible, high-throughput quantum device fabrication within a shared user facility. Key Responsibilities \u2022 Develop and implement software-based control frameworks for existing automated machinery and robotics systems \u2022 Collaborate with Foundry staff, students, and other users to design, implement, and maintain research tools and automated fabrication systems \u2022 Troubleshoot and optimize integrated hardware/software systems to meet production and quality goals \u2022 Provide training and technical support to facility users and staff \u2022 Continuously evaluate and improve systems to enhance reliability, safety, and throughput \u2022 Ensure systems comply with safety standards and operational protocols in a research laboratory setting \u2022 Support and guide students and researchers using foundry systems \u2022 Occasional travel to partner institutions (e.g., Montana State University, University of Utah) may be required for collaboration and system integration. This is a one year appointment, renewable based on the need for the position, availability of funding, and continued satisfactory level of performance in the role. Regular, reliable, and non-disruptive attendance is an essential job duty, as is the ability to create and maintain collegial, harmonious working relationships with others. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor\u2019s degree in Robotics, Mechanical Engineering, Electrical Engineering, Computer Engineering, Computer Science, or a related field At least four to seven years of experience in robotics, automation, or autonomous systems Strong programming skills in Python with experience in control systems, automation, or robotics software Experience with JavaScript/HTML for user interfaces and Git-based version control workflows Demonstrated experience integrating hardware and software in complex robotic or automation environments Hands-on experience with system debugging, troubleshooting, and deployment in lab or field settings Familiarity with robotic subsystems (e.g., mobility platforms, robotic arms, grippers, sensors, safety systems, embedded electronics) Ability to manage multiple projects and adapt to evolving technical requirements Preferred Qualifications: Experience in research lab environments, user facilities, or shared instrumentation settings Experience with CAD tools (e.g., SolidWorks, Fusion 360) and mechanical system design Background in semiconductor, cleanroom, or advanced manufacturing environments Demonstrated experience mentoring students and overseeing their work Additional Information: This position is a Designated Research Position \u00a0and is regulated by the Arkansas Research Education Protection Act of 2025 .\u00a0 Prior to issuance of an offer of employment, the University is required to request and obtain additional information about an applicant\u2019s background and, if required, conduct an additional review of that background information. This position is renewable annually based on continued need for the position, availability of funding, and satisfactory job performance. Salary Information: $65,000 Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Recruitment Contact Information: Hugh Churchill, Professor and Director of the Arkansas Materials Institute, hchurch@uark.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Special Instructions to Applicants: Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas seeks to attract, develop and retain high quality faculty, staff and administrators that consistently display practices and behaviors to advance a culture that embeds equal opportunity, educational excellence and unparalleled access for all. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All Application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/RN-Neonatal-Intensive-Care-Unit-F5-H5_R0090821": {"title": "RN Neonatal Intensive Care Unit F5/H5", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/15/2026 Type of Position: Clinical Staff - Nursing Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | WISL Neonatal ICU IP C Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Registered Nurse (RN) provides direct patient care to assigned patients in our Neonatal Intensive Care Unit (F5/H5). This is a 64 bed NICU (Neonatal Intensive Care Unit) with single-room design providing care for early high-risk, low birth weight infants as well as acutely ill full-term newborns. NICU is a Level IIIB Nursery and provides 24/7 physician and nursing care to serve the citizens of the State of Arkansas. High level developmental and technological care is combined with the specialized neonatal expertise of our health care team. The dedication of our NICU team allows us to provide patient- and family-centered care through Comfort, Hope and Healing to each infant and their family. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Graduate of an accredited Nursing Program with Associates Degree, Nursing Diploma, Bachelors in Nursing, or Master's in Nursing. Valid RN License 1 year of Registered nursing experience Excellent communication skills Basic computer skills Strong work ethics and accountability. Preferred Qualifications: 2 or more years of Registered nursing experience with current BLS. NICU experience Employees in this role must be fitted for, capable of donning and performing routine tasks in personal protective equipment to include N95 masks, Powered Air Purifying Respirators (PAPR) or Controlled Air Purifying Respirators (CAPR). Additional Information: Job Requirements: Delivers nursing care according to the standard of care defined by UAMS, ANA and Standards for specialty patient population with support and mentoring by other team members Collects and documents assessment data Develops a Plan of Care (POC) per standard Implements POC including medical order and interdisciplinary approach Evaluates the progress of patient toward attainment of desired outcomes Provides effective patient/family education/discharge planning Administers medication per standard including drug information to patients/families Acts as a resource/supports others; Delivers patient care using the principles of the defined nursing modality Delegates care based on UAMS standards, legal and regulatory requirements, specific job description and individual level of education and training Contributes to a positive work environment that is conducive to clinical education while serving as a resource for student nurses and staff. Other duties as assigned PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS Stand: Frequently Sit: Frequently Walk: Occasionally Bend, crawl, crouch, kneel, stoop or reach overhead: Frequently Lift and carry weight: 25 lbs Push and pull weight: 25 lbs Use hands to touch, handle or feel: Frequently Talk: Continuously Hear: Continuously Taste or smell: Occasionally Read, concentrate, think analytically: Continuously Physical Environment : Inside Medical Facility Environment Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry, Substance Abuse Testing This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Hearing Frequent Physical Activity: Feeling, Grasping, Lifting, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Pulling, Pushing, Sharps, Standing, Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Crawling, Crouching, Kneeling, Reaching, Sitting, Stooping Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Volunteer-Coordinator_R0090817-1": {"title": "Volunteer Coordinator", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/15/2026 Type of Position: Professional Staff - Project/Program Administration Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | CORE Volunteer Services IOP NC Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The position of Volunteer Coordinator reports directly to the Director of the UAMS Medical Center Department of Volunteer Engagement and is responsible for assisting the Director with recruiting, training, coordinating, scheduling and supervising the 200-250 regular volunteers and additional special projects volunteers. At the direction of the Director, the Volunteer Coordinator will act in the Director\u2019s absence. Outstanding oral and written communication skills and decision-making skills are required; ability to think independently while fostering team interactions are essential in this highly visible position. As part of the UAMS Center for Patients and Families, the Volunteer Coordinator fosters patient- and family-centered care and works in respectful, supportive, and collaborative ways with patients and families. This position is committed to a patient- and family-centered approach to care, an approach that is collaborative and encourages the active engagement of the patient and family in care and decision-making. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelors Degree and two (2) years of event planning or non-profit experience.\u00a0 Certified Volunteer Manager or willing to work toward certification within 18 months Proficient in Windows, Microsoft Office (Word, Publisher, Excel, PowerPoint) Preferred Qualifications: Workday and other software programs including Volgistics-Volunteer Program Software \u00a0Experience with maintaining financial records/reports Additional Information: Job Requirements: Participates on a multidisciplinary patient intake team for their assigned clinic by greeting and escorting new patients and connecting them to volunteer resources. Prepares materials for and conducts new patient orientation sessions for the clinic. Performs inpatient rounds to assess patient psychosocial needs and concerns and provides reporting back to clinical staff. Perform other duties as needed. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS Stand: Frequently Sit: Frequently Walk: Occasionally Bend, crawl, crouch, kneel, stoop or reach overhead: Frequently Lift and carry weight: 25 lbs Push and pull weight: 25 lbs Use hands to touch, handle or feel: Frequently Talk: Continuously Hear: Continuously Taste or smell: Occasionally Read, concentrate, think analytically: Continuously Physical Environment : Inside Medical Facility Environment Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience. Required Documents to Apply: List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Criminal Background Check This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Data-Integrity-Technician_R0090728-1": {"title": "Data Integrity Technician", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Clerical Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Little Rock The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is a metropolitan research university that provides an accessible, quality education through flexible learning and unparalleled internship opportunities. At UA Little Rock, we prepare our more than 8,900 students to be innovators and responsible leaders in their fields. Committed to its metropolitan research university mission, UA Little Rock is a driving force in Little Rock's thriving cultural community and a major component of the city and state's growing profile as a regional leader in research, technology transfer, economic development, and job creation. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . Department: Admissions Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Data Integrity Technician in the Office of Admissions and Recruitment plays an important role in supporting the extensive use of the customer relationship management (CRM) to strategically communicate with prospective students throughout the funnel by ensuring the accuracy of the data in the CRM and student information system (SIS). \u00a0 Qualifications: Required Education and/or Experience: The formal education equivalent of a high school diploma, plus one year of specialized training in business management, business education, or a related field. OTHER JOB-RELATED EDUCATION AND/OR EXPERIENCE MAY BE SUBSTITUTED FOR ALL OR PART OF THESE BASIC REQUIREMENTS, EXCEPT FOR THE HIGH SCHOOL DIPLOMA REQUIREMENT. \u00a0 Preferred Education and/or Experience: Demonstrated experience with spreadsheets in a Windows environment; Demonstrated experience with customer relationship management (CRM) software; Experience in developing a positive team environment.\u00a0 Job Duties and Responsibilities: Scrub CRM data to resolve duplicates, fulfill unsubscribe requests, and update undelivered emails; Perform lead address cleanup to assign new leads to appropriate territories; Load standardized test data into SIS; Prepare data for variable print publication production; Format data appropriately for bulk imports into CRM; Prepare lists for bulk mail fulfillment; Support office processes as needed; Perform other duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Ability to follow directions and work independently as part of a larger team; Must be detail-oriented; Must be self-motivated, creative, and customer-service focused; Demonstrate ability to work in a fast-paced multi-tasking environment; Strong interpersonal and relationship-building skills. Additional Information: Salary Information: $30,773 Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Jordan Breckenridge Enrollment Services Manager 501-916-3127 All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Repetitive Motion, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Feeling, Grasping, Lifting, Pulling, Pushing Occasional Physical Activity: Climbing, Crawling, Kneeling, Lifting, Pulling, Pushing Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Grants-and-Contracts-Accounting-Specialist_R0090826": {"title": "Grants and Contracts Accounting Specialist", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/15/2026 Type of Position: Professional Staff (Non-Classified) Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Little Rock The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is a metropolitan research university that provides an accessible, quality education through flexible learning and unparalleled internship opportunities. At UA Little Rock, we prepare our more than 8,900 students to be innovators and responsible leaders in their fields. Committed to its metropolitan research university mission, UA Little Rock is a driving force in Little Rock's thriving cultural community and a major component of the city and state's growing profile as a regional leader in research, technology transfer, economic development, and job creation. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . Department: Research and Sponsored Programs - Post Award Department's Website: https://ualr.edu/orsp/ Summary of Job Duties: The Grants and Contracts Accounting Specialist reports to the Associate Director for Post Award Activities in the Office of Research and Sponsored Programs, and will perform accounting functions associated with the administration of fiscal activities related to sponsored grants and contracts, analyze fiscal and project activity in relation to sponsor terms and conditions, and will communicate with principal investigators and funding sources to resolve issues and gather information. This position is governed by state and federal laws, and agency/institution policy. Qualifications: Required Education and/or Experience: A Bachelor\u2019s degree in accounting, finance, business administration or closely related discipline. Preferred Education and/or Experience: One (1) year of general accounting experience. Proficiency using Microsoft Office applications. Experience utilizing Microsoft Excel to compile and analyze financial data. Experience with Workday and Ellucian Banner a plus. Job Duties and Responsibilities: Set up new grants, contracts, awards and agreements; manage a portfolio of sponsored programs to include: monthly, quarterly, ad hoc and/or final invoicing and reporting applicable to post award activities and maintaining appropriate documentation in ORSP\u2019s internal spreadsheets and award files. 25% Provide technical assistance in the management of research grants, contracts, awards and agreements, including fielding daily inquiries from principal investigators and/or their administrative staff, as well as other personnel and units throughout the University. 20% Review terms and conditions of grants, contracts, awards and agreements to ensure compliance with institutional, federal, state and/or local regulations. Initiate necessary corrective actions where applicable. 10% Review and monitor expenditures of grants, contracts, awards and agreements for accuracy, allocability, allowability, completeness, and reasonableness. Initiate necessary corrective actions where applicable. 10% Review and approve grant related business processes submitted through Workday, as well as paper forms,\u00a0including but not limited to: Ad Hoc forms,\u00a0 Student Ad Hoc forms, and Special Meeting forms. Initiate necessary corrective actions where applicable. 10% Deposit and apply sponsored program receivables, apply electronic receivables, and maintain appropriate documentation in ORSP\u2019s internal spreadsheets and award files. 10% Participate in and provide documentation for audits performed of sponsored programs. 5% Assist in the delivery of a variety of workshops, training sessions, and other outreach instruments that instruct internal and external constituents about the evolving research and sponsored programs administrative and compliance landscape. 5% Other duties as assigned. 5% Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Ability to interpret and apply accounting policies and procedures Knowledge of general accounting principles, financial operations, laws, and terminology Accuracy and attention to detail is essential Ability to design, analyze, and prepare financial reports Ability to set priorities and manage several projects at once, under deadline pressure Knowledge of federal and non-federal regulations related to research and sponsored grants and contracts preferred Ability to instill confidence in internal and external ORSP constituents in the competence and commitment to service of the office Strong interpersonal skills with a high degree of analytical ability Verbal and written communication skills Ability to maintain confidentiality. Additional Information: Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Shawna Diaz Associate Director, Post-award sldiaz@ualr.edu 501-916-6231 All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Financial Credit Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting Frequent Physical Activity: Grasping, Hearing, Reaching, Repetitive Motion, Standing, Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Kneeling, Lifting, Pulling, Pushing Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Fayetteville/Teaching-Assistant-Professor-in-Advertising-and-Public-Relations_R0090702-1": {"title": "Teaching Assistant Professor in Advertising and Public Relations", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com, then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at all University of Arkansas institutions will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students.\u201d University of Arkansas, Fayetteville students will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Student Jobs at UAF.\u201d All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. Closing Date: Type of Position: Faculty - Non-Tenure Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Academic Term (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: Yes Institution Name: University of Arkansas, Fayetteville Founded in 1871, the University of Arkansas is a land grant institution, classified by the Carnegie Foundation among the nation\u2019s top 2 percent of universities with the highest level of research activity. The University of Arkansas works to advance the state and build a better world through education, research, and outreach by providing transformational opportunities and skills, fostering a welcoming climate, and nurturing creativity, discovery, and the spread of new ideas and innovations. The University of Arkansas campus is located in Fayetteville, a welcoming community ranked as one of the best places to live in the U.S. The growing region surrounding Fayetteville is home to numerous Fortune 500 companies and one of the nation\u2019s strongest economies. Northwest Arkansas is also quickly gaining a national reputation for its focus on the arts and overall quality of life. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10% of employee salary. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions, you should review before applying for the opening. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process, please submit a request via the Disability Accommodations | OEOC | University of Arkansas (uark.edu) : Request an Accommodation. Appli\u00adcants are required to submit a request for each position of which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 479.575.5351. Department: School of Journalism and Strategic Media Department's Website: https://journalism.uark.edu/ Summary of Job Duties: The School of Journalism and Strategic Media in the Fulbright College of Arts and Sciences at the University of Arkansas invites applications for a non-tenure track Teaching Assistant Professor in Advertising and Public Relations, a teaching-focused position beginning August 2027. This is a standard nine-month non-tenure track faculty appointment. We welcome candidates who can teach a range of core Advertising and Public Relations (ADPR) courses, including Advertising Principles, Public Relations Principles, Public Relations Writing, Media Planning & Strategy, Account Planning, Campaigns, and digital and social media, as well as develop courses in their areas of expertise responsive to evolving industry needs. We particularly welcome candidates with professional experience working with consumer-packaged goods (CPG) brands or clients and managing teams and client-based projects. The successful candidate will teach a 4\u20134 load of core and elective courses in the ADPR degree program within the School of Journalism and Strategic Media. The position also includes service responsibilities within the School. This is an on-campus position. Regular, reliable, and non-disruptive attendance is an essential job duty, as is the ability to create and maintain collegial, harmonious working relationships with others. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: A terminal degree in advertising, public relations, mass communication, or a closely related field from an accredited institution of higher education conferred by the date of initial appointment A demonstrated record of effective college-level teaching in advertising, public relations, strategic communication, or a closely related field At least three years of professional experience in advertising, public relations, strategic communication, marketing, or a closely related field Preferred Qualifications: Professional experience working with consumer-packaged goods (CPG) brands or clients, with expertise relevant to advertising and public relations instruction, including areas such as new business acquisitions, new product development and positioning research, brand strategy, consumer insights, media planning, social and influencer marketing, retail media/e-commerce, omnichannel communication, or related areas, particularly in categories such as food and beverages and mass merchandise retail Professional experience managing teams and/or client-based advertising, public relations, or strategic communication projects Evidence of effective mentoring or advising of undergraduate, honors, and/or graduate students, including advising applied projects, independent studies, or theses, and advising student organizations such as Ad Club and the Public Relations Student Society of America (PRSSA) Evidence of current engagement with the advertising and/or public relations professions through professional practice, consulting, industry partnerships, or professional organizations Experience developing or updating courses and curricula in response to evolving industry practices and technologies Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities (KSAs): Current knowledge of emerging advertising and public relations practices, technologies, and industry trends, including areas such as artificial intelligence, digital and social media, e-commerce and retail media, and audience analytics Skilled in using professional-grade tools for content creation, media planning, social media management, analytics, and campaign management (e.g., Adobe Creative Cloud, Cision, Meltwater, Sprout Social, Hootsuite, or comparable platforms) Strong communication and interpersonal skills Ability to integrate real-world professional experience and networks into the academic environment to create a dynamic learning experience for students Evidence of or potential for scholarly, professional, and/or creative activity relevant to advertising and public relations Additional Information: About the Department: The School of Journalism and Strategic Media at the University of Arkansas is fully-accredited by ACEJMC, offering a Bachelor of Arts in Journalism with concentrations in Broadcast Journalism, Journalism, and Multimedia Journalism and a Bachelor of Arts in Advertising and Public Relations. SJSM also offers a Master of Arts in Journalism \u2013 in total serving more than 950 undergrads and grads in AY25-26.\u00a0 Duties will include: 80% Teaching 10% Research 10% Academic Service Salary Information: Salary is commensurate with experience and qualifications. Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Curriculum Vitae, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Statement of Teaching Philosophy Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Recruitment Contact Information: Dr. Sisi Hu, search committee chair, sisih@uark.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Special Instructions to Applicants: Completed applications received by October 11, 2026, will be assured full consideration. Late applications will be reviewed as necessary to fill the position. For additional inquiries, please contact the search committee chair, Dr. Sisi Hu, at sisih@uark.edu. Applicants must submit: \u2022 Curriculum vitae \u2022 Cover letter/letter of application \u2022 Teaching philosophy statement which may include evidence of teaching effectiveness (not to exceed three pages) \u2022 List of three professional references (name, title, email address, and phone number) willing to provide letters of recommendation if requested during the application process. Letters of recommendation will be requested only for candidates selected for interviews. Review of applications will begin October 11, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas seeks to attract, develop and retain high quality faculty, staff and administrators that consistently display practices and behaviors to advance a culture that embeds equal opportunity, educational excellence and unparalleled access for all. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All Application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Associate-Program-Manager_R0090691-1": {"title": "Associate Program Manager", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 10/01/2026 Type of Position: Professional Staff - Project/Program Administration Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: TRI | Clinical Research Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Associate Program Manager serves as a navigator to connect faculty investigators with the Translational Research Institute's (TRI\u2019s) broad portfolio of resources and services. Primary responsibilities include managing the TRI Clinical Trial Innovation Unit\u2019s (CTIU) portfolio of new clinical trial opportunities, including matching new study opportunities with UAMS investigators, leading pre-study site selection activities, to include feasibility assessments and facilitating pre-study site visits for prospective research sponsors. The Associate Program Manager will participate in the national Clinical and Translational Science Award (CTSA) initiatives, including serving as UAMS\u2019 liaison to the CTSA Trial Innovation Network (TIN) and will work independently to create, manage, and oversee projects for the TRI. Leads cross-functional project teams and tracks progress of projects to ensure timely completion of project deliverables. Position requires exceptional communication skills and involves constant collaboration with TRI leadership and staff, UAMS faculty, and other institutional stakeholders. Qualifications: Bachelor\u2019s degree plus two (2) years of project/program management experience required. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities: High-level written and verbal communication skills. \u00a0 Ability to create and track project deadlines and communicate the progress of projects with others. Requires frequent interaction with various levels of campus leadership, and therefore requires an ability to resolve issues professionally. \u00a0 Leadership and communication skills. Experience working with teams. Ability to complete project outcomes. Responsibilities: Manage new clinical trial opportunities by matching study opportunities with interested investigators.\u00a0 Establishes initial contact with study sponsors and contract research organizations.\u00a0 Facilitates confidentiality/non-disclosure agreements required for vetting of new study opportunities.\u00a0 Completes site information forms and feasibility assessments to enable the site selection process.\u00a0 Organizes and schedules pre-study site visits for prospective research sponsors to include facility tours and facilitating meetings with TRI staff and other UAMS stakeholders. Collects essential study documents from sponsors/lead study site before releasing to other CTIU teams to begin active study start-up.\u00a0 Thoroughly documents pre-study activities in research informatics systems to enable reporting of metrics and continuous quality improvement of clinical trial start-up processes. Serves as the initial point of contact for TRI hub investigators to request resources, services, or consultation from the TRI.\u00a0 Facilitates access to TRI resources and services by connecting each requestor with the appropriate core leadership and subject matter expert(s) to evaluate the request and provide services.\u00a0 Contributes to continuous quality improvement efforts by tracking relevant metrics for each request via the TRI Services Portal. Regularly represents TRI by participating in national CTSA activities.\u00a0 Serves as a primary point of contact for the CTSA Trial Innovation Network (TIN) and acts as liaison for TIN activities across all TRI hub sites.\u00a0 Leads and/or assists with organizing and planning TRI-sponsored special events and projects.\u00a0 Performs other duties as assigned. Additional Information: Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: No Background Check Required This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting, Standing, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Lifting, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAM--Monticello-Campus/Post-Doc-Research-Associate_R0090864-1": {"title": "Post Doc Research Associate", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Researchers Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Monticello UAM, one of twenty campuses of the University of Arkansas System, is located in southeastern Arkansas in the beautiful timberlands, rich in outdoor recreation activities, and approximately 100 miles south of Little Rock. UAM is a comprehensive, residential and commuter, undergraduate institution also offering selected master\u2019s degree programs. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please submit a request via the OEOC website: \u00a0Applicants are required to submit a request for each position to which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 870-460-1422 . Department: Forestry / Agri / Nat. Resourc Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The postdoctoral researcher will contribute to high-impact publications, collaborate with a broad network of research and management partners, assist in developing competitive research proposals, and help shape future research directions within the Snowden Waterfowl Center of Excellence. The successful candidate should possess strong quantitative and analytical skills, experience with spatial ecology and movement analyses, and the ability to work effectively in a collaborative, multidisciplinary research environment. Qualifications: Applicants must have earned a Ph.D. in wildlife science, landscape ecology, geospatial science, waterfowl ecology, or a closely related field. Preferred qualifications include experience with: GPS telemetry and animal movement analyses. Geospatial analysis, GIS, and remote sensing. Statistical, ecological, and machine-learning modeling using modern analytical software (e.g., R or Python). Google Earth Engine and cloud-based geospatial analysis. Spatial visualization, mapping applications, and predictive ecological modeling. Applicants must possess a valid U.S. driver's license (or obtain one within 60 days of employment). The position will include fieldwork, overnight travel, and attendance at scientific conferences. Additional Information: Salary Information: $65,000 Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Curriculum Vitae, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Dr. Douglas Osborne osborne@uamont.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Motor Vehicle Reports Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Driving, Reaching, Repetitive Motion Occasional Physical Activity: Crouching, Feeling, Grasping, Kneeling, Lifting, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Fordyce/Administrative-Specialist-III_R0090815-1": {"title": "Administrative Specialist III", "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Clerical Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: Division of Agriculture of the University of Arkansas The University of Arkansas System Division of Agriculture is a state wide campus, with faculty based on University campuses, at Research and Extension Centers and in every Arkansas county. It consists of the Arkansas Agricultural Experiment Station (AES) and the Arkansas Cooperative Extension Service (CES), and is home to more than 1400 employees.\u00a0 The Division was established in 1959 and is headed by the Vice-President for Agriculture.\u00a0 The Division headquarters is located in Little Rock with the rest of the University of Arkansas System Administration.\u00a0 As an employer, the University of Arkansas System Division of Agriculture offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance.\u00a0 Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process and require reasonable accommodations, please contact the Division's Office of Program & Employment Compliance at compliance@uada.edu . For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-671-2219 or 479-502-9820. Department: CEA * Staff Chair * Dallas County Department's Website: https://uaex.uada.edu/counties/dallas/ Summary of Job Duties: The Administrative Specialist\u00a0III\u00a0is responsible for coordinating office activities, researching and preparing special reports, and developing, revising, and recommending administrative policies and procedures as directed by supervisor. Self-Management: \u2022 Organizes and prioritizes tasks effectively \u2022 Deals appropriately with interruptions. \u2022 Uses good judgment and decision making skills. \u2022 Possess strong organizational skills with the ability to multi-task. \u2022 Follows attendance and leave policies. \u2022 Practices emotional control. \u2022 Exhibits professional behavior and appearance. \u2022 Ability to handle sensitive information in a confidential manner. \u2022 Ability to work without close supervision. Quality and Quantity of Work: \u2022 Produces high-quality and error free work \u2022 Orders and maintains sufficient stock of office supplies for county staff. \u2022 Maintains hard copy and electronic files with ability to efficiently retrieve needed information. \u2022 Weeds files based on file retention policies. \u2022 Maintains civil rights files and documents including meeting attendance logs, County Extension Council membership lists, and committee minutes. \u2022 Processes agricultural samples for mailing. \u2022 Updates calendar with itineraries and scheduled events. \u2022 Submits weekly itineraries to District Office. \u2022 Assists county staff with arrangements for upcoming meetings. \u2022 Maintains accurate mailing lists. \u2022 Enters and Submits agent\u2019s monthly travel claim into Workday program. \u2022 Completes and submits monthly postage and copier report. \u2022 Receives, sorts and distributes incoming mail. \u2022 Processes outgoing mail. \u2022 Checks and responds to email regularly throughout the day. \u2022 Provides administrative support for all agents. \u2022 Assists agents and program assistants in reporting data in program areas of Agriculture and Natural Resources, Family and Consumer Sciences, 4H, and Community and Economic Development. \u2022 Performs other duties as assigned Technical Expertise: \u2022 Uses Workday, the U of A Systems cloud based program to track expenditures, county depository documentation, procurement, purchases, requisitions, time, travel and other financial management applications. \u2022 Uses software such as Microsoft word, Excel, PowerPoint, and other programs to support Extension educational programs. \u2022 Maintains equipment. \u2022 Maintains inventory control of computers and equipment. \u2022 Attends training to maintain and upgrade skills. \u2022 Performs support work such as word processing, creating spreadsheets, data entry and retrieval, reviews and proofreads forms, data and other information to ensure accuracy and conformance to established procedures and policies. \u2022 Generates reports and records. Financial Recordkeeping: \u2022 Keeps record of all revenue and expenses from County depository account. \u2022 Enters purchase requisitions, expense reports, spend authorizations, and procurement card transactions into Workday. \u2022 Retrieves Workday reports and balances for various accounts and funds managed by staff chair and agents. \u2022 Accepts invoices and bills for office utilities and prepares affidavits to send to county judge\u2019s office for payment. Communication: \u2022 Communicates respectfully, professionally, and accurately to internal and external clients. \u2022 Receives, greets, and directs visitors to appropriate office/agent. \u2022 Answers telephone promptly using prescribed telephone etiquette and greeting and directs calls to appropriate agent. \u2022 Takes accurate messages for staff. \u2022 Responds to inquiries and requests for information. \u2022 Possess excellent written and verbal communication skills. Teamwork: \u2022 Listens to and respects the ideas of other team members \u2022 Keeps abreast of due dates, clientele requests, and scheduled programs and creates tickler file to remind agents of upcoming deadlines. \u2022 Shares information, expertise, resources and ideas of ways to improve or streamline processes for the benefit of the entire county team/staff. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: The formal education equivalent of a high school diploma, plus three years of experience in a related field applicable to the work performed, is required.\u00a0 Completion of an associate degree may substitute for two years of the required experience. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities: Knowledge of the principles and practices of mathematics and statistics. Knowledge of research and analysis techniques and methods. Knowledge of work-related subject area. Knowledge of computers and software applications. Ability to prepare, present, and review oral and written information and reports. Ability to research and analyze related work program information. Ability to develop, recommend, interpret, and apply policies and procedures. Ability to analyze financial records and prepare reports. Ability to plan, organize, and direct the work of others. Additional Information: Applicants for this position are required to upload a Resume, Cover letter, and a list of three (3) references including name, phone number and email address (if available) prior to submitting the application. Once an application is submitted, the applicant will not be able to edit the application or upload additional documents. If you have technical issues uploading a document or if you have a need to provide additional documentation after submitting your application, email humanresources@uada.edu Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: JoAnn Vann, County Extension Agent - Staff Chair, 870-352-3505, jvann@uada.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Motor Vehicle Reports Check The University of Arkansas System Division of Agriculture may conduct pre-employment background checks on certain positions for applicants being considered for employment. \u00a0 The background checks may include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. \u00a0 Required checks are identified in the position listing. \u00a0 A criminal background check or arrest pending adjudication information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absences of a relationship to the requirements of the position. \u00a0 Background check information will be used in a consistent, non-discriminatory manner consistent with the state and federal law. \u00a0 The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Sitting, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Feeling, Grasping, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Reaching, Repetitive Motion Occasional Physical Activity: Driving, Lifting, N/A, Standing Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Benton/Instrument-Technician---UAMS-Health-Benton-Bryant_R0090917-1": {"title": "Instrument Technician \u2013 UAMS Health Benton/Bryant", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/15/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Shift Vary (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: INA | Institutional Admin Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Instrument Tech will be responsible for decontamination, assembling and inspecting, packaging, testing and sterilizing instruments and/or sets. Maintain records of loads and items being removed from department for processing, transports loads to and from SSD and prepare proper storage for equipment. Performs routine testing including biological test for steam autoclaves, Sterrad and System 1E. Assist Operating Room (OR) staff with needed supplies and equipment at the UAMS Health Benton/Bryant location. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: High School Diploma/GED. \u200b Preferred Qualifications: Certified Instrument Tech. Work experience as an Instrument Tech. Experience fulfilling orders/requests (packing, assembling & stocking items). Additional Information: Responsibilities: Decontaminate (dis-assemble, clean by hand and/or machine) medical instruments/materials. Assemble and package, inspect and test instruments, re-assemble sets, place sets in proper containers and/or wrapping and load/transport loaded carts with prepared sets. Maintain record of loads and items being removed from department for processing. Transport loads to and from CSS and prepare proper storage of instruments and equipment. Use and test sterilizing equipment; perform dart and biological tests for autoclaves; perform diagnostic and biological tests for Steris sterilizer. Record and accurately interpret results of tests; assist OR staff; help locate needed supplies and equipment. Communicate professionally even when under pressure/fulfilling demanding and/or stressful requests. Position revolves around serving the Operating Room's (OR\u2019s) sterile instrument and equipment needs. Must understand the URGENCY of the OR staff\u2019s requests. Answer directly to the Sterile Processing Supervisor. Other related duties as assigned. Physical Requirements: Constant Physical Activity: Hear, Read, Concentrate, Think Analytically, Frequent Physical Activity: Stand Occasional Physical Activity: Bend, sit, crawl, crouch, kneel, stoop or reach overhead Lift/Carry Weight:\u00a011 - 25 Lbs. or more Push/Pull Weight:\u00a0100 Lbs. or more Physical Environment: Inside medical Facility Noise Level:\u00a0Moderate Visual Requirements:\u00a0Color discrimination, Depth perception, Far visual acuity Near visual acuity Hazards: Biological, Dust, Fumes/Gases/Odors, Radiation, Sharp objects/tools Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Benton/Cardiovascular-Technologist---UAMS-Health-Benton-Bryant_R0090916-1": {"title": "Cardiovascular Technologist \u2013 UAMS Health Benton/Bryant", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/15/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Shift Vary (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: INA | Institutional Admin Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Cardiovascular Cath Lab, Structural and Electrophysiology Lab Technologist works under supervision and reads/interprets health record documentation to identify all diagnoses and procedures that affect the outpatient encounter visit. This position will also be responsible for producing Cath Lab images for medical interpretation but will not supervise other Cath Lab technologists. This position is located at the UAMS Health Benton/Bryant location. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Graduate from a 2-year certificate program certified by the ASRT in Radiology Technology Registered by the American Registry of Radiologic Technologists Licensed by the State of Arkansas in Radiology Technology Preferred Qualifications: Baccalaureate Degree One or more years of experience Cath Lab Advanced Certification by the American Registry of Radiologic Technologists Additional Information: Responsibilities: Prepares patients for procedures by reviewing medical history, draping and positioning the patient, preparing procedural/testing sites, and administering contrast media and/or medications within scope of practice. Assists physician with performing diagnostic and therapeutic vascular interventional procedures. Performs related imaging procedures. Analyzes results and takes appropriate action to resolve image quality issues. Educates patient regarding procedures, equipment, and exam to ensure patient's understanding and cooperation. Assists with monitoring patient condition continually and reports/responds to changes in status as appropriate. Prepares equipment and supplies. Implements safety standards and performs appropriate quality control procedures on equipment. Troubleshoots, resolves, and/or reports equipment malfunctions as necessary. Other duties may be assigned to this position. Physical Requirements : Medium Work | Exerting up to 50 pounds of force occasionally, and/or up to 30 pounds of force frequently, and/or up to 10 pounds of force constantly to move objects. The Employee is required to have visual acuity to determine the accuracy, neatness, and thoroughness of the work assigned (i.e., custodial, general laborer, lab personnel, etc.) or to make general observations of facilities or structures (i.e., security guard). The Employee is subject to hazards. Includes a variety of physical conditions, such as proximity to moving mechanical parts or vehicles, electrical current, working in high places, exposure to chemicals, biological, radiological or hazardous materials. Constant Activities: Feeling; Hearing; Standing; Talking Frequent Activities: Grasping; Sharps; Sitting; Walking Occasional Activities: Lifting; Pulling; Pushing; Reaching Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Benton/Registered-Respiratory-Therapist---UAMS-Health-Benton-Bryant_R0090915-1": {"title": "Registered Respiratory Therapist \u2013 UAMS Health Benton/Bryant", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/15/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Shift Vary (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: INA | Institutional Admin Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Registered Respiratory Therapist (RRT) works under physician direction and under the supervision of the Respiratory Care Clinical Team Manager. They are a professional who works within the limits of their license and credentials adhering to institutional and departmental policies, procedures and standards. The Registered Respiratory Therapist is required to provide quality patient care, promote a healthy work environment, and project a positive image for the UAMS Health Benton/Bryant location. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: High School diploma/GED plus two (2) years of direct respiratory care experience OR an associate\u2019s degree. Applicant must be a Registered Respiratory Therapist (RRT) by hire date. Applicant must hold a current Arkansas Licensed Respiratory Care Practitioner (LRCP) by hire date. Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor\u2019s degree in respiratory care. One or more of the following: ACCS, NPS, ACLS Additional Information: Responsibilities: Performs routine respiratory care procedures including, but not limited to: updrafts, metered dose inhalers (MDI), chest physiotherapy (CPT), arterial blood gases (ABG), incentive spirometry, intrapulmonary percussive ventilation (IPV), patient education, mechanical ventilator setup and management. Assists in codes and rapid responses. Calls for, or physically moves, equipment and medical supplies needed into the assigned work areas. Enters patient treatment notes in e-chart system and/or places documentation in patient charts. May perform other duties as assigned. Employees in this role must be fitted for, capable of donning and performing routine tasks in personal protective equipment to include N95 masks, Powered Air Purifying Respirators (PAPR) or Controlled Air Purifying Respirators (CAPR). Physical Requirements: Heavy Work | Exerting up to 100 pounds of force occasionally, and/or up to 50 pounds of force frequently, and/or up to 20 pounds of force constantly to move objects. The Employee is required to have close visual acuity to perform an activity such as: preparing and analyzing data and figures; transcribing; viewing a computer terminal; extensive reading; and/or visual inspection at distances close to the eyes. The Employee is subject to inside environmental conditions. Protection from weather conditions but not necessarily from temperature changes. Constant Activities: Hearing Frequent Activities: Feeling; Grasping; Lifting; Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding; Pulling; Pushing; Sharps; Standing; Talking; Walking Occasional Activities: Crawling; Crouching; Kneeling; Reaching; Sitting; Stooping Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Benton/Medical-Laboratory-Scientist--MLS--I--II----III---UAMS-Health-Benton-Bryant_R0090914-1": {"title": "Medical Laboratory Scientist (MLS) I, II, & III \u2013 UAMS Health Benton/Bryant", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/15/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Shift Vary (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: INA | Institutional Admin Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The MLS I is responsible for processing, evaluating and performing tests to identify microorganisms or antigens according to written procedures and performs susceptibilities. This person will also record and evaluate daily, weekly, and monthly QC in their assigned areas for further review by the supervisor. This position requires one to maintain safe work practices, follow all regulatory requirements and engage supervisor, manager, or director as appropriate. The MLS II performs a variety of technical procedures including HLA typing by rSSO and next generation sequencing methods, Luminex based HLA Antibody identification, and donor/recipient flow cytometric cross-matching. They are expected to keep all instrumentation in good working order and identify and notify the supervisor or lead tech of instrument malfunctions. The MLS II fulfills all the responsibilities and tasks of a MLS I as well as performing quality assurance metric studies, and training/competency assessments. The MLS III performs complex medical laboratory tests and procedures in a clinical laboratory setting. Analyzes and interprets results, troubleshoots issues, and ensures accuracy and quality control. Provides guidance and training to less experienced staff, assists in developing new laboratory protocols, and may participate in research projects. The MLS III fulfills all the responsibilities and tasks of a MLS I & II as well as performing quality assurance metric studies, and training/competency assessments. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: MLS I Bachelor\u2019s Degree in Medical Technology or Medical Laboratory Sciences OR an approved ASCP discipline (30 semester hours in biology and chemistry, which may be obtained within, or in addition to, the Bachelor's). ASCP or another accrediting agency certified or eligible (Certification must be obtained within one year of employment). MLS II Bachelor's degree in a chemistry, biology, or medical laboratory science 2 years of experience in a clinical laboratory CHT (ABHI) certification within 1 year of eligibility. If eligible at time of hire then within 1 year of hire date. Must be able to identify and report abnormal test results as well as communicate and interact with reviewing Pathologists and submitting clinicians. Must be able to work independently, multi-task, and make subjective decisions. Must be able to communicate effectively both orally and in writing. MLS III Bachelor of Science in Medical Technology (BSMT) / Medical Laboratory Scientist (BSMLS) or Bachelor of Science or higher degree, including sufficient biology and chemistry course credits in an ASCP approved discipline 3 years of clinical laboratory experience. ASCP or equivalent certification as a Medical Laboratory Scientist/Medical Technologist or have been grandfathered in before ASCP requirement. All staff, including BS/BA employees, must have Cytogenetics (ASCP), certification within 24 months of hire. MLS III Preferred Qualifications: BSMT or BSMLS degree or degree in Cytogenetics 5 years of Cytogenetics experience Previous MLS(ASCP) certification and/or related specialty such as MB(ASCP), in addition to required CG(ASCP) Evidence of excellent knowledge of clinical laboratory quality control practices such as having previous experience as a CAP inspector. Additional Information: Responsibilities: MLS I Conducts inventory counts on assigned areas, restocks supplies as needed, reports supplies to be ordered, and stores received supplies per storage requirements and regulations. Interacts with staff from various departments to coordinate the proper acquisition, testing, and reporting of patient test results. Performs function checks on analyzers, lab equipment and automation equipment. Completes machine maintenance, calibrations, and troubleshoots problems as required. Works with service representatives as needed to facilitate instrument repairs. Perform other duties as needed. MLS II Assists Medical Director and supervisor with analyzing and implementing new tests. Performs additional studies as required for quality assurance initiatives, research support or verification/validation of new equipment or methods. Completes validation and verification of new instrumentation and testing. Ensures the accuracy of instrument calibration and that preventative maintenance is performed. Leads training for new employees, students, and residents and performs employee competencies as assigned. Serves as a resource to assist other technologists in the Microbiology Laboratory. Maintains all aspects of quality control and quality assurance, assesses for acceptability, and takes corrective action as required. Performs testing of patient samples, interprets, reviews, and prepares patient test results for review by the Supervisor and/or Medical Director. Interacts with staff from various departments to coordinate the proper acquisition, testing, and reporting of patient test results. Performs other duties as assigned. MLS III Oversees daily operations in area of responsibility, ensuring adequate staff of demonstrated competency is available to meet the workload. Adjusts staff and testing priorities as required. Supervises and provides general oversight to staff. Contributes to the development of job descriptions, screens and interviews potential hires, trains staff, and engages in ongoing disciplinary actions as needed. Implements projects, establishes schedules, and assigns staff as needed to meet project requirements as it relates to quality initiatives, research, or validation studies. Adheres to department budget goals by overseeing the purchasing of supplies, ensuring adequate inventory is on hand to meet operational needs. Oversees compliance with regulatory requirements of accrediting agencies such as the College of American Pathologists (CAP), Joint Commission on Accreditation of Healthcare Organizations (JCAHO), Food and Drug Administration (FDA), and Clinical Laboratory Improvement Amendments (CLIA). Participates in CAP inspections both as a direct contact for inspections and as an inspector for other facilities. Completes required testing on the bench including maintenance, quality control, and function checks as needed. Performs other duties as assigned. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS: Stand: Frequently Sit: Frequently Walk: Occasionally Bend, crawl, crouch, kneel, stoop or reach overhead: Frequently Lift and carry weight: 25 lbs Push and pull weight: 25 lbs Use hands to touch, handle or feel: Frequently Talk: Continuously Hear: Continuously Taste or smell: Occasionally Read, concentrate, think analytically: Continuously Physical Environment : Inside Medical Facility Environment Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Benton/Patient-Services-Associate---UAMS-Health-Benton-Bryant_R0090913-1": {"title": "Patient Services Associate \u2013 UAMS Health Benton/Bryant", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/15/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Shift Vary (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: INA | Institutional Admin Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: As a Patient Services Associate (PSA) at the UAMS Health Benton/Bryant location, the primary responsibilities include providing front desk support by greeting patients, checking them in and out, verifying insurance and demographic information, and collecting co-pays. The PSA schedules and manages appointments, answers phone calls, and communicates with patients and clinical staff to ensure efficient coordination of care. The PSA assists in maintaining accurate medical records, preparing patient charts, and supporting the overall flow of the clinic. This role requires strong customer service skills, attention to detail, and the ability to work compassionately with patients experiencing high-risk pregnancies, all while adhering to HIPAA and UAMS policies. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: High School Diploma or GED. One (1) year of Patient Care experience in a health care setting. Excellent communication skills, basic computer skills, strong work ethics and accountability. Successful completion of patient care technician course is required within 3 months of employment. Preferred Qualifications: Experience in an acute care setting.\u200b Healthcare/Patient Care experience. CPR Certified/Licensed Additional Information: Responsibilities: Assists patients with direct patient care. Accepts directions from RN and team members and follows through on delegated patient care activities. Provides appropriate grooming/oral hygiene and comfort measures and assists patients with mobility-related activities. Accurately and promptly documents all patient care tasks, vital signs, ADL, wave tests, and I & O's per unit and department standards.\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Obtains patient report and communicates with RN regarding patient care. Informs nurses of patient requests or complaints. Carries out Plan of Care for patient using a Multidisciplinary Approach delegated by Team Leader. Communicates effectively with other team members to facilitate patient care. Assists patients and visitors with information and/or solutions to problems. Serves as a resource to support department member in performance of duties. Notifies appropriate staff of problems requiring prompt intervention. Assists with admission, transfer, and discharge of patients. Transports patients to other areas of the hospital as directed. Performs other duties as assigned. Physical Requirements: Medium Work | Exerting up to 50 pounds of force occasionally, and/or up to 30 pounds of force frequently, and/or up to 10 pounds of force constantly to move objects. The Employee is required to have close visual acuity to perform an activity such as: preparing and analyzing data and figures; transcribing; viewing a computer terminal; extensive reading; and/or visual inspection at distances close to the eyes. The Employee is subject to inside environmental conditions. Protection from weather conditions but not necessarily from temperature changes. Constant Activities: Hearing; Standing; Walking Frequent Activities: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding; Sitting; Talking Occasional Activities: Kneeling; Lifting; Pulling; Pushing Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Benton/Patient-Care-Technician--PCT----UAMS-Health-Benton-Bryant_R0090912-2": {"title": "Patient Care Technician (PCT) \u2013 UAMS Health Benton/Bryant", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/15/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Shift Vary (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: INA | Institutional Admin Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Patient Care Technician (PCT) works under the direct supervision of the Registered Nurse(s) and performs tasks and duties which do not require a license, professional judgment or intervention. The PCT is a trained member of the unit-based team who supports the on-going delivery of care as identified by the multidisciplinary patient management team at the UAMS Health Benton/Bryant location. The PCT must pass the required competencies. The PCT works within the Department of Nursing Standards. The PCT adheres to UAMS clinical programs, policies, procedures and standards and guest care guidelines. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications:\u00a0 High School Diploma/GED Successful completion of patient care technician course within 3 months of hire.\u00a0 Must have excellent communication skills, ability to follow oral instructions, basic computer skills, strong work ethics and accountability. Must be able to lift 100 lbs. to waist height. \u00a0 Preferred Qualifications: Certification as a nursing assistant or military corpsman, One (1) year of previous Patient Care Technician experience CNA experience in acute care setting. Additional Information: Responsibilities: Obtains patient report and has on-going communication with R.N. regarding patient care/changes in condition; Informs nurse of patient requests or complaints. Assists with admission, transfer, and discharge of patients. Transports patients to other areas of the hospital as directed. Carries out the Plan of Care for Patient using a Multidisciplinary Approach as Delegated by Team Leader. Communicates effectively with other team members to facilitate patient care. Accepts directions from R.N.s and team members. Follows through on delegated patient care activities. Provides appropriate grooming/oral hygiene and comfort measures and assists patients with activities (ambulation, up in chair, turn and reposition). Documents all patient care activities/tasks, vital signs, ADL, wave tests, I&O's accurately and timely and per unit and department standards. Assists patients and visitors with information and/or solutions to problems. Serves as resources person to support department members in performance of duties. Notifies appropriate staff members of problems requiring prompt intervention. May perform other duties as assigned. Physical Requirements: Employees in this role must be fitted for, capable of donning and performing routine tasks in personal protective equipment to include N95 masks, Powered Air Purifying Respirators (PAPR) or Controlled Air Purifying Respirators (CAPR). Constant Physical Activity: Hear, Read, Concentrate, Think Analytically, Frequent Physical Activity: Stand, Walk, Talk, Use hands to touch, handle or feel, Occasional Physical Activity: Sit, Bend, crawl, crouch, kneel, stoop, reach overhead, Taste or Smell, Lift/Carry Weight: 100 Lbs. or more Push/Pull Weight: 100 Lbs. or more Physical Environment: Inside medical Facility Noise Level: Moderate Visual Requirements: Near Visual Acuity, Far Visual Acuity, Color Discrimination, Depth Perception, Peripheral Vision Hazards: Biological, Chemical, Electrical, Radiation, Sharp Objects/Tools, Dust Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Benton/Lab-Support-Technician--LST--II---UAMS-Health-Benton-Bryant_R0090911-1": {"title": "Lab Support Technician (LST) II \u2013 UAMS Health Benton/Bryant", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/15/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Shift Vary (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: INA | Institutional Admin Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Lab Support Technician II will be expected to perform clerical duties including, but not limited to, triaging phone calls, triaging specimens, assigning identification numbers to specimens along with patient name and specimen type, reviewing, verifying, and logging all incoming consultation cases from outside facilities into the UAMS system, and verifying patient status, insurance coverage and proper authorizations prior to services. The LST II is responsible for collecting patient information and data within regulations as well as guaranteeing patient identification throughout every process. The LST II is located at the UAMS Health Benton/Bryant location and works to support other staff members and the department as needed. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: High School diploma or GED equivalent. Two (2) years of experience as a Lab Tech or Assistant in a Clinical Laboratory or 60 hours of completed higher education in a health sciences program. Additional Information: Responsibilities: Accessioning specimen outreach and Surgical Pathology. Verifying correct insurance for each patient. Clerical work for Gross Department. Triage all calls made to gross lab. Customer service: Assist clinics looking for results. Correcting incorrect patient information. Fulfilling any requests outside clinics may need, i.e. supplies, requisitions, etc. Maintaining a clean and organized area. Other duties as assigned. Physical Requirements : Light Work | Exerting up to 20 pounds of force occasionally, and/or up to 10 pounds of force frequently, and/or a negligible amount of force constantly to move objects. If the use of force is greater than that for sedentary work and the worker sits most of the time, the job is rated for light work. The Employee is required to have close visual acuity to perform an activity such as: preparing and analyzing data and figures; transcribing; viewing a computer terminal; extensive reading; and/or visual inspection at distances close to the eyes. The Employee is required to have visual acuity to determine the accuracy, neatness, and thoroughness of the work assigned (i.e., custodial, general laborer, lab personnel, etc.) or to make general observations of facilities or structures (i.e., security guard). The Employee is not substantially exposed to adverse environmental conditions (such as in typical office or administrative work). The Employee is subject to hazards. Includes a variety of physical conditions, such as proximity to moving mechanical parts or vehicles, electrical current, working in high places, exposure to chemicals, biological, radiological or hazardous materials. Constant Activities : N/A Frequent Activities : Hearing; Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding; Sitting; Talking Occasional Activities : Kneeling; Lifting; Pulling; Pushing; Reaching; Stooping; Walking Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Benton/Diagnostic-Radiology-Technologist---UAMS-Health-Benton-Bryant_R0090908-1": {"title": "Diagnostic Radiology Technologist \u2013 UAMS Health Benton/Bryant", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/15/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Shift Vary (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: INA | Institutional Admin Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Diagnostic Radiology Technologist at the UAMS Health Benton/Bryant location is responsible for producing high-quality radiographic images for medical interpretation and assisting in patient examinations and treatments as needed. This role operates under the supervision of the manager and involves interpreting health record documentation to identify diagnoses and procedures affecting outpatient visits. The position does not include supervisory responsibilities over other diagnostic radiology technologists. Be a part of a team that is shaping the future of healthcare in Arkansas. If you are passionate about diagnostic imaging and providing exceptional patient care, we encourage you to apply today! Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications : High School Diploma; completion of a two-year certification program or an associate degree that is accredited by the ASRT in Radiology Technology. Three (3) years or more of experience working as a Radiology Technologist preferred. Registered with the American Registry of Radiologic Technologist and Licensed by the State of Arkansas in Radiology Technology. Knowledge, Skills, & Abilities : Strong knowledge of radiographic imaging techniques and patient care protocols. Ability to work collaboratively in a multidisciplinary healthcare environment. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills to ensure patient-centered care. Ability to read, write, and follow oral instructions. Knowledge of all required supplies and equipment necessary for each procedure. Knowledge of the Anatomy of vessels and organs in the body (for proper positioning). Additional Information: Responsibilities : Operate radiographic equipment to produce diagnostic-quality images. Assist in patient examinations and treatments as required. Review and interpret health record documentation to ensure accurate identification of diagnoses and procedures. Adhere to UAMS policies, including Core Concepts of Patient and Family Centered Care, which emphasize dignity, respect, information sharing, participation, and collaboration. May perform other duties as assigned. Physical Requirements: Sedentary Work | Exerting up to 10 pounds of force occasionally and/or negligible amount of force frequently or constantly. Sedentary work involves sitting most of the time. Employee is required to have close visual acuity to perform an activity such as: preparing and analyzing data and figures; transcribing; viewing a computer terminal; extensive reading; and/or visual inspection at distances close to the eyes. The employee is not substantially exposed to adverse environmental conditions (such as in typical office or administrative work). Constant Activities : Feeling; Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding; Pulling; Pushing Frequent Activities : Hearing; Lifting; Reaching; Repetitive Motion; Sitting; Standing; Talking; Walking Occasional Activities : Balancing; Crouching Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Fayetteville-AR/Coordinator-of-Recruitment--Outreach--and-Summer-Programs_R0090569-1": {"title": "Coordinator of Recruitment, Outreach, and Summer Programs", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com, then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at all University of Arkansas institutions will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students.\u201d University of Arkansas, Fayetteville students will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Student Jobs at UAF.\u201d All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. Closing Date: 09/08/2026 Type of Position: Recruitment and Admissions Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas, Fayetteville Founded in 1871, the University of Arkansas is a land grant institution, classified by the Carnegie Foundation among the nation\u2019s top 2 percent of universities with the highest level of research activity. The University of Arkansas works to advance the state and build a better world through education, research, and outreach by providing transformational opportunities and skills, fostering a welcoming climate, and nurturing creativity, discovery, and the spread of new ideas and innovations. The University of Arkansas campus is located in Fayetteville, a welcoming community ranked as one of the best places to live in the U.S. The growing region surrounding Fayetteville is home to numerous Fortune 500 companies and one of the nation\u2019s strongest economies. Northwest Arkansas is also quickly gaining a national reputation for its focus on the arts and overall quality of life. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10% of employee salary. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions, you should review before applying for the opening. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process, please submit a request via the Disability Accommodations | OEOC | University of Arkansas (uark.edu) : Request an Accommodation. Appli\u00adcants are required to submit a request for each position of which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 479.575.5351. Department: College of Engineering Assistant Director of Recruitment, Outreach, and Summer Programs Department's Website: https://engineering.uark.edu/ Summary of Job Duties: Under the supervision of the Associate Director of Enrollment Management, the Coordinator of Recruitment, Outreach, and Summer Programs coordinates and implements initiatives that introduce prospective students and community partners to the College of Engineering. The position organizes recruitment events and communications, supports engineering outreach assists in [BH1.1]the operational planning and delivery of summer programs, and recruits, trains, and coordinates [BH2.1]student staff who represent the College. The coordinator serves as a visible representative of the College and works closely with University admissions personnel, faculty and department leaders, school counselors, community partners, prospective students, families, and student employees. The role requires responsive communication, detailed event and program management, and the flexibility to travel and work outside regular business hours when programs and recruitment activities require it. Regular, reliable and non-disruptive attendance is an essential job duty, as is the ability to create and maintain collegial, harmonious working relationships with others. This position requires travel in order to develop and maintain partner relationships and execute programs and events. Workload will shift during peak recruitment, outreach, and summer-program periods. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor\u2019s degree from an accredited institution of higher education Experience in student recruitment, outreach, or summer camps Valid driver\u2019s license Applicable equivalencies may be considered on the above qualifications. Preferred Qualifications: At least one year of experience in higher education, event planning, program development and implementation, or a related field Experience working with STEM students or programs Experience supervising, training, or mentoring student employees or seasonal staff Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Excellent written and oral communication skills Proficient skills with the Microsoft Office suite Strong organizational and interpersonal skills Strong communication skills: written, verbal, listening, public speaking and presentation skills Excellent organizational skills Ability to work alone and in a team setting Ability to analyze financial records and prepare reports Additional Information: This position is renewable annually based on continued need for the position, availability of funding, and satisfactory job performance. Salary Information: $46,383.00 Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Recruitment Contact Information: Teresa Simpson, Associate Director for Enrollment Management, tksimpso@uark.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Special Instructions to Applicants: Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Motor Vehicle Reports Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas seeks to attract, develop and retain high quality faculty, staff and administrators that consistently display practices and behaviors to advance a culture that embeds equal opportunity, educational excellence and unparalleled access for all. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All Application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-Arkansas-Community-College-at-Batesville/Faculty-Nursing_R0090863": {"title": "Faculty-Nursing", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. Closing Date: Type of Position: Faculty - Non-Tenure Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas Community College at Batesville The University of Arkansas Community College at Batesville (UACCB) is a comprehensive community college committed to providing learning experiences that improve the lives of those we serve. UACCB provides affordable access to technical education and college transfer programs that meet the diverse higher education needs of the citizens of north central Arkansas. \u00a0 These programs are provided to the traditional college student as well as to high school students through a state approved Secondary Area Career Center. \u00a0 The College also promotes economic development and an enhanced quality of life for the community through adult education, developmental education, customized business and industry training, and continuing education programs. UACCB's mission is to provide quality educational opportunities within a supportive learning environment. We promote success through community partnerships, responsive programs, and an enduring commitment to improvement. Thank you for your interest. \u00a0 We hope you will be joining us soon! After reviewing the Job Duties and Qualifications listed below, click the Apply button at the top of the page to begin the application process. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process or for general application assistance, please contact the Human Resource Office at (870) 612-2045. Department: Director of Nursing Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Basic Functions The 12-Month Nursing Faculty member provides instruction, supervision, and academic support to nursing students in theory, lab, and clinical settings. This position is responsible for curriculum delivery, student evaluation, advising, and participation in program development to ensure high-quality, student-centered nursing education.\u202f Caring Campus Responsibilities: As a member of the UACCB community, each employee is responsible for advancing the Caring Campus culture to enhance student connection and success and to embody the campus purpose: Improve Lives. Key duties include adhering to the campus name badge policy, treating all visitors as guests, engaging with the campus community by reviewing institutional communications, participating in campus events, and supporting a collaborative, positive workplace environment. Position Duties 75% \u2013 Classroom and Laboratory Instruction and Student Learning Provide instruction in both online and traditional tracks, including theory, lab, and clinical components. Create and maintain a student-centered learning environment that promotes critical thinking, professional behavior, and achievement of course and program learning outcomes. Post weekly coursework and learning materials prior to the scheduled content week, complete required clinical hours, and ensure timely grading and feedback for theory and practicum courses. Teaching duties in both online and traditional tracks. Creating an intellectual environment that promotes critical thinking. Ensuring student-centered learning. Posting weekly coursework and learning materials prior to the scheduled content week. Completing all grading in a timely manner for theory and practicum courses. Completing required clinical hours. Being on time for all courses. Maintaining professionalism inside and outside of the classroom. 20% \u2013 Curriculum Development and Program Effectiveness Plan, implement, and evaluate curriculum; participate in the development and revision of the nursing program philosophy, organizational framework, policies, and procedures; and assist with maintaining appropriate clinical and laboratory learning environments, including skills check-offs. Collaborate with faculty to ensure curriculum alignment and instructional consistency. Planning, implementing, and evaluating curricula. Participating in the development and revision, as deemed necessary, of the philosophy and organizational framework for the nursing program. Collaborating in the development and revision, as deemed necessary, of nursing program policies and procedures. Selecting and maintaining appropriate clinical learning environments, including laboratory experiences and skills check-offs. Keeping equipment and instructional resources up to date. 15% \u2013 Student Retention and Recruitment Directs efforts toward nursing student success by implementing retention strategies designed to identify, support, and intervene with students at risk of withdrawal or academic difficulty. The instructor provides academic advising and counseling to support student progression through the nursing program and maintains regular office hours to ensure consistent access for guidance and early intervention. This position also actively participates in recruitment and outreach activities to promote the nursing programs within the community, healthcare facilities, and local high schools. Providing academic advising, counseling, and program guidance to nursing students Assuming responsibility for student recruitment, academic counseling, and program advising Assisting with recruitment and retention efforts to support enrollment and student success Maintaining accurate and confidential student records in accordance with program and institutional policies Supporting student progression and retention throughout the nursing program 5% \u2013 Institutional Service and Industry Collaboration Participate in faculty meetings, committee assignments, and shared governance activities; collaborate as part of a team-based faculty approach; assist with budgeting processes and renewal of clinical affiliation agreements as assigned; and support departmental and college initiatives. Perform other duties as assigned. Participating in faculty meetings, including monthly faculty meetings. Participating in faculty and committee assignments. Being part of a team-based faculty approach to teaching. Assisting with the budgeting process. Assisting with renewal of clinical affiliation agreements. 5% \u2013 Professional Practice and Development Maintain current knowledge of nursing practice and nursing education, participate in professional development activities, demonstrate and encourage high standards of professional nursing practice, and model professionalism in all academic and clinical settings. Remaining current with trends in nursing education and nursing practice. Maintaining expertise through participation in professional development. Demonstrating and encouraging high standards of professional nursing practice. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Knowledge Principles and practices of clinical nursing education within a community college setting. Arkansas State Board of Nursing (ASBN) Rules and Regulations, including ASBN Rule Part 125 \u2013 Standards for Nursing Education Programs (formerly Chapter 6), as they relate to nursing program approval, faculty roles, and clinical instruction. Federal, state, and institutional policies affecting nursing education and clinical supervision (e.g., FERPA, ADA/Section 504). Strategies to support student learning, clinical skill development, and successful progression in nursing programs. Use of approved evaluation tools, documentation, and performance data to assess student learning and clinical outcomes. Current clinical practices, evidence-based nursing care, and technologies utilized in healthcare and clinical education settings. Use of institutional research, data analysis, and performance metrics for planning and evaluation. Current technologies supporting teaching, learning, and academic operations. Skills Effective classroom, laboratory, and clinical instruction that supports student learning and achievement of course and program outcomes. Strong oral, written, and interpersonal communication skills to interact professionally with students, faculty, clinical staff, and administrators. Ability to provide timely, constructive feedback, manage student concerns, and promote professional behavior, accountability, and academic integrity. Demonstrated proficiency in the use of Microsoft Office applications, including Outlook, Word, Excel, and PowerPoint, for effective communication, documentation, data tracking, reporting, and instructional support. Ability to use technology efficiently to manage schedules, maintain accurate records, analyze data, and communicate professionally with students, faculty, and administrative staff. Abilities Teach, supervise, and evaluate students in theory, lab, and clinical settings while maintaining patient safety and adherence to scope of practice Collaborate effectively with faculty and clinical partners as part of a team-based approach to nursing education. Adapt instructional strategies to diverse learning environments, delivery modalities (online and traditional), and evolving program or regulatory requirements. Qualifications: Qualifications \u00a0 Bachelor of Science in Nursing\u202f\u202f \u00a0 Have an unencumbered Registered Nursing license with\u202fprivilege to practice in Arkansas\u202f \u00a0 Have a minimum of two years of clinical healthcare experience\u202f \u00a0 \u00a0 Preferred Qualifications \u00a0 Master\u2019s\u202fof Science\u202fin Nursing\u202f\u202f \u00a0 Nurse educator experience\u202f\u202f \u00a0 Higher education experience\u202f\u202f \u00a0 \u00a0 Additional Information: Salary Information: $56,000-$58,000 Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume, Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Human Resources hr@uaccb.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Motor Vehicle Reports Check, Sex Offender Registry, Substance Abuse Testing UACCB is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check for all applicants.\u00a0 Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Repetitive Motion Frequent Physical Activity: Feeling, Grasping, Kneeling, Lifting, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Sharps, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Stooping Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Fayetteville-AR/Postdoctoral-Researcher_R0090639-2": {"title": "Postdoctoral Researcher", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com, then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at all University of Arkansas institutions will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students.\u201d University of Arkansas, Fayetteville students will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Student Jobs at UAF.\u201d All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. Closing Date: 09/08/2026 Type of Position: Researchers and Scientists Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Fixed Duration of Project/Grant (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas, Fayetteville Founded in 1871, the University of Arkansas is a land grant institution, classified by the Carnegie Foundation among the nation\u2019s top 2 percent of universities with the highest level of research activity. The University of Arkansas works to advance the state and build a better world through education, research, and outreach by providing transformational opportunities and skills, fostering a welcoming climate, and nurturing creativity, discovery, and the spread of new ideas and innovations. The University of Arkansas campus is located in Fayetteville, a welcoming community ranked as one of the best places to live in the U.S. The growing region surrounding Fayetteville is home to numerous Fortune 500 companies and one of the nation\u2019s strongest economies. Northwest Arkansas is also quickly gaining a national reputation for its focus on the arts and overall quality of life. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10% of employee salary. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions, you should review before applying for the opening. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process, please submit a request via the Disability Accommodations | OEOC | University of Arkansas (uark.edu) : Request an Accommodation. Appli\u00adcants are required to submit a request for each position of which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 479.575.5351. Department: Post Docs, GAs and Hourly Employees Department's Website: https://engineering.uark.edu/ Summary of Job Duties: As a member of a multidisciplinary research team, the Postdoctoral Researcher will conduct research to advance novel machine learning and data harmonization approaches for water quality monitoring and assessment. Responsibilities include developing and validating computational methods to standardize and infer nutrient and sediment observations from existing datasets; evaluating impacts of expanded datasets on watershed-scale assessments; developing and maintaining open-source software tools and R packages; disseminating findings through publications and presentations; and collaborating with university and federal partners to improve national water quality science and decision support. Regular, reliable, and non-disruptive attendance is an essential job duty, as is the ability to create and maintain collegial, harmonious working relationships with others. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Ph.D. in Biological Engineering, Agricultural Engineering, Environmental Engineering, Civil Engineering, Environmental Science, Hydrology, Data Science, Computer Science, Statistics, Geography, Water Resources, or a closely related field from an accredited institution of higher education Preferred Qualifications: Experience applying machine learning or artificial intelligence methods to environmental, hydrologic, or water quality datasets Strong computational background in statistical modeling, reproducible workflows, and large-scale data processing Experience with water quality, nutrient, sediment, watershed, or hydrologic datasets Experience developing, maintaining, and documenting open-source software tools or R packages Experience with geospatial analysis, environmental databases, and cloud or high-performance computing workflows Demonstrated record of peer-reviewed publications Experience collaborating with interdisciplinary teams and/or federal agencies (e.g., USGS) Familiarity with version control systems (Git/GitHub) and open science practices Additional Information: This position is renewable annually based on continued need for the position, availability of funding, and satisfactory job performance. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume, Statement of Research Philosophy Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Recruitment Contact Information: Dr. Becca Muenich Associate Professor rlogsdo@uark.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Special Instructions to Applicants: Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas seeks to attract, develop and retain high quality faculty, staff and administrators that consistently display practices and behaviors to advance a culture that embeds equal opportunity, educational excellence and unparalleled access for all. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All Application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAPBDAWSONDawson-Hicks-Hall/Pine-Bluff-Community-Schools-Site-Coordinator_R0090759": {"title": "Pine Bluff Community Schools Site Coordinator", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Education Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff The University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff is an 1890 Land-Grant HBCU with a diverse student population, competitive degree offerings and stellar faculty. For more than 140 years, the University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff has worked to create an environment that inculcates learning, growth and productivity while affording a basic need to its students \u2013 a chance to advance. The 15:1 student to teacher ratio makes it possible to maintain a learning environment with close interaction between students and faculty while challenging curricula encourage our students to seek and fulfill their potential. You can excel in your chosen field of study through a curriculum of \u00a0 Certificate and Associates degree programs,\u00a0 more than thirty\u00a0 Undergraduate programs, Master\u2019s degree programs and a Doctorate program in Aquaculture/Fisheries. You can also develop workplace readiness through internships, co-ops and fellowships in the U.S. and abroad. Out-of-class experiences and student involvement include more than 90 student organizations, an internationally renowned Vesper Choir, Marching Band, Concert Bands, Wind Symphony, nationally recognized debate team, award-winning theater department and accomplished athletic program. Though the main campus is in Pine Bluff, its reach is worldwide. UAPB has an extended campus in North Little Rock and offers as well as online courses. With the addition of the Arkansas Research and Education Optical Network (ARE-ON), students can engage in information exchange with others anywhere in the world. There are also Research and Extension offices in Lonoke, Newport and Lake Village and collaborations with other colleges and universities in the State through the National Science Foundation funded STEM (Science, Technology, Engineering and Mathematics) Academy. As the second oldest land-grant institution in the state of Arkansas, the mission of this No Excuse University remains the same \u2013 to provide a high quality, affordable education with a personal touch. We invite you to Become a Part of the Pride at the University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process and require reasonable accommodations, please contact Human Resources at 870.575.8400 . Department: School of Education Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Essential Duties & Responsibilities **Pillar 1: Integrated Student Supports** \u25cf Coordinate health, mental health, and social services to remove barriers to learning. \u25cf Build and maintain partnerships with community agencies that provide counseling, trauma-informed care, food assistance, housing support, and other critical wraparound services. \u25cf Work with UAMS STARLITE, Jefferson Regional Medical Center, and other providers to expand telehealth, school-based clinics, and wellness programming. \u25cf Ensure services are culturally responsive, accessible, and aligned with student and family needs. \u25cf Collect and track data on service utilization and outcomes to measure impact. **Pillar 2: Expanded Learning Time & Opportunities** \u25cf Coordinate after-school, weekend, and summer learning programs, including enrichment in STEM, literacy, and arts. \u25cf Partner with Boys & Girls Club, UAPB, and local organizations to expand tutoring, mentoring, and youth leadership opportunities. \u25cf Integrate UAPB students into service-learning roles to provide academic support and mentoring. \u25cf Leverage Title I funds and community resources to increase access to expanded learning opportunities. **Pillar 3: Family & Community Engagement** \u25cf Establish and facilitate a School-Based Community Council that includes families, staff, students, and partners. \u25cf Support and assist the Mobile Parent Resource Center, offering Wi-Fi, laptops, books, GED/job readiness tools, and access to community agencies. \u25cf Support family engagement activities such as adult literacy workshops, financial education, and health fairs. \u25cf Build family leadership capacity by ensuring parents and guardians are decision-makers in planning and evaluation. \u25cf Strengthen partnerships with organizations such as 100 Families Jefferson County and United Way to provide holistic family support. **Pillar 4: Collaborative Leadership & Practice** \u25cf Collaborate with principals, teachers, and staff to embed the community schools' model into everyday practice. \u25cf Facilitate professional development for staff and partners on trauma-informed care, family engagement and equity Qualifications: \u25cf Bachelor\u2019s degree required (education, social work, public health, or related field). Master\u2019s preferred. \u25cf At least two (2) years of experience in public schools, youth development, or community engagement. \u25cf Knowledge of community school principles, whole-child strategies, and culturally responsive practices. \u25cf Demonstrated ability to manage multiple projects, build partnerships, and analyze data. \u25cf Strong organizational, interpersonal, and communication skills. Additional Information: Salary Information: $50,000.00 Required Documents to Apply: Curriculum Vitae, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants (Please upload all required documents in the \"Resume\" attachment section of your application to be considered for this position) : Recruitment Contact Information: Sharron Williams, Employment Manager williamssm@uapb.edu 870-575-8403 All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check The University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff may conduct pre-employment background checks on certain positions for applicants being considered for employment. \u00a0 The background checks may include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. \u00a0 Required checks are identified in the position listing. \u00a0 A criminal background check or arrest pending adjudication information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absences of a relationship to the requirements of the position. \u00a0 Background check information will be used in a consistent, non-discriminatory manner consistent with the state and federal law. \u00a0 The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Reaching, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Reaching, Repetitive Motion, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Reaching, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Bentonville/Administrative-Specialist-III_R0090649-1": {"title": "Administrative Specialist III", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Clerical Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: Division of Agriculture of the University of Arkansas The University of Arkansas System Division of Agriculture is a state wide campus, with faculty based on University campuses, at Research and Extension Centers and in every Arkansas county. It consists of the Arkansas Agricultural Experiment Station (AES) and the Arkansas Cooperative Extension Service (CES), and is home to more than 1400 employees.\u00a0 The Division was established in 1959 and is headed by the Vice-President for Agriculture.\u00a0 The Division headquarters is located in Little Rock with the rest of the University of Arkansas System Administration.\u00a0 As an employer, the University of Arkansas System Division of Agriculture offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance.\u00a0 Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process and require reasonable accommodations, please contact the Division's Office of Program & Employment Compliance at compliance@uada.edu . For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-671-2219 or 479-502-9820. Department: CEA * Staff Chair * Benton County Department's Website: uada.edu Summary of Job Duties: The Administrative Specialist\u00a0III\u00a0is responsible for coordinating office activities, researching and preparing special reports, and developing, revising, and recommending administrative policies and procedures as directed by supervisor. Self-Management \u2022 Organizes and prioritizes tasks effectively. \u2022 Deals appropriately with interruptions. \u2022 Uses good judgment and decision-making skills. \u2022 Possess strong organizational skills with the ability to multi-task. \u2022 Follows attendance and leave policies. \u2022 Practices emotional control. \u2022 Exhibits professional behavior and appearance. \u2022 Ability to handle sensitive information in a confidential manner. \u2022 Ability to work without close supervision. Quality and Quantity of Work \u2022 Produces high-quality and error free work. \u2022 Orders and maintains sufficient stock of office supplies for county staff. \u2022 Maintains hard copy and electronic files with ability to efficiently retrieve needed information. \u2022 Weeds files based on file retention policies. \u2022 Maintains civil rights files and documents including meeting attendance logs, County Extension Council membership lists, and committee minutes. \u2022 Processes agricultural samples for mailing. \u2022 Updates calendar with itineraries and scheduled events. \u2022 Submits weekly itineraries to District Office. \u2022 Assists county staff with arrangements for upcoming meetings. \u2022 Maintains accurate mailing lists. \u2022 Enters and Submits agent\u2019s monthly travel claim into Workday program. \u2022 Completes and submits monthly postage and copier report. \u2022 Receives, sorts and distributes incoming mail. \u2022 Processes outgoing mail. \u2022 Checks and responds to email regularly throughout the day. \u2022 Provides administrative support for all agents. \u2022 Assists agents and program assistants in reporting data in program areas of Agriculture and Natural Resources, Family and Consumer Sciences, 4H, and Community and Economic Development. \u2022 Performs other duties as assigned. Technical Expertise \u2022 Uses Workday, the U of A system\u2019s cloud-based program to track expenditures, county depository documentation, procurement, purchases, requisitions, time, travel and other financial management applications. \u2022 Uses software such as Microsoft word, Excel, PowerPoint, and other programs to support Extension educational programs. \u2022 Maintains equipment. \u2022 Maintains inventory control of computers and equipment. \u2022 Attends training to maintain and upgrade skills. \u2022 Performs support work such as word processing, creating spreadsheets, data entry and retrieval, reviews and proofreads forms, data and other information to ensure accuracy and conformance to established procedures and policies. \u2022 Generates reports and records. Financial Recordkeeping \u2022 Keeps record of all revenue and expenses from County depository account. \u2022 Enters purchase requisitions, expense reports, spend authorizations, and procurement card transactions into Workday. \u2022 Retrieves Workday reports and balances for various accounts and funds managed by staff chair and agents. \u2022 Accepts invoices and bills for office utilities and prepares affidavits to send to county judge\u2019s office for payment. Communication \u2022 Communicates respectfully, professionally, and accurately to internal and external clients. \u2022 Receives, greets, and directs visitors to appropriate office/agent. \u2022 Answers telephone promptly using prescribed telephone etiquette and greeting and directs calls to appropriate agent. \u2022 Takes accurate messages for staff. \u2022 Responds to inquiries and requests for information. \u2022 Possess excellent written and verbal communication skills. Teamwork \u2022 Listens to and respects the ideas of other team members \u2022 Keeps abreast of due dates, clientele requests, and scheduled programs and creates tickler file to remind agents of upcoming deadlines. \u2022 Shares information, expertise, resources and ideas of ways to improve or streamline processes for the benefit of the entire county team/staff. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: The formal education equivalent of a high school diploma, plus three years of experience in a related field applicable to the work performed, is required.\u00a0 Completion of an associate degree may substitute for two years of the required experience. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities: Knowledge of the principles and practices of mathematics and statistics. Knowledge of research and analysis techniques and methods. Knowledge of work-related subject area. Knowledge of computers and software applications. Ability to prepare, present, and review oral and written information and reports. Ability to research and analyze related work program information. Ability to develop, recommend, interpret, and apply policies and procedures. Ability to analyze financial records and prepare reports. Ability to plan, organize, and direct the work of others. Additional Information: Applicants for this position are required to upload a Resume, Cover letter, and a list of three (3) references including name, phone number and email address (if available) prior to submitting the application. Once an application is submitted, the applicant will not be able to edit the application or upload additional documents. If you have technical issues uploading a document or if you have a need to provide additional documentation after submitting your application, email humanresources@uada.edu Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Johnny Gunsaulis, jgunsaulis@uada.edu, 479-271-1060 All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Motor Vehicle Reports Check The University of Arkansas System Division of Agriculture may conduct pre-employment background checks on certain positions for applicants being considered for employment. \u00a0 The background checks may include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. \u00a0 Required checks are identified in the position listing. \u00a0 A criminal background check or arrest pending adjudication information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absences of a relationship to the requirements of the position. \u00a0 Background check information will be used in a consistent, non-discriminatory manner consistent with the state and federal law. \u00a0 The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Sitting, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Feeling, Grasping, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Reaching, Repetitive Motion Occasional Physical Activity: Lifting, Standing Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Assistant-Associate-Professor_R0089164-1": {"title": "Assistant/Associate Professor", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 10/03/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: COP | Pharmaceutical Science Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The faculty level position is a 12-month position within Pharmaceutical Sciences on the UAMS main campus in Little Rock. Non-modified faculty member appointments participate in the three mission areas of teaching, service, and research and are expected to be good academic citizens. The faculty member will teach and develop pharmacy educational materials in one or more of the following areas: physiology, pharmacology, biochemistry, medicinal chemistry, pharmacokinetics, and pharmaceutics. The faculty appointment will be in the Department of Pharmaceutical Sciences in the College of Pharmacy. While the primary focus of this position is education and scholarship, commitment to research activities and service to the College, University, and profession are also expected. The successful candidate will provide functions in teaching, research/scholarly activities, professional development, academic citizenship, and administrative academic service. Candidates with a focus on student-centered engagement and active learning approaches that emphasize discussions, problem-solving, case studies, and hands-on activities are encouraged to apply. Other educational and/or institutional opportunities may be available depending on faculty members experience and interests. Academic rank will be commensurate with experience. Qualifications: PhD, PharmD, or terminal degree in an appropriate field required. Responsibilities: Provides functions in teaching, research/scholarly activities, professional development, academic citizenship, and administrative academic service. \u200b This position is a Designated Research Position and is regulated by the Arkansas Research Education Protection Act of 2025 . Prior to issuance of an offer of employment, the University is required to request and obtain additional information about an applicant\u2019s background and, if required, conduct an additional review of that background information. Additional Information: Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding Occasional Physical Activity: Pulling, Pushing, Repetitive Motion, Sitting, Standing, Walking Salary Information: \"Salary is commensurate with Education and Experience\" Required Documents to Apply: Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Harrisburg/Post-Doctoral-Fellow_R0090004-1": {"title": "Post Doctoral Fellow", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/08/2026 Type of Position: Researchers Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: Division of Agriculture of the University of Arkansas The University of Arkansas System Division of Agriculture is a state wide campus, with faculty based on University campuses, at Research and Extension Centers and in every Arkansas county. It consists of the Arkansas Agricultural Experiment Station (AES) and the Arkansas Cooperative Extension Service (CES), and is home to more than 1400 employees.\u00a0 The Division was established in 1959 and is headed by the Vice-President for Agriculture.\u00a0 The Division headquarters is located in Little Rock with the rest of the University of Arkansas System Administration.\u00a0 As an employer, the University of Arkansas System Division of Agriculture offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance.\u00a0 Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process and require reasonable accommodations, please contact the Division's Office of Program & Employment Compliance at compliance@uada.edu . For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-671-2219 or 479-502-9820. Department: Research Agronomy Department's Website: https://crop-soil-environmental-sciences.uark.edu/ Summary of Job Duties: The Research Agronomy Program at the University of Arkansas Division of Agriculture's Northeast Rice Research and Extension Center (NERREC) seeks a highly motivated Postdoctoral Research Associate to support research focused on improving the productivity, profitability, and sustainability of rice and soybean production systems in Arkansas and the Mid-South. The employment term will be one year, with the option to extend by one year based on employee performance. One primary research emphasis is on furrow-irrigated rice production systems, including irrigation management, nitrogen management, and seeding rate optimization, while also conducting research in flood-irrigated rice and soybean production systems. Current soybean research areas include planting date and plant growth regulator management. The successful candidate will primarily focus on data analysis, scientific writing, and publication development. The postdoctoral associate will work closely with faculty and research staff to synthesize findings from ongoing and completed projects, develop peer-reviewed manuscripts, and communicate research outcomes to scientific and stakeholder audiences. The opportunity to actively participate in regional and national research conferences will be available. Opportunities will also exist to contribute to research planning, grant proposal development, and the mentoring of graduate and undergraduate students. This position is ideal for an individual seeking to build a strong publication record, superior grantsmanship, and expertise in applied agronomic research relevant to Mid-South rice and soybean production. Primary Responsibilities (% Effort) 1. Data analysis, interpretation, and manuscript preparation \u2013 50% - Analyze field research data using appropriate statistical methods. - Lead and contribute to peer-reviewed journal manuscripts. - Prepare research reports, summaries, and technical publications. - Develop figures, tables, and data visualizations. 2. Grant development and scientific communication \u2013 25% - Assist with grant proposal preparation and reporting requirements. - Present research findings at scientific conferences and stakeholder meetings. - Contribute to extension and outreach materials, including fact sheets, as appropriate. 3. Research project support and data collection \u2013 20% - Assist with experimental design and treatment development. - Support field research activities, data collection, and quality control. - Introduce novel data collection methods to the research program. 4. Student mentoring and professional service \u2013 5% - Assist in mentoring graduate students involved in research projects. Qualifications: Required: \u2022 Ph.D. in Agronomy, Crop Science, or a related field. Degree must be obtained prior to hire date. \u2022 Experience publishing scientific results in peer-reviewed journals Preferred: \u2022 Experience with rice production \u2022 Grant-writing experience Additional Information: Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Curriculum Vitae, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Tabatha Gonzalez, Dept. Manager, tgonzalez@uada.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Motor Vehicle Reports Check The University of Arkansas System Division of Agriculture may conduct pre-employment background checks on certain positions for applicants being considered for employment. \u00a0 The background checks may include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. \u00a0 Required checks are identified in the position listing. \u00a0 A criminal background check or arrest pending adjudication information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absences of a relationship to the requirements of the position. \u00a0 Background check information will be used in a consistent, non-discriminatory manner consistent with the state and federal law. \u00a0 The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Repetitive Motion, Sitting Frequent Physical Activity: Balancing, Standing, Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Crouching, Driving, Feeling, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAFS--University-of-Arkansas-Fort-Smith/Adjunct-Faculty--History--Social-Sciences--and-Philosophy_R0077109": {"title": "Adjunct Faculty- History, Social Sciences, and Philosophy", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Adjunct Faculty Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Less than Annual Appointment (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Shift Vary (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Fort Smith University of Arkansas \u2013 Fort Smith The University of Arkansas - Fort Smith is a dynamic, mid-sized public university that\u2019s redefining higher education. We\u2019re on a mission to provide transformative, hands-on learning experiences for students of all backgrounds and aspirations. Our multi-faceted approach to education offers a wealth of opportunities, with over 70 academic programs, including certificates, associate, bachelor\u2019s, and master\u2019s degrees. We\u2019re committed to building a diverse community that mirrors Arkansas\u2019s rich tapestry, reflecting our dedication to serving the state\u2019s varied population while enhancing the quality of our institution. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life, and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10 percent of employee salary. \u00a0 Fort Smith, Arkansas Nestled along the Arkansas River, this vibrant city offers a perfect blend of history, culture, and natural beauty. Immerse yourself in the rich heritage of the Old West at the Fort Smith National Historic Site, explore the eclectic local art scene, or take a scenic stroll along the picturesque riverfront trails. With a welcoming community, diverse dining options, and a thriving downtown, Fort Smith is the ideal destination for history enthusiasts and those seeking modern amenities. Thank you for your interest in joining our university. Below you will find details for the position including any supplementary documentation and/or questions you should review before submitting your application. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at (479) 788-7080. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 479-788-7080. Applicants are required to submit a request for each position to which they have applied. Department: History, Social Sciences, and Philosophy Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Teach in one of the following subject areas as assigned: Anthropology, History, Philosophy, Political Science, Religion, Sociology. This is a pool position. Applicants will be contacted as positions become available. The position reports to the department head/program director/dean who assigns responsibilities regarding student needs and course outcomes. Qualifications: Required Education and/or Work Experience: Qualifications of instructors teaching in the classroom for both lower and/or upper-level courses leading to an associate or bachelor\u2019s degree requires a master\u2019s degree in the discipline or related field with a minimum of 18 graduate credits in the subject area. Courses leading to a master\u2019s require a doctorate degree. Adjunct faculty with a clinical assignment must be prepared at the level required by accreditation. Instructors in occupational and technical areas are generally required to have a minimum of an associate\u2019s degree and related work experience. Other job-related education and/or experience may be substituted for part of these requirements. Preferred Education and/or Work Experience: Prior teaching experience. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: To perform the job successfully, the following competencies are required for the essential functions of this position: \u00b7 Current knowledge of the relevant discipline. \u00b7 Good organizational skills and timeliness in responding to student inquiries. \u00b7 Ability to respond to needs of learners from a variety of educational backgrounds in a multicultural environment. \u00b7 Ability to deliver course outcomes and content through a variety of teaching/learning styles. \u00b7 Ability to use technology effectively in teaching. \u00b7 Ability to communicate effectively both orally and in writing. \u00b7 Ability to establish and maintain effective interpersonal relationships with students and colleagues. This is a pool position. Applicants will be contacted as positions become available. Job Responsibilities \u00b7 Classroom and online instruction \u00b7 Assess and evaluate student learning \u00b7 Responsible for maintaining a positive work atmosphere by acting and communicating in a manner to foster teamwork and by providing leadership to subordinates. \u00b7 Requires consistent on-time attendance. \u00b7 Other duties as assigned. Additional Information: Working Relationships: Work with a dynamic team of faculty, staff, and students in a fast-paced, growth-oriented environment. May possibly have contact with vendors, personnel from other agencies and institutions, and the general public. List Employees Supervised: None Special Job Dimensions: Work performed primarily in an office setting. While performing the duties of this job, the employee regularly exhibits digital dexterity when entering data into computer. The employee frequently sits for extended periods of time, and occasionally stands and walks. Vision demands include close, relatively detailed vision when focusing on a computer screen. Employee regularly talks and hears. Employee occasionally lifts items up to 50 pounds. Routine work schedule Monday through Friday, 8:00am to 5:00pm with occasional overtime and travel required Background Check Requirements. Criminal Background Check and Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) Check. May also include a drug screen, child maltreatment check, and proof of immunizations depending upon area of study. Salary Information: Dependent upon department Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: HR All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position may be subject to a pre-employment criminal background check, sex offender registry check, financial history background check, and/or drug screening. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication and/or adverse financial history alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background checks and drug screening information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Intern---Audiology_R0088135-1": {"title": "Intern - Audiology", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/30/2026 Type of Position: Housestaff - Intern Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | SUSL Surgical Specialties Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Audiology Intern will provide supervised audiologic services to patients with hearing and balance disorders while completing the final year of a Doctor of Audiology (Au.D.) program. Under the direct supervision of a licensed audiologist, the extern will participate in diagnostic evaluations, hearing rehabilitation services, cochlear implant services, vestibular assessments, and hearing aid management. The intern will also assist with clinic operations, inventory management, equipment maintenance, and process improvement initiatives to support efficient delivery of patient-centered care. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Must be enrolled full-time in a Doctor of Audiology program Additional Information: Responsibilities: Conduct and interpret complete balance evaluations using state-of-the-art Videonystagmography (VNG), and Computerized Dynamic Posturography (CDP). Provide complete diagnostic hearing evaluations including tympanometry, acoustic reflex testing, air and bone-conduction threshold testing, and a battery of standard and specialized speech assessments. Complete specialized diagnostic assessments, including aided threshold measures, AZ Bio sentence tests, and CNC word tests in soundfield, and interpret outcomes to make recommendations for cochlear implant candidacy. Plan and coordinate hearing rehabilitation activities, including but not limited to: consultation, selection, and fitting of state-of-the-art hearing aids, cochlear implants, bone-anchored hearing aids, and assistive listening devices. Perform verification of amplification devices in an on-ear, probe mic fashion, such as Speech Mapping/Real-Ear measurements. Provide complete care for patients by servicing a wide range of hearing amplification devices, including troubleshooting and repairs. Complete accurate and thorough chart notes and dictation in a timely manner. Provide patient education of procedures to be performed Manage incoming and outgoing shipments of hearing aids and supplies. Maintains hearing aid inventory by checking in hearing aids upon arrival from the manufacturer and returning unwanted/unfit aids to the manufacturer. Program new and repaired hearing aids and prepare new hearing aid fitting packages. Maintain and record manufacturer paperwork. Restock supplies in clinic rooms and maintain supply inventory. Evaluate equipment for repair. Complete minor hearing device repairs in the office. Participate in ongoing hospital and clinical performance assessments and process improvement projects. Ensure continual department performance improvement and assessment. Create and revise work processes to enhance customer satisfaction and reduce waste. Adhere to UAMS Code of Conduct and Departmental policies. Conduct professional Audiologic services in accordance with the American Speech-Language and Hearing Association (ASHA) Code of Ethics. Adopt practices to improve work processes, enhance guest satisfaction, and reduce waste. Serve as a resource person to support department members in the performing of duties. Participate in professional/institutional advancement. Actively participate in continuing education opportunities specific to the growth and advancement of the clinic and hospital.\u00a0 Promotes a safe working environment by complying with department and institutional safety policies. Observes safe work practices and provides input on safety issues. Responds in emergency situations. Intervenes in unsafe situations by taking action. Other duties may be assigned to this position.\u00a0 Salary Information: 35,000.00 USD Annual Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Criminal Background Check, Substance Abuse Testing This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: Feeling, Grasping, Hearing, Kneeling, Lifting, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Repetitive Motion, Sharps, Sitting, Standing, Stooping, Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAMS/Research-Technician_R0090258-1": {"title": "Research Technician", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/15/2026 Type of Position: Staff - Engineering, Science, Agriculture Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: COM | Physiology & Cell Biology Novak Lab Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Research Technician will provide technical, operational, and administrative support to the laboratory of Dr. Sanja Novak, Assistant Professor in the Department of Physiology and Cell Biology. This position supports laboratory research activities with a primary focus on animal experimentation, mouse colony management, surgical procedures, bone and cartilage analysis, regulatory compliance, laboratory organization, and training. Working collaboratively with the Principal Investigator and other laboratory personnel, the Research Technician will help ensure research activities are conducted consistently, efficiently, and in accordance with established laboratory procedures, institutional requirements, and applicable regulations governing animal research. Qualifications: High School Diploma or GED. PLUS experience with animal experimentation and animal surgical procedures. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities: Proficiency with Microsoft Office applications, including Outlook, Word, and Excel, and experience with reference management software. Strong organizational skills with the ability to manage multiple projects and priorities. Strong attention to detail and ability to maintain accurate research records and documentation. Effective written and verbal communication skills. Ability to work collaboratively in a laboratory and research environment. Ability to follow established research protocols, safety procedures, regulatory requirements, and quality standards. Additional Information: Responsibilities Support animal experimentation, mouse colony maintenance, animal databases, and coordination of animal care activities. Perform animal surgical procedures and technical analyses of bone and cartilage using established laboratory and histomorphometric methods. Assist with developing and maintaining Animal Use Protocols (AUPs), Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs), surgical protocols, and other research documentation. Support regulatory compliance, laboratory inspections, accurate recordkeeping, and adherence to institutional and federal animal research requirements. Train and provide technical guidance to laboratory personnel, fellows, and students on animal procedures, surgical techniques, and research protocols. Coordinate laboratory operations, including supply ordering, inventory, research documentation, and communication with University Animal Laboratory personnel. Coordinate laboratory and research meetings, including agendas, minutes, action items, and follow-up activities. Support multiple research projects while ensuring accuracy, consistent protocols, effective communication, and adherence to established quality standards. Perform other duties as assigned in support of laboratory and departmental research activities. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: No Background Check Required This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Repetitive Motion, Sharps, Standing, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Grasping, Reaching, Sitting Occasional Physical Activity: Climbing, Crouching, Feeling, Kneeling, Lifting, Pulling, Pushing Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAFS--University-of-Arkansas-Fort-Smith/Part-Time-Assistant-Coach--Baseball_R0090705": {"title": "Part Time Assistant Coach, Baseball", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Professional Staff - Assistant Coach Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Fort Smith University of Arkansas \u2013 Fort Smith The University of Arkansas - Fort Smith is a dynamic, mid-sized public university that\u2019s redefining higher education. We\u2019re on a mission to provide transformative, hands-on learning experiences for students of all backgrounds and aspirations. Our multi-faceted approach to education offers a wealth of opportunities, with over 70 academic programs, including certificates, associate, bachelor\u2019s, and master\u2019s degrees. We\u2019re committed to building a diverse community that mirrors Arkansas\u2019s rich tapestry, reflecting our dedication to serving the state\u2019s varied population while enhancing the quality of our institution. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life, and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10 percent of employee salary. \u00a0 Fort Smith, Arkansas Nestled along the Arkansas River, this vibrant city offers a perfect blend of history, culture, and natural beauty. Immerse yourself in the rich heritage of the Old West at the Fort Smith National Historic Site, explore the eclectic local art scene, or take a scenic stroll along the picturesque riverfront trails. With a welcoming community, diverse dining options, and a thriving downtown, Fort Smith is the ideal destination for history enthusiasts and those seeking modern amenities. Thank you for your interest in joining our university. Below you will find details for the position including any supplementary documentation and/or questions you should review before submitting your application. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at (479) 788-7080. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 479-788-7080. Applicants are required to submit a request for each position to which they have applied. Department: Baseball Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Responsible for assisting the head coach in the management and administration of an effective and efficient baseball program. The position reports to the Head Baseball Coach. Qualifications: Required Education and/or Work Experience: Minimum qualifications include the following: Bachelor\u2019s Degree Verifiable experience coaching baseball. Essential Job Duties and Responsibilities: Provides leadership including recruitment, player development, and social development of student-athletes. Assist in the management of the program budget. Prepare and conduct practice sessions. Assist in game day operations. Assist in travel and scheduling. Field operations. Create fitness and conditioning programing. Monitors academic progress toward degree of student-athletes in conjunction with the compliance office. Ability to guide athletes toward successful completion of an undergraduate degree while participating in intercollegiate athletics. Other Job Duties and Responsibilities: Other duties as assigned. Responsible for maintaining a positive work atmosphere by acting and communicating in a manner to foster teamwork. Requires consistent on-time attendance. Other Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: To perform the job successfully, the following competencies are required for the essential functions of this position: Knowledge of all aspects of the game of baseball. Familiarity with university policies regarding athletics, Division II baseball programs, MIAA Conference rules, and NCAA legislation and regulations Additional Information: List Employees Supervised: N/A Working Relationships: Work in a dynamic team of diverse faculty, staff, and students in a fast paced, growth-oriented collegiate environment. Frequent contact required with boosters, personnel from other agencies and institutions and the general public. Special Job Dimensions: Work performed primarily in an outdoor setting. Frequent travel and extended hours required. Coaches may be called upon to assist with fundraising for the athletic department and to provide staff support to the other sports programs during their respective seasons. Valid driver\u2019s license required. Background Check Requirements: Criminal, sex offender registry check and MVR (motor vehicle registry) check. Salary Information: $20,451.60 Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume, Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: HR 479-788-7080 All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Child Maltreatment, Criminal Background Check, Financial Credit Check, Motor Vehicle Reports Check, Sex Offender Registry This position may be subject to a pre-employment criminal background check, sex offender registry check, financial history background check, and/or drug screening. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication and/or adverse financial history alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background checks and drug screening information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/North-Little-Rock/Maintenance-Operation-Manager_R0090854": {"title": "Maintenance Operation Manager", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 11/30/2026 Type of Position: Professional Staff - Project/Program Administration Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas Pulaski Technical College University of Arkansas - Pulaski Technical College at North Little Rock is an integral part of the Arkansas Technical and Community College System maintained by the State of Arkansas. The college is governed by the University of Arkansas System Board of Trustees and a seven-member Board of Visitors and derives its support largely from student tuition and fees and legislative appropriations. UA - Pulaski Tech, a comprehensive two-year college, offers associate degree and certificate programs for students who plan to transfer to four-year colleges and universities and/or for career preparation and advancement. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply link/button. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at (501) 812-2839. Department: Asst. Director Faciliities Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Maintenance Manager is responsible for managing the installation, repair, prevention, and overall upkeep of an agency's facilities, equipment, and infrastructure. This role requires a strategic leader who not only manages day-to-day maintenance activities but also drives long-term planning initiatives, budget oversight, process improvements, and compliance with safety and regulatory standards. The Maintenance Manager plays a crucial role in ensuring operational efficiency, reducing downtime, and extending the life of physical assets across multiple sites or a single large facility. \u2022 Follows all integrity guidelines and procedures and ensures no manipulation of data. \u2022 Develop, implement, and monitor maintenance plans and preventive maintenance programs to ensure equipment and facilities operate smoothly. Conducts building inspections. \u2022 Directs activities of in-house construction projects. \u2022 Prepare and manage the maintenance section's budget, monitoring expenses and implementing cost control measures. Analyze maintenance costs and report on key performance indicators (e.g., downtime, repair frequencies, and maintenance return on investment). \u2022 Lead and mentor a team of technicians and supervisors, setting clear performance standards and providing ongoing training and development. \u2022 Negotiate service contracts, supervise vendor performance, and ensure quality, timely service, and adherence to agency standards. \u2022 Maintains appropriate personal attendance, accountability, and work productivity standards. \u2022 Plans, prioritizes and organizes assignments to meet established goals and deadlines. \u2022 Shows respect and courtesy to students, employees, and all campus guests. \u2022 Provides quality services for students and staff ensuring that quality is maintained and needs are met. \u2022 Exchanges ideas and information, both orally and in writing, in a clear and concise manner and contributes meaningfully to group efforts by offering relevant ideas and knowledge. \u2022 Works in partnership with staff from all Departments to ensure effective supervision and services are provided. \u2022 Accepts direction and supervision to include assignments to temporarily perform job responsibilities of other positions and time frames. \u2022 Other duties as assigned. Knowledge, Abilities, & Skills \u2022 In-depth knowledge of mechanical, electrical, Heating, Ventilation, and Air Conditioning, and plumbing systems \u2022 Excellent leadership qualities combined with the ability to communicate effectively with technical teams, vendors, and senior management. \u2022 Sound decision-making, conflict resolution, and the ability to motivate teams in high-pressure environments. \u2022 Abilities to assess maintenance issues, identify trends, and develop effective long-range solutions \u2022 Organized in planning and prioritizing tasks, projects, and resources effectively \u2022 Ability to conduct on-site inspections of buildings to determine quality of maintenance and condition of physical structure. Qualifications: Required Qualifications The formal education equivalent of a high school diploma; Associates Degree or License in Technical field a plus Five years of experience in the building trades, or related area Two years in a managerial or supervisory capacity. Physical requirements include sitting, standing, climbing, walking, lifting, pulling and/or pushing, carrying, reaching, stooping and crouching. Valid Driver's License required. Additional Information: Salary Information: $50,000 Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants Recruitment Contact Information: Human Resources humanresources@uaptc.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Financial Credit Check, Motor Vehicle Reports Check University of Arkansas - Pulaski Technical College is committed to providing a safe campus community. Title IX protects the college community from sexual harassment in a school's education programs and activities. This means that Title IX protects the college community in connection with all academic, educational, extracurricular, athletic, and other programs of the school, whether those programs take place in a school's facilities, in college transportation, at a class or training program sponsored by the school at another location, or elsewhere. \u00a0 We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Repetitive Motion, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Balancing, Climbing, Grasping, Hearing Occasional Physical Activity: Stooping, Talking Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Surgical-Technician_R0090819-1": {"title": "Surgical Technician", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/14/2026 Type of Position: Clinical Staff - Medical Ancillary Support Job Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | WISL Nursing Services L&D IP C Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Surgical Scrub Technician assembles supplies for surgical procedures, maintains the sterile field, passes surgical instruments, and assists in room preparation in Labor and Delivery (E5). UAMS Labor and Delivery unit is located in the Harry P. Ward Clinical Tower. The unit consists of 14 LDR rooms, four triage observational beds, two operating rooms suites, a three bed recovery room area and two state of the art Neonatal Stabilization rooms used to stabilize acutely ill neonates with specially trained staff from the Intensive Care Nursery. Labor and Delivery provides high-risk obstetrical care for patients all over the state. On average, this unit performs approximately 300-330 deliveries per month. The LDR rooms allow the expectant mother to labor, deliver, and recover in the birthing suites with family support. E5 Labor and Delivery supports patient and family centered care and as a result, the newborns, if stable, are allowed to stay with their mother\u2019s after delivery to promote bonding. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Graduate of an accredited Scrub Technologist school/program or 2 years of experience as a surgical technologist. Ensures that the instruments are cleaned arranged and transported to the soiled utility room according to department policy. Assists with instrument reprocessing tasks when assigned cases are completed and time permits; Ensures that the operating rooms are case-ready for the following day\u2019s cases. Admits and discharges patients, ensure front desk logs and phone books are maintained, and manage infant security system alarms as needed. Sets up rooms in preparation for new admissions, ensure ante-rooms and patient rooms are stocked Preferred Qualifications: High School Diploma/GED Must be a Graduate of an Accredited Surgical Technologist Program.\u00a0\u00a0 Must have One (1) year of previous experience as a Surgical Scrub Technologist.\u00a0 Excellent communication skills Strong work ethics, and accountability. Two (2) years of previous experience as a Surgical Scrub Technologist with current BLS. Ensures that the room has been prepared for the upcoming cases, with appropriate equipment availab complete other duties as assigned. Participates in continuing education by completing the required staff development hours annually and in professional/institutional advancement of self and co-workers. May perform other duties as assigned. E mployees in this role must be fitted for, capable of donning and performing routine tasks in personal protective equipment to include N95 masks, Powered Air Purifying Respirators (PAPR) or Controlled Air Purifying Respirators (CAPR).This position is subject to a pre-employment criminal background check and drug screen.\u00a0 A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Additional Information: Job Requirements: Ability to maintain required state or national credentials, as applicable. Knowledge of surgical procedures, sterile technique, aseptic practices, and infection prevention . Ability to properly prepare and maintain the operating room before, during, and after procedures. Knowledge of surgical instruments, equipment, supplies, and instrumentation . Ability to anticipate the needs of the surgeon and surgical team . Ability to perform instrument, sponge, and needle counts accurately. Strong attention to detail and ability to follow safety and infection-control protocols. Effective communication and teamwork skills. Ability to work effectively in a fast-paced, high-stress environment . Ability to stand for extended periods and safely lift/move equipment or supplies. Previous operating-room experience may be preferred , particularly for senior-level positions. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS Stand: Frequently Sit: Frequently Walk: Occasionally Bend, crawl, crouch, kneel, stoop or reach overhead: Frequently Lift and carry weight: 25 lbs Push and pull weight: 25 lbs Use hands to touch, handle or feel: Frequently Talk: Continuously Hear: Continuously Taste or smell: Occasionally Read, concentrate, think analytically: Continuously Physical Environment : Inside Medical Facility Environment Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry, Substance Abuse Testing This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Hearing Frequent Physical Activity: Feeling, Grasping, Lifting, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Pulling, Pushing, Sharps, Standing, Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Crawling, Crouching, Kneeling, Reaching, Sitting, Stooping Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Intermediate-Clinical-Billing-Specialist_R0084863-1": {"title": "Intermediate Clinical Billing Specialist", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/15/2026 Type of Position: Staff - Clerical Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: FIN | CORE CCBO Medicare Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Intermediate Clinical Billing Specialist is responsible for timely and accurate management of payer rejections in the clearinghouse, claim edits in EPIC, and ensuring claims go out to the payer within timely filing deadlines with a goal of clean claim submission. This position must understand 3rd party billing requirements; analyze patient account balances and various payer contract terms, have basic accounting skills and be able to utilize a calculator and systems functionality to calculate expected reimbursement from payers. The Intermediate Clinical Billing Specialist must be detail oriented and demonstrate strong verbal and written communication skills. *******Position is On-Site******** Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in a related field or equivalent combination of education and experience. Associate's degree in a related field plus two (2) years of experience in a healthcare revenue cycle related function. High School diploma/GED plus four (4) years of experience in a healthcare revenue cycle related or bookkeeping function. Preferred: Six (6) months of medical billing experience preferred with a basic understanding of CPT and ICD 10, and familiarity with the Windows environment and billing software; Basic understanding of HCPCS coding; EPIC experience is also a plus. Additional Information: KEY RESPONSIBILITIES:\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Complete electronic and paper specialized billing while reviewing claims for accuracy \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Review and correct claims that fail the billing system edits and document all actions \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Review accounts in EPIC and other systems to avoid duplicate claims and billing \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Contact payers or patients to collect additional information required to bill the account \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Report claim billing issues to management \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Answer questions and provide information to team members regarding the billing process and requirements \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Identify improvements to billing processes and provide recommendations; collaborate with management on effective changes, achieving optimal financial outcomes, in compliance with regulations \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Attend in-services, review online information, and review information from payers and fiscal intermediaries \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Follow up with payers to ensure timely reimbursement \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Participate in compliance and regulatory programs \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Work effectively in a team environment, coordinate workflow, and ensure a productive and efficient environment \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Comply with safety principles, laws, regulations and standards including CMS, Joint Commission, and EMTALA \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Comply with UAMS and Centralized Business Office Department related policies and procedures \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Demonstrate time management skills, integrity and innovative thinking \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Complete or assist on special projects \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Participate in regular reviews and utilize feedback for continued quality improvement \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Maintain good working relationship with patients and families, visitors, physician and others \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Perform other duties as assigned Salary Information: 17.50/hour Required Documents to Apply: List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Feeling, Grasping, Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Reaching, Repetitive Motion, Sitting, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Pulling, Pushing, Standing, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Lifting Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Assistant-Professor---Law_R0090729": {"title": "Assistant Professor - Law", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Faculty - Tenure/Tenure Track Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Academic Term (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Little Rock The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is a metropolitan research university that provides an accessible, quality education through flexible learning and unparalleled internship opportunities. At UA Little Rock, we prepare our more than 8,900 students to be innovators and responsible leaders in their fields. Committed to its metropolitan research university mission, UA Little Rock is a driving force in Little Rock's thriving cultural community and a major component of the city and state's growing profile as a regional leader in research, technology transfer, economic development, and job creation. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . Department: Bowen School of Law Department's Website: https://ualr.edu/law/ Summary of Job Duties: The University of Arkansas at Little Rock William H. Bowen School of Law seeks to hire an entry-level, tenure-track Assistant Professor of Law. The successful candidate will teach Torts and other courses as needed, likely including Remedies and Professional Responsibility. The position begins in August 2027. Bowen\u2019s mission is guided by three core values: access to justice, public service, and professionalism. The law school\u2019s rigorous curriculum aims to balance theory, skill development, and experiential learning. This position is governed by state and federal laws, and agency/institution policy. Qualifications: Required Education and/or Experience: Candidates must hold a J.D. from an ABA-accredited law school; \u00a0Strong writing and interpersonal skills. Preferred Education and/or Experience: Outstanding academic credentials; Law review or moot court service; Prior experience in law school teaching. Job Duties and Responsibilities Teach classes as assigned and achieve teaching goals; Publish excellent and engaging scholarship; Support the law school and university through internal and external service. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Demonstrate ability to teach; Demonstrated ability to advise students; Demonstrated ability to communicate in person, in writing, and through electronic means; Demonstrated ability to work as a team player, and collaborate with colleagues. Additional Information: Interested parties must apply online with a curriculum vitae, cover letter, statement of teaching philosophy, research agenda, and list of three references. Applications will be considered until the position is filled. \u00a0 This position is subject to a pre-employment criminal background check. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Curriculum Vitae, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Statement of Research Philosophy, Statement of Teaching Philosophy Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Interested parties must apply online with a curriculum vitae, cover letter, statement of teaching philosophy, research agenda, and list of three references. Applications will be considered until the position is filled. This position is subject to a pre-employment criminal background check. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. Recruitment Contact Information: Shanna Fitzgerald, Director of Finance, semorris@ualr.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting, Standing, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting, Standing, Talking Occasional Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting, Standing, Talking Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Fayetteville-AR/Property-Accounting-Tagging-Specialist_R0090713-1": {"title": "Property Accounting Tagging Specialist", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com, then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at all University of Arkansas institutions will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students.\u201d University of Arkansas, Fayetteville students will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Student Jobs at UAF.\u201d All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. Closing Date: 09/07/2026 Type of Position: Accounting Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas, Fayetteville Founded in 1871, the University of Arkansas is a land grant institution, classified by the Carnegie Foundation among the nation\u2019s top 2 percent of universities with the highest level of research activity. The University of Arkansas works to advance the state and build a better world through education, research, and outreach by providing transformational opportunities and skills, fostering a welcoming climate, and nurturing creativity, discovery, and the spread of new ideas and innovations. The University of Arkansas campus is located in Fayetteville, a welcoming community ranked as one of the best places to live in the U.S. The growing region surrounding Fayetteville is home to numerous Fortune 500 companies and one of the nation\u2019s strongest economies. Northwest Arkansas is also quickly gaining a national reputation for its focus on the arts and overall quality of life. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10% of employee salary. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions, you should review before applying for the opening. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process, please submit a request via the Disability Accommodations | OEOC | University of Arkansas (uark.edu) : Request an Accommodation. Appli\u00adcants are required to submit a request for each position of which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 479.575.5351. Department: Inventory Management Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Property Accounting Tagging Specialist will be responsible for tagging university equipment in the various buildings on the University of Arkansas campus. Responsibilities: \u2022 Tagging University Equipment using the University of Arkansas barcode tags \u2022 Using a handheld scanner in buildings on campus \u2022 Writing and verbally communicating with various individuals on campus \u2022 Assisting with other duties as assigned by Property Accounting Staff This position is Governed by State and Federal law and Governmental Accounting Standards Board (GASB). Regular, reliable, and non-disruptive on campus attendance is an essential job duty, as is the ability to create and maintain collegial, harmonious working relationships with others. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: The formal education equivalent of a high school diploma Experience with Microsoft Office Suite Experience communicating successfully with stakeholders at various levels of an organization through personal face-to-face contact, email, and telephone contact Must be able to stand, squat, lift, bend and walk for long periods throughout the day to tag equipment as a regular part of daily operations Knowledge, Skills & Abilities: Knowledge of filing and record-keeping procedures Ability to record data to generate reports and documents Ability to interpret department policies and procedures Additional Information: Salary Information: $36,300 Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Proof of Veteran Status Recruitment Contact Information: Crystal Ellis, Strategic Talent Acquisition Specialist, ce031@uark.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Special Instructions to Applicants: Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Motor Vehicle Reports Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas seeks to attract, develop and retain high quality faculty, staff and administrators that consistently display practices and behaviors to advance a culture that embeds equal opportunity, educational excellence and unparalleled access for all. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All Application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Talking Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Fayetteville-AR/Hourly-Testing-Assistant_R0090158-2": {"title": "Hourly Testing Assistant", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com, then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at all University of Arkansas institutions will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students.\u201d University of Arkansas, Fayetteville students will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Student Jobs at UAF.\u201d All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. Closing Date: 09/07/2026 Type of Position: Staff - Clerical Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas, Fayetteville Founded in 1871, the University of Arkansas is a land grant institution, classified by the Carnegie Foundation among the nation\u2019s top 2 percent of universities with the highest level of research activity. The University of Arkansas works to advance the state and build a better world through education, research, and outreach by providing transformational opportunities and skills, fostering a welcoming climate, and nurturing creativity, discovery, and the spread of new ideas and innovations. The University of Arkansas campus is located in Fayetteville, a welcoming community ranked as one of the best places to live in the U.S. The growing region surrounding Fayetteville is home to numerous Fortune 500 companies and one of the nation\u2019s strongest economies. Northwest Arkansas is also quickly gaining a national reputation for its focus on the arts and overall quality of life. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10% of employee salary. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions, you should review before applying for the opening. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process, please submit a request via the Disability Accommodations | OEOC | University of Arkansas (uark.edu) : Request an Accommodation. Appli\u00adcants are required to submit a request for each position of which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 479.575.5351. Department: Testing Services Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Hourly Testing Assistant provides secure, accessible, and professional administration of academic, accommodated, vendor, and professional examinations. This position performs a variety of testing, customer service, and operational duties, including candidate check-in, test administration, testing room monitoring, exam preparation, and maintaining testing security and confidentiality. The Hourly Testing Assistant may assist with coordinating testing activities and providing guidance to other staff as assigned. This position is expected to exercise sound judgment within established procedures, promptly communicate testing concerns or irregularities, and refer complex issues or matters requiring additional authority to full-time Testing Services staff. Because this position supports the administration of professional and credentialing examinations, employees must successfully complete all required testing partner onboarding, certification, and security clearance processes. These requirements may include background checks, fingerprinting, identity verification, and the submission of identifying documentation in accordance with testing partner policies. This position requires flexibility to work shifts outside of typical business hours as operational needs or departmental priorities require. Regular, reliable, and non-disruptive attendance is an essential job duty, as is the ability to create and maintain collegial, harmonious working relationships with others. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: The formal education equivalent of a high school diploma At least one year of experience in a specialized or related area applicable to work performed Availability to work Saturdays and some evenings Preferred Qualifications Bachelor's degree from an accredited institution of higher education Two years of customer service experience Knowledge, Skills and Abilities (KSAs): Excellent communication skills, customer service experience, and demonstrated professionalism. Ability to comprehend and assimilate technical and business-related documents Ability to work independently, as well as with a team Ability to multitask and be detail-oriented Ability to prepare, present, and review oral and written information and reports Ability to research and analyze related work program information Ability to develop, recommend, interpret, and apply policies and procedures Ability to plan, organize, and direct the work of others \u00a0 Additional Information: Due to the nature of the position, applicants must be non-students to be selected for role. Salary Information: $15.50 per hour Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Recruitment Contact Information: Miriam Burns, miriamb@uark.edu, Human Resources Business Partner GSIE All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Special Instructions to Applicants: Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas seeks to attract, develop and retain high quality faculty, staff and administrators that consistently display practices and behaviors to advance a culture that embeds equal opportunity, educational excellence and unparalleled access for all. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All Application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Repetitive Motion, Standing, Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Mena/Advising-Center-Assistant_R0090543-1": {"title": "Advising Center Assistant", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Professional Staff - Student Affairs Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas Community College Rich Mountain The University of Arkansas Rich Mountain\u2019s main campus in Mena is situated on a pristine 40-acre campus at the foot of Arkansas\u2019 second highest peak, Rich Mountain, with satellite campuses located in Waldron and Mount Ida. A two-year public community college offering six associate degrees, seven associate workforce degrees, fifteen technical/certificate programs and a growing list of athletic programs, UA Rich Mountain provides transformative education to all learners with an average 14:1 student to faculty ratio. Thank you for your interest. We hope you\u2019ll be joining us in the heart of UARM\u2019s Buck country soon! Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the\u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process, please notify Human Resources. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at (479) 394-7622 ext. 1570. Department: Student Pathways Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Advising Center Assistant reports to the Director of Advising & Retention and is responsible for a variety of clerical and advising duties focused on increasing student persistence and retention. The assistant will maintain and review student records as they pertain to degree completion. Additionally, supplemental documents, digital resources, and orientation materials will be created/maintained as student resources. The Advising Center assistant will participate in academic and career advising sessions which require confidential communication with students. The assistant will also be responsible for other institutional duties as assigned. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: \u00a0 Associate\u2019s degree \u00a0 Preferred Qualifications: \u00a0 Bachelor\u2019s degree Background in higher education admissions or student services \u00a0 Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Microsoft Office Suite \u00a0 and Google Suite Strong people skills Multi-media material creation Excellent oral and written communication skills Time management for reporting deadlines Strict compliance with confidentiality regulations Additional Information: Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience. Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Charlotte Wiles Director of Academic Advising/Retention 479.394.7622 EXT. 1460 All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check The University of Arkansas Rich Mountain is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/APRN---Peds-Pulmonary_R0090599-1": {"title": "APRN - Peds Pulmonary", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/05/2026 Type of Position: Clinical Staff - Nursing Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: COM | Peds Pulmonary APRN Support Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: *Work Schedule: Monday - Friday 8:00am-5:00pm, no weekends; may work some holidays* The APRN is a skilled healthcare provider who has completed an educational program that provides specialized certification and is regulated by the Arkansas State Board of Nursing. An APRN manifests a high level of expertise in assessing, diagnosing, and treating actual and potential health problems of pediatric patients and their families. An APRN possesses an advanced knowledge level, skill, and competence in the provision of care to specific patient and family populations and serves across the care continuum as a clinical resource for patients, families, staff, and the community. Qualifications: Graduate from an accredited nursing program with at least a Master\u2019s in Nursing. National Certification as an Advanced Practice Registered Nurse in the specialty of pediatrics. May have a certification as a Pediatric Nurse Practitioner in either acute or primary care, although primary care is preferred. Preferred Qualifications : Basic Life Support (BLS). Pediatric Advanced Life Support (PALS). \u00a0 Responsibilities: Provide direct clinical services for patients according to established protocols and utilizing evidence-based clinical practice standards in collaboration with a physician. Obtain patient health histories, complete physical examinations, and interpret hemodynamic data. Document pertinent normal and abnormal findings. Order and interpret appropriate diagnostic and laboratory tests. Formulate and implement a treatment plan for the management of acute and chronic\u00a0 illnesses in collaboration with the physician. Document in medical records appropriately.\u00a0 Provide family-centered care to meet the child\u2019s health care needs. Utilize current research and evidence-based decision-making in all clinical practice. Participate in staff education and educate other APRN/PA students, residents, and/or fellows. Provide leadership and professional interaction within your team or to team members. Coordinate with families the care and progress of their child in person, by telephone, or by email as\u00a0 appropriate. Communicate with others with mutual respect and professional demeanor. Adhere to all standard policies and procedures. Participate in QI or research projects as deemed necessary by your department. Perform other duties as assigned. Additional Information: Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/County-Extension-Agent-Intern_R0090851-1": {"title": "County Extension Agent Intern", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: Division of Agriculture of the University of Arkansas The University of Arkansas System Division of Agriculture is a state wide campus, with faculty based on University campuses, at Research and Extension Centers and in every Arkansas county. It consists of the Arkansas Agricultural Experiment Station (AES) and the Arkansas Cooperative Extension Service (CES), and is home to more than 1400 employees.\u00a0 The Division was established in 1959 and is headed by the Vice-President for Agriculture.\u00a0 The Division headquarters is located in Little Rock with the rest of the University of Arkansas System Administration.\u00a0 As an employer, the University of Arkansas System Division of Agriculture offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance.\u00a0 Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process and require reasonable accommodations, please contact the Division's Office of Program & Employment Compliance at compliance@uada.edu . For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-671-2219 or 479-502-9820. Department: District Director * Ouachita (Carla Due) Department's Website: uada.edu Summary of Job Duties: Job Description \u2022 Seeks information from mentors and colleagues regarding the history, purpose, and mission of the University of Arkansas Division of Agriculture. \u2022 Works with County Extension Agents to coordinate and implement educational program events and activities, aimed to improve lives and communities in the areas of Agriculture, Family & Consumer Sciences, 4-H youth Development and Community, Policy and Economic Development. \u2022 Participates in meetings where local issues are identified and prioritized, and program results and plans are discussed. \u2022 Assists in preparations for planned events and activities by gathering information, assembling materials, contacting participants, and soliciting support from external sources. As appropriate, conducts the teaching, training, or other program presentation. \u2022 In some cases, the intern may identify and develop a value-added process, program or training tool that may be implemented within the hosting unit\u2019s current operations. This contribution should provide a substantial addition to the intern\u2019s resume as practical and applicable work experience. \u2022 Maintains a log, or journal outlining internship experiences to complete the required Record of Internship. Completes and submits Record of Internship at the conclusion of the internship. \u2022 Compensation: Interns will work up to 40 hours per week for a maximum of 10 weeks in the summer at an hourly rate of $12.50. Travel will be reimbursed at the current rate of .52 per mile. \u2022 Housing is not provided. However, County faculty may be able to assist in finding an affordable place to live. Qualifications: Students must be enrolled in a Bachelor\u2019s degree program at an accredited institution and possess a cumulative minimum GPA of 2.5 or higher based on a 4.0 scale. Priority will be given to those students with a minimum of 30 credit hours at time of application. You must be in good academic standing with the university. An UNOFFICIAL transcript, resume and cover letter are required to be included. Interns must be enrolled in an area of Agriculture, Horticulture, or Family & Consumer Sciences (FCS). Job related travel including overnight stays; visiting clientele at sites throughout the county (including farms); standing/walking for long periods of time; handling of objects up to 25 pounds. Must have demonstrated ability to communicate orally and in writing with groups and individuals and through mass media. Ability to use the computer for program deliver and management. Ability to visit clientele at sites throughout the county/area/ Ability to plan and teach educational programs. Demonstrated leadership and ability to serve as a positive role model. Additional Information: Salary Information: $12.50 hourly Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Letters of Recommendation, Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Carla Due, District Director cdue@uada.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: The University of Arkansas System Division of Agriculture may conduct pre-employment background checks on certain positions for applicants being considered for employment. \u00a0 The background checks may include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. \u00a0 Required checks are identified in the position listing. \u00a0 A criminal background check or arrest pending adjudication information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absences of a relationship to the requirements of the position. \u00a0 Background check information will be used in a consistent, non-discriminatory manner consistent with the state and federal law. \u00a0 The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Fayetteville-AR/Fiscal-Support-Specialist_R0090375-1": {"title": "Fiscal Support Specialist", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Accounting, Finance, Business Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: Division of Agriculture of the University of Arkansas The University of Arkansas System Division of Agriculture is a state wide campus, with faculty based on University campuses, at Research and Extension Centers and in every Arkansas county. It consists of the Arkansas Agricultural Experiment Station (AES) and the Arkansas Cooperative Extension Service (CES), and is home to more than 1400 employees.\u00a0 The Division was established in 1959 and is headed by the Vice-President for Agriculture.\u00a0 The Division headquarters is located in Little Rock with the rest of the University of Arkansas System Administration.\u00a0 As an employer, the University of Arkansas System Division of Agriculture offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance.\u00a0 Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process and require reasonable accommodations, please contact the Division's Office of Program & Employment Compliance at compliance@uada.edu . For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-671-2219 or 479-502-9820. Department: PLPA | Accounting Office Support Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Fiscal Support Specialist is responsible for performing a variety of fiscal, accounting, purchasing, travel, and grant-related support functions for the department. The successful incumbent will perform purchasing, accounts payable, travel, and grant administration functions for the department. Responsibilities include processing receiving entries, reviewing and allocating P-Card and T-Card transactions, reconciling receipts, coordinating vendor payments, processing Foundation payments, and maintaining procurement and financial records. The position processes requisitions and procurement authorizations in accordance with university and state guidelines, reconciles cost centers, prepares financial reports, assists with budget preparation, and supports faculty with financial management. Additional duties include processing travel requests and reimbursements, monitoring grant accounts for compliance and available funding, maintaining fiscal records, archiving annual financial documents, processing MV-5 reports, and performing other duties as assigned. The position requires strong organizational, analytical, and customer service skills, with the ability to manage multiple deadlines, maintain accurate financial records, and effectively communicate with faculty, staff, vendors, and university stakeholders. Other duties may be assigned as needed. In addition to core fiscal support duties, provide direct assistance to the Departmental Fiscal Manager by completing a variety of financial, budgetary, and administrative projects. Prepare reports for grants approaching expiration (within 60 days) and communicate remaining balances to faculty. Run and monitor reports for pending financial transactions, following up with faculty and staff to ensure timely approvals. Generate budget reports for the Fiscal Manager, assist with monthly account reconciliations and balance reporting for faculty and departmental accounts, track expenses, reimbursements, and requisitions. Support month-end financial processes by running reports for open purchase orders, coordinating with the appropriate departments or vendors to resolve outstanding items, and closing purchase orders as needed. Coordinate laboratory equipment repairs by submitting work orders, monitoring progress, and managing the process through invoicing and payment to ensure timely completion and accurate financial documentation. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications The formal education equivalent of a high school diploma; plus two years of bookkeeping, basic accounting, billing, or related experience. Candidates must possess strong analytical, organizational, and problem-solving skills; excellent attention to detail; the ability to prioritize multiple assignments and meet deadlines; strong verbal and written communication skills; proficiency with Microsoft Office applications, particularly Excel; and the ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with faculty, staff, students, vendors, and other stakeholders. Regular and dependable attendance is required. Preferred Qualifications Experience with Workday or other University of Arkansas financial systems, purchasing and accounts payable processes, grant accounting and sponsored project administration, budget and cost center reconciliation, travel and expense processing, and work within a University of Arkansas departmental office. Additional Information: Salary Information: 44,000 Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Shauna Weseman, swesema@uark.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check The University of Arkansas System Division of Agriculture may conduct pre-employment background checks on certain positions for applicants being considered for employment. \u00a0 The background checks may include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. \u00a0 Required checks are identified in the position listing. \u00a0 A criminal background check or arrest pending adjudication information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absences of a relationship to the requirements of the position. \u00a0 Background check information will be used in a consistent, non-discriminatory manner consistent with the state and federal law. \u00a0 The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: Grasping, Reaching Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Fayetteville-AR/Custodial-Worker_R0090645-1": {"title": "Custodial Worker", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/16/2026 Type of Position: Staff - Skilled Labor Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: Division of Agriculture of the University of Arkansas The University of Arkansas System Division of Agriculture is a state wide campus, with faculty based on University campuses, at Research and Extension Centers and in every Arkansas county. It consists of the Arkansas Agricultural Experiment Station (AES) and the Arkansas Cooperative Extension Service (CES), and is home to more than 1400 employees.\u00a0 The Division was established in 1959 and is headed by the Vice-President for Agriculture.\u00a0 The Division headquarters is located in Little Rock with the rest of the University of Arkansas System Administration.\u00a0 As an employer, the University of Arkansas System Division of Agriculture offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance.\u00a0 Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process and require reasonable accommodations, please contact the Division's Office of Program & Employment Compliance at compliance@uada.edu . For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-671-2219 or 479-502-9820. Department: AREC | Maintenance Support Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: This position is responsible for general cleaning of areas in and around office buildings and laboratories, conference rooms, building common areas, grounds around these buildings and other areas as required. The job duties will include vacuuming, mopping, sweeping, dusting, and emptying small office trash cans as well as large trash cans. This position will be responsible for using carpet and floor cleaning equipment. The custodial worker will be responsible for cleaning commodes, sinks, water fountains, etc. This position will also be responsible for snow/ice removal during winter months. This position will have a regular defined work schedule; however, on occasional event days this position will adjust work hours to fit the event. Regular, reliable, and non-disruptive attendance is an essential job function of this job, as is the ability to create and maintain collegial, harmonious working relationships with others. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications\nThe formal education equivalent of a high school diploma.\n\nPreferred Qualifications\nAt least one year of custodial work experience in a commercial/corporate industry\n\nKnowledge, Skills & Abilities\n\u2022 Knowledge of basic cleaning techniques\r\n\u2022 Knowledge of cleaning equipment operation and maintenance\r\n\u2022 Ability to follow instructions and perform repetitive manual work\r\n\u2022 Ability to use cleansers and other agents\r\n\u2022 Ability to clean floors and furniture\r\n\u2022 Ability to use housekeeping cleaning supplies and equipment\r\n\u2022 Ability to work independently without close supervision\r\n\u2022 Ability to follow oral and/or written instructions\r\n\u2022 Ability to perform multiple tasks and to prioritize assignments\r\n\u2022 Ability to perform repetitive manual work\r\n\u2022 Ability to do required lifting (up to 50 lbs) Additional Information: Salary Information: Commensurate with experience. Required Documents to Apply: List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Tommy Clark tclarkjr@uark.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas System Division of Agriculture may conduct pre-employment background checks on certain positions for applicants being considered for employment. \u00a0 The background checks may include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. \u00a0 Required checks are identified in the position listing. \u00a0 A criminal background check or arrest pending adjudication information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absences of a relationship to the requirements of the position. \u00a0 Background check information will be used in a consistent, non-discriminatory manner consistent with the state and federal law. \u00a0 The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Standing, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Grasping, Kneeling, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching Occasional Physical Activity: Climbing, Crouching, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAPTC--LRS--Culinary-Arts--Hospitality-Management-Inst/Admin-III-CAHMI_R0090711": {"title": "Admin III CAHMI", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-29\nPosted: Posted 6 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 11/30/2026 Type of Position: Clerical Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas Pulaski Technical College University of Arkansas - Pulaski Technical College at North Little Rock is an integral part of the Arkansas Technical and Community College System maintained by the State of Arkansas. The college is governed by the University of Arkansas System Board of Trustees and a seven-member Board of Visitors and derives its support largely from student tuition and fees and legislative appropriations. UA - Pulaski Tech, a comprehensive two-year college, offers associate degree and certificate programs for students who plan to transfer to four-year colleges and universities and/or for career preparation and advancement. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply link/button. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at (501) 812-2839. Department: Culinary Arts and Hospitality Management Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Administrative Specialist III is responsible for coordinating office activities, researching and preparing special reports, and developing, revising, and recommending administrative policies and procedures as directed by supervisor. This position is governed by state and federal laws and agency policy. Serve as the primary receptionist by answering phone calls, directing inquiries, taking messages, and overseeing the operation and maintenance of office equipment, including usage reporting. Perform a variety of clerical tasks such as drafting correspondence, preparing meeting minutes, and providing administrative support to Directors, Department Chairs, Faculty, and Students. Handle general purchasing duties for office and classroom supplies. Manage point-of-sale and reservation systems for CAHMI dining services. Coordinate CAHMI events, meetings, and participate in college-sponsored functions as a departmental representative. Maintain inventory and organization of instructional materials, office supplies, linens, and event-related items; duties also include laundering linens and staging supplies for CAHMI events. Collaborate with the PR/Marketing department by providing content and updates related to student and faculty activities for social media. Track and maintain records on current and former students (graduates, transfers, stop-outs, etc.). Conduct tours of CAHMI and the LRS campus for prospective students, school groups, and community visitors. Process incoming and outgoing mail, correspondence and input program related data. Distribute mail and packages to designated areas in both the LRS Auto-Tech and CAHMI buildings. Maintain confidentiality while handling sensitive or private information. Qualifications: Associate degree from an accredited institution or two years of comparable work experience. Proficiency with computers and commonly used office software and technology. Minimum of one year of customer service experience. Strong organizational, communication, and time-management skills. Ability to manage multiple tasks, work independently, and meet established deadlines. Strong attention to detail and ability to maintain accurate records and information Additional Information: Salary Information: $30,000 Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants Recruitment Contact Information: Jan Lewandowski, Executive Director CAHMI, jlewandowski@uaptc.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Motor Vehicle Reports Check, Sex Offender Registry University of Arkansas - Pulaski Technical College is committed to providing a safe campus community. Title IX protects the college community from sexual harassment in a school's education programs and activities. This means that Title IX protects the college community in connection with all academic, educational, extracurricular, athletic, and other programs of the school, whether those programs take place in a school's facilities, in college transportation, at a class or training program sponsored by the school at another location, or elsewhere. \u00a0 We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Feeling, Grasping, Hearing, Kneeling, Lifting, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding Frequent Physical Activity: Feeling, Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding Occasional Physical Activity: Crouching, Kneeling Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Online-Learning-Program-Manager_R0090684": {"title": "Online Learning Program Manager", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-29\nPosted: Posted 6 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/14/2026 Type of Position: Professional Staff - Project/Program Administration Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: Criminal Justice Institute The Criminal Justice Institute (CJI) is a campus of the\u00a0University of Arkansas System\u00a0that serves a unique population of non-traditional students\u2014certified law enforcement professionals who are actively employed within our State\u2019s police departments and sheriff\u2019s offices. The Institute is committed to making communities safer by supporting law enforcement professionals through training, education, resources and collaborative partnerships. Utilizing both classroom-based instruction and practical, hands-on application, CJI provides an educational experience designed to enhance the performance and professionalism of law enforcement in progressive areas of criminal justice, including law enforcement leadership and management, crime scene investigation, computer applications, traffic safety, illicit drug investigations and school safety.\u00a0\u00a0 If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process or have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-570-8021.\u00a0 Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. Department: Administrative Services Department's Website: www.cji.edu Summary of Job Duties: The Online Learning Program Manager leads the design, development, modernization, and continuous improvement of CJI's online, blended, and technology-enhanced education and training programs. The position serves as a lead instructional designer while managing programs and projects, supervising assigned staff, modernizing digital content, and evaluating emerging learning technologies. The position is expected to identify opportunities to improve instructional effectiveness, streamline processes, modernize technology, strengthen accessibility, and responsibly incorporate artificial intelligence and other emerging technologies. The position collaborates closely with the Associate Director, subject matter experts, CJI staff, University/System resources, technology personnel, vendors, and other stakeholders. This position is governed by CJI and the University of Arkansas policy and procedures and state and federal law. Regular, reliable, and non-disruptive attendance is an essential job duty, as is the ability to create and maintain collegial, harmonious working relationships with others. This position is not eligible for remote work and requires on-site attendance at the Criminal Justice Institute office in Little Rock, Arkansas. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications Bachelor's degree from an accredited institution in Instructional Design, Instructional Technology, Educational Technology, Learning Sciences, Education, or related field. Master's degree preferred. At least five years of progressively responsible experience in instructional design, curriculum development, digital learning, educational technology, training development, or a related field. Demonstrated experience applying instructional design methodologies and adult learning principles to develop online, blended, or classroom-based learning. Demonstrated experience converting traditional curriculum into engaging, interactive, and accessible online learning. Demonstrated proficiency with an e-learning authoring tool such as Articulate Storyline and/or Rise and experience with an enterprise LMS such as Anthology Blackboard Learn or comparable platform. Experience developing learning objectives, instructional strategies, assessments, storyboards, scripts, multimedia, and digital learning materials. Knowledge of Section 508 and WCAG accessibility requirements. Demonstrated experience leading projects, programs, and teams, including establishing priorities, coordinating resources, managing timelines and deliverables, resolving issues, and providing leadership and direction to achieve organizational objectives. Knowledge of emerging learning technologies, including artificial intelligence, automation, multimedia, analytics, and other technology-enabled learning solutions. Strong written, verbal, organizational, analytical, and critical thinking skills. Demonstrated leadership experience supervising and coaching employees, including assigning work, providing ongoing feedback, developing employee capabilities, addressing performance and professional development needs, and fostering a collaborative, accountable, and high-performing team environment. Preferred Qualifications Master's degree in Instructional Design, Educational Technology, Learning Sciences, or related field. Seven or more years of relevant instructional design or digital learning experience. Experience leading curriculum modernization or digital transformation initiatives. Experience applying generative AI or automation to instructional design and content development. Experience with learning analytics, multimedia production, interactive learning, or emerging learning technologies. Experience with LMS implementation, upgrades, integrations, or technology evaluation. Project management or process-improvement certification. Five or more years of experience leading, supervising, or managing people. Additional Information: Core Competencies The successful candidate will demonstrate: Advanced instructional design and adult learning expertise. Strong digital learning and e-learning development skills. Ability to modernize curriculum and lead content renewal. Ability to evaluate and implement emerging learning technologies. Practical understanding of AI and automation. Strong\u00a0program, project, and\u00a0team leadership skills. Demonstrated ability to supervise, coach, mentor, and develop employees. Strong accessibility and quality-assurance knowledge. Ability to lead change and communicate effectively with technical and nontechnical stakeholders. Ability to establish priorities, manage competing demands, and align programs and projects with organizational objectives. Position Expectations This position is intended for an experienced instructional designer\u00a0and learning professional who can also provide strong leadership of programs, projects, people, technology modernization, and innovation.\u00a0The successful candidate should be capable of evaluating CJI's current learning environment, identifying opportunities for improvement, and leading the organization toward more effective, efficient, accessible, and technologically advanced education and training. The position requires demonstrated leadership capability, including experience supervising and coaching staff, developing employee performance and capabilities, managing complex projects, and competing priorities, and building collaborative teams. The successful candidate is expected to exercise sound judgment, take initiative, lead change, and effectively translate organizational priorities into measurable program and project outcomes. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: For the professional references, please also provide a phone number. Also, one of the references must be from a current or former supervisor. Recruitment Contact Information: Amber Jackson | Human Resources Program Manager | aljackson@cji.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Motor Vehicle Reports Check, Sex Offender Registry The Criminal Justice Institute is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check is required. Required checks are identified in the position listing. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting Frequent Physical Activity: Hearing, Repetitive Motion, Standing, Talking Occasional Physical Activity: Driving, Lifting Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Fayetteville/Assistant-Professor-of-Social-Work_R0090762-1": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Social Work", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com, then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at all University of Arkansas institutions will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students.\u201d University of Arkansas, Fayetteville students will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Student Jobs at UAF.\u201d All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. Closing Date: Type of Position: Faculty - Tenure/Tenure Track Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: Yes Institution Name: University of Arkansas, Fayetteville Founded in 1871, the University of Arkansas is a land grant institution, classified by the Carnegie Foundation among the nation\u2019s top 2 percent of universities with the highest level of research activity. The University of Arkansas works to advance the state and build a better world through education, research, and outreach by providing transformational opportunities and skills, fostering a welcoming climate, and nurturing creativity, discovery, and the spread of new ideas and innovations. The University of Arkansas campus is located in Fayetteville, a welcoming community ranked as one of the best places to live in the U.S. The growing region surrounding Fayetteville is home to numerous Fortune 500 companies and one of the nation\u2019s strongest economies. Northwest Arkansas is also quickly gaining a national reputation for its focus on the arts and overall quality of life. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10% of employee salary. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions, you should review before applying for the opening. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process, please submit a request via the Disability Accommodations | OEOC | University of Arkansas (uark.edu) : Request an Accommodation. Appli\u00adcants are required to submit a request for each position of which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 479.575.5351. Department: School of Social Work Department's Website: https://socialwork.uark.edu/ Summary of Job Duties: The School of Social Work in the Fulbright College of Arts and Sciences at the University of Arkansas invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor to start in August 2027. This is a standard nine-month faculty appointment. This faculty position is part of the Arkansas Health Research and Solutions cluster hire at the University of Arkansas. Driven by three Fortune 500 companies, booming steel and lithium sectors, world-class museums, and rich natural beauty, Arkansas is becoming a vibrant hub of opportunity and innovation. Yet Arkansas also faces significant health challenges. Too many Arkansans experience chronic disease, high rates of infant and maternal mortality, mental health crises, and limited access to healthcare. Through this cluster hire initiative, the University will advance its land-grant mission by expanding capacity to address our state\u2019s most pressing challenges. Building on existing campus expertise, these new faculty members will advance their research agendas through collaborative work\u2014both with other scholars and with communities across the state\u2014that yields peer-reviewed publications, external funding, and new approaches to healthcare. The successful candidate for this position will join a multidisciplinary community of scholars committed to confronting major issues, generating new knowledge, and providing research-based solutions that improve health outcomes for people living in Arkansas and beyond. This is an in-person position. Regular, reliable, and non-disruptive attendance is an essential job duty, as is the ability to create and maintain collegial, harmonious working relationships with others. About the Department: The School of Social Work at the University of Arkansas, housed within the Fulbright College of Arts and Sciences, advances social, economic, and environmental justice through excellence in education, research, and community engagement. As part of Arkansas' land-grant institution, the School prepares ethical, competent, and evidence-informed social work practitioners committed to improving the quality of life for individuals, families, and communities across Arkansas, the Ozark region, nationally, and globally. The School offers fully accredited Bachelor of Social Work (BSW) and Master of Social Work (MSW) degree programs, delivering rigorous curricula across traditional face-to-face and online learning platforms. Our faculty lead dynamic research programs in rural health disparities, health equity, child welfare, aging, the criminal justice system, macro policy analysis, and behavioral health. The School emphasizes interdisciplinary collaboration, robust community partnerships, and student-centered mentorship in an academic environment that values research excellence and applied practice. We are dedicated to fostering a community of culturally competent social work leader-practitioners. Through student-centered experiential learning, rigorous research, and committed community engagement, we prepare our students to become advocates for social and economic justice and equity. Our program integrates classroom knowledge with real-world application. We aim to empower social workers who will enhance the quality of life for individuals, families and communities in Arkansas and globally, believing that through our efforts, Arkansas can truly be a land of opportunity for all. Duties will include: \u2022 40% Teaching or Professional Performance \u2022 40% Research/Scholarly and/or Creative Activities \u2022 20% Academic Service Activities Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Ph.D. in Social Work or a closely related field from an accredited institution (ABD considered, provided doctorate is completed prior to the start date) conferred by the start of employement Eligibility for social work licensure in Arkansas Demonstrated potential for excellence in university-level teaching\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Demonstrated potential for developing a strong, sustainable research agenda and securing external funding Preferred Qualifications: At least two years of post-MSW practice experience Demonstrated track record of community-engaged research or interdisciplinary collaboration Strong record of successful publication and/or external funding in the thematic and/or methodological areas of position focus Additional Information: This position is a Designated Research Position \u00a0and is regulated by the Arkansas Research Education Protection Act of 2025 .\u00a0 Prior to issuance of an offer of employment, the University is required to request and obtain additional information about an applicant\u2019s background and, if required, conduct an additional review of that background information. Salary Information: Salary is commensurate with experience and qualifications. Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Curriculum Vitae, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Other (see special instructions for details), Writing Sample Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Recruitment Contact Information: Marcia Shobe, professor, mshobe@uark.edu LaShawnda Fields, associate professor, lnfields@uark.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Special Instructions to Applicants: APPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS Completed applications received by October 25, 2026, will be assured full consideration. Late applications will be reviewed as necessary to fill the position. For additional inquiries, please contact the search committee co-chairs, Marcia Shobe and LaShawnda Fields at mshobe@uark.edu or lnfields@uark.edu . Applicants must submit: 1) A cover letter 2) Narrative detailing teaching philosophy, research agenda, and qualification fit 3) A curriculum vitae 4) Three (3) Professional Reference Letters (including name, title, institution, email, and phone number) 5) A sample of scholarly writing or publication 6) Teaching evaluations when applicable We will begin reviewing applications immediately and continue until the position is filled. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas seeks to attract, develop and retain high quality faculty, staff and administrators that consistently display practices and behaviors to advance a culture that embeds equal opportunity, educational excellence and unparalleled access for all. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All Application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAMS/GME-Program-Coordinator--Jonesboro--AR-_R0090737-1": {"title": "GME Program Coordinator (Jonesboro, AR)", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/28/2026 Type of Position: Instructional Development Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: REP | Northeast Jonesboro Residency Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: We are seeking a dynamic and organized individual to join our team as a Graduate Medical Education (GME) Program Coordinator at UAMS\u2019s Northeast Campus in Jonesboro, AR. This position provides administrative and operational support for a mature, long-standing Family Medicine Residency Program. The GME Program Coordinator will work closely with the program director to ensure compliance with Accreditation Council for Graduate Medical Education (ACGME) standards and program-specific requirements and with the GME office on institutional compliance and operational support. The coordinator will also serve as a liaison between trainees, faculty, staff, hospital administration, and external departments. The ideal candidate is highly organized, detail-oriented, responsive, able to manage competing priorities, and comfortable working with confidential information in a fast-paced academic clinical environment.If you are passionate about medical education and ready to make a difference, we encourage you to apply today. Qualifications: Minimum qualifications: Bachelor's degree in business, education, general liberal arts, or related field plus three (3) years of\u00a0project management or office coordination experience. OR High School diploma/GED plus seven (7) years of project management\u00a0or office coordination experience. Preferred Qualifications:\u00a0 Experience in the Graduation Medical Education field.\u00a0 TAGME Certification Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Strong organizational, communication, and customer service skills. Proficient with Microsoft Office and electronic scheduling, database, and document management systems. Ability to manage complex schedules, changing deadlines, and multiple priorities with accuracy. Demonstrated ability to handle confidential and sensitive information professionally. Exceptional attention to detail and follow-through. Professional, clear, and timely written and verbal communication. Independent judgment, initiative, and problem-solving skills. Strong project management and time management skills. Ability to build collaborative working relationships with residents, faculty, staff, applicants, and institutional partners. Commitment to supporting a respectful, inclusive, and high-quality learning environment. Additional Information: Key Responsibilities Coordinate resident, faculty, clinic, call, conference, inpatient, and rotation schedules; communicate schedule changes promptly to all affected stakeholders. Support resident onboarding, contracts, licensure, credentialing, training verification, evaluations, graduation, and transition-to-practice activities. Maintain accurate, secure, and confidential resident and program records. Assist the Program Director with ACGME compliance, accreditation readiness, annual reporting, self-studies, site visits, Program Evaluation Committee activities, and continuous quality-improvement efforts. Coordinate resident evaluations, faculty evaluations, milestone documentation, work-hour monitoring, conference attendance, procedure logs, and other required educational data. Organize resident orientation, conferences, faculty meetings, educational events, and graduation activities. Manage administrative aspects of residency recruitment, including ERAS application processing, applicant communication, interview scheduling, selection committee support, NRMP rank-list preparation, and Match Week activities. Maintain data in relevant systems, including New Innovations, ACGME WebADS, ERAS, NRMP, GME Track, AAFP, ABFM, AMA FREIDA, and other required platforms. Prepare reports, correspondence, meeting materials, and program communications. Coordinate Family Medicine clerkship students and visiting medical students, as assigned. Update program policies, handbooks, recruitment materials, website content, and other program resources. Perform other related duties and special projects as assigned by the Residency Program Director or GME leadership. Works with other Administrators, Little Rock offices, and other Regional Programs to provide and exchange information as needed. Maintains timely template changes. Other duties as assigned. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience. Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of five Professional References (name, email, business title), Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Please upload any applicable certifications. Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Motor Vehicle Reports Check, No Background Check Required This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Repetitive Motion, Sitting, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Feeling, Grasping, Kneeling, Standing, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Feeling, Pulling, Pushing, Stooping Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Professor_R0090690-2": {"title": "Professor", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/11/2026 Type of Position: Faculty - Non-Tenure Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Shift Vary (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: COM | Internal Med Hem-Onc Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Professor is expected to promote academic excellence, provide patient care (when applicable), search for translational opportunities, and promote the health & wellness of Arkansans. Qualifications: Ph.D., M.D., or D.O. required. Residency/Fellowship (if applicable). \u00a0 Responsibilities: Provide coordination, continuity, and consistency in patient care, community outreach, research, and instruction. Perform various responsibilities in the areas of patient care, medical education, and/or research.\u00a0 Perform direct patient care, medical teaching, and research collaborations. Engage in clinical care and/or scholarly activities that advance clinical medicine are to be included. Additional Information: Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Feeling, Sitting, Standing Occasional Physical Activity: Lifting Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Fayetteville/Assistant-Professor-of-Childhood-Education_R0090731-1": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Childhood Education", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com, then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at all University of Arkansas institutions will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students.\u201d University of Arkansas, Fayetteville students will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Student Jobs at UAF.\u201d All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. Closing Date: Type of Position: Faculty - Tenure/Tenure Track Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas, Fayetteville Founded in 1871, the University of Arkansas is a land grant institution, classified by the Carnegie Foundation among the nation\u2019s top 2 percent of universities with the highest level of research activity. The University of Arkansas works to advance the state and build a better world through education, research, and outreach by providing transformational opportunities and skills, fostering a welcoming climate, and nurturing creativity, discovery, and the spread of new ideas and innovations. The University of Arkansas campus is located in Fayetteville, a welcoming community ranked as one of the best places to live in the U.S. The growing region surrounding Fayetteville is home to numerous Fortune 500 companies and one of the nation\u2019s strongest economies. Northwest Arkansas is also quickly gaining a national reputation for its focus on the arts and overall quality of life. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10% of employee salary. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions, you should review before applying for the opening. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process, please submit a request via the Disability Accommodations | OEOC | University of Arkansas (uark.edu) : Request an Accommodation. Appli\u00adcants are required to submit a request for each position of which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 479.575.5351. Department: Department of Curriculum and Instruction Department's Website: https://cied.uark.edu/ Summary of Job Duties: The Department of Curriculum and Instruction in the College of Education and Health Professions at the University of Arkansas is seeking candidates for a nine-month tenure-track Assistant Professor of Childhood Education faculty position with a specialization in elementary literacy. The Assistant Professor of Childhood Education is a full-time, nine-month position to begin August 16, 2027. The successful candidate will join a vibrant team of faculty in a department growing in stature and recognized for excellence in teaching, research, faculty development, and student success. The Assistant Professor of Childhood Education will be expected to teach undergraduate coursework in literacy methods across foci such as emergent and developmental literacy, reading comprehension and/or writing; conduct research that results in peer-reviewed publications and professional presentations; pursue external funding through grant proposal submissions; participate in student advisement and mentoring, including service on dissertation committees; and collaborate with P-6 schools/educators to coordinate clinical experiences for preservice teachers or provide programmatic support. Providing service to the university, college, department, program, profession and community are foundational expectations. Through teaching, research, and service, this position supports the University\u2019s 150 Forward priorities of student success, research excellence, and an employer-of-choice environment. This is an in-person position. On-campus presence is an essential function of this position. Extensive in-person engagement in activities such as office hours, student advising, collaborative work, and departmental, college, and university committee meetings is required to advance student success, departmental effectiveness, and the mission of the college and the university. Regular, reliable, and non-disruptive attendance is an essential job duty, as is the ability to create and maintain collegial, harmonious working relationships with others. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: An earned doctorate from a nationally recognized and accredited institution of higher education focused on primary/elementary literacy education in programs such as Elementary Education, Curriculum and Instruction, or a closely related field conferred by the start of employment Evidence and/or promise of exemplary performance in research in elementary literacy education Evidence and/or promise of effective teaching and advising at the higher education level. Evidence of relevant, productive service or potential to actively contribute to the program, department, university, and profession related to literacy education Preferred Qualifications : Evidence of successful teaching in literacy methods courses with a distinct focus on foundational literacy skills, from emergent literacy practices through advanced reading comprehension and writing instruction Evidence of teaching and/or preparation of in-service teachers for primary/elementary settings Evidence of primary/elementary classroom experience (3 years) in the United States Familiarity with clinical models of teacher preparation (such as immersive field placements and Professional Development Schools) Additional Information: This position is a Designated Research Position \u00a0and is regulated by the Arkansas Research Education Protection Act of 2025 .\u00a0 Prior to issuance of an offer of employment, the University is required to request and obtain additional information about an applicant\u2019s background and, if required, conduct an additional review of that background information. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Curriculum Vitae, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title) Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Recruitment Contact Information: Dr. Heather Young Associate Professor hkindall@uark.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Special Instructions to Applicants: Completed applications received by October 1, 2026, will be assured full consideration. Late applications will be reviewed as necessary to fill the position. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas seeks to attract, develop and retain high quality faculty, staff and administrators that consistently display practices and behaviors to advance a culture that embeds equal opportunity, educational excellence and unparalleled access for all. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All Application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Hearing Occasional Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Fayetteville/Assistant-Professor-of-Special-Education_R0090720-1": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Special Education", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com, then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at all University of Arkansas institutions will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students.\u201d University of Arkansas, Fayetteville students will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Student Jobs at UAF.\u201d All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. Closing Date: Type of Position: Faculty - Tenure/Tenure Track Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: Yes Institution Name: University of Arkansas, Fayetteville Founded in 1871, the University of Arkansas is a land grant institution, classified by the Carnegie Foundation among the nation\u2019s top 2 percent of universities with the highest level of research activity. The University of Arkansas works to advance the state and build a better world through education, research, and outreach by providing transformational opportunities and skills, fostering a welcoming climate, and nurturing creativity, discovery, and the spread of new ideas and innovations. The University of Arkansas campus is located in Fayetteville, a welcoming community ranked as one of the best places to live in the U.S. The growing region surrounding Fayetteville is home to numerous Fortune 500 companies and one of the nation\u2019s strongest economies. Northwest Arkansas is also quickly gaining a national reputation for its focus on the arts and overall quality of life. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10% of employee salary. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions, you should review before applying for the opening. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process, please submit a request via the Disability Accommodations | OEOC | University of Arkansas (uark.edu) : Request an Accommodation. Appli\u00adcants are required to submit a request for each position of which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 479.575.5351. Department: Department of Curriculum and Instruction Department's Website: https://cied.uark.edu/ Summary of Job Duties: The Department of Curriculum and Instruction in the College of Education and Health Professions at the University of Arkansas is seeking candidates for a nine-month tenure-track Assistant Professor of Special Education faculty position with a specialization in applied behavior analysis. The Assistant Professor of Special Education is a full-time, nine-month position to begin August 16, 2027. The successful candidate will join a vibrant team of faculty in a department growing in stature and recognized for excellence in teaching, research, faculty development, and student success. The Assistant Professor of Special Education will be expected to teach primarily graduate courses in applied behavior analysis online though the program and department includes undergraduate and doctoral level on campus courses; conduct research that results in peer-reviewed publications and professional presentations; pursue external funding through grant proposal submissions; participate in student advisement and mentoring, including service on thesis and dissertation committees; and collaborate with partners to coordinate clinical experiences for students or provide programmatic support. Providing service to the university, college, department, program, profession and community are foundational expectations. Through teaching, research, and service, this position supports the University\u2019s 150 Forward priorities of student success, research excellence, and an employer-of-choice environment. This is an in-person position. On-campus presence is an essential function of this position. Extensive in-person engagement in activities such as office hours, student advising, collaborative work, and departmental, college, and university committee meetings is required to advance student success, departmental effectiveness, and the mission of the college and the university. Regular, reliable, and non-disruptive attendance is an essential job duty, as is the ability to create and maintain collegial, harmonious working relationships with others. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: An earned doctorate from a nationally recognized and accredited institution of higher education focused on special education, psychology and/or applied behavior analysis conferred by the start of employment Certification as a Board-Certified Behavior Analyst\u2122 (BCBA or BCBA-D) Evidence and/or promise of exemplary performance in research in the area of special education, psychology, and/or applied behavior analysis Evidence and/or promise of effective teaching and advising at the higher education level. Evidence of relevant, productive service or potential to actively contribute to the program, department, university, and profession related to special education and applied behavior analysis Preferred Qualifications: Evidence of successful teaching of behavior analysis coursework for at the college/university level Experience using online teaching modalities Evidence of ability to collaborate across disciplines Applied/clinical experience working as a behavior analyst Successful experience mentoring and supervising students in applied behavior analysis Additional Information: This position is a Designated Research Position \u00a0and is regulated by the Arkansas Research Education Protection Act of 2025 .\u00a0 Prior to issuance of an offer of employment, the University is required to request and obtain additional information about an applicant\u2019s background and, if required, conduct an additional review of that background information. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Curriculum Vitae, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title) Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Recruitment Contact Information: Dr. Elizabeth Lorah Professor of Special Education lorah@uark.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Special Instructions to Applicants: Completed applications received by October 1, 2026, will be assured full consideration. Late applications will be reviewed as necessary to fill the position. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas seeks to attract, develop and retain high quality faculty, staff and administrators that consistently display practices and behaviors to advance a culture that embeds equal opportunity, educational excellence and unparalleled access for all. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All Application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding Occasional Physical Activity: Hearing Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Fayetteville/Chief-of-Staff-to-the-Provost_R0090808-2": {"title": "Chief of Staff to the Provost", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com, then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at all University of Arkansas institutions will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students.\u201d University of Arkansas, Fayetteville students will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Student Jobs at UAF.\u201d All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. Closing Date: 09/05/2026 Type of Position: Administrative Strategy Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas, Fayetteville Founded in 1871, the University of Arkansas is a land grant institution, classified by the Carnegie Foundation among the nation\u2019s top 2 percent of universities with the highest level of research activity. The University of Arkansas works to advance the state and build a better world through education, research, and outreach by providing transformational opportunities and skills, fostering a welcoming climate, and nurturing creativity, discovery, and the spread of new ideas and innovations. The University of Arkansas campus is located in Fayetteville, a welcoming community ranked as one of the best places to live in the U.S. The growing region surrounding Fayetteville is home to numerous Fortune 500 companies and one of the nation\u2019s strongest economies. Northwest Arkansas is also quickly gaining a national reputation for its focus on the arts and overall quality of life. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10% of employee salary. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions, you should review before applying for the opening. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process, please submit a request via the Disability Accommodations | OEOC | University of Arkansas (uark.edu) : Request an Accommodation. Appli\u00adcants are required to submit a request for each position of which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 479.575.5351. Department: Provost and Executive Vice Chancellor for Academic Affairs Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The University of Arkansas invites applications for the Chief of Staff to the Provost, a key leadership role supporting strategic priorities. The Chief of Staff to the Provost serves as a senior advisor and trusted partner to the Provost. This position supports the advancement of academic and institutional priorities by facilitating coordination, communication, and implementation across the units reporting to the Provost. This position is well-suited for a professional with strong judgment, discretion, and the ability to navigate complex organizational environments while advancing high-impact work. The Chief of Staff to the Provost serves as a senior advisor and trusted partner to the Provost. This position supports the advancement of academic and institutional priorities by facilitating coordination, communication, and implementation across the units reporting to the Provost. Acting with delegated authority on behalf of the Provost, the Chief of Staff works closely with Vice Provosts, Deans, and other academic leaders to ensure alignment of initiatives, effective follow-through on key priorities, and thoughtful engagement with the university\u2019s shared governance processes. The Chief of Staff also supports the Provost in navigating and maintaining effective relationships with external partners, University of Arkansas System leaders, and other key stakeholders, coordinating with the appropriate university offices to promote alignment and advance institutional priorities. The Chief of Staff plays a critical role in ensuring coordination of communications, requests, and matters directed to or originating from the Office of the Provost. The position assesses and routes inquiries, facilitates timely and appropriate responses, and ensures that communications involving the Provost\u2019s Office are coordinated, consistent, and aligned with university priorities. This role requires sound judgment, discretion, and the ability to navigate a complex, decentralized academic environment. Regular, non-disruptive and reliable attendance is required, as well as the ability to create and maintain collegial, harmonious working relationships with others. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor\u2019s degree from an accredited institution of higher education At least four years of progressively responsible professional experience in higher education, government, or a similarly complex organization At least two years supporting or working directly with senior leadership Demonstrated experience leading or coordinating cross-functional initiatives or projects involving multiple departments, units, or stakeholders Preferred Qualifications: Master\u2019s degree from an accredited institution of higher education At least eight years of progressively responsible professional experience, preferably in higher education, government, or a similarly complex organizations Demonstrated experience preparing executive-level materials, such as briefings, reports, presentations, or communications for senior leadership Experience supporting or participating in institutional processes, initiatives, or governance activities (e.g., strategic planning, policy development, board or committee support, academic or administrative initiatives) Core Competencies: Executive Judgment & Advising: Provides thoughtful and well-informed counsel on complex and sensitive matters Relationship Building: Establishes effective working relationships across academic and administrative units Coordination & Follow-Through: Ensures priorities are advanced in a timely and organized manner Institutional Awareness: Understands the structure, culture, and governance of a public research university Communication: Prepares clear, concise, and well-organized materials for a variety of audiences Discretion and Integrity :\u00a0 Demonstrated ability to handle confidential information with professionalism and care Adaptability & Discretion: Manages competing priorities with professionalism and sound judgment Additional Information: Salary Information: $125,000 - $140,000 Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Recruitment Contact Information: Lucciana Lorenzetti llorenze@uark.edu Strategic Talent Acquisition Specialist All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Special Instructions to Applicants: Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas seeks to attract, develop and retain high quality faculty, staff and administrators that consistently display practices and behaviors to advance a culture that embeds equal opportunity, educational excellence and unparalleled access for all. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All Application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAM--Monticello-Campus/Assistant-Director-of-Admissions-and-Recruitment_R0090566-1": {"title": "Assistant Director of Admissions and Recruitment", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Professional Staff - Project/Program Administration Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Monticello UAM, one of twenty campuses of the University of Arkansas System, is located in southeastern Arkansas in the beautiful timberlands, rich in outdoor recreation activities, and approximately 100 miles south of Little Rock. UAM is a comprehensive, residential and commuter, undergraduate institution also offering selected master\u2019s degree programs. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please submit a request via the OEOC website: \u00a0Applicants are required to submit a request for each position to which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 870-460-1422 . Department: Admissions Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Assist with recruitment, admissions, disability services, international services, and special events handled through the Office of Admissions. Must learn and maintain records for federal guidelines with International Services and Disability Services. Assist with budgeting and preparation of office documents as needed. Office training as needed. Travel required, sometimes nights, weekends and as needed within the office. Assist with publications, materials, inventory, work orders. Familiarity with word, excel, power point, and other technology programs. Other duties as assigned. Qualifications: Master's degree preferred. Bachelor's degree required, with emphasis in Communications, Marketing, Human Resources preferred. Experience with Work Day preferred. Additional Information: Background check, good driving record, must be able to lift up to 30 pounds. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience. Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Mary Whiting Associate Vice Chancellor of Enrollment All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Repetitive Motion, Talking Occasional Physical Activity: Crouching, Feeling, Kneeling, Stooping Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAMS/Education-Coordinator_R0090408-1": {"title": "Education Coordinator", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/19/2026 Type of Position: Instructional Development Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: CON | College of Nursing Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Education Coordinator for Student Services and Recruitment provides operational, administrative, and programmatic support for the College of Nursing Student Services Office. Reporting to the Associate Dean for Student Affairs and collaborating closely with the Director of Recruitment and Outreach and the Director of Student Services, this position supports recruitment, admissions, student engagement, onboarding, retention initiatives, scholarship processes, student communications, and student-centered events across undergraduate and graduate nursing programs. The Education Coordinator assists with coordinating recruitment activities, processing admissions materials, maintaining student records and Student Services processes, managing communications and outreach initiatives, updating website and marketing content, and implementing student support activities from recruitment through graduation. This position serves as a key point of contact for prospective and current students while supporting the efficient daily operations of the Student Services Office and promoting a positive, responsive, and student-centered experience. Qualifications: Bachelor\u2019s degree in education, computer science, information technology, or a related field. Three years of experience coordinating educational programs. Experience with public speaking and delivering presentations. Advanced proficiency with Microsoft Office Suite. Preferred Qualifications Experience using a student information system or other student services technology. Experience supporting student recruitment, admissions, advising, or student services in a higher education environment. Experience coordinating events, outreach programs, or student engagement initiatives. Additional Information: Responsibilities Coordinate recruitment, outreach, and engagement activities for prospective and current nursing students. Assist with admissions processing, application review workflows, onboarding activities, and student communications. Respond to inquiries from prospective students, applicants, current students, faculty, staff, and community partners. Support student retention initiatives, scholarship processes, and other student success programs. Plan and coordinate student-centered events, including recruitment programs, orientations, information sessions, and other College of Nursing activities. Prepare presentations and represent the College of Nursing at recruitment events, information sessions, and community outreach activities. Maintain accurate student records, reports, databases, and Student Services documentation in accordance with university policies and applicable requirements. Develop, review, and distribute communications through email, websites, social media, and other outreach platforms. Coordinate updates to recruitment materials, website content, and marketing resources to ensure information is accurate and current. Collaborate with College of Nursing leadership, faculty, staff, and university partners to support undergraduate and graduate nursing programs. Perform other duties as assigned. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Repetitive Motion Occasional Physical Activity: Lifting Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Proton-Dosimetrist_R0090722": {"title": "Proton Dosimetrist", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/28/2026 Type of Position: Clinical Staff - Clinical Support Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | CASL Proton Dosimetry Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: This position is responsible for providing physicians and therapists with treatment planning, calculations, quality assurance planning, constructing custom blocks as needed for patient treatment, taking required measurements on patients, consulting with physicians and other therapists in planning and delivering patient treatments and maintaining quality control. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree plus certification as a Medical Dosimetrist by the Medical Dosimetry Certification Board (MDCB) or eligible after completion of a JRCERT-accredited program in Medical Dosimetry Certification as a Medical Dosimetrist by the Medical Dosimetry Certification Board (MDCB) within 18 months of hire Preferred Qualifications: MDCB certification Technical skill in mathematics and physics as normally acquired in freshman and sophomore college level coursework for science majors or in completing an accredited dosimetry dosimetry program. Math coursework should include 2 semesters of algebra, one semester of pre-ca pre-calculus and one semester of calculus. Math coursework requirements may be for waived for appropriate amount of amount of workplace experience obtained by working in the medical dosimetry field. Additional Information: Responsibilities: Designs patient treatment plans and prepares dose calculations by using computers, calculators, and manual techniques for external beam treatment planning. Consults with physicians and therapists to ensure accurate patient information and dose calculations. Collaborates with radiation therapy staff to assess and improve patient treatments and/or set-up techniques. Shares results and recommendations with their supervisor, as appropriate. Assists radiation therapists with patient set-up procedures at the treatment machine and/or simulator as needed. Completes proper records, patient data forms, planning documents, and billing information logs. Checks patient charts for accuracy and proper documentation according to established procedures. Monitors and adheres to general radiation safety guidelines. Participates in clinical research and quality improvement processes, as necessary. Performs other duties as assigned. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Criminal Background Check, Substance Abuse Testing This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Reaching, Repetitive Motion, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Grasping, Stooping Occasional Physical Activity: Crouching, Kneeling Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Fayetteville-AR/Teaching-Assistant-Professor_R0090589-1": {"title": "Teaching Assistant Professor", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com, then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at all University of Arkansas institutions will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students.\u201d University of Arkansas, Fayetteville students will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Student Jobs at UAF.\u201d All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. Closing Date: 09/29/2026 Type of Position: Faculty - Non-Tenure Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Academic Term (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas, Fayetteville Founded in 1871, the University of Arkansas is a land grant institution, classified by the Carnegie Foundation among the nation\u2019s top 2 percent of universities with the highest level of research activity. The University of Arkansas works to advance the state and build a better world through education, research, and outreach by providing transformational opportunities and skills, fostering a welcoming climate, and nurturing creativity, discovery, and the spread of new ideas and innovations. The University of Arkansas campus is located in Fayetteville, a welcoming community ranked as one of the best places to live in the U.S. The growing region surrounding Fayetteville is home to numerous Fortune 500 companies and one of the nation\u2019s strongest economies. Northwest Arkansas is also quickly gaining a national reputation for its focus on the arts and overall quality of life. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10% of employee salary. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions, you should review before applying for the opening. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process, please submit a request via the Disability Accommodations | OEOC | University of Arkansas (uark.edu) : Request an Accommodation. Appli\u00adcants are required to submit a request for each position of which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 479.575.5351. Department: Accounting Department's Website: https://walton.uark.edu/departments/accounting/ Summary of Job Duties: The William Dillard Department of Accounting in the Sam M. Walton College of Business at the University of Arkansas seeks applications from interested candidates to fill a non-tenure track Teaching Assistant Professor position effective August 16, 2027. A Teaching Assistant Professor is expected to teach eight courses per year with a mix of face-to-face and online courses, as needed. Salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience; benefits are competitive. Regular on-campus availability, in-person teaching, and active contribution to the life of the department, including exhibiting respect and cooperation in shared academic and administrative tasks are essential duties. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: \u00a0 Hold a Ph.D. with an emphasis in accounting from a nationally or internationally accredited university Evidence of high-quality teaching in undergraduate and/or graduate accounting courses Evidence or potential to provide both face-to-face and online undergraduate and/or graduate accounting courses Must meet standards to be classified as Scholarly Academic under AACSB (this could include recent publications in peer-reviewed journals and/or engagement in professional practice through outreach, consulting, or other activities consistent with AACSB standards.) Preferred Qualifications: \u00a0 Experience teaching courses focused on individual and/or corporate taxation Evidence or potential to publish in peer-reviewed accounting journals with a primary research emphasis in tax accounting Additional Information: The William Dillard Department of Accounting: The department develops outstanding students and faculty who meaningfully impact the global accounting community. The department currently has eleven tenured or tenure-track faculty members, eight teaching/clinical faculty members, two full-time Executive in Residence faculty members, six full-time instructors, and several part-time lecturers. The department offers an undergraduate degree program in accounting and graduate programs at both the master\u2019s and doctoral levels. The department also offers a five-year integrated program, which leads to the simultaneous awarding of an undergraduate degree and a master\u2019s degree. The department\u2019s programs are accredited by the AACSB, which ensures quality and promotes excellence and continuous improvement in undergraduate and graduate education. The department was named as part of a gift provided in honor of William Dillard Sr. \u202f\u00a0 The Sam M. Walton College of Business:\u202f The Sam M. Walton College of Business promotes the values of being \u201cEPIC\u201d, which stands for Excellence, Professionalism, Innovation and Collegiality. The Walton College has nearly 10,000 students. The Walton College has an innovative cross-functional business core program that focuses on business processes, and several new cross-disciplinary minors and concentrations. The Walton College has consistently been ranked among the nation\u2019s top 25 public undergraduate business schools since 2005, according to\u202f U.S. News and World Report .\u00a0 The University of Arkansas: The flagship campus of the University of Arkansas has a total enrollment of approximately 34,000 students. It recently completed a successful capital campaign that raised about $1.45 billion.\u00a0 Location : The University of Arkansas is located in Fayetteville, in the Ozark Mountains of Northwest Arkansas. Fayetteville offers a high quality of life, a mild climate, excellent health care, a variety of restaurants, a cost-of-living index of 92.9, and is minutes from lakes and rivers for fishing, swimming, and boating. Fayetteville\u2019s Walton Arts Center and Theatre Squared offer a rich variety of Broadway, symphony, dance, jazz, and other performances and special events. US News consistently ranks Fayetteville among the 10 best places to live in the U.S., with the most recent ranking (2023) of #10. Fayetteville is a city of approximately 85,000 with a regional (Northwest Arkansas) population of about 535,000. Northwest Arkansas has one of the highest growth rates in the U.S. and was ranked 40th among the \u201cbest places for Business and Careers\u201d by Forbes in 2023. Several Fortune 500 companies have their headquarters in Northwest Arkansas, including Walmart, Tyson Foods, and J.B. Hunt Transportation.\u00a0 Check out this site for more information: https://walton.uark.edu/about/ Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Curriculum Vitae, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title) Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Recruitment Contact Information: Caleb Rawson Associate Professor of Accounting Sam M. Walton College of Business CRawson@walton.uark.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Special Instructions to Applicants: Job posting will close at 12:01 AM on close date above. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas seeks to attract, develop and retain high quality faculty, staff and administrators that consistently display practices and behaviors to advance a culture that embeds equal opportunity, educational excellence and unparalleled access for all. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All Application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Education-Resource-Specialist_R0090694-1": {"title": "Education Resource Specialist", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/18/2026 Type of Position: Instructional Development Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: AA | Office of Academic Services Admin Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Education Resource Specialist serves as the campus functional administrator for room scheduling software (Series25) used for the scheduling of classrooms. This includes maintaining all classroom inventories and scheduling databases. The Education Resource Specialist trains new users of the software and acts as a back-up for the main event Coordinator. This includes assisting in the university-wide academic facility scheduling process for assigning academic and special event activities into academic spaces while working closely with all stakeholders in the process. Qualifications: Bachelor\u2019s degree in computer science or other computer/technology-related field, plus two (2) years of experience in a computer maintenance, networking, or software troubleshooting field or Associate\u2019s degree in computer science or other computer/technology-related field, plus four (4) years of experience in a computer maintenance, networking, or software troubleshooting field or High School diploma/GED plus six (6) years of experience in a computer maintenance, networking, or software troubleshooting field required. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities: Advanced proficiency with computers (Mac, PC, and mobile devices). Advanced proficiency with standard office computer programs (e.g., MS Office Suite). Website creation and maintenance\u00a0experience. Excellent customer service skills. Responsibilities: Contributes to developing, maintaining, and testing all systems required for the room scheduling process.\u00a0 Updates and maintains documentation on procedures and policies for the area.\u00a0 Assists with the implementation of room scheduling software and the scheduling of events.\u00a0\u00a0 Trains new users of the room scheduling software. Supervises, trains, and makes daily assignments to support personnel.\u00a0 Acts as a backup for the Room Scheduling Coordinator. Performs other duties as assigned. Additional Information: Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: No Background Check Required This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Hearing Frequent Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting, Talking Occasional Physical Activity: Standing, Walking Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Medical-Laboratory-Scientist-I--Chemistry-PRN_R0088647-1": {"title": "Medical Laboratory Scientist I- Chemistry PRN", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/11/2026 Type of Position: Clinical Staff - Medical Ancillary Support Job Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Shift Vary (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | LPSL CPATH Chemistry Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Medical Laboratory Scientist I (MLS I) performs routine and moderately complex laboratory testing on patient specimens to support the diagnosis, treatment, and prevention of disease. Working under the supervision of laboratory leadership and in collaboration with pathologists, physicians, and other healthcare professionals, the MLS I operates laboratory instrumentation, ensures quality control, maintains regulatory compliance, and reports accurate and timely test results. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor\u2019s Degree in Chemistry, Biology, Medical Technology or Medical Laboratory Sciences OR an approved ASCP discipline (30 semester hours in biology and chemistry, which may be obtained within, or in addition to, the Bachelor's). ASCP or another accrediting agency certified or eligible (Certification must be obtained within one year of employment). Preferred Qualifications: Previous clinical laboratory experience ASCP certification Additional Information: Job Requirements: Processes and evaluates specimens and performs appropriate tests to assist with detection, diagnosis, and treatment. \u00a0Records and evaluates daily, weekly, and monthly quality control issues in their assigned areas for further review by the supervisor.\u00a0 Maintains safe work practices, follows all regulatory requirements and engages supervisor, manager, or director as appropriate. Assists with day-to-day operations of assigned section in Core Lab. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS Stand: Frequently Sit: Frequently Walk: Occasionally Bend, crawl, crouch, kneel, stoop or reach overhead: Frequently Lift and carry weight: 25 lbs Push and pull weight: 25 lbs Use hands to touch, handle or feel: Frequently Talk: Continuously Hear: Continuously Taste or smell: Occasionally Read, concentrate, think analytically: Continuously Physical Environment : Inside Medical Facility Environment Salary Information: $33.76 per hour Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), Proof of Veteran Status, Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Criminal Background Check, Substance Abuse Testing This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding Frequent Physical Activity: Feeling, Grasping, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Repetitive Motion, Sharps, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Crouching, Lifting, Stooping Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Helena-Campus/Industrial-Technology-Instructor_R0090790": {"title": "Industrial Technology Instructor", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Faculty - Non-Tenure Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: Phillips Community College of the University of Arkansas The first community college established in Arkansas, Phillips Community College of the University of Arkansas (PCCUA) is a multi-campus, two-year college serving Eastern Arkansas. PCCUA has academic, occupational/technical and continuing education programs and offers over 25 associate degree programs with campuses in DeWitt, Helena-W. Helena and Stuttgart. Thank you for your interest, and we hope you\u2019ll be joining our Ridge Runner family soon! Below you will find the details for the position as well as any specific application requirements you should review before applying for this opening. To apply for this position, please click the Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process, please call Human Resources at (870) 338-6474, ext. 1271. Department: Workforce Training Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Development and delivery of manufacturing/processing credit and non-credit training programs that may include plant automation, mechanical systems maintenance, industrial safety, pump maintenance, hydraulics/pneumatics, welding, industrial electricity, industrial supervision, programmable logic controllers, etc. Performs other related responsibilities as required. Qualifications: Able to work a flexible schedule that may include evening and weekends. Bachelor\u2019s degree in industrial technology or engineering technology is preferred.\u00a0 Strong organizational, computer, and interpersonal skills are a must.\u00a0 Prior teaching or training experience preferred.\u00a0 Industry maintenance certification a plus. Additional Information: Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Joe St Columbia All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check For general application assistance, or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at (870) 338-6474, ext. 1271. PCCUA is committed to providing a safe campus community. We will conduct criminal background checks and a sex offender registry check for applicants seeking employment. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Balancing, Crouching, Grasping, Hearing, Kneeling, Lifting, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Pulling, Pushing, Sharps, Stooping, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Garvan-Woodland-Gardens/Garvan-Gardens-Technology-Specialist_R0090557-1": {"title": "Garvan Gardens Technology Specialist", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com, then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at all University of Arkansas institutions will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students.\u201d University of Arkansas, Fayetteville students will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Student Jobs at UAF.\u201d All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. Closing Date: 09/09/2026 Type of Position: IT Support Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas, Fayetteville Founded in 1871, the University of Arkansas is a land grant institution, classified by the Carnegie Foundation among the nation\u2019s top 2 percent of universities with the highest level of research activity. The University of Arkansas works to advance the state and build a better world through education, research, and outreach by providing transformational opportunities and skills, fostering a welcoming climate, and nurturing creativity, discovery, and the spread of new ideas and innovations. The University of Arkansas campus is located in Fayetteville, a welcoming community ranked as one of the best places to live in the U.S. The growing region surrounding Fayetteville is home to numerous Fortune 500 companies and one of the nation\u2019s strongest economies. Northwest Arkansas is also quickly gaining a national reputation for its focus on the arts and overall quality of life. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10% of employee salary. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions, you should review before applying for the opening. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process, please submit a request via the Disability Accommodations | OEOC | University of Arkansas (uark.edu) : Request an Accommodation. Appli\u00adcants are required to submit a request for each position of which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 479.575.5351. Department: Computer Lab Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Located onsite in Hot Springs, Arkansas, the Garvan Gardens Technology Specialist is responsible for the administration, support, maintenance, and enhancement of technology systems that support daily operations, guest experiences, events, education programs, and business functions throughout Garvan Woodland Gardens. This position serves as the primary technology resource for staff and coordinates technology services across the Gardens, including computer systems, networking, audiovisual technology, security systems, telecommunications, and digital visitor engagement platforms. The Technology Specialist provides both strategic and hands-on technical support to ensure reliable, secure, and efficient technology services while promoting exceptional customer service for staff, visitors, volunteers, and event partners. This position reports to University IT Services and will work cross functionally across multiple teams at IT Services and coordinates support for Business Applications, Network Infrastructure, and IT Support when escalation is required. Additionally, this position may be required to do asset inventory and other duties as assigned. As a University of Arkansas, Fayetteville employee, minimal travel to Fayetteville will be required two to three times a year. Regular, reliable, and non-disruptive attendance is an essential job duty, as is the ability to create and maintain collegial, harmonious relationships with others. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications : \u00a0 The formal education equivalent of a technical degree from an accredited institution At least three years of computer support experience OR \u00a0 The formal education equivalent of a high school diploma At least five years of computer support experience \u00a0 Preferred Qualifications :\u00a0 \u00a0 Experience with device management software, such as KACE, SCCM, JAMF, Intune, or similar \u00a0 Experience providing customer support to stakeholders at all levels of an organization \u00a0 Experience with VBO or other ticketing software Experience with network infrastructure such as network switches or wireless access points\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 Knowledge, Skills, & Abilities: \u00a0 In-depth knowledge of Windows and Mac operating systems \u00a0 Strong customer service skills \u00a0 Strong written and verbal communication skills \u00a0 Ability to analyze computer system problems/errors and devise corrective measures \u00a0 Ability to read and interpret technical literature and documentation \u00a0 Additional Information: This position is located in-person in Hot Springs, AR and remote work is not offered. As a University of Arkansas, Fayetteville employee, minimal travel to Fayetteville will be required two to three times a year. \u00a0 Salary Information: $43,923 Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Proof of Veteran Status Recruitment Contact Information: Crystal Ellis, Strategic Talent Acquisition Specialist, ce031@uark.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Special Instructions to Applicants: Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas seeks to attract, develop and retain high quality faculty, staff and administrators that consistently display practices and behaviors to advance a culture that embeds equal opportunity, educational excellence and unparalleled access for all. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All Application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/RN---BHSL--CDU_R0090751-2": {"title": "RN - BHSL- Child Diagnostic Unit", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/11/2026 Type of Position: Clinical Staff - Nursing Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Night Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | BHSL Child PRI 5S IP C Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Registered Nurse (RN) in the Behavioral Health Service Line (BHSL) Child Diagnostic Unit (CDU). The CDU is a 10-bed unit that treats children ages 2 to 12 and represents a new approach in treatment for children with mental illness. The unit takes a multidisciplinary approach, relying on specialists in psychiatry, psychology, nursing, social work, and education as well as speech, language and occupational therapy. The staff uses a unique approach involving Collaborative Problem Solving (CPS) while working with the children to identify their individual needs based on how they interact with others. Once the patient is discharged, the institute staff will continue to follow the child to integrate the treatment plan with community-based caregivers. The RN delivers nursing care for patients in within the limits of the Nurse Practice Act of the State of Arkansas and adheres to institutional policies, procedures and standards. The RN is responsible to adhere to the standard of care defined by UAMS, ANA, and Standards for specialty patient population with support and mentoring by other team members. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Graduate of an accredited Nursing Program with Associate Degree, Nursing Diploma, Bachelor's in Nursing, or Master's in Nursing\u00a0 Valid RN License Minimum of 1 year Registered Nursing experience 1 year psychiatric experience Ability to pass Child Abuse and Neglect Registry check and State Police Background check \u200b Preferred Qualifications: 2 or more years nursing experience with current BLS Additional Information: Responsibilities: The Registered Nurse (RN) delivers nursing care for patients within the limits of the Nurse Practice Act of the State of Arkansas and adheres to institutional policies, procedures and standards. The RN is responsible to adhere to the standard of care defined by UAMS, ANA, and Standards for specialty patient population with support and mentoring by other team members. Collects and documents assessment data. Develops a Plan of Care (POC) per standard. Implements POC including medical order and interdisciplinary approach. Evaluates the progress of patient toward attainment of desired outcomes. Provides effective patient/family education/discharge planning. Administers medication per standard including drug information to patients/families. Acts as a resource/supports others. Delivers patient care using the principles of the defined nursing modality. Delegates care based on UAMS standards, legal and regulatory requirements, specific job description and individual level of education and training. Contributes to a positive work environment that is conducive to clinical education while serving as a resource for student nurses and staff. May perform other duties as assigned. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS Stand: Frequently Sit: Frequently Walk: Occasionally Bend, crawl, crouch, kneel, stoop or reach overhead: Frequently Lift and carry weight: 25 lbs Push and pull weight: 25 lbs Use hands to touch, handle or feel: Frequently Talk: Continuously Hear: Continuously Taste or smell: Occasionally Read, concentrate, think analytically: Continuously Physical Environment : Inside Medical Facility Environment Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Child Maltreatment, Criminal Background Check, Substance Abuse Testing This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Standing, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting Occasional Physical Activity: Kneeling, Lifting Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAMS/Administrative-Coordinator_R0090282-1": {"title": "Administrative Coordinator (TEMP)", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/19/2026 Type of Position: Professional Staff - Fiscal Affairs Job Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: CHP | Physician Assistant Studies Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: This is a temporary position. The Administrative Coordinator within the College of Health Professions reports directly to the Chair/Program Director and provides comprehensive administrative support to promote the efficient operation of the Physician Assistant Program. Key responsibilities include coordinating clinical education activities and student placements; supporting student recruitment and admissions; preparing and processing contracts and affiliation agreements; maintaining program records and databases; coordinating communication, scheduling, and reporting; and assisting with office equipment and inventories of educational, clinical, and office supplies. The position also prepares and processes work orders for facilities, telecommunications, and creative services. This position serves as a primary point of contact for the program and works collaboratively with students, faculty, clinical sites, preceptors, healthcare facilities, and institutional partners. Assignments are determined by the Chair/Program Director based on program and departmental needs. The College of Health Professions (CHP) serves Arkansas through education, service, and research in the allied health professions. As the only college of its kind within an academic health sciences center in Arkansas, CHP prepares highly qualified healthcare professionals to serve the state\u2019s healthcare delivery system. The College comprises ten academic departments offering programs in Audiology and Speech Pathology; Dental Hygiene; Dietetics and Nutrition; Genetic Counseling; Imaging and Radiation Sciences; Laboratory Sciences; Occupational Therapy; Physical Therapy; Physician Assistant Studies; and Respiratory Care. Qualifications: Bachelor\u2019s degree plus two (2) years or a high school diploma/GED plus six (6) years of administrative or related experience. Proficiency in Microsoft Office applications, including Outlook, Word, Excel, SharePoint, and Microsoft Forms. Strong organizational, problem-solving, and time-management skills, with the ability to manage multiple priorities and meet deadlines. Excellent written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills. Detail-oriented, self-directed, motivated, and able to work effectively both independently and as part of a team. Preferred Qualifications Three (3) years of experience providing administrative support in an executive or professional office environment. Additional Information: Responsibilities: Coordinating student clinical placements in collaboration with clinical sites, preceptors, healthcare facilities, and program faculty. Securing and maintaining required clinical experiences for students. Tracking affiliation agreements and maintaining supporting documentation. Maintaining clinical placement databases, student assignments, rotation records, evaluations, and required reports. Monitoring required documentation for students and clinical sites to ensure compliance with program, institutional, and accreditation requirements. Coordinating clinical schedules and communicating placement details to students, faculty, and preceptors. Assisting with the resolution of placement-related questions and concerns. Supporting clinical education meetings, orientations, and other activities necessary for successful clinical experiences. Preparing correspondence, letters, reports, and memoranda. Scheduling meetings, maintaining calendars, and preparing agendas and meeting materials. Maintaining departmental files and records. Processing purchasing and travel documentation. Assisting with the inventory of office and educational supplies. Supporting program events, accreditation activities, and other departmental operations. Performs additional duties and special projects as assigned to support the Physician Assistant Program. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding Frequent Physical Activity: Sitting, Standing, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Talking Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-Arkansas---Pulaski-Technical-College/Career-Coach_R0087510": {"title": "Career Coach", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 11/30/2026 Type of Position: Professional Staff - Project/Program Administration Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas Pulaski Technical College University of Arkansas - Pulaski Technical College at North Little Rock is an integral part of the Arkansas Technical and Community College System maintained by the State of Arkansas. The college is governed by the University of Arkansas System Board of Trustees and a seven-member Board of Visitors and derives its support largely from student tuition and fees and legislative appropriations. UA - Pulaski Tech, a comprehensive two-year college, offers associate degree and certificate programs for students who plan to transfer to four-year colleges and universities and/or for career preparation and advancement. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply link/button. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at (501) 812-2839. Department: JAG & Career Coach Program Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Career Coach reports to the Vice Chancellor for Enrollment Management at the University of Arkansas Pulaski Technical College and is responsible for providing services to students located at a Little Rock School District High School. This is a 12-month position. More information can be found by visiting uaptc.edu/career-coach General Responsibilities 1. Providing early outreach to low-income students with information about the importance of postsecondary education, as well as accurate information on how to prepare, apply, and pay for it. 2. Providing interest inventories and skills assessments to assist individuals in making informed career decisions. 3. Facilitating the development of individual career plans and portfolios. 4. Assisting students with enrolling in education or training programs. 5. Providing information on careers, career pathways, and educational requirements. Providing opportunities for job shadowing, mentoring, internships, visits to business and industry, and other career awareness activities. 6. Providing or connecting low-income students to support services that will ease the transition to postsecondary education. 7. Connecting educationally disadvantaged students to \u201cbridge programs\u201d that teach basic academic skills in the context of training for advancement to better jobs and postsecondary education. 8. Connecting students to academic enrichment activities such as study groups, tutoring, and workshops on study skills 9. Providing a continuum of career guidance to ease the transition from middle school to high school to postsecondary education or training and ultimately to the workplace. 10. Complete reporting related to student interaction, progression, and contacts. 11. Other duties may be assigned, which relate to the mission and goals of the Arkansas Works program. Qualifications: 1. Bachelor\u2019s degree required, master\u2019s degree preferred. 2. Experience in higher education or a public school environment is preferred. 3. Must be highly motivated and able to work with minimal direct supervision. 4. Excellent computer skills with a strong background in Word, PowerPoint, and Excel. 5. Must have excellent interpersonal and organizational skills and the ability to communicate effectively orally, in writing and in public presentation settings. 6. Background check required. Additional Information: Salary Information: $44,048 Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants Recruitment Contact Information: humanresources@uaptc.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Motor Vehicle Reports Check, Sex Offender Registry University of Arkansas - Pulaski Technical College is committed to providing a safe campus community. Title IX protects the college community from sexual harassment in a school's education programs and activities. This means that Title IX protects the college community in connection with all academic, educational, extracurricular, athletic, and other programs of the school, whether those programs take place in a school's facilities, in college transportation, at a class or training program sponsored by the school at another location, or elsewhere. \u00a0 We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Standing, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/RN---BHSL---PRN_R0090726-1": {"title": "RN - BHSL - PRN", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/11/2026 Type of Position: Clinical Staff - Nursing Job Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Shift Vary (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | BHSL PRN Clinical Staff Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Registered Nurse (RN) in the Behavioral Health Service Line (BHSL) consistently provides effective direct care to a variety of patients, will work as part of the interdisciplinary team, based on licensure, title and competencies. The RN seeks, as well as provides, feedback for improved clinical practice. The RN integrates theory and research into clinical practice. The RN provides leadership to members of the nursing team in order to maintain patient care standards. The RN works under the direct supervision of the Clinical Services Manager (CSM). Promotion is based on years of experience, satisfactory performance appraisals and recommendation by manager. Employee must successfully complete a UAMS-sponsored conflict management training to identify, prevent, and mitigate disruptive behaviors using methods such as non-escalation, de-escalation, personal protection from physical assaults, and physical alternatives within six months of hire. PRI Inpatient Units include the General Adult Inpatient Unit, the Women\u2019s Unit, the Child Diagnostic Unit, the off-campus Pulaski County Regional Crisis Stabilization Unit, and the Interventional Hospital-Based Clinic. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Graduate of an accredited nursing program with an Associate's Degree in Nursing, Nursing Diploma, Bachelor's Degree in Nursing, or Master's Degree in Nursing Minimum 1 year of Registered Nurse experience Current and valid Registered Nurse License in the State of Arkansas Excellent communication skills, basic computer skills, strong work ethic and accountability Preferred Qualifications: 2 or more years of Registered Nurse experience Current BLS Additional Information: Responsibilities: The Registered Nurse (RN) delivers nursing care for patients within the limits of the Nurse Practice Act of the State of Arkansas and adheres to institutional policies, procedures and standards. The RN is responsible to adhere to the standard of care defined by UAMS, ANA, and Standards for specialty patient population with support and mentoring by other team members. Collects and documents assessment data. Develops a Plan of Care (POC) per standard. Implements POC including medical order and interdisciplinary approach. Evaluates the progress of patient toward attainment of desired outcomes. Provides effective patient/family education/discharge planning. Administers medication per standard including drug information to patients/families. Acts as a resource/supports others. Delivers patient care using the principles of the defined nursing modality. Delegates care based on UAMS standards, legal and regulatory requirements, specific job description and individual level of education and training. Contributes to a positive work environment that is conducive to clinical education while serving as a resource for student nurses and staff. May perform other duties as assigned. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS Stand: Frequently Sit: Frequently Walk: Occasionally Bend, crawl, crouch, kneel, stoop or reach overhead: Frequently Lift and carry weight: 25 lbs Push and pull weight: 25 lbs Use hands to touch, handle or feel: Frequently Talk: Continuously Hear: Continuously Taste or smell: Occasionally Read, concentrate, think analytically: Continuously Physical Environment : Inside Medical Facility Environment Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Adult Maltreatment, Annual TB Screening, Child Maltreatment, Criminal Background Check, Substance Abuse Testing This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting Occasional Physical Activity: Kneeling, Lifting, Pulling, Pushing, Standing, Walking Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/RN---BHSL-Women-s-Unit_R0090701-1": {"title": "RN - BHSL-Women's Unit", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/11/2026 Type of Position: Clinical Staff - Nursing Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Night Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | BHSL Womens PRI 5N IP C Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Registered Nurse (RN) in the Behavioral Health service Line (BHSL) Women's Inpatient Unit consistently provides effective direct care to a variety of patients, will work as part of the interdisciplinary team, based on licensure, title and competencies. The RN seeks, as well as provides, feedback for improved clinical practice. The RN integrates theory and research into clinical practice. The RN provides leadership to members of the nursing team in order to maintain patient care standards. The RN works under the direct supervision of the Clinical Services Manager (CSM). Promotion is based on years of experience, satisfactory performance appraisals and recommendation by manager. Employee must successfully complete a UAMS-sponsored conflict management training to identify, prevent, and mitigate disruptive behaviors using methods such as non-escalation, de-escalation, personal protection from physical assaults, and physical alternatives within six months of hire. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Graduate of an accredited nursing program with an Associate's Degree in Nursing, Nursing Diploma, Bachelor's Degree in Nursing, or Master's Degree in Nursing Minimum 1 year of Registered Nurse experience Current and valid Registered Nurse license in the State of Arkansas Excellent communication skills, basic computer skills, strong work ethic and accountability Preferred Qualifications: 2 or more years of Registered Nurse experience Current BLS Additional Information: Job Requirements: The Registered Nurse (RN) delivers nursing care for patients within the limits of the Nurse Practice Act of the State of Arkansas and adheres to institutional policies, procedures and standards. The RN is responsible to adhere to the standard of care defined by UAMS, ANA, and Standards for specialty patient population with support and mentoring by other team members. Collects and documents assessment data. Develops a Plan of Care (POC) per standard. Implements POC including medical order and interdisciplinary approach. Evaluates the progress of patient toward attainment of desired outcomes. Provides effective patient/family education/discharge planning. Administers medication per standard including drug information to patients/families. Acts as a resource/supports others. Delivers patient care using the principles of the defined nursing modality. Delegates care based on UAMS standards, legal and regulatory requirements, specific job description and individual level of education and training. Contributes to a positive work environment that is conducive to clinical education while serving as a resource for student nurses and staff. May perform other duties as assigned. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS Stand: Frequently Sit: Frequently Walk: Occasionally Bend, crawl, crouch, kneel, stoop or reach overhead: Frequently Lift and carry weight: 25 lbs Push and pull weight: 25 lbs Use hands to touch, handle or feel: Frequently Talk: Continuously Hear: Continuously Taste or smell: Occasionally Read, concentrate, think analytically: Continuously Physical Environment : Inside Medical Facility Environment Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Adult Maltreatment, Annual TB Screening, Child Maltreatment, Criminal Background Check, Substance Abuse Testing This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Hearing Frequent Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Kneeling, Lifting, Reaching Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Medical-Laboratory-Scientist-I--Molecular-Biology_R0085391-1": {"title": "Medical Laboratory Scientist I- Molecular Biology", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/11/2026 Type of Position: Clinical Staff - Medical Ancillary Support Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | LPSL CPATH Molecular Biology Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Medical Laboratory Scientist in the Molecular Biology Laboratory will be responsible for performing a variety of Molecular based testing in PCR or FISH. This will include, but not limited to, processing and evaluating patient specimens, and performing, reviewing and documenting test results according to written procedures. In addition, the technologist will perform daily, weekly and monthly QC and preventative maintenance in their assigned areas for further review by the supervisor or Medical Director. This position requires one to maintain safe work practices, follow all regulatory requirements and procedures and engage supervisor, manager, and director as appropriate. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor of Science Degree in Medical Laboratory Sciences, Medical Technology, Cytotechnology, Molecular Biology or an ASCP approved discipline. ASCP Clinical Laboratory Scientist certification (CLS), Medical Technologist (MT) certification, Cytogenetics (CG) certification, Cytotechnologist (CT) certification or Molecular Biology (MB) certification passed within 24 months of hire. Preferred Qualifications: Previous clinical laboratory experience Additional Information: Job Responsibilities: Performs testing of patient samples in assigned FISH and/or PCR area, interprets, reviews and prepares patient test results. May or may not be trained on all benches but is progressively increasing in knowledge and experience. Interacts with staff from various departments to coordinate proper acquisition, testing and reporting of patient test results. Performs machine maintenance, calibrations, and troubleshoots problems as required. Ensures that the supplies used in the testing of patient samples are available in adequate quantities and that they are used efficiently. Maintains all aspects of QC and QA in assigned FISH area relevant to the CAP certification standards. \u00a0Special Projects and other duties as assigned. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS Stand: Frequently Sit: Frequently Walk: Occasionally Bend, crawl, crouch, kneel, stoop or reach overhead: Frequently Lift and carry weight: 25 lbs Push and pull weight: 25 lbs Use hands to touch, handle or feel: Frequently Talk: Continuously Hear: Continuously Taste or smell: Occasionally Read, concentrate, think analytically: Continuously Physical Environment : Inside Medical Facility Environment Noise Level : Moderate Visual Requirements: Color discrimination, Depth perception, Far visual acuity, Near visual acuity Hazards: Biological, Chemical, Dust, Electrical, Fumes/Gases/Odors, Radiation, Sharp objects/tools Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), Proof of Veteran Status, Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Criminal Background Check, Substance Abuse Testing This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: Feeling, Hearing, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Crawling, Crouching, Kneeling, Reaching, Stooping Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Clinical-Services-Manager_R0083198-1": {"title": "Clinical Services Manager - Behavioral Health Service Line", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/28/2026 Type of Position: Clinical Staff - Medical Services Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | BHSL Clinical Staff Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Behavioral Health Service Line (BHSL) Clinical Services Manager (CSM) is a clinical leadership position within the Psychiatric Research Institute (PRI) on the main UAMS campus. It is responsible for supervising and coordinating daily operations of the designated clinic/units, including patient care and clinic/unit business processes. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's Degree in Nursing (BSN) 5 or more years of experience in the field of Nursing, with 3 years nursing management/leadership experience (recent acute psychiatry experience preferred) Registered Nurse license in the state of Arkansas by the State Board of Nursing Strong interpersonal and communication skills, flexible, ability to independently problem solve Must possess strong leadership and mentoring abilities Preferred Qualifications: Master's Degree in Nursing (MSN) At least 5 years of nursing experience, and 3 years of nursing inpatient management/leadership experience (3 years of acute psychiatry experience) Scheduling for inpatient, knowledge and skill to interpret and apply clinical inpatient attendance policies Additional Information: Job Requirements: The CSM is responsible for leading, managing and mentoring 90+ inpatient staff. The CSM reports to the BHSL Senior Director of Nursing and is part of a team that supports the daily operations of the BHSL Adult Inpatient Unit and the Interventional Psychiatry Hospital-Based Outpatient Department. The CSM identifies problems impacting patient care activities and assists in the ongoing evaluation of the unit\u2019s goals for patient care. The CSM will attend meetings and participate on various BHSL and hospital committees and will be part of a team that ensures adherence to UAMS standards of patient care. Employees in this role may be fitted for, capable of donning and performing routine tasks in personal protective equipment to include N95 masks, Powered Air Purifying Respirators (PAPR) or Controlled Air Purifying Respirators (CAPR). Employee must successfully complete a UAMS-sponsored conflict management training (currently Level 2 & 3 Vistelar) to identify, prevent, and mitigate disruptive behaviors using methods such as non-escalation, de-escalation, personal protection from physical assaults, and physical alternatives within 6 months of hire. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Adult Maltreatment, Annual TB Screening, Child Maltreatment, Criminal Background Check, Substance Abuse Testing This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Standing, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting Occasional Physical Activity: Kneeling, Lifting, Pulling, Pushing Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Fiscal-Support-Analyst_R0090618-1": {"title": "Fiscal Support Analyst", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/12/2026 Type of Position: Accounting, Finance, Business Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: FIN | Finance SC Property Services Admin Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Fiscal Support Specialist maintains inventory, processes inventory asset records in FMS and Workday for the entire campus, and maintains an audit trail. This position loads data from FMS and Workday, runs inventory reports, analyzes asset data in the tracking system, and maintains data integrity, and researches queries for reports as needed. The successful candidate will review reports for Property officials to reflect their status. The Fiscal Support Specialist will perform data entry of inventory and assist with information for the internal automated tracking and reporting system or other appropriate systems after reviewing documents for accuracy. Qualifications: Associate's degree plus two (2) years of customer service experience required. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities: Computer, Typing, Microsoft Office. Knowledge of computers. Ability to analyze data and prepare reports. Knowledge of general accounting principles. Inventory Control Process. Responsibilities: Processes and maintains inventory records and reconciliation in FMS and Workday. Performs data entry of all assets\u2019 records. Completes a physical inventory for all departments on campus and off-campus sites. Performs other duties as assigned. Additional Information: Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: List of three Professional References (name, email, business title) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Criminal Background Check This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Driving, Hearing, Kneeling, N/A, Reaching, Sitting, Standing, Stooping, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Lifting Occasional Physical Activity: Climbing Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Fayetteville-AR/Research-Associate-or-Full-Professor--open-rank-_R0090652-1": {"title": "Research Associate or Full Professor (open rank)", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com, then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at all University of Arkansas institutions will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students.\u201d University of Arkansas, Fayetteville students will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Student Jobs at UAF.\u201d All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. Closing Date: 09/28/2026 Type of Position: Faculty - Non-Tenure Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Academic Term (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas, Fayetteville Founded in 1871, the University of Arkansas is a land grant institution, classified by the Carnegie Foundation among the nation\u2019s top 2 percent of universities with the highest level of research activity. The University of Arkansas works to advance the state and build a better world through education, research, and outreach by providing transformational opportunities and skills, fostering a welcoming climate, and nurturing creativity, discovery, and the spread of new ideas and innovations. The University of Arkansas campus is located in Fayetteville, a welcoming community ranked as one of the best places to live in the U.S. The growing region surrounding Fayetteville is home to numerous Fortune 500 companies and one of the nation\u2019s strongest economies. Northwest Arkansas is also quickly gaining a national reputation for its focus on the arts and overall quality of life. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10% of employee salary. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions, you should review before applying for the opening. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process, please submit a request via the Disability Accommodations | OEOC | University of Arkansas (uark.edu) : Request an Accommodation. Appli\u00adcants are required to submit a request for each position of which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 479.575.5351. Department: Supply Chain Management Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The J.B. Hunt Transport Department of Supply Chain Management in the Sam M. Walton College of Business at the University of Arkansas invites applications and nominations for a non-tenure-track research faculty position in Supply Chain Management, at the rank of Research Associate Professor or Research Professor, beginning August 16, 2027. Rank will be determined by the candidate\u2019s qualifications, experience, accomplishments, and demonstrated impact. This position is part of a coordinated faculty cluster hire in supply chain management focused on contested logistics and defense-relevant supply chain research. The department is concurrently recruiting multiple tenure-track and research faculty whose collective expertise will extend the University of Arkansas\u2019s leadership in contested logistics, military and defense logistics, and national security supply chains, in close partnership with the Contested Logistics Consortium and the Supply Chain Management Research Center (SCMRC). This cluster in contested logistics and supply chain aligns with one of the University\u2019s and College\u2019s key strategic priorities and builds critical mass in a high-importance academic and research domain. It advances the land-grant mission by connecting research, instruction, and outreach to pressing state and societal needs. This position is designed for a scholar-practitioner or research faculty member who can produce industry-relevant, analytically rigorous, and practically actionable research addressing important supply chain challenges facing companies, public-sector organizations, defense stakeholders, and broader society. The successful candidate will focus primarily on industry-engaged research, applied research translation, outreach, research partnership development, and practitioner-facing thought leadership, while contributing to the department and college\u2019s broader research, teaching, and service mission. A central emphasis of this role is research, translation, and engagement that directly supports military and defense logistics stakeholders, including activities associated with the Contested Logistics Consortium and Department of War-related research priorities. The department is especially interested in candidates who can bridge academic research, industry practice, and external engagement. Successful candidates should be capable of developing research outputs that may include practitioner journal articles, white papers, industry reports, research briefs, executive-facing insights, case studies, applied research projects, conference presentations, and, where appropriate, peer-reviewed academic publications. The ideal candidate will have the ability to translate complex research into insights useful to executives, policymakers, supply chain leaders, faculty colleagues, students, and external partners. This role is intentionally focused on industry-facing research and outreach. The successful candidate will help expand the department and Supply Chain Management Research Center\u2019s ability to identify and frame high-value supply chain research questions emerging from industry, government, defense, nonprofit, and public-sector partners, conduct applied research that is rigorous, credible, and useful to supply chain decision makers, translate research into practitioner-oriented publications, executive education content, industry briefings, workshops, and public thought leadership, build sustained relationships with corporate, public-sector, and professional partners, support externally engaged research initiatives that enhance the visibility, relevance, and impact of the department and Walton College, and collaborate with tenure-track faculty, clinical faculty, research center leaders, doctoral students, executives in residence, and external stakeholders. This position is intended to strengthen the department\u2019s capacity for externally engaged research, industry outreach, applied scholarship, and research translation. Regular on-campus availability, in-person teaching, and active contribution to the life of the department, including exhibiting respect and cooperation in shared academic and administrative tasks are essential duties. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Doctoral degree in supply chain management, logistics, operations management, or a closely related field completed by the position start date Demonstrated ability to conduct high-quality research related to supply chain management, logistics, operations, analytics, or a closely related domain U.S. citizenship, due to access to export-controlled information, restricted federal data, and security-sensitive research environments Demonstrated record of developing and securing externally sponsored research funding, or an exceptional record of senior military or defense logistics leadership and accomplishment Preferred Qualifications: Experience leading large-scale research initiatives, external partnerships, outreach programs, or multidisciplinary research efforts Demonstrated record of producing practitioner-oriented research outputs, such as white papers, industry reports, executive briefs, applied research studies, case studies, benchmarking reports, or practitioner journal articles Experience designing and facilitating industry workshops, executive briefings, roundtables, conferences, webinars, or professional education programs Professional experience in supply chain management, logistics, transportation, procurement, retail, manufacturing, defense logistics, public-sector logistics, analytics, consulting, technology, or related fields An active U.S. security clearance, or eligibility to obtain and maintain one Significant military, defense logistics, or national security supply chain experience Knowledge, Skills and Abilitie s (KSAs): Strong written and oral communication skills, including the ability to translate complex ideas for practitioners and executive audiences Ability to work collaboratively with faculty, staff, students, industry partners, and external stakeholders Ability to collaborate with tenure-track faculty on research projects that may contribute to peer-reviewed academic publications Ability to contribute to the mission of a research-oriented business school and a highly engaged supply chain, business, and university faculty Additional Information: This position is a Designated Research Position \u00a0and is regulated by the Arkansas Research Education Protection Act of 2025 .\u00a0 Prior to issuance of an offer of employment, the University is required to request and obtain additional information about an applicant\u2019s background and, if required, conduct an additional review of that background information. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Recruitment Contact Information: Marc Scott Assistant Chair Department of Supply Chain Management MScott@walton.uark.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Special Instructions to Applicants: Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas seeks to attract, develop and retain high quality faculty, staff and administrators that consistently display practices and behaviors to advance a culture that embeds equal opportunity, educational excellence and unparalleled access for all. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All Application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Fayetteville-AR/Assistant-Professor_R0090609-1": {"title": "Assistant Professor (Two Open Positions)", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com, then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at all University of Arkansas institutions will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students.\u201d University of Arkansas, Fayetteville students will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Student Jobs at UAF.\u201d All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. Closing Date: 08/28/2026 Type of Position: Faculty - Tenure/Tenure Track Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas, Fayetteville Founded in 1871, the University of Arkansas is a land grant institution, classified by the Carnegie Foundation among the nation\u2019s top 2 percent of universities with the highest level of research activity. The University of Arkansas works to advance the state and build a better world through education, research, and outreach by providing transformational opportunities and skills, fostering a welcoming climate, and nurturing creativity, discovery, and the spread of new ideas and innovations. The University of Arkansas campus is located in Fayetteville, a welcoming community ranked as one of the best places to live in the U.S. The growing region surrounding Fayetteville is home to numerous Fortune 500 companies and one of the nation\u2019s strongest economies. Northwest Arkansas is also quickly gaining a national reputation for its focus on the arts and overall quality of life. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10% of employee salary. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions, you should review before applying for the opening. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process, please submit a request via the Disability Accommodations | OEOC | University of Arkansas (uark.edu) : Request an Accommodation. Appli\u00adcants are required to submit a request for each position of which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 479.575.5351. Department: Supply Chain Management Department's Website: https://walton.uark.edu/departments/supplychain/ Summary of Job Duties: The J.B. Hunt Transport Department of Supply Chain Management in the Sam M. Walton College of Business at the University of Arkansas invites applications and nominations for two tenure-track Assistant Professor positions in Supply Chain Management, beginning August 16, 2027. These positions are part of a coordinated faculty cluster hire in supply chain management focused on contested logistics and defense-relevant supply chain research. The department is concurrently recruiting multiple tenure-track and research faculty whose collective expertise will extend the University of Arkansas\u2019s leadership in contested logistics, military and defense logistics, and national security supply chains, in close partnership with the Contested Logistics Consortium and the Supply Chain Management Research Center (SCMRC). This cluster in contested logistics and supply chain aligns with one of the University\u2019s and College\u2019s key strategic priorities and builds critical mass in a high-importance academic and research domain. It advances the land-grant mission by connecting research, instruction, and outreach to pressing state and societal needs. This is a research-focused faculty position for a scholar with strong potential to publish high-impact, theoretically rigorous, and managerially relevant research in leading peer-reviewed supply chain management, logistics, operations, and business journals. The successful candidate will be expected to contribute to the department\u2019s continued research excellence, teach undergraduate and graduate courses, engage meaningfully with students and doctoral candidates, and participate in service activities consistent with rank and career stage. The department is especially interested in candidates whose research addresses important supply chain challenges facing firms, industries, public institutions, and society. Areas of interest may include, but are not limited to resilience, risk, supply chain visibility, analytics, technology-enabled supply chains, defense and critical infrastructure supply chains, global networks, inventory and distribution systems, disruption management, and the interface between commercial and public-sector logistics systems. Consistent with the cluster hire strategy, the department has particular interest in candidates whose research directly addresses military logistics, contested logistics, and defense supply chain challenges, with opportunities to engage with the Contested Logistics Consortium and military and defense stakeholders. Candidates should demonstrate potential to produce research that is publishable in premier academic journals, with that research also generating insights that can inform industry practice, practitioner-oriented publications, executive audiences, and applied research partnerships. The position is aligned with the department\u2019s broader commitment to academically excellent, industry-relevant scholarship and the Walton College\u2019s distinctive access to leading companies, entrepreneurial ventures, public-sector partners, and supply chain innovators. Regular on-campus availability, in-person teaching, and active contribution to the life of the department, including exhibiting respect and cooperation in shared academic and administrative tasks are essential duties. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: A completed Ph.D. in supply chain management, logistics, operations management, or a closely related field from an AACSB-accredited business school or equivalent accredited institution completed by the position start date Demonstrated record or strong potential to publish research in top-tier supply chain management, logistics, operations, or business journals Evidence of research that has potential relevance for both academic journals and practitioner audiences Candidates must meet standards to be classified as a Scholarly Academic for AACSB purposes U.S. citizen, due to access to export-controlled information, restricted federal data, and security-sensitive research environments Preferred Qualifications: Strong research record and demonstrated leadership roles in research projects that result in top-tier journal publications Strong pipeline of research including manuscripts under second or third revision at top tier supply chain management journals Experience teaching courses related to logistics, procurement, transportation, operations, analytics, or supply chain strategy Research interests related to resilience and risk, supply chain visibility, analytics, robotics and automation, technology-enabled supply chains, defense and critical infrastructure supply chains, the interface between commercial and public-sector logistics systems, or other areas of strategic industry importance Industry work experience in supply chain management, logistics, operations, analytics, transportation, procurement, retail, manufacturing, defense, or related field An active U.S. security clearance, or eligibility to obtain and maintain one Significant military, defense logistics, or national security supply chain experience Knowledge, Skills and Abilities (KSAs): High-quality oral and written communication skills Ability to work collaboratively and collegially as a contributing member of a research-active faculty team Ability to engage with industry professionals, firms, public-sector organizations, or applied research partners Ability to teach in face-to-face, hybrid/blended, online, graduate, executive, or professional education formats Additional Information: This position is a Designated Research Position \u00a0and is regulated by the Arkansas Research Education Protection Act of 2025 .\u00a0 Prior to issuance of an offer of employment, the University is required to request and obtain additional information about an applicant\u2019s background and, if required, conduct an additional review of that background information. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Recruitment Contact Information: Marc Scott Assistant Chair Sam M. Walton College of Business MScott@walton.uark.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Special Instructions to Applicants: Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas seeks to attract, develop and retain high quality faculty, staff and administrators that consistently display practices and behaviors to advance a culture that embeds equal opportunity, educational excellence and unparalleled access for all. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All Application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Fayetteville-AR/Assistant-or-Associate-Professor--Open-Rank-_R0090606-2": {"title": "Assistant or Associate Professor (Open Rank)", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com, then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at all University of Arkansas institutions will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students.\u201d University of Arkansas, Fayetteville students will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Student Jobs at UAF.\u201d All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. Closing Date: 09/28/2026 Type of Position: Faculty - Tenure/Tenure Track Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas, Fayetteville Founded in 1871, the University of Arkansas is a land grant institution, classified by the Carnegie Foundation among the nation\u2019s top 2 percent of universities with the highest level of research activity. The University of Arkansas works to advance the state and build a better world through education, research, and outreach by providing transformational opportunities and skills, fostering a welcoming climate, and nurturing creativity, discovery, and the spread of new ideas and innovations. The University of Arkansas campus is located in Fayetteville, a welcoming community ranked as one of the best places to live in the U.S. The growing region surrounding Fayetteville is home to numerous Fortune 500 companies and one of the nation\u2019s strongest economies. Northwest Arkansas is also quickly gaining a national reputation for its focus on the arts and overall quality of life. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10% of employee salary. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions, you should review before applying for the opening. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process, please submit a request via the Disability Accommodations | OEOC | University of Arkansas (uark.edu) : Request an Accommodation. Appli\u00adcants are required to submit a request for each position of which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 479.575.5351. Department: Supply Chain Management Department's Website: https://walton.uark.edu/departments/supplychain/ Summary of Job Duties: The J.B. Hunt Transport Department of Supply Chain Management in the Sam M. Walton College of Business at the University of Arkansas invites applications and nominations for a tenure-track Assistant or Associate Professor position in Supply Chain Management, beginning August 16, 2027. This position is designed for an outstanding scholar whose research advances knowledge in supply chain management. Candidates at the Assistant Professor level should have demonstrated a record of publications in leading peer-reviewed journals and evidence of a sustained pipeline of research. Candidates at the Associate Professor level should have an established record of high-quality scholarship, evidence of a strong research pipeline, a pattern of accomplishments consistent with progress toward a national or international reputation, and qualifications consistent with AACSB Scholarly Academic expectations. Regular on-campus availability, in-person teaching, and active contribution to the life of the department, including exhibiting respect and cooperation in shared academic and administrative tasks are essential duties. Departmental service activities commensurate with tenure and rank are expected. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: A completed Ph.D. in supply chain management, logistics, operations management, or a closely related field from an AACSB-accredited business school or equivalent accredited institution by the position start date conferred by the start of employment Demonstrated record of published research in top-tier supply chain management, logistics, operations, or business journals Demonstrated ability or potential to teach supply chain management courses effectively at the undergraduate or graduate level. Candidates must meet standards to be classified as a Scholarly Academic for AACSB purposes Preferred Qualifications A strong research record and demonstrated leadership roles in research projects that result in top-tier journal publications Strong pipeline of research including manuscripts under second or third revision at top tier supply chain management journals Experience teaching courses related to logistics, procurement, transportation, operations, analytics, or supply chain strategy. Research interests related to resilience and risk, supply chain visibility, analytics, robotics and automation, technology-enabled supply chains, defense and critical infrastructure supply chains, the interface between commercial and public-sector logistics systems, or other areas of strategic industry importance Industry work experience in supply chain management, logistics, operations, analytics, transportation, procurement, retail, manufacturing, or related fields Knowledge, Skills and Abilities (KSAs): High-quality oral and written communication skills Ability to work collaboratively and collegially as a contributing member of a research-active faculty team Ability to teach in face-to-face, hybrid/blended, online, graduate, executive, or professional education formats Demonstrated record of engagement with industry professionals, firms, public-sector organizations, or applied research partners Additional Information: Department and College Context \u00a0 The J.B. Hunt Transport Department of Supply Chain Management in the Sam M. Walton College of Business at the University of Arkansas is nationally recognized for research, teaching, industry engagement, and innovation in supply chain education is nationally recognized for research, teaching, industry engagement, and innovation in supply chain education. In 2020, 2022, and 2024 the supply chain undergraduate program was ranked #1 in North America by Gartner. As a result of its success in high quality and industry relevant integrated supply chain management education and collaborative industry partnerships the department was named the J.B. Hunt Transport Department of Supply Chain Management in 2022. Candidates should aspire to contribute to the college and department\u2019s goals to promote a rich educational environment and promote industry-relevant, applied, experiential pedagogy for learners. \u00a0 The department offers educational programming across undergraduate, graduate, executive, and doctoral levels and has built a strong reputation for high-quality, industry-relevant, integrated supply chain management education. The Walton College and the department benefit from a unique location in Northwest Arkansas, a business ecosystem that is home to major global companies including Walmart, Tyson Foods, and J.B. Hunt, and near other major business centers across the region. \u00a0 J.B. Hunt Transport Department of Supply Chain Management consistently ranks in the top five departments for empirical supply chain research as ranked by the SCM Journal List rankings http://www.scmlist.com/home/scm-journal-list-endorsers/university-rankings/ .In addition, our faculty, and doctoral students, have received best paper awards from journals and conferences, serve in editorial positions at numerous top journals, and have held leadership positions in the Journal of Business Logistics and the Journal of Supply Chain Management . \u00a0 The University of Arkansas is home to the Contested Logistics Consortium, which brings together defense practitioners, industry partners, and academic researchers to address logistics problems involving resilience, sustenance, degraded networks, operationally grounded talent, AI-enabled decision support, robotics and automation, transportation resilience, cybersecurity, network operations, and related capabilities. Candidates with research interests that could naturally complement these kinds of supply chain challenges are encouraged to apply. \u00a0 \u00a0 The Sam M. Walton College of Business, founded at the University of Arkansas in 1926 and accredited by AACSB International since 1931, has been ranked as a top 30 public business school for over 15 years in a row by U.S. News & World Report. U.S. News currently ranks Walton College 25th. Four Walton College graduates serve as CEOs of Fortune 500 companies and nearly 30 Walton alumni occupy executive offices at Fortune 500 companies. In 1998, the Walton Family Charitable Support Foundation gave the Walton College an endowment of $50 million, at that time the single largest up-front cash gift to a business school. The college has experienced strong growth in enrollment over the past several years (over 19% increase since fall 2022). Fall 2025 enrollment in the Walton College of Business included over 9500 undergraduate and 780 graduate students .\u00a0 The Walton College of Business is located on a four-building business campus including the Business Building, housing most undergraduate and Ph.D. education, Willard J. Walker Hall, home of our graduate programs, the Donald W. Reynolds Center for Enterprise Development and the J.B. Hunt Transport Center for Academic Excellence, site of our state-of-the-art behavioral research lab. A fifth building, Mandy and Bill Dillard II Hall, will break ground in summer of 2027.\u00a0 \u00a0 For more information about the Sam M. Walton College and the Northwest Arkansas area: https://walton.uark.edu/about/ \u00a0 Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Recruitment Contact Information: Marc Scott Assistant Chair Department of Supply Chain Management Sam M. Walton College of Business MScott@walton.uark.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Special Instructions to Applicants: Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas seeks to attract, develop and retain high quality faculty, staff and administrators that consistently display practices and behaviors to advance a culture that embeds equal opportunity, educational excellence and unparalleled access for all. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All Application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-Arkansas-Fayetteville/Coordinator-of-Facilities-and-Risk-Management_R0090613": {"title": "Coordinator of Facilities and Risk Management", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com, then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at all University of Arkansas institutions will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students.\u201d University of Arkansas, Fayetteville students will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Student Jobs at UAF.\u201d All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. Closing Date: 09/17/2026 Type of Position: Facilities Management and Services Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas, Fayetteville Founded in 1871, the University of Arkansas is a land grant institution, classified by the Carnegie Foundation among the nation\u2019s top 2 percent of universities with the highest level of research activity. The University of Arkansas works to advance the state and build a better world through education, research, and outreach by providing transformational opportunities and skills, fostering a welcoming climate, and nurturing creativity, discovery, and the spread of new ideas and innovations. The University of Arkansas campus is located in Fayetteville, a welcoming community ranked as one of the best places to live in the U.S. The growing region surrounding Fayetteville is home to numerous Fortune 500 companies and one of the nation\u2019s strongest economies. Northwest Arkansas is also quickly gaining a national reputation for its focus on the arts and overall quality of life. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10% of employee salary. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions, you should review before applying for the opening. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process, please submit a request via the Disability Accommodations | OEOC | University of Arkansas (uark.edu) : Request an Accommodation. Appli\u00adcants are required to submit a request for each position of which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 479.575.5351. Department: Facility Operations Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Coordinator of Facilities and Risk Management will support the daily operations of the UREC Natatorium. This role involves overseeing the recruitment, training, and supervision of over 30 part-time student staff members in areas such as risk management, customer service, and facility inspections. The coordinator will manage the swim lesson program, including registration, finances, updates, and ensuring adherence to national standards. This position also assists with budget management for the UREC Natatorium and swim lesson program, while overseeing pool operations, including aquatic reservations and events. Regular, reliable, and non-disruptive attendance is an essential job duty, as is the ability to create and maintain collegial, harmonious working relationships with others. Responsibilities: 60% Facility Operations: Develop, supervise, and evaluate over 20 student staff in part-time positions. Develop and enforce policies and procedures within facilities including program and staff manuals. Manage equipment, operations, and maintenance for all the UREC Natatorium. Oversee swim meet management and aquatic reservations. Ensure up to date maintenance of all equipment, preventative maintenance, and repair needs. 20% Programming: Develop, supervise, and evaluate 10 swim lesson instructors. Oversees the quality and success of the swim lesson program. 20% Administration: Prepare, forecast, and monitor all annual income and expenses for pool operations and swim lesson program including payroll and maintenance. Maintain comprehensive participation and program records for activity, semester, and annual reporting. Be knowledgeable with program and departmental software application and website maintenance. Assess risk management and maintain program compliance. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications A Bachelor\u2019s degree in recreation, sport management, higher education, or related field from an accredited institution of higher education \u00a0 At least one year experience in recreation, collegiate/recreational sports, gym or pool operations \u00a0 Experience supervising part-time staff \u00a0 Preferred Qualifications A Master\u2019s degree in recreation, sport management, higher education, or related field from an accredited institution of higher education \u00a0 At least two-year's experience in recreation, collegiate/recreational sports, gym or pool operations American Red Cross Water Safety Instructor certification \u00a0 American Red Cross Lifeguard certification \u00a0 Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities:\u00a0 \u00a0 Knowledge of facility operations \u00a0 Knowledge of applicable codes and standards related to pools and facilities \u00a0 Knowledge of facility programming \u00a0 Ability to obtain Red Cross Lifeguard Certification \u00a0 Ability to obtain Certified Pool Operator (CPO) or Aquatic Facility Operator (AFO) Certification Ability to obtain Red Cross Lifeguard Instructor Certification \u00a0 Ability to obtain water safety instructor certification \u00a0 Additional Information: Salary Information: $46,383 (Commensurate with education and experience) Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Recruitment Contact Information: Katherine Belcher, Assistant Director, UREC Outdoors, kgmiller@uark.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Special Instructions to Applicants: Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Motor Vehicle Reports Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas seeks to attract, develop and retain high quality faculty, staff and administrators that consistently display practices and behaviors to advance a culture that embeds equal opportunity, educational excellence and unparalleled access for all. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All Application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Sitting, Standing Occasional Physical Activity: Kneeling, Lifting, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAM--Crossett-Campus/Extra-Help---Faculty_R0090697-1": {"title": "Extra Help - Faculty", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Adjunct Faculty Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Monticello UAM, one of twenty campuses of the University of Arkansas System, is located in southeastern Arkansas in the beautiful timberlands, rich in outdoor recreation activities, and approximately 100 miles south of Little Rock. UAM is a comprehensive, residential and commuter, undergraduate institution also offering selected master\u2019s degree programs. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please submit a request via the OEOC website: \u00a0Applicants are required to submit a request for each position to which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 870-460-1422 . Department: College of Technology-Crossett Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Instructor will help with tutoring, study skills, and deliver other instruction as needed to PN students. Will work as needed under the supervision of the Director of the PN program. Qualifications: Must be a licensed RN in good standing with the state of Arkansas with at least 5 years nursing experience in clinical settings. Additional Information: Salary Information: $28.00 per hour Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Dr. Tracy Tucker, Vice Chancellor UAM-CTC (870) 460-2027 TuckerTS@uamont.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAM--Crossett-Campus/Non-Student-Extra-Help--Clinical-Supervisor-_R0090724-1": {"title": "Non-Student Extra Help (Clinical Supervisor)", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Clerical Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Monticello UAM, one of twenty campuses of the University of Arkansas System, is located in southeastern Arkansas in the beautiful timberlands, rich in outdoor recreation activities, and approximately 100 miles south of Little Rock. UAM is a comprehensive, residential and commuter, undergraduate institution also offering selected master\u2019s degree programs. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please submit a request via the OEOC website: \u00a0Applicants are required to submit a request for each position to which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 870-460-1422 . Department: College of Technology-Crossett Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Extra Help-Clinical Supervisor is responsible for providing skilled or unskilled labor or performing basic tasks in a state agency or institution. This position is governed by state and federal laws and agency policy. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications Additional Information: Salary Information: $28.00 per hour Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), Resume, Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Dr. Tracy Tucker, Vice Chancellor UAM-CTC (870) 460-2027 TuckerTS@uamont.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAM--Monticello-Campus/Non-Student-Extra-Help--Athletic-Training-_R0090718-1": {"title": "Non-Student Extra Help (Athletic Training)", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Clerical Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Monticello UAM, one of twenty campuses of the University of Arkansas System, is located in southeastern Arkansas in the beautiful timberlands, rich in outdoor recreation activities, and approximately 100 miles south of Little Rock. UAM is a comprehensive, residential and commuter, undergraduate institution also offering selected master\u2019s degree programs. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please submit a request via the OEOC website: \u00a0Applicants are required to submit a request for each position to which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 870-460-1422 . Department: Athletic Trainer Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Assist in training room with paperwork and treatment of athletes. Qualifications: Must be organized and self motivated. Additional Information: Salary Information: $11.00/hour Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Shellye Byrd Head Athletic Trainer 870-460-1658 All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: No Background Check Required The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Standing, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Standing, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Lifting Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAFS--University-of-Arkansas-Fort-Smith/PT-Women-s-Basketball-Assistant-Coach_R0090423": {"title": "PT Women's Basketball Assistant Coach", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Professional Staff - Assistant Coach Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Fort Smith University of Arkansas \u2013 Fort Smith The University of Arkansas - Fort Smith is a dynamic, mid-sized public university that\u2019s redefining higher education. We\u2019re on a mission to provide transformative, hands-on learning experiences for students of all backgrounds and aspirations. Our multi-faceted approach to education offers a wealth of opportunities, with over 70 academic programs, including certificates, associate, bachelor\u2019s, and master\u2019s degrees. We\u2019re committed to building a diverse community that mirrors Arkansas\u2019s rich tapestry, reflecting our dedication to serving the state\u2019s varied population while enhancing the quality of our institution. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life, and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10 percent of employee salary. \u00a0 Fort Smith, Arkansas Nestled along the Arkansas River, this vibrant city offers a perfect blend of history, culture, and natural beauty. Immerse yourself in the rich heritage of the Old West at the Fort Smith National Historic Site, explore the eclectic local art scene, or take a scenic stroll along the picturesque riverfront trails. With a welcoming community, diverse dining options, and a thriving downtown, Fort Smith is the ideal destination for history enthusiasts and those seeking modern amenities. Thank you for your interest in joining our university. Below you will find details for the position including any supplementary documentation and/or questions you should review before submitting your application. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at (479) 788-7080. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 479-788-7080. Applicants are required to submit a request for each position to which they have applied. Department: Women's Basketball Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Assist with the management and administration of an effective and efficient basketball program. The position reports to the head women\u2019s basketball coach. Qualifications: Required Education and/or Work Experience: Minimum qualifications: verifiable experience coaching basketball. Essential Job Duties and Responsibilities: \u00b7 Responsible for all aspects of practice and game preparation as directed by head coach \u00b7 Responsible for overseeing all aspects of game day operations. Coordinate all travel operations. Manage all administrative duties for the program \u00b7 Assist in the recruitment of players by identifying and assessing talent, communicating with prospective student athletes. Coordinate with respective departments for on campus visits \u00b7 Responsible for academic supervision of players and communication with academic advisor and Faculty Athletic Representative. Assist in academic accountability for student athletes with measurable outcomes available. \u00b7 Responsible for building good relationships with players, faculty, staff, donors and the community. Monitoring possible disciplinary situations, serving as a liaison between players and head coach \u00b7 Game film coordinator. Breakdown and analyzation of game/practice for education sessions to head coach and to student athletes \u00b7 Assist in scheduling practices coordination and coordinating with opposing teams for game day oversight. \u00b7 Responsible for student athlete development projects. Ex: meetings to invest in the holistic environment for setting student athletes up for success and accountability. Providing resources outside of on the court coaching practice and game day teaching \u00b7 Oversee and create all social media content for all women\u2019s basketball social media platforms. Other Job Duties and Responsibilities: \u00b7 Other duties as assigned. Responsible for maintaining a positive work atmosphere by acting and communicating in a manner to foster teamwork and by providing leadership to subordinates. Requires consistent on-time attendance. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: To perform the job successfully, the following competencies are required for the essential functions of this position: \u00b7 Knowledge of all aspects of the game of basketball. \u00b7 Familiarity with university policies regarding athletics, Division II basketball programs, MIAA Conference rules, and NCAA rules and regulations. \u00b7 Successful completion of the NCAA coach\u2019s test. Additional Information: Working Relationships: Work in a dynamic team of diverse faculty, staff, and students in a fast paced, growth-oriented collegiate environment. Frequent contact required with basketball boosters, personnel from other agencies and institutions and the general public. List Employees Supervised: Student managers Special Job Dimensions: Frequent travel and extended hours required. Coaches may be called upon to assist with fundraising for the athletic department and to provide staff support to the other sports programs during their respective seasons. Valid driver\u2019s license required. Background Check Requirements . Background check required Salary Information: $17141.25 Required Documents to Apply: List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume, Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: HR 479-788-7080 All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position may be subject to a pre-employment criminal background check, sex offender registry check, financial history background check, and/or drug screening. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication and/or adverse financial history alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background checks and drug screening information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Talking Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-Arkansas-at-Pine-Bluff/Associate-for-Administration_R0090641-1": {"title": "Associate for Administration", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Professional Staff - Project/Program Administration Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff The University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff is an 1890 Land-Grant HBCU with a diverse student population, competitive degree offerings and stellar faculty. For more than 140 years, the University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff has worked to create an environment that inculcates learning, growth and productivity while affording a basic need to its students \u2013 a chance to advance. The 15:1 student to teacher ratio makes it possible to maintain a learning environment with close interaction between students and faculty while challenging curricula encourage our students to seek and fulfill their potential. You can excel in your chosen field of study through a curriculum of \u00a0 Certificate and Associates degree programs,\u00a0 more than thirty\u00a0 Undergraduate programs, Master\u2019s degree programs and a Doctorate program in Aquaculture/Fisheries. You can also develop workplace readiness through internships, co-ops and fellowships in the U.S. and abroad. Out-of-class experiences and student involvement include more than 90 student organizations, an internationally renowned Vesper Choir, Marching Band, Concert Bands, Wind Symphony, nationally recognized debate team, award-winning theater department and accomplished athletic program. Though the main campus is in Pine Bluff, its reach is worldwide. UAPB has an extended campus in North Little Rock and offers as well as online courses. With the addition of the Arkansas Research and Education Optical Network (ARE-ON), students can engage in information exchange with others anywhere in the world. There are also Research and Extension offices in Lonoke, Newport and Lake Village and collaborations with other colleges and universities in the State through the National Science Foundation funded STEM (Science, Technology, Engineering and Mathematics) Academy. As the second oldest land-grant institution in the state of Arkansas, the mission of this No Excuse University remains the same \u2013 to provide a high quality, affordable education with a personal touch. We invite you to Become a Part of the Pride at the University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process and require reasonable accommodations, please contact Human Resources at 870.575.8400 . Department: COS | Chief of Staff Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Office of the Chancellor is seeking a highly organized, dynamic, and team-oriented candidate for the position of **Associate for Administration**. The successful candidate will provide comprehensive administrative support to the Office of the Chancellor and will be responsible for performing a full range of confidential administrative and support activities. Responsibilities include welcoming and assisting guests, answering and directing telephone calls, managing incoming and outgoing email correspondence, and receiving, sorting, logging, and distributing daily incoming mail and deliveries. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: 1.\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Bachelor\u2019s degree\u00a0 2.\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Strong background in customer service, in person and by phone.\u00a0 3.\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Demonstrated reliability. 4.\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Five years of clerical, secretarial, administrative support experience\u00a0 5.\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0 Demonstrated word-processing and computer training and expertise in MS Office, including Excel spreadsheets, Word, Outlook, PowerPoint, as well as Outlook and web applications 6.\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Exceptional organizational skills and an ability to resolve routine office problems professionally, efficiently, effectively, and independently. 7.\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Strong written and oral communication skills with the ability to interact effectively with internal and external constituents 8.\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Strong interpersonal skills and work ethic 9.\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Ability to work under tight deadlines, manage multiple assignments efficiently, and effectively work independently with minimum supervision 10.\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Highest levels of discretion, diplomacy, flexibility, collegiality, and care in dealing with complex and sensitive governance matters and engaging effectively with board members and senior university officers, public officials, and the general public \u00a0 Preferred Qualifications 5 years of administrative experience in higher education. Essential Duties: 1.\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Provide a professional, helpful, welcoming atmosphere and a positive attitude for faculty, staff, students, families, callers, and visitors of the Office of the Chancellor.\u00a0 2.\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Provide coverage for the front desk including on behalf of the staff.\u00a0 3.\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Assists in the development of information needed for calendar events for the Chancellor\u2019s calendar. 4.\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Safeguards the confidentiality of University administration by exercising discretion in communicating information to faculty, students, staff, and the various publics served by the University and in handling administrative records, files, and similar confidential items. 5.\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Receive, sort, log, and distribute daily incoming mail and deliveries.\u00a0 6.\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Arranges efficient and cost-effective official travel for the Chancellor and other official visitors by making travel arrangements and preparing associated approval forms and expense reports for travelers. 7.\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Coordinate staff recognition materials and events; coordinate receptions and social functions, and meetings for the Chancellor with the Vice-Chancellors and other staff. 8.\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Responds to concerns and complaints from employees, students, and the public; discusses with the Chief of Staff or Chancellor as necessary, and implements timely solutions as appropriate. 9.\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Prepares a variety of materials as requested and which may be sensitive, privileged, and highly confidential, either independently or as directed. 10.\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Assists in performing routine office tasks and may act as a back-up to the chancellor\u2019s office staff in work overloads and their absence, as needed, or requested. 11.\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Facilitates the work of the Office of the Chancellor by distributing and keeping accurate records of documents requiring the Chancellor\u2019s signature.\u00a0 12.\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Serves as a liaison between the department and other University offices 13.\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Order, receive, and maintain office supplies; anticipate supply needs and ensure that supplies will be available. 14.\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0May represent the Chancellor or Chief of Staff to other University offices, the public outside, the public or outside agencies in administrative matters; 15.\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Performs other duties as assigned. \u00a0 Additional Information: Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience. Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of five Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants (Please upload all required documents in the \"Resume\" attachment section of your application to be considered for this position) : Recruitment Contact Information: Sharron Williams Employment Manager williamssm@uapb.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: The University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff may conduct pre-employment background checks on certain positions for applicants being considered for employment. \u00a0 The background checks may include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. \u00a0 Required checks are identified in the position listing. \u00a0 A criminal background check or arrest pending adjudication information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absences of a relationship to the requirements of the position. \u00a0 Background check information will be used in a consistent, non-discriminatory manner consistent with the state and federal law. \u00a0 The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/RN---Head-and-Neck-Oncology-Clinic_R0090725-1": {"title": "RN - Head and Neck Oncology Clinic", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/27/2026 Type of Position: Clinical Staff - Nursing Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | CASL CA Head-Neck Clinic Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Registered Nurse (RN) will provide direct patient care as a Clinic RN. This professional nursing role will require the ability to coordinate care for patients, triage patients, and work collaboratively with clinic providers, fellows, and staff. Requires the ability to effectively work with patient referral sources, facilitate appointments, coordinate transitions of care, and provide patient education on complex conditions. The RN will work with the individual patient, their families, and providers of care to develop and implement individual health plans. Come work with our wonderful group of Physician's at the UAMS Cancer Institute. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor\u2019s degree in Nursing, Associate\u2019s degree in Nursing, Diploma RN, or Master\u2019s degree in Nursing. Must be a graduate of an accredited RN nursing program Minimum of 1 year of Registered Nursing experience Valid Registered Nursing License Excellent communication skills. Strong work ethic and accountability Basic computer skills. Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor\u2019s degree in Nursing Oncology Nursing Experience Current BLS National Nursing Certification Additional Information: Responsibilities: Collects and documents assessment data from patients and/or others per UAMS standard.\u00a0 Develops patient's Plan of Care (POC) per department/unit standards utilizing assessment data.\u00a0 Evaluates the progress of patients toward attainment of desired outcomes. Administers medication following department/unit standards and Nurse Practice Act.\u00a0 Verifies and evaluates care delivered to ensure it is consistent with patient and family centered care principles, practice standards and regulatory requirements. Supports the integration of current evidence into nursing practices.\u00a0 Promotes an environment conducive to positive educational experience for all students and staff.\u00a0 Provides effective patient/family education/discharge planning. Effectively collaborates and communicates with nursing staff at all levels, interdisciplinary teams, executive leaders, and other stakeholders.\u00a0 Communicates care appropriately through documentation in the medical record. Reports variances in care/ systems/ processes through the appropriate means.\u00a0 Participates in recruitment/retention of staff.\u00a0 Facilitates development and implementation of nursing practice standards that are evidence-based and in compliance with ANA standards. May perform other duties as assigned. Salary Information: commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Criminal Background Check, Substance Abuse Testing This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Kneeling, Lifting, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Repetitive Motion, Standing, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Balancing, Feeling, Grasping, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Sharps Occasional Physical Activity: Crouching Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Searcy/RN-PRN---Kids-First---Searcy--AR_R0090615-1": {"title": "RN PRN \u2013 Kids First \u2013 Searcy, AR", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 10/03/2026 Type of Position: Clinical Staff - Nursing Job Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: COM | Peds Kids First Searcy Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: *This position is located in Searcy, Arkansas* The RN (PRN) provides clinical nursing care for children enrolled in local KIDS FIRST clinics. Acts as a clinical resource for clinic staff. Qualifications: Graduate of an accredited Nursing Program with an Associate's degree, Nursing diploma, Bachelor's in Nursing, or Master's in Nursing Valid RN License Minimum of 2 years of Registered Nursing experience or 2 years of clinical nursing experience Knowledge, Skills & Abilities: Excellent communication skills. Basic computer skills. Strong work ethics and accountability. Preferred Qualifications: BSN or MSN with three (3) or more years of nursing experience. Pediatric Care experience. Current BLS. Responsibilities: Implements the nursing process to manage patient care problems of a complex and changing nature as demonstrated by documentation and observation. Assumes accountability and responsibility for all aspects of care for the assigned group of patients, with respect for developmental level and age-specific issues. Administers medications and treatments and performs procedures according to UAMS and KIDS FIRST policies. Evaluates children to identify signs of illness or injury and intervenes appropriately. Maintains current and accurate records and ensures confidentiality. Teaching/learning needs of patients and families are identified, addressed, and documented.\u00a0 Acts as a resource for staff in the areas of health, safety, and infection control.\u00a0 Assumes responsibility for acquiring knowledge and experience to meet professional goals. Develops and maintains close working relationships with the clinic director, the Medical Director, nursing managers, the clinic nurse, and other team members.\u00a0 Actively works with contacts to coordinate care and promote referrals to the program.\u00a0\u00a0 Collaborates with KIDS FIRST staff, PCPs, UAMS resources, and others to implement and revise plan of care as needed.\u00a0\u00a0 Provides employment documentation such as annual TB screening, CPR /nursing license renewal verification, etc., promptly. Performs other duties as assigned. Additional Information: Salary Information: $38.00/hr. Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), Proof of Veteran Status, Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Adult Maltreatment, Child Maltreatment, Criminal Background Check, FBI Background Check, Sex Offender Registry This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Climbing, Crawling, Crouching, Grasping, Kneeling, Lifting, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Repetitive Motion, Standing, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Sitting Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Hot-Springs/Operations-Technician---Garvan-Woodland-Gardens_R0090451-1": {"title": "Operations Technician \u2013 Garvan Woodland Gardens", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com, then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at all University of Arkansas institutions will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students.\u201d University of Arkansas, Fayetteville students will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Student Jobs at UAF.\u201d All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. Closing Date: Type of Position: Staff - Clerical Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Shift Vary (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas, Fayetteville Founded in 1871, the University of Arkansas is a land grant institution, classified by the Carnegie Foundation among the nation\u2019s top 2 percent of universities with the highest level of research activity. The University of Arkansas works to advance the state and build a better world through education, research, and outreach by providing transformational opportunities and skills, fostering a welcoming climate, and nurturing creativity, discovery, and the spread of new ideas and innovations. The University of Arkansas campus is located in Fayetteville, a welcoming community ranked as one of the best places to live in the U.S. The growing region surrounding Fayetteville is home to numerous Fortune 500 companies and one of the nation\u2019s strongest economies. Northwest Arkansas is also quickly gaining a national reputation for its focus on the arts and overall quality of life. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10% of employee salary. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions, you should review before applying for the opening. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process, please submit a request via the Disability Accommodations | OEOC | University of Arkansas (uark.edu) : Request an Accommodation. Appli\u00adcants are required to submit a request for each position of which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 479.575.5351. Department: Holiday Lights Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Garvan Woodland Gardens, one of top attractions in Arkansas is hiring! We are looking for positive, motivated, personable new team members to join our crew. Work outdoors in a setting voted in the top 10 most colorful places on the planet by Trip Advisor. We would love for you to come grow with us! Garvan Woodland Gardens, a 210-acre botanical garden situated on a peninsula surrounded by scenic Lake Hamilton located in Hot Springs, AR is seeking a skilled and dedicated Operations Technician. The Operations Technician is responsible for assisting in multiple departments as needed. The Operations Technician will assist with the Special Events team, providing technical support, as well as aide in the set-ups of the spaces. This position will also assist with Holiday Lights set-up, disassembly, repair, inventory records, fabrication, etc. of Holiday Lights Display materials. In addition, this position will be an assistant to the Building Maintenance team as required. This temporary position will be for up to 40 hours a week; this is a temporary position that will require work outside in the elements regardless of weather. This position will require evening and weekend work. Working hours will shift during the Holiday Light season to include night work. Pay $13-15 per hour based on experience and skill level. Operations Technician is a part-time, temporary position limited to the 1250-hour University of Arkansas policy. The campus is a non-smoking facility. This position requires a valid driver\u2019s license. Regular, reliable, and non-disruptive attendance is an essential job duty, as is the ability to create and maintain collegial, harmonious working relationships with others. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 High School Diploma or equivalent \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Valid Driver\u2019s License \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Background Checks Required: Criminal Background Check, Motor Vehicle Report Check, Sex Offender Registry \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Must be able to lift 50 pounds \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 No previous experience required, as individuals will be trained on site Preferred Qualifications: \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Experience working in a public garden \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Experience with electrical, electronic, lighting, sound, or welding Additional Information: Graduate Students are subject to background check Salary Information: $13.00 to $15.00 per hour Required Documents to Apply: None Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Recruitment Contact Information: Leslie Pounds, HR Partner, pounds@uark.edu; Minnie Hahn, Sr Manager of Design, minnie@uark.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Special Instructions to Applicants: Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Motor Vehicle Reports Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas seeks to attract, develop and retain high quality faculty, staff and administrators that consistently display practices and behaviors to advance a culture that embeds equal opportunity, educational excellence and unparalleled access for all. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All Application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Lifting, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Repetitive Motion, Standing, Stooping, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Balancing, Crouching, Feeling, Grasping, Hearing, Kneeling, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Talking Occasional Physical Activity: Climbing, Crawling, Driving, Sharps, Sitting Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Helena-Campus/Dance-Asst_R0086216-1": {"title": "Dance Asst.", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Adjunct Faculty Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Less than Annual Appointment (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: Phillips Community College of the University of Arkansas The first community college established in Arkansas, Phillips Community College of the University of Arkansas (PCCUA) is a multi-campus, two-year college serving Eastern Arkansas. PCCUA has academic, occupational/technical and continuing education programs and offers over 25 associate degree programs with campuses in DeWitt, Helena-W. Helena and Stuttgart. Thank you for your interest, and we hope you\u2019ll be joining our Ridge Runner family soon! Below you will find the details for the position as well as any specific application requirements you should review before applying for this opening. To apply for this position, please click the Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process, please call Human Resources at (870) 338-6474, ext. 1271. Department: Community Service Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Assist dance instructors 3-4 days a week or as needed. Qualifications: 5 years of dance experience Additional Information: Salary Information: commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: None Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Wandra Williams All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: For general application assistance, or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at (870) 338-6474, ext. 1271. PCCUA is committed to providing a safe campus community. We will conduct criminal background checks and a sex offender registry check for applicants seeking employment. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Fayetteville-AR/Career-Consultant_R0090503-2": {"title": "Career Consultant", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com, then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at all University of Arkansas institutions will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students.\u201d University of Arkansas, Fayetteville students will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Student Jobs at UAF.\u201d All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. Closing Date: 09/11/2026 Type of Position: Career Services Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas, Fayetteville Founded in 1871, the University of Arkansas is a land grant institution, classified by the Carnegie Foundation among the nation\u2019s top 2 percent of universities with the highest level of research activity. The University of Arkansas works to advance the state and build a better world through education, research, and outreach by providing transformational opportunities and skills, fostering a welcoming climate, and nurturing creativity, discovery, and the spread of new ideas and innovations. The University of Arkansas campus is located in Fayetteville, a welcoming community ranked as one of the best places to live in the U.S. The growing region surrounding Fayetteville is home to numerous Fortune 500 companies and one of the nation\u2019s strongest economies. Northwest Arkansas is also quickly gaining a national reputation for its focus on the arts and overall quality of life. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10% of employee salary. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions, you should review before applying for the opening. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process, please submit a request via the Disability Accommodations | OEOC | University of Arkansas (uark.edu) : Request an Accommodation. Appli\u00adcants are required to submit a request for each position of which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 479.575.5351. Department: Career Center Undergraduate Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Career Consultants in Walton Career Connections provide guidance, coaching, programming, and education to Walton students through consulting, collaboration with employers, and identification of industry trends. Career Consultants will be responsible for managing a portfolio of undergraduate and graduate students, collaborating with team and academic departments regarding programming, and tracking outcomes. In coordination with the Senior Director for Career Services, the Career Consultants will develop strategies to grow opportunities for students in diverse industries and locations, ensuring alignment with academic and career goals. Must be able to provide in-person support of programming/events during office hours, Monday-Friday 8am-5pm, and occasional evenings and weekends, less than 10 evenings or weekends a semester. Regular, non-disruptive, and in-person, reliable attendance is an essential job duty, as well as the ability to create and maintain collegial, harmonious working relationships with others. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in business, marketing, human resources, or related field from an accredited institution of higher education At least two years of professional work experience that includes recruiting or career development for corporate functions (such as finance, accounting, marketing, sales, operations, Consumer Packaged Goods (CPG), etc.) or relevant recruiting experience for corporate clients in related functional areas Experience with business education (specifically within Accounting and Finance; Marketing, Sales, Supply Chain Management and CPG; Human Resource Management and Entrepreneurship; Economics and Information Systems; and MBA and Specialty Master\u2019s Programs) Experience with resume writing, interviewing and job search skills Experience with web-based resources, spreadsheet and presentation software required (MS Word, PowerPoint, Outlook and Excel) Preferred Qualifications: Master\u2019s degree in business, marketing, human resources or related field from an accredited institution of higher education Experience with pivot tables in Excel for data analysis Experience with Applicant Tracking Systems, Learning Management Systems (e.g., Canvas) and/or Career Services platforms (e.g., Handshake, etc.) Experience working with students in a higher education environment Knowledge, Skills and Abilities (KSAs): Knowledge of project management Knowledge of job search and process management Demonstrated ability to establish and maintain effective rapport with students, alumni, and recruiters Excellent oral and written communications Ability to develop effective presentations and speak confidently to large audiences Ability to coach and motivate others Ability to build rapport quickly, to listen actively, to adapt to changing situations Additional Information: Salary Information: $63,000 Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Recruitment Contact Information: Heather Wilson Lead Career Consultant Walton College of Business hwilson8@uark.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Special Instructions to Applicants: Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas seeks to attract, develop and retain high quality faculty, staff and administrators that consistently display practices and behaviors to advance a culture that embeds equal opportunity, educational excellence and unparalleled access for all. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All Application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Fayetteville-AR/Career-and-Internship-Connections-Coordinator_R0090586-1": {"title": "Career and Internship Connections Coordinator", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com, then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at all University of Arkansas institutions will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students.\u201d University of Arkansas, Fayetteville students will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Student Jobs at UAF.\u201d All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. Closing Date: 09/11/2026 Type of Position: Administrative Operations and Support Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas, Fayetteville Founded in 1871, the University of Arkansas is a land grant institution, classified by the Carnegie Foundation among the nation\u2019s top 2 percent of universities with the highest level of research activity. The University of Arkansas works to advance the state and build a better world through education, research, and outreach by providing transformational opportunities and skills, fostering a welcoming climate, and nurturing creativity, discovery, and the spread of new ideas and innovations. The University of Arkansas campus is located in Fayetteville, a welcoming community ranked as one of the best places to live in the U.S. The growing region surrounding Fayetteville is home to numerous Fortune 500 companies and one of the nation\u2019s strongest economies. Northwest Arkansas is also quickly gaining a national reputation for its focus on the arts and overall quality of life. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10% of employee salary. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions, you should review before applying for the opening. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process, please submit a request via the Disability Accommodations | OEOC | University of Arkansas (uark.edu) : Request an Accommodation. Appli\u00adcants are required to submit a request for each position of which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 479.575.5351. Department: Career Center Undergraduate and Student Programs Support Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: In support of Walton Career Connections, the Career and Internships Connections Coordinator provides coordination and administrative support for internships and broader career-related opportunities. This role supports the administration of academic internship courses, including oversight of the application and approval processes for BUSI 3100V \u2013 Internship and BUSI 3200V \u2013 International Internships. The Coordinator maintains internship-related content and resources across Career Connections platforms, ensuring accurate, timely, and student-centered information. The Coordinator also contributes to reporting efforts and continuous improvement of Career Connections initiatives. The Internship Coordinator will also assist in planning and executing events, programs, and official functions hosted by Career Connections. Regular, non-disruptive, and reliable attendance is an essential job duty, as well as the ability to create and maintain collegial, harmonious working relationships with others. This position will require office hours of 8am-5pm, Monday-Friday, with in-person support of programming/events during office hours and occasionally nights and weekends. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor\u2019s Degree from an accredited institution of higher education Experience providing administrative support in a professional office setting Preferred Qualifications: At least one year experience working with students in higher education setting. Experience in the field of career services and/or recruitment. Experience working with a Customer Relationship Management system. At least six months of higher education experience Knowledge, Skills and Abilities (KSAs): Strong interpersonal, organizational and administrative skills Strong computer skills in particular Microsoft Office Ability to work independently and with collaborative teams. Additional Information: Salary Information: $41,000 Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Recruitment Contact Information: Lindsey Steiger-Muck Senior Director of Walton Career Connections and Industry Relations Sam M. Walton College of Business LSteiger-Muck@walton.uark.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Special Instructions to Applicants: Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas seeks to attract, develop and retain high quality faculty, staff and administrators that consistently display practices and behaviors to advance a culture that embeds equal opportunity, educational excellence and unparalleled access for all. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All Application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Fayetteville/Walton-Classroom-Tech-Support_R0090488-2": {"title": "Walton Classroom Tech Support", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com, then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at all University of Arkansas institutions will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students.\u201d University of Arkansas, Fayetteville students will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Student Jobs at UAF.\u201d All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. Closing Date: 09/11/2026 Type of Position: Staff - Clerical Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas, Fayetteville Founded in 1871, the University of Arkansas is a land grant institution, classified by the Carnegie Foundation among the nation\u2019s top 2 percent of universities with the highest level of research activity. The University of Arkansas works to advance the state and build a better world through education, research, and outreach by providing transformational opportunities and skills, fostering a welcoming climate, and nurturing creativity, discovery, and the spread of new ideas and innovations. The University of Arkansas campus is located in Fayetteville, a welcoming community ranked as one of the best places to live in the U.S. The growing region surrounding Fayetteville is home to numerous Fortune 500 companies and one of the nation\u2019s strongest economies. Northwest Arkansas is also quickly gaining a national reputation for its focus on the arts and overall quality of life. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10% of employee salary. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions, you should review before applying for the opening. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process, please submit a request via the Disability Accommodations | OEOC | University of Arkansas (uark.edu) : Request an Accommodation. Appli\u00adcants are required to submit a request for each position of which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 479.575.5351. Department: Finance and Administration Hourly Support Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Classroom Technology Support Technician provides frontline support for classroom technology in WCOB, WJWH, RCED, JBHT, BREW, and the McMillon Studio in HAPG. This is a hands-on role ideal for current university students who are reliable, tech-savvy, and comfortable assisting faculty and instructors in live classroom settings. Technicians are responsible for ensuring technology in classrooms functions properly and for providing in-person assistance with audiovisual, projection, and computer systems when issues arise. Full training and ongoing support will be provided \u2014 no prior technical experience is necessary, just a willingness to learn and the confidence to help on the spot. Hours of Operation: \u2022Monday, Wednesday, Friday: 7:00 AM \u2013 8:45 PM \u2022Tuesday, Thursday: 7:30 AM \u2013 8:45 PM \u2022Optional: 1 Saturday per month to support Walton professional program classes Key Responsibilities: \u2022Respond promptly to in-class technology issues during scheduled hours \u2022Troubleshoot common classroom technology problems (e.g., projectors, classroom PCs, microphones, and display systems) \u2022Assist instructors in operating AV or computing equipment \u2022Perform basic checks of classroom tech setups to ensure functionality before and between classes \u2022Communicate unresolved technical problems to full-time support staff or escalate as necessary \u2022Maintain a professional and helpful presence in classroom environments \u2022Document incidents and support activities using provided reporting tools \u2022Provide front office reception support \u2022Support faculty and staff computers including new setup and troubleshooting existing issues as they arise \u2022Other duties as assigned Regular, reliable, and non-disruptive attendance is an essential job duty, as is the ability to create and maintain collegial, harmonious working relationships with others. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Currently enrolled in the University of Arkansas, Fayetteville Comfortable entering classrooms during active sessions and providing in-the-moment support Reliable, punctual, and professional demeanor Strong communication and interpersonal skills Basic familiarity with computers and AV equipment is helpful, but not required Ability to learn and apply new technical knowledge quickly through training Must be able to navigate between buildings and classrooms during assigned shifts Available to commit to at least 1 opening shift per week Additional Information: Salary Information: $14.00 per hour Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: Recruitment Contact Information: Christy Wade, christyw@uark.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Special Instructions to Applicants: Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas seeks to attract, develop and retain high quality faculty, staff and administrators that consistently display practices and behaviors to advance a culture that embeds equal opportunity, educational excellence and unparalleled access for all. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All Application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Law-Enforcement-Instructor_R0069342-1": {"title": "Law Enforcement Advancement Instructor", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: Criminal Justice Institute The Criminal Justice Institute (CJI) is a campus of the\u00a0University of Arkansas System\u00a0that serves a unique population of non-traditional students\u2014certified law enforcement professionals who are actively employed within our State\u2019s police departments and sheriff\u2019s offices. The Institute is committed to making communities safer by supporting law enforcement professionals through training, education, resources and collaborative partnerships. Utilizing both classroom-based instruction and practical, hands-on application, CJI provides an educational experience designed to enhance the performance and professionalism of law enforcement in progressive areas of criminal justice, including law enforcement leadership and management, crime scene investigation, computer applications, traffic safety, illicit drug investigations and school safety.\u00a0\u00a0 If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process or have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-570-8021.\u00a0 Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. Department: Operations Department's Website: www.cji.edu Summary of Job Duties: The Criminal Justice Institute\u2019s Law Enforcement Instructor is responsible for increasing student learning through: 1. The development of a relevant and progressive curriculum to enhance the knowledge, skills, and abilities of Arkansas law enforcement professionals by providing leadership and management courses customized to meet the dynamic and unique challenges of law enforcement across the State. 2. The design and implementation of effective learning strategies and environments. 3. Delivering high-quality instruction and presenting lesson plans on scheduled class days in an engaging and well-communicated manner. 4. Supporting various learning styles by providing several strategies for consuming the same content (ex: slides, lecturing, videos, and/or readings). 5. Providing students with additional support and guidance when asked. 6. Adjusting course outlines on an annual basis to ensure information is up-to-date and relevant. Qualifications: Instructor Qualifications: \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Subject Matter Expert in the area of instruction. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Previous instructional experience. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0At least five years\u2019 experience in the [either law enforcement/criminal justice industry/field or school administration] and/or field of instruction. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Satisfactory background check (certified law enforcement and school administrators excluded). \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Agreement of terms and conditions of Lecturer/Instructor employment agreement. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Ability to travel to instruction site. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0A minimum of an Associate\u2019s is required for all degree program courses. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Other job-related education and/or experience may be substituted for all or part of these basic requirements upon approval of the Director of the Criminal Justice Institute. \u00a0 \u00a0 Additional Information: Instructor Core Skills: Organization Interpersonal communication Instructor-led training Subject matter expert Time management Cultural sensitivity Engagement Mentoring Presentation skills Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience. Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Carol Waddle Associate Director 501-570-8021 cdwaddle@cji.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: The Criminal Justice Institute is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check is required. Required checks are identified in the position listing. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Diagnostic-Radiology-Technologist---TOSH-Urology-Clinic_R0090716-1": {"title": "Diagnostic Radiology Technologist - TOSH/Urology Clinic", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/27/2026 Type of Position: Clinical Staff - Medical Ancillary Support Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | IGSL Outpatient Clinic TOSH/UROLOGY Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: This position produces radiographic images for medical interpretation, interacts with all healthcare staff, many clerical staff members, all patient care departments and with patient's families and visitors. This position is held accountable for performing the correct radiologic exams and producing high quality images while supervising others. This position will work at TOSH and Urology clinics. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Graduate of an approved Radiology program Registered or eligible by the American Registry of Radiologic Technologist Licensed by the State of Arkansas in Radiology Technology Additional Information: Responsibilities: Prepares patients for procedures by reviewing medical history, draping and positioning the patient, preparing procedural/testing sites, including necessary supplies and equipment, and administering contrast media and/or medications within the scope of practice. Assists the physician with performing diagnostic and therapeutic vascular interventional procedures, such as flushing catheters. Maintains knowledge of all products and their use; and performs related imaging procedures, including fluoroscopy (FL). Analyzes results and takes appropriate action to resolve image quality issues, including quality assurance (QA), sending images, and pixel shifting. Educates patient regarding procedures, equipment, and exam to ensure patient's understanding and cooperation, and helps monitor patient condition, reporting and responding to changes as appropriate Ensures that supplies and equipment are stocked and in proper working order. Implements safety standards and performs appropriate quality control procedures on equipment by troubleshooting, resolving, and reporting equipment malfunctions as necessary. Performs other duties as assigned. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Criminal Background Check, Substance Abuse Testing This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Feeling, Grasping, Hearing, Lifting, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Repetitive Motion, Sharps, Sitting, Standing, Stooping, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Crouching, Feeling, Grasping, Hearing, Lifting, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Repetitive Motion, Sitting, Standing, Stooping, Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Balancing, Climbing, Crawling, Feeling, Grasping, Hearing, Kneeling, Lifting, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Repetitive Motion, Sitting, Standing, Stooping, Talking, Walking Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Diagnostic-Radiology-Technologist---TOSH-Pain-Clinic_R0090714-1": {"title": "Diagnostic Radiology Technologist - TOSH Pain Clinic", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/27/2026 Type of Position: Other Health Care - Medical Ancillary Support Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | IGSL Outpatient Clinic TOSH/UROLOGY Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: This position produces radiographic images for medical interpretation, interacts with all healthcare staff, many clerical staff members, all patient care departments, and with patients' families and visitors. This position is held accountable for performing the correct radiologic exams and producing high-quality images while supervising others. This position will work at the Orthopedic and Spine Hospital Pain Clinic. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Graduate of an approved Radiology Technology program Registered or eligible by the American Registry of Radiologic Technologists Licensed by the State of Arkansas in Radiology Technology Additional Information: Responsibilities: Prepares patients for procedures by reviewing medical history, draping and positioning the patient, preparing procedural/testing sites, including necessary supplies and equipment, and administering contrast media and/or medications within the scope of practice. Assists the physician with performing diagnostic and therapeutic vascular interventional procedures, such as flushing catheters. Maintains knowledge of all products and their use; and performs related imaging procedures, including fluoroscopy (FL). Analyzes results and takes appropriate action to resolve image quality issues, including quality assurance (QA), sending images, and pixel shifting. Educates patient regarding procedures, equipment, and exam to ensure patient's understanding and cooperation, and helps monitor patient condition, reporting and responding to changes as appropriate Ensures that supplies and equipment are stocked and in proper working order. Implements safety standards and performs appropriate quality control procedures on equipment by troubleshooting, resolving, and reporting equipment malfunctions as necessary. Performs other duties as assigned. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Criminal Background Check, Substance Abuse Testing This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Repetitive Motion, Sitting, Standing, Stooping, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Feeling, Grasping, Kneeling, Lifting, Pulling, Pushing Occasional Physical Activity: Climbing, Crawling, Crouching Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAMS/Senior-Grants-Administrator_R0088870-2": {"title": "Senior Grants Administrator", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/18/2026 Type of Position: Management - Operations Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: COM | Peds Accounting Office Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Senior Grants Administrator is a professional staff-level position in the Department of Pediatrics. The incumbent will provide leadership, content expertise and professional concepts in accordance with Grants/Costs Accounting processes, UAMS policies and procedures, State laws, and Federal regulations to solve complex problems effectively. Oversees the processing of post-award grant activities to include, but not limited to, award setup, financial reporting, invoicing, effort reporting, and other grant-related responsibilities. Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in business or related\u00a0field\u00a0plus seven (7) years of experience as a Grants Administrator or equivalent required. Minimum of three (3) years of experience in financial management of sponsored programs or related. Knowledge of Microsoft Office. Preferred Qualifications: Master\u2019s degree in business or related field. Knowledge of federal agency policies in 2 CFR 200. Seven (7) plus years of experience in grants and costs accounting at an IHE. RACC Certified Research Administrator (CRA). Strong Excel skills. Responsibilities: Manage payroll allocations, journal entries and accounting adjustments, payroll accounting adjustments, monthly report preparation and review, and grant budget management for the Department of Pediatrics. Oversee the full grant cycle, including attending kick off meetings and close out meetings. Collaborates with Arkansas Children\u2019s Research Institute, Grants Accounting Office, and Administrators to manage grants and awards. Prepares/reviews complex and detailed documents, reports, and/or related materials. Prepares complex analysis to assist the Director of Finance & Peds administration team for compliance decision-making. Shares leadership for advanced complex reports and events (i.e., Uniform Guidance audit, financial compliance reviews, NSF Survey, SEFA, F&A proposal development) through proper understanding of requested data and determining the most effective way to prepare and present that information in a report format or as requested. Manage the effective closeout of awards in accordance with Federal and State requirements. Use critical thinking and problem-solving skills to effectively manage large cash transactions. Adept at navigating complex electronic environments for the purpose of effective cash management. Makes independent judgments. Influences the resolution of complex issues to achieve outcomes and resolve issues. Reviews complex contracts and legal documents and negotiate to an acceptable resolution regarding financial compliance. Reviews subcontracts, amendments and modifications to provide subject matter expertise. Works both independently or within a complex structured team. Ability to understand user needs, requirements and requests to identify priorities; manage and resolve urgent and/or conflicting requests. Collegial interpersonal skills and an ability to communicate effectively in person, writing, and by phone. Skilled in establishing, nurturing, and maintaining effective professional working relationships. Knowledge and understanding of multiple unit objectives/goal with ability to work effectively across boundaries involving potential conflicts. Interprets guidelines and explains financial compliance/regulatory requirements as needed. Meets with department leadership and provides training to faculty and staff as needed. Works one-on-one with department and specific researchers when needed. May determine methods and procedures on new assignments and provide guidance. Exercises judgment within broadly defined practices & policies in selecting methods, techniques & evaluation criteria for obtaining results. Supervisory review of results and objectives. Serves as liaison to management on policies, plans, and objectives. Interacts with senior internal and external personnel on significant technical matters. Performs other duties as assigned. \u00a0 Additional Information: Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Substance Abuse Testing This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-Arkansas-Community-College-at-Batesville/Extra-Help--Testing-Proctor_R0090686": {"title": "Extra Help -Testing Proctor", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. Closing Date: Type of Position: Staff - Clerical Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas Community College at Batesville The University of Arkansas Community College at Batesville (UACCB) is a comprehensive community college committed to providing learning experiences that improve the lives of those we serve. UACCB provides affordable access to technical education and college transfer programs that meet the diverse higher education needs of the citizens of north central Arkansas. \u00a0 These programs are provided to the traditional college student as well as to high school students through a state approved Secondary Area Career Center. \u00a0 The College also promotes economic development and an enhanced quality of life for the community through adult education, developmental education, customized business and industry training, and continuing education programs. UACCB's mission is to provide quality educational opportunities within a supportive learning environment. We promote success through community partnerships, responsive programs, and an enduring commitment to improvement. Thank you for your interest. \u00a0 We hope you will be joining us soon! After reviewing the Job Duties and Qualifications listed below, click the Apply button at the top of the page to begin the application process. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process or for general application assistance, please contact the Human Resource Office at (870) 612-2045. Department: Access and Testing Services Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Proctor exams for UACCB courses Be available for a mix of day, evening, and possibly Saturday to work. Maintain FERPA and other privacy rules that apply to student information and test information. Maintain privacy of information seen on Blackboard regarding student information, grades, exam and quiz information and any other information such as but not limited to passwords and login information. Communicate clearly to supervisor and students who are testing. If students have concerns about the test that only the instructor can answer, call and/or email the instructor. If you are aware that accommodations such as extra time or a screen reader should be provided to a student and the student states it is NOT showing this, ask the student to NOT start the test and you should contact the instructor ASAP. Other accommodations may also apply. These should be confirmed by the instructor. Caring Campus Responsibilities: As a member of the UACCB community, each employee is responsible for advancing the Caring Campus culture to enhance student connection and success and to embody the campus purpose: Improve Lives. Key duties include adhering to the campus name badge policy, treating all visitors as guests, engaging with the campus community by reviewing institutional communications, participating in campus events, and supporting a collaborative, positive workplace environment. Communicate with your supervisor, ASAP if you will not be able to proctor during a certain time period. If communication is by email, make sure you get a reply or contact the next person listed to notify. Confirm your work schedule each week with your supervisor. Enter time worked in WorkDay on the 15th and 30th of each month, or at the end of each week. For testing violations, notify the instructor via email as soon as possible, the day of the test. Any irregularities should be emailed to the instructor and supervisor Qualifications: Qualifications \u00a0 Required: ability to communicate verbally and in writing with others; attention to detail; experience with computers and Microsoft Word and Excel; able to work independently and follow instructions. Must be comfortable with using computers and have problem-solving skills Preferred: \u00a0 associate's or bachelor's \u00a0 degree from an accredited institution; experience with Blackboard or other student learning management system; has proctoring experience \u00a0 Additional Information: Salary Information: $15.00/Hr Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Human Resources hr@uaccb.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Child Maltreatment, Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry UACCB is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check for all applicants.\u00a0 Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Feeling, Lifting, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Repetitive Motion Occasional Physical Activity: Climbing, Crouching Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Fayetteville-AR/Post-Doctoral-Fellow-Researcher---Robotics--Advanced-Manufacturing-and-Materials-Innovation--12-MONTH_R0090037-1": {"title": "Post Doctoral Fellow Researcher - Robotics, Advanced Manufacturing and Materials Innovation- 12 MONTH", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com, then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at all University of Arkansas institutions will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students.\u201d University of Arkansas, Fayetteville students will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Student Jobs at UAF.\u201d All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. Closing Date: 09/07/2026 Type of Position: Researchers Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas, Fayetteville Founded in 1871, the University of Arkansas is a land grant institution, classified by the Carnegie Foundation among the nation\u2019s top 2 percent of universities with the highest level of research activity. The University of Arkansas works to advance the state and build a better world through education, research, and outreach by providing transformational opportunities and skills, fostering a welcoming climate, and nurturing creativity, discovery, and the spread of new ideas and innovations. The University of Arkansas campus is located in Fayetteville, a welcoming community ranked as one of the best places to live in the U.S. The growing region surrounding Fayetteville is home to numerous Fortune 500 companies and one of the nation\u2019s strongest economies. Northwest Arkansas is also quickly gaining a national reputation for its focus on the arts and overall quality of life. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10% of employee salary. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions, you should review before applying for the opening. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process, please submit a request via the Disability Accommodations | OEOC | University of Arkansas (uark.edu) : Request an Accommodation. Appli\u00adcants are required to submit a request for each position of which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 479.575.5351. Department: Architecture Hourly C Department's Website: https://fayjones.uark.edu/ Summary of Job Duties: The Postdoctoral Fellow Research in Robotics, Advanced Manufacturing and Materials Innovation will join an interdisciplinary research group working at the intersection of robotics, artificial intelligence, advanced manufacturing, and materials innovation. The researcher will work closely with Dr. Kaicong Wu, Arkansas Research Alliance Innovation Scholar and Assistant Professor of Architecture in Design Studio and Advanced Digital Technologies in Department of Architecture at the Fay Jones School of Architecture and Design. The position is supported by the Arkansas Research Alliance and is intended to advance high-impact research addressing state and national priorities in sustainable material systems, advanced manufacturing, automation in construction, and workforce development. The successful candidate will contribute to the research team addressing regenerative design and construction through the integration of: \uf0a7 Reversible timber construction; \uf0a7 Wood by-product composites; \uf0a7 Adaptive robotic fabrication and advanced manufacturing; \uf0a7 Human\u2013robot collaboration in construction; and \uf0a7 Multimodal foundation models and AI-enabled agentic systems. The successful candidate will: \uf0a7 Conduct interdisciplinary research in robotics, artificial intelligence, advanced manufacturing, and materials innovation; \uf0a7 Have substantial agency to propose and develop research projects aligned with their individual research trajectory and the broader mission of the group; \uf0a7 Develop and implement foundation-model-enabled robotic fabrication, assembly, disassembly, perception, and human\u2013robot collaboration workflows; \uf0a7 Contribute to experimental research involving timber construction systems, wood by-product composites, additive manufacturing, and reversible/circular construction; \uf0a7 Work closely with Dr. Wu and collaborating faculty, students, research groups, and external partners; \uf0a7 Take a leading role in producing high-quality scholarship, including peer-reviewed journal articles and competitive conference papers; \uf0a7 Document research methods, prototypes, experimental results, datasets, and workflows; \uf0a7 Contribute to the preparation of external research proposals and collaborative grant applications; \uf0a7 Support the translation of research into demonstrators, intellectual property, commercialization opportunities, and job-creating innovation. \uf0a7 Depending on the appointee\u2019s interests and professional goals, opportunities may also include participation in exhibitions, installations, design-build projects, and supportive teaching activities related to robotic fabrication, advanced digital technologies, and design-build education. The postdoctoral researcher will join the Department of Architecture to contribute to establishing its research culture, technical infrastructure, external partnerships, and scholarly profile. This is an in-person position, not a remote position. Extensive in-person engagement in both supervisory activities and formal and informal interactions with colleagues contributes to successful leadership, coordination, and collaboration and is essential to the expectations for the position. Regular, reliable, and non-disruptive attendance is an essential job duty, as is the ability to create and maintain collegial, harmonious working relationships with others. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Ph.D. in robotics, computer science, mechanical engineering, or a closely related field from an accredited institution of higher education, conferred by the start of employment Demonstrated research experience in one or more of the following areas: robotics and autonomous systems; advanced manufacturing or robotic fabrication; automation in construction; human\u2013robot collaboration; computer vision, sensing, or perception; artificial intelligence, deep learning, or foundation models; additive manufacturing; material innovation or computational materials research; strong programming, computational, experimental, or robotic systems-development skills; evidence of the ability to conduct independent and collaborative research A demonstrated capacity or strong potential to publish peer-reviewed scholarly work Preferred Qualifications: Experience in architecture, industrial design, computational design, or another design discipline Experience with robotics applications in architecture, engineering, and construction Experience with timber construction, reversible building systems, or design for disassembly Experience with wood-based composites, bio-based materials, or circular material systems Experience with industrial robotic arms, linear tracks, end-effectors, extrusion systems, or robotic additive manufacturing (3D printing) Experience with robot operating systems (ROS), motion planning, computer vision, multimodal AI, or foundation-model-enabled agentic systems Experience with physical prototyping and experimental fabrication Experience conducting interdisciplinary research involving design, engineering, computation, and material science Experience preparing research proposals or contributing to externally funded projects Experience translating research into industry collaboration, intellectual property, or commercialization Additional Information: Salary Information: $52,000.00 Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Curriculum Vitae, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Writing Sample Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Recruitment Contact Information: Dr. Kaicong Wu, Assistant Professor - Design Studio and Advanced Digital Technologies, kawu@uark.edu 479/575-6369 All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Special Instructions to Applicants: The selected candidate is expected to begin employment on or around October 1, 2026. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas seeks to attract, develop and retain high quality faculty, staff and administrators that consistently display practices and behaviors to advance a culture that embeds equal opportunity, educational excellence and unparalleled access for all. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All Application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Fayetteville/Associate-Director-for-Industry-Relations_R0090091-1": {"title": "Associate Director for Industry Relations", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com, then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at all University of Arkansas institutions will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students.\u201d University of Arkansas, Fayetteville students will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Student Jobs at UAF.\u201d All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. Closing Date: 09/05/2026 Type of Position: Business Development Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas, Fayetteville Founded in 1871, the University of Arkansas is a land grant institution, classified by the Carnegie Foundation among the nation\u2019s top 2 percent of universities with the highest level of research activity. The University of Arkansas works to advance the state and build a better world through education, research, and outreach by providing transformational opportunities and skills, fostering a welcoming climate, and nurturing creativity, discovery, and the spread of new ideas and innovations. The University of Arkansas campus is located in Fayetteville, a welcoming community ranked as one of the best places to live in the U.S. The growing region surrounding Fayetteville is home to numerous Fortune 500 companies and one of the nation\u2019s strongest economies. Northwest Arkansas is also quickly gaining a national reputation for its focus on the arts and overall quality of life. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10% of employee salary. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions, you should review before applying for the opening. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process, please submit a request via the Disability Accommodations | OEOC | University of Arkansas (uark.edu) : Request an Accommodation. Appli\u00adcants are required to submit a request for each position of which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 479.575.5351. Department: Career Center Undergraduate and Student Programs Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Associate Director for Industry Relations supports the effectiveness and strategic direction of employer engagement efforts within Walton College Career Connections through data analysis, program coordination, and operational execution. This role works closely with the Senior Director and employer-facing team members to ensure that industry engagement strategies are informed by accurate data, aligned with student outcomes, and executed efficiently. The Associate Director is responsible for analyzing employer engagement and internship/employment outcomes data, developing reports and dashboards, and translating insights into actionable recommendations. In addition, this role provides critical operational support, including coordinating meetings, tracking initiatives, managing timelines, and ensuring follow-through across projects and partnerships. Success in this role requires strong analytical skills, attention to detail, and the ability to manage multiple priorities while keeping team initiatives organized and on track. The Associate Director collaborates across Career Connections, academic programs, and external partners to enhance the quality, efficiency, and impact of employer engagement efforts. Must be able to provide in-person support of programming/events during office hours, Monday-Friday 8am-5pm, and occasional evenings and weekends, less than 10 evenings or weekends a semester Regular, non-disruptive, and in-person, reliable attendance is an essential job duty, as well as the ability to create and maintain collegial, harmonious working relationships with others. This position will require office hours of 8am-5pm, Monday-Friday, with in-person support of programming/events during office hours and occasionally nights and weekends. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in business, communications, marketing, human resources, or related field from an accredited institution of higher education Experience in two or more career fields within business education (such as Accounting and Finance; Marketing, Sales, Consumer Packaged Goods (CPG); Supply Chain Management and/or Operations; Human Resource Management and Entrepreneurship; Economics and Information Systems; and MBA and other Specialty Master\u2019s Programs) Experience and high proficiency with web-based resources, spreadsheet and presentation software (MS Word, PowerPoint, Outlook and Excel) Preferred Qualifications: Master's degree in business, communications, marketing, human resources, or related field from an accredited institution of higher education Experience that demonstrates growth and/or advancement within the fields of corporate human resources, professional, or executive recruitment Experience tracking record of success in developing and implementing recruiting strategies and programming Experience to establishing and maintaining effective rapport with companies, executives, alumni, and recruiters Experience in job search and process management Experience with pivot tables in Excel for data analysis Experience with Applicant Tracking Systems, Learning Management Systems (e.g., Canvas) and/or Career Services platforms (e.g., Handshake, or similar) Experience working with students in a higher education environment Additional Information: Salary Information: $58,000 Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Recruitment Contact Information: Lindsey Steiger-Muck Senior Director of Career Services Sam M. Walton College of Business LSteiger-Muck@walton.uark.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Special Instructions to Applicants: Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Motor Vehicle Reports Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas seeks to attract, develop and retain high quality faculty, staff and administrators that consistently display practices and behaviors to advance a culture that embeds equal opportunity, educational excellence and unparalleled access for all. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All Application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Curriculum---Catalog-Coordinator_R0090550": {"title": "Curriculum & Catalog Coordinator", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/10/2026 Type of Position: Professional Staff - Institutional Affairs Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Little Rock The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is a metropolitan research university that provides an accessible, quality education through flexible learning and unparalleled internship opportunities. At UA Little Rock, we prepare our more than 8,900 students to be innovators and responsible leaders in their fields. Committed to its metropolitan research university mission, UA Little Rock is a driving force in Little Rock's thriving cultural community and a major component of the city and state's growing profile as a regional leader in research, technology transfer, economic development, and job creation. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . Department: AVCAA Continuous Improvement Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Curriculum & Catalog Coordinator helps facilitate the curriculum and program change process for assigned colleges, maintains assigned portions of official academic catalogs (undergraduate and graduate), and provides operational and academic support for the Office of the Provost. The Curriculum & Catalog Coordinator works collaboratively with the corresponding curriculum and catalog coordinator in the Office of the Provost. This position is a direct report to the Associate Vice Chancellor (AVC) for Continuous Improvement with non-curricular duties reporting to the Provost Chief of Staff. Qualifications: Required Education and/or Experience: Earned Bachelor's degree; A minimum of two (2) years of experience in higher education or relevant professional experience; Workday experience. \u00a0 Job Duties and Responsibilities: Curriculum Coordination Monitors, routes, reviews and tracks curriculum and program change forms (routing, signatures, and status updates) for assigned colleges; Serves as the primary liaison for assigned college curriculum and program change forms, and provides guidance while communicating updates throughout the curriculum and program change process; Enters approved curriculum changes into Courseleaf; Coordinates with key university partners, ensuring seamless implementation of curriculum and program changes; Works collaboratively with Curriculum & Catalog Coordinator counterpart on curriculum and program changes; Serves as backup for Curriculum & Catalog Coordinator counterpart. Catalog Coordination Directly updates and maintains the official academic catalogs (undergraduate and graduate catalog) for assigned colleges to ensure accuracy and prevent data mismatch; Ensures timely review of catalog content and effectively works with key university partners/offices to perform routine catalog edits and updates; Researches internal and external policies and regulations to ensure non-curricular catalog sections are in compliance with university, UA Board of Trustees, and state and federal policies and regulations. Operational and Academic Support Works with the Associate Vice Chancellor (AVC) of Continuous Improvement with program change inquiries and clarifies external approval processes; Assists Executive Vice Chancellor and Provost, AVCs, Finance Director, and Provost Chief of Staff as needed; Updates UA Little Rock academic affairs websites and non-curricular academic publications under the direction of the Provost Chief of Staff and the AVC for Continuous Improvement; Provides the Provost Office with operational support for special projects, procurement, events, front desk coverage, and travel support; Processes Faculty Senate legislation and provides operational support to Faculty Senate; Other duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Knowledge of rules, regulations, and requirements related to higher education, specifically Academic Affairs; Proficiency with Microsoft Office Suite and Google Suite, Workday, and Courseleaf; Exceptional organizational skills; Meticulous attention to detail; Excellent writing and editing skills; Excellent problem-solving skills with attention to detail and a focus on quality; Ability to effectively work independently and collaboratively; Ability to maintain strict confidentiality of sensitive or legally protected information. Additional Information: Salary Information: $55,000 Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Sharon Sims, Director of Finance, scsims@ualr.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Balancing, Feeling, Grasping, Hearing, Lifting, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Repetitive Motion, Sitting, Standing, Stooping, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Hearing, Lifting, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Reaching, Repetitive Motion, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Kneeling Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Morrilton/Director-of-Workforce-Development_R0090643": {"title": "Director of Workforce Development", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Management - Student Affairs Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas Community College at Morrilton The University of Arkansas Community College at Morrilton (UACCM) is a proud member of the University of Arkansas System.\u00a0 The University of Arkansas System is comprised of land-grant research institutions, a teaching hospital, five community colleges, two schools of law, a presidential school, a residential math and science high school, and an online university, as well as divisions of agriculture, archaeology and criminal justice. These entities exhibit unmatched economic and social impact across the state by providing numerous academic and professional opportunities. Below you will find the details for the position currently available at UACCM including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.\u00a0 To apply for the position, please click the Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please submit a request via Email to: UACCMHRDept@uaccm.edu or by phone at (501) 208-5309 or (501) 977-2016.\u00a0\u00a0 Applicants are required to submit a separate request for each position in which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at UACCMHRDept@uaccm.edu or by phone at (501) 208-5309 or (501) 977-2016. Department: Workforce Education & Training Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Title: Director of Workforce Development Appropriated Position: Director of Workforce Development FLSA: Non-Exempt Safety Sensitive: No Essential Worker: No Provisional: No The Director of Workforce Development works under the supervision of the Associate Vice Chancellor of Workforce Education and Training and is responsible for all activities related to the UACCM workforce development program. The Director\u2019s primary responsibilities will be working with Business and Industry partners to development, implement, and schedule non-credit workforce training programs. JOB DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES INCLUDE: Develop, coordinate, promote, and evaluate workforce training programs that support regional workforce needs and economic development efforts. Build and maintain strong partnerships with business, industry, government agencies, workforce organizations, and community stakeholders to identify training needs and workforce opportunities. Conduct needs assessments with employers and develop customized training solutions. Coordinate the scheduling, implementation, and assessment of non-credit workforce training programs, short-term credentials, and professional development offerings. Facilitate specialized training when appropriate for businesses and industries. Collaborate with academic divisions and college departments to align workforce initiatives with credit programs, career pathways, and community needs. Coordinate outreach activities with secondary schools, career centers, and community organizations to promote workforce education and training opportunities. Recruit, select, supervise, and evaluate full- and part-time trainers and facilitators of short-term training courses as needed. Maintain accurate program, enrollment, and training records and provide required reports to internal and external stakeholders. Assist with the development, implementation, management, and reporting requirements of workforce-related grants and special projects. Represent the College and Division in professional manner at civic meetings, statewide meetings, and other events. Participate in strategic initiatives that support the mission and goals of Workforce Education and Training and UACCM. Perform other duties and special projects as assigned. Qualifications: MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS: \u00a0 The formal education equivalent of a bachelor\u2019s degree in economic/workforce development, community development, industrial relations, business or a related field. \u00a0 Three years of supervisory experience \u00a0 Other job-related education and/or experience may be substituted for all or part of the minimum qualifications upon approval of the Chancellor. \u00a0 \u00a0 PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS: \u00a0 A master\u2019s degree with an emphasis in economic/workforce development, community development, industrial relations, business or a related field. \u00a0 Prior work experience in h igher education, workforce training, economic development, or business and industry engagement. \u00a0 Experience managing grants, contracts, or workforce-funded initiatives. \u00a0 \u00a0 APPLICATION REQUIREMENTS: \u00a0 Cover Letter \u00a0 Resume\u2019 \u00a0 List of three professional references \u00a0 Copies of college transcripts, related licensure, certification \u00a0 Additional Information: \u00a0 KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, AND ABILITIES: \u00a0 Able to communicate effectively both orally and in writing to individuals and large groups.\u202f \u00a0 Proficient in the use of computer software and applications, such as but not limited to, Microsoft Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Outlook, and Access.\u00a0 \u00a0 Knowledge of employee management principles, methods, and procedures. \u00a0 Able to perform basic research, analyze information and prepare reports in a logical and informative manner .\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0 Able to problem solve, organize and prioritize work, multi-task, and be flexible and accepting of change. \u00a0 Able to work independently and cooperatively with a team to achieve the mission/goal. \u00a0 Able to work effectively with people of various cultural backgrounds.\u00a0 \u00a0 Able to lift and move objects that may weight up to 25 lbs.\u00a0 \u00a0 Knowledge of planning, research, and analysis techniques and procedures. \u00a0 Knowledge of department operations, policies, and procedures. \u00a0 Knowledge of applicable laws and regulations. \u00a0 Ability to conduct research and perform quantitative quality assurance reviews. \u00a0 Ability to research, prepare, and present comprehensive written and oral reports. \u00a0 Ability to organize and conduct meetings and workshops. \u00a0 \u00a0 All employees at UACCM must have a commitment to work cooperatively with all campus personnel to fulfill the Mission of UACCM, and have the ability to deliver quality customer services. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience, $60,000 - $70,000 Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume, Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Shelby Beck HR Analyst 501-208-5309 All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Child Maltreatment, Criminal Background Check, Motor Vehicle Reports Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas Community College at Morrilton (UACCM) is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check, sex offender registry check, and drug screen. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check and/or a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check.\u00a0 A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting, Standing Frequent Physical Activity: Hearing, Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Grasping, Lifting, Reaching, Stooping Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Pharmacist-I-PRN----Cancer-Institute-Pharmacy_R0090676-1": {"title": "Pharmacist I PRN  - Cancer Institute Pharmacy", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/10/2026 Type of Position: Clinical Staff - Medical Ancillary Support Job Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Shift Vary (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: PTSL Cancer Institute OP Technicians Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Pharmacist I PRN in the Cancer Institute Pharmacy ensures the safe, accurate and appropriate use of medications, by evaluating orders for dosing, allergies, and contraindications. The Pharmacist I helps oversee and direct the work of supportive pharmacy personnel, including technicians and students. They prepare and dispense medications, including oral and injectable medications and hazardous drugs (including chemotherapy). The Pharmacist I is responsible for prioritizing the work in a way that best meets the needs of patients, the pharmacy, and other stakeholders and customers. They will answer pharmacy-related questions for patients, other health professionals, and the public. The Pharmacist I will report adverse drug events and medication safety events, and will document interventions in the medical record. They will recommend appropriate and cost-effective drug therapy options and provide medication counseling to patients and their families. The Pharmacist I promotes and participates in the defined missions of the service line and the strategic goals of the health system. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications : Bachelor's degree in Pharmacy plus 1 year of experience working as a pharmacist (or pharmacy intern) \u00a0 in a retail or hospital setting. Pharmacy technician license through the Arkansas State Board of Pharmacy or eligible for AR licensure. Preferred Qualifications : Proficiency in utilization of electronic health record and other computer systems, excellent customer service, broad knowledge of pharmacy regulations and practices, knowledge of proper aseptic technique, sterile compounding, and hazardous drug handling regulations and best practices Pharm.D. 2 years applicable experience (i.e. previous hospital experience, sterile compounding experience, hazardous drug handling, etc.) Aseptic technique/sterile compounding Additional Information: Responsibilities: Reviews and verifies medication orders, including checking for appropriateness, proper dosing, contraindications, allergies, proper volumes and concentrations, mixing instructions, administration instructions, etc. Ensures proper preparation and labeling of oral & injectable medications Performs sterile compounding of hazardous and non-hazardous medications Performs final check of all medications before dispensing Properly utilizes technology to perform job, including all hoods, pumps, computers, barcode scanners, the electronic medical record, IV workflow software, investigational drug inventory software, etc. Dispenses investigational drugs accurately Collaborates regularly with RNs, APRNs and physicians in the provision and coordination of patient care As needed or assigned, provides pharmacist coverage in the myeloma/stem-cell transplant infusion center, performing tasks such as medication reconciliation, proactive order & treatment plan review, troubleshooting, clarifying orders, providing educations to patients, nurses, and providers Understands and complies with relevant regulatory standards and all departmental policies Has a thorough knowledge of regulations, enforceable standards, and best practices for compounded sterile products and hazardous drug handling, and practices strict aseptic technique at all times Documents interventions in the medical record \u2022 Reports all patient safety events in the appropriate medication safety reporting tool Calibrates Repeater pumps when appropriate, and documents calibration on the appropriate log sheet Performs and documents monthly inspection of assigned medication storage area Promptly reports to supervisor or other appropriate individual if there are any deficiencies or problems with any equipment, facilities, or drug distribution Other duties as assigned Salary Information: $65 per hour Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Criminal Background Check, Substance Abuse Testing This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: Feeling, Grasping, Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Reaching, Repetitive Motion, Sharps, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Crouching, Kneeling, Lifting, Pulling, Pushing, Stooping Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Monitor-Tech_R0090334-1": {"title": "Monitor Tech", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/26/2026 Type of Position: Clinical Staff - Nursing Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | NRSL EKG Heart Station IN C Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Monitor Technician is a trained member of the nursing team within the Telemetry department. Monitor Technicians provide 24/7 telemetry monitoring and observation for inpatients from all disciplines throughout the hospital. The department focus is aiding in identification and prevention of acute medical events by providing monitoring across multiple platforms, and to help ensure our patients receive the highest possible care available. The Telemetry department strives to maintain the most updated evidence-based practices and equipment needed to facilitate our goals. Monitor Technicians are an integral part of the multidisciplinary team approach we implement at UAMS. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: High school diploma/GED,\u00a0PLUS\u00a0 Six (6) months direct patient care related experience. PCT certified within three (3) months of hire (training provided). Current certification or competency of EKG acquisition Preferred Qualifications: Certified as a nursing assistant or military corpsman. Current BLS. Certification in EKG or Dysrhythmia course. Special knowledge, abilities and skills: Must\u00a0complete the dysrhythmia course within 90 day evaluation period and maintain competency as a telemetry technician.\u00a0 Must have\u00a0excellent communication skills, ability to follow oral instructions, basic computer skills, strong work ethics and accountability. Microsoft Office experience EPIC EMR Kronos Physical Requirements: Must be able to lift 100 pounds Additional Information: Job Requirements: Continuously monitor cardiac rhythms and telemetry data for assigned patients. Recognize and promptly report abnormal cardiac rhythms, rate changes, and potentially life-threatening arrhythmias to nursing staff. Maintain accurate documentation of telemetry observations and significant rhythm changes. Perform routine rhythm interpretation according to department standards and established protocols. Apply, replace, and troubleshoot telemetry monitoring equipment and electrodes as needed. Ensure monitoring equipment is functioning properly and report equipment malfunctions promptly. Maintain constant observation of assigned telemetry monitors and respond appropriately to alarms. Communicate critical monitor findings clearly and promptly to the appropriate nurse or clinical team member. Assist with admission, transfer, and discharge processes related to telemetry monitoring. Maintain patient safety by identifying monitoring interruptions, loose leads, artifact, or signal loss. Collaborate with nurses, physicians, and other healthcare professionals to support timely patient care. Maintain confidentiality of patient information and comply with HIPAA and organizational policies. Follow established procedures for emergency situations and immediately escalate critical changes in patient condition. Maintain a clean, organized, and safe monitoring environment. Participate in quality improvement activities, competency assessments, and required departmental training. Demonstrate attention to detail, effective communication, and the ability to remain focused in a fast-paced clinical environment. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS Stand: Frequently Sit: Frequently Walk: Occasionally Bend, crawl, crouch, kneel, stoop or reach overhead: Frequently Lift and carry weight: 25 lbs Push and pull weight: 25 lbs Use hands to touch, handle or feel: Frequently Talk: Continuously Hear: Continuously Taste or smell: Occasionally Read, concentrate, think analytically: Continuously Physical Environment : Inside Medical Facility Environment Salary Information: commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Criminal Background Check, Substance Abuse Testing This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Feeling, Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Standing, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Lifting, Reaching, Standing Occasional Physical Activity: Pulling, Pushing, Sitting Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Fayetteville-AR/Chief-Business-Officer---Division-of-Research-and-Innovation--VCRI-_R0090367-1": {"title": "Chief Business Officer - Division of Research and Innovation (VCRI)", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-26\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com, then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at all University of Arkansas institutions will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students.\u201d University of Arkansas, Fayetteville students will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Student Jobs at UAF.\u201d All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. Closing Date: 09/28/2026 Type of Position: Administrative Strategy Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas, Fayetteville Founded in 1871, the University of Arkansas is a land grant institution, classified by the Carnegie Foundation among the nation\u2019s top 2 percent of universities with the highest level of research activity. The University of Arkansas works to advance the state and build a better world through education, research, and outreach by providing transformational opportunities and skills, fostering a welcoming climate, and nurturing creativity, discovery, and the spread of new ideas and innovations. The University of Arkansas campus is located in Fayetteville, a welcoming community ranked as one of the best places to live in the U.S. The growing region surrounding Fayetteville is home to numerous Fortune 500 companies and one of the nation\u2019s strongest economies. Northwest Arkansas is also quickly gaining a national reputation for its focus on the arts and overall quality of life. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10% of employee salary. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions, you should review before applying for the opening. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process, please submit a request via the Disability Accommodations | OEOC | University of Arkansas (uark.edu) : Request an Accommodation. Appli\u00adcants are required to submit a request for each position of which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 479.575.5351. Department: Assistant Vice Chancellor for Business Services Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Chief Business Officer (CBO) serves as the financial leader for the Division of Research and Innovation (VCRI). The CBO will provide strategic leadership and oversight for financial planning and analysis, budgeting, forecasting, organizational administration and resource allocation, operational effectiveness, and the administration and tracking of key research support programs, including start-up commitments and cost-share obligations, across the division and the research enterprise. The position provides financial oversight for division units including, but not limited to, the Office of Research Administration (which includes sponsored programs, research compliance, contracting, and campus services), Research Technology & Infrastructure, Technology Ventures, Research Security, Research Advancement, and Research Operations, as well as research centers and core facilities such as the Arkansas High Performance Computing Center and the Arkansas Materials Institute. The CBO partners closely with division leadership, academic units, associate deans of research and department heads; central administrative offices; and external stakeholders such as the Arkansas Biosciences Institute and Arkansas Research Alliance to support the university\u2019s strategic research objectives, ensure responsible stewardship of resources, and strengthen operational infrastructure. This position reports directly to the Assistant Vice Chancellor for Capital and Financial Planning and indirectly to the Vice Chancellor for Research and Innovation Regular, reliable, and non-disruptive attendance is an essential job duty, as is the ability to create and maintain collegial, harmonious working relationships with others. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor\u2019s degree in finance, accounting or related field from an accredited institution of higher education At least four years of financial planning and analysis experience At least two years of experience in a supervisory role At least three years of accounting experience related to research enterprise activities Experience with written and verbal presentations of financial activity Experience developing, implementing and monitoring budgets Experience working with federal and state regulation of sponsored research Preferred Qualification: Master\u2019s degree in business, accounting or a related field Experience working with federal uniform guidance and related federal regulatory systems At least four years financial planning and analysis experience in post-secondary higher education Successful completion of a CPA or similar professional certificate Director level experience Experience managing financial operations, accounting, budget, and reporting functions in a post-secondary environment Workday experience Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: In depth understanding and knowledge of best practices in the areas of budgeting, analytics, operations and planning Excellent communication skills both oral and written Time management skills Decision-making and problem-solving skills Ability to read, analyze and interpret financial data Ability to collaborate and work well with others Ability to work under time constraints Proficient abilities with Microsoft Office Suite \u2013 with expertise in Word and Excel Additional Information: Salary Information: $148,500 - $196,000 Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Recruitment Contact Information: Crystal Ellis, Strategic Talent Acquisition Specialist, ce031@uark.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Special Instructions to Applicants: Applications will be reviewed upon receipt within the posting period. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Financial Credit Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas seeks to attract, develop and retain high quality faculty, staff and administrators that consistently display practices and behaviors to advance a culture that embeds equal opportunity, educational excellence and unparalleled access for all. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All Application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Feeling, Grasping Occasional Physical Activity: Standing, Walking Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAMS/Health-Educator--West-Memphis--AR-_R0090372-1": {"title": "Health Educator (West Memphis, AR)", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-26\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/30/2026 Type of Position: Instructional Development Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: REP | East West Memphis Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Join a dynamic, mission-driven team dedicated to transforming health in Eastern Arkansas, based out of our West Memphis, AR office site. As the Health Educator for the UAMS East Regional Campus, you will lead community outreach partnerships, deliver proven educational interventions, and inspire broader engagement across schools, churches, and community organizations. This role combines hands-on program leadership with strategic collaboration to elevate health literacy and healthy living in the region. The ideal candidate is passionate about public health, possesses excellent communication skills, and has a track record of successful community engagement. If you are eager to make a meaningful impact and drive health improvements in Eastern Arkansas, we encourage you to apply today. Join us in our mission to create healthier communities through education and collaboration! Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's Degree in Education, Public Health or a health-related field Three (3) years of experience in Health Education, Administrative Roles, or Program assessment/development. Knowledge, Skills, & Abilities: Communication: clear, persuasive oral and written communication tailored to diverse audiences; effective public speaking and presentation skills. Community Engagement: ability to build trust, establish partnerships, and maintain ongoing community relationships. Program Development: design, implement, and evaluate educational programs and interventions. Project Management: plan timelines, manage multiple initiatives concurrently, and meet deadlines. Data Management: accurate data entry, record-keeping, and basic evaluation metrics. Collaboration: working effectively with multidisciplinary teams and external partners. Problem-Solving: identify needs, propose practical solutions, and adjust programs as needed. Adaptability: flexibility to respond to changing community needs and event schedules. Resourcefulness: ability to create promotional materials and leverage community networks. Preferred Qualifications: Master's in Heath Education or a related field. Certified Health Education Specialist (CHES). Experience working with SPSS Statistics Software and/or\u00a0REDCap Software. Additional Information: Key Responsibilities: Lead Kids for Health: deliver a 10-week curriculum in schools, covering health topics from hygiene to exercise. Diabetes Education (DEEP): plan, execute, and assess community diabetes education programs. Child Safety and Baby Safety Showers: organize and evaluate parent-focused safety trainings. Car Seat Checks and Installation: conduct safety checks and promote proper installation. Health Screenings/Fairs: prepare and present information at community screenings. Community Health Programs: design and evaluate initiatives promoting nutrition, activity, and healthy lifestyles. Outreach and Promotion: assist with event planning, create promotional materials, and coordinate public communications. Collaboration: partner with pre-professionals to plan initiatives like MASH, CHAMPS, and Day in the Life. Guest Relations: represent UAMS with professionalism and warmth at events. Administrative Duties: daily site reporting, data entry, weekly logs, and program publicity. May perform other duties as assigned to support the mission of UAMS East Regional Campus. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: No Background Check Required This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting Frequent Physical Activity: Feeling, Grasping, Hearing, Standing, Talking Occasional Physical Activity: Kneeling, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Standing, Talking, Walking Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Lab-Support-Technician-I--Lab-Support-Services_R0090636-1": {"title": "Lab Support Technician I- Lab Support Services", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-26\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/09/2026 Type of Position: Clinical Staff - Medical Ancillary Support Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Shift Vary (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | LPSL Laboratory Support Services Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: This position works under the supervision of the section Supervisor and Senior Tech. This position provides comprehensive support for patient care activities in the Core Lab. This positions schedule could change due to staffing issues with a two week notice. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: High School Diploma, GED or formal education equivalent. \u200b Preferred Qualifications: Previous clinical laboratory experience Additional Information: Job Requirements: Receives specimens from all sources and verifies that specimens are properly collected and labeled.\u00a0 Ensure test is received in the correct tube type.\u00a0 Sorts all specimens and place them in the proper racks or bucket to be received.\u00a0 Load racks on the appropriate automation line to be received in and tested.\u00a0 Scan specimens into the EPIC system and re-label the specimens as needed.\u00a0 Enter orders into EPIC through requisition entry for all outside institutions.\u00a0 Process add-on test.\u00a0 Answers phone calls concerning results, faxing reports, specimen collection and ordering test.\u00a0 Process timed urine specimens.\u00a0 Reconcile packing list.\u00a0 Process Reference, VA and ACH specimens.\u00a0 Process mail-in specimens.\u00a0 Scan requisitions received with labs from institutional accounts into EPIC.\u00a0 Call critical results as needed.\u00a0 Fill out all Safety Intelligence reports and deliver to the Core Lab Manager. Perform other duties as needed. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS Stand: Frequently Sit: Frequently Walk: Occasionally Bend, crawl, crouch, kneel, stoop or reach overhead: Frequently Lift and carry weight: 25 lbs Push and pull weight: 25 lbs Use hands to touch, handle or feel: Frequently Talk: Continuously Hear: Continuously Taste or smell: Occasionally Read, concentrate, think analytically: Continuously Physical Environment : Inside Medical Facility Environment Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Criminal Background Check, Substance Abuse Testing This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Feeling, Grasping, Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Hearing, Reaching, Repetitive Motion, Sharps, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Crouching, Driving, Kneeling, Lifting, Pulling, Pushing, Stooping Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAMS/Emergency-Medicine-Physicians---Leadership-Opportunities--Evergreen-_R0088043-2": {"title": "Emergency Medicine Physicians & Leadership Opportunities (Evergreen)", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-26\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/27/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: COM | Emergency Medicine Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) Department of Emergency Medicine is seeking exceptional physicians to join our nationally recognized department. We are recruiting board-certified and board-eligible physicians across a variety of clinical, academic, subspecialty, and leadership roles. Whether your passion is community emergency medicine, academic practice, residency education, medical toxicology, or physician leadership, UAMS offers opportunities to build a rewarding career while advancing patient care, education, and research. As Arkansas's only academic health sciences center and home to the state's only Level 1 Trauma Center, UAMS provides physicians with the opportunity to care for a diverse patient population while working alongside nationally recognized faculty in an innovative academic environment. We are currently recruiting physicians for the following positions: Emergency Medicine Physician \u2013 Community Practice Emergency Medicine Physician \u2013 Academic Clinical Faculty Medical Toxicologist Assistant/Associate Residency Program Director Medical Director \u2013 Community Emergency Medicine Candidates may indicate their area(s) of interest during the recruitment process. Qualifications: Additional \u00a0 qualifications may apply depending on the position. Doctor of Medicine (MD), Doctor of Osteopathic Medicine (DO), or equivalent degree\u00a0 \u00a0 Board certification or board eligibility in Emergency Medicine (ABEM or ABOEM), or specialty-specific board certification where applicable\u00a0 \u00a0 Eligibility for \u00a0 or \u00a0 current Arkansas medical licensure\u00a0 \u00a0 Demonstrated commitment to patient-centered, evidence-based care\u00a0 \u00a0 Excellent communication and collaborative practice skills\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 Preferred Qualifications\u00a0 Depending on the position, preferred experience may include: \u00a0 Academic medicine and physician education\u00a0 \u00a0 Community emergency medicine\u00a0 \u00a0 Residency leadership or graduate medical education\u00a0 \u00a0 Medical Toxicology fellowship training\u00a0 \u00a0 Clinical research and scholarly activity\u00a0 \u00a0 Quality improvement and patient safety\u00a0 \u00a0 Physician leadership and administrative experience\u00a0 \u00a0 Curriculum development and learner mentorship\u00a0 \u00a0 Multidisciplinary collaboration\u00a0 \u00a0 Additional Information: \u00a0 Responsibilities \u00a0 Provide comprehensive emergency medical care for patients across the lifespan\u00a0 \u00a0 Evaluate, diagnose, and manage acute illnesses and injuries\u00a0 \u00a0 Perform emergency procedures consistent with specialty training\u00a0 \u00a0 Deliver \u00a0 timely , compassionate, evidence-based care\u00a0 \u00a0 Teach and supervise residents, fellows, and medical students\u00a0 \u00a0 Participate \u00a0 in curriculum development and educational programming\u00a0 \u00a0 Mentor trainees and junior faculty\u00a0 \u00a0 Lead clinical operations and departmental initiatives\u00a0 \u00a0 Support provider recruitment, onboarding, and professional development\u00a0 \u00a0 Participate in strategic planning and operational improvement\u00a0 \u00a0 Promote patient safety and quality initiatives\u00a0 \u00a0 Participate in research and scholarly activity\u00a0 \u00a0 Present at regional or national meetings\u00a0 \u00a0 Publish scholarly work as appropriate\u00a0 \u00a0 Contribute to innovation within Emergency Medicine\u00a0 \u00a0 Work collaboratively with physicians, advanced practice providers, nursing, pharmacy, EMS, hospital administration, and multidisciplinary care teams\u00a0 \u00a0 Support departmental goals focused on quality, efficiency, patient experience, and operational excellence\u00a0 \u00a0 Other duties as assigned \u00a0 Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Curriculum Vitae, Letters of Recommendation, License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), Listing of Publications, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Other (see special instructions for details), Proof of Veteran Status, Resume, Statement of Teaching Philosophy Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAMS/Building-Manager_R0089878-1": {"title": "Building Manager", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-26\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/10/2026 Type of Position: Management - Operations Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: OPS | Regulatory Compliance, Campus Operations Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Building Manager is responsible for the day-to-day oversight of multiple UAMS buildings, ensuring facility safety, functionality, space integrity, and regulatory compliance. As a key member of UAMS Building & Space Management, the Building Manager is responsible for a wide range of facility and space management activities, providing a high level of customer service while collaborating closely with stakeholders across UAMS. This includes serving as a liaison to Engineering & Operations, Planning, Design & Construction, Environmental Services, IT, Environmental/Occupational Health & Safety, and Security Support Services. Qualifications: Bachelor\u2019s degree in facility management, operations, safety, business administration, or a related field, or an equivalent combination of education and relevant experience. PLUS one (1) year of experience in building operations, facility management, space management, safety, or a related area. Skills, Knowledge, and Abilities: Ability to understand and follow oral and written instructions and communicate clearly and professionally. Demonstrated customer service skills, with a commitment to supporting employees, visitors, and the public. Familiarity with applicable regulatory codes and compliance standards, including NFPA, The Joint Commission, CMS, ADH, and DFA requirements. Working knowledge of NCES and FICM space-use standards. Strong interpersonal, organizational, problem-solving, and communication skills. Proficiency in Microsoft Office applications and facility or space-management platforms. Ability to manage multiple priorities and collaborate effectively with internal departments, contractors, and other stakeholders. Preferred Qualifications Master\u2019s degree in facility management, operations, safety, business administration, or a related field. Two to five years of experience in building operations, facility management, space management, safety, or a related area. Experience working in a healthcare, higher education, or academic medical center environment. Experience coordinating employee or departmental moves, furniture reallocation, and facility reconfiguration projects. Familiarity with AutoCAD, computer-aided facility management systems, or other space-management software. Knowledge of security, building-access, and access-control protocols. Additional Information: Responsibilities Proactively monitor building conditions to ensure assigned facilities remain safe, functional, and compliant. Conduct routine environmental, safety, and facility inspections. Identify and coordinate the timely resolution of operational, compliance, maintenance, and facility-related issues across assigned buildings. Support space-planning initiatives to ensure the effective and appropriate use of UAMS facilities. Coordinate occupant moves, furniture relocations, and facility reconfiguration projects. Maintain accurate building, room, occupancy, and space-management records. Collaborate with internal departments and stakeholders to minimize disruptions during moves and facility projects. Ensure assigned spaces comply with institutional policies, NCES/FICM space standards, and applicable healthcare, life-safety, accessibility, and regulatory requirements. Other duties as assigned. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience. Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Outpatient-Occupational-Therapist----Hand-Therapy_R0090382-1": {"title": "Outpatient Occupational Therapist  - Hand Therapy", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-26\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/24/2026 Type of Position: Clinical Staff - Rehabilitation Therapy Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | MUSL Hand Therapy-Rodney Parham ( Christopher K Oholendt) Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Come join our dynamic outpatient therapy, community fitness and sports medicine family as a hand therapist working closely with our physician partners at Rodney Parham Clinic! We value mentorships, continuing education, and a healthy caseload to provide individualized care as appropriate. Candidates should have a passion for hand and upper extremity conditions within an orthopaedic patient population. The hand therapist possesses a comprehensive knowledge of the upper limb structures that includes the hand, wrist, elbow, and shoulder girdle along with function and activity. Specialized skills are utilized in assessment, treatment, and therapeutic interventions to prevent dysfunction, restore function and/or reverse the progression of pathology of the upper limb in order to enhance an individual's ability to execute tasks and to participate fully in life situations. The hand therapist possesses the ability to work independently with initiative in a fast-paced clinic to manage outpatient upper limb referrals. Post-operative assessment and treatment may require CHT collaboration to gain expertise in orthotic fabrication & adjustment, modalities, and wound care along with gaining working knowledge and skill in treatment of advanced hand and upper extremity protocols. The hand therapist completes all continuum of care expectations to include the following: evaluation and establishing plans of care, therapy reassessments to adjust plans of care when appropriate, functional performance reassessment for discharge planning, screenings to determine appropriateness of therapy, and daily treatments along with appropriate patient documentation per department, HIPAA and JCAHO standards where applicable. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor\u2019s Degree in Occupational Therapy PLUS two (2)\u00a0years of experience in Occupational Therapy OR Master's Degree in Occupational Therapy Certified by the National Board for Certification of Occupational Therapy (NBCOT) or eligible to apply for the examination Current Arkansas Occupational Therapy License or eligible to obtain license within one (1) month of date of hire Preferred Qualifications: Doctoral Degree in Occupational Therapy, CHT Additional Information: Responsibilites: Performs comprehensive examination of patients using appropriate tests/measures based on population. Completes the evaluation and formulates an individualized plan of care. Provides evidence based quality patient treatments and monitors patient for physiological status during sessions. Provides individualized patient education. Documents evaluations treatment sessions/education sessions and submits accurate charges according to regulatory policies. Participates in multidisciplinary and department communication, including patient care discussions and/or meetings and unit/department/hospital meetings. Provides education regarding occupational therapy discipline. May serve as a clinical instructor, a mentor for a clinical observer, or provide education to other disciplines within UAMS and/or the community. Performs other duties as assigned. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Criminal Background Check, Substance Abuse Testing This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: Balancing, Climbing, Crawling, Crouching, Feeling, Grasping, Hearing, Kneeling, Lifting, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Repetitive Motion, Sharps, Sitting, Standing, Stooping, Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Diagnostic-Radiology-Technologist-PRN---Main-Hospital_R0090647-1": {"title": "Diagnostic Radiology Technologist PRN - Main Hospital", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-26\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/26/2026 Type of Position: Clinical Staff - Medical Ancillary Support Job Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Shift Vary (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | IGSL General Diagnostics IOP C Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Diagnostic Radiology Technologist produces radiographic images for medical interpretation, interacts with all healthcare staff, many clerical staff members, all patient care departments, and with patients\u2019 families and visitors. This position is held accountable for performing the correct radiologic exams and producing high-quality images. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Associates - Graduate of an approved Radiology program, Registered or eligible by the American Registry of Radiologic Technologists (ARRT) Licensed by the State of Arkansas in Radiology Technology Preferred Qualifications: BS Degree More than one (1) year of experience in diagnostic radiology or a related field Additional Information: Responsibilities: Consists of performing optimal x-rays, and must be able to lift 25lbs. or more. Rotate through several modalities, portables on the floors, surgery, fluoro, and the emergency department performing X-rays, as well as coverage of diagnostic imaging at UAMS. Communicates with patients, patients' family members, co-workers, and physicians. Continues education and learning new procedures on a day-to-day basis. Duties will include answering the phones and communicating with different floors in the hospital. Moving C-ARM and OARM\u2019s Other duties may be assigned to this position.\u00a0 Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Criminal Background Check, Substance Abuse Testing This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Pulling, Pushing, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Feeling, Grasping, Kneeling, Lifting, Reaching, Repetitive Motion, Standing Occasional Physical Activity: Sharps Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Surgical-Scrub-Tech-Educator---Main-OR_R0090623-1": {"title": "Surgical/Scrub Tech Educator - Main OR", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-26\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/09/2026 Type of Position: Instructional Development Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | PERIOP QUALITY & ADMINISTRATION Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Surgical Technologist Education and Practice Coordinator (STEPC) role is an integral team member that provides essential leadership and oversight of surgical technologist practice in the operating rooms. This leader promotes recruitment and retention of STs by ensuring effective onboarding, competency validation and ongoing enhancement of clinical skills. The STEPC is actively involved in quality/performance improvement including data collection (audits, surveys), analysis, actions and evaluation. Coordination of activities to ensure regulatory compliance standards is a priority and expectation. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: 5 years of Surgical technologist experience in comparable setting Achievement of CST certification within 1 year of hire Superior organizational skills Proficient communication, leadership and interpersonal skills ability to provide instructions one-on-oneand in groups Skills in MS Office and database software Preferred Qualifications : 10 years of surgical technologist experience Experience in Level 1 Trauma hospital CST or CSFA certification AST member Leadership experience Additional Information: Responsibilities: Assist in assessing educational needs and identifying gaps in knowledge, skill or practice of identified learners. Assists leaders with training inexperienced staff members and providing clarification on matters of organizational policies and processes. Provides re-fresher courses; stays abreast of changes in accreditation and service standards and ensures current training programs are providing the proper education. Maintains training manuals and documentation of new processes. Follows through with all compliance, quality assurance, and budgetary guidelines set forth for educational program. Perform other duties as assigned. Salary Information: commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Criminal Background Check, Substance Abuse Testing This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Pulling, Pushing Occasional Physical Activity: Kneeling, Reaching, Sharps Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/RN---BHSL-General-Adult-Unit_R0090600-2": {"title": "RN - BHSL General Adult Unit", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-26\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/16/2026 Type of Position: Clinical Staff - Nursing Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | BHSL Adult PRI 6N/6S IP C Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Registered Nurse (RN) for the Behavioral Health Service Line (BHSL) General Adult Inpatient Unit consistently provides effective direct care to a variety of patients, will work as part of the interdisciplinary team, based on licensure, title and competencies. The RN seeks, as well as provides, feedback for improved clinical practice. The RN integrates theory and research into clinical practice. The RN provides leadership to members of the nursing team in order to maintain patient care standards. The RN works under the direct supervision of the Clinical Services Manager (CSM). Promotion is based on years of experience, satisfactory performance appraisals and recommendation by manager. Employee must successfully complete a UAMS-sponsored conflict management training to identify, prevent, and mitigate disruptive behaviors using methods such as non-escalation, de-escalation, personal protection from physical assaults, and physical alternatives within six months of hire. The BHSL General Adult Inpatient Unit is located in the Psychiatric Research Institute building on the main UAMS campus. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Graduate of an accredited nursing program with an Associate's Degree in Nursing, Nursing Diploma, Bachelor's Degree in Nursing, or Master's Degree in Nursing\u00a0 Minimum 1 year of Registered Nurse experience\u00a0 Current and valid Registered Nurse license in the State of Arkansas\u00a0 Excellent communication skills, basic computer skills, strong work ethic and accountability\u00a0 Preferred Qualifications: 2 or more years of Registered Nurse experience\u00a0 Current BLS\u00a0 Additional Information: Job Requirements: The Registered Nurse (RN) delivers nursing care for patients within the limits of the Nurse Practice Act of the State of Arkansas and adheres to institutional policies, procedures and standards. The RN is responsible to adhere to the standard of care defined by UAMS, ANA, and Standards for specialty patient population with support and mentoring by other team members. Collects and documents assessment data. Develops a Plan of Care (POC) per standard. Implements POC including medical order and interdisciplinary approach. Evaluates the progress of patient toward attainment of desired outcomes. Provides effective patient/family education/discharge planning. Administers medication per standard including drug information to patients/families. Acts as a resource/supports others. Delivers patient care using the principles of the defined nursing modality. Delegates care based on UAMS standards, legal and regulatory requirements, specific job description and individual level of education and training. Contributes to a positive work environment that is conducive to clinical education while serving as a resource for student nurses and staff. May perform other duties as assigned. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS Stand: Frequently Sit: Frequently Walk: Occasionally Bend, crawl, crouch, kneel, stoop or reach overhead: Frequently Lift and carry weight: 25 lbs Push and pull weight: 25 lbs Use hands to touch, handle or feel: Frequently Talk: Continuously Hear: Continuously Taste or smell: Occasionally Read, concentrate, think analytically: Continuously Physical Environment : Inside Medical Facility Environment Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Adult Maltreatment, Annual TB Screening, Child Maltreatment, Criminal Background Check, Substance Abuse Testing This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting Occasional Physical Activity: Kneeling, Lifting, Pulling, Pushing Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Extra-Help-PRN-Triple-P-Program_R0090350": {"title": "Extra Help_PRN_Triple P Program", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-26\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Clerical Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Little Rock The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is a metropolitan research university that provides an accessible, quality education through flexible learning and unparalleled internship opportunities. At UA Little Rock, we prepare our more than 8,900 students to be innovators and responsible leaders in their fields. Committed to its metropolitan research university mission, UA Little Rock is a driving force in Little Rock's thriving cultural community and a major component of the city and state's growing profile as a regional leader in research, technology transfer, economic development, and job creation. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . Department: MidSouth Department's Website: midsouth.ualr.edu Summary of Job Duties: This position is responsible for Triple P family in-home education sessions. This position has regular contact with DCFS, other public agencies, and community professionals. The Trainer is directly responsible to the Parenting Program Director. This position requires extensive in-state travel and work outside regular office hours. This position is governed by state and federal laws and agency/institution policy. Qualifications: Required Education and/or Experience: Degree in Social Work with LSW, LMSW, or LCSW licensure OR Master\u2019s degree in Psychology, Sociology, Education, or related Human/Social Science field, OR Bachelor's degree in Psychology, Sociology, Education, Social Work or related Human/Social Science field with experience working with children or families. The successful candidate will be trained and certified in Triple-P. Experience with children or families is required. Preferred Education and/or Experience: Experience in writing home assessments, psycho-social histories, in-home visiting, direct DCFS experience, or trainer/instructor experience is preferred; Appropriate professional licensure preferred, e.g.,\u00a0LMSW,\u00a0CPC Job Duties and Responsibilities: Facilitate parent education sessions for identified parents; Communicate with program participants by (phone, email, mail, virtual setting, etc.) as needed; Work with the education team to consider the individual needs of families in the program and implement programming accordingly (ex., needed accommodations such as translators, interpreters, etc.); Work with children in the family system as required by the DCFS parenting program; Assist in program documentation, evaluation, and reporting requirements. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Excellent skills in facilitating groups from diverse backgrounds; Skills in conducting home visits; Ability to use assessment tools and collect data; Ability to travel in-state; Knowledge of teaching principles and methods; Ability to coordinate and conduct training programs; Ability to prepare reports and maintain records; Ability to work outside of regular office hours is required; Ability to adapt to organizational change and handle multiple tasks; Good computer skills, including Microsoft Office. Additional Information: Please upload all required documents before hitting the \"Submit\" button. \u00a0 Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Mary Tillman, Administrative Support Manager, mjtillman@midsouth.ualr.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Child Maltreatment, Criminal Background Check, Motor Vehicle Reports Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Driving, Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding Occasional Physical Activity: Grasping, Kneeling, Repetitive Motion Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/RN---Weekend-Option---AM_R0085698-1": {"title": "RN - Weekend Option - AM", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-26\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/27/2026 Type of Position: Clinical Staff - Nursing Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | CORE PA IDHI Nursing Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Registered Nurse (RN) performs telephonic patient triage using decision-making software, assists with patient consults and transports, uses videoconferencing equipment for telemedicine operations. The RN practices within the limits of the Nurse Practice Act of the State of Arkansas and adheres to institutional policies, procedures and standards. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Graduate of an accredited Nursing Program with Associates Degree, Nursing Diploma, Bachelors in Nursing, or Master's in Nursing. \u00a0 Valid RN License\u00a0 1 year of Registered Nursing experience Excellent communication skills Basic computer skills Strong work ethics and accountability. Preferred Qualifications: Critical Care, ED experience, Phone Triage, Hospital Transfer, Case Coordination, Telephone etiquette, Labor and Delivery or High Risk antepartum service. Additional Information: Responsibilities: The Registered Nurse (RN) delivers nursing care for patients within the limits of the Nurse Practice Act of the State of Arkansas and adheres to institutional policies, procedures and standards. The RN is responsible to adhere to the standard of care defined by UAMS, ANA, and Standards for specialty patient population with support and mentoring by other team members. Collects and documents assessment data. Develops a Plan of Care (POC) per standard. Implements POC including medical order and interdisciplinary approach. Evaluates the progress of patient toward attainment of desired outcomes. Provides effective patient/family education/discharge planning. Administers medication per standard including drug information to patients/families. Acts as a resource/supports others. Delivers patient care using the principles of the defined nursing modality. Delegates care based on UAMS standards, legal and regulatory requirements, specific job description and individual level of education and training. Contributes to a positive work environment that is conducive to clinical education while serving as a resource for student nurses and staff. May perform other duties as assigned. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS Stand: Frequently Sit: Frequently Walk: Occasionally Bend, crawl, crouch, kneel, stoop or reach overhead: Frequently Lift and carry weight: 25 lbs Push and pull weight: 25 lbs Use hands to touch, handle or feel: Frequently Talk: Continuously Hear: Continuously Taste or smell: Occasionally Read, concentrate, think analytically: Continuously Physical Environment : Inside Medical Facility Environment Noise Level : Moderate Visual Requirements: Color discrimination, Depth perception, Far visual acuity, Near visual acuity Hazards: Biological, Chemical, Dust, Electrical, Fumes/Gases/Odors, Radiation, Sharp objects/tools Salary Information: commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Criminal Background Check, Substance Abuse Testing This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Standing, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Lifting Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Lead-Student-Service-Specialist_R0087033-1": {"title": "Lead Student Service Specialist", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-26\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/10/2026 Type of Position: Management - Operations Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: FIN | Student Financial Svcs Oper Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: A Lead Student Service Specialist is responsible for coordinating and overseeing complex student financial aid processes while providing guidance and support to students, families, and institutional stakeholders. This role ensures compliance with federal, state, and institutional financial aid regulations through the accurate processing, verification, awarding, and disbursement of student financial aid. Responsibilities include reviewing financial aid applications and supporting documentation, processing verifications and professional judgment requests, monitoring student aid databases, and ensuring timely and accurate awarding and disbursement activities. The Lead Student Service Specialist serves as a subject matter resource for financial aid policies and procedures, responds to inquiries from prospective and current students, parents, faculty, and staff, and assists in resolving complex financial aid concerns. This position also supports operational efficiency through daily monitoring of aid processing activities, collaboration on special projects, and participation in professional development opportunities to remain current on evolving federal and state regulations. The role contributes to student success by helping students understand and access financial aid resources while ensuring compliance, accuracy, and exceptional customer service throughout the student aid process. Qualifications: Bachelor\u2019s degree or plus five (5) years of experience in federal student aid processing or Associate's degree plus seven (7) years of experience in federal student aid processing or High School diploma/GED plus nine (9) years of experience in federal student aid processing required. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities: Workday Student experience Proficient in Microsoft applications. Responsibilities: Oversees daily management of two SFS staff members and the processing and awarding of student financial aid according to federal and state regulations. This is accomplished by obtaining the appropriate legal documentation, collecting required forms, gathering the necessary information for completing the application, and inputting all the information into the appropriate financial aid student database(s). Monitors the various databases to ensure financial aid applications are processed accurately and within the required timeframe. Oversees two SFS staff members and review/signs off on the processing of federal student aid Verifications. Prepares Title IV Return of Funds calculations. Reviews the requests for Professional Judgment. Processes private loan applications. Reviews and clears student aid disbursement rosters daily and for each College Registration cycle. Provides the optimum amount of financial aid to every student while operating within the constraints of federal and state regulations and available balances by monitoring the various student financial aid federal, state, and private databases for available student financial aid funding. Attends professional development conferences on an annual basis to stay current on regulations. Responds to inquiries via telephone, e-mail, and/or in person from prospective and current students, parents, and administrators concerning the processing and awarding of financial aid. Assists with special projects and other duties as needed. Interacts with and assists the public in a professional and friendly manner as needed. Demonstrates effective communication skills; communicates accurate and complete information; maintains strict confidentiality when necessary. Demonstrates positive working relationships with co-workers, management team, and ancillary departments; follows the Core Concepts of Patient and Family Centered Care and the Basic Code of Conduct Guidelines. Assists internal and external stakeholders as needed with exceptional customer service. Performs other duties as assigned. Additional Information: Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/RN--Medical-Oncology-Clinic_R0090633-2": {"title": "RN- Medical Oncology Clinic", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-26\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/26/2026 Type of Position: Clinical Staff - Nursing Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | CASL CA Medical Oncology Clinic Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Registered Nurse (RN) will provide direct patient care as an RN. This professional nursing role will require the ability to coordinate care for patients, triage patients, and work collaboratively with clinic providers, fellows, and staff. Requires the ability to effectively work with patient referral sources, facilitate appointments, coordinate transitions of care, and provide patient education on complex conditions. The RN will work with the individual patient, their families, and providers of care to develop and implement individual health plans. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor\u2019s degree in Nursing, Associate\u2019s degree in Nursing, Diploma RN, or Master\u2019s degree in Nursing. Must be a graduate of an accredited RN nursing program. Minimum of 1 year of Registered Nursing experience Valid Registered Nursing License Basic computer skills. Excellent communication skills. Strong work ethics and accountability. Preferred Qualifications:\u00a0 Bachelor\u2019s degree in Nursing One or more years Oncology Nursing experience Current BLS National Nursing Certification Additional Information: Responsibilities: Collects and documents assessment data from patients and/or others per UAMS standard.\u00a0 Develops patient's Plan of Care (POC) per department/unit standards utilizing assessment data.\u00a0 Evaluates the progress of patients toward attainment of desired outcomes. Administers medication following department/unit standards and Nurse Practice Act.\u00a0 Verifies and evaluates care delivered to ensure it is consistent with patient and family centered care principles, practice standards and regulatory requirements. Supports the integration of current evidence into nursing practices.\u00a0 Promotes an environment conducive to positive educational experience for all students and staff.\u00a0 Provides effective patient/family education/discharge planning. Effectively collaborates and communicates with nursing staff at all levels, interdisciplinary teams, executive leaders, and other stakeholders.\u00a0 Communicates care appropriately through documentation in the medical record. Reports variances in care/ systems/ processes through the appropriate means.\u00a0 Participates in recruitment/retention of staff.\u00a0 Facilitates development and implementation of nursing practice standards that are evidence-based and in compliance with ANA standards. May perform other duties as assigned. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Criminal Background Check, Substance Abuse Testing This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Feeling, Grasping, Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Repetitive Motion, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Crouching, Lifting, Stooping Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Patient-Care-Technician---Emergency-Department_R0081098-1": {"title": "Patient Care Technician - Emergency Department", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-26\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/26/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Shift Vary (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | EMSL UAPs OP C Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: This posting will be used to fill multiple positions The Patient Care Technician (PCT) performs patient care tasks and duties which do not require a license. The PCT is a trained member of the unit based team who supports the on-going delivery of care as identified by the multidisciplinary patient management team. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: High School Diploma/GED and successful completion of patient care technician course within 3 months of hire.\u00a0 Must have\u00a0excellent communication skills, ability to follow oral instructions, basic computer skills, strong work ethics and accountability. Must be able to lift 100 lbs. to waist height. \u200b \u00a0 Preferred Qualifications: \u00a0 Certification as a nursing assistant or military corpsman 1 year Patient care experience in acute care setting. The Patient Care Technician (PCT) works under the direct supervision of the Registered Nurse(s) and performs tasks and duties which do not require a license, professional judgment or intervention. The PCT must pass the required competencies. The PCT works within the Department of Nursing standards. The PCT adheres to UAMS clinical programs, policies, procedures and standards and guest care guidelines. Obtains patient report and has on-going communication with R.N. regarding patient care/changes in condition; Informs nurse of patient requests or complaints. Assists with admission, transfer, and discharge of patients. Transports patients to other areas of the hospital as directed. Carries out the Plan of Care for Patient using a Multidisciplinary Approach as Delegated by Team Leader. Communicates effectively with other team members to facilitate patient care. Accepts directions from R.N.s and team members. Follows through on delegated patient care activities. Provides appropriate grooming/oral hygiene and comfort measures and assists patients with activities (ambulation, up in chair, turn and reposition). Documents all patient care activities/tasks, vital signs, ADL, wave tests, I&O's accurately and timely and per unit and department standards. Assists patients and visitors with information and/or solutions to problems. Serves as resources person to support department members in performance of duties. Notifies appropriate staff members of problems requiring prompt intervention. May perform other duties as assigned. Additional Information: All new Patient Care Technicians are required to complete 5 weeks of training Monday - Friday 8:00AM - 5:00PM after being hired. Employees in this role must be fitted for, capable of donning and performing routine tasks in personal protective equipment to include N95 masks, Powered Air Purifying Respirators (PAPR) or Controlled Air Purifying Respirators (CAPR). Constant Physical Activity : Hear, Read, Concentrate, Think Analytically, Frequent Physical Activity : Stand, Walk, Talk, Use hands to touch, handle or feel, Occasional Physical Activity : Sit, Bend, crawl, crouch, kneel, stoop, reach overhead, Taste or Smell, Lift/Carry Weight: 100 Lbs. or more Push/Pull Weight: 100 Lbs. or more Physical Environment : Inside medical Facility Noise Level: Moderate Visual Requirements: Near Visual Acuity, Far Visual Acuity, Color Discrimination, Depth Perception, Peripheral Vision Hazards : Biological, Chemical, Electrical, Radiation, Sharp Objects/Tools, Dust Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Fayetteville/Assistant-Director-or-Director-of-Business-Procurement---Operations_R0090573-1": {"title": "Assistant Director or Director of Business Procurement & Operations", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-26\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com, then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at all University of Arkansas institutions will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students.\u201d University of Arkansas, Fayetteville students will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Student Jobs at UAF.\u201d All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. Closing Date: 09/02/2026 Type of Position: Procurement Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas, Fayetteville Founded in 1871, the University of Arkansas is a land grant institution, classified by the Carnegie Foundation among the nation\u2019s top 2 percent of universities with the highest level of research activity. The University of Arkansas works to advance the state and build a better world through education, research, and outreach by providing transformational opportunities and skills, fostering a welcoming climate, and nurturing creativity, discovery, and the spread of new ideas and innovations. The University of Arkansas campus is located in Fayetteville, a welcoming community ranked as one of the best places to live in the U.S. The growing region surrounding Fayetteville is home to numerous Fortune 500 companies and one of the nation\u2019s strongest economies. Northwest Arkansas is also quickly gaining a national reputation for its focus on the arts and overall quality of life. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10% of employee salary. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions, you should review before applying for the opening. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process, please submit a request via the Disability Accommodations | OEOC | University of Arkansas (uark.edu) : Request an Accommodation. Appli\u00adcants are required to submit a request for each position of which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 479.575.5351. Department: Internal Engagement, Finance and Capital Projects Department's Website: https://arkansasrazorbacks.com/ https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=j9ihImu88OQ&t=9s Summary of Job Duties: The Assistant Director OR Director of Business Procurement & Operations will report to the Associate Athletic Director Finance & Reporting and work with the Senior Associate Athletic Director/CFO and the General Counsel for Athletics. The role supports the financial and operational functions of the Athletic Business Office. The responsibilities for this position will be immersed in the depths of the business office: procurement process, contract flow, primary contact for assigned sports/units, researching best practice, supporting the unit\u2019s processes, and aiding in additional finance tasks in Workday. This position will be asked to help implement a new contract management system. The ideal candidate is highly organized, detail-oriented, process-driven, and comfortable working across multiple departments while handling confidential and sensitive information. Regular, reliable, and non-disruptive attendance is an essential job duty, as is the ability to create and maintain collegial, harmonious working relationships with others. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Assistant Director: \u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Master\u2019s degree in Business, Finance, Accounting, Sports Management, related degree, or related professional certification such as CPA, CMA AND at least one year relevant experience OR Bachelor\u2019s degree in Business, Finance, Accounting, or Sports Management with at least more than one year of relevant experience OR Bachelor\u2019s degree with more than three years of relevant experience Director: Master\u2019s degree in Business, Finance, Accounting, Sports Management, related degree, or related professional certification such as CPA, CMA with at least three years of relevant experience OR Bachelor\u2019s degree in Business, Finance, Accounting, or Sports Management with at least five years of relevant experience OR Bachelor\u2019s degree with at least more than five years of relevant experience Relevant Experience: Accounting, Procurement, Contracting, Project Management or Athletic Operations \u00a0 Preferred Qualifications: At least 3 years of experience with administrative support in a professional setting At least 3 years of experience with business and fiscal related duties At least 3 years of experience with procurement or contract functions At least 3 years of experience with Workday or similar Enterprise Resource Planning systems At least 3 years of experience with contract management or project management software At least 1 year of experience Leveraging AI to Solve Problems Knowledge, Skills, & Abilities: Knowledge of business operations and administrative functions within a complex professional organization, including procurement, purchasing, travel, fiscal management, and related business processes Knowledge of applicable University policies, NCAA, SEC, state and federal laws, regulations, and guidelines governing assigned areas of responsibility Knowledge of procurement practices, contract administration, purchasing processes, and applicable fiscal policies and procedures Knowledge of financial and business systems, computer applications, and software used to manage and analyze operational and fiscal data Knowledge of communication, customer service, and relationship management techniques in a cross functional department Knowledge of computers, Microsoft Office Suite, and software application programs Knowledge of how to leverage artificial intelligence and emerging technologies to improve business processes, efficiency, and decision-making Ability to prepare, analyze, and present professional reports, findings, recommendations, and other business documents to leadership Ability to record, reconcile, analyze, and manipulate fiscal data to generate complex reports and support informed decision-making Ability to conduct research, perform quantitative and qualitative analyses, and complete quality assurance reviews to ensure accuracy and compliance Ability to learn in a fast-paced environment and support the advancement of the organization Ability to solve problems and present alternative solutions Ability to identify opportunities for improvement while developing solutions. Ability to work nights and weekends if needed Additional Information: Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Recruitment Contact Information: Krista Hoover, Senior HR Partner - Athletics, kristah@uark.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Special Instructions to Applicants: Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Financial Credit Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas seeks to attract, develop and retain high quality faculty, staff and administrators that consistently display practices and behaviors to advance a culture that embeds equal opportunity, educational excellence and unparalleled access for all. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All Application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Fayetteville-AR/Departmental-Accountant_R0090407-1": {"title": "Departmental Accountant", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-26\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/03/2026 Type of Position: Professional Staff - Project/Program Administration Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: Division of Agriculture of the University of Arkansas The University of Arkansas System Division of Agriculture is a state wide campus, with faculty based on University campuses, at Research and Extension Centers and in every Arkansas county. It consists of the Arkansas Agricultural Experiment Station (AES) and the Arkansas Cooperative Extension Service (CES), and is home to more than 1400 employees.\u00a0 The Division was established in 1959 and is headed by the Vice-President for Agriculture.\u00a0 The Division headquarters is located in Little Rock with the rest of the University of Arkansas System Administration.\u00a0 As an employer, the University of Arkansas System Division of Agriculture offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance.\u00a0 Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process and require reasonable accommodations, please contact the Division's Office of Program & Employment Compliance at compliance@uada.edu . For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-671-2219 or 479-502-9820. Department: CSES | Crop, Soil and Environmental Sciences Department's Website: https://crop-soil-environmental-sciences.uark.edu/ Summary of Job Duties: The Departmental Accountant will serve as a key financial resource for the department, working closely with the Department Head, faculty, staff, students, and other UADA and UARK offices. This position is well suited for someone who brings strong accounting skills, enjoys working collaboratively to solve problems, and finds purpose in helping others navigate financial processes so they can accomplish their work and advance the department\u2019s mission of teaching, research, extension, and service. The Departmental Accountant will maintain positive and proactive working relationships with department personnel; communicate financial information and purchasing policies clearly; oversee purchasing in the department and ensure compliance with applicable requirements; manage and provide monthly financial reports for state, grant, Foundation, and service center accounts and recommend action as needed to the Department Head and faculty; maintain salary distributions for department employees; assist with preparation of the annual operations budget; oversee and act as backup for vehicle fleet reporting and travel claims; investigate and resolve accounting discrepancies and irregularities; and other duties as assigned. The Departmental Accountant will work closely with faculty, staff, and students to understand their financial needs, clearly communicate applicable requirements, and help identify appropriate solutions and next steps. The position will also proactively communicate deadlines, funding concerns, potential delays, and other financial matters that may affect departmental operations. The Departmental Accountant will supervise two accounting staff and is responsible for creating a positive, helpful, and team-focused work environment that values accuracy, timeliness, communication, teamwork, cross-training, and good service. Qualifications: Minimum qualifications: Bachelor's degree in accounting. Bachelor's degree in a related field may be accepted with two years of accounting experience. Preferred qualifications: Experience as a supervisor or manager. Experience with Workday or similar accounting software system. Knowledge and experience working in higher education or government. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Strong knowledge of accounting principles, financial statements, ledgers, and financial reporting, with a commitment to accuracy and responsible stewardship of departmental resources. Ability to analyze financial information, anticipate concerns, solve problems, and provide clear guidance that helps others make informed decisions. Ability to interpret and apply laws, policies, and financial requirements while helping faculty, staff, and students understand how to successfully navigate those requirements. Ability to listen and understand what others are trying to accomplish, then work collaboratively to identify appropriate solutions and next steps. Ability to build positive working relationships, communicate with clarity and respect, and contribute to a team culture where people share knowledge, support one another, and work toward common goals. Proficiency with Microsoft Office, particularly Excel, and Workday Financials or similar systems, with a willingness to continually learn and improve processes that better support the department. Additional Information: Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Tabatha Gonzalez, Dept. Manager, tabathag@uark.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Motor Vehicle Reports Check The University of Arkansas System Division of Agriculture may conduct pre-employment background checks on certain positions for applicants being considered for employment. \u00a0 The background checks may include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. \u00a0 Required checks are identified in the position listing. \u00a0 A criminal background check or arrest pending adjudication information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absences of a relationship to the requirements of the position. \u00a0 Background check information will be used in a consistent, non-discriminatory manner consistent with the state and federal law. \u00a0 The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Repetitive Motion, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Standing, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Kneeling Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Fayetteville-AR/Public-Safety-Security-Officer_R0090100-1": {"title": "Public Safety/Security Officer", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-25\nPosted: Posted 10 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com, then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at all University of Arkansas institutions will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students.\u201d University of Arkansas, Fayetteville students will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Student Jobs at UAF.\u201d All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. Closing Date: 12/31/2027 Type of Position: Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Shift Vary (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas, Fayetteville Founded in 1871, the University of Arkansas is a land grant institution, classified by the Carnegie Foundation among the nation\u2019s top 2 percent of universities with the highest level of research activity. The University of Arkansas works to advance the state and build a better world through education, research, and outreach by providing transformational opportunities and skills, fostering a welcoming climate, and nurturing creativity, discovery, and the spread of new ideas and innovations. The University of Arkansas campus is located in Fayetteville, a welcoming community ranked as one of the best places to live in the U.S. The growing region surrounding Fayetteville is home to numerous Fortune 500 companies and one of the nation\u2019s strongest economies. Northwest Arkansas is also quickly gaining a national reputation for its focus on the arts and overall quality of life. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10% of employee salary. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions, you should review before applying for the opening. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process, please submit a request via the Disability Accommodations | OEOC | University of Arkansas (uark.edu) : Request an Accommodation. Appli\u00adcants are required to submit a request for each position of which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 479.575.5351. Department: Police Services Lieutenant Department's Website: https://uapd.uark.edu/ Summary of Job Duties: The Public Safety/Security Officer provides a variety of security and safety related functions while involved in safeguarding students, faculty, staff, and visitors. This position provides security for equipment and real property in assigned areas. The Public Safety/Security Officer communicates effectively and respectfully with members of the campus community, supervisors, and peers. This position provides information and directions as needed. May be assigned to a specific zone or geographical work area. Regular, reliable, and non-disruptive attendance is an essential job function of this job, as is the ability to create and maintain collegial, harmonious working relationships with others Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: The formal education equivalent of a high school diploma\u00a0 Preferred Qualifications: Experience in a security related field Completion of 30 educational hours at an institution of higher education Certification in CPR Additional Information: Pre-employment Screening Requirements:\u00a0 Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry Check, Financial Credit Check, Substance Abuse Testing, Motor Vehicle Registry Check. Please Note: \u00a0This posting will be used to collect applications to fill current openings as well as anticipated future openings. Future openings are anticipated but not guaranteed. This posting will expire on the posting end date indicated. Applicants wishing to be considered after this date must reapply. Salary Information: $42,000 Required Documents to Apply: List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Proof of Veteran Status Recruitment Contact Information: Ben Velasco, Administrative Police Lieutenant, bvelasc@uark.edu, Caitlin Hughes, Strategic Talent Acquisition Specialist, cmmitche@uark.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Special Instructions to Applicants: Special Instructions to Applicants Physical Demands of Position: Light Work | Exerting up to 20 pounds of force occasionally, and/or up to 10 pounds of force frequently, and/or a negligible amount of force constantly to move objects. If the use of force is greater than that for sedentary work and the worker sits most of the time, the job is rated for light work. Employee is required to have close visual acuity to perform an activity such as: preparing and analyzing data and figures; transcribing; viewing a computer terminal; extensive reading; and/or visual inspection at distances close to the eyes. Employee is required to have visual acuity to operate motor vehicles and/or heavy equipment. The employee is subject to inside environmental conditions. Protection from weather conditions but not necessarily from temperature changes. The employee is subject to outside environmental conditions. No effective protection from the weather. This position is weather/event essential and approved for shift differential. The employee is subject to noise. Employee may be subject to noise that would required shouting in order to be heard above ambient noise level. Physical Activities Associated with Position: Constant: Hearing, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Frequent: Driving, Feeling, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Repetitive Motion Occasional: Balancing, Climbing, Crawling. Crouching, Grasping Pre-employment Screening Requirements: The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas seeks to attract, develop and retain high quality faculty, staff and administrators that consistently display practices and behaviors to advance a culture that embeds equal opportunity, educational excellence and unparalleled access for all. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All Application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Fayetteville-AR/Police-Officer-Recruit_R0090095-1": {"title": "Police Officer/Recruit", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-25\nPosted: Posted 10 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com, then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at all University of Arkansas institutions will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students.\u201d University of Arkansas, Fayetteville students will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Student Jobs at UAF.\u201d All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. Closing Date: 12/31/2027 Type of Position: Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Shift Vary (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas, Fayetteville Founded in 1871, the University of Arkansas is a land grant institution, classified by the Carnegie Foundation among the nation\u2019s top 2 percent of universities with the highest level of research activity. The University of Arkansas works to advance the state and build a better world through education, research, and outreach by providing transformational opportunities and skills, fostering a welcoming climate, and nurturing creativity, discovery, and the spread of new ideas and innovations. The University of Arkansas campus is located in Fayetteville, a welcoming community ranked as one of the best places to live in the U.S. The growing region surrounding Fayetteville is home to numerous Fortune 500 companies and one of the nation\u2019s strongest economies. Northwest Arkansas is also quickly gaining a national reputation for its focus on the arts and overall quality of life. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10% of employee salary. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions, you should review before applying for the opening. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process, please submit a request via the Disability Accommodations | OEOC | University of Arkansas (uark.edu) : Request an Accommodation. Appli\u00adcants are required to submit a request for each position of which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 479.575.5351. Department: Police Services Lieutenant Department's Website: https://uapd.uark.edu/ Summary of Job Duties: The Police Officer/Recruit is certified by the State of Arkansas to enforce law and safeguard our campus community. Primary responsibilities include the following: Engage with members of the community to build positive relationships, address community issues, and promote trust and cooperation. Conduct proactive patrols in assigned areas to deter criminal activity and maintain order. Enforce traffic laws and regulations, conduct traffic enforcement and respond to accidents to ensure road safety. Respond promptly to emergency calls and incidents, ensuring public safety and providing assistance as needed. Collaborate with other law enforcement agencies, emergency services, and community organizations to address public safety concern and implement crime prevention strategies. Maintain accurate records of incidents, arrests, and activities and prepare detailed reports for documentation and analysis. This position is governed by law enforcement standards, state and federal laws, and agency policy. Regular, reliable, and non-disruptive attendance is an essential job duty, as is the ability to create and maintain collegial, harmonious working relationships with others Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications:\u00a0 The formal education equivalent of a high school diploma\u00a0 Must possess a valid state motor vehicle operators license\u00a0 Must be a United States Citizen Must be at least 20 years + 6 months of age Per the Commission on Law Enforcement Standards and Training (CLEST) - Rule 1002: Every officer employed by a law enforcement agency must be a citizen of the United State of America or a Marshallese citizen and must be at least twenty-one (21) years of age at the time of hire Additional Information: Pre-employment Screening Requirements: \u00a0Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry, Financial Credit Check, Substance Abuse Testing, Motor Vehicle Registry. Please Note: \u00a0This posting will be used to collect applications to fill current openings as well as anticipated future openings. Future openings are anticipated but not guaranteed. This posting will expire on the posting end date indicated. Applicants wishing to be considered after this date must reapply. Salary Information: Starting rate $55,000 after academy certification $61,000 Required Documents to Apply: List of five Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Proof of Veteran Status Recruitment Contact Information: Ben Velasco, Administrative Police Lieutenant, bvelasc@uark.edu, Caitlin Hughes, Strategic Talent Acquisition Specialist, cmmitche@uark.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Special Instructions to Applicants: Special Instructions to Applicants Physical Demands of Position: Heavy Work: Exerting up to 100 pounds of force occasionally, and/or up to 30 pounds of force frequently, and/or up to 10 pounds of force constantly to move objects. Visual Acuity: Employee is required to have close visual acuity to perform an activity such as: preparing and analyzing data and figures; transcribing; viewing a computer terminal; extensive reading; and/or visual inspection at distances close to the eyes; visual acuity to determine the accuracy, neatness, and thoroughness of the work assigned or to make general observations of facilities or structures; visual acuity to operate motor vehicles and/or heavy equipment. The employee is subject to environmental conditions. Activities occur inside and outside and may subject employee to extreme cold or heat and to other environmental conditions such as wind and humidity. The employee is subject to noise. Employee may be subject to noise that would required shouting in order to be heard above ambient noise level. Physical Activities Associated with Position: Constant: driving, hearing, manipulate items with fingers (including keyboard), reaching, repetitive motion, sitting, standing, talking, walking Frequent: balancing, grasping, kneeling, lifting, pulling, pushing Occasional: climbing, crawling, crouching, feeling, stooping Pre-employment Screening Requirements: The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas seeks to attract, develop and retain high quality faculty, staff and administrators that consistently display practices and behaviors to advance a culture that embeds equal opportunity, educational excellence and unparalleled access for all. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All Application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/OR-Surgical-Technician--TOSH_R0090564-1": {"title": "OR Surgical Technician -TOSH", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-25\nPosted: Posted 10 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/25/2026 Type of Position: Clinical Staff - Medical Ancillary Support Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | MUSL | TOSH Operating Room Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: As individuals dedicated to ensuring the safety and quick recovery of our patients, surgical technologists are integral members of a team dedicated to providing the best care for patients through collaboration, communication and patient safety. As part of the TOSH teams, operating room scrub technicians define their practice through attention to detail with excellence and outstanding patient care, are driven by their expertise, compassion and dedication to evidence-based practice, and operate at a higher level of practice. If you are a Surgical Technician who has current Operating Room experience, we invite you to consider a career with The Orthopaedic & Spine Hospital at UAMS Health. The Surgical Technician will assembles supplies for surgical procedures, set up and maintains the sterile field, passes surgical instruments, and assists in room preparation. This professional nursing role will require the ability to coordinate care the needs for the surgical case the surgeon, nurses, other members of the team to provide an optimal outcome for the patient and work collaboratively with clinic providers, fellows, and staff. Requires the ability to effectively communicate. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: High School Diploma or GED NBSTSA-accredited Surgical Technology program OR NCCT-approved Surgical Technology program OR completed military surgical/scrub tech training OR have two or more years of on-the-job surgical/scrub experience in an acute care facility or ambulatory surgery center. Additional Information: Responsibilities: Assessment of the surgical procedure. Ensures availability of appropriate instrumentation, supplies and equipment for assigned cases. Preparation of the OR. Ensures that the room has been prepared for the upcoming cases, with appropriate equipment available and ready for surgical use. Ensures that the instruments are cleaned arranged and transported to the soiled workroom according to department policy. Independently assists with instrument reprocessing tasks when assigned cases are completed and time permits. Ensures that the operating rooms are ready for the following day\u2019s cases. Exhibits practical knowledge of OR equipment including maintenance and safety aspects. Utilizes available communication tools. Demonstrates teamwork by offering assistance to other team members. Shares knowledge of information and expertise with other staff. Attends departmental in-services and other educational offerings. Consistently demonstrates new knowledge and skills through incorporation into actual clinical practice. Willing to learn new techniques. \u00a0Other duties assigned Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry, Substance Abuse Testing This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding Frequent Physical Activity: Balancing, Feeling, Grasping, Kneeling, Lifting, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Repetitive Motion, Sharps, Standing, Stooping, Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Climbing, Sitting Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Medical-Laboratory-Scientist-II--Reference-Lab_R0090601-2": {"title": "Medical Laboratory Scientist II- Reference Lab", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-25\nPosted: Posted 10 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/08/2026 Type of Position: Other Health Care - Medical Ancillary Support Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Shift Vary (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | LPSL CPATH Reference Lab Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Medical Laboratory Scientist II (MLS II) receives specimens from IP, OP Clinics, External Entities, and UAMS Health Regional Programs. The MLS II verifies each specimen has proper collection and labeling, and each test is received in the correct tube type. This Position\u2019s schedule is Monday Thru Friday 10:30 am to 7:00pm Qualifications: \u200bMinimum Qualifications: Bachelor of Science Degree in Medical Laboratory Sciences, Medical Technology, or an ASCP approved discipline. - Minimum 2 years of experience in a Clinical Laboratory -ASCP certification or equivalent Additional Information: Job Requirements: Sends out specimens to referral laboratories according to hospital and laboratory policies and in accordance with state and federal regulations. \u00a0Enters results from referral laboratories into the laboratory information system. \u00a0Assists clients with ordering the correct reference tests and performs research into potential new referral laboratories. \u00a0 Consults with pathologists and other experts as needed for reference test requests. \u00a0 Assists with inventory needs. Process add-on tests, answers phone calls concerning results, fax reports, collect specimens and order tests. The MLS II is responsible for calling critical results to licensed personnel in a timely manner. This position is responsible for coordinating incoming calls to the laboratory. This position is responsible for making sure all necessary forms or reports are received by requesting providers.\u00a0 Perform other duties as needed. \u00a0 PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS Stand: Frequently Sit: Frequently Walk: Occasionally Bend, crawl, crouch, kneel, stoop or reach overhead: Frequently Lift and carry weight: 25 lbs Push and pull weight: 25 lbs Use hands to touch, handle or feel: Frequently Talk: Continuously Hear: Continuously Taste or smell: Occasionally Read, concentrate, think analytically: Continuously Physical Environment : Inside Medical Facility Environment Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), Proof of Veteran Status, Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Criminal Background Check, Substance Abuse Testing This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Feeling, Grasping, Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding Frequent Physical Activity: Kneeling, Reaching, Repetitive Motion, Sitting, Standing, Stooping, Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Crouching, N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/COSMOS---Postdoctoral-Fellow-IV_R0090541": {"title": "COSMOS \u2013 Postdoctoral Fellow IV", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-25\nPosted: Posted 10 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Researchers Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Little Rock The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is a metropolitan research university that provides an accessible, quality education through flexible learning and unparalleled internship opportunities. At UA Little Rock, we prepare our more than 8,900 students to be innovators and responsible leaders in their fields. Committed to its metropolitan research university mission, UA Little Rock is a driving force in Little Rock's thriving cultural community and a major component of the city and state's growing profile as a regional leader in research, technology transfer, economic development, and job creation. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . Department: COSMOS - Provisional Positions Department's Website: https://cosmos.ualr.edu/ Summary of Job Duties: The Postdoctoral Fellow position is a full-time, provisional position with the COSMOS Research Center (cosmos.ualr.edu) at the University of Arkansas and is funded through a grant or contract. The position renewal is contingent upon continued grant funding and satisfactory job performance. Postdoctoral Fellow will develop socio-computational models to advance our understanding of cyber campaigns run on social media, grounded in the dynamics of various social and communication processes such as group formation, activation, decentralized decision-making, and collective action. The Postdoctoral Fellow will help extract relevant open-source information in a guided snowball data collection manner by leveraging cyber forensics and deep web search-based methodologies. Postdoctoral Fellow will work with the research team in developing predictive models of various socio-technical behaviors on different social media platforms (including multimedia-rich platforms), and usable tools/software to identify key actors and key groups responsible for coordinating cyber campaigns and disseminating propaganda. This is an on-campus position. This position is governed by state and federal laws, and agency/institution policy. The position reports to Prof. Nitin Agarwal (nxagarwal@ualr.edu), Maulden-Entergy Endowed Chair & Donaghey Distinguished Professor, and Director, COSMOS Research Center at UA-Little Rock. Qualifications: Required Education and/or Experience: The candidate must have a Ph.D. degree in Computer Science, Information Science, or a related discipline; The candidate must have 4+ years of research experience in social media mining, computational modeling of social science theories, working with social network analysis tools, and examining cyber campaigns conducted on social media. The research experience must be demonstrated through published research articles in leading journals and conferences relevant to the topics mentioned above; and The candidate must have 3+ years of experience in grant writing and management. Grant writing experience must be demonstrated through a successful grant acquisition and management record. Preferred Education and/or Experience: Candidates with extensive research experience in computer programming and data management will be given preference. Candidates with successful grant-writing experience and a strong publication record will be given preference. Job Duties and Responsibilities: Prepare, submit, and manage multiple grants for extramural funding; Manage multiple projects (e.g., setting and tracking deadlines and progress of team members, providing reports to the supervisor); Lead project meetings, including agenda setting and minute-taking; Provide oversight for complex or multi-faceted research projects and help shape strategic direction; Contribute to the conceptualization and development of new research project ideas; Expand the collaboration network and partnerships with the Center; Conduct social media analysis to support research projects, including hypothesis generation, behavioral evaluation, data collection, cleaning, preprocessing, and analysis; Analyze multimedia-rich content within online information environments; Document and communicate research findings through reports, publications, and presentations at conferences, scientific venues, program reviews, and other professional settings; Develop and implement software modules to transition research outcomes into practical tools. Train stakeholders in the use and application of research methodologies and developed tools; Mentor and oversee graduate students involved in research, supporting their development and gaining valuable academic leadership experience; Perform other duties and provide additional support as assigned. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Expert in data analysis, modeling, machine learning, and AI, using Python and SQL, with extensive experience in libraries and frameworks such as Pandas, NumPy, scikit-learn, Gensim, BERTopic, TensorFlow, PyTorch, and LLMs; Expert in data visualization using Matplotlib, Seaborn, and ggplot2, and experienced in managing research projects with tools like Git/GitHub, ClickUp, and Jupyter Notebooks; Expert in NLP, text mining, and graph analytics, including the use of NLTK, spaCy, TextBlob, VADER, and transformer-based models (e.g., BERT, GPT); Expert in social network analysis (SNA) using NetworkX, igraph, and Gephi for complex network and graph-based data exploration; Successful research grant writing and management record for federal (e.g., NSF, DoD, NIH) and state (e.g., ARA) funding agencies and foundations; Expert in computational social science and social network analysis; Demonstrated expertise in social media mining and analysis of cyber campaigns; Extensive experience in studying multimedia-rich social media platforms and their impacts; Expert in qualitative data collection and analysis techniques; Proven ability to transition research into practical, user-oriented tools; Strong programming skills and experience with data management and analysis tools; Excellent interpersonal skills, with the ability to work effectively with individuals from diverse disciplinary backgrounds; Superior written and verbal communication skills, including public speaking, technical writing, and collaborative communication; Experience supervising and mentoring student researchers and managing team dynamics; Excellent organizational and project management skills with the ability to prioritize tasks and meet multiple deadlines; Ability to work independently and collaboratively within interdisciplinary research teams. Additional Information: Salary Information: $110,000 annual Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Letters of Recommendation, Listing of Publications, List of five Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume, Statement of Research Philosophy Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Prof. Nitin Agarwal <nxagarwal@ualr.edu> Jerry L. Maulden-Entergy Chair and Donaghey Distinguished Professor Director, COSMOS Research Center All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Repetitive Motion, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Repetitive Motion, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Repetitive Motion, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/RN---Radiation-Oncology-Clinic_R0090565-1": {"title": "RN - Radiation Oncology Clinic", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-25\nPosted: Posted 10 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/25/2026 Type of Position: Clinical Staff - Nursing Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | CASL CA ROC Clinical Ops Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Registered Nurse (RN) will provide direct patient care as an RN. This professional nursing role will require the ability to coordinate care for patients, triage patients, and work collaboratively with clinic providers, fellows, and staff. Requires the ability to effectively work with patient referral sources, facilitate appointments, coordinate transitions of care, and provide patient education on complex conditions. The RN will work with the individual patient, their families, and providers of care to develop and implement individual health plans. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: G raduate of an accredited Nursing Program with Associates Degree, Nursing Diploma, Bachelors in Nursing, or Master's in Nursing\u00a0 Valid RN License Minimum of 1 year Registered Nursing experience Additional Information: Responsibilities: Collects and documents assessment data from patients and/or others per UAMS standard.\u00a0 Develops patient's Plan of Care (POC) per department/unit standards utilizing assessment data.\u00a0 Evaluates the progress of patients toward attainment of desired outcomes. Administers medication following department/unit standards and Nurse Practice Act.\u00a0 Verifies and evaluates care delivered to ensure it is consistent with patient and family centered care principles, practice standards and regulatory requirements. Supports the integration of current evidence into nursing practices.\u00a0 Promotes an environment conducive to positive educational experience for all students and staff.\u00a0 Provides effective patient/family education/discharge planning. Effectively collaborates and communicates with nursing staff at all levels, interdisciplinary teams, executive leaders, and other stakeholders.\u00a0 Communicates care appropriately through documentation in the medical record. Reports variances in care/ systems/ processes through the appropriate means.\u00a0 Participates in recruitment/retention of staff.\u00a0 Facilitates development and implementation of nursing practice standards that are evidence-based and in compliance with ANA standards. May perform other duties as assigned. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Criminal Background Check, Substance Abuse Testing This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Crawling, Crouching, Feeling, Grasping, Hearing, Kneeling, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Reaching, Repetitive Motion, Stooping Frequent Physical Activity: Lifting, Pulling, Pushing, Sharps, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Balancing, Climbing Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/COSMOS---Postdoctoral-Fellow-III_R0090537": {"title": "COSMOS \u2013 Postdoctoral Fellow III", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-25\nPosted: Posted 10 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Researchers Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Little Rock The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is a metropolitan research university that provides an accessible, quality education through flexible learning and unparalleled internship opportunities. At UA Little Rock, we prepare our more than 8,900 students to be innovators and responsible leaders in their fields. Committed to its metropolitan research university mission, UA Little Rock is a driving force in Little Rock's thriving cultural community and a major component of the city and state's growing profile as a regional leader in research, technology transfer, economic development, and job creation. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . Department: COSMOS - Provisional Positions Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Postdoctoral Fellow position is a full-time, provisional position with the COSMOS Research Center (cosmos.ualr.edu) at the University of Arkansas and is funded through a grant or contract. The position renewal is contingent upon continued grant funding and satisfactory job performance. Postdoctoral Fellow will develop socio-computational models to advance our understanding of cyber campaigns run on social media, grounded in the dynamics of various social and communication processes such as group formation, activation, decentralized decision-making, and collective action. The Postdoctoral Fellow will help extract relevant open-source information in a guided snowball data collection manner by leveraging cyber forensics and deep web search-based methodologies. Postdoctoral Fellow will work with the research team in developing predictive models of various socio-technical behaviors on different social media platforms (including multimedia-rich platforms), and usable tools/software to identify key actors and key groups responsible for coordinating cyber campaigns and disseminating propaganda. This is an on-campus position. This position is governed by state and federal laws, and agency/institution policy. The position reports to Prof. Nitin Agarwal (nxagarwal@ualr.edu), Maulden-Entergy Endowed Chair, Distinguished Professor, and Director, COSMOS Research Center at UA-Little Rock. Qualifications: Required Education and/or Experience:\u00a0 The candidate must have a Ph.D. degree in Computer Science, Information Science, or a related discipline; The candidate must have 3+ years of research experience in social media mining, computational modeling of social science theories, working with social network analysis tools, and examining cyber campaigns conducted on social media. The research experience must be demonstrated through published research articles in leading journals and conferences relevant to the topics mentioned above; and The candidate must have 1+ years of experience in grant writing and management. Grant writing experience must be demonstrated through a successful grant acquisition and management record. Preferred Education and/or Experience:\u00a0 Candidates with extensive research experience in computer programming and data management will be given preference. Candidates with successful grant-writing experience and a strong publication record will be given preference. Job Duties and Responsibilities:\u00a0 Prepare and submit grant applications for external funding; Project management (e.g., setting and tracking deadlines and progress of team members, providing reports to the supervisor); Lead and coordinate project meetings, including agenda setting and minute-taking; Assist in developing new research initiatives aligned with the Center\u2019s mission; Manage complex research projects, offering strategic direction and oversight; Conduct social media analysis to support research projects, including ideation, hypothesis generation, data collection, preprocessing, and analysis of cyber behaviors; Analyze multimedia-rich content within online information environments; Synthesize research findings into written reports and scholarly publications, and present at conferences, program reviews, and other scientific venues; Develop software modules to operationalize and transition research outcomes into practical tools; Support stakeholder training in research methodologies and developed tools; Mentor and oversee graduate students involved in research, preparing for an academic or professional career; Perform other duties and provide additional support as assigned. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities:\u00a0 Advanced in data analysis, modeling, machine learning, and AI, using Python and SQL, with extensive experience in libraries and frameworks such as Pandas, NumPy, scikit-learn, Gensim, BERTopic, TensorFlow, PyTorch, and LLMs; Advanced in data visualization using Matplotlib, Seaborn, and ggplot2, and experienced in managing research projects with tools like Git/GitHub, ClickUp, and Jupyter Notebooks; Advanced in NLP, text mining, and graph analytics, including the use of NLTK, spaCy, TextBlob, VADER, and transformer-based models (e.g., BERT, GPT); Familiar with social network analysis (SNA) using NetworkX, igraph, and Gephi for complex network and graph-based data exploration; Successful research grant writing and management record for federal (e.g., NSF, DoD) and state (e.g., ARA) funding agencies and foundations; Advanced understanding of research methodologies, data collection strategies, and statistical/analytical techniques; Advanced in computational social science, including social network analysis and social media mining; Extensive experience researching cyber campaigns on social media platforms; Skilled in analyzing multimedia content in dynamic and complex online environments; Proficient in qualitative and mixed-methods data collection and analysis; Demonstrated ability to translate research into usable, operational tools or applications; Strong computer programming and data management skills; Culturally competent and able to work effectively with individuals from diverse disciplinary backgrounds; Exceptional written and verbal communication skills for scholarly publication, collaboration, and public engagement; Experience supervising and mentoring student researchers and volunteers; Excellent organizational and project management capabilities, with the ability to prioritize and manage multiple tasks and deadlines; Proven ability to work both independently and collaboratively within a multidisciplinary research team. Additional Information: Salary Information: $95,000 annual Required Documents to Apply: Letters of Recommendation, Listing of Publications, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Prof. Nitin Agarwal <nxagarwal@ualr.edu> Jerry L. Maulden-Entergy Chair and Donaghey Distinguished Professor Director, COSMOS Research Center All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Repetitive Motion, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Repetitive Motion, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Repetitive Motion, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/COSMOS---Postdoctoral-Fellow-II_R0090538": {"title": "COSMOS - Postdoctoral Fellow II", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-25\nPosted: Posted 10 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Researchers Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Little Rock The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is a metropolitan research university that provides an accessible, quality education through flexible learning and unparalleled internship opportunities. At UA Little Rock, we prepare our more than 8,900 students to be innovators and responsible leaders in their fields. Committed to its metropolitan research university mission, UA Little Rock is a driving force in Little Rock's thriving cultural community and a major component of the city and state's growing profile as a regional leader in research, technology transfer, economic development, and job creation. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . Department: COSMOS - Provisional Positions Department's Website: https://cosmos.ualr.edu/ Summary of Job Duties: The Postdoctoral Fellow position is a full-time, provisional position with the COSMOS Research Center (cosmos.ualr.edu) at the University of Arkansas and is funded through a grant or contract. The position renewal is contingent upon continued grant funding and satisfactory job performance. Postdoctoral Fellow will develop socio-computational models to advance our understanding of cyber campaigns run on social media, grounded in the dynamics of various social and communication processes such as group formation, activation, decentralized decision-making, and collective action. The Postdoctoral Fellow will help extract relevant open-source information in a guided snowball data collection manner by leveraging cyber forensics and deep web search-based methodologies. Postdoctoral Fellow will work with the research team in developing predictive models of various socio-technical behaviors on different social media platforms (including multimedia-rich platforms), and usable tools/software to identify key actors and key groups responsible for coordinating cyber campaigns and disseminating propaganda. This is an on-campus position. This position is governed by state and federal laws, and agency/institution policy. The position reports to Prof. Nitin Agarwal (nxagarwal@ualr.edu), Maulden-Entergy Endowed Chair & Donaghey Distinguished Professor, and Director, COSMOS Research Center at UA-Little Rock. Qualifications: Required Education and/or Experience: \u00a0 The candidate must have a Ph.D. degree in Computer Science, Information Science, or a related discipline; The candidate must have 2+ years of research experience in social media mining, computational modeling of social science theories, working with social network analysis tools, and examining cyber campaigns conducted on social media. The research experience must be demonstrated through published research articles in leading journals and conferences relevant to the topics mentioned above. Preferred Education and/or Experience: \u00a0 Candidates with extensive research experience in computer programming and data management will be given preference. Candidates with grant-writing experience and a strong publication record will be given preference. Job Duties and Responsibilities: \u00a0 Conduct social media analysis to support research projects, including ideation, hypothesis generation, and evaluation of cyber behaviors; Lead tasks in data collection, cleaning, preprocessing, analysis, and interpretation; Analyze multimedia-rich online information environments to identify patterns and trends; Dissemination of findings through reports, publications, and presentations at conferences, scientific meetings, program reviews, and other venues; Contribute substantially to the preparation of grant proposals and technical reports; Develop software modules to integrate research outcomes into practical tools and applications; Provide training and technical assistance to stakeholders on research findings, methodologies, and developed tools; Project management (e.g., setting and tracking deadlines and progress of team members, providing reports to the supervisor); Mentor and supervise graduate students involved in research projects, preparing for a potential future academic career; Organize and coordinate research team meetings (involving researchers and data engineers), lead discussions, and document meeting minutes; \u00b7 Perform other duties and provide additional support as assigned. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: \u00a0 Proficient in data analysis, modeling, machine learning, and AI, using Python and SQL, with extensive experience in libraries and frameworks such as Pandas, NumPy, scikit-learn, Gensim, BERTopic, TensorFlow, PyTorch, and LLMs; Skilled in data visualization using Matplotlib, Seaborn, and ggplot2, and experienced in managing research projects with tools like Git/GitHub, ClickUp, and Jupyter Notebooks; Specialized in NLP, text mining, and graph analytics, including the use of NLTK, spaCy, TextBlob, VADER, and transformer-based models (e.g., BERT, GPT); Familiar with social network analysis (SNA) using NetworkX, igraph, and Gephi for complex network and graph-based data exploration; Experience with research grant writing for federal (e.g., NSF, DoD) and state (e.g., ARA) funding agencies and foundations; Intermediate-level understanding of research methodology, data collection techniques, and statistical/analytical methods; Familiarity with computational social science, including social network analysis and social media mining; Experience in researching cyber campaigns and multimedia content on social media platforms; Demonstrated ability to translate research outcomes into usable tools or applications; Proficient in computer programming and data management; Ability to engage effectively with individuals from diverse disciplinary backgrounds; Strong oral and written communication skills, including the ability to present research findings clearly and collaborate effectively in team environments; Experience in mentoring students, researchers, data engineers, and volunteers; Excellent organizational and project management abilities, with proven capacity to manage multiple priorities and deadlines; Ability to work independently as well as collaboratively as part of a multidisciplinary research team. Additional Information: Salary Information: $85,000 annual Required Documents to Apply: Letters of Recommendation, Listing of Publications, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Prof. Nitin Agarwal <nxagarwal@ualr.edu> Jerry L. Maulden-Entergy Chair and Donaghey Distinguished Professor Director, COSMOS Research Center All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Repetitive Motion, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Repetitive Motion, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Repetitive Motion, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/COSMOS---Postdoctoral-Fellow-I_R0090539": {"title": "COSMOS - Postdoctoral Fellow I", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-25\nPosted: Posted 10 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Researchers Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Little Rock The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is a metropolitan research university that provides an accessible, quality education through flexible learning and unparalleled internship opportunities. At UA Little Rock, we prepare our more than 8,900 students to be innovators and responsible leaders in their fields. Committed to its metropolitan research university mission, UA Little Rock is a driving force in Little Rock's thriving cultural community and a major component of the city and state's growing profile as a regional leader in research, technology transfer, economic development, and job creation. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . Department: COSMOS - Provisional Positions Department's Website: https://cosmos.ualr.edu/ Summary of Job Duties: The Postdoctoral Fellow position is a full-time, provisional position with the COSMOS Research Center (cosmos.ualr.edu) at the University of Arkansas and is funded through a grant or contract. The position renewal is contingent upon continued grant funding and satisfactory job performance. The Postdoctoral Fellow will develop socio-computational models to advance our understanding of cyber campaigns on social media, grounded in the dynamics of social and communication processes such as group formation, activation, decentralized decision-making, and collective action. The Postdoctoral Fellow will help extract relevant open-source information in a guided snowball data collection manner by leveraging cyber forensics and deep web search-based methodologies. Postdoctoral Fellow will work with the research team in developing predictive models of various socio-technical behaviors on different social media platforms (including multimedia-rich platforms), and usable tools/software to identify key actors and key groups responsible for coordinating cyber campaigns and disseminating propaganda. This is an on-campus position. This position is governed by state and federal laws, and agency/institution policy. The position reports to Prof. Nitin Agarwal (nxagarwal@ualr.edu), Maulden-Entergy Endowed Chair & Donaghey Distinguished Professor, and Director, COSMOS Research Center at UA-Little Rock. Qualifications: Required Education and/or Experience: \u00a0 The candidate must have a Ph.D. degree in Computer Science, Information Science, or a related discipline; The candidate must have at least 1+ years of research experience in social media mining, computational modeling of social science theories, working with social network analysis tools, and examining cyber campaigns conducted on social media. The research experience must be demonstrated through published research articles in leading journals and conferences relevant to the topics mentioned above. Preferred Education and/or Experience: Candidates with strong experience in computer programming and data management will be given preference. Job Duties and Responsibilities: \u00a0 Support research projects through ideation, social media analysis, hypothesis generation, and evaluation to understand cyber behaviors; Assist with data collection, cleaning, preprocessing, analysis, and interpretation of findings; Contribute to writing research findings and presenting at conferences, program reviews, and other academic or professional venues; Develop software modules to support the transition of research into functional tools; Assist in analyzing multimedia-rich content from online information environments; Provide training and support to stakeholders on research findings and tool usage; Mentor and oversee graduate students involved in the research, providing valuable experience for future academic careers; Contribute to the preparation of research reports and publications; Support grant writing and proposal development; Coordinate team meetings and lead research-related discussions; Record and maintain accurate minutes of meetings; Perform other duties and provide additional support as assigned. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: \u00a0 Proficient in data analysis, modeling, machine learning, and AI, using Python and SQL, with extensive experience in libraries and frameworks such as Pandas, NumPy, scikit-learn, Gensim, BERTopic, TensorFlow, PyTorch, and LLMs; Skilled in data visualization using Matplotlib, Seaborn, and ggplot2, and experienced in managing research projects with tools like Git/GitHub, ClickUp, and Jupyter Notebooks; Specialized in NLP, text mining, and graph analytics, including the use of NLTK, spaCy, TextBlob, VADER, and transformer-based models (e.g., BERT, GPT); Familiar with social network analysis (SNA) using NetworkX, igraph, and Gephi for complex network and graph-based data exploration; Foundational understanding of computational social science and social network analysis; Expertise in social media mining and analysis; Research experience examining cyber campaigns conducted via social media platforms; Familiarity with analyzing multimedia-rich content in online environments; Experience in transitioning research concepts into practical tools; Proficiency in computer programming and data management; Strong analytical thinking and problem-solving capabilities; Ability to collaborate with individuals from diverse disciplinary backgrounds; Excellent written and verbal communication skills for disseminating research findings and engaging with stakeholders; Strong organizational and time management skills; Ability to work independently as well as collaboratively within a research team. Additional Information: Salary Information: $70,000 annual Required Documents to Apply: Letters of Recommendation, Listing of Publications, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Prof. Nitin Agarwal <nxagarwal@ualr.edu> Jerry L. Maulden-Entergy Chair and Donaghey Distinguished Professor Director, COSMOS Research Center All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Repetitive Motion, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Repetitive Motion, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Repetitive Motion, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Carpenter_R0079987-1": {"title": "Carpenter", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-25\nPosted: Posted 10 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/26/2026 Type of Position: Professional Staff - Facilities Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: OPS | Campus Operation EO Clinical Maint Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: This position performs advanced carpentry duties with only general supervision to include (but not limited to): Driving to and from construction sites or UAMS Main Campus; independently reading and understanding architectural plans and specifications, developing a work timeline and defining material requirements for a projects of a range of sizes; efficiently assess actual conditions of the space being renovated or remodeled and develops templates, minimizes material requirements and develops and implements plans to avoid known and unforeseen obstructions; ability to work independently or as the advanced carpenter on a team guiding others to construct walls, install doorframes and doors, install suspended ceilings and sheetrock ceilings, and hang drywall; skills and precision work required to handle specialty materials such as metals and plastics and a wide range of projects such as cabinetry installation, finishing and/or manufacturing and cross trained with an advanced level of proficiency in other areas of maintenance and construction such as finishing drywall for final painting, painting, staining, and installation and repair of multiple types of floor coverings including but not limited to carpet, carpet tile, vinyl tile, sheet vinyl, and ceramic tile. Complete documentation essential for the Engineering & Operations work order system and preventative maintenance program. This position has a high level of technical skills supporting independent identification and resolution of challenges and others seek their input when dealing with new challenges. Capable of providing oversite 3rd party contractor work. This position is an experienced craftsman responsible for renovating and remodeling the Medical, Educational, and Research facilities on the UAMS Campus. These duties are vital to the safety, comfort, and general wellbeing of patients, students and employees. This position is also responsible for assisting with all problems and/or emergencies relating to facility issues on the UAMS Campus. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: High School Diploma/GED plus 5-year carpentry experience Valid driver's license with fewer than 12 points on their Motor Vehicle Record. Basic Computer/Tablet/Smartphone skills. Must be able to read and interpret constriction drawings. Preferred Qualifications: Experience in a healthcare or other regulated environment. Intermediate Computer skills. Reading schematics, symbols and blueprints, roofing material repairs, cold and hot welding flooring materials, construction/maintenance measurements. Additional Information: Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience. Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Criminal Background Check This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Crawling, Crouching, Feeling, Kneeling, Reaching, Stooping Frequent Physical Activity: Hearing, Standing, Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Sitting Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Senior-Clinical-Therapist---Student-Wellness-Program_R0090383-2": {"title": "Senior Clinical Therapist - Student Wellness Program", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-25\nPosted: Posted 10 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/08/2026 Type of Position: Clinical Staff - Psychiatry Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | BHSL PRI Wellness Prg OP C Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Senior Clinical Therapist for the Student Wellness Program will provide direct clinical services such as diagnostic assessment, individual therapy, family therapy, group therapy, and crisis intervention to eligible UAMS students using evidence-based interventions. Direct and indirect clinical services are provided in the office. The Senior Clinical Therapist works directly under the supervision of the Student Wellness Program Medical Director. The Senior Clinical Therapist must have the ability to make decisions related to treatment planning. They must understand mental health diagnosis and treatment. Adaptable technological skills are required. In addition, the Senior Clinical Therapist will be responsible for ongoing communications with their supervisor and other members of the treatment team. They complete clinical and administrative processes and documentation in compliance with relevant policies and procedures. They will participate in staff meetings, trainings, supervision, and continuing education activities as needed to maintain quality provision and coordination of care as well as professional licensure and/or certification. They will participate in outreach events for students. The Student Wellness Program is located in the Mediplex building on the main UAMS campus in Little Rock. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Master's degree in Psychology, Social Work, Counseling, or related field Current and valis license by Arkansas Professional Board - Licensed Certified Social Worker (LCSW) or Licensed Professional Counselor (LPC) or Licensed Marriage and Family Therapist (LMFT) Preferred Qualifications: 3 years of direct clinical outpatient behavioral health experience Evidence-based treatment background, trauma-informed care model Additional Information: Job Requirements: Provide comprehensive clinical assessments for patients experiencing mental health, behavioral, emotional, and psychosocial concerns. Develop, implement, and evaluate individualized treatment plans based on patient needs and clinical goals. Provide individual, family, and group therapy using evidence-based therapeutic interventions. Conduct crisis assessments and provide appropriate crisis intervention, stabilization, and safety planning. Assess patients for suicide, self-harm, violence, substance use, and other behavioral health risks and initiate appropriate interventions. Monitor patient progress and modify treatment plans as clinically indicated. Provide clinical consultation and support to therapists, social workers, nurses, physicians, and other members of the interdisciplinary team. Serve as a senior clinical resource for complex or high-risk patient cases. Provide clinical supervision, mentoring, coaching, and guidance to less-experienced therapists and behavioral health staff, as permitted by licensure. Participate in multidisciplinary treatment team meetings, case reviews, and care coordination activities. Coordinate referrals to community providers, psychiatric services, substance-use programs, and other supportive resources. Assist with discharge planning and promote continuity of behavioral healthcare services. Provide education to patients, families, and caregivers regarding diagnoses, treatment options, coping skills, and community resources. Maintain timely, accurate, and clinically appropriate documentation in the electronic medical record. Ensure clinical services are provided in accordance with organizational policies, ethical standards, regulatory requirements, and applicable licensure guidelines. Participate in quality improvement initiatives, program development, clinical audits, and performance improvement activities. Assist leadership with developing clinical workflows, policies, procedures, and behavioral health programs. Respond to behavioral health emergencies and collaborate with the care team to promote patient and staff safety. Maintain patient confidentiality and adhere to HIPAA and all applicable privacy requirements. Facilitate staff education, clinical training, and professional development activities. Promote trauma-informed, culturally responsive, patient-centered care across the behavioral health program. Perform other duties as needed. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS Stand: Frequently Sit: Frequently Walk: Occasionally Bend, crawl, crouch, kneel, stoop or reach overhead: Frequently Lift and carry weight: 25 lbs Push and pull weight: 25 lbs Use hands to touch, handle or feel: Frequently Talk: Continuously Hear: Continuously Taste or smell: Occasionally Read, concentrate, think analytically: Continuously Physical Environment : Inside Medical Facility Environment Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Adult Maltreatment, Annual TB Screening, Child Maltreatment, Criminal Background Check, Substance Abuse Testing This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Standing, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Kneeling, Lifting, Pulling, Pushing Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Audit-and-Billing-Compliance-Specialist_R0088165-1": {"title": "Audit and Billing Compliance Specialist", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-25\nPosted: Posted 10 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/09/2026 Type of Position: Professional Staff - Fiscal Affairs Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: FIN | Compliance Hospital & Professional Coding Auditing Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Audit & Billing Compliance Specialist works under the general direction of the Clinical Billing Compliance Director and reviews medical records and billing system programs to determine coding and billing accuracy and to ensure that all federal and state guidelines for coding and billing are followed. Conducts inpatient and outpatient coding and billing audit functions according to the audit plan schedule with the focus on hospital billing according to the Center for Medicare and Medicaid Systems (CMS) laws and regulations. Provides education and training to coding staff as well as ancillary department staff. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Baccalaureate degree plus 3 years\u2019 experience in inpatient and outpatient coding/auditing functions OR High School diploma plus 7 years\u2019 experience in inpatient and outpatient coding/auditing functions. Must have one of the following CURRENT coding certifications: Certified Coding Specialist (CCS), Certified Inpatient Coder (CIC), Registered Health Information Administrator (RHIA), or Registered Health Information Technician (RHIT). Must have demonstrated ability to present information verbally and have strong written communication skills with attention to detail. Must have the ability to make reasonable decisions based upon the information gathered, interpret regulatory information and deliver learned information to physicians. and explain the financial impact to the hospital. Preferred Qualifications: Prefer degree in Health Information Management, Healthcare Administration, or related field Additional Information: Responsibilities: FACILITIES CODING AUDITS Conducts inpatient and outpatient coding & billing audit/monitoring functions according to the audit plan schedule, with focus on hospital billing according to the Center for Medicare and Medicaid Systems (CMS) laws and regulations. Audits departmental systems and processes to ensure that they comply with state and federal laws and regulations. Provides audit results to the affected areas and educates staff regarding errors. Prepares detailed audit reports for the Clinical Billing Compliance Director and Associate Vice Chancellor review as well as dissemination to Hospital Administration, Revenue Cycle and Department Managers as appropriate. This position works very independently and must have good decision-making skills. TRAINING AND DEVELOPMENT Develops and presents educational in-service programs on new regulatory issues for all inpatient and outpatient coders.\u00a0 REQUIRED PROFESSIONAL PROFICENCIES Keeps abreast of current trends, problems and activities relating to coding. Proficient and keeps current with all COM/UAMS coding and billing policies and procedures and applicable federal and state regulations. Serves as a resource to assigned departments on current regulations, coding issues, charge and billing issues, facility charging and billing as well as regulatory concerns. Disseminates regulatory and compliance information to Ancillary departments and Clinic areas as necessary. PERFORM EXTERNAL AGENCY and SPECIAL AUDITS Performs specific audits outside the audit plan schedule as needed (to include, but not limited to, Office of Inspector General (OIG) audits, \u00a0Medicare Administrative Contractor (MAC) audits, Recovery Audit Contractor (RAC) audits, Medicaid Integrity Contractor (MIC) audits, etc.). Reviews RAC audits for any Diagnosis-Related Group (DRG) issues as needed. Writes RAC appeal letters for DRG changes. Communicates with regulatory agencies (Medicaid, Novitas Solutions, etc.) as necessary for clarification of regulations or for assistance with audit issues or coding issues as needed. DIVISION SUPPORT/COMMITMENT TO INSTITUTIONAL COMPLIANCE Participates in special projects as assigned by the Senior Director of Clinical Billing Compliance and/or the Associate Vice Chancellor for Institutional Compliance/Chief Compliance Officer and other duties as assigned. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience. Required Documents to Apply: List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: This position requires at least one of the following coding certifications in CURRENT status: Certified Coding Specialist (CCS), Certified Inpatient Coder (CIC), Registered Health Information Administrator (RHIA), or Registered Health Information Technician (RHIT) Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: No Background Check Required This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting Frequent Physical Activity: Hearing, Talking Occasional Physical Activity: Reaching, Standing, Walking Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Research-Program-Manager_R0086597-1": {"title": "Research Program Manager", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-25\nPosted: Posted 10 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/09/2026 Type of Position: Clinical Staff - Medical Services Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: TRI | Community Engagement Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Research Program Manager for the Translational Research Institute (TRI) Community Stakeholders and Engagement Core (CSE) is responsible for maintaining an overall administrative leadership role while building, directing, managing, and ensuring a high-quality successful community engagement operation. The Research Program Manager will work with the CSE leadership to develop, implement, and coordinate community engagement activities for the Translational Research Institute. The Research Program Manager will facilitate lay, practice, and research partnerships and capacity building for community engagement, and support communications and dissemination of information to lay community members and others. Assist researchers requesting community-engaged services. Assist researchers with developing and implementing research results dissemination plans. Assist research teams with developing and implementing study participant recruitment and retention strategies. Participate in national community engagement networking opportunities. Complete all administrative duties (schedule, secure virtual links, book venues, order food, handle travel, produce written materials, take notes, meeting follow up activities, manage email list serves, etc.) for in-person and virtual community engaged focused meetings. Coordinate community activities for disseminating research findings to lay and stakeholder communities. Serve as the primary point of contact to link interested community groups with academic or provider groups for the purpose of research. Qualifications: Bachelor's degree with 5 years of experience in Program Coordination or Community Engagement OR Master\u2019s degree with 3 years of Program Coordination or Community Engagement OR High School Diploma with 9 years of experience in Program Coordination or Community Engagement. Additional Information: Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: No Background Check Required This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/RN---Main-OR_R0090442-2": {"title": "RN - Main OR", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-25\nPosted: Posted 10 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/08/2026 Type of Position: Clinical Staff - Nursing Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | PeriopSvc Main Operating Room 2A Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Registered Nurse (RN) will provide direct patient care as an RN. This professional nursing role will require the ability to coordinate care for patients, triage patients, and work collaboratively with clinic providers, fellows, and staff. Requires the ability to effectively work with patient referral sources, facilitate appointments, coordinate transitions of care, and provide patient education on complex conditions. The RN will work with the individual patient, their families, and providers of care to develop and implement individual health plans. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Graduate of an accredited Nursing Program with Associates Degree, Nursing Diploma, Bachelors in Nursing, or Master's in Nursing Valid RN License Minimum of 1 year Registered Nursing experience Additional Information: Responsibilities: \u00a0The Registered Nurse (RN) delivers nursing care for patients within the limits of the Nurse Practice Act of the State of Arkansas and adheres to institutional policies, procedures and standards. The RN is responsible to adhere to the standard of care defined by UAMS, ANA, and Standards for specialty patient population with support and mentoring by other team members. \u00a0 Collects and documents assessment data.\u00a0 Develops a Plan of Care (POC) per standard. \u00a0 Implements POC including medical order and interdisciplinary approach. \u00a0 Evaluates the progress of patient toward attainment of desired outcomes. \u00a0 Provides effective patient/family education/discharge planning. \u00a0 Administers medication per standard including drug information to patients/families. \u00a0 Acts as a resource/supports other. \u00a0 Delivers patient care using the principles of the defined nursing modality. \u00a0 Delegates care based on UAMS standards, legal and regulatory requirements, specific job description and individual level of education and training. \u00a0 Contributes to a positive work environment that is conducive to clinical education while serving as a resource for student nurses and staff. May perform other duties as assigned. Salary Information: commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Criminal Background Check, Substance Abuse Testing This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Standing, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Sitting, Stooping Occasional Physical Activity: Grasping, Kneeling, Repetitive Motion, Sharps Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Medical-Laboratory-Scientist-I---Chemistry_R0090326-1": {"title": "Medical Laboratory Scientist I - Chemistry", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-25\nPosted: Posted 10 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/08/2026 Type of Position: Clinical Staff - Medical Ancillary Support Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Shift Vary (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | LPSL CPATH Chemistry Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Medical Laboratory Scientist I (Chemistry) performs routine and complex laboratory testing in the Chemistry department to assist physicians and healthcare providers in the diagnosis, treatment, and prevention of disease. This position is responsible for analyzing patient specimens, operating and maintaining laboratory instrumentation, ensuring quality control standards are met, and reporting accurate and timely test results in accordance with regulatory and organizational requirements. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor\u2019s Degree in Chemistry, Biology, Medical Technology or Medical Laboratory Sciences OR an approved ASCP discipline (30 semester hours in biology and chemistry, which may be obtained within, or in addition to, the Bachelor's). ASCP or another accrediting agency certified or eligible (Certification must be obtained within one year of employment). Preferred Qualifications: Previous clinical laboratory experience ASCP certification Additional Information: Job Requirements: Daily quality control review. Organize and clean workspaces. Ensure adequate supplies required for daily operations are available by restocking inventory, preparing reagents, rotating stock as required. Communicate with clinics, physicians and external staff regarding sample integrity issues and/or critical values. Set-up, maintain and operate lab automation systems used to process samples. Operate, calibrate and maintain equipment used in analysis such as spectrophotometers, analyzers, microscopes, slide stainers, diluters, and computer controlled high volume analyzers, mixers, rotators, pipettes. Perform basic troubleshooting on equipment used to perform testing. Maintain equipment used for personal protection and safety such as eyewashes, safety showers, biohazard containers, hoods, chemical cabinets and personal protective equipment. Maintain temperature dependent equipment such as refrigerators, freezers, incubators, water baths, heat blocks. Perform other duties as needed. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS Stand: Frequently Sit: Frequently Walk: Occasionally Bend, crawl, crouch, kneel, stoop or reach overhead: Frequently Lift and carry weight: 25 lbs Push and pull weight: 25 lbs Use hands to touch, handle or feel: Frequently Talk: Continuously Hear: Continuously Taste or smell: Occasionally Read, concentrate, think analytically: Continuously Physical Environment : Inside Medical Facility Environment Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), Proof of Veteran Status, Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Criminal Background Check, Substance Abuse Testing This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding Frequent Physical Activity: Feeling, Grasping, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Repetitive Motion, Sharps, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Crouching, Kneeling, Lifting, Stooping Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/RN---Main-OR_R0090422-1": {"title": "RN - Main OR", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-25\nPosted: Posted 10 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/08/2026 Type of Position: Clinical Staff - Nursing Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main ca