k/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: COP | Poison Control & Drug Information Ctr Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: **Position is an overnight position - 9:30 pm to 5:30 am** Professional position that provides clinical information and recommendations regarding toxic or potentially toxic exposures received from health care providers and the public throughout the APDIC\u2019s designated region. In addition, providing clinical information regarding the use of medications to healthcare providers and the public throughout APDIC\u2019s designated region. Qualifications: Must be a licensed nurse/RN Preferred ED or Critical Care experience but new graduates with past LPN experience in those areas will be considered. Additional Information: Providing information and treatment advice to callers regarding toxic exposures or potentially toxic exposures. Creating and updating the electronic medical records created by these inquires.\u00a0 Providing educational information on toxic substances and drug substances to callers. Assisting in the education/instruction of professional students and residents. Other duties as assigned. Salary Information: Salary commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Substance Abuse Testing This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Sitting, Standing Occasional Physical Activity: Walking Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Benton/Cook--UAMS-Health-Benton-Bryant-_R0090218-2": {"title": "Cook (UAMS Health Benton/Bryant)", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-19\nPosted: Posted 16 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/08/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Shift Vary (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: INA | Institutional Admin Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Cook collaborates with other cooks and food prep techs under the direction of a supervisor to requisition, prepare, season, and cook a wide range of foods, including soups, salads, bakery and entrees for patients, employees, or patrons. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: High School diploma/GED plus 1 year experience in institutional or commercial cooking. Must be able to work during Inclement Weather. Must be able to work rotating Weekends and Holidays. Preferred Qualifications: Formal Culinary Education and ServSafe Certified. Additional Information: Responsibilities: Cleans, cut, and cook food items according to menus, special dietary or nutritional restrictions, or numbers of portions to be served. \u00a0\u00a0 Clean and inspect gallery equipment, kitchen appliances, and work areas to ensure cleanliness and functional operation.\u00a0 Apportion and serve food to patients, employees, and patrons. Other duties as assigned.\u00a0 Physical Requirements: Constant Physical Activity : Read, Concentrate, Think Analytically, Frequent Physical Activity : Stand Walk Bend, crawl, crouch, kneel, stoop or reach overhead Hear Taste or Smell Use hands to touch, handle or feel Lift/Carry Weight: 26 - 50 Lbs. Push/Pull Weight: 26 - 50 Lbs. Physical Environment : Inside Medical Facility Noise Level: Loud Visual Requirements: Color discrimination, Depth perception, Far visual acuity, Near visual acuity Hazards : Biological, Fumes/Gases/Odors, Sharp objects/tools, Chemical Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Benton/Dietetic-Technician--UAMS-Health-Benton-Bryant-_R0090220-1": {"title": "Dietetic Technician (UAMS Health Benton/Bryant)", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-19\nPosted: Posted 16 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/08/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Shift Vary (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: INA | Institutional Admin Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Dietetic Technician is responsible for daily routines and functions in order to see that all patients receive meals in a timely fashion and the meals meet the Physician order and patient preferences. The Dietetic Technician Level I is responsible for assisting in planning and implementing nutritional programs and services in the hospital. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: High School diploma/GED plus 2 years of experience in customer service. Ideal candidate is team-oriented and has great customer service skills. Must be able to work during Inclement Weather. Must be able to work rotating Weekends and Holidays. Preferred Qualifications:\u00a0 Experience in a food service or patient care setting. Additional Information: Responsibilities: Assisting patients and ensures that patients receive meals and nourishments in accordance to current diet orders and food allergens. Proactively seeks patients\u2019 food orders for those who did not call the call center, may have difficulty speaking, hearing or seeing, and those that may need language assistance. Takes food orders, promptly and accurately within the constraints of the diet order, at the bedside with IPads. Makes selections into the electronic meal selection on room service assist and house selection criteria. Updates and records patient information from the electronic medical record, correct menu choices based on meal patterns, allergies and patient preferences while alerting the Lead Room Service Ambassadors or Supervisors to any issues. Serves trays in a timely manner according to the departmental policies and procedures. Accurately identifies patient and appropriate tray by using two patient identifiers. Assesses and trouble-shoots issues at the point of service that may impact patient satisfaction. Responds to patient requests by communicating with appropriate staff. Retrieves trays from assigned patient units after the patients have finished their meals. Prepares beverages following thickened policies when required. Stocks coolers, freezers and dry storage items in the patient food area. Stores supplies and food according to department standards. Ensures FIFO, proper temperatures, and properly labeling standards are applied Follows cleaning checklist and maintains a clean and organized work area Greets customers in a courteous manner, identifying themselves by name and department, maintains eye contact and offers assistance. Serves as a role model for other employees by modeling appropriate behaviors including taking initiative to cross-train and assist others, exhibiting flexibility, and maintaining a focus on customer service.\u00a0 Demonstrates integrity, compassion, respect, and a positive attitude to co- workers, patients, visitors, and UAMS staff regardless of race, gender, sexual orientation, ethnicity, religious belief, age and/or disability. Completes other duties as assigned by management. Physical Requirements: Stand: Continuously Sit: Never Walk: Frequently Bend, crawl, crouch, kneel, stoop or reach overhead: Frequently Lift and carry weight: 26 - 50 lbs Push and pull weight: 26 - 50 lbs Use hands to touch, handle or feel: Continuously Talk: Continuously Hear: Continuously Taste or smell: Occasionally Read, concentrate, think analytically: Continuously Physical Environment: Inside Medical Environment Noise Level: Loud Hazards: Chemicals, Electrical, Fumes/Gases/Odors, Heavy Machinery Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Benton/Institutional-Services-Assistant-Kitchen-Helper--UAMS-Health-Benton-Bryant-_R0090215-1": {"title": "Institutional Services Assistant/Kitchen Helper (UAMS Health Benton/Bryant)", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-19\nPosted: Posted 16 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/08/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Shift Vary (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: INA | Institutional Admin Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Institutional Services Assistant/Kitchen Helper, in conjunction with other assistants and under the direction of a supervisor, cleans dishes, the kitchen area, food preparation equipment, and utensils. The Institutional Services Assistant also removes trash while maintaining a clean, safe, and sanitary environment. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: High School Diploma or GED Able to exert up to 50 pounds of force occasionally and/or up to 20 pounds of force frequently or constantly to lift, carry, push, pull, or otherwise move objects Additional Information: Responsibilities: Washes dishes, glassware, flatware, pots, or pans using a dishwasher or manually then places the equipment in designated storage areas. Maintains kitchen work areas, floors, equipment, or utensils. Uses and stores chemical and cleaning supplies. Sorts and removes trash, placing it in designated pickup areas and clean/line garbage containers. May perform other duties as assigned. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS: Stand: Continuously Sit: Never Walk: Frequently Bend, crawl, crouch, kneel, stoop or reach overhead: Frequently Lift and carry weight: 26 - 50 lbs Push and pull weight: 26 - 50 lbs Use hands to touch, handle or feel: Continuously Talk: Occasionally Hear: Continuously Taste or smell: Occasionally Read, concentrate, think analytically: Occasionally Physical Environment: Inside Medical Facility Environment Noise Level: Loud Visual Requirements: Color discrimination, Depth perception, Far visual acuity, Near visual acuity Hazards: Chemical, Dust, Electrical, Fumes/Gases/Odors, Heavy machinery, Sharp objects/tools Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Benton/Maintenance-Specialist--UAMS-Health-Benton-Bryant-_R0089940-1": {"title": "Maintenance Specialist (UAMS Health Benton/Bryant)", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-19\nPosted: Posted 16 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/08/2026 Type of Position: Professional Staff - Facilities Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Shift Vary (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: INA | Institutional Admin Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: This position is responsible for general maintenance and repair duties for the facilities at the UAMS Health Benton/Bryant location. These duties are vital to the safety, comfort, and general wellbeing of patients, visitors and employees. This position is also responsible for assisting with all problems and or emergencies relating to facility issues. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: High school diploma/GED and 5 years of maintenance experience. Valid driver\u2019s License with fewer than 12 points on their Motor Vehicle Record Preferred Qualifications: Maintenance experience in a healthcare setting Boiler/Heating Plant Operation experience Additional Information: Responsibilities: Operates and maintains the low pressure condensing boiler heating water system and associated components, including pumps, electronic valves, temperature sensors, controllers, and motors. Conducts regular building inspections and makes necessary adjustments and repairs; replaces lightbulbs, batteries, and filters; moves furniture and other items as requested. Performs preventative maintenance inspections and activities in accordance with schedules and applicable codes. Performs a wide variety of tradesman duties, including general flooring and roof repairs, carpentry, painting, and plumbing; coordinates outside tradespeople and arranges pest control services when necessary. Completes documentation essential for the Engineering & Operations work order system and preventative maintenance program; may drive to and from UAMS work sites. This position is declared essential. Delivers items and supplies around the Benton/Bryant campus. Performs other duties as assigned Salary Information: \"Commensurate with education and experience\") Required Documents to Apply: None Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Criminal Background Check This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Pulling, Pushing, Standing, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Crouching, Hearing, Kneeling, Lifting Occasional Physical Activity: Climbing, Crawling, Sitting Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Buyer_R0090145-1": {"title": "Buyer", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-18\nPosted: Posted 17 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Procurement, Inventory Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Little Rock The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is a metropolitan research university that provides an accessible, quality education through flexible learning and unparalleled internship opportunities. At UA Little Rock, we prepare our more than 8,900 students to be innovators and responsible leaders in their fields. Committed to its metropolitan research university mission, UA Little Rock is a driving force in Little Rock's thriving cultural community and a major component of the city and state's growing profile as a regional leader in research, technology transfer, economic development, and job creation. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . Department: Procurement Services Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Buyer is responsible for processing the procurement of all commodities and services. This position is governed by state and federal laws and agency/institution policy. Qualifications: REQUIRED EDUCATION AND EXPERIENCE: Associates degree in Business or Finance from an accredited university or in place of a degree, four (4) years of relevant experience; and a minimum of two (2) years of experience in procurement, bookkeeping, basic accounting, billing, asset accounting, travel, or related experience. JOB DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES: Process orders in an automated procurement system; manages the placement of purchase orders with vendors, including quote and/ or contact documentation; Review purchase requests to determine the need for term contacts; develop new contracts and /or prepare history sheet and product specifications; determine the appropriate list of bidders for products; and notifies potential bidders; Interview and work closely with vendors to obtain and develop desired products; Prepare specifications for competitive bids and competitive seals bids; manages bid openings, evaluation criteria, and vendor list; receives and evaluates bids to determine lowest bid and delivery requirements within cost limit; and awards bids; Examine, select, order, and purchase merchandise at most favorable price consistent with quality, quantity specification requirements, and other factors; Expedite and review purchase order invoices, return of merchandise, and shipment; Maintain vendor ordering accounts for office supplies on the Internet and in an automated procurement system; Maintain requisition and purchases orders in an automated procurement system for all documentation necessary for the related purchase order.\u00a0 KNOWLEDGE, ABILITIES, AND SKILLS: Knowledge of purchasing principles, procedures, and methods; Knowledge of state and university purchasing laws and regulations; Ability to research and draft clear, concise, and competitive purchasing specifications and evaluate product acceptability and/or quality; Ability to perform basic mathematical computations; Ability to maintain accurate and systematic procurement records; Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with purchasing agents/officials, vendors, and manufacturers; Excellent written and verbal communication. Additional Information: Salary Information: $44,675 Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Tierra Hutley, Procurement Manager, 501-916-5727 All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Financial Credit Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Repetitive Motion, Sitting, Standing, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting, Talking Occasional Physical Activity: Kneeling, Lifting Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAM--Monticello-Campus/Non-Student-Extra-Help-School-of-Nursing_R0090112-1": {"title": "Non-Student Extra Help-School of Nursing", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-18\nPosted: Posted 17 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Clinical Staff - Nursing Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Monticello UAM, one of twenty campuses of the University of Arkansas System, is located in southeastern Arkansas in the beautiful timberlands, rich in outdoor recreation activities, and approximately 100 miles south of Little Rock. UAM is a comprehensive, residential and commuter, undergraduate institution also offering selected master\u2019s degree programs. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please submit a request via the OEOC website: \u00a0Applicants are required to submit a request for each position to which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 870-460-1422 . Department: Nursing Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Clinical Instructor Responsible for teaching students in the clinical setting. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications Arkansas or multi-state unencumbered RN licensure and BSN degree Preferred Qualifications Master's degree in Nursing Additional Information: Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience. Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume, Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Amanda Smith, Dean of School of Nursing 870-460-1069 smithak@uamont.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry, Substance Abuse Testing The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Helena/LPN-Helena--AR-_R0090023-1": {"title": "LPN(Helena, AR)", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-18\nPosted: Posted 17 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/30/2026 Type of Position: Clinical Staff - Nursing Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: REP | PCPHSL CS East Helena Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: We are seeking a skilled Licensed Practical Nurse (LPN) to join our team at UAMS Helena Family Medical Center. The LPN supports the on-going delivery of care as identified by the multi-disciplinary scope of practice. This position plays a vital role in providing direct patient care under the supervision of a Registered Nurse, contributing to the assessment, planning, implementation, and evaluation of nursing care for a select group of patients. The LPN works with the individual patient, their families, and providers to implement individual health plans. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications High School, GED, or formal educational equivalent. Graduate of an accredited Licensed Practical Nurse program. Associates Degree in Nursing. One (1) year of work experience in clinical nursing Current Arkansas Licensed Practical Nurse license Current CPR certification Knowledge, Abilities, and Skills: Strong clinical knowledge and technique. Knowledge of basic medical terminology required Strong patient advocacy and patient education skills.\u00a0 Attention to communication, oral, written, and persuasive. Must be able to build collaborative relationships. Possess personal credibility. Ability to make independent judgments that have highly significant impacts on the organization. Ability to provide motivational support to the area of responsibility. Strong customer service orientation. Intermediate computer skills. Professional and courteous telephone etiquette. General knowledge of office machines, including printers, fax machines, and scanners. Preferred Qualifications Two (2) years of work experience in a clinical environment with direct patient care. Good working knowledge of the state immunization registry, care manager. PCMH experience and care management experience. Additional Information: Key Responsibilities: Direct patient care within the limits of the Nurse Practice Act of the State of Arkansas, UAMS policies, procedures, and standards. Accountable for adhering to UAMS care guidelines. Observe patients, charting, and reporting changes in patients\u2019 conditions. Provide basic care and treatment of patients. Administer prescribed medications and start intravenous fluids. Measure and record the patient\u2019s vital signs. Assist patients in standing, walking, bathing, dressing, and moving in bed. Supervise nurses\u2019 aides and assistants. Answer the patient\u2019s call and determine how to assist them. Collect samples such as blood, urine, and sputum from patients and perform routine laboratory tests on samples. Clean rooms and make beds. Inventory and requisition supplies and instruments. Record food and fluid intake and output. Models the Core Values of UAMS \u2013 Excellence in compliance with company guidelines. Performs related responsibilities as required or assigned. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), Resume Optional Documents: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of five Professional References (name, email, business title), Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Criminal Background Check, Substance Abuse Testing This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Feeling, Grasping, Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Repetitive Motion, Sharps, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Kneeling, Lifting, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Stooping Occasional Physical Activity: Balancing, Climbing, Crawling, Crouching Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Patient-Care-Technician---Infusion-Services_R0090162-1": {"title": "Patient Care Technician - Infusion Services", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-18\nPosted: Posted 17 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 10/18/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Shift Vary (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | CASL CA Infusion A Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: *This posting will fill multiple positions* The Patient Care Technician (PCT) works under the direct supervision of the Registered Nurse(s) and performs tasks and duties which do not require a license, professional judgment or intervention. The PCT must pass the required competencies. The PCT works within the Department of Nursing standards. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: \u00a0 High School Diploma/GED ,successful completion of patient care technician course within 3 months of hire.\u00a0 Must have\u00a0excellent communication skills, ability to follow oral instructions, basic computer skills, strong work ethics and accountability. Must be able to lift 100 lbs. to waist height. Preferred Qualifications:\u00a0 Certification as a nursing assistant or military corpsman. Patient care experience in acute care setting. Additional Information: Responsibilities: Obtains patient report and has on-going communication with R.N. regarding patient care/changes in condition; Informs nurse of patient requests or complaints. Assists with admission, transfer, and discharge of patients. Transports patients to other areas of the hospital as directed. Carries out the Plan of Care for Patient using a Multidisciplinary Approach as Delegated by Team Leader. \u00a0Communicates effectively with other team members to facilitate patient care. Accepts directions from R.N.s and team members. Follows through on delegated patient care activities. Provides appropriate grooming/oral hygiene and comfort measures and assists patients with activities (ambulation, up in chair, turn and reposition). Documents all patient care activities/tasks, vital signs, ADL, wave tests, I&O's accurately and timely and per unit and department standards. Assists patients and visitors with information and/or solutions to problems. Serves as resources person to support department members in performance of duties. Notifies appropriate staff members of problems requiring prompt intervention. May perform other duties as assigned. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/RN---Infusion-Services---Cancer-Institute_R0084655-1": {"title": "RN - Infusion Services - Cancer Institute", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-18\nPosted: Posted 17 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/18/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | CASL CA Infusion B Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: \"This posting will fill several positions on all shifts\" Registered Nurse (RN) will provide direct patient care as an RN. This professional nursing role will require the ability to coordinate care for patients, triage patients, and work collaboratively with clinic providers, fellows, and staff. Requires the ability to effectively work with patient referral sources, facilitate appointments, coordinate transitions of care, and provide patient education on complex conditions. The RN will work with the individual patient, their families, and providers of care to develop and implement individual health plans. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Graduate of an accredited Nursing Program with Associates Degree, Nursing Diploma, Bachelors in Nursing, or Master's in Nursing\u00a0 Valid Arkansas RN License Minimum of 1 year Registered Nursing experience Preferred Qualifications: Current BLS Additional Information: Responsibilities: The Registered Nurse (RN) delivers nursing care for patients within the limits of the Nurse Practice Act of the State of Arkansas and adheres to institutional policies, procedures and standards. \u00a0The\u00a0RN is responsible to adhere to the standard of care defined by UAMS, ANA, and Standards for specialty patient populations with support and mentoring by other team members.\u00a0 Collects and documents assessment data. Develops a Plan of Care (POC) per standard.\u00a0 Implements POC including medical order and interdisciplinary approach.\u00a0 Evaluates the progress of patients toward attainment of desired outcomes.\u00a0 Provides effective patient/family education/discharge planning.\u00a0 Administers medication per standard including drug information to patients/families.\u00a0 Acts as a resource/supports others.\u00a0 Delivers patient care using the principles of the defined nursing modality.\u00a0 Delegates care based on UAMS standards, legal and regulatory requirements, specific job description and individual level of education and training.\u00a0 Contributes to a positive work environment that is conducive to clinical education while serving as a resource for student nurses and staff. Interacts with, and assists, the public in a professional and friendly manner as needed. Demonstrates effective communication skills; communicates accurate and complete information; maintains strict confidentiality when necessary. Demonstrates positive working relationships with co-workers, management team, and ancillary departments; follows the Core Concepts of Patient and Family Centered Care and the Basic Code of Conduct Guidelines. Assists internal and external stakeholders, as needed, with exceptional customer service. May perform other duties as assigned. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/DeValls-Bluff/XMLNAME-4-H-Program-Assistant_R0089844-1": {"title": "4-H Program Assistant", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-18\nPosted: Posted 17 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Clerical Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: Division of Agriculture of the University of Arkansas The University of Arkansas System Division of Agriculture is a state wide campus, with faculty based on University campuses, at Research and Extension Centers and in every Arkansas county. It consists of the Arkansas Agricultural Experiment Station (AES) and the Arkansas Cooperative Extension Service (CES), and is home to more than 1400 employees.\u00a0 The Division was established in 1959 and is headed by the Vice-President for Agriculture.\u00a0 The Division headquarters is located in Little Rock with the rest of the University of Arkansas System Administration.\u00a0 As an employer, the University of Arkansas System Division of Agriculture offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance.\u00a0 Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process and require reasonable accommodations, please contact the Division's Office of Program & Employment Compliance at compliance@uada.edu . For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-671-2219 or 479-502-9820. Department: CEA * Staff Chair * Prairie County Department's Website: https://www.uaex.uada.edu/counties/prairie/ Summary of Job Duties: Summary of Job Duties The Cooperative Extension Service Program Assistant works for an assigned county Extension program under the supervision of a county agent in 4-H and youth development areas. Self-Management \u2022 Organizes and prioritizes tasks effectively. \u2022 Deals appropriately with interruptions. \u2022 Uses good judgment and decision-making skills. \u2022 Follows attendance and leave policies. \u2022 Practices emotional control. \u2022 Exhibits professional behavior and appearance. \u2022 Ability to work without close supervision. Quality and Quantity of Work \u2022 Maintains 4-H Clubs. Periodically attends 4-H Club meetings. \u2022 Maintains working relationship with all 4-H leaders, members, and parents. \u2022 Recruits adult volunteer leaders youth, and volunteers to form 4-H clubs and grow the community 4-H enrollment/program. \u2022 Follows up promptly with questions and requests for information. \u2022 Maintains accurate 4-H records and submits reports by deadlines. \u2022 Displays acknowledge of 4-H policies and procedures. \u2022 Stays informed of all county, district, and state 4-H events, competitions, camps, activities, etc. Informs 4-H leaders, members and parents of all county, district, and state 4-H events, competitions, camps, activities, etc. Assists 4-Her in preparation for events and competitions. \u2022 Plans, organizes, sets-up, conducts, and cleans-up after all 4-H events, competitions, and activities in the county. \u2022 Conducts regular 4-H leader training meetings. Program Delivery \u2022 Shows sensitivity to individual needs based on culture, race, gender and age. \u2022 Coordinated with agents to conducting educational programs in schools and the community. \u2022 Evaluates the county 4-H program for impact. Communication \u2022 Communicates the benefits and goals of the 4-H program to clientele. \u2022 Makes sure youth, parents and adult leaders are aware of events, activates, meetings and any registration deadlines. \u2022 Uses social media, virtual tools and newsletters to communicate. \u2022 Uses local newspaper, social media and other tools to promote 4-H. \u2022 Listens to feedback and acts to improve. Teamwork \u2022 Shares information, expertise and resources with others. \u2022 Is part of the county Extension Service team to insure and success of the whole Extension program. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications High School diploma or equivalent required. Must have reliable transportation for use on the job with liability insurance in effect. Must successfully complete the standard background check which includes the Arkansas Child Abuse and Neglect Central Registry Check. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Ability to conduct programs and work with all clientele regardless of race, color, national origin, religion, gender, age, disability, marital or veteran status, or any other legally protected status. Ability to communicate effectively, both orally and in writing. Ability to keep accurate records and submit timely reports of activities. Ability to respond positively to supervisor direction. Ability to work without close daily supervision. Additional Information: Applicants for this position are required to upload a Resume, Cover letter, and a list of three (3) references including name, phone number and email address (if available) prior to submitting the application. Once an application is submitted, the applicant will not be able to edit the application or upload additional documents. If you have technical issues uploading a document or if you have a need to provide additional documentation after submitting your application, email humanresources@uada.edu Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Jacob Holloway, jholloway@uada.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Motor Vehicle Reports Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas System Division of Agriculture may conduct pre-employment background checks on certain positions for applicants being considered for employment. \u00a0 The background checks may include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. \u00a0 Required checks are identified in the position listing. \u00a0 A criminal background check or arrest pending adjudication information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absences of a relationship to the requirements of the position. \u00a0 Background check information will be used in a consistent, non-discriminatory manner consistent with the state and federal law. \u00a0 The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Driving, Feeling, Grasping, Standing, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Kneeling, Lifting, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Repetitive Motion, Sitting Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Refrigeration-Technician_R0085856-1": {"title": "Refrigeration Technician", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-18\nPosted: Posted 17 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/19/2026 Type of Position: Professional Staff - Facilities Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: OPS | Campus Operations HVAC and Controls Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: This position is responsible for the maintenance, troubleshooting, and modification of Ice Machine and Refrigeration Equipment that serves the medical and research facilities on the UAMS Campus. These systems are essential to patient care and critical research operations, directly impacting patient health and outcomes. The Ice Machine/Refrigeration Technician will be tasked with performing routine maintenance, diagnostics, and repair on a wide range of commercial refrigeration systems. These include, but are not limited to, hermetic and semi-hermetic compressors, air-cooled and water-cooled condensers, evaporative coils, thermostatic expansion valves (TXVs), solenoid valves, and various refrigeration control systems. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications High school diploma/GED plus one year of HVAC Refrigeration experience EPA 608 Universal License Computer program proficiency level: Intermediate Valid driver\u2019s license with fewer than 12 points on their Motor Vehicle Record Preferred Qualifications Technical degree in electronics, may be accepted in place of experience HVAC Mechanical license in Accordance w/ACA 17-33-3001 Additional Information: The role involves performing regular preventive maintenance and emergency repairs on refrigeration systems, ensuring optimal performance and compliance with regulatory standards. The technician will diagnose issues using advanced refrigeration diagnostics, including refrigerant leak detection, pressure testing, and electrical system analysis. This includes executing component repairs and replacements, such as brazing of copper refrigerant lines, evacuation of systems, and recharging with the appropriate refrigerants (e.g., R-404A, R-134a, R-22). Additionally, the role involves calibrating and adjusting control systems, such as thermostats, pressure switches, and defrost timers, to ensure systems are operating within specified parameters. The technician must be proficient in interpreting and analyzing complex technical diagrams, blueprints, and refrigeration piping schematics, as well as utilizing refrigerant pressure-temperature relationship tables to calculate superheat and subcooling, ensuring systems are charged correctly and operating efficiently. Operating and maintaining electrical and mechanical testing equipment, such as multimeters, clamp meters, refrigerant recovery machines, and vacuum pumps, with a focus on safety and precision, is essential. Responsibilities also include maintaining detailed records of all shop inventories, including refrigerants, lubricants, and specialized tools. The technician is expected to identify the need for and request new or specialized equipment, ensuring the shop is equipped to handle the latest refrigeration technologies and systems. Engaging with medical staff and research personnel to understand specific equipment issues, communicating proposed repair or maintenance plans, and providing thorough follow-up is a key aspect of this role. \u00a0Accurately completing all required documentation, including maintenance logs, repair reports, and safety checklists, and collaborating effectively with other technical shops and departments within the Engineering and Operations division are also crucial. This position requires a deep understanding of refrigeration principles, strong technical skills, and the ability to work in a critical healthcare environment where the reliability of equipment is paramount. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: Crawling, Crouching, Feeling, Hearing, Kneeling, Reaching, Standing, Stooping, Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Sitting Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Radiation-Therapist---Radiation-Oncology-Clinic_R0090122": {"title": "Radiation Therapist - Radiation Oncology Clinic", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-18\nPosted: Posted 17 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/18/2026 Type of Position: Clinical Staff - Clinical Support Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Evening Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | CASL CA ROC Clinical Treatment Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Under the direct supervision of the Clinical Operations Director, responsible for radiation therapy procedures, dose calculations, chart and routine consistency checks on the treatment machine and simulator during a treatment day, five days a week. Incumbent is subject to overtime and call back as required by the center. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Associate's degree in Radiation Therapy plus 2 years of experience in a healthcare environment OR Bachelor's degree. Current registration by the American Registry of Radiologic Technologists as a radiation therapist with an accredited program of radiation therapy technology. Current Licensure as a Radiation Therapist with the Arkansas Department of Health. Current BLS certification or must successfully obtain certification within the first\u00a030 days of employment. Additional Information: Responsibilities: Performs radiation therapy procedures according to the physician's orders and departmental guidelines, determines and prepares the setup within established parameters, calculates monitor units, and records patient treatment information in the EMR while maintaining confidentiality. Maintains and submits daily patient EMR information, charges, schedules, and census. Communicates to patients and families pertinent information pertaining to routine during radiation therapy, i.e., appointments, skin care, treatment field care, proper attire, etc. Assesses and evaluates patient needs and treatment problems, recommends intervention, and acts in accordance with physician practices and departmental policies while maintaining confidentiality. Investigates problems or unsatisfactory procedures and recommends possible solutions. Performs checks on patients' EMR for accuracy and proper documentation according to established procedures. Schedules patients for daily treatments. Maintains quality control of patient EMR and treatment parameters by implementing guidelines on a regular basis. Maintains room cleanliness, linens and needed supplies in treatment room and notifies proper personnel of areas needing attention. Performs daily warm-up and start-up procedures of equipment, quality control checks, and notifies proper personnel of equipment malfunction and/or adverse conditions. Constructs patient treatment aids, bolus material, positioning and immobilization devices and checks for suitability and accuracy. Conducts equipment cleaning and lubricating, evaluates accessories for damage, and coordinates repair. Performs checks on the patient's EMR for accuracy and proper documentation according to established procedures. Schedules patients for daily treatments. Maintains quality control of patient EMR and treatment parameters by implementing guidelines on a regular basis. Maintains room cleanliness, linens, and needed supplies in the treatment room and notifies proper personnel of areas needing attention. May perform other duties as assigned. Salary Information: \"Commensurate with education and experience\" Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Criminal Background Check, Substance Abuse Testing This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Lifting, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Stooping Occasional Physical Activity: Crouching, Kneeling Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Proton-Radiation-Therapist---Second-Shift_R0085405-1": {"title": "Proton Radiation Therapist - Second Shift", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-18\nPosted: Posted 17 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/18/2026 Type of Position: Clinical Staff - Clinical Support Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Evening Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | CASL CA ROC Clinical Treatment Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Required to maintain a higher level of vigilance in patient preparation, immobilization, alignment, image-guidance interpretation and beam delivery as prescribed by a radiation oncologist. Expected to work quickly and efficiently at all times. Must be able to or willing to learn how to review x-ray images with heightened demand for accuracy, notifying the clinical team of any discrepant findings. Must understand the intricacies of the proton machine, one of the most sophisticated and labor-intensive treatment delivery systems available in the United States with the Proton Center of Arkansas being only one of 46 operational centers. Must have a deeper understanding of and training in principles of particle therapy. Required to communicate and work in tandem with an on-site engineering team provided by the device vendor and assist in making decisions when managing much more frequent downtime situations and be expected to have more flexibility due to potential for extended/make-up hours. In addition, must be able to perform CT simulations and QACTs appropriate for proton treatment and dose assessment. Under the direct supervision of the Clinical Operations Director; responsible for radiation therapy procedures, dose calculations, chart and routine consistency checks on the treatment machine and simulator during a treatment day, five days a week. This is subject to overtime, cross coverage of photons, and call back as required by the center. *Training can be provided on site upon hire* Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Associate's degree in radiation therapy PLUS two (2) years of experience in a healthcare environment OR Bachelor's degree in radiation therapy Current registration by the American Registry of Radiologic Technologists as a radiation therapist with an accredited program of radiation therapy technology PLUS Current Licensure as a Radiation Therapist with the Arkansas Department of Health. Current BLS certification or must successfully obtain certification within the first\u00a030 days of employment. Additional Information: Responsibilities: Performs proton therapy procedures according to physician's orders and departmental guidelines, determines and prepares set-up within established parameters, calculates monitor units and records patient treatment information in the EMR , while maintaining confidentiality. Maintains and submits daily patient EMR information, charges, schedules, and census. Assesses and evaluates patient needs and treatment related issues, recommends intervention and acts in accordance with physician practices and departmental policies while maintaining confidentiality. \u00a0 Regularly investigates problems or unsatisfactory procedures and recommends possible solutions. Performs checks on patient's EMR for accuracy and proper documentation according to established procedures. Schedules patients for daily treatments. Maintains quality control of patient EMR and treatment parameters by implementing guidelines on a regular basis. Maintains room cleanliness, linens and needed supplies in treatment room and notifies proper personnel of areas needing attention. Evaluates, teaches and monitors the clinical and didactic education of radiation therapist, dosimetry, clinical resident, physics resident, and diagnostic students. May perform other duties as assigned Note: The proton therapists will be expected to have more flexibility than normal due to the fact that there is only one proton unit. In the event of system downtime, the treatment day is commonly extended or rescheduled to assure all patients are treated. Salary Information: \"Commensurate with education and experience\" Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Criminal Background Check, Substance Abuse Testing This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Lifting, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Pulling, Pushing, Repetitive Motion, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Hearing, Lifting, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Pulling, Pushing, Repetitive Motion, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Crouching, Kneeling, Sharps, Stooping Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAFS--University-of-Arkansas-Fort-Smith/Coordinator--Health-Learning-Resource-Center_R0090010": {"title": "Coordinator, Health Learning Resource Center", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-18\nPosted: Posted 17 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Faculty - Non-Tenure (Clinical) Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Fort Smith University of Arkansas \u2013 Fort Smith The University of Arkansas - Fort Smith is a dynamic, mid-sized public university that\u2019s redefining higher education. We\u2019re on a mission to provide transformative, hands-on learning experiences for students of all backgrounds and aspirations. Our multi-faceted approach to education offers a wealth of opportunities, with over 70 academic programs, including certificates, associate, bachelor\u2019s, and master\u2019s degrees. We\u2019re committed to building a diverse community that mirrors Arkansas\u2019s rich tapestry, reflecting our dedication to serving the state\u2019s varied population while enhancing the quality of our institution. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life, and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10 percent of employee salary. \u00a0 Fort Smith, Arkansas Nestled along the Arkansas River, this vibrant city offers a perfect blend of history, culture, and natural beauty. Immerse yourself in the rich heritage of the Old West at the Fort Smith National Historic Site, explore the eclectic local art scene, or take a scenic stroll along the picturesque riverfront trails. With a welcoming community, diverse dining options, and a thriving downtown, Fort Smith is the ideal destination for history enthusiasts and those seeking modern amenities. Thank you for your interest in joining our university. Below you will find details for the position including any supplementary documentation and/or questions you should review before submitting your application. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at (479) 788-7080. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 479-788-7080. Applicants are required to submit a request for each position to which they have applied. Department: College of Health, Education, and Human Sciences Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Coordinator of Health Learning Resource Center (HLRC) has responsibility for all activities, equipment, and resources associated with the HLRC. This includes oversight of the day-to-day operation of simulation activities in the high-fidelity simulation lab as well as in the skills labs. The coordinator also oversees all operation, care, inventory, maintenance, troubleshooting, minor repairs and of simulation equipment, lab equipment, supplies, models, media and low/high fidelity manikins. This is a 12 month position. The position reports to the Dean of the College of Health, Education, and Human Sciences. Qualifications: Required Education and/or Work Experience: Minimum qualifications include a bachelor\u2019s degree in nursing, current license as a registered nurse in the State of Arkansas, and 3-5 years of clinical experience in medical-surgical or intensive care nursing with a solid understanding of human pathophysiology. Preferred Education and/or Work Experience: Bachelor\u2019s degree in nursing. Essential Job Duties and Responsibilities: (9%) Set up and operate simulation equipment with the ability to manipulate physiologic data, follow medical aspects of scenarios, interpret participant\u2019s responses and make appropriate adjustments based on participant\u2019s actions along with audio-video recording, task trainer, and other supplies for simulation exercises to meet training objectives. (9%) Coordinating all aspects of human and non-human simulation activities including but not limited to the following; integrating, maintaining, operating computer and audiovisual technology, performing pre and post simulation activities, executing simulation sessions equipment (patient simulators, task trainers, hospital equipment, supplies, audiovisual equipment, pyxis) and applying moulage as needed. (7%) Contribute to the design, development, testing, and implementation of training materials and scenarios. (4%) Conduct a scenario pre-brief and assist the instructor with after action report (debrief) if needed. (5%) Maintains and updates memorandums of agreements and affiliation agreements with healthcare facilities. (5%) Oversees all operation, care, inventory, maintenance, troubleshooting, minor repairs and of simulation equipment as required along with lab equipment, supplies, models, media and low/high fidelity manikins. (3%) Prepare recommendation for approval of purchasing requisitions of supplies, materials and lab equipment. (13%) Provide remediation of students as requested by faculty on performance-based skills throughout all levels (15%) Set up and prepare equipment for instructional use in skills lab and health assessment lab to meet faculty teaching objectives. (4%) Coordinates student scheduling of campus labs, practices sessions and/or video recording for clinical competency performance examination (CPE). (3%) Orients faculty and students to the use of high-fidelity patient simulators. (2%) Coordinate and provide student logistics, and administration support needs. (4%) Facilitate simulation training and provide feedback to the Lead Faculty and Simulation Coordinator. (1%) Duties may vary and are subject to change based on specific site requirements, training platform, and equipment at each site. Responsible for maintaining a positive work atmosphere by acting and communicating in a manner to foster teamwork and by providing leadership to subordinates. Requires consistent on-time attendance Other Job Duties and Responsibilities: (2%) Oversees biohazard services, maintain safety standards with regard to use of equipment and hazardous waste disposal. (3%) Interviews, hires and evaluates the performance of student workers in the HLRC. (2%) Acts as a liaison between faculty and healthcare facilities in negotiating clinical contracts. (2%) Attends national simulation forums and conferences as appropriate to identify current trends in lab and simulation pedagogies. (2%) Assist in fit testing (N95 mask) for radiology and nursing program. (4%) Maintain faculty compliance in all health sciences department via Castle Branch/ Precheck. (1%) Other duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: To perform the job successfully, the following competencies are required for the essential functions of this position: Must be familiar with varied types of media such as computer software and simulation equipment. Must be a highly motivated self-starter with a high degree of technical computer knowledge. Have excellent verbal and written communication skills. Must have effective organizational and interpersonal skills, creative problem-solving ability, critical thinking and able to balance multiple tasks simultaneously. Additional Information: Working Relationships : Position requires regular contact with staff, students, other campus departments, organizations, and the public. List Employees Supervised: Student worker(s). Special Job Dimensions : Required abilities that include walking, standing for up to eight hours, bending, reaching, turning, listening, observing, and moderate-to-heavy lifting (at least 50 pounds). Must be physically and emotionally able to complete all job requirements. Background Check Requirements: Criminal Background Check, and Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) Check. This job description is not designed to contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties, and/or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time with or without notice. Salary Information: $51,000 Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Please upload a copy of current nursing license Recruitment Contact Information: HR 479-788-7080 All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: No Background Check Required This position may be subject to a pre-employment criminal background check, sex offender registry check, financial history background check, and/or drug screening. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication and/or adverse financial history alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background checks and drug screening information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Benton/Diagnostic-Cardiac-Medical-Sonographer--UAMS-Health-Benton-Bryant-_R0090204-1": {"title": "Diagnostic Cardiac Medical Sonographer (UAMS Health Benton/Bryant)", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-18\nPosted: Posted 17 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/08/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Shift Vary (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: INA | Institutional Admin Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Join the UAMS Health Benton/Bryant team as a Cardiac Echo Technician, where you will play a vital role in performing diagnostic echocardiograms and ensuring patient safety and comfort during procedures. Your role is to explain the procedure to patients, obtain medical histories, and ensure patient comfort during the test. As the Cardiac Echo Technician, you will follow safety protocols and procedures to protect patients and yourself from potential hazards associated with ultrasound imaging. Help us advance patient care and make a difference in the lives of those we serve, Apply today! Qualifications: Qualifications: High School Diploma Graduation from an accredited Medical Sonography Program.\u00a0\u00a0 Cardiac ultrasound experience, including treadmill and pharmacologic stress testing preferred. \u200b Prefer Registered Diagnostic Cardiac Sonographer (RDCS) or Registered Cardiac Sonographer (RCS).\u00a0 Must be registry eligible.\u00a0 Must complete registration within one year of employment. Current BLS required. Knowledge, Skills, & Abilities: Technical Expertise: Skilled in performing echocardiograms with advanced imaging techniques; knowledge of cardiac diseases and pathology. Clinical Skills: Competent in initiating IV access, administering contrast agents, and monitoring patients during procedures. Documentation and Compliance: Experienced with EPIC and CNL documentation guidelines; accurate in billing and coding. Communication and Patient Care: Strong interpersonal skills for explaining procedures and ensuring patient comfort; ability to collaborate with physicians and healthcare teams. Safety and Protocol Adherence: Committed to safety protocols and maintaining high-quality imaging standards. Additional Information: Responsibilities: Patient Preparation and Communication : Explain procedures to patients and obtain their medical histories. Ensure patient comfort and safety during all tests. Echocardiogram Procedures : Conduct transthoracic, treadmill exercise, and pharmacological stress echocardiograms using advanced techniques such as M-Mode, 2D, Doppler, Color Flow, Spectral Doppler, and bubble studies. Assist physicians with procedures and examinations, including transesophageal studies, patient monitoring, and ultrasound equipment operation. Perform online and offline measurements, calculations, and velocities of acquired images. Contrast Administration : Initiate IV access as needed, following UAMS policies and procedures. Administer contrast agents (e.g., perflutren or bubble) in compliance with UAMS guidelines and document usage for performance improvement tracking. Data Analysis and Reporting : Recognize and report critical findings to the reading cardiologist immediately. Identify distinct types of cardiac diseases and pathology. Documentation and Compliance : Accurately complete billing and coding for performed procedures. Document patient information and procedures in EPIC following CNL guidelines. Physical Requirements Constant : Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers (keyboarding), Repetitive motion, Sitting, Standing, Walking Frequent : Grasping, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Sharps Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Benton/Physical-Therapist--UAMS-Health-Benton-Bryant-_R0090199-1": {"title": "Physical Therapist (UAMS Health Benton/Bryant)", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-18\nPosted: Posted 17 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/08/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Shift Vary (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: INA | Institutional Admin Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The physical therapist provides an individualized evaluation, during which the client, family/caregiver, and physical therapist determine the patient's goals, customize interventions to optimize the person's ability to perform functional activities, and continuously assess progress towards goals to ensure goals are being met and/or to modify the intervention plan based on the patient's needs and skills. Functional outcomes data is completed through collection of best practice data via patient questionnaires, performance measures, and documented treatment interventions. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor\u2019s degree in physical therapy if graduated prior to 2002 OR Master\u2019s degree in Physical Therapy if graduated prior to 2016 OR Doctorate degree in Physical Therapy. Licensed as a Physical Therapist by the Arkansas State Board of Physical Therapy or eligible for licensure. Preferred Qualifications: Master's degree OR Doctorate\u00a0in Physical Therapy PLUS (2) two years of experience in Physical Therapy. Inpatient therapy experience with emphasis on orthopedic conditions OCS Additional Information: Responsibilities: Performs comprehensive examination of patients using appropriate tests/measures, completes the evaluation, and formulates an individualized plan of care. Provides evidence-based quality patient treatments and monitors patient for physiological status during sessions. Provides individualized patient education. Documents evaluations, treatment sessions, and education sessions and submits accurate charges according to regulatory policies. Provides education regarding physical therapy discipline. Serves as a clinical instructor/mentor and provides education to other disciplines within UAMS and/or the community. Participates in multidisciplinary and department communication, including patient care discussions and/or meetings and unit/department/hospital meetings. Performs other duties as assigned. Physical Requirements : Constant : Hearing, Manipulating items with fingers (keyboarding), Repetitive motion Frequent : Talking, Standing, Sitting, Reaching, Feeling, Lifting Occasional : Balancing, Climbing, Crawling, Crouching, Driving, Grasping, Kneeling, Pulling, Pushing, Sharps, Stooping Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Benton/Supervisor--Food-Preparation--UAMS-Health-Benton-Bryant-_R0090202-1": {"title": "Supervisor, Food Preparation (UAMS Health Benton/Bryant)", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-18\nPosted: Posted 17 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/08/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Shift Vary (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: INA | Institutional Admin Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Food Preparation Supervisor is responsible for the supervision of food service personnel, directing food service activities, monitoring security and safety practices, coordinating the production and serving of food, ordering supplies, and the preparation of reports. This position is governed by state and federal laws and agency policy. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: High School Diploma or GED. 2 years of experience in institutional or commercial food service operations, including 1 year supervisory experience. Self-directed, flexible and innovative. Good leadership and organizational skills. Preferred Qualifications: Bachelors degree in dietetics or a related field, ServSafe Certified, Certified Dietary Manager. Additional Information: Responsibilities: Perform all task of the cashier and the food preparation technician with proficiency. Helps staff prepare food, make coffee drinks, cleaning, cashiering, and any other tasks that are necessary while providing outstanding customer service. Ensures that the staff are following recipes that are designed by management. Handles questions, concerns and complaints. Trains and supervise all staff while following UAMS policies and procedure. Performs all register counting duties while following the policies and procedures, as well as, holds the staff accountable for the policies and procedures. Completes all documentation daily. Accurately records the temperatures of the coolers and food to ensure customer safety. Audit staff duties and completes daily cleaning checklists for inspection.\u00a0 Performs other duties assigned. \u00a0 PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS: Stand: Continuously Sit: Occasionally Walk: Frequently Bend, crawl, crouch, kneel, stoop or reach overhead: Frequently Lift and carry weight: 26 - 50 lbs Push and pull weight: 26 - 50 lbs Use hands to touch, handle or feel: Continuously Talk: Continuously Hear: Continuously Taste or smell: Occasionally Read, concentrate, think analytically: Continuously Physical Environment: Inside Medical Facility Environment Noise Level: Loud Visual Requirements: Color discrimination, Depth perception, Far visual acuity, Near visual acuity Hazards: Chemical, Electrical, Heavy machinery Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-Arkansas-at-Pine-Bluff/Grants-Development---Research-Specialist_R0089728": {"title": "Grants Development & Research Specialist", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-17\nPosted: Posted 18 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Professional Staff - Project/Program Administration Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff The University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff is an 1890 Land-Grant HBCU with a diverse student population, competitive degree offerings and stellar faculty. For more than 140 years, the University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff has worked to create an environment that inculcates learning, growth and productivity while affording a basic need to its students \u2013 a chance to advance. The 15:1 student to teacher ratio makes it possible to maintain a learning environment with close interaction between students and faculty while challenging curricula encourage our students to seek and fulfill their potential. You can excel in your chosen field of study through a curriculum of \u00a0 Certificate and Associates degree programs,\u00a0 more than thirty\u00a0 Undergraduate programs, Master\u2019s degree programs and a Doctorate program in Aquaculture/Fisheries. You can also develop workplace readiness through internships, co-ops and fellowships in the U.S. and abroad. Out-of-class experiences and student involvement include more than 90 student organizations, an internationally renowned Vesper Choir, Marching Band, Concert Bands, Wind Symphony, nationally recognized debate team, award-winning theater department and accomplished athletic program. Though the main campus is in Pine Bluff, its reach is worldwide. UAPB has an extended campus in North Little Rock and offers as well as online courses. With the addition of the Arkansas Research and Education Optical Network (ARE-ON), students can engage in information exchange with others anywhere in the world. There are also Research and Extension offices in Lonoke, Newport and Lake Village and collaborations with other colleges and universities in the State through the National Science Foundation funded STEM (Science, Technology, Engineering and Mathematics) Academy. As the second oldest land-grant institution in the state of Arkansas, the mission of this No Excuse University remains the same \u2013 to provide a high quality, affordable education with a personal touch. We invite you to Become a Part of the Pride at the University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process and require reasonable accommodations, please contact Human Resources at 870.575.8400 . Department: Research and Graduate Education | Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Position Summary The Grants Development & Research Specialist provides program-wide grant development, proposal submission, and research support across all initiatives of the 15% Set-Aside Programs at the University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff (UAPB), including the Minority Research Center (MRC), Minority Initiative Sub-Recipient Grant Office (MISRGO), and Graduate Addiction Studies Program (GASP). This position identifies funding opportunities; develops and writes competitive grant proposals and funding initiatives; and assists team members in preparing and submitting proposals through the Office of Research and Sponsored Programs (ORSP) (federal grants) and Institutional Advancement (i.e. private foundation grants), ensuring compliance with institutional, state, and federal agency guidelines, deadlines, and reporting requirements. In addition, this position serves as the program's researcher, gathering and synthesizing data, literature, and journal findings on tobacco use, tobacco prevention and cessation, substance use disorders, and minority health disparities to inform proposal development and program strategy across MRC, MISRGO, and GASP. This role plays a critical part in expanding external funding, strengthening program sustainability, and supporting research, education, outreach, and community engagement initiatives that address tobacco use, substance use disorders, tobacco prevention and cessation, minority health disparities, and public health challenges as it relates to tobacco use throughout Arkansas. The successful candidate will work collaboratively with the program directors, university leadership, faculty, researchers, administrative staff, community-based organizations, public health partners, and funding agencies to expand and secure funding and strengthen its impact to advance tobacco prevention and cessation initiatives. Essential Duties and Responsibilities The position will primarily research, write, and support the submission of grant proposals across MISRGO, MRC, and GASP related to tobacco prevention and cessation initiatives, community health promotion and health equity programs, minority health and disparity reduction efforts, youth prevention and engagement programs, capacity-building and community outreach initiatives, and public health education and awareness campaigns. This includes assisting team members with preparing and submitting proposals through ORSP and Institutional Advancement, as well as conducting ongoing research into data, literature, and journal publications relevant to the program's focus areas. Key reporting responsibilities include: \u00b7 Network, research, identify, and pursue funding opportunities from federal, state, local, and private funding sources. \u00b7 Assist Principal Investigators with proposal planning, timelines, and required documentation. \u00b7 Assist team members across MISRGO, MRC, and GASP with preparing and submitting proposals through the Office of Research and Sponsored Programs (ORSP) and Institutional Advancement, including private foundation grants. \u00b7 Collaborate with program staff to develop measurable goals, objectives and evaluation plans. \u00b7 Prepare submission of high-quality competitive grant proposals, applications, budgets, and supporting documentation. \u00b7 Develop compelling narratives that align with programs\u2019 missions, public health priorities and organizational objectives. \u00b7 Coordinate proposal development activities with internal and external stakeholders. \u00b7 Cultivate partnerships with funding agencies and community organizations focused on reducing tobacco use and health disparities in Arkansas. \u00b7 Analyze programs data to demonstrate impact and support funding requests. \u00b7 Serve as the program's researcher: research and synthesize data, statistics, and peer-reviewed journal literature on tobacco use, tobacco prevention and cessation, substance use disorders, and minority health disparities to inform proposal narratives, program design, and reporting. \u00b7 Monitor emerging research, trends, and best practices across program focus areas and share relevant findings with program directors and staff. Qualifications: Required Qualifications Bachelor's degree in Public Health, Public Administration, Research Administration, Communications, Nonprofit Management, English, Business Administration, or a related field. Minimum of three years of experience in grant writing, grant management, program administration, research administration, or nonprofit development. Knowledge of public health, tobacco control, addiction services, or minority health initiatives. Demonstrated success in developing, submitting, and securing grant proposals. Excellent written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills. Excellent editing and proofreading skills. Experience developing budgets and evaluation plans. Strong organizational and project management abilities. Proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite and electronic grants management systems. Ability to analyze data, evaluate programs, and prepare accurate reports. Attention to detail and deadline management. Strong strategic planning and problem-solving skills Ability to work independently and as part of a multidisciplinary team. Experience conducting research and literature reviews using academic databases, journals, and other credible sources to inform proposals and reports. Ability to work effectively in a remote environment, participate in required weekly virtual meetings, and travel to Arkansas at least one week per quarter. Preferred Qualifications Master's degree in Public Health, Public Administration, Research Administration, Communications, Nonprofit Management, English, Business Administration, or a related field. Experience with public health and community-based grant programs. Knowledge of community-based participatory research, health disparities research, and tobacco prevention and cessation strategies. Experience working with underserved and minority populations. Knowledge of federal, state, and local application processes. Experience or desire to work with diverse teams of faculty researchers and staff Familiarity with state and federal grant compliance requirements. Grant Professional Certification (GPC) or Certified Research Administrator (CRA) credential. Additional Information: Work Location and Schedule This is a full-time, benefits-eligible position that may be performed remotely. The successful candidate must be able to work independently in a home office or other remote setting with reliable high-speed internet, a suitable workspace, and the equipment needed to perform essential job functions, and must be available during core UAPB business hours. In-person travel to Arkansas is required at least one week per quarter to meet with program directors, faculty, and community partners; additional in-person visits may be required based on program needs. The employee is responsible for covering their own travel expenses associated with required in-person visits to Arkansas. Weekly virtual team meetings with program directors and staff are required to ensure alignment across MISRGO, MRC, and GASP. Applicant must reside within the United States and be able to travel domestically as required. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants (Please upload all required documents in the \"Resume\" attachment section of your application to be considered for this position) : Recruitment Contact Information: Sharron Williams Employment Manager 870-575-8403 williamssm@uapb.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: The University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff may conduct pre-employment background checks on certain positions for applicants being considered for employment. \u00a0 The background checks may include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. \u00a0 Required checks are identified in the position listing. \u00a0 A criminal background check or arrest pending adjudication information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absences of a relationship to the requirements of the position. \u00a0 Background check information will be used in a consistent, non-discriminatory manner consistent with the state and federal law. \u00a0 The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAPBMCMain-Campus/Assistant-Professor-of-Mathematics---Statistics_R0089890": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Mathematics & Statistics", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-17\nPosted: Posted 18 Days Ago\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Faculty - Tenure/Tenure Track Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff The University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff is an 1890 Land-Grant HBCU with a diverse student population, competitive degree offerings and stellar faculty. For more than 140 years, the University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff has worked to create an environment that inculcates learning, growth and productivity while affording a basic need to its students \u2013 a chance to advance. The 15:1 student to teacher ratio makes it possible to maintain a learning environment with close interaction between students and faculty while challenging curricula encourage our students to seek and fulfill their potential. You can excel in your chosen field of study through a curriculum of \u00a0 Certificate and Associates degree programs,\u00a0 more than thirty\u00a0 Undergraduate programs, Master\u2019s degree programs and a Doctorate program in Aquaculture/Fisheries. You can also develop workplace readiness through internships, co-ops and fellowships in the U.S. and abroad. Out-of-class experiences and student involvement include more than 90 student organizations, an internationally renowned Vesper Choir, Marching Band, Concert Bands, Wind Symphony, nationally recognized debate team, award-winning theater department and accomplished athletic program. Though the main campus is in Pine Bluff, its reach is worldwide. UAPB has an extended campus in North Little Rock and offers as well as online courses. With the addition of the Arkansas Research and Education Optical Network (ARE-ON), students can engage in information exchange with others anywhere in the world. There are also Research and Extension offices in Lonoke, Newport and Lake Village and collaborations with other colleges and universities in the State through the National Science Foundation funded STEM (Science, Technology, Engineering and Mathematics) Academy. As the second oldest land-grant institution in the state of Arkansas, the mission of this No Excuse University remains the same \u2013 to provide a high quality, affordable education with a personal touch. We invite you to Become a Part of the Pride at the University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process and require reasonable accommodations, please contact Human Resources at 870.575.8400 . Department: Math & Computer Science Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Department of Mathematics and Computer Science at the University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff is seeking qualified candidates to apply for a full-time tenure track (FTTT) Assistant Professor of Mathematics & Statistics. Candidates must be able to teach both lower and upper-level undergraduate courses in mathematics, statistics and/or data science, provide academic advising to students, develop, and design curriculum plans to foster student learning, stimulate class discussions, and ensure student engagement. Candidates will be expected to cooperatively and individually initiate research in the field of interest and participate in student co-curricular discipline-related activities which may include research, teaching, and designing new cutting-edge courses, community-based projects, or other extracurricular activities. The successful candidate will be expected to perform the usual curricular and professional duties associated with an academic appointment at the rank of Assistant Professor. For the purposes of reappointment, tenure, and promotion, emphasis will be placed on teaching effectiveness, scholarly, and creative achievements, and service to the University and community including activities in support of student retention. This is a nine 9-month tenured track position, reporting to the Department Chair. Teach a range of graduate and undergraduate courses in Mathematics, Statistics, and Data Science, including but not limited to calculus, linear algebra, probability, statistical modeling, machine learning, and data analysis. Provide mentorship and academic advising to graduate and undergraduate students, offering guidance on academic programs, research opportunities, and career paths in Mathematics, Statistics, and Data Science. Pursue scholarly activities such as publishing research, participate in professional conferences by maintaining memberships. Maintain a research agenda for individual research & support departmental grants efforts. Advise math majors, promote student retention, foster department & university strategic plans. Qualifications: PhD degree in Mathematics, Statistics, Data Science or closely related field from an accredited institution. Additional Information: Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Curriculum Vitae, Listing of Publications, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Statement of Research Philosophy, Statement of Teaching Philosophy, Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants (Please upload all required documents in the \"Resume\" attachment section of your application to be considered for this position) : Recruitment Contact Information: Sharron Williams Employment Manager 870-575-8403 All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check The University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff may conduct pre-employment background checks on certain positions for applicants being considered for employment. \u00a0 The background checks may include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. \u00a0 Required checks are identified in the position listing. \u00a0 A criminal background check or arrest pending adjudication information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absences of a relationship to the requirements of the position. \u00a0 Background check information will be used in a consistent, non-discriminatory manner consistent with the state and federal law. \u00a0 The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Feeling, Grasping, Hearing, Kneeling, Lifting, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Pulling Frequent Physical Activity: Grasping, Hearing, Kneeling, Lifting, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Pulling Occasional Physical Activity: Feeling, Grasping, Hearing, Kneeling, Lifting, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Pulling, Reaching, Sitting, Standing, Stooping, Talking, Walking Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Medical-Laboratory-Scientist-I--HLA_R0090024-1": {"title": "Medical Laboratory Scientist I- HLA", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-17\nPosted: Posted 18 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/17/2026 Type of Position: Clinical Staff - Medical Ancillary Support Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Shift Vary (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | LPSL CPATH Human Lympho Antibodies Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: This position will work under the supervision and direction of the HLA laboratory supervisor. Medical Laboratory Scientists I in the HLA laboratory perform a variety of technical procedures including HLA typing by rSSO and next generation sequencing methods, Luminex based HLA Antibody identification, and donor/recipient flow cytometric cross-matching. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in Medical Laboratory Science, Medical Technology, Chemistry, or Biology. ASCP or another accrediting agency certified or eligible (Certification must be obtained within one year of employment). Preferred Qualifications: Bachelors degree in Medical Laboratory Sciences ASCP Certified Previous HLA experience Additional Information: Job Requirements: They are expected to keep all instrumentation in good working order and identify and notify the supervisor or lead tech of instrument malfunctions. They should be able to aid in instrument repair. They should be able to identify abnormal or discrepant results. They will have limited participation in student teaching and assisting of other personnel rotating through the section. They will have limited administrative duties. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status, Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Criminal Background Check, Substance Abuse Testing This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding Frequent Physical Activity: Feeling, Grasping, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Repetitive Motion, Sharps, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Crouching, Kneeling, Lifting, Stooping Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/North-Little-Rock/HVAC-Skilled-Tradesman_R0090061": {"title": "HVAC Skilled Tradesman", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-17\nPosted: Posted 18 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 11/30/2026 Type of Position: Skilled Labor Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas Pulaski Technical College University of Arkansas - Pulaski Technical College at North Little Rock is an integral part of the Arkansas Technical and Community College System maintained by the State of Arkansas. The college is governed by the University of Arkansas System Board of Trustees and a seven-member Board of Visitors and derives its support largely from student tuition and fees and legislative appropriations. UA - Pulaski Tech, a comprehensive two-year college, offers associate degree and certificate programs for students who plan to transfer to four-year colleges and universities and/or for career preparation and advancement. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply link/button. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at (501) 812-2839. Department: Maintenance Operations Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The responsibilities of the HVAC Skilled Trades Helper include performing routine maintenance, replacing parts, repairing machinery, and assisting with general maintenance of buildings and equipment. General Responsibilities: \u2022 The HVAC Skilled Trades Helper maintains, repairs, and trouble shoots on HVAC systems and the associated equipment. \u2022 Under supervision, you'll change filters, clean coils, assist with installs, and check ductwork for leaks. \u2022 Assist with other maintenance tasks when needed. \u2022 Regular, reliable and non-disruptive attendance is an essential job duty, as is the ability to create and maintain collegial, harmonious working relationships with others. \u2022 Other duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills, & Abilities: \u2022 Knowledge of tools, equipment, and materials used in HVAC and maintenance areas. \u2022 Ability to learn to perform manual labor under varying working conditions \u2022 Ability to understand and follow oral instructions Qualifications: Required Qualifications: The formal education equivalent of a high school diploma Physical requirements include lifting, stooping, pulling, pushing, reaching, and climbing. EPA 608 Universal Technician Certification Valid Drivers License Preferred Qualifications: Three years\u2019 experience in the HVAC & Refrigeration Additional Information: Salary Information: $34,000 Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants Must have EPA and Valid Drivers License Recruitment Contact Information: Robert A Cole Maintenance & Operation Manager rcole@uaptc.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: University of Arkansas - Pulaski Technical College is committed to providing a safe campus community. Title IX protects the college community from sexual harassment in a school's education programs and activities. This means that Title IX protects the college community in connection with all academic, educational, extracurricular, athletic, and other programs of the school, whether those programs take place in a school's facilities, in college transportation, at a class or training program sponsored by the school at another location, or elsewhere. \u00a0 We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-Arkansas-Community-College-at-Batesville/Welcome-Center-Office-Manager_R0089989": {"title": "Welcome Center Office Manager", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-17\nPosted: Posted 18 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. Closing Date: Type of Position: Staff - Clerical Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas Community College at Batesville The University of Arkansas Community College at Batesville (UACCB) is a comprehensive community college committed to providing learning experiences that improve the lives of those we serve. UACCB provides affordable access to technical education and college transfer programs that meet the diverse higher education needs of the citizens of north central Arkansas. \u00a0 These programs are provided to the traditional college student as well as to high school students through a state approved Secondary Area Career Center. \u00a0 The College also promotes economic development and an enhanced quality of life for the community through adult education, developmental education, customized business and industry training, and continuing education programs. UACCB's mission is to provide quality educational opportunities within a supportive learning environment. We promote success through community partnerships, responsive programs, and an enduring commitment to improvement. Thank you for your interest. \u00a0 We hope you will be joining us soon! After reviewing the Job Duties and Qualifications listed below, click the Apply button at the top of the page to begin the application process. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process or for general application assistance, please contact the Human Resource Office at (870) 612-2045. Department: Director of Academic Services Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Welcome Center Office Manager oversees daily front-desk operations, visitor traffic, and institutional communications for the Welcome Center. This role manages student scheduling, check-in and departure workflows, and main-line communications (phone, email, and text) to ensure a seamless experience for students connecting with College Navigators and campus services. Additionally, this position serves as a central hub for student outreach, maintaining contact lists, and deploying targeted messaging campaigns to support enrollment and retention. Caring Campus Responsibilities: As a member of the UACCB community, each employee is responsible for advancing the Caring Campus culture to enhance student connection and success and to embody the campus purpose: Improve Lives. Key duties include adhering to the campus name badge policy, treating all visitors as guests, engaging with the campus community by reviewing institutional communications, participating in campus events, and supporting a collaborative, positive workplace environment. Qualifications: Qualifications \u00a0 High School Diploma/GED \u00a0 Two years of experience in office management, customer service, or administrative role featuring high-volume scheduling, calendar management, and direct public interaction.\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 Preferred Qualifications \u00a0 Associate\u2019s degree in business, management, or related field.\u00a0 \u00a0 Experience managing digital communications, customer management databases (CRMs), or mass-messaging software. \u00a0 Prior experience in a school, college, community agency, or customer-facing administrative environment.\u00a0 \u00a0 Additional Information: Salary Information: $35,000 Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume, Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Optional Documents: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Human Resources hr@uaccb.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry UACCB is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check for all applicants.\u00a0 Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Reaching, Repetitive Motion, Sitting, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Standing, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Lifting, Pulling, Pushing, Stooping Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Van-Buren/Program-Assistant---4-H_R0089811-1": {"title": "Program Assistant - 4-H", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-17\nPosted: Posted 18 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Clerical Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: Division of Agriculture of the University of Arkansas The University of Arkansas System Division of Agriculture is a state wide campus, with faculty based on University campuses, at Research and Extension Centers and in every Arkansas county. It consists of the Arkansas Agricultural Experiment Station (AES) and the Arkansas Cooperative Extension Service (CES), and is home to more than 1400 employees.\u00a0 The Division was established in 1959 and is headed by the Vice-President for Agriculture.\u00a0 The Division headquarters is located in Little Rock with the rest of the University of Arkansas System Administration.\u00a0 As an employer, the University of Arkansas System Division of Agriculture offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance.\u00a0 Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process and require reasonable accommodations, please contact the Division's Office of Program & Employment Compliance at compliance@uada.edu . For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-671-2219 or 479-502-9820. Department: CEA * Staff Chair * Crawford County Department's Website: uada.edu Summary of Job Duties: The Cooperative Extension Service Program Assistant works for an assigned county Extension program under the supervision of a county agent in 4-H and youth development areas. Duties: Self-Management \u2022 Organizes and prioritizes tasks effectively. \u2022 Deals appropriately with interruptions. \u2022 Uses good judgment and decision-making skills. \u2022 Follows attendance and leave policies. \u2022 Practices emotional control. \u2022 Exhibits professional behavior and appearance. \u2022 Ability to work without close supervision. Quality and Quantity of Work \u2022 Maintains 4-H Clubs. Periodically attends 4-H Club meetings. \u2022 Maintains working relationship with all 4-H leaders, members, and parents. \u2022 Recruits adult volunteer leaders youth, and volunteers to form 4-H clubs and grow the community 4-H enrollment/program. \u2022 Follows up promptly with questions and requests for information. \u2022 Maintains accurate 4-H records and submits reports by deadlines. \u2022 Displays acknowledge of 4-H policies and procedures. \u2022 Stays informed of all county, district, and state 4-H events, competitions, camps, activities, etc. Informs 4-H leaders, members and parents of all county, district, and state 4-H events, competitions, camps, activities, etc. Assists 4-Her in preparation for events and competitions. \u2022 Plans, organizes, sets-up, conducts, and cleans-up after all 4-H events, competitions, and activities in the county. \u2022 Conducts regular 4-H leader training meetings. Program Delivery \u2022 Shows sensitivity to individual needs based on culture, race, gender and age. \u2022 Coordinated with agents to conducting educational programs in schools and the community. \u2022 Evaluates the county 4-H program for impact. Communication \u2022 Communicates the benefits and goals of the 4-H program to clientele. \u2022 Makes sure youth, parents and adult leaders are aware of events, activates, meetings and any registration deadlines. \u2022 Uses social media, virtual tools and newsletters to communicate. \u2022 Uses local newspaper, social media and other tools to promote 4-H. \u2022 Listens to feedback and acts to improve. Teamwork \u2022 Shares information, expertise and resources with others. \u2022 Is part of the county Extension Service team to insure and success of the whole Extension program. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications \u2022 High School diploma or equivalent required. \u2022 Must have reliable transportation for use on the job with liability insurance in effect. \u2022 Must successfully complete the standard background check which includes the Arkansas Child Abuse and Neglect Central Registry Check. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Ability to conduct programs and work with all clientele regardless of race, color, national origin, religion, gender, age, disability, marital or veteran status, or any other legally protected status. Ability to communicate effectively, both orally and in writing. Ability to keep accurate records and submit timely reports of activities. Ability to respond positively to supervisor direction. Ability to work without close daily supervision. Additional Information: Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Landon Gunnell, Staff Chair, 479-474-5286 All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Motor Vehicle Reports Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas System Division of Agriculture may conduct pre-employment background checks on certain positions for applicants being considered for employment. \u00a0 The background checks may include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. \u00a0 Required checks are identified in the position listing. \u00a0 A criminal background check or arrest pending adjudication information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absences of a relationship to the requirements of the position. \u00a0 Background check information will be used in a consistent, non-discriminatory manner consistent with the state and federal law. \u00a0 The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Driving, Feeling, Grasping, Standing, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Kneeling, Lifting, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Repetitive Motion, Sitting Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAMS/HVAC-Technician_R0085167": {"title": "HVAC Technician", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-14\nPosted: Posted 21 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/15/2026 Type of Position: Professional Staff - Facilities Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: OPS | Campus Operations HVAC and Controls Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The HVAC Technician is responsible for the maintenance, repair, and modification of HVAC/R systems supporting medical, educational, and research facilities across the UAMS campus. These systems are critical to ensuring a safe, comfortable, and compliant environment for patients, students, and employees. This role responds to routine maintenance needs as well as urgent facility-related issues and emergencies, providing timely and effective solutions to support continuous campus operations. Qualifications: High School Diploma/GED PLUS One (1) year HVAC/R installation and repair experience Technical degree in HVAC/R or related may be accepted in lieu of experience Valid Driver's License Preferred Qualifications: EPA 608 Universal License Additional Information: Responsibilities: Perform maintenance, repair, and installation of HVAC/R systems across campus facilities Troubleshoot and diagnose mechanical, electrical, and control system issues Conduct routine inspections and preventive maintenance to ensure optimal system performance Respond to service calls, work orders, and emergency situations in a timely manner Monitor and adjust building automation systems (BAS) as needed Ensure compliance with safety standards, codes, and regulatory requirements Maintain accurate records of maintenance, repairs, and service activities Collaborate with team members and other departments to resolve facility-related issues Assist with equipment upgrades, system modifications, and special projects as assigned Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Criminal Background Check This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: Crawling, Crouching, Feeling, Hearing, Kneeling, Reaching, Sitting, Standing, Stooping, Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Fayetteville-AR/Data-Science-Program-Teaching-Associate-Professor---12-MONTH_R0089660-1": {"title": "Data Science Program Teaching Associate Professor - 12 MONTH", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-14\nPosted: Posted 21 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com, then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at all University of Arkansas institutions will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students.\u201d University of Arkansas, Fayetteville students will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Student Jobs at UAF.\u201d All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. Closing Date: 09/14/2026 Type of Position: Faculty - Non-Tenure Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Annual Appointment (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas, Fayetteville Founded in 1871, the University of Arkansas is a land grant institution, classified by the Carnegie Foundation among the nation\u2019s top 2 percent of universities with the highest level of research activity. The University of Arkansas works to advance the state and build a better world through education, research, and outreach by providing transformational opportunities and skills, fostering a welcoming climate, and nurturing creativity, discovery, and the spread of new ideas and innovations. The University of Arkansas campus is located in Fayetteville, a welcoming community ranked as one of the best places to live in the U.S. The growing region surrounding Fayetteville is home to numerous Fortune 500 companies and one of the nation\u2019s strongest economies. Northwest Arkansas is also quickly gaining a national reputation for its focus on the arts and overall quality of life. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10% of employee salary. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions, you should review before applying for the opening. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process, please submit a request via the Disability Accommodations | OEOC | University of Arkansas (uark.edu) : Request an Accommodation. Appli\u00adcants are required to submit a request for each position of which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 479.575.5351. Department: Karl Schubert Reports Department's Website: https://datascience.uark.edu Summary of Job Duties: The Data Science Program Teaching Associate Professor is a 12-month 100% appointed, non-tenure track position that provides instruction and assists with the development of course materials for the undergraduate and future graduate Data Science Program and undergraduate and future graduate Data Science Program course sequence, supports academic advising to undergraduate and graduate data science students, supports summer orientation for future graduate data science students, and serves on college and university committees as appropriate. Regular, reliable, and non-disruptive attendance is an essential job duty, as is the ability to create and maintain collegial, harmonious working relationships with others. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Ph.D. or similar terminal degree in Data Science, Data Analytics, or closely related fields (e. g., computer science, statistics, operations research, industrial engineering) from an accredited institution of higher education; conferred by the start of employment Demonstrated effective experience as a teacher for undergraduate and graduate data science, data analytics, or closely related fields courses at the third-year and fourth-year levels Experience with programming in Python, R, and SQL Experience working on multi-disciplinary teams Preferred Qualifications: A record of sustained excellence in teaching and scholarship Recognition for teaching excellence at a regional or national level Knowledge, Skills, & Abilities: Ability to display a commitment to undergraduate and graduate data science students in developing their academic skills, especially upper-level students Ability and interest in developing graduate level course work in data science Additional Information: Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Curriculum Vitae, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title) Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Recruitment Contact Information: Karl Schubert, Director of Data Science, schubert@uark.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Special Instructions to Applicants: Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas seeks to attract, develop and retain high quality faculty, staff and administrators that consistently display practices and behaviors to advance a culture that embeds equal opportunity, educational excellence and unparalleled access for all. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All Application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Skilled-Tradesman-Structural-Carpenter_R0089860": {"title": "Skilled Tradesman/Structural Carpenter", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-14\nPosted: Posted 21 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Skilled Labor Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Little Rock The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is a metropolitan research university that provides an accessible, quality education through flexible learning and unparalleled internship opportunities. At UA Little Rock, we prepare our more than 8,900 students to be innovators and responsible leaders in their fields. Committed to its metropolitan research university mission, UA Little Rock is a driving force in Little Rock's thriving cultural community and a major component of the city and state's growing profile as a regional leader in research, technology transfer, economic development, and job creation. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . Department: Structural Services Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Skilled Tradesman/Structural Carpenter is responsible for the construction or installation and repair of a variety of materials requiring accuracy and good appearance, such as doors, stairs, roofs, partitions, walls, hardware, and fixtures. Make repairs to office furniture, cabinets, etc. Operate a variety of power hand tools and woodworking machinery as required. This position is governed by state and federal laws, and agency/institution policy. Qualifications: Required Education &/or Experience: The formal education equivalent of a high school diploma; Five years of verifiable experience in one or more of the skilled trades; Possess a valid driver\u2019s license and have the ability to drive a vehicle. Preferred Education &/or Experience: Possess or the ability to obtain a Commercial Driver\u2019s License (CDL); Experience operating construction equipment such as forklift, personnel lift, skid-steer, and backhoe. Job Duties & Responsibilities: Install, maintain, repair materials made from wood, wood substitutes, light weight steel and other materials; Install a variety of wall and floor finish materials such as wood, tile, carpet, paint, tape and float sheet rock, and erect or remove walls and ceiling systems; Fit and install trim items, such as doors, stairs, moldings and hardware; Use accepted methods, practices, and safety precautions in completion of skilled trades work; Prepare accurate cost estimates for clients; Understand verbal and written instructions; Willingness to work with a team, assist other skilled tradesmen to complete projects that require multiple trades and tradesmen to work together; Communicate professionally and appropriately with campus community and coworkers; Use work order software program to track assignments, document notes, and log time and materials used; Perform other duties as assigned; which may include painting, roofing, locksmithing, or other overlapping skilled trades. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities : Knowledge of the accepted practices, processes, materials, and tools of the various skilled trades; Knowledge of the laws and regulations relating to one or more of the skilled trades; Ability to provide mathematical and analytical skills necessary to do material estimates for one or more of the skilled trades; Ability to read and interpret blueprints, manuals, schematics, building plans, and/or work drawings to determine specifications and calculate requirements; Ability to maintain, repair, and renovate buildings as assigned; Ability to maintain inventory on needed parts and tools for one or more of the skilled trades; Ability to operate power tools; Ability to measure, cut, shape, assemble, and join moldings, wood materials, drywall and plastic materials, etc.; Ability to fit and install or apply doors, stairs, moldings, hardware, framing, sheet rock walls, drop-in ceiling systems, tile, carpet, and paint; Ability to work on a team, supervise apprentices and other construction workers; Ability to work a flexible schedule which may include nights, weekends, and holidays as assigned; Possess a valid driver\u2019s license and have the ability to drive a vehicle; Work inclement weather schedule as assigned. Additional Information: Salary Information: $40,568.00 Required Documents to Apply: List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Emily Mills, Director of Planning, Design, and Construction email: egmills@ualr.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Motor Vehicle Reports Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Driving, Lifting, Pulling, Pushing, Talking Occasional Physical Activity: Climbing, Crawling, Driving, Kneeling, Sitting, Standing Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAMS/Child-Development-Technician-Searcy--AR_R0085921-1": {"title": "Child Development Technician Searcy, AR", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-14\nPosted: Posted 21 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 10/03/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: COM | Peds Kids First Searcy Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Make a Difference Where It Matters Most! \u2728This position is in Searcy, AR. Kids First is a compassionate, child-centered program dedicated to serving children with special healthcare needs from six weeks to five years old. Within our pediatric day healthcare clinics, children for with developmental delays and other special medical needs receive intensive, nurturing, and individualized early developmental services\u2014setting the foundation for lifelong growth and success. About the Role: Child Development Technician: In this hands-on and rewarding role, the Child Development Technician partners closely with the Early Childhood Development Specialist to provide daily care, support, and developmental interventions for children from birth to age five with special medical and developmental needs. This position is perfect for someone who is: *Passionate about early childhood development *Caring, patient, and energetic *Motivated to positively impact children and families \ud83c\udf1f Why Join KIDS FIRST? Because here, your work isn\u2019t just a job it\u2019s a calling. Every day, you help children grow, thrive, and reach their full potential which truly changes lives. Qualifications: High School diploma/GED plus 6 months of experience working in the care of children required. Candidate must pass state abuse registry checks and drug screening, submit to a TB skin test, and have required immunizations or provide proof of immunizations. Additional education, including CCOT, CDA, AA, or a Bachelor\u2019s degree in Early Childhood Education, Child Development, or a related field. Additional Information: Responsibilities: Provides quality direct patient care for a group of young children, including serving mealtimes, assisting with feeding, diapering, and dressing. Providing developmentally appropriate behavioral guidance within daily scheduled activities. Follow the direction of the ECDS to provide individualized developmental services in their assigned treatment rooms in a manner that is child-centered, family-focused, and demonstrates evidence-based or best practice. Establishes exciting learning environments for young children and applies the curriculum to address the objectives contained in each child\u2019s treatment plan. Perform other duties as assigned.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Feeling, Hearing Frequent Physical Activity: \u00a0Crawling, Crouching, Kneeling, Lifting, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Standing, Stooping, Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: \u00a0Sitting Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Proof of Veteran Status, Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAM--Monticello-Campus/Associate-Professor_R0080077-1": {"title": "Associate Professor", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-14\nPosted: Posted 21 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Faculty - Tenure/Tenure Track Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Monticello UAM, one of twenty campuses of the University of Arkansas System, is located in southeastern Arkansas in the beautiful timberlands, rich in outdoor recreation activities, and approximately 100 miles south of Little Rock. UAM is a comprehensive, residential and commuter, undergraduate institution also offering selected master\u2019s degree programs. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please submit a request via the OEOC website: \u00a0Applicants are required to submit a request for each position to which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 870-460-1422 . Department: Nursing Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Responsibilities: 1. Collaborate with peers and the SON dean to develop, implement, and evaluate the curriculum. 2. Participate in theoretical and clinical instruction as assigned by the course coordinator (assist in more than one course/program if the need arises). 3. Participate in the team teaching approach as assigned by the course coordinator. 4. Participate in academic advising and counseling. 5. Maintain security and confidentiality of all records and exams and submit test items to the course coordinator at least two weeks before the test date. 6. Attend and participate in meetings as scheduled by the course coordinator. 7. Adhere to course objectives and program outcomes in developing appropriate class content and objectives. 8. Participate in the faculty, student, and program evaluation process. 9. Use appropriate current instructional resources to facilitate student progress toward meeting objectives. 10. Maintain appropriate records regarding student evaluation and progress. 11. Maintain office hours for student consultation (at least 10 hours per week). 12. Select appropriate clients for students\u2019 clinical experiences. Utilize the appropriate form for posting assignments. 13. Assist in the development of standards for the admission, progression, and graduation of nursing students. 14. Serve as a professional role model for students. 15. Participate in the activities of the total faculty in ways that benefit the University, the SON, the faculty, and students. 16. Develop effective working relationships within the SON, the University, and the community. 17. Participate in professional and community activities to bring education, service, and research findings together for the improvement of health care. 18. Submit goals and objectives including plans for faculty development, to the SON dean by September 1 of each calendar year. Relate achievement of goals and objectives to annual self- evaluation. 19. Furnish evidence of TB skin test, Faculty Statement of TB skin Test or chest x-ray annually, CPR certification biannually and an unencumbered Arkansas or compact agreement state RN license on renewal. 20. Update curriculum vitae by December 1 of each calendar year and submit to SON dean. 21. Consistently participate in scholarly, professional renewal, and service activities as outlined in this handbook. 22. Maintain a copy of all prepared lecture materials in an agreed upon electronic or secure place. 23. Promote the goals, objectives and reputation of the SON within the SON, University, and community. 24. Participate in continuing education programs to remain professionally updated and proficient. 25. Promote cohesiveness between faculty and students and with the SON faculty and staff. 26. Participate in recruitment and retention of students in the SON. Qualifications: Master's degree or higher with a major in nursing and teaching experience. Current unencumbered licensure as a Registered Nurse in Arkansas or compact agreement state. Additional Information: Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience. Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Amanda Smith, MSN, RN 870-460-1669 smithak@uamont.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry, Substance Abuse Testing The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAM--Monticello-Campus/Assistant-Professor-of-Nursing_R0084689-1": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Nursing", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-14\nPosted: Posted 21 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Faculty - Tenure/Tenure Track Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Monticello UAM, one of twenty campuses of the University of Arkansas System, is located in southeastern Arkansas in the beautiful timberlands, rich in outdoor recreation activities, and approximately 100 miles south of Little Rock. UAM is a comprehensive, residential and commuter, undergraduate institution also offering selected master\u2019s degree programs. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please submit a request via the OEOC website: \u00a0Applicants are required to submit a request for each position to which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 870-460-1422 . Department: Nursing Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Assistant Professor of Nursing accepts the responsibility of maintaining high standards of quality nursing education. The faculty member is a member of university faculty at large, with all rights, freedoms, privileges, and responsibilities of every other faculty member. Nursing faculty members are responsible for adhering to the regulation in the UAM Faculty Handbook and the School of Nursing Faculty Handbook. Instructions include didactic and clinical components. Responsibilities include collaboration with peers to develop, implement, and evaluation curriculum; participate in academic advising; maintain security and confidentiality of all records and exams; attending meetings as scheduled; participate in student and peer evaluations; maintain appropriate student records; maintain office hours consistent with university policy; serve as a professional role model for students; participate in scholarly activities; promote goal, objectives, and reputation of the SON, University, and community; and other duties as assigned by the School of Nursing Dean. Qualifications: Masters degree required; major in nursing and teaching experience preferred; Applicants enrolled in a master's program may be considered. Current unencumbered licensure as a Registered Nurse in Arkansas or compact agreement state. A background check and drug screen are required. Additional Information: Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Curriculum Vitae, License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Amanda Smith, School of Nursing Dean smithak@uamont.edu 870-460-1069 All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry, Substance Abuse Testing The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Clinical-Services-Manager---Central-Arkansas-Primary-Care-Clinics_R0085277-1": {"title": "Clinical Services Manager - Central Arkansas Primary Care Clinics", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-14\nPosted: Posted 21 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/14/2026 Type of Position: Clinical Staff - Medical Services Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | PCPHSL | Primary Care Clinics #1 Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: This position is for Central Arkansas Outpatient Primary Care Clinics (M-F). The Clinical Services Manager (CSM) plays a vital role in the UAMS Family Medical Clinics above. Their primary responsibility is to oversee the daily operations of the nursing department and ensure that all essential functions are running smoothly. This includes staffing, development, budgeting, patient satisfaction, professional growth, and quality outcomes. The CSM will also collaborate with the Medical Director, Residency Director, physicians, and leadership within the organization to ensure that quality patient care and exceptional customer service are delivered while adhering to regulations and requirements set by UAMS, insurance companies, government agencies, and internal goals/strategies. Clinical Service Managers (CSMs) are responsible for implementing the organizational vision, mission, philosophy, core values, evidence-based practices, and standards, as well as nursing support services in their areas of responsibility. The CSM practices in accordance with the scope and standards of practice of the UAMS, the American Nurses Association, and the Nursing Social Policy Statement. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor of Science in Nursing (BSN) degree\u00a0 Five (5) or more years of clinical experience in the field of Nursing At least three (3) years of experience in a leadership capacity Current Registered Nurse License in the State of Arkansas.\u00a0 Current BLS certification or must successfully obtain certification within the first 30 days of employment. \u200b Preferred Qualifications: Master of Science in Nursing (MSN) degree Two Years of Pediatric Experience Ambulatory clinic experience National Nursing Certification Knowledge, Skills & Abilities: Strong organizational and leadership skills Excellent communication and interpersonal skills Ability to adapt to changing priorities and handle multiple tasks simultaneously Knowledge of healthcare regulations and compliance Proficient in using healthcare software and databases Desire to foster a culture of continuous learning and professional development Demonstrates empathy, compassion, and a commitment to delivering quality patient care Additional Information: Responsibilities: Responsible for recruiting, hiring, and onboarding qualified nursing staff for the department. This includes conducting interviews, evaluating candidates, and ensuring proper training and orientation are provided to new hires. Coordinate and monitor the workload of nursing staff to ensure adequate coverage and efficient operations. Contributes to the development of the nursing department by staying updated on industry trends, best practices, and advancements in healthcare. Identify opportunities for improvement and implement strategies to enhance the quality of care provided. This may include conducting training seminars or workshops, implementing new protocols or technologies, and collaborating with other departments for interdisciplinary collaboration. Responsible for developing and managing the nursing department's budget. Collaborate with leadership to identify cost-saving opportunities while maintaining adequate staffing levels and ensuring the highest quality patient care. Continuously monitors patient satisfaction levels and works to address any concerns or issues promptly. Actively engage with patients, their families, and healthcare providers to gather feedback, identify areas of improvement, and implement strategies to enhance the overall patient experience. Fosters a culture of continuous learning and professional development within the nursing department. Mentor and guide individual staff members, conduct performance evaluations, and assist with career advancement opportunities. Promote a culture of teamwork, collaboration, and open communication among nursing staff. Responsible for monitoring and maintaining the highest level of quality in the nursing department. Collaborate with the Medical Director, Residency Director, and other leadership to establish quality metrics, measure performance, and identify areas for improvement. Ensure that nursing practices adhere to UAMS, regulatory, and internal standards, and that patient outcomes are consistently exceptional. Serves as a liaison between the nursing department and other departments within the organization, including the Medical Director, Residency Director, physicians, and leadership. Facilitate effective communication, coordinate efforts, and ensure that nursing department activities are aligned with the overall goals and objectives of the organization. Ensures that all regulations and requirements set by UAMS, insurance companies, government agencies, and internal goals/strategies are adhered to. May perform other duties as assigned. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Letters of Recommendation, Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Criminal Background Check, Substance Abuse Testing This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Feeling, Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Repetitive Motion, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Reaching, Sharps, Standing, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Lifting, N/A, Pulling, Pushing, Sitting Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/RN---TOSH-OR_R0087141": {"title": "RN - TOSH OR", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-13\nPosted: Posted 22 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/14/2026 Type of Position: Clinical Staff - Nursing Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | MUSL | TOSH Operating Room Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: As individuals dedicated to ensuring the safety and quick recovery of our patients, nurses are integral members of a team dedicated to providing the best care for patients through collaboration, communication and patient safety. As part of the TOSH teams, operating room nurses define their practice through attention to nursing excellence and outstanding patient care, are driven by their expertise, compassion and dedication to evidence-based practice, and operate at a higher level of practice. If you are an RN who has current Operating Room experience, we invite you to consider a career with The Orthopaedic & Spine Hospital (TOSH) at UAMS Health. The Registered Nurse (RN) will provide direct patient care as an RN. This professional nursing role will require the ability to coordinate and triage patient care and to work collaboratively with clinic providers, fellows, and staff. Requires the ability to effectively work with patient referral sources, facilitate appointments, coordinate transitions of care, and provide patient education on complex conditions. The RN will work with the individual patient, their families, and providers of care to develop and implement individual health plans. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor\u2019s degree in Nursing, Associate\u2019s degree in Nursing, Diploma RN, or Master\u2019s degree in Nursing. Must be a graduate of an accredited RN nursing program Valid Registered Nursing License Minimum of 1 year of Registered Nursing experience; Basic computer skills. Excellent communication skills. Strong work ethics and accountability. Preferred Qualifications Current BLS ACLS certification Scrubbing experience Orthopedic experience a plus Additional Information: Responsibilities: Collects and documents assessment data from patients and/or others per UAMS standard.\u00a0 Develops patient's Plan of Care (POC) per department/unit standards utilizing assessment data.\u00a0 Evaluates patients' progress toward the attainment of desired outcomes. Administers medication following department/unit standards and Nurse Practice Act.\u00a0 Verifies and evaluates care delivered to ensure it is consistent with patient and family-centered care principles, practice standards, and regulatory requirements. Supports the integration of current evidence into nursing practices.\u00a0 Promotes an environment conducive to positive educational experience for all students and staff.\u00a0 Provides effective patient/family education/discharge planning. Effectively collaborates and communicates with nursing staff at all levels, interdisciplinary teams, executive leaders, and other stakeholders.\u00a0 Communicates care appropriately through medical record documentation. Reports variances in care/ systems/ processes through the appropriate means.\u00a0 Participates in staff recruitment and retention.\u00a0 Facilitates the development and implementation of nursing practice standards that are evidence-based and in compliance with ANA standards. May perform other duties as assigned. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry, Substance Abuse Testing This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding Frequent Physical Activity: Balancing, Feeling, Grasping, Lifting, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Repetitive Motion, Sharps, Standing, Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Climbing, Crawling, Crouching, Kneeling, Sitting, Stooping Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAMS/Clinic-Assistant-Instructor_R0086713-1": {"title": "Clinic Assistant Instructor", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-13\nPosted: Posted 22 Days Ago\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/19/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: CON | Baccalaureate Education Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Positions located in Central Arkansas and Northwest Arkansas The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) College of Nursing (CON) is seeking a dedicated and experienced Clinic Instructor to provide teaching support for the Fall semester. The Clinic Instructor will deliver course content, engage students in meaningful learning experiences, and support academic instruction as assigned by the department. Responsibilities may include classroom, laboratory, simulation, and/or clinical teaching, student evaluation, and collaboration with faculty to support program objectives. The Clinic Instructor will contribute to the educational mission of the department by promoting student success and maintaining excellence in teaching and professional practice. Qualifications: \u00a0Ba chelor of Science in Nursing (BSN) \u00a0 Additional Information: Responsibilities: Deliver assigned course content for the fall semester in alignment with curriculum standards \u00a0 Prepare and present lectures, instructional materials, and learning activities \u00a0 Facilitate classroom and/or clinical instruction as applicable \u00a0 Evaluate student performance and provide\u00a0 timely \u00a0feedback \u00a0 Maintain\u00a0 accurate \u00a0records of attendance, grades, and student progress \u00a0 Support student engagement and promote a positive learning environment \u00a0 Collaborate with faculty and department leadership on course delivery \u00a0 Adhere to university policies, procedures, and academic standards \u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: \u00a0 Hearing, Standing, Talking \u00a0 Frequent Physical Activity: \u00a0 Feeling, Sitting, Walking \u00a0 Occasional Physical Activity: \u00a0 Driving, Pulling, Pushing \u00a0 \u00a0 Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Curriculum Vitae, Resume, Writing Sample Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Computer-Tomography-Technologist_R0089880-1": {"title": "Computer Tomography Technologist", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-13\nPosted: Posted 22 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/13/2026 Type of Position: Clinical Staff - Medical Ancillary Support Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Evening Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | IGSL Computed Tomography IOP C Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The CT technologist will be responsible for providing quality diagnostic imaging for medical interpretation. Duties will include: operating CT equipment, handling patients, venipuncture, post-processing of images, patient transport, working with electronic medical records, and communication with physicians and other services. This position also includes call and holidays. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: HS diploma/GED PLUS Graduate of an approved Radiology program; New graduate or less than one (1) year of experience; Registry eligible - or registered - by the American Registry of Radiologic Technologist; ART license must be obtained prior to start date and CT Advanced Certification obtained within 12 months of hire; Ability to follow oral instructions, read, and write Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor\u2019s Degree in Radiological Sciences One (1) year of CT experience Advanced Registry by the American Registry of Radiologic Technologists in Computed Tomography Additional Information: Responsiblities: Executes imaging exams and manage exam data, including documenting contrast administrations and line placement/removal and verifying images are available for dictation. Provides patient care, including coordination of patient preparation and scans. Communicates with patients and their physicians about exam information and results. May assist in managing staff scheduling. Performs other duties as assigned. Salary Information: Required Documents to Apply: Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Criminal Background Check, Substance Abuse Testing This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Feeling, Grasping, Hearing, Lifting, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Repetitive Motion, Sharps, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Feeling, Grasping, Hearing, Kneeling, Lifting, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Repetitive Motion, Sharps, Sitting, Standing, Stooping, Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Crouching Benefits Eligible:"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Parent-Support-Mentor--Pulaski-County--HEI-Program-Coordinator_R0089783": {"title": "Parent Support Mentor (Pulaski County)-HEI Program Coordinator", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-13\nPosted: Posted 22 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Clerical Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Little Rock The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is a metropolitan research university that provides an accessible, quality education through flexible learning and unparalleled internship opportunities. At UA Little Rock, we prepare our more than 8,900 students to be innovators and responsible leaders in their fields. Committed to its metropolitan research university mission, UA Little Rock is a driving force in Little Rock's thriving cultural community and a major component of the city and state's growing profile as a regional leader in research, technology transfer, economic development, and job creation. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . Department: MidSOUTH Department's Website: midsouth.ualr.edu Summary of Job Duties: The Parent Support Mentor is a grant-funded position. This position is located in Pulaski County. The Parent Support Mentor provides training activities and will be a part of a larger team within the county Women Infants & Children (WIC) office. This position will communicate with the grantor and community partners, assist with building training capacity, and collect data for program evaluation. This position is governed by state and federal laws and agency/institution policy. Qualifications: Required Education and/or Experience: High School Diploma or equivalent and (other job-related experience and education may be substituted for all or parts of these basic requirements); \u200b Preferred Experience: Bachelor's degree; plus one (1) year of specialized training in business management, business education, or a related field.\u200b Job Duties and Responsibilities: Administrative Coordination: Research and analyze data pertinent to work programs and/or agency/institution goals and objectives and prepare reports explaining findings and recommendations; Assists clients in obtaining pertinent information outlined by the program related to their particular needs and how to fulfill those needs; Teaches and demonstrates health behavior skills to clients; Provide informal education and social skills supports for clients based on identified needs and provide formal educational information based on the Baby and Me curriculum; Coordinate communication between community groups, local health unit supervisor, and program supervisor to ensure everyone receives timely updates of program and/or client changes; Assist in developing or revising policies, procedures, and directives based on research findings and submit to supervisor for approval; Compile program-related information used by the supervisor to formulate budget proposals to determine resources needed and respond to participant correspondence in a timely manner; Review and answer or prepare correspondence relating to agency/institution programs; Interpret agency administrative directives, policies, and procedures to ensure consistent application; Provide information, assistance, and clarifications to interested parties concerning agency/institution programs, policies, and procedures; Recordkeeping : Assist supervisor by maintaining leave records, appointment calendar, and prioritizing incoming correspondence; Travel to other local health units as needed to provide community outreach services; Maintain timely and accurate data in the database using new RedCap software; Submit a weekly work log of day-to-day client activities to Baby and Me Coordinator. Perform related responsibilities as required and assigned. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Knowledge of the principles and practices of mathematics and statistics; Knowledge of the work-related subject areas; Knowledge in family health and child development; Knowledge of computers and software applications; Ability to prepare, present, and review oral and written information and reports; Ability to work as a part of a team; Ability to research and analyze related work program information; Strong interpersonal and organizational skills; Ability to analyze financial records and prepare reports; Ability to develop, recommend, interpret, and apply policies and procedures; Ability to plan, organize, and direct the work of others; Must have good communication skills; Ability to travel occasionally, as needed; Ability to work a flexible schedule; Ability to work independently. Additional Information: Salary Information: $36,000 Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume, Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Mary Tillman, Administrative Support Manager, mjtillman@midsouth.ualr.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Child Maltreatment, Criminal Background Check, Motor Vehicle Reports Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Lifting, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Repetitive Motion, Sitting, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Lifting, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting, Talking Occasional Physical Activity: Driving, Kneeling, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Repetitive Motion Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Jonesboro/APRN-PA--ENT-Clinic--Jonesboro--AR-_R0089806-1": {"title": "APRN/PA- ENT Clinic (Jonesboro, AR)", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-12\nPosted: Posted 23 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 10/03/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | SUSL ENT Mid Level Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: We are currently seeking a qualified provider to join our patient-centered care team as an Advanced Practice Nurse/Physician Assistant (APRN/PA) at the University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS). In this role, you will support the operations at the Jonesboro Family Medical Center (FMC) by serving as a key clinical extension. Your responsibilities will include managing clinic workflows efficiently, coordinating complex visit schedules, and performing ENT procedures with accuracy. You will independently handle patient evaluations in collaboration with supervising physicians to ensure seamless, high-quality outpatient care. The APRN/PA will conduct clinical assessments, assist with care coordination, respond to messages via MyChart and in-basket, address patient inquiries, and manage prescriptions. In the outpatient setting, duties include evaluating new and follow-up patients, reviewing pathology and imaging results, and providing comprehensive patient education and follow-up planning. The ideal candidate will possess advanced clinical expertise to accurately assess, diagnose, and treat patient issues. Additionally, the APRN/PA will serve as a primary communicator between the care team and patients, ensuring timely and accurate information exchange. We invite motivated and skilled APRN/PAs who are passionate about ENT care and committed to excellence in patient service to consider this opportunity. If you thrive in a collaborative environment and are dedicated to delivering exceptional care, we encourage you to apply and become a valued member of our ENT team at UAMS Jonesboro FMC. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: APRN Master\u2019s Degree in Nursing Three (3) years of nursing experience Licensed Registered Nurse in Arkansas APRN License Minimum Qualifications:\u00a0 PA Master's Education PA Licensure Outpatient expectations\u00a0 See and evaluate postoperative and established patients for medication management of common ear, nose, and throat in conjunction with otolaryngologists.\u00a0 Perform otomicroscopy with cerumen removal, flexible fiberoptic laryngoscopy, videostroboscopy, nasal endoscopy, and sinus debridement with supervision of a physician. Perform skin and soft tissue biopsies of the mouth and throat with assistance of a physician. Additional Information: Key Responsibilities: Coordinates specialized, multidisciplinary care and facilitates consults of patients to ensure timely and appropriate treatment. Provides comprehensive health assessments, determines diagnoses, implements treatment plans, prescribes medical treatments, and manages health issues for patients in collaboration with the designated physician. Collaborates with a variety of health care professionals to diagnose and manage patients' health care problems, serving as a resource, interdisciplinary consultant, and patient advocate. Manages post procedure immunosuppression and labs of the patient in coordination with the physician and pharmacist. Participates in institutional initiatives and encourages the participation of others. Collaborates in policy and program development, implementation, and evaluation using best practices in delivering quality service. Edits and documents results in various critical care systems May undertake additional duties as assigned to support the clinical mission.. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), Resume Optional Documents: Curriculum Vitae, Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Morrilton/Community---Campus-Events-Coordinator_R0089861": {"title": "Community & Campus Events Coordinator", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-12\nPosted: Posted 23 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Staff - Press, Journalism Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas Community College at Morrilton The University of Arkansas Community College at Morrilton (UACCM) is a proud member of the University of Arkansas System.\u00a0 The University of Arkansas System is comprised of land-grant research institutions, a teaching hospital, five community colleges, two schools of law, a presidential school, a residential math and science high school, and an online university, as well as divisions of agriculture, archaeology and criminal justice. These entities exhibit unmatched economic and social impact across the state by providing numerous academic and professional opportunities. Below you will find the details for the position currently available at UACCM including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.\u00a0 To apply for the position, please click the Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please submit a request via Email to: UACCMHRDept@uaccm.edu or by phone at (501) 208-5309 or (501) 977-2016.\u00a0\u00a0 Applicants are required to submit a separate request for each position in which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at UACCMHRDept@uaccm.edu or by phone at (501) 208-5309 or (501) 977-2016. Department: Associate Director of Marketing and Public Relations Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Community and Campus Events Coordinator reports to the Assistant Director of Marketing & Public Relations. JOB DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES INCLUDE: Coordinate community education and non-credit courses, which may include Kids College, Seniors Institute, and non-credit self-improvement, and general interest courses, seminars, and workshops. Coordinate and may facilitate non-credit classes and camps, which will include designing class plans, hiring and supervising instructors, overseeing registrations, completing work orders, and developing payment process. Coordinator will assist with promoting and recruiting participants. Coordinate reservations for the Workforce Training Center Tyson Hall, the Fine Arts Auditorium, and other reservable facilities on campus. The coordinator serves as a college liaison/representative at events, productions, and presentations from outside organizations. Provide event management for internal and external campus events such as meetings, specialty classes, and workshops, including reservation of rooms, staffing, and technology infrastructure support. The coordinator will oversee operation of the college\u2019s audio and visual technology for college-related special events and productions, as well as presentations from outside businesses and organizations. This requires working knowledge of audio and visual technology, including projector, laptop computer, stage lights, and sound booth, including microphone system, DVD and CD players, etc. As needed, assist with photo shoots including assembling equipment, coordinating the photo release paperwork, and helping to set up lighting. Assist with college and Foundation special events and other special campus projects. Serve as a point of contact with secondary schools, businesses and industry, and other organizations for correspondence about UACCM\u2019s potential partnerships, ad sponsorships, and event assistance to discuss details and logistics. Other duties as assigned. Qualifications: MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS \u00a0 Associate\u2019s degree \u00a0 A minimum of one year of work experience in related field or in event management with similar required duties \u00a0 Other job-related education and/or experience may be substituted for all or part of the minimum qualifications upon approval of the Chancellor. \u00a0 APPLICATION REQUIREMENTS: \u00a0 Cover Letter \u00a0 Resume \u00a0 List of three professional references \u00a0 Copies of college transcripts, related licensure, certification \u00a0 Additional Information: \u00a0 KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, AND ABILITIES \u00a0 Excellent Microsoft Office computer skills; proficient with Word and Excel \u00a0 Aptitude for quickly learning modern technology or knowledge of audio and visual technology \u00a0 Work collaboratively and cooperatively with all levels of staff, faculty, donors, and visitors\u00a0 \u00a0 Accountable for accurate , detailed meeting records; timely documentation\u00a0 \u00a0 Demonstrated ability to plan, prioritize and execute multiple tasks on an on-going basis\u00a0 \u00a0 Organized, detail-oriented, and reliable \u00a0 Ambassador for the Colleg e ; exercises professional judgment, behavior, and actions\u00a0 \u00a0 Experience using data management software\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0 Excellent written and verbal communication \u00a0 Excel in relationship-building skills, customer service and problem solving\u00a0 \u00a0 Independent self-starter that performs effectively and accurately with minimal amount of supervision \u00a0 All employees at UACCM must have a commitment to work cooperatively with all campus personnel to fulfill the Mission of UACCM and deliver quality customer services. \u00a0 Salary Information: $33,000 - $37,500 commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume, Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Shelby Beck HR Analyst 501-208-5309 All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Child Maltreatment, Criminal Background Check, Motor Vehicle Reports Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas Community College at Morrilton (UACCM) is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check, sex offender registry check, and drug screen. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check and/or a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check.\u00a0 A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Sitting, Standing, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Driving, Lifting, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Repetitive Motion, Stooping, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Crouching, Feeling, Grasping, Kneeling, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-Arkansas-Community-College-at-Batesville/Extra-Help-Student-Success-Center-Tutor_R0089668-1": {"title": "Extra Help-Student Success Center Tutor", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-12\nPosted: Posted 23 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. Closing Date: Type of Position: Clerical Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Less than Annual Appointment (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas Community College at Batesville The University of Arkansas Community College at Batesville (UACCB) is a comprehensive community college committed to providing learning experiences that improve the lives of those we serve. UACCB provides affordable access to technical education and college transfer programs that meet the diverse higher education needs of the citizens of north central Arkansas. \u00a0 These programs are provided to the traditional college student as well as to high school students through a state approved Secondary Area Career Center. \u00a0 The College also promotes economic development and an enhanced quality of life for the community through adult education, developmental education, customized business and industry training, and continuing education programs. UACCB's mission is to provide quality educational opportunities within a supportive learning environment. We promote success through community partnerships, responsive programs, and an enduring commitment to improvement. Thank you for your interest. \u00a0 We hope you will be joining us soon! After reviewing the Job Duties and Qualifications listed below, click the Apply button at the top of the page to begin the application process. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process or for general application assistance, please contact the Human Resource Office at (870) 612-2045. Department: Dir Student Success Ctr Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Basic Functions The Student Success Center Tutor provides comprehensive academic support to students through structured individual and small group tutoring in assigned subject areas. The tutor facilitates student learning by reinforcing course content, promoting effective study strategies, and fostering academic self-efficacy while encouraging independent learning and appropriate utilization of institutional resources. The role supports the broader mission of student persistence, retention, and completion. Caring Campus Responsibilities: As a member of the UACCB community, each employee is responsible for advancing the Caring Campus culture to enhance student connection and success and to embody the campus purpose: Improve Lives. Key duties include adhering to the campus name badge policy, treating all visitors as guests, engaging with the campus community by reviewing institutional communications, participating in campus events, and supporting a collaborative, positive workplace environment. Position Duties 25% - Direct Academic Tutoring and Instruction Provide individualized and group-based tutoring aligned with course curricula, learning outcomes, and faculty expectations. Assist students in clarifying concepts, practicing skills, and applying knowledge within assigned disciplines while maintaining a student-centered, developmental approach. 25% - Academic Skill Development and Learning Strategies Support students in developing transferable academic skills, including study strategies, time management, note-taking, test preparation, and problem-solving techniques. Reinforce learning behaviors that promote long-term academic success rather than task completion alone. 25% - Faculty and Staff Collaboration and Student Outreach Collaborate with faculty, advisors, and Student Success Center staff to support student learning through outreach initiatives, referrals, classroom support efforts, and indirect academic assistance. Communication trends, common challenges, and resource needs to appropriate personnel to enhance student support services. 25% - Professional Engagement and Program Support Participate in required training, meetings, assessment activities, and professional development. Contribute to a welcoming and inclusive learning environment that reflects the mission and values of the Student Success Center. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Knowledge Foundational knowledge of assigned academic subject areas Understanding of basic tutoring strategies and learning support practices Familiarity with college-level academic expectations and student support services Awareness of FERPA and student confidentiality standards Skills Ability to explain complex concepts in clear, accessible ways Organizational and time management skills Basic computer and technology skills, including scheduling or reporting platforms Strong interpersonal and communication with diverse audiences. Abilities Build and maintain strong relationships with faculty, staff, and students. Work effectively with others from diverse academic, cultural, and socioeconomic backgrounds Adapt tutoring approaches to different learning styles Maintain professionalism, reliability, and ethical standards Work independently and collaboratively within a team environment Qualifications: Qualifications \u00a0 High school diploma or equivalent\u00a0 \u00a0 Successful completion of coursework in the tutoring subject area with strong academic performance or equivalent accomplishment \u00a0 Eligibility for employment under institutional hiring guidelines \u00a0 Availability to work scheduled tutoring hours, including peak academic periods. \u00a0 \u00a0 Preferred Qualifications \u00a0 Associates degree from a regionally accredited institution \u00a0 Coursework or training in education or student development \u00a0 Familiarity with andragogy \u00a0 Experience working in a community college or student support environment \u00a0 Additional Information: Salary Information: $11.00/Hr Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume, Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Human Resources hr@uaccb.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry UACCB is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check for all applicants.\u00a0 Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Standing, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Lifting, Reaching Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Fiscal-Support-Analyst_R0089351": {"title": "Fiscal Support Analyst", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-12\nPosted: Posted 23 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Accounting, Finance, Business Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Little Rock The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is a metropolitan research university that provides an accessible, quality education through flexible learning and unparalleled internship opportunities. At UA Little Rock, we prepare our more than 8,900 students to be innovators and responsible leaders in their fields. Committed to its metropolitan research university mission, UA Little Rock is a driving force in Little Rock's thriving cultural community and a major component of the city and state's growing profile as a regional leader in research, technology transfer, economic development, and job creation. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . Department: Accounts Payable Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Fiscal Support Analyst reports to the Accounts Payable Manager. This position is responsible for accurately and promptly handling accounts payable processes. This role requires strong attention to detail, effective communication, and good customer service skills. This position adheres to Generally Accepted Accounting Principles, as well as state and federal laws, and institutional policies. Qualifications: Required Education and/or Experience Bachelor's Degree in Accounting, General Business, Finance, or Business Administration plus at least 2 years of experience in accounts payable, accounting, finance, or procurement with a demonstrated understanding of accounts payable processes. OR Associate's Degree plus at least 3 years experience in accounts payable, accounting, finance, or procurement with a demonstrated understanding of accounts payable processes. Job Duties and Responsibilities Process authorized documents, invoices, inter-company and ad hoc payments; Follow-up on pending items delaying the payment process; Review statements and contact suppliers for invoices needed; Resolve billing issues; Communicate with campus personnel and suppliers regarding Accounts Payable issues; Settle direct deposit and check payments; Monitor and record the issuance of cash advance payments; Resolve stale-dated checks to prepare the unclaimed liability report; Complete departmental check deposits; Assist with processing positive pay exceptions; Assist with processing wire transfer payments; Provide individual training to department personnel; Monitor the Supplier Return Check log to research and provide information related to returned checks; Manage and process utility and copier contract payments; Assist with the annual 1099 process; Perform other duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Knowledge of computers and software applications including\u00a0ERS; Knowledge of work-related subject areas; Possess the skills to manage multiple projects simultaneously; Possess strong organizational and prioritization skills to complete tasks efficiently and effectively; Ability to utilize Software of ERS system and MSOffice software; Ability to problem solve billing problems; Ability to communicate effectively with campus personnel and suppliers; Ability to communicate with a diverse group of people; Ability to work as a team to achieve shared goals; Ability to follow directions; Ability to complete tasks efficiently; Ability to demonstrate a working knowledge of basic mathematics; Ability to research and analyze related work program information; Demonstrate ability to adjust to and manage change; Exhibit a cooperative and approachable attitude and demeanor. Additional Information: Salary Information: $45,000.00 Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Dr. Vanessa Whitman, Accounts Payable Manager, (501) 916-5743 All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Financial Credit Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding Frequent Physical Activity: Hearing, Sitting, Talking Occasional Physical Activity: Pushing, Reaching, Standing Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/APRN-PA---Peds-Ortho_R0080476-1": {"title": "APRN/PA - Peds Ortho", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-12\nPosted: Posted 23 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/12/2026 Type of Position: Clinical Staff - Nursing Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: COM | Orthopaedics Surgery Bumpass group Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The APRN/PA will be located at ACH in Little Rock, AR, and will assist Orthopaedic Spine physicians with clinic, organizing visits and performing clinic procedures, assist in the operating room, answer pages, and round on inpatients as needed. The APRN/PA will augment a physician's ability to provide medical services to patients; collect and document data, conduct diagnostic and therapeutic procedures, order and schedule laboratory studies and professional consultations, and provide direct patient care services. Will be included in the Orthopaedic after-hours call rotation. Call for urgent and/or emergent treatment of orthopedic conditions is expected and a requirement of the position. This includes the reduction of fractures and other similar orthopedic procedures that can be done in the emergency department. Qualifications: APRN: Graduate from an accredited nursing program with at least a Master\u2019s in Nursing. National Certification as an Advanced Practice Registered Nurse. Certification as a Pediatric Nurse Practitioner in acute care. PA: Graduate from an accredited physician assistant program or eligible as defined by the Arkansas State Medical Board. Current Arkansas Physician Assistant license or eligible for licensure. \u00a0 Preferred Qualifications : Basic Life Support (BLS). Pediatric Advanced Life Support (PALS). Responsibilities: Obtains a relevant health and medical history, performs a physician examination, both focused and comprehensive, depending on patient needs, identifies health risks and needs, updates and records changes in health status, and assesses mental and functional status. Formulates an appropriate differential diagnosis based on history, physical exam, and clinical findings, and identifies the needs of the individual and family as a result of the patient interview (history) and physical exam. Will be included in the Orthopaedic after-hours call rotation. Provides an acceptable plan of care that maximizes the patient\u2019s health potential and takes into account: ordering of appropriate diagnostic tests, identifying and prescribing appropriate pharmacologic agents when needed, and identifying and planning non-pharmacologic interventions when appropriate, and develops a plan for education of the patient and their family or caregiver. Consults with physicians and other health professionals when needed. Plans are based on established priorities and include: accurately conducting and interpreting diagnostic tests, prescribing pharmacologic agents under prescriptive protocols, providing relevant and timely patient and caregiver education, and making appropriate referrals to other health professionals. Follows up on the client by phone calls, rounds, scheduled visits, and lab results. Facilitates patient participation and self-care when able, and provides information to patients and families in order for them to make decisions and choices about their health care. Promotes optimal health of the patient by including preventive and health promotion activities into the plan of care, participates in clinical pathway development and quality management activities. Participates as a team member in patient care conferences with other health disciplines and uses a team approach to the provision of care. Participates in clinical case conferences and other department and campus meetings as appropriate. Responsible for appropriate documentation and billing notations for care that is given. Perform diagnostic and therapeutic procedures to assist the physician in diagnosing medical and surgical problems and prescribing necessary treatment and services for quality patient care. Record the normal and abnormal data for review by the physician. Take patient histories, conduct physical examinations, and record the data in the patient's record. Write progress notes and narrative discharge summaries. Prepare patient workups and summaries, noting pertinent positive and negative findings. Order and schedule laboratory studies and diagnostic procedures; explain the necessity, preparation, nature, and anticipated effects of scheduled diagnostic and therapeutic procedures to the patient. Carry out therapeutic procedures such as cast application and removal, wound suturing and dressing changes; monitor progress of patients, report progress to supervising physician, and maintain record of each patient's progress. Participate in basic science and clinical research projects conducted by the supervising physician; prepare statistical reports and analyses setting forth. Perform other duties as assigned. Additional Information: Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Substance Abuse Testing This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAPBMCMain-Campus/High-School-Concurrent-Instructor-1_R0089812": {"title": "High School Concurrent Instructor-1", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-12\nPosted: Posted 23 Days Ago\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Contingent Worker Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Volunteer Faculty Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff The University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff is an 1890 Land-Grant HBCU with a diverse student population, competitive degree offerings and stellar faculty. For more than 140 years, the University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff has worked to create an environment that inculcates learning, growth and productivity while affording a basic need to its students \u2013 a chance to advance. The 15:1 student to teacher ratio makes it possible to maintain a learning environment with close interaction between students and faculty while challenging curricula encourage our students to seek and fulfill their potential. You can excel in your chosen field of study through a curriculum of \u00a0 Certificate and Associates degree programs,\u00a0 more than thirty\u00a0 Undergraduate programs, Master\u2019s degree programs and a Doctorate program in Aquaculture/Fisheries. You can also develop workplace readiness through internships, co-ops and fellowships in the U.S. and abroad. Out-of-class experiences and student involvement include more than 90 student organizations, an internationally renowned Vesper Choir, Marching Band, Concert Bands, Wind Symphony, nationally recognized debate team, award-winning theater department and accomplished athletic program. Though the main campus is in Pine Bluff, its reach is worldwide. UAPB has an extended campus in North Little Rock and offers as well as online courses. With the addition of the Arkansas Research and Education Optical Network (ARE-ON), students can engage in information exchange with others anywhere in the world. There are also Research and Extension offices in Lonoke, Newport and Lake Village and collaborations with other colleges and universities in the State through the National Science Foundation funded STEM (Science, Technology, Engineering and Mathematics) Academy. As the second oldest land-grant institution in the state of Arkansas, the mission of this No Excuse University remains the same \u2013 to provide a high quality, affordable education with a personal touch. We invite you to Become a Part of the Pride at the University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process and require reasonable accommodations, please contact Human Resources at 870.575.8400 . Department: Graduate Education and Continuing Studies | Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Teach concurrent high school classes in their high school Qualifications: Master's degree with 18 graduate level credit hours in the discipline or alternative certifications approved by the Arkansas Department of Higher Education Additional Information: This position is only open to current high school teachers teaching concurrent classes in school districts that have an agreement with UAPB to offer concurrent classes. Salary Information: Required Documents to Apply: Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants (Please upload all required documents in the \"Resume\" attachment section of your application to be considered for this position) : Recruitment Contact Information: All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Child Maltreatment, Criminal Background Check The University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff may conduct pre-employment background checks on certain positions for applicants being considered for employment. \u00a0 The background checks may include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. \u00a0 Required checks are identified in the position listing. \u00a0 A criminal background check or arrest pending adjudication information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absences of a relationship to the requirements of the position. \u00a0 Background check information will be used in a consistent, non-discriminatory manner consistent with the state and federal law. \u00a0 The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting, Standing, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting, Standing, Talking Occasional Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding Benefits Eligible:"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Director-of-Advancement-Services_R0089751-1": {"title": "Director of Advancement Services", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-11\nPosted: Posted 24 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Senior Professional Staff - Advancement Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Little Rock The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is a metropolitan research university that provides an accessible, quality education through flexible learning and unparalleled internship opportunities. At UA Little Rock, we prepare our more than 8,900 students to be innovators and responsible leaders in their fields. Committed to its metropolitan research university mission, UA Little Rock is a driving force in Little Rock's thriving cultural community and a major component of the city and state's growing profile as a regional leader in research, technology transfer, economic development, and job creation. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . Department: Development Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: As the University's fundraising continues to grow through record levels of donors, gifts, and endowment growth, the Director of Advancement Services provides operational leadership that ensures the University's advancement infrastructure continues to evolve to meet increasing organizational complexity and opportunity. The Director leads the daily operations of Advancement Services while continuously improving business processes, technology, data governance, financial stewardship, and customer service that support fundraising success. Working closely with the Associate Vice Chancellor of Advancement Services, the Director provides day-to-day operational leadership for Advancement Services while ensuring the division maintains the organizational capacity, continuity, and operational resilience necessary to support the University's fundraising mission. Through effective leadership, staff development, comprehensive documentation, sustainable business practices, and continuous process improvement, the Director ensures Advancement Services delivers exceptional service, adapts to changing organizational needs, and remains resilient through leadership transitions, personnel changes, and institutional growth. This operational leadership enables senior leadership to focus on strategic initiatives, development performance, organizational planning, technology advancement, and long-range organizational priorities. The Director continually evaluates Advancement Services operations against emerging technologies, industry best practices, and peer and aspirational institutions to identify opportunities that improve efficiency, strengthen data integrity, increase scalability, and enhance the University's fundraising infrastructure. Through innovation, operational excellence, leadership development, and succession planning, the Director strengthens the systems, people, and processes that sustain a high-performing advancement organization and position the University for continued fundraising success. Success in this position is measured by the Director's ability to execute the strategic vision of Advancement Services while maintaining the highest standards of operational integrity, customer service, collaboration, and continuous improvement. The Director is expected not only to maintain operational excellence, but to make Advancement Services stronger by improving systems, developing people, fostering innovation, and building the organizational capacity, resilience, and operational excellence that advance the University's fundraising mission and position the division for long-term success. This position is governed by state and federal laws, and agency/institution policy. Qualifications: Required Education and/or Experience Bachelor's degree in Business Administration, Finance, Accounting, Information Systems, Management Information Systems, Higher Education Administration, Data Analytics, or a related field; Three (3) years of progressively responsible experience in Advancement Services, business operations, finance, information systems, higher education administration, nonprofit management, or a related field; Experience managing complex operational processes, enterprise systems, financial reconciliation, reporting, or business operations; Demonstrated ability to provide responsive, high-quality service and solutions to internal and external constituents. Preferred Education and/or Experience Master's degree in Business Administration, Higher Education Administration, Information Systems, Public Administration, or a related field; Experience with Affinaquest, Salesforce, or comparable advancement CRM platforms; Experience with reporting and business intelligence tools such as Power BI, Tableau, SQL, SOQL, or comparable reporting technologies; Experience implementing technology solutions, systems integrations, workflow automation, or business process improvements; Experience in higher education advancement, nonprofit fundraising, or a related philanthropic environment; Experience working with Foundation accounting, charitable gift administration, financial reconciliation, donor database management, and regulatory compliance; Demonstrated experience leading operational change, documenting business processes, and supporting organizational growth through technology and process improvement. Job Duties and Responsibilities Leadership & Collaboration Supervise Advancement Services staff by establishing expectations, coordinating workloads, coaching employees, fostering professional growth, and promoting a culture of accountability, collaboration, innovation, customer service, and continuous improvement; Foster a proactive, solutions-oriented service culture by encouraging responsiveness, collaboration, professionalism, and a customer-focused mindset that removes barriers and supports the success of donors, development officers, alumni, and campus partners; Coordinate work across Advancement Services to ensure operational consistency, timely service, and efficient support for fundraising activities; Collaborate closely with the Associate Vice Chancellor to execute approved operational priorities, implement organizational initiatives, and advance the goals of the Office of Alumni and Development; Work collaboratively with development officers, University leadership, the University of Arkansas Foundation, Central Information Technology, Finance and Administration, Communications and Marketing, and other campus partners to ensure Advancement Services effectively supports the University's fundraising mission. Financial Management & Gift Administration Oversee financial reconciliation between the Affinaquest CRM and the University of Arkansas Foundation financial records to ensure the accuracy and integrity of all gift-related transactions; Oversee gift administration processes to ensure gifts are accurately documented, receipted, acknowledged, reconciled, and administered in accordance with donor intent, University policy, and Foundation requirements; Design, monitor, and continuously improve gift processing workflows that provide exceptional donor service while striving to complete the gift process from receipt through posting, acknowledgment, and reconciliation within three business days whenever practical; Assist the Associate Vice Chancellor in developing, monitoring, and managing the Office of Alumni and Development operating budget; Ensure compliance with University policies, University of Arkansas Foundation policies, IRS regulations, PCI standards, and other applicable financial and regulatory requirements; Provide financial guidance, reports, and operational support to development officers, campus partners, University leadership, and the University of Arkansas Foundation. Data Governance & Reporting Evaluate and maintain standards for data governance, documentation, reporting, and data quality to ensure reliable and consistent information across Advancement systems; Evaluate, Design and maintain executive dashboards, reports, analytics, and key performance indicators that support fundraising management, operational planning, and organizational decision-making; Coordinate preparation and submission of the annual Voluntary Support of Education (VSE) Survey and other required institutional reports. Serve as the division lead for PCI compliance and related data security initiatives. Business Operations, Compliance & Continuity Review, maintain, and periodically update Advancement Services policies, procedures, and operational standards while collaborating with the Associate Vice Chancellor to develop new policies and procedures as organizational needs evolve; Ensure Advancement Services business processes remain aligned with University policies, Foundation requirements, industry best practices, and the operational priorities established by the Associate Vice Chancellor; Develop and maintain documentation of Advancement Services business processes, Affinaquest functionality, workflows, reporting procedures, system configurations, financial reconciliation processes, and institutional knowledge. Cross-train staff and maintain succession and continuity plans that reduce single points of failure, preserve institutional knowledge, and support uninterrupted operations; Regularly review documentation and operational procedures to ensure they remain current with evolving technology, policies, regulations, and business practices. Technology, Innovation & Business Systems Serve as the functional business lead for Affinaquest, Salesforce, and related Advancement technologies; Collaborate with the Associate Vice Chancellor, Systems Specialist, Central Information Technology, and software vendors to evaluate, prioritize, and implement technology solutions that support fundraising operations. Operational Leadership & Execution Execute the operational vision, priorities, and initiatives established by the Associate Vice Chancellor of Advancement Services; Manage approved projects from planning through implementation, ensuring initiatives are completed efficiently, effectively, and with measurable results; Build and strengthen the operational infrastructure necessary to support continued growth in fundraising, donor engagement, charitable gifts, and endowment activity while ensuring timely, accurate, and customer-focused service to donors, development officers, alumni, and campus partners; Identify opportunities to improve operational effectiveness through technology, automation, artificial intelligence, business process improvement, and innovation, and present recommendations to the Associate Vice Chancellor for consideration; Coordinate the successful implementation of approved technologies, operational initiatives, and business process improvements that advance the priorities established by the Associate Vice Chancellor; Evaluate existing workflows and recommend practical improvements that increase efficiency, improve customer service, strengthen internal controls, and remove operational barriers for development officers. \u00a0 Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Demonstrated ability to execute strategic priorities through effective operational leadership, project management, and successful implementation of organizational initiatives; Broad knowledge of Advancement Services operations and a comprehensive understanding of how business operations support successful fundraising and donor engagement; Strong understanding of financial management, internal controls, reconciliation processes, gift administration, and donor stewardship; Working knowledge of constituent relationship management (CRM) systems, reporting tools, workflow automation, business process improvement, and data management principles; Ability to perform basic system configuration and troubleshoot routine system issues while collaborating effectively with Information Technology staff on more complex technical requests; Ability to analyze operational challenges, identify practical solutions, and implement improvements that strengthen efficiency, customer service, and organizational effectiveness; Demonstrated ability to document complex business processes, operational procedures, and institutional knowledge to support continuity and succession planning; Ability to communicate technical concepts to non-technical audiences and translate operational needs into clear business requirements; Excellent analytical, organizational, problem-solving, interpersonal, verbal, and written communication skills; Must have a valid driver's license; Ability to manage multiple priorities, meet deadlines, exercise sound judgment, maintain confidentiality, and adapt to changing organizational needs. Additional Information: Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Chris Hamilton, Associate Vice Chancellor of Advancement Services, clhamilton@ualr.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Financial Credit Check, Motor Vehicle Reports Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Repetitive Motion, Sitting, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: Lifting, Pulling, Pushing Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Assistant-Director---Pharmacy-Operations_R0089554-1": {"title": "Assistant Director of Pharmacy and Therapeutics", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-11\nPosted: Posted 24 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/07/2026 Type of Position: Senior Professional Staff - Clinical Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | PTSL OSP/Diversion Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Assistant Director of Pharmacy for P&T and Formulary Management provides strategic leadership and operational oversight for the health system\u2019s Pharmacy and Therapeutics (P&T) Committee and the broader formulary system. This role helps ensure that the medication-use process is safe, evidence-based, and cost-effective. The manager leads the development of pharmacy policies, coordinates medication-use evaluations (MUEs), and supports the implementation of policy and formulary changes. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Graduate of an ACPE-accredited School of Pharmacy with a Bachelor of Science in Pharmacy degree or PharmD, plus 6 years of applicable experience, including 2 years of progressively responsible experience related to pharmacy management (PGY1 and PGY2 residency both equate to 3 years of experience) Licensed Registered Pharmacist by the Arkansas State Board of Pharmacy Advanced proficiency in literature evaluation and biostatistics. Strong project management skills. Excellent written and verbal communication for presenting to medical staff leadership. Knowledge of FOCUS-PDCA or similar quality improvement methodologies. Preferred Qualifications : Doctor of Pharmacy (Pharm.D.) Experience in a large multi-hospital health system or academic medical center Board Certification (e.g., BCPS) Additional Information: Responsibilities: Serve as a core leader on the P&T Committee and related medication stewardship subcommittees, coordinating the development, review, and implementation of medication-use policies and procedures. Serve as the primary coordinator for the P&T Committee, including setting agendas, coordinating the preparation of evidence-based monographs, and ensuring accurate documentation of minutes and decisions. Coordinate the clinical and economic evaluation of new drug entities and therapeutic classes, utilizing a formal grading system to assess the quality of evidence. Manage the formal disclosure process for committee members and requesting practitioners to ensure unbiased decision-making. Oversee the \"living document\" of the formulary, including regular therapeutic class reviews and the management of drug shortages and therapeutic interchanges. Monitor non-formulary medication usage to identify opportunities for formulary improvement and assess internal compliance with medication-use policy. Ensure effective communication of formulary, policy, and medication-use process changes to all stakeholders. Support the development and execution of an annual organization-specific MUE plan focused on high-risk, high-cost, or high-volume medications. Lead interdisciplinary teams in conducting MUEs using performance improvement models such as FOCUS-PDCA to identify variances in care and implement corrective actions. Present MUE findings and recommendations to the P&T Committee, ensuring that data drives clinical policy changes. Draft and review all system-wide medication-use policies. Ensure all medication-use policies and processes comply with The Joint Commission (TJC), CMS, DEA, and state board of pharmacy regulations. Collaborate with nursing and medical leadership to standardize medication administration protocols and clinical practice guidelines across all sites of care. Collaborate with academic institutions to provide robust training and rotation opportunities for pharmacy residents, student interns, and pharmacy technician trainees within the scope of medication-use policy. Support professional development and education efforts for pharmacy department employees related to medication-use process, policy, and professional practice. Other duties as assigned Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Curriculum Vitae, Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Criminal Background Check, Substance Abuse Testing This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Hearing Frequent Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Registered-Nurse_R0088069": {"title": "Registered Nurse", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-11\nPosted: Posted 24 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Professional Staff - Student Affairs Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Little Rock The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is a metropolitan research university that provides an accessible, quality education through flexible learning and unparalleled internship opportunities. At UA Little Rock, we prepare our more than 8,900 students to be innovators and responsible leaders in their fields. Committed to its metropolitan research university mission, UA Little Rock is a driving force in Little Rock's thriving cultural community and a major component of the city and state's growing profile as a regional leader in research, technology transfer, economic development, and job creation. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . Department: Health Services Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: This position provides the services of a Registered Nurse to the operations of UA Little Rock Health Services. This is a full time, benefits eligible position that reports to the Director of Health Services. Clinical practice is governed by the Arkansas Nurse Practice Act under the auspices of the Arkansas State Board of Nursing. This position is governed by state and federal laws and agency/institutional policy. Qualifications: Required Education and/or Experience: Successful completion of an accredited nursing degree\u00a0program; \u00a0Current licensure as a Registered Nurse by the Arkansas State Board of Nursing or current multistate license from a Nurse Licensure Compact (NLC) member state; Current CPR certification. Preferred Education and/or Experience: At least two (2) years of experience as a Registered Nurse in an outpatient, primary care clinic; Experience with college-age populations. Job Duties and Responsibilities Provide triage assessments, by telephone and in person, and appropriately directs patients to urgent care, same day, future appointments and referrals to off-site services as indicated; Administer medications & immunizations within scope or practice, as ordered by APRNs and MDs, and in accordance with the Arkansas Department of Health (ADH) and Center for Disease Control and Prevention (CDCP) recommendations and standards; Provide appropriate and effective health education to patients regarding their health problems, behavioral risk assessment, interventions, and medications; Document all findings and patient care interventions accurately and legibly and according to professional and legal standards; in Medicat (Electronic Health Record); Appropriately refer patients to Advanced Practice Registered Nurses (APRNs), Physicians, and off-site services; Follow client confidentiality policies and procedures for UA Little Rock Health Services and according to HIPAA guidelines; Comply with OSHA and clinic protocols regarding infectious disease prevention and control, including proper handling and disposal of infectious waste, gloving and sharps management/disposal, and proper disinfection of exam rooms and equipment; Maintain and order adequate supplies of medications, vaccines, and general clinic supplies; Document monthly equipment checks Maintain and document proper storage of vaccines as per ADH protocols, including completion of daily temperature log for refrigerator and freezer and regular inspection of expiration dates and proper disposal of expired vaccines; Participate and contribute to the development and implementation of campus health outreach programs; Perform CLIA waived tests and collect, package, route, and track lab specimens to off-site reference laboratory as directed; Create policies and compliance logs per CDC regulations; Deliver lab boxes to designated shipping carrier if needed; Perform tuberculosis screening and follow-up; Assist with reviewing students\u2019 immunization records to ensure they meet the University\u2019s requirements; Participate in regular staff meetings and contribute to progress toward developing and addressing Health Services\u2019 goals and objectives; Participate and contribute to quality improvement programs for Health Services; Participate and contribute to staff in-services and educational programs; Assist receptionist as needed with check-in procedures, making appointments, and answering the telephone; Mentor/train new RN staff Other duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Knowledge of computers and software applications (Microsoft, Internet, e-mail); Knowledge or ability to learn appropriate use of the Medicat Electronic Health Record system; Strong communication skills to provide effective education to clients and accurately relate client concerns to consulting professionals; Strong ability to work with diverse constituencies and persons with disabilities. Additional Information: Salary Information: $60,000 Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Please upload your Nursing license and CPR certification. Recruitment Contact Information: Chanell Smith, APRN Director of Health Services 501-916-3188 ccsmith2@ualr.edu Candi Barnum HR Business Partner 501-916-5713 cdbarnum@ualr.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Adult Maltreatment, Annual TB Screening, Child Maltreatment, Criminal Background Check, Financial Credit Check, Sex Offender Registry, Substance Abuse Testing The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Sitting Frequent Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Talking Occasional Physical Activity: Lifting Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/North-Little-Rock/Human-Resources-Specialist_R0089737": {"title": "Human Resources Specialist", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-10\nPosted: Posted 25 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 11/13/2026 Type of Position: Human Resources Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas Pulaski Technical College University of Arkansas - Pulaski Technical College at North Little Rock is an integral part of the Arkansas Technical and Community College System maintained by the State of Arkansas. The college is governed by the University of Arkansas System Board of Trustees and a seven-member Board of Visitors and derives its support largely from student tuition and fees and legislative appropriations. UA - Pulaski Tech, a comprehensive two-year college, offers associate degree and certificate programs for students who plan to transfer to four-year colleges and universities and/or for career preparation and advancement. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply link/button. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at (501) 812-2839. Department: Human Resources Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Human Resources Specialist is responsible for performing human resources related activities such as recruitment, interviewing, and orientation; monitoring and providing oversight and correction to processes related to area of assignment. HR Specialist is responsible for personnel-related administrative tasks and duties involving a wide range of support activities for human resources. This position reports to the Director of Human Resources and is governed by state and federal laws and institution policy. General Responsibilities: \u2022 Answers phones, schedules appointments, processes and routes mail, and makes travel arrangements. \u2022 Provides excellent customer service to employees, applicants, and visitors. \u2022 Works with a high level of initiative and concern for excellence. \u2022 Maintains confidentiality in all HR matters. \u2022 Analyzes and evaluates employment applications received from internal and external applicants to determine if applicants meet minimum qualifications. \u2022 Participates in pre-employment interview panels to assist with personnel issues and make certain that proper procedures are followed. Prepares and coordinates the flow of appropriate paperwork for each interviewee. \u2022 Conducts pre-employment background checks, criminal history background checks, and sex offender registry. \u2022 Assists with orienting new or returning employees when needed by explaining policies and procedures, and obtaining required employee information. \u2022 Responsible for maintaining a current centrally located employee bulletin board with all Department of Labor required information. \u2022 Prepares spreadsheets and databases to track employee related information. \u2022 Prepares and submits various bi-weekly, monthly, quarterly, and annual personnel reports on employee status including new hires, terminations, transfers, promotions, worker\u2019s compensation claims, salary, and leave accrual/usage. \u2022 Responds to inquiries and provides information on state and federal policy to management and staff. \u2022 Monitors and provides technical direction by assisting, advising, and correcting personnel actions keyed into human resources databases. \u2022 Responsible for processing motor vehicle reports. \u2022 Responsible for posting positions to external and internal job posting sites. \u2022 Serves as the point of contact for Tuition Waivers/Discounts for the HR department. \u2022 Responsible for creating the employee ID badges. \u2022 Performs other duties as assigned. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications : The educational equivalent of a high school diploma. Plus, three years of human resources related experience. Detail Oriented and Proficient in Microsoft Office Suite. Preferred Qualifications Higher Education Experience \u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0 Additional Information: Salary Information: $31,200 Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume, Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants Recruitment Contact Information: Natalie Hibdon, MBA Director of Human Resources nhibdon@uaptc.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Motor Vehicle Reports Check, Sex Offender Registry University of Arkansas - Pulaski Technical College is committed to providing a safe campus community. Title IX protects the college community from sexual harassment in a school's education programs and activities. This means that Title IX protects the college community in connection with all academic, educational, extracurricular, athletic, and other programs of the school, whether those programs take place in a school's facilities, in college transportation, at a class or training program sponsored by the school at another location, or elsewhere. \u00a0 We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Grasping, Hearing, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Feeling, Standing Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Stuttgart-Campus/Library-Technician_R0089735": {"title": "Library Technician", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-10\nPosted: Posted 25 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Clerical Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: Phillips Community College of the University of Arkansas The first community college established in Arkansas, Phillips Community College of the University of Arkansas (PCCUA) is a multi-campus, two-year college serving Eastern Arkansas. PCCUA has academic, occupational/technical and continuing education programs and offers over 25 associate degree programs with campuses in DeWitt, Helena-W. Helena and Stuttgart. Thank you for your interest, and we hope you\u2019ll be joining our Ridge Runner family soon! Below you will find the details for the position as well as any specific application requirements you should review before applying for this opening. To apply for this position, please click the Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process, please call Human Resources at (870) 338-6474, ext. 1271. Department: Library Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Assists library patrons with copies, circulation, computer, research requests - 40% Manages Serials for the Library - 15% Trains work-study students and others in library processes - 15% Receives, processes, shelves and maintains materials for the library - 25% Coordinates Interlibrary Loan for the Helena, Stuttgart and DeWitt campuses - 5% Qualifications: High school diploma required. Associate's degree preferred. Additional Information: Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Keri Simpson, KSimpson@pccua.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check For general application assistance, or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at (870) 338-6474, ext. 1271. PCCUA is committed to providing a safe campus community. We will conduct criminal background checks and a sex offender registry check for applicants seeking employment. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Crouching, Grasping, Hearing, Kneeling, Lifting, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Stooping, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Adjunct-Part-time-Lecturer_R0089651": {"title": "Adjunct/Part-time Lecturer", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-10\nPosted: Posted 25 Days Ago\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Adjunct Faculty Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Less than Annual Appointment (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Little Rock The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is a metropolitan research university that provides an accessible, quality education through flexible learning and unparalleled internship opportunities. At UA Little Rock, we prepare our more than 8,900 students to be innovators and responsible leaders in their fields. Committed to its metropolitan research university mission, UA Little Rock is a driving force in Little Rock's thriving cultural community and a major component of the city and state's growing profile as a regional leader in research, technology transfer, economic development, and job creation. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . Department: College of Humanities Arts, Social Sciences & Education Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The University of Arkansas at Little Rock seeks non-tenure-track Lecturers in the College of Humanities, Arts, Social Sciences, and Education. Lecturers will lead classroom instruction, develop course content, grade and evaluate coursework and exams, and undertake other duties associated with their course and its modalities of instruction. Qualified candidates will be considered for positions in Anthropology, Applied Communications, Art and Design, Education, English, History, Mass Communications, Music, Philosophy, Psychology, Rhetoric and Writing, the School of Public Affairs, Sociology, Theatre, and Spanish when positions become available. This position is governed by state and federal laws, and agency/institution policy. Qualifications: Required Education and/or Experience: Bachelor\u2019s degree.\u00a0 Preferred Education and/or Experience: Master\u2019s degree in the field of instruction or equivalent experience.\u00a0\u00a0 Experience teaching at the college level. \u00a0 Job Duties and Responsibilities:\u00a0 Meet classes as scheduled; notify the appropriate Chair/Director, Assistant Dean, or Dean in\u00a0advance if they are to be absent, and, if possible, arrange for a substitute instructor or assignments for his or her class. Be accessible to students through email, wireless/cellular technology, or scheduled office hours including arranging, when necessary, additional time for appointments. Prepare and distribute syllabi in accordance with established procedures and guidelines and follow the published final exam schedule. Maintain accurate records of students\u2019 academic standing; promptly provide final grades, attendance, and other information as required by the administration. Respect the confidentiality of student information; refrain from discussing or releasing such information except within recognized limits. Evaluate students based solely on their academic performance and to respond promptly student grade questions and/or appeals. Follow university policies and procedures.\u00a0 Knowledge, Skills, Abilities: \u00a0 Be able to navigate Blackboard and Google Suite.\u00a0 Be able to communicate clearly and effectively.\u00a0\u00a0 Be able to manage time effectively.\u00a0 Be able to keep good records. Additional Information: Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Please upload all required documents in the \"Resume\" attachment section of your application (before hitting the submit button), if you want to be considered for this position. Recruitment Contact Information: Kris McAbee, Associate Dean, kxmcabee@ualr.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: No Background Check Required The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Sitting, Standing Frequent Physical Activity: Hearing, Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAPBSJPRS-J-Parker-Agriculture-Research-Building/Landscape-Specialist_R0089553": {"title": "Landscape Specialist", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-10\nPosted: Posted 25 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Skilled Labor Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff The University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff is an 1890 Land-Grant HBCU with a diverse student population, competitive degree offerings and stellar faculty. For more than 140 years, the University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff has worked to create an environment that inculcates learning, growth and productivity while affording a basic need to its students \u2013 a chance to advance. The 15:1 student to teacher ratio makes it possible to maintain a learning environment with close interaction between students and faculty while challenging curricula encourage our students to seek and fulfill their potential. You can excel in your chosen field of study through a curriculum of \u00a0 Certificate and Associates degree programs,\u00a0 more than thirty\u00a0 Undergraduate programs, Master\u2019s degree programs and a Doctorate program in Aquaculture/Fisheries. You can also develop workplace readiness through internships, co-ops and fellowships in the U.S. and abroad. Out-of-class experiences and student involvement include more than 90 student organizations, an internationally renowned Vesper Choir, Marching Band, Concert Bands, Wind Symphony, nationally recognized debate team, award-winning theater department and accomplished athletic program. Though the main campus is in Pine Bluff, its reach is worldwide. UAPB has an extended campus in North Little Rock and offers as well as online courses. With the addition of the Arkansas Research and Education Optical Network (ARE-ON), students can engage in information exchange with others anywhere in the world. There are also Research and Extension offices in Lonoke, Newport and Lake Village and collaborations with other colleges and universities in the State through the National Science Foundation funded STEM (Science, Technology, Engineering and Mathematics) Academy. As the second oldest land-grant institution in the state of Arkansas, the mission of this No Excuse University remains the same \u2013 to provide a high quality, affordable education with a personal touch. We invite you to Become a Part of the Pride at the University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process and require reasonable accommodations, please contact Human Resources at 870.575.8400 . Department: Vince Wiley | Agriculture Farm Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Landscape Specialist will work under the supervision of the Farm Manager and will be responsible for edging grass/sidewalks, mowing, trimming hedges, pruning trees, maintaining ornamental areas, planting flowers/plants/shrubs, removing grass from flower beds, and general grounds upkeep for the 1890 Research and Extension buildings. The selected candidate will also assist in maintaining research plots and the daily care of farm animals. Qualifications: The formal education equivalent of a high school diploma; plus four years of experience in landscaping, grounds maintenance or related area. Additional Information: Salary Information: $40,000 Required Documents to Apply: List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants (Please upload all required documents in the \"Resume\" attachment section of your application to be considered for this position) : Please submit your resume and list of 3 professional references under Resume' on your application. Recruitment Contact Information: Sharron Williams All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Motor Vehicle Reports Check The University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff may conduct pre-employment background checks on certain positions for applicants being considered for employment. \u00a0 The background checks may include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. \u00a0 Required checks are identified in the position listing. \u00a0 A criminal background check or arrest pending adjudication information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absences of a relationship to the requirements of the position. \u00a0 Background check information will be used in a consistent, non-discriminatory manner consistent with the state and federal law. \u00a0 The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Climbing, Crawling, Crouching, Driving, Feeling, Grasping, Hearing, Kneeling, Lifting, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Repetitive Motion, Sharps, Sitting, Standing, Stooping, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, N/A, Repetitive Motion Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/RN---EP-Cardiology-Clinic_R0089580-1": {"title": "RN - EP Cardiology Clinic", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-10\nPosted: Posted 25 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/10/2026 Type of Position: Clinical Staff - Nursing Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | CVSL Cardiology Clinic OP C Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Registered Nurse provides professional nursing care to patients receiving services within the Electrophysiology (EP) Clinic. Responsibilities include clinical assessment, patient triage, care coordination, patient education, medication-related inquiries, referral coordination, and collaboration with electrophysiologists, advanced practice providers, technologists, and other interdisciplinary team members. The RN supports patients with cardiac arrhythmias and other electrophysiologic disorders throughout the continuum of care, including coordination of diagnostic testing, procedural planning and follow-up, cardiac implantable electronic device management, remote monitoring, and transitions between inpatient and outpatient care. The RN provides education to patients and families regarding disease processes, medications, procedures, treatment plans, and self-management strategies while contributing to individualized plans of care. This role maintains accountability for patient safety, quality outcomes, patient experience, and efficient delivery of patient-centered care. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Graduate of an accredited Nursing Program with an Associate's Degree, Nursing Diploma, Bachelor's in Nursing, or Master's in Nursing\u00a0 Valid RN License Minimum of 1 year Registered Nursing experience Preferred Qualifications: 2 or more years of RN experience in a cardiac, critical care, or procedural/interventional setting Additional Information: Responsibilities: Collects and documents assessment data from patients and/or others per UAMS standard.\u00a0 Develops patient's Plan of Care (POC) per department/unit standards utilizing assessment data.\u00a0 Evaluates the progress of patients toward attainment of desired outcomes. Administers medication following department/unit standards and Nurse Practice Act.\u00a0 Verifies and evaluates care delivered to ensure it is consistent with patient and family centered care principles, practice standards and regulatory requirements. Supports the integration of current evidence into nursing practices.\u00a0 Promotes an environment conducive to positive educational experience for all students and staff.\u00a0 Provides effective patient/family education/discharge planning. Effectively collaborates and communicates with nursing staff at all levels, interdisciplinary teams, executive leaders, and other stakeholders.\u00a0 Communicates care appropriately through documentation in the medical record. Reports variances in care/ systems/ processes through the appropriate means.\u00a0 Participates in recruitment/retention of staff.\u00a0 Facilitates development and implementation of nursing practice standards that are evidence-based and in compliance with ANA standards. May perform other duties as assigned. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Criminal Background Check, Substance Abuse Testing This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Grasping, Standing, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Lifting, Pulling, Pushing Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAM--Monticello-Campus/Warehouse-Worker_R0089532-1": {"title": "Warehouse Worker", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-10\nPosted: Posted 25 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Procurement, Inventory Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Monticello UAM, one of twenty campuses of the University of Arkansas System, is located in southeastern Arkansas in the beautiful timberlands, rich in outdoor recreation activities, and approximately 100 miles south of Little Rock. UAM is a comprehensive, residential and commuter, undergraduate institution also offering selected master\u2019s degree programs. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please submit a request via the OEOC website: \u00a0Applicants are required to submit a request for each position to which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 870-460-1422 . Department: Motor Pool Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Warehouse Worker works under general supervision and is responsible for maintaining inventory control of incoming and outgoing supplies and materials. Maintains records and inventory of stock levels and notifies the supervisor of items to be reordered to ensure adequate supply. Fills requisitions for supplies from departmental and unit personnel and restocks shelves and bins with items from the warehouse. Unloads shipment of supplies and materials and notifies supervisor of any damaged items. Checks packing slips against invoices to verify order accuracy; stacks items in proper bins or on shelves in the storage area. Delivers shipments to various locations according to schedule. Assists in the maintenance of work area, equipment, and vehicles and maintains vehicle records and dispatches vehicles. Performs related responsibilities as required or assigned. The successful candidate must be able to lift to 55 pounds. This position may require overtime and may include being on call at times. Qualifications: The formal education equivalent of a high school diploma, plus one year of experience in inventory control, stock room or warehouse operations, shipping and receiving, or a related field. \u00a0 Additional Information: Salary Information: $24,038.00 Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Diane Forrest Campus Maintenance Supervisor 135 Forestry Park Dr. Monticello, AR 71656 870.460.1159 forrestd@uamont.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Financial Credit Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Climbing, Driving, Grasping, Kneeling, Lifting, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Sitting, Standing, Stooping, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Climbing, Driving, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Lifting, Pulling Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Director-of-Planning--Design---Construction_R0089354-1": {"title": "Director of Planning, Design & Construction", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-07\nPosted: Posted 28 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/07/2026 Type of Position: Management - Operations Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: CHA | UAMS Institutional Relations Office Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Director of Planning, Design & Construction oversees the planning, design, and execution of capital construction, renovation, and remodeling projects across UAMS. This position provides strategic leadership to the Planning, Design & Construction team, directing projects from initial concept and scope development through planning, design, construction, and project closeout. Reporting to the Associate Vice Chancellor of External Affairs and Facilities\u202fDevelopment, the Director ensures projects are completed safely, efficiently, within budget, and in alignment with the University's operational, regulatory, and strategic objectives.\u202f Qualifications: Bachelor\u2019s degree plus eight (8) years of experience in design, construction, and project management required. Registered Professional Engineer or Licensed Architect. Certified Healthcare C onstruction (CHC) certification preferred. Project Management Certification or experience preferred. \u00a0 Knowledge, Skills & Abilities: Excellent communication and interpersonal skills.\u202f\u00a0 Familiar with technical and construction contractual issues.\u202f\u00a0 Knowledge of health care organization and operations of a health care facility preferred.\u202f\u00a0 Knowledge of regulatory standards such as AIA guidelines, Department of Health Regulations, and The Joint Commission and Life Safety Code preferred.\u202f\u00a0 Exercises sound judgement and\u202fexhibit\u202fexcellent problem-solving skills.\u202f Strong team management skills.\u00a0 Creative thinking skills.\u00a0 \u200b Responsibilities: Directs a team of project planners and project managers as well as contracting and procurement staff in all aspects of project planning, design, and construction management.\u00a0 Works with consultants in translating UAMS-user requirements\u202finto proper design.\u202f\u00a0 Development and management of construction project budgets and schedules to assure that all projects are designed and completed within budget and on time.\u202f\u202f\u00a0 Monitors and provides guidance during general and detailed planning stages of remodel and expansion projects.\u202f\u202f\u202f\u00a0 Serves as a liaison with architects and engineers who are hired to perform these projects.\u202f\u00a0 Participates in developing or modifying the campus masterplan.\u202f\u202f\u00a0 Ensures conformance to the master plan to avoid/minimize future costly changes or change orders.\u202f\u00a0 Presents project concepts and progress to management, staff, and faculty.\u202f\u00a0 Serves as a liaison between UAMS departments and outside contractors (to ensure that the impact of the contractor\u2019s activities is minimized).\u202f\u202f\u00a0 Ensures all projects meet state laws, building codes, and life safety requirements.\u202f\u202f\u00a0 Performs other duties as assigned. Examples\u202finclude:\u202fdeveloping contract documents, overseeing technical and contractual issues with consultants and contractors, and approving consultant and contractor invoices for payment.\u202f\u202f\u00a0 Additional Information: Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Criminal Background Check This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: Crouching, Feeling, Hearing, Kneeling, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Reaching, Sitting, Standing, Stooping, Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-Arkansas-at-Pine-Bluff/Graduate-Research-Assistant-Plant-Molecular-Biology_R0088765-1": {"title": "Graduate Research Assistant-Plant Molecular Biology", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-07\nPosted: Posted 28 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Graduate Assistant Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff The University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff is an 1890 Land-Grant HBCU with a diverse student population, competitive degree offerings and stellar faculty. For more than 140 years, the University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff has worked to create an environment that inculcates learning, growth and productivity while affording a basic need to its students \u2013 a chance to advance. The 15:1 student to teacher ratio makes it possible to maintain a learning environment with close interaction between students and faculty while challenging curricula encourage our students to seek and fulfill their potential. You can excel in your chosen field of study through a curriculum of \u00a0 Certificate and Associates degree programs,\u00a0 more than thirty\u00a0 Undergraduate programs, Master\u2019s degree programs and a Doctorate program in Aquaculture/Fisheries. You can also develop workplace readiness through internships, co-ops and fellowships in the U.S. and abroad. Out-of-class experiences and student involvement include more than 90 student organizations, an internationally renowned Vesper Choir, Marching Band, Concert Bands, Wind Symphony, nationally recognized debate team, award-winning theater department and accomplished athletic program. Though the main campus is in Pine Bluff, its reach is worldwide. UAPB has an extended campus in North Little Rock and offers as well as online courses. With the addition of the Arkansas Research and Education Optical Network (ARE-ON), students can engage in information exchange with others anywhere in the world. There are also Research and Extension offices in Lonoke, Newport and Lake Village and collaborations with other colleges and universities in the State through the National Science Foundation funded STEM (Science, Technology, Engineering and Mathematics) Academy. As the second oldest land-grant institution in the state of Arkansas, the mission of this No Excuse University remains the same \u2013 to provide a high quality, affordable education with a personal touch. We invite you to Become a Part of the Pride at the University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process and require reasonable accommodations, please contact Human Resources at 870.575.8400 . Department: Agriculture Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Understanding the role of Pita genes in Blast disease resistance in Rice Qualifications: 1. Develop a plasmid construct for CRISPR-Cas9 2. Tissue culture of rice seeds 3. Agrobacterium-based transformation 4. Analyze the gene-edited lines using Sanger sequencing 5. Evaluate the mutant lines for resistance to blast isolates Additional Information: Salary Information: $22,000 Graduate Assistant Required Documents to Apply: Resume, Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants (Please upload all required documents in the \"Resume\" attachment section of your application to be considered for this position) : Recruitment Contact Information: Sharron Williams All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: No Background Check Required The University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff may conduct pre-employment background checks on certain positions for applicants being considered for employment. \u00a0 The background checks may include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. \u00a0 Required checks are identified in the position listing. \u00a0 A criminal background check or arrest pending adjudication information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absences of a relationship to the requirements of the position. \u00a0 Background check information will be used in a consistent, non-discriminatory manner consistent with the state and federal law. \u00a0 The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Grasping, Kneeling, Lifting Frequent Physical Activity: Climbing Occasional Physical Activity: Driving Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAPBSTUNIONL-A-Davis-Student-Union/Administrative-Associate_R0088706": {"title": "Administrative Associate", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-07\nPosted: Posted 28 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Clerical Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff The University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff is an 1890 Land-Grant HBCU with a diverse student population, competitive degree offerings and stellar faculty. For more than 140 years, the University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff has worked to create an environment that inculcates learning, growth and productivity while affording a basic need to its students \u2013 a chance to advance. The 15:1 student to teacher ratio makes it possible to maintain a learning environment with close interaction between students and faculty while challenging curricula encourage our students to seek and fulfill their potential. You can excel in your chosen field of study through a curriculum of \u00a0 Certificate and Associates degree programs,\u00a0 more than thirty\u00a0 Undergraduate programs, Master\u2019s degree programs and a Doctorate program in Aquaculture/Fisheries. You can also develop workplace readiness through internships, co-ops and fellowships in the U.S. and abroad. Out-of-class experiences and student involvement include more than 90 student organizations, an internationally renowned Vesper Choir, Marching Band, Concert Bands, Wind Symphony, nationally recognized debate team, award-winning theater department and accomplished athletic program. Though the main campus is in Pine Bluff, its reach is worldwide. UAPB has an extended campus in North Little Rock and offers as well as online courses. With the addition of the Arkansas Research and Education Optical Network (ARE-ON), students can engage in information exchange with others anywhere in the world. There are also Research and Extension offices in Lonoke, Newport and Lake Village and collaborations with other colleges and universities in the State through the National Science Foundation funded STEM (Science, Technology, Engineering and Mathematics) Academy. As the second oldest land-grant institution in the state of Arkansas, the mission of this No Excuse University remains the same \u2013 to provide a high quality, affordable education with a personal touch. We invite you to Become a Part of the Pride at the University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process and require reasonable accommodations, please contact Human Resources at 870.575.8400 . Department: Emerging Scholars & Leadership Academy Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Supporting the Emerging Scholar and Leadership Institute, the Administrative Associate will be responsible for managing key administrative and financial processes within Workday. This position will help ensure that purchases, travel, reimbursements, timekeeping, and related transactions are completed accurately, promptly, and in accordance with university policies. The selected candidate will: * Create, submit, and monitor requisitions and purchase orders in Workday. * Track requisitions from initial submission through approval, purchase order issuance, receipt, and payment. * Prepare and process spend authorizations for employee and program-related travel. * Complete and submit expense reports, including reviewing receipts, verifying expenses, and ensuring proper documentation. * Assist employees and program participants with resolving errors, missing information, and other Workday transaction issues. * Review and monitor employee time entries to ensure hours, leave, and corrections are submitted accurately and by established deadlines. * Coordinate timekeeping corrections and follow up with employees and supervisors regarding incomplete or inaccurate entries. * Maintain organized records of purchase orders, invoices, receipts, travel documents, expense reports, and approvals. * Communicate with Procurement, Accounts Payable, Human Resources, Payroll, and other university offices to resolve processing concerns. * Monitor the status of Workday transactions and provide regular updates to institute leadership. * Ensure transactions comply with university purchasing, travel, reimbursement, and timekeeping policies. * Assist with budget tracking by reviewing expenses, commitments, and outstanding purchase orders. * Prepare reports related to expenditures, travel, purchasing activity, and administrative operations. * Serve as a Workday resource for institute staff by providing guidance on required documentation, approval processes, and submission procedures. * Perform other administrative duties necessary to support the daily operations of the Emerging Scholar and Leadership Institute. Qualifications: The formal education equivalent of a high school diploma is required. Candidates must also have at least three years of directly related administrative experience, including demonstrated experience with Workday processes such as requisitions, purchase orders, spend authorizations, expense reports, and timekeeping. Specialized training in business management, business education, accounting, or a related field is preferred. Additional Information: Salary Information: $35,000 Required Documents to Apply: List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants (Please upload all required documents in the \"Resume\" attachment section of your application to be considered for this position) : Recruitment Contact Information: Sharron Williams, Employment Manager/Recruiter Human Resources williamssm@uapb.edu 870-575-8403 All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check The University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff may conduct pre-employment background checks on certain positions for applicants being considered for employment. \u00a0 The background checks may include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. \u00a0 Required checks are identified in the position listing. \u00a0 A criminal background check or arrest pending adjudication information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absences of a relationship to the requirements of the position. \u00a0 Background check information will be used in a consistent, non-discriminatory manner consistent with the state and federal law. \u00a0 The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Sitting Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: Walking Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAPBDHCDelta-Housing-Complex/Director-of-Housing-and-Residential-Experience_R0088980": {"title": "Director of Housing and Residential Experience", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-07\nPosted: Posted 28 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Social Sciences Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff The University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff is an 1890 Land-Grant HBCU with a diverse student population, competitive degree offerings and stellar faculty. For more than 140 years, the University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff has worked to create an environment that inculcates learning, growth and productivity while affording a basic need to its students \u2013 a chance to advance. The 15:1 student to teacher ratio makes it possible to maintain a learning environment with close interaction between students and faculty while challenging curricula encourage our students to seek and fulfill their potential. You can excel in your chosen field of study through a curriculum of \u00a0 Certificate and Associates degree programs,\u00a0 more than thirty\u00a0 Undergraduate programs, Master\u2019s degree programs and a Doctorate program in Aquaculture/Fisheries. You can also develop workplace readiness through internships, co-ops and fellowships in the U.S. and abroad. Out-of-class experiences and student involvement include more than 90 student organizations, an internationally renowned Vesper Choir, Marching Band, Concert Bands, Wind Symphony, nationally recognized debate team, award-winning theater department and accomplished athletic program. Though the main campus is in Pine Bluff, its reach is worldwide. UAPB has an extended campus in North Little Rock and offers as well as online courses. With the addition of the Arkansas Research and Education Optical Network (ARE-ON), students can engage in information exchange with others anywhere in the world. There are also Research and Extension offices in Lonoke, Newport and Lake Village and collaborations with other colleges and universities in the State through the National Science Foundation funded STEM (Science, Technology, Engineering and Mathematics) Academy. As the second oldest land-grant institution in the state of Arkansas, the mission of this No Excuse University remains the same \u2013 to provide a high quality, affordable education with a personal touch. We invite you to Become a Part of the Pride at the University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process and require reasonable accommodations, please contact Human Resources at 870.575.8400 . Department: Housing and Residence Life | Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Reporting to the Dean of Students, the Director of Housing and Residential Experience serves as the chief administrator for the University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff\u2019s residential communities. The Director provides visionary, student-centered, and operational leadership for a comprehensive housing program that includes multiple residence halls and approximately 1,500 beds. The Director oversees all aspects of housing operations, residential education, staffing, facilities coordination, and student support within the residential environment. This role ensures that residential communities are safe, inclusive, well-maintained, and aligned with institutional priorities while fostering a living environment that promotes student success, belonging, retention, and holistic development. As a senior leader within Student Affairs, the Director manages a complex auxiliary operation, supervises professional and student staff, and collaborates extensively with campus partners to advance a high-quality residential experience that supports the University\u2019s mission as an 1890 land-grant HBCU. The position requires sound judgment, strong operational oversight, and the ability to lead both strategic initiatives and daily housing functions. Qualifications: Master's degree in Higher Education, Student Affairs, Business Administration, Human Sciences, or a related field from an accredited institution. Minimum of five years of progressively responsible experience in university housing, residence life, or student affairs administration. Demonstrated experience supervising professional staff and managing student staff teams. Knowledge of housing operations including assignments, occupancy management, and residential education practices. Experience managing budgets, auxiliary services, or complex operational units. Demonstrated ability to address student concerns and navigate complex situations with sound judgment. Strong communication, leadership, and organizational skills. Additional Information: Salary Information: 40,000 to 65,000 Required Documents to Apply: Letters of Recommendation, Resume, Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants (Please upload all required documents in the \"Resume\" attachment section of your application to be considered for this position) : Recruitment Contact Information: Sharron Williams, Employment Manager, 870-575-8403 All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: The University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff may conduct pre-employment background checks on certain positions for applicants being considered for employment. \u00a0 The background checks may include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. \u00a0 Required checks are identified in the position listing. \u00a0 A criminal background check or arrest pending adjudication information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absences of a relationship to the requirements of the position. \u00a0 Background check information will be used in a consistent, non-discriminatory manner consistent with the state and federal law. \u00a0 The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-Arkansas-at-Pine-Bluff/Extension-Program-Aide---EFNEP---Pulaski-Co_R0088959": {"title": "Extension Program Aide - EFNEP - Pulaski Co", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-07\nPosted: Posted 28 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Extension Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff The University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff is an 1890 Land-Grant HBCU with a diverse student population, competitive degree offerings and stellar faculty. For more than 140 years, the University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff has worked to create an environment that inculcates learning, growth and productivity while affording a basic need to its students \u2013 a chance to advance. The 15:1 student to teacher ratio makes it possible to maintain a learning environment with close interaction between students and faculty while challenging curricula encourage our students to seek and fulfill their potential. You can excel in your chosen field of study through a curriculum of \u00a0 Certificate and Associates degree programs,\u00a0 more than thirty\u00a0 Undergraduate programs, Master\u2019s degree programs and a Doctorate program in Aquaculture/Fisheries. You can also develop workplace readiness through internships, co-ops and fellowships in the U.S. and abroad. Out-of-class experiences and student involvement include more than 90 student organizations, an internationally renowned Vesper Choir, Marching Band, Concert Bands, Wind Symphony, nationally recognized debate team, award-winning theater department and accomplished athletic program. Though the main campus is in Pine Bluff, its reach is worldwide. UAPB has an extended campus in North Little Rock and offers as well as online courses. With the addition of the Arkansas Research and Education Optical Network (ARE-ON), students can engage in information exchange with others anywhere in the world. There are also Research and Extension offices in Lonoke, Newport and Lake Village and collaborations with other colleges and universities in the State through the National Science Foundation funded STEM (Science, Technology, Engineering and Mathematics) Academy. As the second oldest land-grant institution in the state of Arkansas, the mission of this No Excuse University remains the same \u2013 to provide a high quality, affordable education with a personal touch. We invite you to Become a Part of the Pride at the University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process and require reasonable accommodations, please contact Human Resources at 870.575.8400 . Department: Agri FCS Program Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff Cooperative Extension Program is searching to fill the position of Extension Program Aide in the School of Agriculture, Fisheries, and Human Sciences. The Extension Program Aide (Extension Nutrition Educator) SNAP-Ed works under the immediate supervision of the Interim Family and Consumer Sciences Program Leader. Must have competencies in the following areas: food preparation, nutrition, diet, and health. The successful candidate must have good workforce ethics and be able to plan, organize, conduct and evaluate educational programs (using the skills above) with adult and youth audiences. FUNCTIONS Program Aide will teach nutrition education to SNAP-Ed recipients (formerly food stamp program). Coordinates nutrition education programs in Pulaski and Jefferson. Develop strategies for identifying and involving target audience. Maintains client participation data, and prepares appropriate reports and documents required to effectively evaluate program outcomes in Pulaski and Jefferson. KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS & ABILITIES Ability to learn the subject matter, speak and write clearly, work and motivate others, follow oral and written instructions, accept supervision, maintain confidentiality, and relate to clientele. Computer Skills desirable. Travel required within assigned areas(s). The successful applicant must have transportation for use on the job, a current driver\u2019s license, and liability insurance in effect. Qualifications: MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS High school diploma with course work within area School Agriculture, Fisheries and Human Sciences family and consumer sciences or related areas preferred. The ability to work without close supervision is required. Transportation for use on the job with liability insurance in effect is required. Additional Information: ADDITIONAL INFORMATION Work Hours: M-F 8:00 a.m. to 5:00 p.m., Flexible work hours may vary-night and weekend work may be required. Salary Information: $35,568 Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants (Please upload all required documents in the \"Resume\" attachment section of your application to be considered for this position) : Recruitment Contact Information: Sharron Williams All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Child Maltreatment, Motor Vehicle Reports Check The University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff may conduct pre-employment background checks on certain positions for applicants being considered for employment. \u00a0 The background checks may include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. \u00a0 Required checks are identified in the position listing. \u00a0 A criminal background check or arrest pending adjudication information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absences of a relationship to the requirements of the position. \u00a0 Background check information will be used in a consistent, non-discriminatory manner consistent with the state and federal law. \u00a0 The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Balancing, Climbing, Crawling, Crouching, Driving, Feeling, Grasping, Hearing, Kneeling, Lifting, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Repetitive Motion, Sharps, Sitting, Standing, Stooping, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-Arkansas-at-Pine-Bluff/STEM-Academy-Instructor-Mentor-1_R0085607": {"title": "STEM Academy Instructor/Mentor-1", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-07\nPosted: Posted 28 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Clerical Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff The University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff is an 1890 Land-Grant HBCU with a diverse student population, competitive degree offerings and stellar faculty. For more than 140 years, the University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff has worked to create an environment that inculcates learning, growth and productivity while affording a basic need to its students \u2013 a chance to advance. The 15:1 student to teacher ratio makes it possible to maintain a learning environment with close interaction between students and faculty while challenging curricula encourage our students to seek and fulfill their potential. You can excel in your chosen field of study through a curriculum of \u00a0 Certificate and Associates degree programs,\u00a0 more than thirty\u00a0 Undergraduate programs, Master\u2019s degree programs and a Doctorate program in Aquaculture/Fisheries. You can also develop workplace readiness through internships, co-ops and fellowships in the U.S. and abroad. Out-of-class experiences and student involvement include more than 90 student organizations, an internationally renowned Vesper Choir, Marching Band, Concert Bands, Wind Symphony, nationally recognized debate team, award-winning theater department and accomplished athletic program. Though the main campus is in Pine Bluff, its reach is worldwide. UAPB has an extended campus in North Little Rock and offers as well as online courses. With the addition of the Arkansas Research and Education Optical Network (ARE-ON), students can engage in information exchange with others anywhere in the world. There are also Research and Extension offices in Lonoke, Newport and Lake Village and collaborations with other colleges and universities in the State through the National Science Foundation funded STEM (Science, Technology, Engineering and Mathematics) Academy. As the second oldest land-grant institution in the state of Arkansas, the mission of this No Excuse University remains the same \u2013 to provide a high quality, affordable education with a personal touch. We invite you to Become a Part of the Pride at the University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process and require reasonable accommodations, please contact Human Resources at 870.575.8400 . Department: CCI/CIE Grant Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: STEM Academy Instructors and Mentors are tasked with delivering innovative STEM concepts and mentoring k-12 students all over Arkansas. Qualifications: Subject for review. Additional Information: Salary Information: $20/Hr Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants (Please upload all required documents in the \"Resume\" attachment section of your application to be considered for this position) : Recruitment Contact Information: Sharron Williams, Employment Manager, williamssm@uapb.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: No Background Check Required The University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff may conduct pre-employment background checks on certain positions for applicants being considered for employment. \u00a0 The background checks may include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. \u00a0 Required checks are identified in the position listing. \u00a0 A criminal background check or arrest pending adjudication information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absences of a relationship to the requirements of the position. \u00a0 Background check information will be used in a consistent, non-discriminatory manner consistent with the state and federal law. \u00a0 The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Standing Frequent Physical Activity: Talking Occasional Physical Activity: Walking Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Pharmacy-Technician-I---Specialty-Pharmacy-Operations_R0086827-1": {"title": "Pharmacy Technician I - Specialty Pharmacy Operations", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-07\nPosted: Posted 28 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/07/2026 Type of Position: Clinical Staff - Medical Ancillary Support Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | PTSL Specialty Pharmacy Operations Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Pharmacy Technician I works under the supervision of the pharmacist and assists with the preparation, delivery, and shipping of medication. Performs tasks within regulations set forth by state, federal and accreditation bodies. The technician will provide excellent pharmacy services. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: High School Diploma or GED Arkansas Pharmacy Technician License or eligible for licensure by the Arkansas State Board of Pharmacy Preferred Qualifications: Undergraduate degree 1 year of pharmacy technician experience PTCB National Certification ASHP/ACPE-accredited technician training or certificate program (i.e., Advanced Certified Pharmacy Technician) Additional Information: Responsibilities: Prioritizes the order of filling (waiting, pickup, same-day shipment, next-day shipment) to meet patient needs and ensure patient satisfaction. Labels all prescription bottles accurately and with pharmaceutical elegance and applies all appropriate auxiliary labels. Ensures appropriate paperwork is included with each prescription fill. Accurately fills orders to meet and improve metrics surrounding errors while processing prescriptions. Documents appropriate information during the filling process to meet UAMS Policies and Procedures and URAC and ACHC Accreditation Standards. Understands and follows all UAMS Policies related to medication processing and filling, including adherence to HIPAA laws. Demonstrates understanding and proper handling of Hazardous Drugs. Communicates with Specialty Pharmacy staff to ensure seamless pharmaceutical care for Specialty patients. Maintains cleaning logs for supplies used in Specialty Pharmacy Operations. Displays courtesy and respect toward all patients and employees. Demonstrates cultural sensitivity. Strives to provide excellent pharmacy services. Values patient safety as a priority.\u00a0 Promotes health equity. Displays teamwork ability. Works creatively to solve problems and improve services. Participates in the training of staff. Assures medication supply is sufficient for needs and alerts the buyer to any deficiencies. Proactively addresses supply to ensure availability for next-day shipping. Completes regularly scheduled inventory counts and reviews (including but not limited to: cycle counts, annual inventory, out-of-date stock review). Manages and updates inventory procedures, ensuring all responsible parties complete assigned inventory tasks. Other duties as assigned. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), Resume Optional Documents: List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Criminal Background Check, Substance Abuse Testing This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding Frequent Physical Activity: Reaching, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Kneeling, Lifting, Pulling, Pushing Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/North-Little-Rock/Adjunct-Faculty---Psychology_R0089647": {"title": "Adjunct Faculty - Psychology", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-07\nPosted: Posted 28 Days Ago\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Less than Annual Appointment (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas Pulaski Technical College University of Arkansas - Pulaski Technical College at North Little Rock is an integral part of the Arkansas Technical and Community College System maintained by the State of Arkansas. The college is governed by the University of Arkansas System Board of Trustees and a seven-member Board of Visitors and derives its support largely from student tuition and fees and legislative appropriations. UA - Pulaski Tech, a comprehensive two-year college, offers associate degree and certificate programs for students who plan to transfer to four-year colleges and universities and/or for career preparation and advancement. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply link/button. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at (501) 812-2839. Department: Social Science Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: University of Arkansas - Pulaski Technical College is an integral part of the Arkansas Technical and Community College System maintained by the State of Arkansas. The college is governed by the University of Arkansas System Board of Trustees and a seven-member Board of Visitors and derives its support largely from student tuition and fees and legislative appropriations. UA - Pulaski Tech, a comprehensive two-year college, offers associate degree and certificate programs for students who plan to transfer to four-year colleges and universities and/or for career preparation and advancement. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply link/button. Summary of Duties: Teach one or more classes as needed in Psychology History. Classes include but are not limited to Psychology and the Human Experience, Developmental Psychology, Abnormal Psychology and Behavioral Statistics. Classes may be offered online, virtual (at anytime), or evenings as noted on the schedule. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications : 18 graduate hours in Psychology. Preferred Qualifications : PhD in Psychology. Additional Information: Salary Information: $675/credit hour Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Resume, Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants Recruitment Contact Information: Recruitment Contact (Name, Title, Contact Info) Human Resources humanresources@uaptc.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: University of Arkansas - Pulaski Technical College is committed to providing a safe campus community. Title IX protects the college community from sexual harassment in a school's education programs and activities. This means that Title IX protects the college community in connection with all academic, educational, extracurricular, athletic, and other programs of the school, whether those programs take place in a school's facilities, in college transportation, at a class or training program sponsored by the school at another location, or elsewhere. \u00a0 We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Scholarship-Support-Specialist_R0089477": {"title": "Scholarship Support Specialist", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-07\nPosted: Posted 28 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Clerical Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Little Rock The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is a metropolitan research university that provides an accessible, quality education through flexible learning and unparalleled internship opportunities. At UA Little Rock, we prepare our more than 8,900 students to be innovators and responsible leaders in their fields. Committed to its metropolitan research university mission, UA Little Rock is a driving force in Little Rock's thriving cultural community and a major component of the city and state's growing profile as a regional leader in research, technology transfer, economic development, and job creation. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . Department: Scholarships Department's Website: ualr.edu/scholarships Summary of Job Duties: The Scholarship Support Specialist is responsible for administrative support functions of the scholarship team in the Office of Financial Aid and Scholarships; providing direct service and support to students, families, and other constituents as needed; and assisting the Assistant Director of Scholarships. This position is governed by state and federal laws and agency/institution policy. Qualifications: Required Education and/or Experience: The formal education equivalent of a high school diploma; At least two years of experience in specialized or a related field applicable to work performed. OTHER JOB-RELATED EDUCATION AND/OR EXPERIENCE MAY BE SUBSTITUTED FOR ALL OR PART OF THESE BASIC REQUIREMENTS. Job Duties and Responsibilities : Assist with and maintain a database for verifying eligibility for transfer scholarships; Assist with assessing and scoring all scholarship applications received as well as gathering any additional supporting documentation requested; Maintain and process all required post-acceptance documentation associated with private scholarship awards; Maintain a shared database for donor letters received for Development; Assist with record-keeping and imaging of all third-party scholarship checks received; Manage office supplies and printed materials; Support office functions, including personnel and purchasing; Answer phone calls through the main phone line in the office as needed; Provide exceptional service and support to both internal and external clients; Other duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Superior verbal and written communication; Good interpersonal skills; Ability to work with a team; Ability to multi-task; Must be detail-oriented; Must be organized; Must be self-motivated. Additional Information: Salary Information: $30,773 Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Brittany Richards Assistant Director of Financial Aid & Scholarships bkrichards@ualr.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Grasping, Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Sitting, Standing Occasional Physical Activity: Sitting, Standing Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-Arkansas-at-Pine-Bluff/Director-of-Facilities-Planning_R0073834": {"title": "Director of Facilities Planning", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-07\nPosted: Posted 28 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Management - Facilities Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff The University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff is an 1890 Land-Grant HBCU with a diverse student population, competitive degree offerings and stellar faculty. For more than 140 years, the University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff has worked to create an environment that inculcates learning, growth and productivity while affording a basic need to its students \u2013 a chance to advance. The 15:1 student to teacher ratio makes it possible to maintain a learning environment with close interaction between students and faculty while challenging curricula encourage our students to seek and fulfill their potential. You can excel in your chosen field of study through a curriculum of \u00a0 Certificate and Associates degree programs,\u00a0 more than thirty\u00a0 Undergraduate programs, Master\u2019s degree programs and a Doctorate program in Aquaculture/Fisheries. You can also develop workplace readiness through internships, co-ops and fellowships in the U.S. and abroad. Out-of-class experiences and student involvement include more than 90 student organizations, an internationally renowned Vesper Choir, Marching Band, Concert Bands, Wind Symphony, nationally recognized debate team, award-winning theater department and accomplished athletic program. Though the main campus is in Pine Bluff, its reach is worldwide. UAPB has an extended campus in North Little Rock and offers as well as online courses. With the addition of the Arkansas Research and Education Optical Network (ARE-ON), students can engage in information exchange with others anywhere in the world. There are also Research and Extension offices in Lonoke, Newport and Lake Village and collaborations with other colleges and universities in the State through the National Science Foundation funded STEM (Science, Technology, Engineering and Mathematics) Academy. As the second oldest land-grant institution in the state of Arkansas, the mission of this No Excuse University remains the same \u2013 to provide a high quality, affordable education with a personal touch. We invite you to Become a Part of the Pride at the University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process and require reasonable accommodations, please contact Human Resources at 870.575.8400 . Department: Finance & Administration | Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff is accepting applications for an experienced professional for the position of Director of Facilities Planning. Under the direction of the Vice Chancellor for Finance and Administration. This position is responsible for managing and coordinating the maintenance and day-to-day operation of the Facilities Management, institutional services, grounds, and equipment. Qualifications: Bachelor\u2019s degree in business management, industrial maintenance, civil engineering or related field and at least five years experience in building construction or maintenance operations including two years in managerial/supervisory capacity. A Master\u2019s Degree is preferred. Additional Information: Salary Information: $85,000.00 - $110,000.00 Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume, Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants (Please upload all required documents in the \"Resume\" attachment section of your application to be considered for this position) : Recruitment Contact Information: Sharron Williams, Employment Manager, williamss@uapb.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: The University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff may conduct pre-employment background checks on certain positions for applicants being considered for employment. \u00a0 The background checks may include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. \u00a0 Required checks are identified in the position listing. \u00a0 A criminal background check or arrest pending adjudication information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absences of a relationship to the requirements of the position. \u00a0 Background check information will be used in a consistent, non-discriminatory manner consistent with the state and federal law. \u00a0 The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Inpatient-Social-Worker---Behavioral-Health-Service-Line_R0089584-1": {"title": "Inpatient Social Worker - Behavioral Health Service Line", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-07\nPosted: Posted 28 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/07/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | BHSL IP Social Workers Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: * This job posting will select either a Certified Social Worker or Master Social Worker* The Licensed Social Worker in the Behavioral Health Service Line\u2019s adult inpatient units functions in the role of assisting the patient, family, and interdisciplinary team throughout the care episode. Primary duties, in addition to any discharge planning activities, include individual, group, and family therapy to the adult population, communicating with the patients, and assisting in the development of a specific treatment plan that reflects the therapeutic intervention to address the patient\u2019s needs. The Behavioral Health Service Line inpatient units are located in the Psychiatric Research Institute building on the main UAMS campus. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Master's Degree in Social Work Must be licensed by a professional board - Licensed Master Social Worker (LMSW) or Licensed Certified Social Worker (LCSW) Ability to use Microsoft Office programs - Word, Excel, Outlook Preferred Qualifications: Experience in the field of acute, adult mental health Two (2) years of work experience in the behavioral health field Required CPI upon hire; CPR prior to hire Additional Information: Responsibilities: Provide therapeutic interventions through group therapy related to identified patient needs. Provide psychosocial services to include initial assessment upon admission; patient and family education, advocacy, counseling, and interventions with individuals, families, and groups for purposes of assessment and enhancement of problem-solving and coping capacities.\u00a0 Discharge planning and aftercare coordination through community referrals and safety planning \u200b \u00a0 Participate in treatment meetings for the adult units and complex case review meetings as requested and other collaboration in order to develop, plan, and manage the treatment of patients from admission through discharge. Attend team meetings and participate in quality improvement projects. \u00a0 \u200b \u200b \u00a0 Provide accurate and timely documentation of all interactions \u00a0 related \u00a0 to the treatment of the patient. \u00a0 Serve as a consultant for processing guardianship, power of attorney, health care proxy, and advance directives in conformance with UAMS policy May perform other duties as assigned. Physical Demands: Bending - 50% Standing - 60% Speaking - 100% Eyesight - 100% Hearing - 100% Walking - 50% Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/RN-Care-Manager-FT-PT_R0085202-1": {"title": "RN Care Manager FT/PT", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-07\nPosted: Posted 28 Days Ago\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 10/07/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | CORE PA IP Care Management 1 IP C Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The RN Care Manager is responsible for managing the continuum of care for admission through discharge for assigned patients. The role reflects appropriate knowledge of the RN scope of practice, current state requirements, CMS Conditions of Participation, EMTALA, Patient Bill of Rights, AB 1203 and other Federal or State regulatory agency requirements specific to discharge planning. The RN Care Manager partners with the multi-disciplinary team, utilizes scientific evidence for best practices, relevant data and compliance with the Mission and Core Values of UAMS. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications:\u00a0 Baccalaureate Degree in Nursing, ADN, or Diploma RN Degree \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Three (3) years RN experience with current BLS certification Valid Arkansas Registered Nursing License Preferred Qualifications:\u00a0 National Nursing Certification BSN preferred; Certified Case Manager (CCM) or American Case Management (ACM) certification Additional Information: Additional Responsibilities/Competencies: Excellent communication skills Basic computer skills Strong work ethics and accountability\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 Nursing Process: Initiates appropriate referrals to internal and external interdisciplinary teams. Establishes a working diagnosis on every patient at the time of the initial review. Communicates the target length of stay estimated discharge on every patient at the time of the initial review and coordinates the discharge planning process in collaboration with the interdisciplinary team.\u00a0 Documents all team, physician, and patient/family communication and concerns pertaining to coordinating of care and services. Communicates with physicians regarding the level of care or admission status when appropriate criteria are not met for inpatient, observation, or continued stay review. Identifies, intervenes on taking a proactive approach to ensure right time discharges and documents avoidable and denied days and discharge delays. Identifies patients/families with psychosocial and/or non-medical discharge planning needs and refers to the Social Work team member as appropriate. Assesses the patient prior to discharge to determine if the plan is appropriate and makes necessary revisions. Identifies and refers cases appropriate for Ethics Committee consideration. Education/EBP/Research /QI: Participates in Performance Improvement, Evidenced Based Practice/Research process. Systematically evaluates the quality and effectiveness of nursing practice. Supports the integration of current evidence into nursing practices. Promotes an environment conducive to positive educational experience for all students and staff. Provides effective patient/family education (link to PFCC). Communication/Collaboration: Implements POC using an approach that is interdisciplinary with Patient and Family Centered Care. Effectively collaborates and communicates with the multidisciplinary team at all levels. Communicates care appropriately through documentation in the medical record. Reports variances in care/systems/processes through the appropriate means. Leadership: Acts as a resource to others in the performance of duties. Demonstrates a commitment to the personal and professional development of other UAMS employees. Participates in recruitment/retention of staff. Facilitates development and implementation of nursing practice standards that are evidence-based and in compliance with standards. May perform other duties as assigned. Salary Information: \"Commensurate with education and experience\" Required Documents to Apply: List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Proof of Veteran Status, Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Adjunct--Lecturer-Counseling-1_R0089523": {"title": "Adjunct  Lecturer/Counseling-1", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-07\nPosted: Posted 28 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Adjunct Faculty Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Less than Annual Appointment (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Little Rock The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is a metropolitan research university that provides an accessible, quality education through flexible learning and unparalleled internship opportunities. At UA Little Rock, we prepare our more than 8,900 students to be innovators and responsible leaders in their fields. Committed to its metropolitan research university mission, UA Little Rock is a driving force in Little Rock's thriving cultural community and a major component of the city and state's growing profile as a regional leader in research, technology transfer, economic development, and job creation. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . Department: Counseling, Adult, & Rehabilitation Education Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Adjunct Lecturer/Counselor teaches courses within the Counseling and Counselor Education tracks in the Counseling Program housed in the School of Counseling, Human Performance, and Rehabilitation (.25 FTE - 1 class per semester). This position is governed by state and federal laws, and agency/institution policy. Qualifications: Required Education and/or Experience: \u00a0Must have a PhD degree in Counseling or a very closely related field, preferably from a CACREP-accredited program OR a PhD degree in Counselor Education or a very closely related field; May substitute a Master\u2019s degree with 3 years\u2019 experience for fieldwork teaching. Preferred Education and/or Experience:\u00a0 Graduate online teaching experience; Professional experience in the CRC field; Valid state license in applicable field of Counseling. Job Duties and Responsibilities: Teach courses for the Counseling or Counselor Education tracks of the Counseling program in the School of Counseling, Human Performance, and Rehabilitation. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: \u00a0Virtual instruction. Additional Information: Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Curriculum Vitae, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: David Montague - Interim Director; School of Counseling, Human Performance, and Rehabilitation - drmontague@ualr.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: No Background Check Required The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Hearing, Sitting Occasional Physical Activity: Lifting Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Assistant-Professor-of-Management---9-MONTH_R0089401": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Management - 9 MONTH", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-07\nPosted: Posted 28 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Faculty - Tenure/Tenure Track Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Little Rock The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is a metropolitan research university that provides an accessible, quality education through flexible learning and unparalleled internship opportunities. At UA Little Rock, we prepare our more than 8,900 students to be innovators and responsible leaders in their fields. Committed to its metropolitan research university mission, UA Little Rock is a driving force in Little Rock's thriving cultural community and a major component of the city and state's growing profile as a regional leader in research, technology transfer, economic development, and job creation. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . Department: Management, Marketing, & Technology Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Assistant Professor of Management is a 9-month tenure-track position in the Management, Marketing, and Technology department. Responsibilities include teaching required courses per semester. Classes take place in the mornings, at night (1 night/week), and/or online. During summers (subject to funding, department need, and availability) all full-time faculty members, including Instructors, may teach an additional 2 courses for 15% of their 9-month salary, over a 5-week period of time. Serve on University, College, School, and Department committees. Engage with the regional business community. This position is governed by state and federal laws, and agency/institution policy. Qualifications: Required Education and/or Experience: Ph.D. or D.B.A. degree in Management, Organizational Behavior, Human Resource Management, Leadership, or a closely related field from an AACSB-accredited school.\u00a0 Preferred Education and/or Experience:\u00a0 \u00a0N/A Job Duties and Responsibilities: Teach required courses per semester (fall and spring), of which 2 to 3 may be different courses; Classes take place in the mornings, at night (1 night/week), and/or online; During summers (subject to funding, department need, and availability) all full-time faculty members, including Instructors, may teach an additional 2 courses for 15% of their 9-month salary, over a 5-week period of time; Serve on University, College, School, and Department committees; Engage with regional business community; Publish scholarly research; Other duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Teaching experience; Professional work experience supporting teaching assignments; Record of research; Experience in the industry, teaching, and research is preferred. Additional Information: Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Curriculum Vitae, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Yue Zhao; Department Chair of Management, Marketing and Technology; yzhao@ualr.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Hearing Occasional Physical Activity: Kneeling, Lifting Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Helena-Campus/Adjunct-Spanish-Instructor_R0089566-1": {"title": "Adjunct Spanish Instructor", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-06\nPosted: Posted 29 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Adjunct Faculty Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Less than Annual Appointment (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: Phillips Community College of the University of Arkansas The first community college established in Arkansas, Phillips Community College of the University of Arkansas (PCCUA) is a multi-campus, two-year college serving Eastern Arkansas. PCCUA has academic, occupational/technical and continuing education programs and offers over 25 associate degree programs with campuses in DeWitt, Helena-W. Helena and Stuttgart. Thank you for your interest, and we hope you\u2019ll be joining our Ridge Runner family soon! Below you will find the details for the position as well as any specific application requirements you should review before applying for this opening. To apply for this position, please click the Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process, please call Human Resources at (870) 338-6474, ext. 1271. Department: Arts and Sciences - Phillips County Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Responsible for delivering engaging, standards-based instruction in Spanish language and culture while creating a supportive learning environment that promotes student achievement, cultural awareness, and language proficiency in reading, writing, listening, and speaking. Qualifications: Required Qualifications: Fluency in both Spanish and English. Bachelor's degree in related field. Strong communication and interpersonal skills Preferred Qualifications: Master\u2019s degree in Spanish, Latin American studies, or a related field. Past experience teaching at the college level. Additional Information: Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Carol Birth, CBirth@pccua.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check For general application assistance, or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at (870) 338-6474, ext. 1271. PCCUA is committed to providing a safe campus community. We will conduct criminal background checks and a sex offender registry check for applicants seeking employment. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Helena-Campus/Criminal-Justice--Adjunct-Instructor_R0089559": {"title": "Criminal Justice, Adjunct Instructor", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-06\nPosted: Posted 29 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Faculty (Non-Classified) Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Less than Annual Appointment (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: Phillips Community College of the University of Arkansas The first community college established in Arkansas, Phillips Community College of the University of Arkansas (PCCUA) is a multi-campus, two-year college serving Eastern Arkansas. PCCUA has academic, occupational/technical and continuing education programs and offers over 25 associate degree programs with campuses in DeWitt, Helena-W. Helena and Stuttgart. Thank you for your interest, and we hope you\u2019ll be joining our Ridge Runner family soon! Below you will find the details for the position as well as any specific application requirements you should review before applying for this opening. To apply for this position, please click the Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process, please call Human Resources at (870) 338-6474, ext. 1271. Department: Arts and Sciences - Phillips County Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Teach full compliment of courses according to ACTS and course catalog, including but not limited to law enforcement, criminology, corrections and contemporary issues. Courses primarily will be delivered face-to-face, but will also include online options. Assist with recruiting and retention efforts as well as campus and college activities/projects/committees to further the mission of the college. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelors degree in law, criminal justice or closely related field preferred. Experience and ability to conduct coursework online, utilize course delivery platforms such as Blackboard, ability to conduct virtual/online labs and integrate technology into instruction to meet the needs of students from a variety of backgrounds. Preferred Qualifications: Three (3) or more years of teaching experience, preferably in a higher education setting. Experience with Blackboard, Workday and Zoom/Teams a plus. Ability to work in a team setting. Additional Information: Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Carol Birth, CBirth@pccua.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check For general application assistance, or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at (870) 338-6474, ext. 1271. PCCUA is committed to providing a safe campus community. We will conduct criminal background checks and a sex offender registry check for applicants seeking employment. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAMS/Community-Health-Worker-I-III--ACWIH-_R0086748-1": {"title": "Community Health Worker I-III (ACWIH)", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-06\nPosted: Posted 29 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/06/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: COM | OB & GYN ACWIH Programs Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Join the Arkansas Center for Women & Infant Health in an impactful role as a Community Health Worker I-III (CHW)! This position is central to improving health outcomes for women, infants, and families across Arkansas. As a CHW, you will be on the front lines of addressing health disparities, empowering communities, and delivering education and resources tailored to the unique needs of diverse populations. As a CHW, you will work alongside multidisciplinary teams, collaborate with local organizations, and play a pivotal role in creating culturally relevant, community-driven solutions. Whether you're engaging with hard-to-reach populations, delivering group education, or shaping public health responses, your work will directly contribute to healthier communities and stronger families. This tiered position offers opportunities for growth and specialization: Level I: Focuses on direct patient engagement and resource connection. Level II: Coordinates outreach and engagement activities using a community-informed approach to address disparities. Level III: Designs, plans, and delivers outreach materials and interventions as part of a multidisciplinary outreach and implementation team. Level III CHWs also mentor and supervise CHW I and CHW II team members. The CHW role at the Arkansas Center for Women & Infant Health offers an opportunity to make a difference, Apply today and be a catalyst for change! This position will be used to fill multiple vacancies in throughout the state. Applicants must live, have strong connections in these areas, and willing commute daily to one of the following service areas: \u2022 Desha / Chicot \u2022 Scott / Polk \u2022 Garland \u2022 Sebastian \u2022 Crittenden \u2022 Carroll / Boone \u2022 Jackson / Independence / Woodruff \u2022 Sevier Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Level I: High School Diploma/GED Must enroll in a certified CHW Training Program within 45 days of employment Level II: Bachelor's Degree or High School Diploma/GED Completed certified CHW training program Two (2) years experiences as a CHW Mastered all CHW Competencies for Level I Level III: Bachelor's Degree or High School Diploma/GED Requires CHW Certification from ARCHWA or another state (willing to receive ARCWA Certification within 6 months of employment) Mastered all CHW Competencies for Level I & II Four (4) years experiences as a CHW Knowledge, Skills, & Abilities: Reliable transportation, a working cell phone, and internet access are essential. Strong interpersonal and communication skills. Experience in community outreach, public health, or related fields. Ability to mentor and supervise team members (CHW III). Proficiency in case management and group education. Knowledge of health disparities and culturally appropriate outreach strategies. Organizational and multitasking abilities\u00a0 Additional Information: Key Responsibilities: Collaborates with Program Director to ensure that the program meets or exceeds all accreditation requirements. CHW I: Outreach & Recruitment: Conducts outreach to individuals, communities, service providers, and groups Identifies and recruits individuals, families, and community groups to services and systems Educates health and social service systems and providers about community perspectives and cultural norms Facilitates cross-cultural communication among individuals, communities, and health/social service system workers Responsible for the translation and cultural adaptions of resources and educational materials Care Coordination: Coordinates care, provides case management support and assists individuals and communities in navigating health and social service systems Community Coordination: Participates in design, implementation, and interpretation of community-level assessments (e.g. windshield survey of community assets and challenges, community asset mapping) Presents at local agencies and community events to share information and educate individuals and communities about health and social service concerns and resources CHW II (in addition to CHW I responsibilities) Health Education & Clinical Navigation: Motivates and encourages people to obtain care and other services Supports self-management of disease prevention and management of health conditions, including chronic disease Assists individuals in building and expanding their personal capacity to identify and manage their health conditions, obtain services as needed, identify opportunities to help others, and represent their needs through communication and advocacy Provides basic health support services (e.g. first aid, diabetic foot checks) Community Coordination: Assists communities in building capacity by identifying resources, coordinating service and support providers, linking groups or systems that provide synergistic support, and implementing advocacy strategies to address unmet needs Collects and distributes materials that meet basic needs (e.g. provides food, blankets, clothing to those in need) CHW III (in addition to CHW I & II responsibilities) Health Education and Care Coordination: Provides culturally appropriate health education and information. Educates individuals and communities about how to use health and social service systems Conducts health promotion and disease prevention education in a manner that matches linguistic and cultural needs of participants or community Provides individual support and coaching Motivates and encourages people to obtain care and other services Supports self-management of disease prevention and management of health conditions, including chronic disease Assists individuals in building and expanding their personal capacity to identify and manage their health conditions, obtain services as needed, identify opportunities to help others, and represent their needs through communication and advocacy Assists communities in building capacity by identifying resources, coordinating service and support providers, linking groups or systems that provide synergistic support, and implementing advocacy strategies to address unmet needs Coaching & Mentoring: Identifies and works with CHW peers to help others grow professionally, act ethically, and meet the needs of the individuals and communities served Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Hot-Springs/Horticulture-Assistant---Garvan-Woodland-Gardens_R0089385-1": {"title": "Horticulture Assistant \u2013 Garvan Woodland Gardens", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-06\nPosted: Posted 29 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com, then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at all University of Arkansas institutions will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students.\u201d University of Arkansas, Fayetteville students will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Student Jobs at UAF.\u201d All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. Closing Date: 11/06/2026 Type of Position: Staff - Clerical Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas, Fayetteville Founded in 1871, the University of Arkansas is a land grant institution, classified by the Carnegie Foundation among the nation\u2019s top 2 percent of universities with the highest level of research activity. The University of Arkansas works to advance the state and build a better world through education, research, and outreach by providing transformational opportunities and skills, fostering a welcoming climate, and nurturing creativity, discovery, and the spread of new ideas and innovations. The University of Arkansas campus is located in Fayetteville, a welcoming community ranked as one of the best places to live in the U.S. The growing region surrounding Fayetteville is home to numerous Fortune 500 companies and one of the nation\u2019s strongest economies. Northwest Arkansas is also quickly gaining a national reputation for its focus on the arts and overall quality of life. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10% of employee salary. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions, you should review before applying for the opening. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process, please submit a request via the Disability Accommodations | OEOC | University of Arkansas (uark.edu) : Request an Accommodation. Appli\u00adcants are required to submit a request for each position of which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 479.575.5351. Department: Horticulture Operations Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Garvan Woodland Gardens, one of the top attractions in Arkansas is hiring! We are looking for positive, motivated, personable new team members to join our crew. Work outdoors in a setting voted in the top 10 most colorful places on the planet by Trip Advisor. We would love for you to come grow with us! Garvan Woodland Gardens, a 210-acre botanical garden situated on a peninsula surrounded by scenic Lake Hamilton located in Hot Springs, AR is seeking a skilled and dedicated Horticulture Assistant. The Horticulture Assistant will be responsible for weeding, watering, mulching, tilling, raking, planting, removing plantings, and other duties as assigned. This position requires physical work outside year-round. This team member will be expected to work well with others and under the supervision of an experienced staff member. Pay $13-15 per hour based on experience and skill level. Landscape Maintenance Technician is a part-time, temporary position limited to the 1250-hour University of Arkansas policy. The campus is a non-smoking facility. This position requires a valid driver\u2019s license. Some night and weekend work will be required seasonally. Regular, reliable, and non-disruptive attendance is an essential job duty, as is the ability to create and maintain collegial, harmonious working relationships with others. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: High School Diploma or equivalent Valid Driver\u2019s License Background Checks Required: Criminal Background Check, Motor Vehicle Reports Check, Sex Offender Registry Must be able to lift 30 pounds No previous experience required as individuals will be trained on site Preferred Qualifications: Experience working in a public garden Experience with planting, gardening, landscaping, etc. is preferred Formal education in horticulture or a related field Additional Information: Graduate students are subject to background check. Salary Information: $13 - 16 per hour Required Documents to Apply: None Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Recruitment Contact Information: Leslie Pounds, HR Partner, pounds@uark.edu; Minnie Hahn, Sr Manager, minnie@uark.edu; Heather Boyett, Business Coordinator, hd024@uark.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Special Instructions to Applicants: Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Motor Vehicle Reports Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas seeks to attract, develop and retain high quality faculty, staff and administrators that consistently display practices and behaviors to advance a culture that embeds equal opportunity, educational excellence and unparalleled access for all. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All Application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Crouching, Kneeling, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Repetitive Motion, Standing, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Balancing, Feeling, Grasping, Hearing, Lifting, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Stooping, Talking Occasional Physical Activity: Climbing, Crawling, Driving, Sharps, Sitting Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAM--Crossett-Campus/UAM-STA-Education-Specialist-Recruiter_R0089513-1": {"title": "UAM-STA Education Specialist/Recruiter", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-06\nPosted: Posted 29 Days Ago\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Professional Staff - Project/Program Administration Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Monticello UAM, one of twenty campuses of the University of Arkansas System, is located in southeastern Arkansas in the beautiful timberlands, rich in outdoor recreation activities, and approximately 100 miles south of Little Rock. UAM is a comprehensive, residential and commuter, undergraduate institution also offering selected master\u2019s degree programs. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please submit a request via the OEOC website: \u00a0Applicants are required to submit a request for each position to which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 870-460-1422 . Department: College of Technology-Crossett Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Education Specialist/Recruiter for the UAM-STA will be responsible for organizing and scheduling classes to be held through the UAM-STA and will coordinate with multiple agencies, organizations, and schools to recruit workers/students to forestry-related programs and careers. Qualifications: Successful applicant will have obtained a credential in a field related to the Sustainable Trades Alliance, with a bachelor's degree and/or 5 years of experience in the field (or a related field) preferred. Successful applicant should have vast knowledge of the impact of the forestry and manufacturing industries in Arkansas. Organization, collaboration, and ability to manage tasks are key traits for the successful applicant. Knowledge of K-12 career and technical education pathways preferred. Additional Information: Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Resume, Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Dr. Tracy Tucker, Vice Chancellor UAM-CTC (870) 460-2027 tuckerts@uamont.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Child Maltreatment, Criminal Background Check, FBI Background Check, Motor Vehicle Reports Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Driving, Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Balancing, Climbing, Pulling, Pushing Occasional Physical Activity: Crouching, Kneeling, Repetitive Motion Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/APRN---Movement-Disorder-Clinic_R0084932-1": {"title": "APRN - Movement Disorder Clinic", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-06\nPosted: Posted 29 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/06/2026 Type of Position: Clinical Staff - Nursing Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | NUSL Mid-Level Outpatient OP C Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Advanced Practice Nurse will assist the collaborative physician with clinic patients, organizing visits and performing clinic procedures, assist in the procedural room, and answer calls on daily basis for the Interventional Pain subspecialty for evaluation, treatment, and procedures for the Interventional pain patient population. The APRN will be responsible for managing the care of outpatients independently or with the physician, answering telephone inquiries and filling prescriptions, and performing injections. A nurse must have a high level of expertise to perform assessments/diagnosis/treatment of actual/potential problems of patients. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Master's Degree in Nursing (MSN) Current AR APRN License Licensed AR RN License Additional Information: Job Requirements: Assess patients by taking medical histories and performing physical exams Diagnose illnesses and conditions using clinical judgment and diagnostic tests Order and interpret tests (labs, X-rays, etc.) Develop treatment plans based on evidence-based practice Prescribe medications (authority varies by state laws) Provide primary or specialty care (family practice, pediatrics, mental health, etc.) Manage chronic conditions like diabetes or hypertension Treat acute illnesses and injuries Educate patients on disease prevention and healthy lifestyles Work with physicians and healthcare teams (or independently in some states) Supervise or mentor registered nurses (RNs) and support staff Participate in care coordination across services PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS Stand: Frequently Sit: Frequently Walk: Occasionally Bend, crawl, crouch, kneel, stoop or reach overhead: Frequently Lift and carry weight: 25 lbs Push and pull weight: 25 lbs Use hands to touch, handle or feel: Frequently Talk: Continuously Hear: Continuously Taste or smell: Occasionally Read, concentrate, think analytically: Continuously Physical Environment : Inside Medical Facility Environment Noise Level : Moderate Visual Requirements: Color discrimination, Depth perception, Far visual acuity, Near visual acuity Hazards: Biological, Chemical, Dust, Electrical, Fumes/Gases/Odors, Radiation, Sharp objects/tools Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Criminal Background Check, Substance Abuse Testing This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Kneeling, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, N/A, Reaching, Repetitive Motion Frequent Physical Activity: Feeling, N/A, Pulling, Sitting, Standing, Stooping, Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Hope/Recruiter_R0089441-1": {"title": "Recruiter", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-06\nPosted: Posted 29 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Professional Staff - Student Affairs Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas Community College at Hope - Texarkana The University of Arkansas Community College at Hope-Texarkana (UACCHT) is a proud member of the University of Arkansas System.\u00a0 The University of Arkansas System is comprised of land-grant research institutions, a teaching hospital, five community colleges, two schools of law, a presidential school, a residential math and science high school, and an online university, as well as divisions of agriculture, archaeology and criminal justice. These entities exhibit unmatched economic and social impact across the state by providing numerous academic and professional opportunities. Below you will find the details for the position currently available at UACCHT including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.\u00a0 To apply for the position, please click the Apply link/button. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the\u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please submit a request via Email to: wendy.jones@uaht.edu or by phone at 870-722-8176.\u00a0\u00a0 Applicants are required to submit a separate request for each position in which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at wendy.jones@uaht.edu or by phone at 870-722-8176. Department: Enrollment Management Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Recruiter works as a member of the Student Services division reporting to the Dean of Enrollment Management. This position serves as the primary college recruiter and coordinates student recruitment efforts with other student services offices, instructional divisions and the College Relations and Marketing office. ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES 1. Works directly with the Dean of Enrollment Management and the Director of Student Relations in coordinating and implementing the student recruitment activities of the College 2. Maintains effective contacts with area high school counselors, teachers, principals, and prospective students, serving as an information liaison between the College and these persons 3. Coordinates the College\u2019s program of high school visitation and coordinates the College\u2019s representation at all major career days and college nights scheduled by area high schools and other groups within the College\u2019s 26 high school service area 4. Assists prospective students by providing admissions counseling, including applications for admission and financial aid, and other admission areas as they arise 5. Assists advisors with student advisement for undecided majors and/or students who are required to take academic skills courses in preparation for college-level course work 6. Arranges and/or conducts campus tours for prospective students 7. Maintains an accurate record-keeping system of all recruiting activities and efforts for use in evaluating on-going recruiting programs 8. Works cooperatively with other staff members in Student Services, especially the Enrollment Management, Student Relations, Registrar, and Financial Aid offices, and the instructional divisions who are involved in student recruitment 9. Assists in the planning and implementation of Freshman Orientation 10. Serves on College committees as requested by the Dean of Enrollment Management or Vice Chancellor for Student Services. 11. Performs other duties that are deemed necessary by the Dean of Enrollment Management, Vice Chancellor for Student Services or the Chancellor Qualifications: Bachelor Degree Ability to speak Spanish a plus Excellent computer skills required with strong background in Microsoft Office applications Exceptional interpersonal skills with a strong background in written and oral communications Exhibits qualities essential to being a team player Committed to providing exceptional service to students, staff, other educational entities and the public Must be able to work a flexible schedule including some evenings and occasionally on weekends Must hold a valid driver\u2019s license and be eligible to drive a College vehicle Additional Information: Salary Information: $33,500.00 Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume, Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Wendy Jones Director of Human Resources 870-722-8176 All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check The University of Arkansas Community College at Hope-Texarkana (UACCHT) is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check, sex offender registry check, and drug screen. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check and/or a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check.\u00a0 A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Driving, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Standing Frequent Physical Activity: Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Hearing Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAFS--University-of-Arkansas-Fort-Smith/Administrative-Specialist-III---Early-College-Programs_R0089504": {"title": "Administrative Specialist III - Early College Programs", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-06\nPosted: Posted 29 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Clerical Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Fort Smith University of Arkansas \u2013 Fort Smith The University of Arkansas - Fort Smith is a dynamic, mid-sized public university that\u2019s redefining higher education. We\u2019re on a mission to provide transformative, hands-on learning experiences for students of all backgrounds and aspirations. Our multi-faceted approach to education offers a wealth of opportunities, with over 70 academic programs, including certificates, associate, bachelor\u2019s, and master\u2019s degrees. We\u2019re committed to building a diverse community that mirrors Arkansas\u2019s rich tapestry, reflecting our dedication to serving the state\u2019s varied population while enhancing the quality of our institution. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life, and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10 percent of employee salary. \u00a0 Fort Smith, Arkansas Nestled along the Arkansas River, this vibrant city offers a perfect blend of history, culture, and natural beauty. Immerse yourself in the rich heritage of the Old West at the Fort Smith National Historic Site, explore the eclectic local art scene, or take a scenic stroll along the picturesque riverfront trails. With a welcoming community, diverse dining options, and a thriving downtown, Fort Smith is the ideal destination for history enthusiasts and those seeking modern amenities. Thank you for your interest in joining our university. Below you will find details for the position including any supplementary documentation and/or questions you should review before submitting your application. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at (479) 788-7080. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 479-788-7080. Applicants are required to submit a request for each position to which they have applied. Department: Western AR Area Technical Center Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Manage the day-to-day operation of the WATC office by providing technical support, general administrative support, and clerical support functions for the Western Arkansas Technical Center and Early College Programs Works in tandem with the other WATC staff to accomplish departmental goals and to provide support for the director, program coordinator, and program faculty as well as staff at the Peak Innovation Center. This position reports to the Executive Director of Early College Programs. Background and child maltreatment central registry checks are required. This position is a twelve month assignment. Qualifications: Education & Work Experience : This position requires a high school diploma or its equivalent plus three or more years of general administrative experience. Other job related education and/or experience may be substituted for part of these requirements. An associate degree is preferred. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: Performs all phases of reception and clerical duties for the department and for the executive director, including answering phones, greet, direct and provide general information for employees and visitors, typing of documents, student files. This includes assistance in answering phones and greeting visitors at the Peak Innovation Center. Coordinate all purchases and tracking for required instructional and administrative supplies as well as purchases for student licensures. Responsible for a variety of assigned reports, projects, and documentation included in the taking and recording of student attendance and maintains staff calendars. This includes managing daily records of student arrival/departure. Performs data entry and updates concurrent student records in appropriate databases. Responsible for entering mileage and travel needs for faculty, staff and students. Organize details for staff meetings, programs, and other events by arranging times and facilities. Other Duties and Responsibilities: Other duties as assigned. Employees Supervised: \u00a0 None. Education & Work Experience : This position requires a high school diploma or its equivalent plus three or more years of general administrative experience. Other job related education and/or experience may be substituted for part of these requirements. An associate degree is preferred. Other Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: To perform the job successfully, the following competencies are required for the essential functions of this position: Knowledge of the basic policies of the university and student conduct. Problem solving \u2013 Ability to identify and resolve problems in a timely manner; and to gather and analyze information skillfully. Interpersonal skills \u2013 Ability to maintain confidential information with absolute discretion in all matters including staff, student grades, attendance, and discipline. Ability to remain open to other\u2019s ideas and try new things. \u00a0 Communication Skills \u2013 Ability to write and speak clearly and persuasively in positive or negative situations; professional group presentation skills; read and interpret written information. Ability to edit work for accuracy and thoroughness and to monitor own work to ensure quality. Requires STRONG attention to detail.\u00a0 Planning/Organizing \u2013 Ability to prioritize and plan work activities; use time efficiently; and develop realistic action plans. Adaptability \u2013 Ability to adapt to changes in work environment, manage competing demands, and deal with frequent changes, delays or unexpected events. Dependability \u2013 Ability to arrive at work on time, consistently; follow instructions; respond to administrative direction; and solicit feedback to improve performance. Additional Information: Working Relationships: Has frequent contact with faculty, staff, students, regional school districts, and vendors. Special Job Dimensions: Work performed primarily in an office setting and is located at the Peak Innovation Center. Occasional travel required. Occasional lifting of up to 40 pounds. Occasional overtime required. Background Check Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Child Maltreatment Central Registry Check, and Training as a Mandated Reporter for Child Maltreatment. Salary Information: $31,315 Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume, Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: HR 479-788-7080 All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Child Maltreatment, Criminal Background Check, Motor Vehicle Reports Check This position may be subject to a pre-employment criminal background check, sex offender registry check, financial history background check, and/or drug screening. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication and/or adverse financial history alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background checks and drug screening information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: Lifting Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Dental-Assistant---Oral-Health-Clinic_R0086003-1": {"title": "Dental Assistant - Oral Health Clinic", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-06\nPosted: Posted 29 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/06/2026 Type of Position: Other Health Care - Medical Ancillary Support Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | PCPHSL Oral Health Clinical Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Dental Assistant will support dentists during procedures, prepare treatment rooms, sterilize instruments, and provide excellent patient care. The ideal candidate should be organized, have strong communication skills, and be committed to ensuring a comfortable and positive experience for every patient. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: High school diploma/GED PLUS completion of a dental assisting training program AND a minimum of 1 year of experience as a dental assistant. Must be currently licensed/certified in the State of Arkansas as a registered dental assistant Candidates must meet the training and experience qualifications in order to be considered, and are advised to contact the training facility/source to verify accreditation status. Must be trained in four-handed dentistry; Must possess a thorough working knowledge of Current Dental Terminology (CDT) codes, OSHA regulations, and the Arkansas Dental Practice Act. Must possess a permit for the following expanded functions: 1) radiography, 2) coronal polishing, and 3) nitrous oxide administration. Additional Information: Responsibilities: Organize and assist dental hygienists in the delivery of dental procedures in the Oral Health Clinic Guide patients through dental processes before treatment, Educate patients in oral hygiene instruction and provide postoperative instructions Perform assessments that include obtaining and reviewing patient health histories Taking/recording blood pressure and other vital signs Perform appropriate dental charting and treatment documentation in the electronic record Expose and process dental radiographs of diagnostic quality Administer nitrous oxide/oxygen analgesia and monitor sedation cases Perform coronal polishing Perform in-office whitening Perform daily and routine maintenance of dental hygiene equipment as assigned Clean and sterilize dental instruments, supplies, and dental assist units, and maintain Organization and supply ofthe sterilization area Establish and maintain an organized, efficient, cost-effective inventory control system Continually monitoring supply levels and re-ordering by working with athe ssigned purchaser Maintain a stock of daily supplies in all hygiene clinic rooms Review daily schedules and resolve conflicts as necessary Perform a variety of clerical and administrative duties (answer telephones. Make appointments, and other duties as assigned Assist with front desk/business administration duties as assigned Perform duties as assigned. Salary Information: \"Commensurate with education and experience\" Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Other (see special instructions for details), Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Nitrous Certification required Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Adult Maltreatment, Annual TB Screening, Child Maltreatment, Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry, Substance Abuse Testing This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Balancing, Grasping, Hearing, Lifting, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Pulling, Pushing, Sitting, Standing, Stooping, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: Climbing, Crawling, Crouching Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAMS/Child-Development-Technician--Kids-First--Springdale--AR-_R0089520-1": {"title": "Child Development Technician (Kids First, Springdale, AR)", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-06\nPosted: Posted 29 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 10/07/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: COM | Peds Kids First Springdale Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Kids First Springdale, is looking for a Child Development Technician that loves children and wants to help them grow while learning. We need someone who is experienced in providing care and intervention to a group of young children birth to age 5 with developmental delays and special medical needs. Kids First serves children with special healthcare needs ranging in age from six weeks to five years. In our pediatric day healthcare clinics, children diagnosed as having a medical condition known to place them at risk for developmental delays and disabilities receive intensive intervention. Qualifications: High School Diploma or GED PLUS six (6) months experience working in the care of children other education can be substituted for experience including CCOT, CDA, AA, or Bachelor\u2019s degree in Early Childhood Education, Child Development, or a related filed. Candidate must pass state abuse registry checks, drug screen, submit to a TB skin test and required immunizations or provide proof of immunizations. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Strong organizational skills Ability to identify educational and developmental needs of children Ability to establish and maintain positive relationships with parents, staff, and other child care professionals Excellent communication skills Knowledge of early childhood curriculum Additional Information: Responsibilities Provides quality direct patient care for a group of young children including serving mealtimes, assisting with feeding, diapering, and dressing Provides developmentally appropriate behavioral guidance within daily scheduled activities Follows the direction of the ECDS to provide individualized developmental services of their assigned treatment rooms in a manner that is child-centered, family focused, and demonstrates evidence-based or best practice Establishes exciting learning environments for young children and apply curriculum to address the objectives contained in each child\u2019s treatment plan Constant Physical Activity: Feeling, Hearing, Listening Frequent Physical Activity: Climbing, Crawling, Crouching, Grasping, Kneeling, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Repetitive Motion, Standing, Stooping, Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Sitting Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Curriculum Vitae, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Proof of Veteran Status, Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Mammography-Technologist-PRN---Breast-Center_R0088253-1": {"title": "Mammography Technologist PRN - Breast Center", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-06\nPosted: Posted 29 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/11/2026 Type of Position: Clinical Staff - Medical Ancillary Support Job Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | IGSL Mammovan OP C Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Mammography Technologist will be responsible for producing quality images and providing patient care in the UAMS Breast Center. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: High School Diploma, Graduate of a Radiological Technology Program Registered with ARRT Arkansas Radiologic Technologist License. Preferred Qualifications: RT(R) Mammography Registered Additional Information: Responsibilities: Operates specialized radiologic equipment to perform high quality breast imaging exams including mammography and breast ultrasounds. Maintains adequate level of supplies and keeps workspace clean.\u00a0 \u00a0 Communicates mammography exam procedures to patients and enlists patient cooperation in positioning for radiological examination. \u00a0 Provides patient education regarding mammography and breast health. Assists with records management and scheduling appointments. Obtains patient history and enters into Electronic Medical Records (EMR).\u00a0 Schedules exams and reviews pervious records to determine correct studies are performed.\u00a0 Ensures exams are completed and images are in Picture Archiving and Communication (PACS) systems.\u00a0 Enrolls patients in BreastCare Program as appropriate. Maintains knowledge of breast procedures including ultrasound biopsy, stereotactic biopsy, MRI guided biopsy, and needle localizations through continuing education and professional development. Completes other duties as requested. #UAMSRadiology Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Criminal Background Check, Substance Abuse Testing This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Feeling, Hearing, Repetitive Motion Frequent Physical Activity: Balancing, Driving, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting, Talking Occasional Physical Activity: Crawling, Crouching, Kneeling, Lifting, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Stooping Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/RN--Apheresis_R0089493": {"title": "RN- Apheresis", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-05\nPosted: Posted 30 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/05/2026 Type of Position: Clinical Staff - Nursing Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | LPSL CPATH ACC Apheresis Program Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The purpose of this position is to monitor and care for patients during the collection of HPC and during therapeutic plasma exchanges, TP, photopheresis, white blood cell reduction, and platelet reduction. This position will assist the CSM with preparation for FACT inspections, update policies and procedures, analyze quality driven data, provide continuing education to the staff, attend apheresis associated meetings. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Graduate of an accredited Nursing Program with an Associate's Degree, Nursing Diploma, Bachelor's in Nursing, or Master's in Nursing Valid RN License Minimum of 1 year Registered Nursing experience. Preferred Qualifications: 2+ years of experience in apheresis Additional Information: Responsibilities: Collects and documents assessment data from patients and/or others per UAMS standard.\u00a0 Develops patient's Plan of Care (POC) per department/unit standards utilizing assessment data.\u00a0 Evaluates the progress of patients toward attainment of desired outcomes. Administers medication following department/unit standards and Nurse Practice Act.\u00a0 Verifies and evaluates care delivered to ensure it is consistent with patient and family centered care principles, practice standards and regulatory requirements. Supports the integration of current evidence into nursing practices.\u00a0 Promotes an environment conducive to positive educational experience for all students and staff.\u00a0 Provides effective patient/family education/discharge planning. Effectively collaborates and communicates with nursing staff at all levels, interdisciplinary teams, executive leaders, and other stakeholders.\u00a0 Communicates care appropriately through documentation in the medical record. Reports variances in care/ systems/ processes through the appropriate means.\u00a0 Participates in recruitment/retention of staff.\u00a0 Facilitates development and implementation of nursing practice standards that are evidence-based and in compliance with ANA standards. May perform other duties as assigned. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Criminal Background Check, Substance Abuse Testing This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding Frequent Physical Activity: Feeling, Grasping, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Repetitive Motion, Sharps, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Crouching, Kneeling, Lifting, Stooping Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Pharmacy-Technician-IV---Ambulatory-Pharmacy_R0089460-1": {"title": "Pharmacy Technician IV - Ambulatory Pharmacy", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-05\nPosted: Posted 30 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/05/2026 Type of Position: Clinical Staff - Medical Ancillary Support Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: PTSL Ambulatory Pharmacy (Central) Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Under the direct supervision of the Manager of Pharmacy for Ambulatory Care, the Clinical Pharmacy Technician (Ambulatory Operational and Patient Assistance) will have primary responsibility for supervising and coordinating operational assistance within clinics in the Integrated Medicine Service Line (IMSL) and/or the Primary Care and Population Health Service Line (PCPHSL). This position is an upper-level technician position. The employee in this position must demonstrate special skills, knowledge, and task completion not required by the other pharmacy technicians. The programs to be coordinated and monitored include, but are not limited to, MAP (Medication Assistance Program), retail drug PAPs (free drug), prior authorizations, and Medicare assistance/enrollment. This position will support operations ensuring patients receive the lowest out-of-pocket expense possible utilizing assistance from various programs, PBMs, and manufacturers. This includes, but is not limited to, researching data, connecting patients with appropriate assistance, assisting in applications, processing prescriptions, and communicating with billing and patient follow-up. Additionally, the Pharmacy Technician will work directly with a clinical pharmacy specialist to coordinate operational tasks within the clinic(s), including, but not limited to, obtaining information and coordination of care with external facilities and aiding in transitions of care. The Pharmacy Technician IV will work with pharmacy leadership to maintain and improve program workflows, expansion, and compliance. In addition to these duties, they may perform the duties of the Pharmacy Technician I/II/III, including assisting the pharmacists in day-to-day operations, patient outreach, and other facets of patient care. The Pharmacy Technician IV will prioritize work based on immediate need and changing workload. They will work as a team member to perform day-to-day work efficiently and accurately, along with any additional tasks or projects to help achieve departmental goals. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: HS/GED plus 4 yrs Pharmacy Tech Experience (i.e., previous lead technician in a sterile compounding setting, etc.) or a Bachelor's Degree in Pharmaceutical Sciences; 1 year to obtain ASHP/ACPE accredited technician training or certificate program; National Technician Certification (PTCB); Arkansas Pharmacy Technician Licensure Within one year of start date, will complete a specialized certificate program in sterile compounding (i.e., ASHP or PTCB) Preferred Qualifications: B.S. or higher degree ASHP/ACPE accredited technician training Previous sterile compounding experience, hazardous drug handling, etc. Previous management or team leader experience Specialized certificate or certification (i.e., PTCB Certified Compounded Sterile Preparation Technician, ASHP Sterile Compounding Certificate, 340B Certification, etc.) Additional Information: Responsibilities: Oversees day-to-day pharmacy operations, including entering prescription orders, operating the point-of-sale system, and providing customer service. Supervises pharmacy staff, including technicians, volunteers, and students. Hires, trains, evaluates, and administers human resources functions for direct reports. Provides patient support by conducting bedside deliveries and preparing intravenous medications as needed. Collaborates with department leadership to support initiatives including planning for future programs and services, patient and staff safety, and operational improvements. Manages the controlled substance storage and distribution program in compliance with all federal and state laws regarding controlled substances. Performs other duties as needed. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Criminal Background Check, Substance Abuse Testing This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Feeling, Grasping, Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Repetitive Motion, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Crouching, Kneeling, Lifting, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Stooping Occasional Physical Activity: Balancing, Climbing, Crawling, Crouching Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/North-Little-Rock/Fiscal-Support-Specialist---Cashier_R0089307": {"title": "Fiscal Support Specialist - Cashier", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-05\nPosted: Posted 30 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 11/30/2026 Type of Position: Accounting, Finance, Business Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas Pulaski Technical College University of Arkansas - Pulaski Technical College at North Little Rock is an integral part of the Arkansas Technical and Community College System maintained by the State of Arkansas. The college is governed by the University of Arkansas System Board of Trustees and a seven-member Board of Visitors and derives its support largely from student tuition and fees and legislative appropriations. UA - Pulaski Tech, a comprehensive two-year college, offers associate degree and certificate programs for students who plan to transfer to four-year colleges and universities and/or for career preparation and advancement. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply link/button. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at (501) 812-2839. Department: Cashiers (SO902553) Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Fiscal Support Specialist -Cashier is responsible for receipting and posting payments for tuition/fees and miscellaneous charges to student accounts. The primary location for this position will be at the Main Campus in North Little Rock. Generally Accepted Accounting Principles, state and federal laws and institution policy, govern this position. Qualifications: Essential Duties and Responsibilities: Provides excellent customer service to students, employees, and visitors in person and on the phone Provides information, assistance, and clarification regarding student accounts Works with a high level of initiative and concern for excellence Maintains confidentiality in all student account matters in accordance with the Family Educational Rights and Privacy Act (FERPA) Reconciles cash receipts daily Maintains manual and computerized files, reviews files for accuracy and corrects information as needed Scans, imports, and retrieves documents to/from imaging system Assists with accounts receivables as needed/assigned Verifies and disburses financial aid funds to students Files and maintains cashier reports Performs other duties as assigned Knowledge, Abilities, and Skills: Knowledge of customer service techniques Knowledge of database accounting and management principles Knowledge of computers and software applications Knowledge of applicable laws and regulations of assigned section Ability to record fiscal data and manipulate data to generate complex reports and documents Ability to conduct research and compile data into report form Ability to maintain filing systems accurately Ability to communicate both orally and in writing Ability to handle multiple tasks and meet deadlines in a fast paced environment Ability to receive constructive criticism and work on a fast paced team Qualifications Minimum Education and/or Experience: The formal education equivalent of a high school diploma; plus two years of bookkeeping, basic accounting, billing, or related experience. Preferred Education and/or Experience: Associates Degree with three years of experience in customer service, bookkeeping, basic accounting, billing, or related experience. OTHER JOB RELATED EDUCATION AND/OR EXPERIENCE MAY BE SUBSTITUTED FOR ALL OR PART OF THESE BASIC REQUIREMENTS, EXCEPT FOR CERTIFICATION OR LICENSURE REQUIREMENTS, UPON APPROVAL OF THE QUALIFICATIONS REVIEW COMMITTEE. Additional Information: Salary Information: $30,576.00 Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants Recruitment Contact Information: Human Resources humanresources@uaptc.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Motor Vehicle Reports Check, Sex Offender Registry University of Arkansas - Pulaski Technical College is committed to providing a safe campus community. Title IX protects the college community from sexual harassment in a school's education programs and activities. This means that Title IX protects the college community in connection with all academic, educational, extracurricular, athletic, and other programs of the school, whether those programs take place in a school's facilities, in college transportation, at a class or training program sponsored by the school at another location, or elsewhere. \u00a0 We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Repetitive Motion, Sitting, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Kneeling, Lifting, Stooping Occasional Physical Activity: Pulling, Pushing Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Lab-Support-Technician-II--Gross-Room_R0089427-1": {"title": "Lab Support Technician II- Gross Room", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-05\nPosted: Posted 30 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/05/2026 Type of Position: Other Health Care - Clinical Support Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Shift Vary (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | LPSL APATH Gross Room Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Lab Support Technician II will be expected to perform clerical duties including, but not limited to, triaging phone calls, triaging specimens, assigning identification numbers to specimens along with patient name and specimen type, reviewing, verifying, and logging all incoming consultation cases from outside facilities into the UAMS system, and verifying patient status, insurance coverage and proper authorizations prior to services. The LST II is responsible for collecting patient information and data within regulation as well as guaranteeing patient identification throughout every process. The LST II works to support other staff members and the department as needed. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: High School diploma or GED equivalent and two (2) years of experience as a Lab Tech or Assistant in a Clinical Laboratory or 60 hours of completed higher education in a health sciences program Additional Information: Responsibilities: Accessioning specimen outreach and Surgical Pathology. Verifying correct insurance for each patient. Clerical work for Gross Department. Triage all calls made to gross lab. Customer service: Assist clinics looking for results. Correcting incorrect patient information. Fulfilling any requests outside clinics may need, i.e. supplies, requisitions, etc. Maintaining a clean and organized area. Other duties as assigned. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Criminal Background Check, Substance Abuse Testing This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting, Talking Occasional Physical Activity: Kneeling, Lifting, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Stooping, Walking Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Groundskeeper_R0082065-2": {"title": "Groundskeeper", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-05\nPosted: Posted 30 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/05/2026 Type of Position: Professional Staff - Facilities Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: OPS | Campus Operation Landscape Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Under direction of the UAMS Landscape Manager, this position is responsible for maintaining the landscaping and grounds maintenance for the the healthcare, education, and research facilities on the UAMS Campus. This position is also responsible for assisting with all problems and/or emergencies relating to facility issues on the UAMS Campus. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: High School Diploma/GED plus 1 year of experience in Landscaping and/or schooling in the trade Valid AR Driver's license with fewer than 12 points on their Motor Vehicle Record Basic computer experience required Additional Information: Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Criminal Background Check This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Feeling, Hearing, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Crawling, Crouching, Kneeling, Reaching, Sitting, Standing, Stooping, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Medical-Laboratory-Scientist-II---Blood-Bank_R0089430-1": {"title": "Medical Laboratory Scientist II - Blood Bank", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-05\nPosted: Posted 30 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/05/2026 Type of Position: Clinical Staff - Medical Ancillary Support Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Shift Vary (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | LPSL CPATH Transfusion Service Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The MLS II position is an important role within the Blood Bank department that assists with validations, quality control performance, staff safety training, inventory management, and LIS support. This position collaborates closely with the Blood Bank Supervisor in order to maintain day-to-day operations. This position will also focus on improving patient outcomes by performing advanced blood banking techniques, dispensing blood and blood components, and educating students. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor degree in Medical Technology, Medical Laboratory Sciences, Chemistry, or Biology 2 years of experience in a clinical laboratory setting ASCP Certification or equivalent \u00a0 Preferred Qualifications: Knowledge of LIS configuration and support, Laboratory Safety Officer, Validations, Staff Training and Education, Performance of Quality Control Previous blood bank or transfusion medicine experience Additional Information: Responsibilities: Provide direct patient care by supplying the patient with appropriate blood \u00a0components\u00a0 Perform ABO/Rh, IAT, DAT, antibody identification, \u00a0crossmatching units of blood, and running the\u00a0automated ABO/RH, IAT equipment Wash red blood cells and platelets Perform platelet crossmatching and platelet antibody identification Perform daily reagent QC and equipment preventive maintenance \u00a0 Issue blood and blood components to the floors\u00a0 Understand the importance of massive trauma and to issue blood and blood components as set\u00a0forth in the Massive Transfusion Protocol Communicate effectively with the blood bank customers including physicians, nurses, and other\u00a0UAMS staff members Receive samples and to ensure all samples are appropriately labeled and collected properly for the\u00a0Blood Bank Assist in training of new staff and students Maintain competency and train on all revised and new policy/procedures in a timely manner\u00a0 Report any deviation from standard operating procedures to the supervisor in a timely manner Perform daily reagent QC and equipment preventive maintenance with 100% accuracy. Assist with\u00a0performance of quarterly, semi-annual, and annual quality control May perform other duties as assigned. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status, Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Criminal Background Check, Substance Abuse Testing This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Standing, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Crawling, Crouching, Feeling, Kneeling, Reaching, Sitting, Stooping, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAM--Monticello-Campus/Assistant-Softball-Coach_R0089398-1": {"title": "Assistant Softball Coach", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-04\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Professional Staff - Assistant Coach Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Monticello UAM, one of twenty campuses of the University of Arkansas System, is located in southeastern Arkansas in the beautiful timberlands, rich in outdoor recreation activities, and approximately 100 miles south of Little Rock. UAM is a comprehensive, residential and commuter, undergraduate institution also offering selected master\u2019s degree programs. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please submit a request via the OEOC website: \u00a0Applicants are required to submit a request for each position to which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 870-460-1422 . Department: Athletics Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Duties include assisting in the implementation and management of all phases of a competitive NCAA Division II women\u2019s softball program in accordance with NCAA, Great American Conference, and University regulations including coaching, recruiting, scheduling, traveling, managing budget, supervising athletes, fund-raising, promoting and monitoring academic progress of student athletes, and part-time teaching in the area of health and physical education. Other duties may be assigned by the Head Coach. Physical education class instruction is an expectation in a variety of traditional classes. Qualifications: Baccalaureate degree is required, Master\u2019s degree is preferred. Knowledge of NCAA and Great American Conference bylaws, commitment to the academic success of student athletes, and the ability to organize and motivate student athletes to maximum performance level. A competitive background in college, high school, and/or junior college coaching with teaching experience preferred. The ability to work, communicate, and develop rapport with students, faculty, administration, alumni, community groups, and media required. Additional Information: Salary Information: Required Documents to Apply: Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Balancing, Climbing, Crawling, Crouching, Driving, Feeling, Grasping, Hearing, Kneeling, Lifting, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Repetitive Motion, Sharps, Sitting, Standing, Stooping, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Balancing, Climbing, Crawling, Crouching, Driving, Feeling, Grasping, Hearing, Kneeling, Lifting, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Repetitive Motion, Sharps, Sitting, Standing, Stooping, Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Balancing, Climbing, Crawling, Crouching, Driving, Feeling, Grasping, Hearing, Kneeling, Lifting, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Repetitive Motion, Sharps, Sitting, Standing, Stooping, Talking, Walking Benefits Eligible:"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAM--McGehee-Campus/Non-Student-Extra-Help--Adult-Education--for-Correctional-Facility-in-Pine-Bluff_R0089342-1": {"title": "Non-Student Extra Help (Adult Education) for Correctional Facility in Pine Bluff", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-04\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Clerical Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Monticello UAM, one of twenty campuses of the University of Arkansas System, is located in southeastern Arkansas in the beautiful timberlands, rich in outdoor recreation activities, and approximately 100 miles south of Little Rock. UAM is a comprehensive, residential and commuter, undergraduate institution also offering selected master\u2019s degree programs. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please submit a request via the OEOC website: \u00a0Applicants are required to submit a request for each position to which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 870-460-1422 . Department: Adult Education Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: This teaching position will be at the Juvenile Correctional Facility in Pine Bluff. Must hold a current Ar teaching license. Responsibilities: This individual is responsible for instructing classes, developing lesson plans and other instructional material, assisting with coordinating classes, maintaining student records, performing involved office duties requiring critical thinking skills and independent judgment, provide assistance to centers lead teachers. The Workforce Ed Instructor is responsible for all aspects of the Adult Education program. Duties include, but are not limited to: \u00b7 Schedule all students for the TABE test. \u00b7 Monitor student\u2019s attendance and advise teachers on when students should post-test. \u00b7 Schedule all TABE test for students. \u00b7 Administer all TABE test for students. \u00b7 Schedule all GED ready test for students. \u00b7 Administer all GED ready test for students. \u00b7 Schedule all GED test. \u00b7 Performing all student intakes. \u00b7 Adding new students to DRC. \u00b7 Producing reports from DRC. \u00b7 Creating and maintaining student files. \u00b7 Entering data accurately into LACES. \u00b7 Regular work attendance is a must! \u00b7 Attend all mandated state meetings. \u00b7 Conduct faculty & staff professional development. Qualifications: Qualifications: The formal education equivalent to an associate\u2019s degree with intentions of getting Bachelor\u2019s within two years. Preferred qualification of bilingual (Spanish and English). Salary: Commensurate with education and experience including excellent fringe benefits. (Contingent upon availability of funds) Additional Information: Salary Information: $20.00-$22.00/hour Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Dr. Dorissa Kaufman Director of Adult Education Kaufmand@uamont.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Motor Vehicle Reports Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Crouching, Grasping, Hearing, Kneeling, Lifting, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Repetitive Motion, Sitting, Standing, Stooping, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Crouching, Feeling, Grasping, Hearing, Kneeling, Lifting, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Repetitive Motion, Sitting, Standing, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Balancing, Climbing, Crawling, Talking Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Skilled-Trades-Helper_R0089343": {"title": "Skilled Trades Helper", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-04\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 11/30/2026 Type of Position: Skilled Labor Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas Pulaski Technical College University of Arkansas - Pulaski Technical College at North Little Rock is an integral part of the Arkansas Technical and Community College System maintained by the State of Arkansas. The college is governed by the University of Arkansas System Board of Trustees and a seven-member Board of Visitors and derives its support largely from student tuition and fees and legislative appropriations. UA - Pulaski Tech, a comprehensive two-year college, offers associate degree and certificate programs for students who plan to transfer to four-year colleges and universities and/or for career preparation and advancement. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply link/button. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at (501) 812-2839. Department: Maintenance Operations Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Skilled Trades Helper performs duties in one or more of the following skilled trades: HVAC mechanics, plumbing, electrical, carpentry, painting, or grounds maintenance. General Responsibilities: \u2022Provide grounds maintenance by way of mowing, trimming of trees, bushes, and other ground debris. Assist and train under supervision in a variety of skilled trades duties, such as carpentry; installation of electrical wiring, electrical fixtures, and computer cable lines; assembly, installation, and repairing of air, gas, water, and waste disposal systems, according to specifications and plumbing codes; and inspections, preventive maintenance, and repairs of boilers, air compressors, and related equipment. \u2022 Checks hallways, stairways, and other public areas for non-working lights, and changes out any ballasts, transformers, fuses, or switches. \u2022 May provide assistance to painters, plasterers, or welders in preparing surfaces for repair and/or re-finishing. \u2022 Regular, reliable, and non-disruptive attendance is an essential job duty, as is the ability to create and maintain collegial, harmonious working relationships with others. \u2022 Performs other duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities: \u2022 Knowledge of basic measuring tools, equipment, and materials used in the various skilled trades. \u2022 Ability to perform manual labor under various working conditions. \u2022 Ability to use hand and power tools in various working conditions. \u2022 Completion of sufficient education or training to read and write. \u2022 Ability to understand and follow oral and written instructions. \u2022 Ability to communicate information and ideas in various environments. \u2022 Skilled in the use, operation, and care of tools and machinery. Position schedule: Monday through Friday Minimal overtime. Qualifications: Required Qualifications: \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 The formal education equivalent of a high school diploma \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 At least 18 years of age \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Valid Driver's License \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Must be able to lift, push, and pull 50lbs. \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 One year experience in chosen trade area. Education may be substituted for experience.\u00a0 \u00a0 Preferred Qualifications: \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Experience working and/or assisting an Electrician, Plumber, HVAC Technician or Mechanic \u00a0 Additional Information: Salary Information: $31,200 Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants Recruitment Contact Information: Human Resources humanresources@uaptc.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: University of Arkansas - Pulaski Technical College is committed to providing a safe campus community. Title IX protects the college community from sexual harassment in a school's education programs and activities. This means that Title IX protects the college community in connection with all academic, educational, extracurricular, athletic, and other programs of the school, whether those programs take place in a school's facilities, in college transportation, at a class or training program sponsored by the school at another location, or elsewhere. \u00a0 We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Grasping, Hearing, Kneeling, Lifting, Pulling, Pushing, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAPBCORBINCorbin-Hall/Administrative-Specialist-III---University-College_R0088921": {"title": "Administrative Specialist III - University College", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-04\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Clerical Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff The University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff is an 1890 Land-Grant HBCU with a diverse student population, competitive degree offerings and stellar faculty. For more than 140 years, the University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff has worked to create an environment that inculcates learning, growth and productivity while affording a basic need to its students \u2013 a chance to advance. The 15:1 student to teacher ratio makes it possible to maintain a learning environment with close interaction between students and faculty while challenging curricula encourage our students to seek and fulfill their potential. You can excel in your chosen field of study through a curriculum of \u00a0 Certificate and Associates degree programs,\u00a0 more than thirty\u00a0 Undergraduate programs, Master\u2019s degree programs and a Doctorate program in Aquaculture/Fisheries. You can also develop workplace readiness through internships, co-ops and fellowships in the U.S. and abroad. Out-of-class experiences and student involvement include more than 90 student organizations, an internationally renowned Vesper Choir, Marching Band, Concert Bands, Wind Symphony, nationally recognized debate team, award-winning theater department and accomplished athletic program. Though the main campus is in Pine Bluff, its reach is worldwide. UAPB has an extended campus in North Little Rock and offers as well as online courses. With the addition of the Arkansas Research and Education Optical Network (ARE-ON), students can engage in information exchange with others anywhere in the world. There are also Research and Extension offices in Lonoke, Newport and Lake Village and collaborations with other colleges and universities in the State through the National Science Foundation funded STEM (Science, Technology, Engineering and Mathematics) Academy. As the second oldest land-grant institution in the state of Arkansas, the mission of this No Excuse University remains the same \u2013 to provide a high quality, affordable education with a personal touch. We invite you to Become a Part of the Pride at the University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process and require reasonable accommodations, please contact Human Resources at 870.575.8400 . Department: Student and Faculty Success | Center for Student Success and Academic Excellence | Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Administrative Specialist III is responsible for coordinating office activities and managing Workday requisitions and related tasks for the Division of University College. This role requires flexibility, the ability to maintain confidentiality, work both independently and as part of a team, and to work efficiently and productively. May require travel to other campus locations as needed. General Responsibilities: - Research, prepare, examine, and verify documents and special reports, as well as develop, revise, and recommend administrative policies and procedures as directed by the Dean. - Ensure that supplies and equipment are ordered and delivered in a timely manner and recorded properly in Workday. - Maintain meeting minutes as needed, schedule meetings, and follow up for advisory committee meetings and other activities. - Assist with the AA degree application process. - Collaborate with procurement and finance for equipment and supply orders. - Perform other duties as assigned. Qualifications: Required Requirements Associate\u2019s degree or higher 1-2 years of experience in an administrative role with increasing responsibilities. Demonstrates professionalism and exceptional customer service skills Team oriented Proficient in MS Word, Excel, and PowerPoint Displays a positive attitude and effective written and oral communication skills. Prepares spreadsheets, documents, reports, and presentations. Excellent organizational skills and attention to detail Provides clerical and administrative support to supervisory and professional staff. Serves as administrative manager for Dean's office. Works with students to ensure their needs are met regarding referrals, paperwork assistance, advisement appointments, etc. Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor's degree Professional administration experience in a higher education environment. 2-3 years of experience in an administrative role with increasing responsibilities Experience working in a higher education environment Additional Information: Salary Information: $35,000 Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants (Please upload all required documents in the \"Resume\" attachment section of your application to be considered for this position) : Recruitment Contact Information: Sharron Williams Employment Manager williamssm@uapb.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check The University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff may conduct pre-employment background checks on certain positions for applicants being considered for employment. \u00a0 The background checks may include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. \u00a0 Required checks are identified in the position listing. \u00a0 A criminal background check or arrest pending adjudication information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absences of a relationship to the requirements of the position. \u00a0 Background check information will be used in a consistent, non-discriminatory manner consistent with the state and federal law. \u00a0 The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-Arkansas-at-Pine-Bluff/Extra-Help-Skilled-Tradesman-2_R0089305": {"title": "Extra Help Skilled Tradesman-2", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-04\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Skilled Labor Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff The University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff is an 1890 Land-Grant HBCU with a diverse student population, competitive degree offerings and stellar faculty. For more than 140 years, the University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff has worked to create an environment that inculcates learning, growth and productivity while affording a basic need to its students \u2013 a chance to advance. The 15:1 student to teacher ratio makes it possible to maintain a learning environment with close interaction between students and faculty while challenging curricula encourage our students to seek and fulfill their potential. You can excel in your chosen field of study through a curriculum of \u00a0 Certificate and Associates degree programs,\u00a0 more than thirty\u00a0 Undergraduate programs, Master\u2019s degree programs and a Doctorate program in Aquaculture/Fisheries. You can also develop workplace readiness through internships, co-ops and fellowships in the U.S. and abroad. Out-of-class experiences and student involvement include more than 90 student organizations, an internationally renowned Vesper Choir, Marching Band, Concert Bands, Wind Symphony, nationally recognized debate team, award-winning theater department and accomplished athletic program. Though the main campus is in Pine Bluff, its reach is worldwide. UAPB has an extended campus in North Little Rock and offers as well as online courses. With the addition of the Arkansas Research and Education Optical Network (ARE-ON), students can engage in information exchange with others anywhere in the world. There are also Research and Extension offices in Lonoke, Newport and Lake Village and collaborations with other colleges and universities in the State through the National Science Foundation funded STEM (Science, Technology, Engineering and Mathematics) Academy. As the second oldest land-grant institution in the state of Arkansas, the mission of this No Excuse University remains the same \u2013 to provide a high quality, affordable education with a personal touch. We invite you to Become a Part of the Pride at the University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process and require reasonable accommodations, please contact Human Resources at 870.575.8400 . Department: Agriculture, Fisheries & Human Science Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Perform general carpentry work, including framing, decking, siding, and finishing carpentry. Install, repair, and replace roofing systems (shingles, metal, flat roofs, etc.). Measure, cut, and shape materials according to specifications. Inspect roofs and structures for damage and recommend repairs. Install flashing, gutters, and related roofing components. Follow blueprints, building plans, and safety regulations Maintain tools, equipment, and clean job sites Communicate effectively with team members Qualifications: Proven experience as a carpenter and/or roofer (3+ years preferred) Strong knowledge of roofing systems and carpentry techniques Ability to read blueprints and technical drawings Proficient with hand and power tools Ability to work at heights and in various weather conditions Strong attention to detail and craftsmanship Valid driver\u2019s license and reliable transportation OSHA certification (preferred but not required) Physical Requirements Ability to lift 50+ pounds Comfortable climbing ladders and working on rooftops Ability to stand, bend, kneel, and work for extended periods Additional Information: Salary Information: $20-$24 hourly temporary position Required Documents to Apply: List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants (Please upload all required documents in the \"Resume\" attachment section of your application to be considered for this position) : Recruitment Contact Information: Sharron Williams All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Motor Vehicle Reports Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff may conduct pre-employment background checks on certain positions for applicants being considered for employment. \u00a0 The background checks may include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. \u00a0 Required checks are identified in the position listing. \u00a0 A criminal background check or arrest pending adjudication information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absences of a relationship to the requirements of the position. \u00a0 Background check information will be used in a consistent, non-discriminatory manner consistent with the state and federal law. \u00a0 The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAFS--University-of-Arkansas-Fort-Smith/Director--Center-for-Business-and-Professional-Development_R0089285-1": {"title": "Director, Center for Business and Professional Development", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-04\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Professional Staff - Project/Program Administration Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Fort Smith University of Arkansas \u2013 Fort Smith The University of Arkansas - Fort Smith is a dynamic, mid-sized public university that\u2019s redefining higher education. We\u2019re on a mission to provide transformative, hands-on learning experiences for students of all backgrounds and aspirations. Our multi-faceted approach to education offers a wealth of opportunities, with over 70 academic programs, including certificates, associate, bachelor\u2019s, and master\u2019s degrees. We\u2019re committed to building a diverse community that mirrors Arkansas\u2019s rich tapestry, reflecting our dedication to serving the state\u2019s varied population while enhancing the quality of our institution. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life, and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10 percent of employee salary. \u00a0 Fort Smith, Arkansas Nestled along the Arkansas River, this vibrant city offers a perfect blend of history, culture, and natural beauty. Immerse yourself in the rich heritage of the Old West at the Fort Smith National Historic Site, explore the eclectic local art scene, or take a scenic stroll along the picturesque riverfront trails. With a welcoming community, diverse dining options, and a thriving downtown, Fort Smith is the ideal destination for history enthusiasts and those seeking modern amenities. Thank you for your interest in joining our university. Below you will find details for the position including any supplementary documentation and/or questions you should review before submitting your application. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at (479) 788-7080. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 479-788-7080. Applicants are required to submit a request for each position to which they have applied. Department: Center for Economic Development Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Reporting directly to the Associate Vice Chancellor for Economic and Workforce Development, the Director of the Center for Business & Professional Development leads and manages the Center for Business & Professional Development (CBPD). CBPD provides noncredit professional development, customized training, contract training, and open enrollment learning opportunities for regional employers, community partners, and individuals. The Director is responsible for program leadership, employer engagement, faculty and staff supervision, revenue generation, budget administration, customer service, and alignment with the mission of the University of Arkansas - Fort Smith and the Center for Economic Development. Qualifications: Required Education and/or Work Experience: Master\u2019s degree in business, management, leadership, education, workforce development, organizational development, or a related field. Five or more years of progressive experience in business, industry, workforce development, professional development, higher education, nonprofit leadership, or a closely related field. Demonstrated leadership, budget management, customer relationship, and oral and written communication skills. Other job-related education and/or experience may be substituted for part of these requirements. Preferred Education and/or Work Experience: Doctorate or additional graduate/professional degree from an accredited institution. More than five years of progressive leadership experience in business, industry, higher education, workforce development, professional development, or nonprofit leadership. Experience with customized training, revenue generation, grants, contracts, marketing, sales, business development, event management, employer engagement, and profit/loss or budget responsibility. Essential Job Duties and Responsibilities: Strategic Leadership and Program Development: \u2022 Lead, manage, and advance CBPD as a primary noncredit business and professional development training unit within the Center for Economic Development. \u2022 Develop annual business, budget, marketing, and operational plans for CBPD that are consistent with UAFS priorities and the strategic direction of the Center for Economic Development. \u2022 Establish short- and long-term goals that support CBPD\u2019s mission, promote regional workforce capacity, and strengthen the financial sustainability of the center. \u2022 Use employer feedback, regional workforce data, participant evaluations, and financial performance measures to assess program effectiveness and identify new training opportunities. Employer Engagement and Training Solutions: \u2022 Build and maintain strong relationships with regional employers, chambers of commerce, economic development organizations, workforce partners, nonprofit organizations, and community stakeholders. \u2022 Lead employer needs assessments and develop responsive customized training solutions, proposals, and delivery models for business and industry clients. \u2022 Identify, coordinate, and evaluate open enrollment professional development opportunities that meet the needs of individuals, employers, and the broader community. \u2022 Represent CBPD and UAFS at community events, employer meetings, professional association meetings, and other workforce and economic development activities. Faculty, Staff, and Instructor Oversight: \u2022 Supervise assigned CBPD faculty, staff, instructors, contractors, and related program personnel. \u2022 Work with faculty and instructors to establish individual performance, program, and financial goals; meet regularly to monitor progress and support continuous improvement. \u2022 Recruit, hire, onboard, and retain qualified faculty, instructors, and staff who support CBPD\u2019s training mission and customer service expectations. \u2022 Set high standards of performance, conduct regular performance evaluations, and encourage professional development for faculty and staff. Financial, Contract, and Grant Administration: \u2022 Develop, monitor, and manage the CBPD budget, including revenue targets, expenses, net revenue, and financial performance for open enrollment and customized training activities. \u2022 Oversee the contract, invoicing, registration, and customer service processes for open enrollment, customized training, and contract training programs. \u2022 Identify, pursue, and administer grants, contracts, sponsorships, and other funding sources that support training efforts and expand access to workforce development opportunities. \u2022 Ensure compliance with university policies, grant and contract requirements, fiscal procedures, and applicable local, state, and federal requirements. Collaboration and Communication: \u2022 Maintain regular communication with the Associate Vice Chancellor for Economic and Workforce Development regarding CBPD operations, opportunities, challenges, financial performance, and strategic priorities. \u2022 Establish effective working relationships with other UAFS departments and colleges to support interdisciplinary programming, employer engagement, and regional service. \u2022 Collaborate with state and regional organizations, including workforce boards, economic development agencies, and training assistance programs, to support monetary training assistance for employers and participants. \u2022 Maintain a positive work atmosphere by acting and communicating in a manner that fosters teamwork, professionalism, accountability, and service to internal and external customers. Other Job Duties and Responsibilities: \u2022 Attend and participate in required faculty, staff, administrative, university, commencement, and community events as appropriate. \u2022 Maintain consistent and timely attendance and fulfill other duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: To perform the job successfully, the following competencies are required for the essential functions of this position: \u2022 Knowledge of professional development, customized training, workforce development, business operations, budget management, marketing, sales, and customer relationship management. \u2022 Ability to lead faculty and staff, manage multiple projects, build partnerships, evaluate program effectiveness, and use data to support decision-making. \u2022 Strong communication, organization, prioritization, problem-solving, and teamwork skills. \u2022 Ability to work effectively with diverse employers, participants, faculty, staff, students, community partners, and public agencies. Additional Information: Working Relationships: The Director of the Center for Business & Professional Development reports directly to the Associate Vice Chancellor for Economic and Workforce Development. The position involves frequent contact with university faculty and staff, regional employers, community leaders, workforce partners, public agencies, professional associations, and the general public. The Director must maintain positive collaboration with regional employers in business and industry and effective working relationships with UAFS colleges and departments. List Employees Supervised : Assigned CBPD faculty, staff, instructors, contractors, and related program personnel. Special Job Dimensions: Work is performed primarily in an office, classroom, training, and event setting. The position requires frequent meetings and occasional travel for employer visits, community events, conferences, and out-of-town activities. Extended hours, evening, or weekend work may occasionally be required. While performing the duties of this job, the employee regularly uses a computer and other office technology, communicates verbally and in writing, and may sit or stand for extended periods. The employee may occasionally lift materials up to 10 pounds. Background Check Requirements : Criminal Background Check and Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) Check. Position requires employee to complete Arkansas Mandated Reporter training prior to employment. This job description is not designed to contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties, and/or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time with or without notice. Salary Information: $90,000 - $95,000/year, commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume, Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Full consideration will be given to applications received by August 31, 2026. Recruitment Contact Information: HR 479-788-7080 All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Motor Vehicle Reports Check This position may be subject to a pre-employment criminal background check, sex offender registry check, financial history background check, and/or drug screening. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication and/or adverse financial history alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background checks and drug screening information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Hearing Frequent Physical Activity: Talking Occasional Physical Activity: Walking Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAMS/Child-Development--Technician--Kids-First--Pine-Bluff-_R0086682-1": {"title": "Child Development  Technician (Kids First, Pine Bluff)", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-04\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/05/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: COM | Peds Kids First Pine Bluff Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Make a Difference Where It Matters Most! \u2728This position is in Pine Bluff , AR. KIDS FIRST is a compassionate, child-centered program dedicated to serving children with special healthcare needs from six weeks to five years old. Within our pediatric day healthcare clinics, children for with developmental delays and other special medical needs receive intensive, nurturing, and individualized early developmental services\u2014setting the foundation for lifelong growth and success. About the Role: Child Development Technician: In this hands-on and rewarding role, the Child Development Technician partners closely with the Early Childhood Development Specialist to provide daily care, support, and developmental interventions for children from birth to age five with special medical and developmental needs. This position is perfect for someone who is: *Passionate about early childhood development *Caring, patient, and energetic *Motivated to positively impact children and families \ud83c\udf1f Why Join KIDS FIRST? Because here, your work isn\u2019t just a job it\u2019s a calling. Every day, you help children grow, thrive, and reach their full potential which truly changes lives. Kids First serves children with special healthcare needs ranging in age from six weeks to five years. In our pediatric day healthcare clinics, children diagnosed as having a medical condition known to place them at risk for developmental delays and disabilities receive intensive intervention. Qualifications: High School Diploma or GED PLUS six (6) months experience working in the care of children other education can be substituted for experience including CCOT, CDA, AA, or Bachelor\u2019s degree in Early Childhood Education, Child Development, or a related filed. Candidate must pass state abuse registry checks, drug screen, submit to a TB skin test and required immunizations or provide proof of immunizations. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Strong organizational skills Ability to identify educational and developmental needs of children Ability to establish and maintain positive relationships with parents, staff, and other child care professionals Excellent communication skills Knowledge of early childhood curriculum Additional Information: Responsibilities Provides quality direct patient care for a group of young children including serving mealtimes, assisting with feeding, diapering, and dressing. Provides developmentally appropriate behavioral guidance within daily scheduled activities. Follows the direction of the ECDS to provide individualized developmental services of their assigned treatment rooms in a manner that is child-centered, family focused, and demonstrates evidence-based or best practice. Establishes exciting learning environments for young children and apply curriculum to address the objectives contained in each child\u2019s treatment plan. Constant Physical Activity: Feeling, Hearing, Listening Frequent Physical Activity: Climbing, Crawling, Crouching, Grasping, Kneeling, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Repetitive Motion, Standing, Stooping, Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Sitting Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Proof of Veteran Status, Resume, Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Alma/Program-Associate---12-MONTH_R0089173-1": {"title": "Program Associate - 12 MONTH", "description": "Start date: 2026-08-04\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 08/22/2026 Type of Position: Researchers Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: Division of Agriculture of the University of Arkansas The University of Arkansas System Division of Agriculture is a state wide campus, with faculty based on University campuses, at Research and Extension Centers and in every Arkansas county. It consists of the Arkansas Agricultural Experiment Station (AES) and the Arkansas Cooperative Extension Service (CES), and is home to more than 1400 employees.\u00a0 The Division was established in 1959 and is headed by the Vice-President for Agriculture.\u00a0 The Division headquarters is located in Little Rock with the rest of the University of Arkansas System Administration.\u00a0 As an employer, the University of Arkansas System Division of Agriculture offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance.\u00a0 Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process and require reasonable accommodations, please contact the Division's Office of Program & Employment Compliance at compliance@uada.edu . For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-671-2219 or 479-502-9820. Department: VGSS | Vegetable Research Station Department's Website: https://aaes.uada.edu/research-locations/vegetable-research-station/ Summary of Job Duties: The Program Associate reports to the Resident Director in Charge of the Vegetable Research Station. Duties and responsibilities of the Program Associate are managing and carrying out all facets of field plot research to include equipment operation, plot planning, soil preparation, planting, spraying, irrigation, maintenance, harvesting, recording, and detailed record keeping of all activities on the Research Station. Duties involve the direct supervision of classified and seasonal hourly employees. Oversee the maintenance of equipment and facilities. Work closely with project leaders from various Departments on campus and the Cooperative Extension Service. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications\nB.S. Degree in Horticulture or related field plus three years of experience OR an M.S. Degree in Horticulture or related field.\n\nKnowledge, Skills & Abilities\nKnowledge of statistical analysis of field plot data. Oversee the maintenance of equipment and facilities. Must have a demonstrated ability for written and oral presentations of research work and communication skills. Additional Information: Salary Information: $46,000/year Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Christina Boren Administrative Support Supervisor cml015@uark.edu or (479) 474-0475 All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Motor Vehicle Reports Check The University of Arkansas System Division of Agriculture may conduct pre-employment background checks on certain positions for applicants being considered for employment. \u00a0 The background checks may include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. \u00a0 Required checks are identified in the position listing. \u00a0 A criminal background check or arrest pending adjudication information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absences of a relationship to the requirements of the position. \u00a0 Background check information will be used in a consistent, non-discriminatory manner consistent with the state and federal law. \u00a0 The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Crouching, Feeling, Grasping, Sitting Occasional Physical Activity: Driving, Hearing, Lifting, Standing, Stooping Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Fayetteville-AR/Assistant-Associate-Full-Professor--Open-Rank----Criminal-Practice-Clinic_R0088927-2": {"title": "Assistant/Associate/Full Professor (Open Rank) - Criminal Practice Clinic", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-31\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com, then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at all University of Arkansas institutions will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students.\u201d University of Arkansas, Fayetteville students will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Student Jobs at UAF.\u201d All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. Closing Date: Type of Position: Faculty - Tenure/Tenure Track Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas, Fayetteville Founded in 1871, the University of Arkansas is a land grant institution, classified by the Carnegie Foundation among the nation\u2019s top 2 percent of universities with the highest level of research activity. The University of Arkansas works to advance the state and build a better world through education, research, and outreach by providing transformational opportunities and skills, fostering a welcoming climate, and nurturing creativity, discovery, and the spread of new ideas and innovations. The University of Arkansas campus is located in Fayetteville, a welcoming community ranked as one of the best places to live in the U.S. The growing region surrounding Fayetteville is home to numerous Fortune 500 companies and one of the nation\u2019s strongest economies. Northwest Arkansas is also quickly gaining a national reputation for its focus on the arts and overall quality of life. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10% of employee salary. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions, you should review before applying for the opening. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process, please submit a request via the Disability Accommodations | OEOC | University of Arkansas (uark.edu) : Request an Accommodation. Appli\u00adcants are required to submit a request for each position of which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 479.575.5351. Department: Dean of Law Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The University of Arkansas School of Law is pleased to announce that it is currently seeking applicants for a 9-month, 100% appointed, tenure/tenure track assistant, associate or full professor (based on qualifications) starting in the 2027-2028 academic year to teach the Criminal Practice Clinic. The candidate selected for this position will be expected to direct and teach the Criminal Practice Clinic each semester. They will supervise student law practice, teach the clinic seminar, manage the clinic\u2019s docket, and provide students regular feedback, including through weekly supervision meetings. They will also collaborate with other faculty and clinic staff on matters related to administration of the clinical program. In addition to teaching, faculty who teach in the clinical program also engage fully in scholarship and service at the law school. Candidates must have a J.D. degree from an ABA accredited law school and must demonstrate a commitment to excellence in teaching and mentoring students. Applicants must demonstrate an excellent record of scholarship or, at the entry level, a strong potential for scholarship. Successful candidates will also show a commitment to service within and outside the University. Lateral candidates are encouraged to apply. The University of Arkansas School of Law offers an environment in which faculty can thrive. We place a premium on teaching excellence and are deeply committed to our students\u2019 academic and professional success. At the same time, our faculty engage in scholarship that is shaping law and policy on the state, national, and global levels. The faculty\u2019s breadth of experience in government service, public interest law, private practice, and other areas of academic study ensures a vibrant intellectual life for students and faculty alike. We seek new colleagues who will meaningfully contribute to this community. The University of Arkansas-Fayetteville is the flagship campus of the University of Arkansas. It is a land grant institution, and is committed to providing the highest levels of public education in service to the State of Arkansas. Located in the northwest corner of the state, Fayetteville is at the heart of a rapidly growing metropolitan area that boasts a dynamic economy, a vibrant cultural community, and world-class outdoor recreation, in a region that regularly championed as a \u201cbest place to live.\u201d The region also offers many opportunities to do meaningful work and to engage in partnerships across campus as well as with community and other organizations across the state, country, and world.\u202f This is an in-person position. Most University classes are offered face-to-face and this role requires regular on-campus presence to support high-quality instruction and student learning. Participation in selected departmental or programmatic activities that advance teaching quality and student success is also expected. Regular, reliable, and non-disruptive attendance is an essential job duty, as is the ability to create and maintain collegial, harmonious working relationships with others. Rank: Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Professor will depend on the level of experience. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: J.D. from an ABA-accredited law school A distinguished academic record Demonstrated scholarly promise A law license and two years of legal experience Eligible for admission to the Arkansas bar Experience teaching, mentoring or supervising law students, legal interns, or attorneys Preferred Qualifications: Tenure-track teaching experience, experience as a visiting law professor or fellow, or one or more years of other clinical teaching experience Three or more years of practical legal experience Additional Information: Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Curriculum Vitae, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title) Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Recruitment Contact Information: Rachel Whitman Leslie Pounds All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Special Instructions to Applicants: Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas seeks to attract, develop and retain high quality faculty, staff and administrators that consistently display practices and behaviors to advance a culture that embeds equal opportunity, educational excellence and unparalleled access for all. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All Application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAMS/LPN--UAMS-FMC-Fort-Smith-_R0087376-1": {"title": "LPN (UAMS FMC Fort Smith)", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-31\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 10/03/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: REP | PCPHSL CS West Fort Smith Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: We are seeking a skilled Licensed Practical Nurse (LPN) to join our team at UAMS Fort Smith Family Medical Center. This position plays a vital role in providing direct patient care under the supervision of a Registered Nurse, contributing to the assessment, planning, implementation, and evaluation of nursing care for a select group of patients. This role is ideal for individuals who are compassionate, detail-oriented, and committed to delivering exceptional patient care in a dynamic healthcare environment. If you are eager to contribute to a team dedicated to excellence in family medicine, we encourage you to apply. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications High School, GED, or formal educational equivalent. Graduate of an accredited Licensed Practical Nurse program. One (1) year of work experience in clinical nursing Current Arkansas Licensed Practical Nurse license Current CPR certification Knowledge, Abilities, and Skills: Strong clinical knowledge and technique. Knowledge of basic medical terminology required Strong patient advocacy and patient education skills.\u00a0 Attention to communication, oral, written, and persuasive. Must be able to build collaborative relationships. Possess personal credibility. Ability to make independent judgments that have highly significant impacts on the organization. Ability to provide motivational support to the area of responsibility. Strong customer service orientation. Intermediate computer skills. Professional and courteous telephone etiquette. General knowledge of office machines, including printers, fax machines, and scanners. Preferred Qualifications Two (2) years of work experience in a clinical environment with direct patient care Associates Degree in Nursing. Good working knowledge of the state immunization registry, care manager. PCMH experience and care management experience. Additional Information: Key Responsibilities: Direct patient care within the limits of the Nurse Practice Act of the State of Arkansas, UAMS policies, procedures, and standards. Accountable for adhering to UAMS care guidelines. Observe patients, charting, and reporting changes in patients\u2019 conditions. Provide basic care and treatment of patients. Administer prescribed medications and start intravenous fluids. Measure and record the patient\u2019s vital signs. Assist patients in standing, walking, bathing, dressing, and moving in bed. Supervise nurses\u2019 aides and assistants. Answer the patient\u2019s call and determine how to assist them. Collect samples such as blood, urine, and sputum from patients and perform routine laboratory tests on samples. Clean rooms and make beds. Inventory and requisition supplies and instruments. Record food and fluid intake and output. Models the Core Values of UAMS \u2013 Integrity, Respect, Diversity, Teamwork, Creativity, and Excellence in compliance with company guidelines. Performs related responsibilities as required or assigned. *This position will be used to fill multiple vacancies.* Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of five Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Fayetteville-AR/Assistant-Associate-Full-Professor-of-Law--Open-Rank-_R0088939-2": {"title": "Assistant/Associate/Full Professor of Law (Open Rank)", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-31\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com, then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at all University of Arkansas institutions will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students.\u201d University of Arkansas, Fayetteville students will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Student Jobs at UAF.\u201d All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. Closing Date: Type of Position: Faculty - Tenure/Tenure Track Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas, Fayetteville Founded in 1871, the University of Arkansas is a land grant institution, classified by the Carnegie Foundation among the nation\u2019s top 2 percent of universities with the highest level of research activity. The University of Arkansas works to advance the state and build a better world through education, research, and outreach by providing transformational opportunities and skills, fostering a welcoming climate, and nurturing creativity, discovery, and the spread of new ideas and innovations. The University of Arkansas campus is located in Fayetteville, a welcoming community ranked as one of the best places to live in the U.S. The growing region surrounding Fayetteville is home to numerous Fortune 500 companies and one of the nation\u2019s strongest economies. Northwest Arkansas is also quickly gaining a national reputation for its focus on the arts and overall quality of life. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10% of employee salary. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions, you should review before applying for the opening. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process, please submit a request via the Disability Accommodations | OEOC | University of Arkansas (uark.edu) : Request an Accommodation. Appli\u00adcants are required to submit a request for each position of which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 479.575.5351. Department: School of Law Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The University of Arkansas School of Law is pleased to announce that it is currently seeking applicants for a 9-month, 100% appointed, tenure/tenure track assistant, associate or full professor (based on qualifications) starting in the 2027-2028 academic year. The successful candidate will teach courses aligned with the needs of the School of Law and its students. Candidates must have a J.D. degree from an ABA accredited law school and must demonstrate a commitment to excellence in teaching and mentoring students. Applicants must demonstrate an excellent record of scholarship or, at the entry level, a strong potential for scholarship. Successful candidates will also show a commitment to service within and outside the University. Lateral candidates are encouraged to apply. The University of Arkansas School of Law offers an environment in which faculty can thrive. We place a premium on teaching excellence and are deeply committed to our students\u2019 academic and professional success. At the same time, our faculty engage in scholarship that is shaping law and policy on the state, national, and global levels. The faculty\u2019s breadth of experience in government service, public interest law, private practice, and other areas of academic study ensures a vibrant intellectual life for students and faculty alike. We seek new colleagues who will meaningfully contribute to this community. The University of Arkansas-Fayetteville is the flagship campus of the University of Arkansas. It is a land grant institution, and is committed to providing the highest levels of public education in service to the State of Arkansas. Located in the northwest corner of the state, Fayetteville is at the heart of a rapidly growing metropolitan area that boasts a dynamic economy, a vibrant cultural community, and world-class outdoor recreation, in a region that regularly championed as a \u201cbest place to live.\u201d This is an in-person position. Most University classes are offered face-to-face and this role requires regular on-campus presence to support high-quality instruction and student learning. Participation in selected departmental or programmatic activities that advance teaching quality and student success is also expected. Regular, reliable, and non-disruptive attendance is an essential job duty, as is the ability to create and maintain collegial, harmonious working relationships with others. Rank: Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Professor will depend on the level of experience. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications JD degree from an ABA-accredited law school or an international law degree A distinguished academic record Demonstrated scholarly promise Preferred Qualifications A law license and two years of practical legal experience Tenure-track teaching experience or experience as a visiting assistant professor or fellow Additional Information: Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Curriculum Vitae, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title) Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Recruitment Contact Information: Rachel Whitman Leslie Pounds All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Special Instructions to Applicants: Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas seeks to attract, develop and retain high quality faculty, staff and administrators that consistently display practices and behaviors to advance a culture that embeds equal opportunity, educational excellence and unparalleled access for all. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All Application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Fayetteville-AR/Assistant-Associate-Full-Professor-of-Law--Open-Rank----Legal-Research---Writing_R0089117-1": {"title": "Assistant/Associate/Full Professor of Law (Open Rank) \u2013 Legal Research & Writing", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-31\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com, then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at all University of Arkansas institutions will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students.\u201d University of Arkansas, Fayetteville students will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Student Jobs at UAF.\u201d All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. Closing Date: Type of Position: Faculty - Tenure/Tenure Track Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas, Fayetteville Founded in 1871, the University of Arkansas is a land grant institution, classified by the Carnegie Foundation among the nation\u2019s top 2 percent of universities with the highest level of research activity. The University of Arkansas works to advance the state and build a better world through education, research, and outreach by providing transformational opportunities and skills, fostering a welcoming climate, and nurturing creativity, discovery, and the spread of new ideas and innovations. The University of Arkansas campus is located in Fayetteville, a welcoming community ranked as one of the best places to live in the U.S. The growing region surrounding Fayetteville is home to numerous Fortune 500 companies and one of the nation\u2019s strongest economies. Northwest Arkansas is also quickly gaining a national reputation for its focus on the arts and overall quality of life. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10% of employee salary. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions, you should review before applying for the opening. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process, please submit a request via the Disability Accommodations | OEOC | University of Arkansas (uark.edu) : Request an Accommodation. Appli\u00adcants are required to submit a request for each position of which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 479.575.5351. Department: School of Law Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The University of Arkansas School of Law is pleased to announce that it is currently seeking applicants for a 9-month, 100% appointed, tenure/tenure track assistant, associate or full professor (based on qualifications) starting in the 2027-2028 academic year to teach Legal Research and Writing. The candidate selected for this position will be expected to develop and deliver instruction in legal analysis, objective and persuasive writing, legal research methodologies, and oral advocacy. They will provide individualized feedback to students, evaluate written assignments, and collaborate with other legal writing faculty to ensure consistency and excellence across courses. Each legal writing faculty member works with two sections of 15-18 students during the fall and spring semesters. Candidates must have a J.D. degree from an ABA accredited law school and must demonstrate a commitment to excellence in teaching and mentoring students. Applicants must demonstrate an excellent record of scholarship or, at the entry level, a strong potential for scholarship. Successful candidates will also show a commitment to service within and outside the University. Lateral candidates are encouraged to apply. The University of Arkansas School of Law offers an environment in which faculty can thrive. We place a premium on teaching excellence and are deeply committed to our students\u2019 academic and professional success. At the same time, our faculty engage in scholarship that is shaping law and policy on the state, national, and global levels. The faculty\u2019s breadth of experience in government service, public interest law, private practice, and other areas of academic study ensures a vibrant intellectual life for students and faculty alike. We seek new colleagues who will meaningfully contribute to this community. The University of Arkansas-Fayetteville is the flagship campus of the University of Arkansas. It is a land grant institution, and is committed to providing the highest levels of public education in service to the State of Arkansas. Located in the northwest corner of the state, Fayetteville is at the heart of a rapidly growing metropolitan area that boasts a dynamic economy, a vibrant cultural community, and world-class outdoor recreation, in a region that regularly championed as a \u201cbest place to live.\u201d This is an in-person position. Most University classes are offered face-to-face and this role requires regular on-campus presence to support high-quality instruction and student learning. Participation in selected departmental or programmatic activities that advance teaching quality and student success is also expected. Regular, reliable, and non-disruptive attendance is an essential job duty, as is the ability to create and maintain collegial, harmonious working relationships with others. Rank: Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Professor will depend on the level of experience. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: J.D. degree from an ABA-accredited law school or international law degree A distinguished academic record Demonstrated scholarly promise Preferred Qualifications: Tenure-track teaching experience or experience as a visiting law professor or fellow A law license and two years of legal experience Additional Information: Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Curriculum Vitae, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title) Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Recruitment Contact Information: Rachel Whitman Leslie Pounds All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Special Instructions to Applicants: Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas seeks to attract, develop and retain high quality faculty, staff and administrators that consistently display practices and behaviors to advance a culture that embeds equal opportunity, educational excellence and unparalleled access for all. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All Application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Fayetteville-AR/Assistant-Associate-Full-Professor-of-Law--Open-Rank-_R0088929-1": {"title": "Assistant/Associate/Full Professor of Law (Open Rank)", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-31\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com, then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at all University of Arkansas institutions will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students.\u201d University of Arkansas, Fayetteville students will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Student Jobs at UAF.\u201d All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. Closing Date: Type of Position: Faculty - Tenure/Tenure Track Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas, Fayetteville Founded in 1871, the University of Arkansas is a land grant institution, classified by the Carnegie Foundation among the nation\u2019s top 2 percent of universities with the highest level of research activity. The University of Arkansas works to advance the state and build a better world through education, research, and outreach by providing transformational opportunities and skills, fostering a welcoming climate, and nurturing creativity, discovery, and the spread of new ideas and innovations. The University of Arkansas campus is located in Fayetteville, a welcoming community ranked as one of the best places to live in the U.S. The growing region surrounding Fayetteville is home to numerous Fortune 500 companies and one of the nation\u2019s strongest economies. Northwest Arkansas is also quickly gaining a national reputation for its focus on the arts and overall quality of life. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10% of employee salary. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions, you should review before applying for the opening. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process, please submit a request via the Disability Accommodations | OEOC | University of Arkansas (uark.edu) : Request an Accommodation. Appli\u00adcants are required to submit a request for each position of which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 479.575.5351. Department: School of Law Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The University of Arkansas School of Law is pleased to announce that it is currently seeking applicants for a 9-month, 100% appointed, tenure/tenure track assistant, associate or full professor (based on qualifications) starting in the 2027-2028 academic year with teaching duties divided between its signature LL.M. Program in Agricultural and Food Law and JD Program. For the LL.M. program courses, there is a strong interest in agriculture and the environment. Candidates must have a J.D. degree from an ABA-accredited law school and must demonstrate a commitment to excellence in teaching and mentoring students. Applicants must demonstrate an excellent record of scholarship or, at the entry level, a strong potential for scholarship. Successful candidates will also show a commitment to service within and outside the University. Lateral candidates are encouraged to apply. The University of Arkansas School of Law offers an environment in which faculty can thrive. We place a premium on teaching excellence and are deeply committed to our students\u2019 academic and professional success. At the same time, our faculty engage in scholarship that is shaping law and policy on the state, national, and global levels. The faculty\u2019s breadth of experience in government service, public interest law, private practice, and other areas of academic study ensures a vibrant intellectual life for students and faculty alike. We seek new colleagues who will meaningfully contribute to this community. The University of Arkansas-Fayetteville is the flagship campus of the University of Arkansas. It is a land grant institution, and is committed to providing the highest levels of public education in service to the State of Arkansas. Located in the northwest corner of the state, Fayetteville is at the heart of a rapidly growing metropolitan area that boasts a dynamic economy, a vibrant cultural community, and world-class outdoor recreation, in a region that regularly championed as a \u201cbest place to live.\u201d This is an in-person position. Most University classes are offered face-to-face and this role requires regular on-campus presence to support high-quality instruction and student learning. Participation in selected departmental or programmatic activities that advance teaching quality and student success is also expected. Regular, reliable, and non-disruptive attendance is an essential job duty, as is the ability to create and maintain collegial, harmonious working relationships with others. Rank: Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Professor will depend on the level of experience. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications JD degree from an ABA-accredited law school or an international law degree A distinguished academic record Demonstrated scholarly promise Preferred Qualifications A law license and two years of practical legal experience Tenure-track teaching experience or experience as a visiting assistant professor or fellow Additional Information: Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Curriculum Vitae, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title) Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Recruitment Contact Information: Rachel Whitman Leslie Pounds All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Special Instructions to Applicants: Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas seeks to attract, develop and retain high quality faculty, staff and administrators that consistently display practices and behaviors to advance a culture that embeds equal opportunity, educational excellence and unparalleled access for all. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All Application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAMS/Biochemistry-Research-Staff-Opportunities--Evergreen-_R0089111-1": {"title": "Biochemistry Research Staff Opportunities (Evergreen)", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-31\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/30/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: COM | Biochemistry & Molecular Admin Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Department of Biochemistry and Molecular Biology is seeking dedicated research professionals to support laboratory operations and research projects. Positions are available at multiple levels, with the working title determined by the selected candidate\u2019s education and directly related experience. Research personnel will conduct experiments, collect and analyze data, maintain laboratory equipment, and assist with reporting research findings. Higher-level positions may lead research activities and train students or other research personnel. Qualifications: Position titles are assigned based on education and experience. Minimum education and work requirements are: Research Technician, High School or GED Research Technologist, Baccalaureate Degree Research Assistant I, Baccalaureate Degree, one year directly related work experience Research Assistant II, Baccalaureate Degree, two years directly related work experience Research Assistant III, Baccalaureate Degree, three years directly related work experience Research Associate I, Baccalaureate Degree, four years directly related work experience Research Associate II, Baccalaureate Degree, five years directly related work experience Research Associate III, Baccalaureate Degree, six years directly related work experience Knowledge, Skills & Abilities: Strong analytical and problem-solving skills. Excellent attention to detail. Effective organizational and presentation skills. Ability to follow research protocols and maintain accurate records. Ability to work independently and collaboratively. Strong written and verbal communication skills for higher-level positions. This position is a Designated Research Position and is regulated by the Arkansas Research Education Protection Act of 2025. Prior to issuance of an offer of employment, the University is required to request and obtain additional information about an applicant\u2019s background and, if required, conduct an additional review of that background information Additional Information: Responsibilities Conduct research and assist with laboratory projects under the direction of researchers or scientists. Perform laboratory tests and experiments. Collect, record, organize, and analyze research data. Prepare research materials and organize samples. Maintain laboratory equipment and supplies. Follow established research protocols and safety requirements. Assist with reports, presentations, and research findings. Support daily laboratory operations. Lead assigned research activities and train research personnel, as appropriate for higher-level positions. Perform other duties as assigned. \u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Feeling, Hearing Frequent Physical Activity: Crawling, Crouching, Kneeling, Lifting, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Standing, Stooping, Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Sitting \u00a0 Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Curriculum Vitae, Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Director-of-Alumni-Engagement_R0089249": {"title": "Director of Alumni Engagement", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-30\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Alumni Relations Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Little Rock The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is a metropolitan research university that provides an accessible, quality education through flexible learning and unparalleled internship opportunities. At UA Little Rock, we prepare our more than 8,900 students to be innovators and responsible leaders in their fields. Committed to its metropolitan research university mission, UA Little Rock is a driving force in Little Rock's thriving cultural community and a major component of the city and state's growing profile as a regional leader in research, technology transfer, economic development, and job creation. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . Department: Alumni Relations Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Director of Alumni Engagement serves as the University's chief relationship builder for more than 150,000 former students and alumni, creating meaningful opportunities for individuals to reconnect with the institution and with one another. Reporting to the Associate Vice Chancellor for Alumni and Development, this position executes the strategic plan for alumni engagement by identifying emerging markets, cultivating volunteer leaders, developing innovative programs, and building partnerships that strengthen lifelong connections between former students, alumni, and the University. As the University enters its second century of service, the Director expands alumni engagement beyond traditional programming by meeting former students and alumni where they live, work, and lead. This position actively seeks opportunities to engage graduates in growing communities across Arkansas and across the nation, celebrating their professional accomplishments while connecting them to the people, programs, and possibilities shaping the University's future. Serving as the primary staff liaison to the Alumni Board of Directors, the Director works collaboratively with development officers, academic leadership, students, volunteers, and campus partners to transform pride in UA Little Rock into meaningful engagement, advocacy, volunteerism, mentorship, and philanthropic investment. The Director is charged with moving the needle on alumni engagement by creating meaningful opportunities, success in this role is measured not simply by the number of programs delivered or events hosted, but by the number of meaningful relationships created, strengthened, and sustained. Through data-informed strategies, innovative programming, regional outreach, volunteer leadership, and strategic partnerships, the Director continually expands the University's network of engaged alumni while deepening the quality of those relationships over time. This position actively identifies underserved alumni populations, emerging markets, geographic regions, industries, and affinity groups, developing targeted engagement strategies that broaden the University's reach and increase participation. The Director believes alumni engagement is about far more than planning events it is about creating relationships that endure across generations. The Director works to open eyes in both directions helping former students and alumni better understand the innovation, research, student success, and momentum shaping their alma mater today, while helping the University recognize, celebrate, and engage the extraordinary accomplishments of its graduates. By strengthening these connections, the Director develops a growing network of engaged ambassadors whose professional success reflects the University's impact and whose continued involvement advances its mission. Working closely with the Director of Alumni, Corporate/Foundation Relations, the National Director of Development, and the University's development team, the Director ensures alumni engagement efforts support the identification, cultivation, and stewardship of prospective donors and volunteer leaders. Every alumni interaction is viewed as an opportunity to deepen relationships, strengthen affinity, identify future philanthropic partners, and advance the University's strategic priorities. Through vision, initiative, and relationship-building, the Director will help shape an alumni engagement program that inspires lifelong connection and positions UA Little Rock for an even stronger second century of service. This position is governed by state and federal laws, and agency/institution policy. Qualifications: Required Education and/or Experience Bachelor's degree from an accredited institution; Three years of professional experience in alumni relations, advancement, development, fundraising, volunteer management, higher education, nonprofit management, or a related field. Preferred Education and/or Experience Demonstrated experience building relationships with diverse constituencies; Experience coordinating programs, projects, volunteer initiatives, or fundraising activities; Master's degree; Experience in higher education advancement, alumni relations, annual giving, or fundraising; Experience working with volunteer boards, advisory councils, or alumni organizations; Experience conducting donor discovery, qualification, or solicitation activities; Experience utilizing CRM systems for constituent engagement and reporting. Job Duties and Responsibilities Alumni Engagement and Relationship Development Develop and implement strategies to increase alumni engagement and participation across the University's alumni community, including affinity-based constituencies such as Donaghey Scholars, former student-athletes, fraternity and sorority alumni, and other priority alumni groups; Develop targeted engagement plans for key alumni affinity groups that strengthen lifelong relationships, expand volunteer leadership, increase event participation, and create pathways for philanthropic support; Identify, cultivate, and maintain relationships with alumni across diverse constituencies; Conduct a minimum of ten (10) meaningful face-to-face visits each week with alumni to cultivate lifelong relationships, increase alumni engagement, identify volunteer leaders, discover philanthropic interests, and strengthen the University's culture of philanthropy; Represent the University at alumni, community, and campus events; Maintain accurate records of alumni interactions and engagement activities within the University's CRM system. Alumni Event Engagement Collaborate with the Director of Alumni, Corporate/Foundation Relations to develop engagement strategies for alumni events and programs; Develop engagement opportunities and programming that encourage participation from priority alumni affinity groups, including Donaghey Scholars, former student-athletes, fraternity and sorority alumni, and other identified constituencies; Identify target alumni audiences and support outreach efforts to increase participation. Utilize alumni events to cultivate relationships, recruit volunteers, identify prospective donors, and strengthen alumni affinity; Coordinate alumni engagement activities associated with University events and initiatives; Evaluate event participation data and engagement outcomes to inform future strategies. Alumni Board Management Serve as the primary staff liaison to the Alumni Board of Directors; Coordinate board meetings, committee meetings, and related activities; Assist with the recruitment, onboarding, and retention of board members; Support the development of board goals, initiatives, and annual work plans; Facilitate communication between board members and University leadership; Encourage board participation in engagement and philanthropic initiatives. Volunteer Engagement Recruit, train, and manage alumni volunteers; Develop opportunities for alumni involvement through mentoring, speaking engagements, networking activities, career development programs, and University initiatives; Maintain a volunteer engagement pipeline and track volunteer participation; Collaborate with campus partners to identify meaningful volunteer opportunities for alumni. Alumni Philanthropy and Pipeline Development Promote alumni participation in annual giving and University fundraising initiatives; Conduct donor discovery and qualification visits to identify philanthropic interests and capacity; Solicit annual and leadership-level gifts from alumni and friends of the University; Identify and refer qualified major gift prospects to development staff; Collaborate with development officers to support cultivation, stewardship, and solicitation strategies; Maintain records of fundraising activity and prospect movement within the CRM. Alumni Communications and Recognition Collaborate with University communications staff to promote alumni engagement opportunities; Identify and highlight alumni achievements and success stories; Coordinate alumni recognition initiatives and outreach efforts; Support alumni communications through digital, print, and social media platforms. Collaboration and Strategic Initiatives Partner with development staff, academic units, and campus leadership to advance institutional priorities; Provide alumni engagement and participation data to support strategic planning and decision-making; Assist in the development and implementation of new alumni engagement programs and initiatives; Support special projects and strategic initiatives as assigned. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Knowledge of alumni relations, advancement, fundraising, volunteer management, or higher education practices; Strong interpersonal and relationship-building skills; Excellent written and verbal communication skills; Ability to recruit, motivate, and engage volunteers and donors; Ability to conduct donor discovery conversations and philanthropic outreach; Ability to manage multiple projects and priorities simultaneously; Proficiency in CRM systems and constituent engagement tracking; Strong organizational, analytical, and problem-solving skills; Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a team environment; Must have a valid driver's license. Additional Information: Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Kristi Smith, Associate Vice Chancellor of Alumni and Development, klsmith4@ualr.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Financial Credit Check, Motor Vehicle Reports Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Sitting, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Driving Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Fayetteville-AR/Postdoctoral-Research-Associate---Chemical-Engineering_R0089084-1": {"title": "Postdoctoral Research Associate - Chemical Engineering", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-30\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com, then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at all University of Arkansas institutions will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students.\u201d University of Arkansas, Fayetteville students will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Student Jobs at UAF.\u201d All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. Closing Date: 09/07/2026 Type of Position: Researchers and Scientists Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas, Fayetteville Founded in 1871, the University of Arkansas is a land grant institution, classified by the Carnegie Foundation among the nation\u2019s top 2 percent of universities with the highest level of research activity. The University of Arkansas works to advance the state and build a better world through education, research, and outreach by providing transformational opportunities and skills, fostering a welcoming climate, and nurturing creativity, discovery, and the spread of new ideas and innovations. The University of Arkansas campus is located in Fayetteville, a welcoming community ranked as one of the best places to live in the U.S. The growing region surrounding Fayetteville is home to numerous Fortune 500 companies and one of the nation\u2019s strongest economies. Northwest Arkansas is also quickly gaining a national reputation for its focus on the arts and overall quality of life. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10% of employee salary. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions, you should review before applying for the opening. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process, please submit a request via the Disability Accommodations | OEOC | University of Arkansas (uark.edu) : Request an Accommodation. Appli\u00adcants are required to submit a request for each position of which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 479.575.5351. Department: Chemical Engineering Department's Website: https://engineering.uark.edu/ Summary of Job Duties: Collaborating closely with Dr. Richardson and students in our group, the Postdoctoral Research Associate - Chemical Engineering will help develop new computational models that integrate molecular reaction networks with AI/ML algorithms in order to predict patient-specific cardiac remodeling and heart disease outcomes across human -omic datasets. In addition, the postdoctoral researcher will be expected to present research findings through journal publications and conference presentations. Regular, reliable, and non-disruptive attendance is an essential job duty, as is the ability to create and maintain collegial, harmonious working relationships with others. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Ph.D. in Biomedical Engineering, Chemical Engineering, Bioinformatics, Biostatistics, Computer Science, or a related field from an accredited institution of higher education, conferred by the start of employment Experience in biomedical AI/ML and/or systems biology Preferred Qualifications: Demonstrated excellence in previous research, supported by scientific publications Experience with personalized medicine, clinical datasets, and/or biomarker discovery Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Excellent communication skills Additional Information: Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Curriculum Vitae, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title) Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Recruitment Contact Information: Michael McAllister, Assistant to the Department Head / Operations Manager, mrmcalli@uark.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Special Instructions to Applicants: Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas seeks to attract, develop and retain high quality faculty, staff and administrators that consistently display practices and behaviors to advance a culture that embeds equal opportunity, educational excellence and unparalleled access for all. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All Application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAFS--University-of-Arkansas-Fort-Smith/Adjunct-Faculty-Graphic-Design_R0080852": {"title": "Adjunct Faculty-Graphic Design", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-30\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Adjunct Faculty Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Less than Annual Appointment (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Fort Smith University of Arkansas \u2013 Fort Smith The University of Arkansas - Fort Smith is a dynamic, mid-sized public university that\u2019s redefining higher education. We\u2019re on a mission to provide transformative, hands-on learning experiences for students of all backgrounds and aspirations. Our multi-faceted approach to education offers a wealth of opportunities, with over 70 academic programs, including certificates, associate, bachelor\u2019s, and master\u2019s degrees. We\u2019re committed to building a diverse community that mirrors Arkansas\u2019s rich tapestry, reflecting our dedication to serving the state\u2019s varied population while enhancing the quality of our institution. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life, and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10 percent of employee salary. \u00a0 Fort Smith, Arkansas Nestled along the Arkansas River, this vibrant city offers a perfect blend of history, culture, and natural beauty. Immerse yourself in the rich heritage of the Old West at the Fort Smith National Historic Site, explore the eclectic local art scene, or take a scenic stroll along the picturesque riverfront trails. With a welcoming community, diverse dining options, and a thriving downtown, Fort Smith is the ideal destination for history enthusiasts and those seeking modern amenities. Thank you for your interest in joining our university. Below you will find details for the position including any supplementary documentation and/or questions you should review before submitting your application. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at (479) 788-7080. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 479-788-7080. Applicants are required to submit a request for each position to which they have applied. Department: Art and Graphic Design Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Teach in one of the following subject areas as assigned: Graphic Design This is a pool position. Applicants will be contacted as positions become available. The position reports to the department head/program director/dean who assigns responsibilities regarding student needs and course outcomes. Qualifications: Required Education and/or Work Experience: Qualifications of instructors teaching in the classroom for both lower and/or upper-level courses leading to an associate or bachelor\u2019s degree requires a master\u2019s degree in the discipline or related field with a minimum of 18 graduate credits in the subject area. Courses leading to a master\u2019s require a doctorate degree. Adjunct faculty with a clinical assignment must be prepared at the level required by accreditation.\u00a0 Instructors in occupational and technical areas are generally required to have a minimum of an associate\u2019s degree and related work experience. Other job-related education and/or experience may be substituted for part of these requirements. Preferred Education and/or Work Experience: Prior teaching experience. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: To perform the job successfully, the following competencies are required for the essential functions of this position: Current knowledge of the relevant discipline.\u00a0 Good organizational skills and timeliness in responding to student inquiries.\u00a0 Ability to respond to needs of learners from a variety of educational backgrounds in a multicultural environment.\u00a0 Ability to deliver course outcomes and content through a variety of teaching/learning styles.\u00a0 Ability to use technology effectively in teaching.\u00a0 Ability to communicate effectively both orally and in writing.\u00a0 Ability to establish and maintain effective interpersonal relationships with students and colleagues.\u00a0 This is a pool position. Applicants will be contacted as positions become available. Job Responsibilities Classroom and online instruction Assess and evaluate student learning Responsible for maintaining a positive work atmosphere by acting and communicating in a manner to foster teamwork and by providing leadership to subordinates. Requires consistent on-time attendance. Other duties as assigned. Additional Information: Salary Information: Dependent upon department. Required Documents to Apply: List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume, Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: HR 479-788-7080 All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position may be subject to a pre-employment criminal background check, sex offender registry check, financial history background check, and/or drug screening. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication and/or adverse financial history alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background checks and drug screening information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAPBSJPRS-J-Parker-Agriculture-Research-Building/Research-Assistant-Farm-Technicians_R0088809": {"title": "Research Assistant/Farm Technicians", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-30\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Research Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff The University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff is an 1890 Land-Grant HBCU with a diverse student population, competitive degree offerings and stellar faculty. For more than 140 years, the University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff has worked to create an environment that inculcates learning, growth and productivity while affording a basic need to its students \u2013 a chance to advance. The 15:1 student to teacher ratio makes it possible to maintain a learning environment with close interaction between students and faculty while challenging curricula encourage our students to seek and fulfill their potential. You can excel in your chosen field of study through a curriculum of \u00a0 Certificate and Associates degree programs,\u00a0 more than thirty\u00a0 Undergraduate programs, Master\u2019s degree programs and a Doctorate program in Aquaculture/Fisheries. You can also develop workplace readiness through internships, co-ops and fellowships in the U.S. and abroad. Out-of-class experiences and student involvement include more than 90 student organizations, an internationally renowned Vesper Choir, Marching Band, Concert Bands, Wind Symphony, nationally recognized debate team, award-winning theater department and accomplished athletic program. Though the main campus is in Pine Bluff, its reach is worldwide. UAPB has an extended campus in North Little Rock and offers as well as online courses. With the addition of the Arkansas Research and Education Optical Network (ARE-ON), students can engage in information exchange with others anywhere in the world. There are also Research and Extension offices in Lonoke, Newport and Lake Village and collaborations with other colleges and universities in the State through the National Science Foundation funded STEM (Science, Technology, Engineering and Mathematics) Academy. As the second oldest land-grant institution in the state of Arkansas, the mission of this No Excuse University remains the same \u2013 to provide a high quality, affordable education with a personal touch. We invite you to Become a Part of the Pride at the University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process and require reasonable accommodations, please contact Human Resources at 870.575.8400 . Department: SAFHS Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The prospective candidate will be responsible for assisting the Livestock Technician in the management of the UAPB Livestock Farm, which includes managing livestock animals (E.g., Cows, goats, sheep, chickens, rabbits, etc.). The candidate will assist the Livestock Technician and the UAPB farm manager. The candidate will also have the following responsibilities. May have to work weekends occasionally. Qualifications: \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Assist with daily livestock care, including feeding, watering, and monitoring animal health and behavior. \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Support research projects by collecting, recording, and organizing experimental data. \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Maintain accurate records of animal weights, feed intake, growth performance, and breeding activities. \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Assist with handling and restraining animals during research procedures and routine health checks. \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Prepare research plots, pens, and equipment for experiments and demonstrations. \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Monitor environmental conditions such as temperature, soil moisture, and pasture quality. \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Assist faculty, farm managers, and graduate students with ongoing agricultural and livestock studies. \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Maintain cleanliness and biosecurity standards in the barns, pens, and research facilities. \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Operate and maintain basic farm equipment and tools safely and efficiently. \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Participate in educational outreach activities, demonstrations, and student training events. \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Support sustainable farming and conservation practices implemented on the farm. Additional Information: Salary Information: $28,125.00 Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants (Please upload all required documents in the \"Resume\" attachment section of your application to be considered for this position) : Recruitment Contact Information: Sharron M. Williams Employment Manager University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff 1200 N. University Drive Mail Slot 4942 Pine Bluff, AR 71601 Phone: (870) 575-8403 All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check The University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff may conduct pre-employment background checks on certain positions for applicants being considered for employment. \u00a0 The background checks may include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. \u00a0 Required checks are identified in the position listing. \u00a0 A criminal background check or arrest pending adjudication information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absences of a relationship to the requirements of the position. \u00a0 Background check information will be used in a consistent, non-discriminatory manner consistent with the state and federal law. \u00a0 The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: Climbing, Crawling, Crouching, Kneeling, Lifting, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Standing, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Driving, Sitting, Talking Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAFS--University-of-Arkansas-Fort-Smith/Resident-Director--Sebastian-Commons_R0089057": {"title": "Resident Director, Sebastian Commons", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-29\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Professional Staff - Student Affairs Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Fort Smith University of Arkansas \u2013 Fort Smith The University of Arkansas - Fort Smith is a dynamic, mid-sized public university that\u2019s redefining higher education. We\u2019re on a mission to provide transformative, hands-on learning experiences for students of all backgrounds and aspirations. Our multi-faceted approach to education offers a wealth of opportunities, with over 70 academic programs, including certificates, associate, bachelor\u2019s, and master\u2019s degrees. We\u2019re committed to building a diverse community that mirrors Arkansas\u2019s rich tapestry, reflecting our dedication to serving the state\u2019s varied population while enhancing the quality of our institution. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life, and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10 percent of employee salary. \u00a0 Fort Smith, Arkansas Nestled along the Arkansas River, this vibrant city offers a perfect blend of history, culture, and natural beauty. Immerse yourself in the rich heritage of the Old West at the Fort Smith National Historic Site, explore the eclectic local art scene, or take a scenic stroll along the picturesque riverfront trails. With a welcoming community, diverse dining options, and a thriving downtown, Fort Smith is the ideal destination for history enthusiasts and those seeking modern amenities. Thank you for your interest in joining our university. Below you will find details for the position including any supplementary documentation and/or questions you should review before submitting your application. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at (479) 788-7080. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 479-788-7080. Applicants are required to submit a request for each position to which they have applied. Department: Housing and Residential Life Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Sebastian Commons Resident Director is a full-time live-in position that reports directly to Assistant Dean of Students for Housing & Campus and Community Engagement. As a member of the Student Affairs staff, they are responsible for the general welfare of all students, encouraging them to maximize their intellectual growth and personal development. They are expected to positively influence, contribute to, and improve the quality of life of the residential student through the residential curriculum, implementing college policies and procedures, and by forming relationships with students in their facility. Qualifications: Required Education and/or Work Experience: Minimum requirements include a bachelor's degree with at least one year significant experience in a student housing employment position or equivalent experience. The position requires knowledge and skills related to human development, programming, conflict resolution, and the fair application of regulations. Other job-related education and/or experience may be substituted for part of these requirements. Preferred Education and/or Work Experience: Candidates with a master's degree in college student personnel, educational administration, or a related field, and previous experience supervising resident assistants, working with a residence hall association, and working with peer student conduct systems are preferred. Excellent verbal and written communication skills, the ability to work with diverse populations effectively, and excellent customer service skills are all expected. Essential Job Duties and Responsibilities: Supervise 8 Resident Assistants through weekly staff meetings, biweekly 1 on 1s, monitoring programming and community development, and semester evaluations Assist in hiring and training of Resident Assistants and other university staff as appointed Participate in the development, coordination and implementation of Housing & Residential Life procedures and programs Coordinate the assignments, contract, and billing processes for Sebastian Commons residents Serve as a University Conduct Administrator. Serve as a conduct officer for assigned residential area. Inform Assistant Dean of Students for Housing & Campus and Community Engagement of any issues. Serve in an on-call capacity with other HRL professional staff. Respond to all situations by answering phone, working with Resident Assistant On Call, and communicating with applicable staff such as the University Police Department, state and local emergency personnel, Assistant Dean of Students for Housing & Campus and Community Engagement and any chief student affairs officer positions. Supervise front desk/ office operations including supervising RAs and student workers in the office, receiving mail and packages, communicating with residents and visitors, and answering the phone Coordinate all move in and move out times and processes. Includes inspection of each room after the students have vacated and before it is occupied again, distribution and collection of applicable housing forms, and timely communication to residents Ensure that the quality and cleanliness of residential area, including outdoor property, is maintained Work jointly with Assistant Dean of Students for Housing & Campus and Community Engagement and Director of Facilities and Environmental Safety to ensure ongoing upkeep of facilities, custodial needs, maintenance efforts, and timely responses to work order requests Coordinate lock and key changes with maintenance and track all key use, loss, and theft Conduct quarterly Health & Safety Inspections of all rooms with the help of Resident Assistants. Document all work order needs and damage. Address any conduct violations. Implement, interpret, and continually develop HRL policies as stated in the Residential Handbook and Student Code of Conduct Serve as a Campus Security Authority (CSA) by understanding and following FERPA, Title IX, and the Clery Act as they pertain to on campus situations. Serve as a mandatory reporter and be trained in Title IX policy. Serve as first-level contact for parents regarding student housing needs and resident concerns Coordinate room changes and consolidation throughout the year Assist in development and implementation of campus emergency and crisis management procedures, programs, and services Assist residents with approved ADA accommodations based on need Maintain residential area budget Maintain confidentiality of all student information Review and create reports on an as-needed basis Establish Resident Assistant On Call schedule by ensuring staff availability for evenings, nights, and weekends Supervise and train summer part-time staff Advise the Resident Assistant Council Serve as the Housing and Residential Life website editor Supervise the HRL Social Media Student Assistant. Other Job Duties and Responsibilities: Adhere to the University of Arkansas \u2013 Fort Smith Employee Handbook Requires consistent on-time attendance Responsible for maintaining a positive work atmosphere by acting and communicating in a manner to foster teamwork and to provide leadership to subordinates. Identify student rooms to serve as tour rooms for Admissions and ensure those rooms are ready when needed Attend all University trainings, as required Take part in university and/or departmental committees as required by the department of Student Affairs or for professional development Advise a hall government system and/or Residence Hall Association Other duties as assigned. Responsible for maintaining a positive work atmosphere by acting and communicating in a manner to foster teamwork and by providing leadership to subordinates. Requires consistent on-time attendance. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: To perform the job successfully, the following competencies are required for the essential functions of this position: Conflict resolution Knowledge of university structures and governance Budget projections and management Communicate well with very diverse constituents Teaching and facilitating with individuals and groups Ability to apply conduct regulations fairly and consistently Ability to identify and draw on resources across campus Skills in conceiving, designing, and implementing educational programming Knowledge of laws and procedures related to university housing Ability to balance and respect individual rights and community rights Knowledge of learning processes and commitment to foster student learning Adaptability \u2013 adapts to changes in the work environment, manages competing demands and is able to deal with frequent change, delays or unexpected events. Dependability \u2013 is consistently at work and on time, follows instructions, responds to management direction and solicits feedback to improve performance. Knowledge of the principles of computer operations to understand the college\u2019s information systems and services which carry out accounting, budgeting, purchasing, human resources, enrollment, and other or similar centralized institution-wide management information functions.\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Additional Information: Working Relationships: Work in a dynamic team of diverse faculty, staff, and students in a fast paced, growth-oriented environment. Frequent contact with vendors, personnel from other agencies and institutions and the general public, student employees, resident assistants, professional staff in student affairs, housing and residential life professional staff, custodial and grounds workers, maintenance workers, faculty, parents, student residents.\u00a0\u00a0 List Employees Supervised: Resident Assistants (8), Social Media Student Assistant (1), Summer Housing Managers (3), Summer Facility Workers (2) Special Job Dimensions: Modest travel required for professional development and accompanying student groups; modest physical demands and stamina needed in working with resident assistants, programming materials, move-ins, on call, etc.; Required abilities include walking, standing, and sitting for extended periods. Visual demands include close, relatively detailed vision when focusing on a computer screen; hours are traditional office hours with evening meetings and programs and on call responsibilities in the overnight, weekends, and holidays; live-in is required. Background Check Requirements. Criminal Background Check, Financial Background Check, and Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) Check ; Position requires employee complete Arkansas Mandated Reporter training prior to employment. This job description is not designed to contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties, and/or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time with or without notice. Salary Information: $37,745.05 plus additional benefits: Furnished apartment to include utilities, wired and wireless internet, reserved parking space, unlimited meal plan, $1,000 in Lion's Cash Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume, Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Full consideration will be given to applications received by August 14, 2026. Recruitment Contact Information: HR 479-788-7080 All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position may be subject to a pre-employment criminal background check, sex offender registry check, financial history background check, and/or drug screening. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication and/or adverse financial history alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background checks and drug screening information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAMS/Diagnostic-Radiology-Technologist---Bentonville-Clinic_R0087428-1": {"title": "Diagnostic Radiology Technologist - Bentonville Clinic", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-29\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/30/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | MUSL NWA Bentonville Clinical Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Diagnostic Radiology Technologist at UAMS Clinic in Bentonville is responsible for producing high-quality radiographic images for medical interpretation and assisting in patient examinations and treatments as needed. This role operates under the supervision of the manager and involves interpreting health record documentation to identify diagnoses and procedures affecting outpatient visits. The position does not include supervisory responsibilities over other diagnostic radiology technologists. Be a part of a team that is shaping the future of healthcare in Arkansas. If you are passionate about diagnostic imaging and providing exceptional patient care, we encourage you to apply today! Qualifications: Minimum Qualification: High School Diploma; completion of a two-year certification program or an associate degree that is accredited by the ASRT in Radiology Technology. Three (3) years or more of experience working as a Radiology Technologist preferred. Registered with the American Registry of Radiologic Technologist and Licensed by the State of Arkansas in Radiology Technology. Knowledge, Skills, & Abilities: Strong knowledge of radiographic imaging techniques and patient care protocols. Ability to work collaboratively in a multidisciplinary healthcare environment. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills to ensure patient-centered care. Ability to read, write, and follow oral instructions. Knowledge of all required supplies and equipment necessary for each procedure. Knowledge of the Anatomy of vessels and organs in the body (for proper positioning). Additional Information: Key Responsibilities: Operate radiographic equipment to produce diagnostic-quality images. Assist in patient examinations and treatments as required. Review and interpret health record documentation to ensure accurate identification of diagnoses and procedures. Adhere to UAMS policies, including Core Concepts of Patient and Family Centered Care, which emphasize dignity, respect, information sharing, participation, and collaboration. May perform other duties as assigned. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience. Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), Resume Optional Documents: List of five Professional References (name, email, business title), Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Augusta/County-Extension-Agent---Family---Consumer-Science_R0088937": {"title": "County Extension Agent - Family & Consumer Science", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-29\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Professional Staff - Extension Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: Division of Agriculture of the University of Arkansas The University of Arkansas System Division of Agriculture is a state wide campus, with faculty based on University campuses, at Research and Extension Centers and in every Arkansas county. It consists of the Arkansas Agricultural Experiment Station (AES) and the Arkansas Cooperative Extension Service (CES), and is home to more than 1400 employees.\u00a0 The Division was established in 1959 and is headed by the Vice-President for Agriculture.\u00a0 The Division headquarters is located in Little Rock with the rest of the University of Arkansas System Administration.\u00a0 As an employer, the University of Arkansas System Division of Agriculture offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance.\u00a0 Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process and require reasonable accommodations, please contact the Division's Office of Program & Employment Compliance at compliance@uada.edu . For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-671-2219 or 479-502-9820. Department: CEA * Staff Chair * Woodruff County Department's Website: https://www.uaex.uada.edu/counties/woodruff/ Summary of Job Duties: The County Extension Agent \u2013 Family & Consumer Science delivers practical, community\u2011based education in nutrition, health, family well\u2011being, food safety, and financial stability while engaging county residents and volunteers to support county programs, a role grounded in community education and family well\u2011being. \u2022 Maintains a thorough knowledge of the social, economic, and political characteristics of the county and will be an effective liaison with local community leaders, agencies and governments. Maintains an up-to-date and working knowledge of Arkansas Extension programs. \u2022 Develops and executes an annual action plan based on issues identified by the programmatic Subcommittee(s) and personal observations. Plans, delivers and teaches educational programs, demonstrations, and activities that address the needs of the county\u2019s clientele. Provides opportunities for program participation at the county, district, and state levels, while also sharing educational information with county government leaders, community organizations and stakeholders to support the overall Extension mission. \u2022 Leverages Extension specialists and research-based information to design, implement and teach educational programs in all Family and Consumer Sciences (FCS) priority areas. Responds to clientele inquiries through phone consultations, e-mails, in-person office and site visits, providing tailored researched based recommendations as required. \u2022 Serve as an advisor to the county (EHC) Extension Homemaker Club officers, board and members. Provides researched and unbiased leader training for EHC clubs. Provide support during and at county, district and state EHC activities. \u2022 Supports the county 4-H program and related activities, including FCS educational programming, training for competitive events, volunteer recruitment and development, and fundraising efforts. Contributes to program delivery at the county, district, and state levels. \u2022 Employs effective evaluation techniques to measure the impact of county FCS and 4-H programs. Compiles and communicates program results to the county advisory committee, Extension Council (if applicable), and county and state government officials on an annual basis. \u2022 Ensures compliance with civil rights requirements and maintains current knowledge of applicable rules and regulations. Promotes inclusivity by ensuring all programs are accessible to the public and maintains accurate records to demonstrate compliance. \u2022 Completes and submits required reports on a monthly basis to ensure accuracy, consistency, and accountability. \u2022 Collaborate with colleagues, partners, and stakeholders to effectively carry out and advance the Extension mission. \u2022 Establish and maintain good working relationships with Extension staff, clientele and general public. \u2022 Build a network of supporters and volunteers to assist in program delivery. \u2022 Maintains a working knowledge of researched based FCS practices and programs by attending in-service trainings offered through Arkansas Extension, professional development associations and other opportunities deemed appropriate by their supervisor. \u2022 Demonstrates knowledge of and adherence to University of Arkansas Division of Agriculture policies and procedures, ensuring alignment with institutional standards in all professional activities. \u2022 Performs additional responsibilities as assigned by the immediate supervisor or district director. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications Bachelor's degree in family & consumer science, education, youth development, or related field of study; degree must be conferred by date of hire or Bachelor\u2019s degree with relevant work experience. Must have reliable transportation for use on the job with liability insurance in effect. Must successfully complete the standard background check which includes the Arkansas Child Abuse and Neglect Central Registry Check. \u00a0Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Knowledge of family & consumer science subject matter appropriate to the county. Ability to plan and conduct programs and work with all clientele regardless of race, color, national origin, religion, gender, age, disability, marital or veteran status, genetic information, sexual preference, pregnancy or any other legally protected status. Ability to speak and write clearly and communicate ideas effectively. Ability to work long and irregular hours and travel frequently. Additional Information: Applicants for this position are required to upload a Resume, Cover letter, Official or Unofficial Transcript, and a list of three (3) references including name, phone number and email address (if available) prior to submitting the application. Once an application is submitted, the applicant will not be able to edit the application or upload additional documents. If you have technical issues uploading a document or if you have a need to provide additional documentation after submitting your application, email humanresources@uada.edu Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume, Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: JJ Jones, Delta District Director, jjjones@uada.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Motor Vehicle Reports Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas System Division of Agriculture may conduct pre-employment background checks on certain positions for applicants being considered for employment. \u00a0 The background checks may include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. \u00a0 Required checks are identified in the position listing. \u00a0 A criminal background check or arrest pending adjudication information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absences of a relationship to the requirements of the position. \u00a0 Background check information will be used in a consistent, non-discriminatory manner consistent with the state and federal law. \u00a0 The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Driving, Feeling, Grasping, Standing, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Kneeling, Lifting, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Repetitive Motion, Sitting Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-Arkansas-Community-College-at-Batesville/Maintenance-Assistant_R0089072-1": {"title": "Maintenance Assistant", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-28\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. Closing Date: Type of Position: Skilled Labor Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas Community College at Batesville The University of Arkansas Community College at Batesville (UACCB) is a comprehensive community college committed to providing learning experiences that improve the lives of those we serve. UACCB provides affordable access to technical education and college transfer programs that meet the diverse higher education needs of the citizens of north central Arkansas. \u00a0 These programs are provided to the traditional college student as well as to high school students through a state approved Secondary Area Career Center. \u00a0 The College also promotes economic development and an enhanced quality of life for the community through adult education, developmental education, customized business and industry training, and continuing education programs. UACCB's mission is to provide quality educational opportunities within a supportive learning environment. We promote success through community partnerships, responsive programs, and an enduring commitment to improvement. Thank you for your interest. \u00a0 We hope you will be joining us soon! After reviewing the Job Duties and Qualifications listed below, click the Apply button at the top of the page to begin the application process. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process or for general application assistance, please contact the Human Resource Office at (870) 612-2045. Department: Director Physical Plant Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Basic Functions Under the supervision of the Maintenance Supervisor or the Facilities Director, the maintenance worker performs a wide range of tasks to ensure that college facilities are safe, functional, and well maintained for students, staff, and visitors. This role involves hands-on work across various trades, general cleaning, grounds and event support.\u202f The Maintenance Assistant is responsible for buildings and grounds maintenance and general labor activities. This position is governed by state and federal laws and institution policy. Caring Campus Responsibilities: As a member of the UACCB community, each employee is responsible for advancing the Caring Campus culture to enhance student connection and success and to embody the campus purpose: Improve Lives. Key duties include adhering to the campus name badge policy, treating all visitors as guests, engaging with the campus community by reviewing institutional communications, participating in campus events, and supporting a collaborative, positive workplace environment. Position Duties 90% - Primary Responsibilities The employee performs general lawn maintenance, operates medium to light equipment and hand tools, assists with general construction tasks, completes routine housekeeping responsibilities, and carries out basic remodeling and construction practices as needed. 10% - Additional Responsibilities The employee performs other duties as assigned to support departmental operations. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Knowledge Knowledge of methods and practices in skilled and unskilled trades. Ability to operate and perform routine maintenance on various types of groundskeeping tools and equipment. Ability to receive, assign, and coordinate work activities. Skills Ability to operate and perform routine maintenance on various types of grounds and facilities management tools and equipment. Abilities Ability to receive, assign and coordinate work activities to complete daily tasks. Maintain strong relationships with faculty, staff, students, and community partners with daily or weekly interactions. Qualifications: Qualifications \u00a0 High school diploma or equivalent from an accredited institution. \u00a0 1 -3 years of job related experience. \u00a0 Must maintain active driver\u2019s license. \u00a0 \u00a0 Preferred Qualifications \u00a0 \u00a0 Technical certificates in skilled trades such as, plumbing, carpentry, and electrical. \u00a0 Three or more years of progressively job-related experience. \u00a0 Additional Information: Salary Information: $32,500 Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume, Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Human Resources hr@uaccb.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Motor Vehicle Reports Check, Sex Offender Registry, Substance Abuse Testing UACCB is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check for all applicants.\u00a0 Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Pulling, Pushing, Sitting Frequent Physical Activity: Climbing, Kneeling, Lifting, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Sharps, Stooping Occasional Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Repetitive Motion, Sharps Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Adjunct-of-Nursing_R0082307": {"title": "Adjunct of Nursing", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-28\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Adjunct Faculty Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Less than Annual Appointment (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Little Rock The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is a metropolitan research university that provides an accessible, quality education through flexible learning and unparalleled internship opportunities. At UA Little Rock, we prepare our more than 8,900 students to be innovators and responsible leaders in their fields. Committed to its metropolitan research university mission, UA Little Rock is a driving force in Little Rock's thriving cultural community and a major component of the city and state's growing profile as a regional leader in research, technology transfer, economic development, and job creation. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . Department: Nursing Department Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Adjunct faculty will be supervising students in the clinical setting while they complete patient care to satisfy the clinical hour requirements for the School of Nursing Associate of Applied Science degree. The adjunct faculty will also be responsible for grading clinical paperwork and mentoring students in their clinical performance. This position is governed by state and federal laws and agency/institution policy. Qualifications: Required Education and/or Experience:\u00a0 BSN Required; Holds a current and unencumbered RN license; 2 Years of Nursing Experience. Preferred Education and/or Experience: Teaching experience. Job Duties and Responsibilities:\u00a0 Supervising students in the clinical setting while they complete patient care to satisfy the clinical hour requirements for the School of Nursing Associate of Applied Science degree; Responsible for grading clinical paperwork; Mentoring students in their clinical performance.\u00a0 Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Nursing knowledge in the assigned clinical area; Basic nursing skills; Ability to work a 9-12 hour clinical shift and navigate Blackboard LMS and Google Suite.\u00a0 Additional Information: Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Curriculum Vitae, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Elizabeth Brook Hopkins Senior Research Assistant/HEI Coordinator bgrimes1@ualr.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Adult Maltreatment, Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry, Substance Abuse Testing The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Crouching, Grasping, Kneeling, Lifting Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAM--McGehee-Campus/Non-Student-Extra-Help--Adult-Education-Teacher-_R0088694-2": {"title": "Non-Student Extra Help (Adult Education Teacher)", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-28\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Faculty - Non-Tenure Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Monticello UAM, one of twenty campuses of the University of Arkansas System, is located in southeastern Arkansas in the beautiful timberlands, rich in outdoor recreation activities, and approximately 100 miles south of Little Rock. UAM is a comprehensive, residential and commuter, undergraduate institution also offering selected master\u2019s degree programs. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please submit a request via the OEOC website: \u00a0Applicants are required to submit a request for each position to which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 870-460-1422 . Department: Adult Education Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Workforce Ed Instructor is responsible for teaching minors in a correctional/treatment facility. Duties include, but are not limited to: \u00b7 Schedule all students for the TABE test. \u00b7 Monitor student\u2019s attendance and advise teachers on when students should post-test. \u00b7 Schedule & Administer all TABE test for students. \u00b7 Schedule and Administer all GED ready test for students. \u00b7 Schedule all GED test. \u00b7 Complete a student intake with each student. \u00b7 Creating and maintaining student files. \u00b7 Entering data accurately into LACES. \u00b7 Performing recruitment and retention activities. \u00b7 Maintaining an accurate call log. \u00b7 Work attendance is a must! \u00b7 Attend all mandated faulty and state meetings. \u00b7 Attend professional development. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications Bachelor's degree. Current Arkansas Teaching License. Additional Information: Salary Information: $20.00-$25.00, depends on adult education experiences. Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), Resume, Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Dr. Dorissa Kaufman Director of Adult Education Kaufmand@uamont.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Motor Vehicle Reports Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding Occasional Physical Activity: Standing Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Program-Technician---Leadership_R0089060-1": {"title": "Program Technician - Leadership", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-28\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Researchers Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Fixed Duration of Project/Grant (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: Division of Agriculture of the University of Arkansas The University of Arkansas System Division of Agriculture is a state wide campus, with faculty based on University campuses, at Research and Extension Centers and in every Arkansas county. It consists of the Arkansas Agricultural Experiment Station (AES) and the Arkansas Cooperative Extension Service (CES), and is home to more than 1400 employees.\u00a0 The Division was established in 1959 and is headed by the Vice-President for Agriculture.\u00a0 The Division headquarters is located in Little Rock with the rest of the University of Arkansas System Administration.\u00a0 As an employer, the University of Arkansas System Division of Agriculture offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance.\u00a0 Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process and require reasonable accommodations, please contact the Division's Office of Program & Employment Compliance at compliance@uada.edu . For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-671-2219 or 479-502-9820. Department: Community Prof. & Economic Development Department's Website: uaex.uada.edu/business-communities Summary of Job Duties: We are seeking a dynamic Program Technician with a focus on leadership to join our team. This position will primarily support the coordination, administration, and delivery of the Ag-tech Career Exploration (ACE) program and the Experiential Scholars Program (ESP), with additional support for other leadership-related initiatives within the University of Arkansas Division of Agriculture Cooperative Extension Service. The Program Technician will assist with program planning, participant communication, logistics, records management, reporting, evaluation, and event support. A secondary component of the role will include marketing and communications support, such as social media, publications, and website updates for leadership programs. Key Responsibilities: \u00b7 Coordinate and help manage the day-to-day operations of the Ag-tech Career Exploration (ACE) program and the Experiential Scholars Program (ESP). \u00b7 Support recruitment, application processing, participant communication, scheduling, and recordkeeping for ACE and ESP. \u00b7 Assist with planning and coordinating seminars, workshops, meetings, travel, and other program activities related to ACE, ESP, and other leadership programs. \u00b7 Prepare program materials, participant resources, correspondence, and reports for ACE and ESP activities. \u00b7 Track program participation, maintain program files and databases, and assist with required documentation and reporting. Job Description: \u00b7 Prepare and administer program evaluations to assess effectiveness and gather participant feedback for ACE, ESP, and related leadership initiatives. \u00b7 Provide logistical and onsite support for seminars, meetings, student activities, and special events. \u00b7 Collaborate with team members, faculty, staff, and external partners to support overall program goals and participant success. \u00b7 Develop and implement marketing and communication strategies to support all leadership programs. \u00b7 Manage social media platforms, create engaging content, and monitor online presence for leadership-related programs. \u00b7 Design and produce publications such as newsletters, brochures, promotional materials, and reports. \u00b7 Update and maintain websites related to leadership programs, ensuring content accuracy and relevance. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications \u00b7 Bachelor\u2019s degree in Communication, Leadership, Education, Marketing, Public Relations, Agricultural Education, or a related field. Preferred Qualifications \u00b7 Experience in program coordination, education, student support, event planning, or administrative support preferred. \u00b7 Strong organizational skills with the ability to manage multiple projects, priorities, and deadlines. \u00b7 Strong writing and communication skills with the ability to create clear, professional correspondence and program materials. \u00b7 Proficiency in Microsoft Office applications, data management, mass communication software, and social media applications. \u00b7 Proficiency in website content management systems and basic understanding of web analytics preferred. \u00b7 Experience in marketing, communications, or public relations is beneficial. \u00b7 Experience in graphic design and desktop publishing preferred. \u00b7 Ability to organize and coordinate logistics for meetings, workshops, travel, and events. \u00b7 Excellent interpersonal and communication skills with a customer service orientation. \u00b7 Detail-oriented with strong analytical, problem-solving, and recordkeeping abilities. \u00b7 Ability to exercise initiative, make sound judgments, work without close supervision, and respond effectively to the needs of supervisors, colleagues, and clientele. Additional Information: This position requires occasional evening or weekend work to support events or deadlines. Travel may be required for onsite event support, program activities, or meetings. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Lisa Davis, Program Associate - Leadership / Community, Professional, & Economic Development Phone: (501) 671-2260 Email: ldavis@uada.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Motor Vehicle Reports Check The University of Arkansas System Division of Agriculture may conduct pre-employment background checks on certain positions for applicants being considered for employment. \u00a0 The background checks may include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. \u00a0 Required checks are identified in the position listing. \u00a0 A criminal background check or arrest pending adjudication information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absences of a relationship to the requirements of the position. \u00a0 Background check information will be used in a consistent, non-discriminatory manner consistent with the state and federal law. \u00a0 The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Standing, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Driving, Lifting, Pushing, Reaching Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Fayetteville-AR/Assistant-Associate-Full-Professor-of-Law--Open-Rank----Property-Law_R0088902-1": {"title": "Assistant/Associate/Full Professor of Law (Open Rank) - Property Law", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-28\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com, then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at all University of Arkansas institutions will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students.\u201d University of Arkansas, Fayetteville students will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Student Jobs at UAF.\u201d All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. Closing Date: Type of Position: Faculty - Tenure/Tenure Track Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas, Fayetteville Founded in 1871, the University of Arkansas is a land grant institution, classified by the Carnegie Foundation among the nation\u2019s top 2 percent of universities with the highest level of research activity. The University of Arkansas works to advance the state and build a better world through education, research, and outreach by providing transformational opportunities and skills, fostering a welcoming climate, and nurturing creativity, discovery, and the spread of new ideas and innovations. The University of Arkansas campus is located in Fayetteville, a welcoming community ranked as one of the best places to live in the U.S. The growing region surrounding Fayetteville is home to numerous Fortune 500 companies and one of the nation\u2019s strongest economies. Northwest Arkansas is also quickly gaining a national reputation for its focus on the arts and overall quality of life. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10% of employee salary. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions, you should review before applying for the opening. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process, please submit a request via the Disability Accommodations | OEOC | University of Arkansas (uark.edu) : Request an Accommodation. Appli\u00adcants are required to submit a request for each position of which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 479.575.5351. Department: School of Law Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The University of Arkansas is pleased to announce that it is seeking applicants for a 9-month, 100% appointed tenure-track or tenured assistant, associate, or full professor (depending on qualifications) to teach property law and related courses for the 2027-2028 academic year. Candidates must have a J.D. degree from an ABA-accredited law school and must demonstrate a commitment to excellence in teaching and mentoring students. Applicants must demonstrate an excellent record of scholarship or, at the entry level, a strong potential for scholarship. Successful candidates will also show a commitment to service within and outside the University. Lateral candidates are encouraged to apply. The University of Arkansas School of Law offers an environment in which faculty can thrive. We place a premium on teaching excellence and are deeply committed to our students\u2019 academic and professional success. At the same time, our faculty engage in scholarship that is shaping law and policy on the state, national, and global levels. The faculty\u2019s breadth of experience in government service, public interest law, private practice, and other areas of academic study ensures a vibrant intellectual life for students and faculty alike. We seek new colleagues who will meaningfully contribute to this community. The University of Arkansas-Fayetteville is the flagship campus of the University of Arkansas. It is a land grant institution, and is committed to providing the highest levels of public education in service to the State of Arkansas. Located in the northwest corner of the state, Fayetteville is at the heart of a rapidly growing metropolitan area that boasts a dynamic economy, a vibrant cultural community, and world-class outdoor recreation, in a region that regularly championed as a \u201cbest place to live.\u201d This is an in-person position. Most University classes are offered face-to-face and this role requires regular on-campus presence to support high-quality instruction and student learning. Participation in selected departmental or programmatic activities that advance teaching quality and student success is also expected. Regular, reliable, and non-disruptive attendance is an essential job duty, as is the ability to create and maintain collegial, harmonious working relationships with others. Rank: Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Professor will depend on the candidate\u2019s level of experience. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications JD degree from an ABA-accredited law school or an international law degree A distinguished academic record Demonstrated scholarly promise Preferred Qualifications A law license and two years of practical legal experience Tenure-track teaching experience or experience as a visiting assistant professor or fellow Additional Information: Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Curriculum Vitae, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title) Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Recruitment Contact Information: Rachel Whitman Leslie Pounds All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Special Instructions to Applicants: Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas seeks to attract, develop and retain high quality faculty, staff and administrators that consistently display practices and behaviors to advance a culture that embeds equal opportunity, educational excellence and unparalleled access for all. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All Application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAMS---NWA/RN--Northwest-Orthopaedic-Outpatient-Clinics_R0089036-1": {"title": "RN- Northwest Orthopaedic Outpatient Clinics", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-27\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/05/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | MUSL NWA Bentonville Clinical Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Registered Nurse (RN) plays a pivotal role in patient care by emphasizing excellence, compassion, and evidence-based practice. This role supports the UAMS Orthopaedics and Sports Medicine Outpatient Clinics in Northwest Arkansas. This posting seeks RNs to fill multiple vacancies in the following areas: Joint Specialty Coordinator and Orthopaedic Surgery Scheduling Coordinator, with opportunities to cover additional orthopaedic and related roles as needed. Primary responsibilities include direct patient care, triage, coordination, and collaboration with providers, patients, and families. The RN will work with patients and referral sources to facilitate appointments, coordinate transitions of care, obtain medical clearances, and provide education on complex conditions. The RN partners with patients, families, and providers to develop and implement individualized health plans. If you are a dedicated and compassionate RN with a passion for orthopaedic and sports medicine, join our team at UAMS and make a meaningful impact on patient care in Northwest Arkansas! Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor\u2019s degree in Nursing, Associate\u2019s degree in Nursing, Diploma RN, or Master\u2019s degree in Nursing. Must be a graduate of an accredited RN nursing program Valid Registered Nursing License Minimum of one (1) year of Registered Nursing experience. Knowledge, Skills, & Abilities: Basic computer skills. Demonstrates effective communication skills; communicates accurate and complete information; Ability to maintain strict confidentiality when necessary. Strong work ethics and accountability. BLS Current Preferred Qualifications Orthopaedic experience a plus EPIC experience Additional Information: Key Responsibilities: Assist surgeons with in-office orthopedic procedures. Assist with patient intake and the rooming process. Educate patients and families on conditions and DME. Obtain medical clearances for surgical patients and prior authorizations for surgery, DME, and medications. Assist with patient physical examinations and laboratory draws. Coordination and scheduling of outpatient surgical procedures. Schedules appointments and responds to and prioritizes incoming patient calls as needed. Telephone interactions require assessment and patient education. Responds to patient questions appropriately, providing reassurance and addressing concerns. Maintains accurate and detailed records with pertinent information and education within Epic. Utilizes current nursing practice to provide patient-focused care while exemplifying service excellence, care, concern, respect, and cooperation. Interacts with and assists the public in a professional and friendly manner as needed. Demonstrates positive working relationships with co-workers, management team, and ancillary departments; follows the Core Concepts of Patient and Family Centered Care and the Basic Code of Conduct\u00a0Guidelines. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), Resume Optional Documents: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Curriculum Vitae, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Lead-Project-Archivist-12-MONTH_R0088813": {"title": "Lead Project Archivist-12 MONTH", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-27\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Archives and Collections Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Little Rock The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is a metropolitan research university that provides an accessible, quality education through flexible learning and unparalleled internship opportunities. At UA Little Rock, we prepare our more than 8,900 students to be innovators and responsible leaders in their fields. Committed to its metropolitan research university mission, UA Little Rock is a driving force in Little Rock's thriving cultural community and a major component of the city and state's growing profile as a regional leader in research, technology transfer, economic development, and job creation. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . Department: Archives & Collections Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The UA Little Rock Center for Arkansas History and Culture seeks a skilled, collaborative Lead Project Archivist to arrange, describe, and preserve the Heifer International records. This is a full-time, on-site, term-limited position with an anticipated three-year duration. The Lead Project Archivist will manage a 2-3 person processing team and collaborate with the Head Archivist to implement processing and digitization plans. This position is well-suited to a more experienced archival professional seeking a focused project role. Headquartered in Little Rock, Heifer International is a global nonprofit whose mission is to end hunger and poverty by supporting local farmers and their communities. The Heifer International records, dating from the 1940s to the 1990s, total approximately 800 boxes. Materials include correspondence, annual reports, shipping records, project reports, financial records, campaign materials, magazines and catalogs, scrapbooks, photographic slides and negatives, reel-to-reel tapes, VHS tapes, hard drives, computer disks, and artifacts. This collection will provide insight into understanding Arkansas\u2019s history and its connections to the world. This is a 12-month grant-funded position. Continued employment is contingent upon the availability of annual grant funding. Qualifications: Required Education and/or Experience: \u25cf Master's degree in information and library science or related field; \u25cf Two or more years of experience processing archival materials in a variety of formats; \u25cf Experience writing finding aids. Preferred Education and/or Experience: \u25cf Demonstrated record of successful project management and supervisory experience; \u25cf Professional experience in an academic or research library, special collections repository, or other relevant setting; \u25cf Experience using ArchivesSpace. Job Duties and Responsibilities: \u25cf Process the Heifer International records. This includes developing a processing plan, researching collection items for identification, arranging and describing materials, rehousing materials for preservation, and creating a DACS-compliant finding aid; \u25cf Supervise 2-3 project archivists and graduate assistants (e.g., organizing workload, delegating responsibility, providing guidance and direction); \u25cf Create and maintain an achievable timeline for the project; \u25cf Manage project documentation, such as progress reports and lead update meetings; \u25cf Select and digitize physical materials and write metadata according to institutional standards; \u25cf Monitor access to sensitive or restricted materials, ensuring compliance with privacy and security protocols; \u25cf Consult and collaborate with CAHC archivists as needed to ensure appropriate processing of varying formats; \u25cf Participate in outreach activities to promote the collection; \u25cf Assist with internal and external research requests related to the collection; \u25cf Perform additional duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: \u25cf Demonstrated experience using best practices to arrange and describe archival collections; \u25cf Knowledge of processing hybrid collections; \u25cf Understanding of privacy, safe handling, confidentiality, copyright, and use issues in an archival setting; \u25cf Thorough knowledge of archival standards and vocabularies, including EAD and DACS; \u25cf Experience with digital asset management systems, including ArchivesSpace and CONTENTdm; \u25cf Ability to establish priorities, set and meet goals and deadlines, and manage project schedules; \u25cf Excellent verbal, written, and interpersonal communication skills; \u25cf Ability to work independently or as a member of a team. Additional Information: Salary Information: $55,000 Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: China Higginbotham, Assistant Director for Finance and Administration, chigginbo@ualr.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Grasping, Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting Frequent Physical Activity: Grasping, Hearing, Lifting, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Kneeling, Pulling, Pushing, Stooping Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Assistant-or-Associate-Professor----Speech-Language-Pathology_R0087196-1": {"title": "Assistant or Associate Professor - Speech-Language Pathology", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-24\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/05/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: Audiology & Speech-Language Pathology Department's Website: https://healthprofessions.uams.edu/audiology-and-speech-pathology/programs/speech-language-pathology/ Summary of Job Duties: The Program: The Master of Science in Speech-Language Pathology Program at UAMS prepares future speech-language pathologists through an innovative educational model that integrates rigorous academic instruction with extensive clinical training on a major academic health sciences campus. The program emphasizes evidence-based practice, clinical excellence, interprofessional collaboration, cultural responsiveness, and compassionate, client-centered care. Students develop the knowledge and skills necessary to assess, diagnose, and treat communication and swallowing disorders across the lifespan while meeting national certification and state licensure standards. The program features small cohort sizes, individualized faculty mentorship, clinical experiences across medical, educational, and community settings, and interprofessional learning opportunities alongside students from other health professions. Graduates are prepared to serve individuals with communication and swallowing disorders in a variety of practice settings, including hospitals, rehabilitation centers, schools, private practice, and outpatient clinics. The Setting: UAMS is Arkansas\u2019 largest basic and applied research institution, providing outstanding clinical services through the main campus as well as eight regional centers. UAMS includes seven institutes of excellence (i.e., Aging, Cancer, Eye, Myeloma, Spine & Neurosciences, Psychiatric Research, and Translational Research), and houses the Brain Imaging Research Center (BIRC) and the Voice and Swallowing Center. UAMS is a certified Advanced Primary Stroke Center and is affiliated with the Central Arkansas Veterans Administration Hospital and Arkansas Children\u2019s Hospital (both also located in Little Rock). Application Process: Applications with a current curriculum vitae, a letter of application, Statement of Research Philosophy, Statement of Teaching Philosophy and at least three professional references is currently being accepted via the UAMS Jobs Portal. References will only be contacted for semi-finalists. Evaluation of the application will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Selection Committee Chair: Kristen Muller, Ph.D., CCC-SLP Assistant Professor UAMS College of Health Professions Department of Audiology and Speech Pathology KMuller@uams.edu Qualifications: Required Qualifications Terminal degree (Ph.D. in Speech-Language Pathology or Communication Sciences and Disorders \u00a0 or Ed.D. PLUS Three (3) or more years of experience in the field of Speech-Language Pathology. Eligibility for the Certificate of Clinical Competence in Speech-Language Pathology (CCC-SLP). Eligibility for Speech-Language Pathology licensure in the State of Arkansas. Preferred Qualifications Demonstrated record of scholarly research and academic productivity. Responsibilities Teach graduate-level courses within the Master of Science in Speech-Language Pathology program. Mentor and supervise graduate student research, projects, and academic progress. Develop and maintain an active scholarly and research agenda. Assist with clinical education and student clinical supervision as assigned. Advise and support graduate students throughout their academic program. Participate in curriculum development, program assessment, and accreditation activities. Collaborate with faculty, staff, and clinical partners to support program goals and student success. Engage in university, community, and professional service activities. Contribute to departmental, college, and university committees and initiatives. Support recruitment, retention, and engagement efforts for students and the Speech-Language Pathology program. Promote a collaborative, inclusive, and student-centered learning environment. Perform other duties as assigned in support of the department's mission and strategic goals. Additional Information: Responsibilities Teach graduate-level courses within the Master of Science in Speech-Language Pathology program. Mentor and supervise graduate student research, projects, and academic progress. Develop and maintain an active scholarly and research agenda. Assist with clinical education and student clinical supervision as assigned. Advise and support graduate students throughout their academic program. Participate in curriculum development, program assessment, and accreditation activities. Collaborate with faculty, staff, and clinical partners to support program goals and student success. Engage in university, community, and professional service activities. Contribute to departmental, college, and university committees and initiatives. Support recruitment, retention, and engagement efforts for students and the Speech-Language Pathology program. Promote a collaborative, inclusive, and student-centered learning environment. Perform other duties as assigned in support of the department's mission and strategic goals. Physical Demands: Constant Physical Activity: Hearng, Standing, Talking Frequent Physical Activity:Feeling, Sitting, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Driving, Pulling, Pushing Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Curriculum Vitae, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Statement of Research Philosophy, Statement of Teaching Philosophy Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAM--Monticello-Campus/Graduate-Assistant_R0088827-1": {"title": "Graduate Assistant", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-24\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Graduate Assistant Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Less than Annual Appointment (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Monticello UAM, one of twenty campuses of the University of Arkansas System, is located in southeastern Arkansas in the beautiful timberlands, rich in outdoor recreation activities, and approximately 100 miles south of Little Rock. UAM is a comprehensive, residential and commuter, undergraduate institution also offering selected master\u2019s degree programs. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please submit a request via the OEOC website: \u00a0Applicants are required to submit a request for each position to which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 870-460-1422 . Department: Forestry / Agri / Nat. Resourc Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Attend graduate classes and perform research duties related to assigned project. Qualifications: Bachelor of Science in natural resources or related field Additional Information: Salary Information: $20,400 Required Documents to Apply: None Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Valerie Harvey, harvey@uamont.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAM--Monticello-Campus/Graduate-Assistant_R0088831-2": {"title": "Graduate Assistant", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-24\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Graduate Assistant Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Less than Annual Appointment (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Monticello UAM, one of twenty campuses of the University of Arkansas System, is located in southeastern Arkansas in the beautiful timberlands, rich in outdoor recreation activities, and approximately 100 miles south of Little Rock. UAM is a comprehensive, residential and commuter, undergraduate institution also offering selected master\u2019s degree programs. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please submit a request via the OEOC website: \u00a0Applicants are required to submit a request for each position to which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 870-460-1422 . Department: Forestry / Agri / Nat. Resourc Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Attend graduate classes and perform research duties related to assigned project. Qualifications: Bachelor of Science in natural resources or related field Additional Information: Salary Information: 20,400 Required Documents to Apply: None Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Valerie Harvey, harvey@uamont.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAMS/Clinical-Instructor-Professor_R0088906-1": {"title": "Clinical Instructor/Professor", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-24\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/05/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: CON | College of Nursing DNP Programs Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Pediatric Nurse Practitioner (PNP) Program Faculty member provides pediatric specialty expertise, instruction, mentorship, and academic support within the UAMS College of Nursing Department of Graduate Studies and Faculty Affairs. This faculty member collaborates with pediatric specialty faculty and colleagues across College of Nursing programs to deliver high-quality graduate nursing education. This is a full-time, 12-month tenure-track or non-tenure-track faculty appointment that may be based at the UAMS Little Rock or Northwest Arkansas campus. The primary focus is teaching and mentoring, with additional contributions to the College of Nursing\u2019s research, scholarship, service, and clinical practice missions. Upon approval, the selected candidate may be eligible for a practice agreement that allows a percentage of the faculty contract to be supported through clinical practice. Qualifications: Doctoral degree in nursing. Current, unencumbered Advanced Practice Registered Nurse license as a Pediatric Nurse Practitioner. Preferred Qualifications Two or more years of teaching experience in a graduate nursing program. Experience with simulation-based learning. Familiarity with a concept-based curriculum. Eligible for advanced practice nursing licensure in Arkansas. Additional Information: Responsibilities Provides graduate-level instruction in pediatric nursing and advanced practice nursing courses. Advises, mentors, and supports graduate nursing students throughout their academic and professional development. Collaborates with pediatric specialty faculty to plan, deliver, and evaluate the pediatric nurse practitioner curriculum. Works collaboratively with faculty and academic leaders across College of Nursing programs. Participates in curriculum development, course evaluation, and continuous program improvement. Supports the achievement of programmatic outcomes, accreditation standards, and academic objectives. Incorporates current evidence, clinical expertise, and best practices into teaching and student mentorship. Participates in simulation-based learning and other innovative instructional methods, as appropriate. Maintains professional expertise and engagement in the pediatric advanced practice nursing specialty. Contributes to research and scholarly activities consistent with faculty expectations. Participates in service to the College of Nursing, university, profession, and community. Engages in clinical practice activities when applicable and approved. Performs other duties as assigned. Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Standing, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Feeling, Sitting, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Driving, Pulling, Pushing Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Curriculum Vitae, Letters of Recommendation, License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of five Professional References (name, email, business title), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Proof of Veteran Status, Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Plumber-II_R0082059-1": {"title": "Plumber II", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-24\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 08/15/2026 Type of Position: Professional Staff - Facilities Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: OPS | Campus Operations Plumbing Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Journeyman Plumber II position is responsible for the maintenance and repair of plumbing systems that serve medical, educational, and research facilities on the UAMS Campus. These systems are vital to the safety, comfort, and general wellbeing of patients, students and employees. This position is also responsible for resolving all problems and or emergencies that arise from these systems and associated equipment on the UAMS Campus. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications:\u00a0 High school diploma/GED plus five (5) years of plumbing experience Must have a Journeyman Plumber license in accordance with ACA 17-38-301 Computer program proficiency level: Novice Valid Driver\u2019s License\u00a0with fewer than 12 points on their Motor Vehicle Record Preferred Qualifications:\u00a0 6 years of plumbing experience Master's plumbing license Additional Information: Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Crawling, Crouching, Feeling, Kneeling, Reaching, Stooping Frequent Physical Activity: Hearing, Standing, Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Sitting Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Plumber-II_R0087528-1": {"title": "Plumber II", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-24\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 08/15/2026 Type of Position: Professional Staff - Facilities Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: OPS | Campus Operations EO Utility Systems Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: This position is responsible for the maintenance and repair of plumbing systems that serve medical, educational, and research facilities on the UAMS Campus. These systems are vital to the safety, comfort, and general wellbeing of patients, students and employees. This position is also responsible for assisting with all problems and/or emergencies relating to facility issues on the UAMS Campus. The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. All UAMS employees will treat others with Dignity and Respect. We communicate and share complete and unbiased information, assuring our colleagues receive timely, complete, and accurate information in order make informed decisions. We participate in institutional initiatives and encourage the participation of others. We collaborate in policy and program development, implementation, and evaluation using best practices in delivering quality service. All duties will be performed in accordance with the UAMS Core Concepts of Patient and Family Centered Care set forth by UAMS. These core concepts allow for an approach to health care that shapes policies, programs, facility design and staff day-to-day interactions. It leads to better health outcomes and wiser allocation of resources, and greater patient and family satisfaction. The core concepts of patient and family centered care consist of Dignity & Respect, Information Sharing, Participation, and Collaboration. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications:\u00a0 HS diploma/GED 5 years of plumbing experience Arkansas Journeyman\u2019s plumbing license Valid driver\u2019s license with fewer than 12 points on their Motor Vehicle Record Computer program proficiency level: Novice Preferred Qualifications:\u00a0 Master\u2019s plumbing license Additional Information: Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Crawling, Crouching, Reaching, Standing, Stooping, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Hearing, Standing, Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Sitting Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/North-Little-Rock/Academic-Advisor_R0088843-1": {"title": "Academic Advisor", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-23\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 10/31/2026 Type of Position: Professional Staff - Academic Affairs Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas Pulaski Technical College University of Arkansas - Pulaski Technical College at North Little Rock is an integral part of the Arkansas Technical and Community College System maintained by the State of Arkansas. The college is governed by the University of Arkansas System Board of Trustees and a seven-member Board of Visitors and derives its support largely from student tuition and fees and legislative appropriations. UA - Pulaski Tech, a comprehensive two-year college, offers associate degree and certificate programs for students who plan to transfer to four-year colleges and universities and/or for career preparation and advancement. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply link/button. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at (501) 812-2839. Department: Assistant Director of Academic Advising- Main Campus Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Job Duties: Academic advisors assist students in the clarification of their life/career goals and in the development of educational plans. Academic Advisors support the decision-making process of students and help students realize their maximum educational potential through communication and information. Advisors serve as facilitators of communication and coordinators of learning experiences through course and career planning and program progress review, and are agents of referral to other campus services as necessary. Academic Advisor Responsibilities: Provide academic and career advising to current, new, and transfer students throughout the year Participate in New Student Orientation activities to assist students in registration Provide holistic advising services to students within the advisor\u2019s caseload Assist undecided students in the selection of a program of study and mapping a plan to degree completion Help students examine interests and abilities, connecting to career choices Assist students with resources and activities for job preparation and job seeking Interpret and articulate test scores, prior college credits, and required developmental courses for desired program of study Assist students with access to other campus services and resources, to include but not limited to, counseling, disability services and tutoring Provide intervention and support for students on Academic Probation and Suspension, as well as Financial Aid Warning and Suspension to increase retention and completion Participate in development and delivery of training for part-time and/or faculty advisors Participate in professional development and other training opportunities to increase advisor knowledge and skill Other duties as assigned Qualifications: Candidate must possess a Bachelor\u2019s degree.\u00a0 Excellent problem solving, communication, interpersonal, and organizational skills. Customer and solutions oriented with a strong commitment to customer service while maintaining compliance with policies. Commitment to the mission of a comprehensive two-year college and an understanding of the different components of a student services operation. Must be able to articulate and execute public speaking at a level students can understand and learn. Must be flexible and willing to work longer hours during peak times. Preferred Qualifications: Master's Degree Bi-Lingual (Spanish speaking) Additional Information: Salary Information: $40,000 Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume, Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants Recruitment Contact Information: Human Resources humanresources@uaptc.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Motor Vehicle Reports Check, Sex Offender Registry University of Arkansas - Pulaski Technical College is committed to providing a safe campus community. Title IX protects the college community from sexual harassment in a school's education programs and activities. This means that Title IX protects the college community in connection with all academic, educational, extracurricular, athletic, and other programs of the school, whether those programs take place in a school's facilities, in college transportation, at a class or training program sponsored by the school at another location, or elsewhere. \u00a0 We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Repetitive Motion, Sitting, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Walking Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/CBHHS-Dean-s-Staff---Administrative-Analyst_R0088726": {"title": "CBHHS Dean's Staff - Administrative Analyst", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-23\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Clerical Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Little Rock The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is a metropolitan research university that provides an accessible, quality education through flexible learning and unparalleled internship opportunities. At UA Little Rock, we prepare our more than 8,900 students to be innovators and responsible leaders in their fields. Committed to its metropolitan research university mission, UA Little Rock is a driving force in Little Rock's thriving cultural community and a major component of the city and state's growing profile as a regional leader in research, technology transfer, economic development, and job creation. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . Department: CBHHS Associate Dean Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The CBHHS Dean's Staff - Administrative Analyst is responsible for office management and clerical support for the Dean and Associate Deans in the College of Business, Health, and Human Services. This position is governed by state and federal laws and agency policy. Qualifications: Required Education and/or Experience: Associate Degree required with one (1) year of experience in Higher Education or experience in a specialized or a related field applicable to work performed. Other job-related education and/or experience may be substituted for all or part of these basic requirements. \u00a0\u00a0 Preferred Education and/or Experience:\u00a0 Bachelor Degree; Customer Service Experience; Office Management Experience. Job Duties Serve as the primary point of contact for the Dean's office, managing front desk reception, screening calls, greeting visitors, handling inquiries, and maintaining the college contact list; Act as liaison between the Dean's office, students, faculty, staff, and external constituencies, addressing day-to-day issues and directing individuals to the appropriate person as needed; Provide comprehensive administrative support to the Dean and Associate Deans, including scheduling appointments, coordinating meetings with school directors, program coordinators, and faculty, and managing travel arrangements; Organize and facilitate meetings and special events, including scheduling, venue coordination, agenda preparation, minute-taking, and post-meeting follow-up actions; Prepare and assist in producing a variety of documents and materials, including letters, reports, newsletters, outreach materials, curricula, catalogs, and bulletins, and assist in updating the college website; Maintain accurate records and databases by gathering, entering, and updating data; ensure timely processing of documents and procedural forms; and manage office supply inventory and mail pickup and delivery; Build and maintain relationships with external vendors and suppliers to ensure timely, quality service; manage all facilities and maintenance requests; and collaborate with the Institutional Assistant and Finance Director to support school directors as needed; Collaborate with administrative staff across the college to plan events, train new staff, relay information, communicate with university departments on relevant projects, and consistently meet deadlines; Maintain strict confidentiality, pursue professional growth through educational programs and workshops, and perform other duties as assigned; Other duties as assigned. Knowledge, Abilities, and Skills: Excellent written and oral communication skills, presentation and organization skills, and a customer service orientation; Strong customer service abilities; Ability to work in a team environment; Strong computer skills; Ability to manipulate data in a spreadsheet. Additional Information: Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Tusty ten Bensel, Associate Dean, ixzohra@ualr.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Financial Credit Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Sitting, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding Occasional Physical Activity: Kneeling, Reaching, Walking Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Administrative-Specialist-III_R0088445-1": {"title": "Administrative Specialist III", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-23\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Clerical Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: Division of Agriculture of the University of Arkansas The University of Arkansas System Division of Agriculture is a state wide campus, with faculty based on University campuses, at Research and Extension Centers and in every Arkansas county. It consists of the Arkansas Agricultural Experiment Station (AES) and the Arkansas Cooperative Extension Service (CES), and is home to more than 1400 employees.\u00a0 The Division was established in 1959 and is headed by the Vice-President for Agriculture.\u00a0 The Division headquarters is located in Little Rock with the rest of the University of Arkansas System Administration.\u00a0 As an employer, the University of Arkansas System Division of Agriculture offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance.\u00a0 Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process and require reasonable accommodations, please contact the Division's Office of Program & Employment Compliance at compliance@uada.edu . For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-671-2219 or 479-502-9820. Department: Vines 4H Center * 4H Center Director Department's Website: https://thevinescenter.org/ Summary of Job Duties: The Administrative Specialist\u00a0III\u00a0for 4-H Operations is responsible for coordinating office activities, researching & preparing special reports, & developing, revising, & recommending administrative policies & procedures as directed by supervisor. The position is located at the Vines 4-H Center. Duties: Ordering office supplies. Assisting in the gift shop when needed. Doing remote bank deposits as well as preparing cash deposits. Supporting the 4-H Foundation by keeping records and sending thank you letters to donors. Assist guests as needed. Answering all incoming calls and transferring calls to the appropriate department/person. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications The formal education equivalent of a high school diploma; plus one year of specialized training in business management, business education, or a related field; plus three years of experience in specialized or a related field applicable to work performed. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Knowledge of the principles & practices of mathematics & statistics. Knowledge of research & analysis techniques & methods. Knowledge of work-related subject area. Knowledge of computers & software applications. Ability to prepare, present, & review oral & written information & reports. Ability to research & analyze related work program information. Ability to develop, recommend, interpret, & apply policies & procedures. Ability to analyze financial records & prepare reports. Ability to plan, organize, & direct the work of others. Additional Information: For technical assistance with the application process, please email humanresources@uada.edu \u00a0 Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience. Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: J.J. Pitman, 4-H Center Director jpitman@uada.edu 501-821-4444 All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas System Division of Agriculture may conduct pre-employment background checks on certain positions for applicants being considered for employment. \u00a0 The background checks may include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. \u00a0 Required checks are identified in the position listing. \u00a0 A criminal background check or arrest pending adjudication information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absences of a relationship to the requirements of the position. \u00a0 Background check information will be used in a consistent, non-discriminatory manner consistent with the state and federal law. \u00a0 The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Talking Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAMS/Assistant-or-Associate-Professor---CHP-Physician-Assistant_R0088752-1": {"title": "Assistant or Associate Professor - CHP Physician Assistant", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-22\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/05/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: CHP | Physician Assistant Studies Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The College of Health Professions at the University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) seeks applicants for a full-time faculty position in the Department of Physician Assistant Studies located at the UAMS campus in Little Rock, Arkansas. This is an exciting opportunity for a creative, resourceful individual to contribute to an established, high quality program that enjoys strong institutional and community support. The faculty position is a 12-month position at the rank of assistant or associate professor. Salary and academic rank are commensurate with qualifications. Position Description A faculty member (Assistant/Associate Professor) will have the primary responsibility of assisting with the implementation, evaluation, and revision of the didactic and clinical curriculum. This individual will be responsible for presenting lectures and laboratory instruction, developing and grading examinations and assignments, and recruiting guest lecturers. They will also be actively involved with student advising and admissions, faculty meetings, committees, and scholarly activity. This will be tenure-track or non-tenure-track position. Reporting The faculty member reports to the PA Chair/Program Director. Annual performance evaluations will be conducted by the PA Program Director with input from faculty and staff. The Program The UAMS Master of Physician Assistant Studies Program is a continuous, 28-month, full-time professional degree program. A new cohort begins each year in mid-May and completes the program at the end of August, approximately two years later. The program prepares physician assistants with a broad foundation of medical knowledge and clinical skills to provide high-quality, compassionate care to diverse patient populations under the supervision of a licensed physician. The cohort-based program follows a structured, lock-step curriculum. Students must successfully complete all courses each semester and remain in good academic standing to progress. Didactic Phase: The first 13 months include intensive classroom instruction, laboratory experiences, seminars, patient simulation, service-learning activities, and clinical patient encounters. Clinical Phase: The final 15 months include 10 core clinical rotations, two elective rotations, a capstone project, and a summative evaluation. Core rotations include family medicine, internal medicine, inpatient medicine, women\u2019s health, emergency medicine, surgical medicine, pediatric medicine, behavioral medicine, orthopedic medicine, and geriatric medicine. Clinical experiences take place at UAMS and partner facilities throughout Arkansas. The program admits a small cohort of 40 students and maintains an approximately 4-to-1 student-to-faculty ratio during the didactic phase. Each student is paired with a faculty advisor throughout the program and benefits from early patient-care experiences and service learning. Unique program resources and experiences include the 12th Street Health and Wellness Center, Student Success Center, Student Wellness Center, interprofessional education, and mindfulness training. Setting The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) is the only academic health sciences university in the state of Arkansas and the state\u2019s largest public employer with more than 12,000 employees in 73 of Arkansas\u2019 75 counties. UAMS offers 64 professional and specialist degree programs and certificates through our Colleges of Health Professions, Medicine, Nursing, Pharmacy, Public Health and Graduate School. The campus offers state of the art library and clinical simulation facilities. Programs at the campus are designed to promote inter-professional learning and clinical experiences. Application Process Application with a current curriculum vitae, a letter of application, and at least three professional references is currently being accepted via the UAMS Jobs Portal. References will only be contacted for semi-finalists. Evaluation of application will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Edward L. Williams, DMSc, M.Ed., PA-C Chair, Department of Physician Assistant Studies Director, Physician Assistant Program Associate Professor UAMS College of Health Professions ELWilliams2@uams.edu For additional information on the Department of Physician Assistant Studies, the College of Health Professions, and UAMS, please visit our website at: https://healthprofessions.uams.edu/physician-assistant/master-of-physician-assistant-studies/about/ Qualifications: Graduation from an accredited physician assistant or medical program. Master\u2019s degree. Current National Commission on Certification of Physician Assistants (NCCPA) certification. At least three years of clinical experience as a practicing physician assistant or physician. Eligibility for professional licensure in the state of Arkansas. Strong commitment to supporting the missions of the department, college, and university. Preferred Qualifications Doctoral degree. Teaching experience in physician assistant education or a related field. Five or more years of clinical experience. Additional Information: Responsibilities Participate in the design, implementation, coordination, evaluation, and revision of the didactic and clinical curricula. Support the ARC-PA continuing accreditation application and maintenance processes. Assist with developing, reviewing, and revising the program\u2019s mission statement, goals, and competencies. Participate in ongoing program self-assessment and evaluation activities, including the Annual Program Assessment Retreat. Serve as course director for assigned didactic courses. Recruit and orient qualified lecturers for didactic courses. Instruct physician assistant students in areas of knowledge and expertise. Provide academic advising to physician assistant students. Ensure remedial instruction is available to students as needed. Participate in student recruitment, admissions, and interviews. Provide laboratory instruction during the didactic and clinical phases of the program. Evaluate student performance by grading written assignments, examinations, Objective Structured Clinical Examinations (OSCEs), practical skill competencies, and oral presentations. Participate in faculty meetings and retreats, as well as departmental, college, and university committees. Maintain current National Commission on Certification of Physician Assistants (NCCPA) certification. Participate in appropriate local, state, and national physician assistant educational and professional associations. Participate in clinical practice or research activities based on the tenure-track or non-tenure-track appointment, as determined by the Department Chair/Program Director. Maintain high standards of professionalism and integrity while serving as a positive role model for physician assistant students. Refrain from serving as a medical provider for students enrolled in the Physician Assistant program. Participate actively in community service and service-learning activities associated with the Physician Assistant program. Perform other duties and responsibilities as assigned by the Department Chair/Program Director. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Curriculum Vitae, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/North-Little-Rock/YouthBuild-BRIDGE-Case-Manager--LCSW_R0088770": {"title": "YouthBuild BRIDGE Case Manager--LCSW", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-22\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 10/31/2026 Type of Position: Staff (Non-Classified) Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas Pulaski Technical College University of Arkansas - Pulaski Technical College at North Little Rock is an integral part of the Arkansas Technical and Community College System maintained by the State of Arkansas. The college is governed by the University of Arkansas System Board of Trustees and a seven-member Board of Visitors and derives its support largely from student tuition and fees and legislative appropriations. UA - Pulaski Tech, a comprehensive two-year college, offers associate degree and certificate programs for students who plan to transfer to four-year colleges and universities and/or for career preparation and advancement. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply link/button. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at (501) 812-2839. Department: Chancellor Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The YouthBuild BRIDGE Case Manager--LCSW will provide specialized services to participants in the YouthBuild BRIDGE program. This is a three year grant with potential for renewal. The LCSW services will include facilitating educational opportunities and addressing participants\u2019 emotional, financial, and community needs, while modeling best practices in psychosocial care for participants\u2019 future endeavors in academia or the skilled workforce. Participants are placed in a cohort model with four cohorts and approximately 17 participants in each cohort. WORK LOCATION(S): University of Arkansas \u2013 Pulaski Technical College is a public technical college in North Little Rock, Arkansas. It is part of the University of Arkansas System and mainly serves the Central Arkansas region, along with Little Rock to the south. This position will primarily work from the I30 South Campus and Providence Park at 6900 Green Road, Mabelvale, Arkansas. POSITION HIGHLIGHTS \u2022 Be responsible for providing a full range of social work services including psychosocial assessment, treatment referral and resource referral(s) \u2022 Collaboration: Works collaboratively with participants, interdisciplinary team members, community resources and agencies. \u2022 Communication: Communicates timely, relevant and accurate information to all parties involved with participants\u2019 matriculation through the program. \u2022 Coordination: Integrates the work of all parties, resources, and services necessary to accomplish agreed-upon goals. \u2022 Advocacy: Advocates on behalf of the participants and identifies needed services and resources. \u2022 Resource Management: Assures appropriate utilization of all resources to achieve optimal outcomes. \u2022 Accountability: Accepts responsibility and accountability for achievement of optimal outcomes within their scope of practice. \u2022 Professionalism: Acquires and maintains knowledge and competence related to the expectations of their position and practices within their scope. GRANT GOALS (some may be repetitive) --Conduct eligibility verification and develop Individual Service Strategies --Coordinate supportive services --Track measurable skill gains and credential attainment --Maintain follow-up contact and retention documentation --Facilitate referral to Adult Education and Career Pathways services PRIMARY JOB RESPONSIBILITIES \u2022 Provide psychosocial support to participants. \u2022 Complete clinical assessments as per program standards. \u2022 In collaboration with a multidisciplinary team, develop and implement participant handbook; select candidates; and connect participants to services available at UA-PTC or community \u2022 Psychoeducation on burnout \u2022 Help participants navigate their own unique pressures \u2022 Provide group therapy- clinical and psycho-educational \u2022 Conduct research and assessment of program and participant successes \u2022 Work with performance and test anxiety \u2022 Provide referrals for learning disability testing \u2022 Substance use therapy and education \u2022 Address food, housing, and transportation insecurities \u2022 Assist with job or registered apprenticeship interview preparation \u2022 Discuss with participants their actual needs and collaborate with steering committee to meet these needs. \u2022 Miscellaneous duties as assigned. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: A Master of Social Work Degree from a program accredited by the Council on Social Work Education LCSW in the state of Arkansas Preferred Qualifications: Experience with construction industry Additional Information: Salary Information: $65,000 Required Documents to Apply: Curriculum Vitae, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume, Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants Recruitment Contact Information: Human Resources humanresources@uaptc.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Motor Vehicle Reports Check, Sex Offender Registry University of Arkansas - Pulaski Technical College is committed to providing a safe campus community. Title IX protects the college community from sexual harassment in a school's education programs and activities. This means that Title IX protects the college community in connection with all academic, educational, extracurricular, athletic, and other programs of the school, whether those programs take place in a school's facilities, in college transportation, at a class or training program sponsored by the school at another location, or elsewhere. \u00a0 We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Repetitive Motion, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Feeling, Grasping, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching Occasional Physical Activity: Crouching Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Administrative-Operations-Coordinator_R0088720": {"title": "Administrative Operations Coordinator", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-22\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Staff (Non-Classified) Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Little Rock The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is a metropolitan research university that provides an accessible, quality education through flexible learning and unparalleled internship opportunities. At UA Little Rock, we prepare our more than 8,900 students to be innovators and responsible leaders in their fields. Committed to its metropolitan research university mission, UA Little Rock is a driving force in Little Rock's thriving cultural community and a major component of the city and state's growing profile as a regional leader in research, technology transfer, economic development, and job creation. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . Department: Student Affairs Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Division of Student Affairs Administrative Operations Coordinator is an administrative support position that serves as an initial point of contact for visitors to the Office of the Vice Chancellor for Student Affairs. This position will provide administrative support, fiscal Support, and communication support. This position requires in-person, on-site work during university business hours (Monday\u2013Friday, 8:00 a.m.\u20135:00 p.m.). This position is governed by state and federal laws, and agency/institution policy. Qualifications: Required Education and/or Experience The formal education equivalent of an associate degree, plus two (2) years of experience in program administration or related area. Other job-related education and/or experience may be substituted for all or part of these basic requirements. Preferred Education and/or Experience Bachelor\u2019s degree; Experience working with a diverse population; Previous experience working with college students; Strong understanding of navigating policies and procedures, procurement, vendors, and other financial tasks. Job Duties and Responsibilities Front Desk & Administrative Support (40%) Manage front desk operations for the Office of the Vice Chancellor for Student Affairs, ensuring professional and responsive service; Serve as the primary point of contact for students, faculty, staff, parents/guardians, and visitors; Answer phones, route calls, and respond to general inquiries; Schedule meetings and assist with calendar coordination for office leadership; Coordinate meeting logistics, room reservations, and preparation of meeting materials;\u00a0 Prepare and format routine correspondence, reports, and meeting materials; Maintain organized filing systems (paper and electronic) Office Operations & Coordination (35%) Coordinate daily office operations, including maintenance requests, supply procurement, and inventory tracking; Assist with organizing and maintaining office systems, records, and shared resources; Coordinate and maintain office systems, records, shared resources, and operational procedures to support efficient office operations;\u00a0 Support workflow coordination and ensure timely completion of administrative tasks; Maintain internal contact lists and resource information to support office operations: Serve as an initial point of contact for student inquiries and concerns and assist with connecting students to appropriate university resources and services;\u00a0 Provide general information and guidance on university services, policies, and procedures; Report student concerns to the Executive Manager for Student Affairs to ensure the\u00a0 Inform the Executive Manager for Student Affairs of routine concerns and of complex or sensitive issues that require escalation. Fiscal & Administrative Support (10%) Assist with purchasing processes, including requisitions and ordering supplies; Support travel authorizations and reimbursement documentation; Maintain basic tracking of expenditures and assist with resolving routine administrative or financial issues; Provide administrative support for financial reporting processes as needed. Program & Staff Support (10%) Assist with coordinating schedules and tasks for student workers; Support onboarding processes and basic training coordination for student employees; Assist with planning and logistics for meetings, events, and divisional activities; Provide general support for employee engagement initiatives and office activities. Assist as needed with division-level communications; Coordinate the development of a regular Student Affairs newsletter; Prepare drafts, letters, memoranda, reports, etc. for final copy. Special Projects & Additional Duties ( 5%) Assist with special projects and divisional initiatives as assigned; Perform other duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Knowledge of Banner and Workday systems; Knowledge of university budget and finance policies, procedures, and operations; Knowledge of state, federal, and university rules, regulations, and procedures; Ability to work in a diverse and dynamic environment; Ability to work collaboratively and independently with common goals as a part of a team; Ability to make sound judgments and assist in resolving student concerns; Effective interpersonal communication, writing, and organizational abilities; Civility in all interactions of a public or confidential nature; Demonstrate follow-up contacts and consultations in a timely manner; Ability to coordinate the activities of campus academic and/or social programs;\u00a0 Ability to evaluate collected information and formulate recommendations; Ability to compile information into report form. Additional Information: Salary Information: $30,733 Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Shannon Maxwell Executive Manager for the Division of Student Affairs 501-916-3328 smaxwell@ualr.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Financial Credit Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Repetitive Motion, Sitting, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Repetitive Motion, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Balancing, Stooping Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Extra-Help---Marketing-Assistant_R0088762": {"title": "Extra Help / Marketing Assistant", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-22\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Clerical Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Little Rock The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is a metropolitan research university that provides an accessible, quality education through flexible learning and unparalleled internship opportunities. At UA Little Rock, we prepare our more than 8,900 students to be innovators and responsible leaders in their fields. Committed to its metropolitan research university mission, UA Little Rock is a driving force in Little Rock's thriving cultural community and a major component of the city and state's growing profile as a regional leader in research, technology transfer, economic development, and job creation. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . Department: ASBTDC Department's Website: asbtdc.org Summary of Job Duties: The Extra Help/Marketing Assistant designs graphics and creates media to support ASBTDC\u2019s traditional and digital marketing efforts. The position also contributes to special projects and events to fulfill the goals and strategic initiatives of the organization. The ideal candidate will be a creative and skilled graphic artist who produces professional-caliber work using a wide variety of media techniques. This is an hourly (20 hours per week), grant-funded, non-benefits eligible position. This position is governed by state and federal laws and agency/institution policy. Qualifications: Required Education and/or Experience: Formal high school diploma; Portfolio of samples of design work. Preferred Education and/or Experience: Significant secondary coursework or bachelor's degree in art, design, marketing, communications, or related field;\u00a0 Experience creating graphics for print and digital output; Small business knowledge or work experience; WordPress knowledge or experience; Video editing knowledge or experience. Job Duties and Responsibilities Design Collaborate on conceiving, developing, and designing materials for use in marketing ASBTDC services to Arkansas entrepreneurs and small businesses and educating key stakeholders on the impact of ASBTDC services; Design digital and print pieces, such as flyers, social media images, e-books, banners, presentations, reels, and maps, for ASBTDC marketing and educational purposes; Distill and interpret statistics to produce easy-to-understand charts, infographics, and reports; Apply established brand guidelines, ensuring colors, typography, and logo usage are uniform across all touchpoints; Organize and maintain design files and templates; Ensure files are correctly formatted and print-ready for vendors; Assist ASBTDC staff and offices to fulfill their design requests and meet event and project deadlines. Other Job Duties Contribute to ASBTDC\u2019s brand, visual identity, and messaging; Support organizational marketing, training, and outreach activities; Work cooperatively with staff to provide high-quality service; Maintain confidentiality and adhere to the University System and ASBTDC Conflict of Interest standards; Perform other duties as assigned to accomplish the goals and mission of the organization. \u00a0 Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Proficiency in Adobe Creative Suite, Canva, Google Workspace, and Microsoft Office Suite; Excellent written and verbal communication skills and the ability to communicate professionally by email, telephone, and face to face; Strong organizational skills and attention to detail; Ability to prioritize and manage multiple projects; Ability to manage multiple assignments and deadlines; Ability to maintain confidentiality. Additional Information: Salary Information: $21/hr Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Other (see special instructions for details), Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Samples of design work (minimum of five pieces) Recruitment Contact Information: Gwen Green, ASBTDC Marketing and Communications Manager, gagreen@ualr.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: No Background Check Required The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting Frequent Physical Activity: Talking Occasional Physical Activity: Grasping, Pulling, Pushing, Walking Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAM--Monticello-Campus/Institutional-Services-Assistant-Custodial-Services_R0088751-2": {"title": "Institutional Services Assistant-Custodial Services", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-22\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Skilled Labor Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Monticello UAM, one of twenty campuses of the University of Arkansas System, is located in southeastern Arkansas in the beautiful timberlands, rich in outdoor recreation activities, and approximately 100 miles south of Little Rock. UAM is a comprehensive, residential and commuter, undergraduate institution also offering selected master\u2019s degree programs. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please submit a request via the OEOC website: \u00a0Applicants are required to submit a request for each position to which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 870-460-1422 . Department: Residence Halls Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Institutional Services Assistant is responsible for general cleaning of areas in and around office buildings, classrooms, lecture halls, conference rooms, auditoriums, resident halls, dining areas, building common areas, and other areas as required. This position is governed by state and federal laws and agency policy. Qualifications: Minimum qualifications include the completion of sufficient education or training to read and write. Job related education and/or experience may be substituted for all or part of these basic requirements. Additional Information: Salary Information: $22,000.00-$23,000.00 Required Documents to Apply: None Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Jessica L. Foxworth Associate Vice Chancellor for Student Engagement and Dean of Students 870-460-1110 All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Crouching, Feeling, Kneeling, Lifting, Reaching, Repetitive Motion, Standing, Stooping, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Crouching, Feeling, Lifting, Reaching, Standing, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Climbing Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAMS/Program-Director--Baptist-Health-UAMS-Transitional-Year-Program_R0088704-1": {"title": "Program Director, Baptist Health UAMS Transitional Year Program", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-20\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 10/03/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: NWA | Administration Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Transitional Year Program Director provides leadership, administration, and educational oversight for the ACGME-accredited Transitional Year Residency Program. The Program Director is responsible for the design, implementation, evaluation, and continuous improvement of the residency program; compliance with ACGME Institutional, Common, and Transitional Year Program Requirements; resident recruitment and development; faculty engagement; and achievement of program aims and outcomes. The Program Director fosters a supportive learning environment that prepares residents for advanced specialty training and promotes excellence in patient care, professionalism, well-being, and scholarly activity. This position serves within the Baptist Health\u2013UAMS Medical Education Program, a partnership between Baptist Health\u2014the largest private health care system in Arkansas\u2014and the University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS), the state\u2019s only academic health sciences university. This collaboration combines the academic excellence and research resources of UAMS with Baptist Health\u2019s community-based care model to train compassionate, skilled family physicians who are prepared to meet the evolving health needs of Arkansas and beyond. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications MD or DO degree from an accredited institution. Board certification by an ABMS or AOA-approved specialty board in a discipline relevant to the educational program. Eligibility for and ability to maintain an unrestricted Arkansas medical license. Minimum of three years of documented educational and/or administrative experience in graduate medical education. Demonstrated commitment to resident education, mentorship, and academic leadership. Excellent interpersonal, communication, organizational, and leadership skills. Preferred Qualifications Prior experience as a Residency Program Director, Associate Program Director, or Core Faculty member. Experience with ACGME accreditation processes, site visits, self-studies, and ADS reporting. Experience in curriculum design, resident assessment, faculty development, and quality improvement. Demonstrated success fostering inclusive learning environments and resident well-being initiatives. Protected Time and Support The position includes protected administrative time and institutional support commensurate with ACGME requirements and program needs. Additional Information: Essential Duties and Responsibilities Provide strategic and operational leadership for all aspects of the Transitional Year Residency Program. Maintain substantial involvement in resident education and program administration. Ensure ongoing compliance with ACGME accreditation requirements, policies, and reporting obligations. Develop, implement, and evaluate curriculum, required rotations, electives, didactics, quality improvement, patient safety, and professional development activities. Lead resident recruitment, selection, onboarding, mentoring, and career advising activities. Oversee competency-based assessments, Milestones reporting, semiannual resident review, promotion, remediation, and graduation decisions. Chair or oversee the Clinical Competency Committee and Program Evaluation Committee. Conduct Annual Program Evaluation and implement continuous quality improvement initiatives. Monitor resident well-being, professionalism, supervision, patient safety, and duty hour compliance. Recruit, support, and develop faculty participating in the residency program. Collaborate with institutional leadership, the DIO, GMEC, participating sites, and specialty departments. Maintain accurate program records, Accreditation Data System updates, and preparation for accreditation reviews and site visits. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Texarkana/Faculty-Welding_R0086234-2": {"title": "Faculty-Welding", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-20\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Faculty - Non-Tenure Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas Community College at Hope - Texarkana The University of Arkansas Community College at Hope-Texarkana (UACCHT) is a proud member of the University of Arkansas System.\u00a0 The University of Arkansas System is comprised of land-grant research institutions, a teaching hospital, five community colleges, two schools of law, a presidential school, a residential math and science high school, and an online university, as well as divisions of agriculture, archaeology and criminal justice. These entities exhibit unmatched economic and social impact across the state by providing numerous academic and professional opportunities. Below you will find the details for the position currently available at UACCHT including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.\u00a0 To apply for the position, please click the Apply link/button. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the\u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please submit a request via Email to: wendy.jones@uaht.edu or by phone at 870-722-8176.\u00a0\u00a0 Applicants are required to submit a separate request for each position in which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at wendy.jones@uaht.edu or by phone at 870-722-8176. Department: Business Trade and Industrial Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Applicants should have three to five years of experience in the welding industry and demonstrate proficiency in Shielded Metal Arc Welding (SMAW), Gas Metal Arc Welding (GMAW/MIG), and Gas Tungsten Arc Welding (GTAW/TIG). Experience with oxy-fuel cutting, plasma cutting, blueprint reading, fabrication, and welding safety practices is preferred. Applicants should demonstrate the ability to teach both classroom and hands-on laboratory instruction while maintaining a safe and productive learning environment. It is also important for this individual to have a willingness to work with local industries and instructors in other technical areas to further the technical offerings at University of Arkansas Community College at Hope-Texarkana. Qualifications: Experience in Welding Technology, Industrial Technology, General Technology, or a related field is required. Comparable formal education or training, including military training, may also be considered. Industry certifications such as American Welding Society (AWS) certifications are a plus. Additional Information: Salary Information: Base $34,800.00. Commensurate with education and teaching experience. Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume, Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Wendy Jones 870-722-8176 All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check The University of Arkansas Community College at Hope-Texarkana (UACCHT) is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check, sex offender registry check, and drug screen. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check and/or a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check.\u00a0 A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Standing, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Sitting, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Hope/Dean-of-Secondary-Programs_R0071853": {"title": "Dean of Secondary Programs", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-20\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Senior Administration - Academic Deans Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas Community College at Hope - Texarkana The University of Arkansas Community College at Hope-Texarkana (UACCHT) is a proud member of the University of Arkansas System.\u00a0 The University of Arkansas System is comprised of land-grant research institutions, a teaching hospital, five community colleges, two schools of law, a presidential school, a residential math and science high school, and an online university, as well as divisions of agriculture, archaeology and criminal justice. These entities exhibit unmatched economic and social impact across the state by providing numerous academic and professional opportunities. Below you will find the details for the position currently available at UACCHT including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.\u00a0 To apply for the position, please click the Apply link/button. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the\u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please submit a request via Email to: wendy.jones@uaht.edu or by phone at 870-722-8176.\u00a0\u00a0 Applicants are required to submit a separate request for each position in which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at wendy.jones@uaht.edu or by phone at 870-722-8176. Department: Division of Academics Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Dean of Secondary Programs provides visionary leadership and oversight for the Hope Collegiate Academy, Texarkana Collegiate Academy, Hope Secondary Career Center, and Texarkana Secondary Career Center. The Dean serves as a critical liaison between the University of Arkansas Hope-Texarkana and area school districts, ensuring high-quality academic and career pathways for high school students while maintaining compliance with state policies and institutional goals. This position supports collaborative planning and implementation of academic programming, student advising, budget management, scheduling, registration, and stakeholder communication. The Dean fosters a culture of academic excellence, student success, and program growth. Key Responsibilities: Collegiate Academy Programs \u00b7 Serve as the primary administrator for the Hope and Texarkana Collegiate Academies. \u00b7 Collaborate with UAHT and local school district leadership to develop and implement academic schedules, daily operations, and instructional programming. \u00b7 Organize and deliver student and parent/guardian orientations. \u00b7 Enroll, register, and advise students each semester. \u00b7 Monitor academic progress and support student success through communication with faculty and administrators. \u00b7 Assist with student discipline in collaboration with the UAHT Dean of Students and Vice Chancellor of Student Services. \u00b7 Develop and manage program budgets and policies. \u00b7 Plan and lead an annual college visit to the University of Arkansas. \u00b7 Work with UAHT Communications and the high schools to market and promote the academies. \u00b7 Help maintain both academies' social media pages. \u00b7 Maintain awareness of state policies, high school graduation requirements, and develop annual MOUs with partner districts. Secondary Career Center Programs \u00b7 Collaborate with service-area school districts to promote and grow enrollment in career center programs. \u00b7 Work with the UAHT Dean of Business, Trade, and Industry to coordinate course scheduling and staffing. \u00b7 Register and advise students enrolled in career and technical education (CTE) pathways. \u00b7 Manage career center budgets and student degree plans. \u00b7 Attend state-level career center director meetings and stay current on CTE policy developments. \u00b7 Develop MOUs for each participating school district and create marketing materials to support enrollment and awareness. \u00b7 Serve as the primary point of contact for school districts regarding career center programming and compliance. \u00b7 Order necessary student supplies. Qualifications: Master\u2019s degree in Education, Educational Leadership, or a related field. \u00b7 At least three years of experience in secondary or postsecondary education, with supervisory or administrative responsibilities. \u00b7 Strong understanding of dual credit/early college high school programs and CTE pathways. \u00b7 Demonstrated ability to collaborate with K\u201312 and higher education stakeholders. \u00b7 Excellent communication, leadership, and organizational skills. Preferred Qualifications: \u00b7 Arkansas building-level or district-level administrator certification. \u00b7 Experience with program development, student advising, or academic scheduling. \u00b7 Budget management experience. \u00b7 Familiarity with state education policies and requirements for high school and career education. Additional Information: Salary Information: $54,000.00 Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume, Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Optional Documents: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions) Special Instructions to Applicants: Must submit all required documents. Recruitment Contact Information: Kathryn Hopkins 870-722-8164 All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Motor Vehicle Reports Check The University of Arkansas Community College at Hope-Texarkana (UACCHT) is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check, sex offender registry check, and drug screen. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check and/or a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check.\u00a0 A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Standing Occasional Physical Activity: Driving Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Hope/Campus-Police-Officer_R0086240-2": {"title": "Campus Police Officer", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-20\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Professional Staff - Public Safety Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas Community College at Hope - Texarkana The University of Arkansas Community College at Hope-Texarkana (UACCHT) is a proud member of the University of Arkansas System.\u00a0 The University of Arkansas System is comprised of land-grant research institutions, a teaching hospital, five community colleges, two schools of law, a presidential school, a residential math and science high school, and an online university, as well as divisions of agriculture, archaeology and criminal justice. These entities exhibit unmatched economic and social impact across the state by providing numerous academic and professional opportunities. Below you will find the details for the position currently available at UACCHT including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.\u00a0 To apply for the position, please click the Apply link/button. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the\u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please submit a request via Email to: wendy.jones@uaht.edu or by phone at 870-722-8176.\u00a0\u00a0 Applicants are required to submit a separate request for each position in which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at wendy.jones@uaht.edu or by phone at 870-722-8176. Department: Security Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Public Safety Officer is responsible for the enforcement of traffic and criminal laws and parking regulations. This position is governed by law enforcement standards, state and federal laws, and agency policy. Job Summary Responsible for providing campus safety and security and the enforcement of traffic and criminal laws, parking regulations, and institutional policies. The position is governed by law enforcement standards, state and federal laws, and institution policy. The position reports to the Chief of Campus Police. Job Duties and Responsibilities \u00b7 Patrolling campus to detect and prevent crimes, enforcing traffic laws and parking regulations, and identifying safety hazards and violators. \u00b7 Performing safety checks of buildings and securing buildings. \u00b7 Conducting investigations of crimes, accidents, and reporting incidents committed on campus. \u00b7 Directing traffic during periods of high density. \u00b7 Arresting violators, writing incident reports, and testifying in court as necessary. \u00b7 Receiving and investigating incident reports and complaints from students, faculty, staff, and visitors. \u00b7 Cooperating with city, county, and state law enforcement officials in serving warrants, apprehending individuals, and obtaining information associated with investigations. \u00b7 Monitoring security and fire panel for security and fire detection, assisting with checking the alarm systems and emergency power supply. \u00b7 Responding to alarms, calls for assistance, checking for locked or unlocked buildings and offices, as necessary, and assisting stranded motorists and others in need of assistance. \u00b7 Using tactics, as trained and equipped, in preserving the safety of citizens, oneself, and fellow officers. \u00b7 Communicating general and public safety information to students, staff, faculty, and the general public. \u00b7 Detecting, investigating, and reporting breaches of facilities, property damage, missing property, and hazardous conditions; maintaining uniforms and equipment; attending training. \u00b7 Assisting in planning and implementing public service programs and training. \u00b7 Perform other duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities \u00b7 Knowledge of general law enforcement methods and techniques; knowledge of traffic and criminal laws, and parking regulations; ability to enforce laws and regulations, direct traffic, and maintain order. \u00b7 General knowledge of computers. \u00b7 Skilled in the operation of firearms. Ability to demonstrate safety and accuracy in use of firearms, and pass annual state requirement for firearms certification, as well as departmental requirements. \u00b7 Communication Skills: Ability to write and speak clearly and persuasively in positive or negative situations; read and interpret written information. Ability to prepare written reports and logs and to edit work for accuracy and thoroughness, and to monitor own work to ensure quality. Requires STRONG attention to detail. \u00b7 Dependability: Ability to arrive at work on time consistently; follow instructions; respond to management direction; and solicit feedback to improve performance. Special Job Dimensions \u00b7 Occasional exposure to hazardous and/or stressful situations. \u00b7 Ability to stand for extended periods of time in indoor settings, outdoor settings, and in all weather conditions at all times of day. \u00b7 Ability to give chase on foot and apprehend and detain subjects as permitted by law. \u00b7 Must be able to perform all job-related duties while wearing required uniform and duty equipment to include a body armor vest. \u00b7 Must be able to be recalled for duty at all times in case of emergency. Qualifications: The formal education equivalent of a high school diploma \u00b7 Certified as a law enforcement officer by the Arkansas Law Enforcement Standards Training Academy, or a similar academy, in accordance with ACA 12-9-106 \u00b7 Possession of a valid state motor vehicle operator\u2019s license. Additional Information: Salary Information: $37,500 Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Letters of Recommendation, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume, Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Wendy Jones 870-722-8176 All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Child Maltreatment, Criminal Background Check, Financial Credit Check, Motor Vehicle Reports Check, Sex Offender Registry, Substance Abuse Testing The University of Arkansas Community College at Hope-Texarkana (UACCHT) is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check, sex offender registry check, and drug screen. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check and/or a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check.\u00a0 A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Balancing, Climbing, Crawling, Driving, Standing, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Crouching, Hearing, Lifting, Pulling Occasional Physical Activity: Sitting, Stooping Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAM--Monticello-Campus/Part-Time-Faculty_R0088531-1": {"title": "Part Time Faculty", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-20\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Adjunct Faculty Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Less than Annual Appointment (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Monticello UAM, one of twenty campuses of the University of Arkansas System, is located in southeastern Arkansas in the beautiful timberlands, rich in outdoor recreation activities, and approximately 100 miles south of Little Rock. UAM is a comprehensive, residential and commuter, undergraduate institution also offering selected master\u2019s degree programs. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please submit a request via the OEOC website: \u00a0Applicants are required to submit a request for each position to which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 870-460-1422 . Department: Arts and Humanities Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Teach courses in disciplines in the College of Arts, Humanities and Social Sciences Qualifications: Master's degree in the discipline or closely-related field. Applicants with life experience equivalent to a master's degree may be considered. Additional Information: Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience. Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Curriculum Vitae, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Mark Sullivan, Administrative Analyst, 870-460-1078; SullivanM@UAMont.edu Steven Harper, Dean, 870-460-1178; HarperS@UAMont.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/DeWitt/XMLNAME-4-H-Program-Assistant_R0087905-1": {"title": "4-H Program Assistant", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-20\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Clerical Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: Division of Agriculture of the University of Arkansas The University of Arkansas System Division of Agriculture is a state wide campus, with faculty based on University campuses, at Research and Extension Centers and in every Arkansas county. It consists of the Arkansas Agricultural Experiment Station (AES) and the Arkansas Cooperative Extension Service (CES), and is home to more than 1400 employees.\u00a0 The Division was established in 1959 and is headed by the Vice-President for Agriculture.\u00a0 The Division headquarters is located in Little Rock with the rest of the University of Arkansas System Administration.\u00a0 As an employer, the University of Arkansas System Division of Agriculture offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance.\u00a0 Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process and require reasonable accommodations, please contact the Division's Office of Program & Employment Compliance at compliance@uada.edu . For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-671-2219 or 479-502-9820. Department: CEA * Staff Chair * Arkansas County Department's Website: uada.edu Summary of Job Duties: The Cooperative Extension Service Program Assistant works for an assigned county Extension program under the supervision of a county agent in 4-H and youth development areas. Self-Management \u2022 Organizes and prioritizes tasks effectively. \u2022 Deals appropriately with interruptions. \u2022 Uses good judgment and decision-making skills. \u2022 Follows attendance and leave policies. \u2022 Practices emotional control. \u2022 Exhibits professional behavior and appearance. \u2022 Ability to work without close supervision. Quality and Quantity of Work \u2022 Maintains 4-H Clubs. Periodically attends 4-H Club meetings. \u2022 Maintains working relationship with all 4-H leaders, members, and parents. \u2022 Recruits adult volunteer leaders youth, and volunteers to form 4-H clubs and grow the community 4-H enrollment/program. \u2022 Follows up promptly with questions and requests for information. \u2022 Maintains accurate 4-H records and submits reports by deadlines. \u2022 Displays acknowledge of 4-H policies and procedures. \u2022 Stays informed of all county, district, and state 4-H events, competitions, camps, activities, etc. Informs 4-H leaders, members and parents of all county, district, and state 4-H events, competitions, camps, activities, etc. Assists 4-Her in preparation for events and competitions. \u2022 Plans, organizes, sets-up, conducts, and cleans-up after all 4-H events, competitions, and activities in the county. \u2022 Conducts regular 4-H leader training meetings. Program Delivery \u2022 Shows sensitivity to individual needs based on culture, race, gender and age. \u2022 Coordinated with agents to conducting educational programs in schools and the community. \u2022 Evaluates the county 4-H program for impact. Communication \u2022 Communicates the benefits and goals of the 4-H program to clientele. \u2022 Makes sure youth, parents and adult leaders are aware of events, activates, meetings and any registration deadlines. \u2022 Uses social media, virtual tools and newsletters to communicate. \u2022 Uses local newspaper, social media and other tools to promote 4-H. \u2022 Listens to feedback and acts to improve. Teamwork \u2022 Shares information, expertise and resources with others. \u2022 Is part of the county Extension Service team to insure and success of the whole Extension program. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications High School diploma or equivalent required. Must have reliable transportation for use on the job with liability insurance in effect. Must successfully complete the standard background check which includes the Arkansas Child Abuse and Neglect Central Registry Check. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Ability to conduct programs and work with all clientele regardless of race, color, national origin, religion, gender, age, disability, marital or veteran status, or any other legally protected status. Ability to communicate effectively, both orally and in writing. Ability to keep accurate records and submit timely reports of activities. Ability to respond positively to supervisor direction. Ability to work without close daily supervision. Additional Information: Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Grant Beckwith, gbeckwith@uada.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Motor Vehicle Reports Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas System Division of Agriculture may conduct pre-employment background checks on certain positions for applicants being considered for employment. \u00a0 The background checks may include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. \u00a0 Required checks are identified in the position listing. \u00a0 A criminal background check or arrest pending adjudication information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absences of a relationship to the requirements of the position. \u00a0 Background check information will be used in a consistent, non-discriminatory manner consistent with the state and federal law. \u00a0 The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Driving, Feeling, Grasping, Standing, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Kneeling, Lifting, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Repetitive Motion, Sitting Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAMS/Child-Development--Technician--Kids-First--Mountain-View-----------------------------Mountain-View-_R0086172-2": {"title": "Child Development  Technician (Kids First, Mountain View)                            Mountain View)", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-20\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/01/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: COM | Peds Kids First Mountain View Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Make a Difference Where It Matters Most! \u2728This position is in Mountain View, AR. Kids First is a compassionate, child-centered program dedicated to serving children with special healthcare needs from six weeks to five years old. Within our pediatric day healthcare clinics, children for with developmental delays and other special medical needs receive intensive, nurturing, and individualized early developmental services\u2014setting the foundation for lifelong growth and success. About the Role: Child Development Technician: In this hands-on and rewarding role, the Child Development Technician partners closely with the Early Childhood Development Specialist to provide daily care, support, and developmental interventions for children from birth to age five with special medical and developmental needs. This position is perfect for someone who is: *Passionate about early childhood development *Caring, patient, and energetic *Motivated to positively impact children and families \ud83c\udf1f Why Join KIDS FIRST? Because here, your work isn\u2019t just a job it\u2019s a calling. Every day, you help children grow, thrive, and reach their full potential which truly changes lives. Qualifications: High School Diploma or GED PLUS six (6) months experience working in the care of children other education can be substituted for experience including CCOT, CDA, AA, or Bachelor\u2019s degree in Early Childhood Education, Child Development, or a related filed. Candidate must pass state abuse registry checks, drug screen, submit to a TB skin test and required immunizations or provide proof of immunizations. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Strong organizational skills Ability to identify educational and developmental needs of children Ability to establish and maintain positive relationships with parents, staff, and other child care professionals Excellent communication skills Knowledge of early childhood curriculum \u00a0 Additional Information: Responsibilities Provides quality direct patient care for a group of young children including serving mealtimes, assisting with feeding, diapering, and dressing. Provides developmentally appropriate behavioral guidance within daily scheduled activities. Follows the direction of the ECDS to provide individualized developmental services of their assigned treatment rooms in a manner that is child-centered, family focused, and demonstrates evidence-based or best practice. Establishes exciting learning environments for young children and apply curriculum to address the objectives contained in each child\u2019s treatment plan. Constant Physical Activity: Feeling, Hearing, Listening Frequent Physical Activity: Climbing, Crawling, Crouching, Grasping, Kneeling, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Repetitive Motion, Standing, Stooping, Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Sitting Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Curriculum Vitae, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Proof of Veteran Status, Resume, Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Clinical-Services-Manager--Labor---Delivery_R0088459-2": {"title": "Clinical Services Manager, Labor & Delivery", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-17\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 11/17/2026 Type of Position: Clinical Staff - Medical Services Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | WISL Inp programs Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Clinical Services Manager (CSM) is responsible for supervising and coordinating daily operations of the Labor & Delivery Unit (E5), including patient care and unit business processes. UAMS Labor and Delivery unit is located in the Harry P. Ward Clinical Tower. The unit consists of 14 LDR rooms, four triage observational beds, two operating rooms suites, a three bed recovery room area and two state of the art Neonatal Stabilization rooms used to stabilize acutely ill neonates with specially trained staff from the Intensive Care Nursery. Labor and Delivery provides high-risk obstetrical care for patients all over the state. The LDR rooms allow the expectant mother to labor, deliver, and recover in the birthing suites with family support. E5 Labor and Delivery supports patient and family centered care and as a result, the newborns, if stable, are allowed to stay with their mother\u2019s after delivery to promote bonding Qualifications: Required Bachelor\u2019s degree in Nursing (BSN) 5 or more years of experience in the field of Nursing, with at least 3 years of experience in a supervisory capacity. Valid Registered Nurse license Preferred Master\u2019s degree in Nursing (MSN) Employees in this role must be fitted for, capable of donning and performing routine tasks in personal protective equipment to include N95 masks, Powered Air Purifying Respirators (PAPR) or Controlled Air Purifying Respirators (CAPR) Additional Information: Key Responsibilities Maintains awareness of unit status and potential problems by functioning as a working supervisor.\u00a0 Serves as a liaison with Director and Administration, exchanging information and identifying problems or needs related to clinical activity. Participates on ad hoc committees, as required, to develop plans related to unit issues. Demonstrates effective analytical abilities to identify unit needs that require intervention and/or revision. Participates in daily unit activity to coordinate unit functions and facilitate problem solving. Demonstrate effective time management and delegation skills to accomplish unit activity within work schedule restrains. Plans measurable unit-related goals and objectives as guidelines for performance. Develops an understanding of the functions of each primary campus departments. Assumes responsibility for successfully fulfilling the standards of licensing and crediting agencies. Develops, interprets, and implements policies, guidelines, protocol, job descriptions, and performance appraisals annually.\u00a0 Interviews, hires, and orients new employees; documents orientation of each new employee, coordinating with personnel and adhering to UAMS policy. Coordinates timely completion of personnel records, including employee promotions/transfers and new employee hiring. Uses both formal and informal evaluation processes to reward or modify employee behavior. Demonstrates good managerial judgment in assigning duties appropriate to each individual, and by conducting all aspects of supervision in a fair, consistent, objective, and professional manner. Maintains a current awareness of the abilities and limitations of each staff member. Monitors and documents tardiness and absenteeism. Coordinates scheduling of leave time. Produces biweekly payroll and maintains documentation of employee time benefits used. \u00a0 Maintains adequate staffing pattern, adjusting assignments and coordination with other Managers as necessary. Supervises and implements Quality Assurance studies, provides reports to appropriate personnel, analyzes and identifies critical factors of patient care to facilitate enhancement of the quality of patient care offered. \u00a0 Conducts annual needs assessment with staff. Participates in formal development of maintenance, capital equipment and staff budgets. Submits documented plan for any physical plant renovation or repair as necessary. Demonstrates cost-conscious awareness by comparing/analyzing unit expenditures monthly against general ledger and effectively utilizing staff, space, and supplies within budgetary restraints. Initiates purchase of new equipment and supplies. Prepares statistical/narrative reports as requested. \u00a0 May perform other duties as assigned. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Annual TB Screening, Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry, Substance Abuse Testing This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Hearing Frequent Physical Activity: Feeling, Grasping, Lifting, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Pulling, Pushing, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Crawling, Crouching, Kneeling, Reaching, Stooping Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/El-Dorado/LPN--El-Dorado--AR-_R0088633": {"title": "LPN (El Dorado, AR)", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-17\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/05/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: REP | CS South El Dorado Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: We are seeking a Licensed Practical Nurse (LPN) at UAMS Family Medical Center in El Dorado, AR! This is your chance to make a real difference by providing personalized, compassionate care to patients and their families. Collaborate with a multidisciplinary team in a vibrant, supportive environment where innovation and patient-centered approaches thrive. As an LPN, you will play a key role in assessing patient needs, administering medications, and facilitating seamless communication between patients and healthcare providers. Under the supervision of a Registered Nurse, you'll work directly with patients and their families to develop and implement tailored health plans. Your responsibilities include triage, assessment, planning, patient education -whether by phone or in-clinic- and ensuring high-quality care at every step. We\u2019re looking for someone who is compassionate, detail-oriented, and energized by delivering exceptional care in a fast-paced, collaborative environment. If you\u2019re ready to contribute to a team dedicated to excellence in family medicine, we want to hear from you. Join us at UAMS and enjoy a fulfilling career where your skills help transform lives! Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: High School, GED or formal educational equivalent. Current and valid LPN license by the State of Arkansas and a Graduate of an accredited nursing program. One\u00a0(1) year of clinical nursing experience or will consider a new grad with a current license and one year of previous medical experience (MA, PCT, CNA). Current BLS certification or must successfully obtain certification within the first 30 days of employment. Must have strong organizational skills and computer knowledge.\u00a0 Preferred Qualifications:\u00a0 Immunization experience.\u00a0\u00a0 CPR certification. Ambulatory experience. EPIC experience. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Strong clinical expertise and technique. Working knowledge of data processing equipment, basic medical terminology, and applications. Attention to communication, oral, written, and persuasive. Must be able to build collaborative relationships. Possess personal credibility. Ability to make independent judgments that have highly significant impacts on the organization. Ability to provide motivational support to an area of responsibility. Strong customer service orientation, patient advocacy, and patient education skills. Must have strong organizational skills and computer knowledge. Intermediate computer skills. Professional and courteous telephone etiquette. General knowledge of office machines, including printers, fax machines, etc. Additional Information: Key Responsibilities : Direct patient care within the limits of the Nurse Practice Act of the State of Arkansas, UAMS policies, procedures, and standards. Accountable for adhering to UAMS care guidelines. Observe patients, charting, and reporting changes in patients' conditions. Provide basic care and treatment of patients. Administer prescribed medications and start intravenous fluids, if needed. Assist patients in standing, walking, and other movements. Answer the patient's call and determine how to assist them. Collect samples such as blood, urine, and sputum from patients and perform routine laboratory tests on samples. Clean rooms and prepare exam room for the next patient. Inventory and requisition supplies and instruments. Record necessary data in regards to intake and output. Models the Core Values of UAMS - Integrity, Respect, Diversity, Teamwork, Creativity, and Excellence in compliance with company guidelines. Performs related responsibilities as required or assigned. *This position will be used to fill multiple vacancies.* Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), Resume Optional Documents: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Letters of Recommendation, List of five Professional References (name, email, business title), Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Resource-Family-Trainer_R0088465": {"title": "Resource Family Trainer", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-16\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Professional Staff - Institutional Affairs Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Little Rock The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is a metropolitan research university that provides an accessible, quality education through flexible learning and unparalleled internship opportunities. At UA Little Rock, we prepare our more than 8,900 students to be innovators and responsible leaders in their fields. Committed to its metropolitan research university mission, UA Little Rock is a driving force in Little Rock's thriving cultural community and a major component of the city and state's growing profile as a regional leader in research, technology transfer, economic development, and job creation. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . Department: MidSOUTH Department's Website: midsouth.ualr.edu Summary of Job Duties: The Resource Family Trainer is responsible for implementing the contracted resource and adoptive parent pre-service training curriculum and completing the home study in partnership with the Division of Children and Family Services. The Resource Family Trainer will receive training and get certified in the contracted resource and adoptive parent training program and the contracted home study model. The person in this position is responsible for the delivery of the contracted training curriculum and home study model to prospective resource and adoptive participants referred to the program for training. This position has regular contact with University personnel, DCFS staff, and other public agencies, community professionals, and the public. This position requires extensive in-state travel and work outside normal office hours. This full-time, annually renewed grant-funded position is directly responsible to the Resource Family Program Director or designee. State and federal laws and agency/institution policy govern this position. Qualifications: Required Education and/or Experience: Bachelor\u2019s Degree in Social Work OR Master\u2019s degree in a related field; One (1) year of professional experience working with families in the child welfare system. \u00a0 Preferred Education and/or Experience: Experience in writing home assessments, psychosocial histories, training in curriculum development, and training delivery; Master\u2019s Degree in Social Work, Psychology, Counseling, with appropriate professional licensure preferred, e.g., LMSW, LCSW, LAC, LPC; Fluent in Spanish. Job Duties and Responsibilities: Training Management: Will receive training and certification in the contracted resource and adoptive parent training program model and the contracted home study model; Facilitate the contracted pre-service training curriculum with prospective resource/adoptive parents who meet the Division's standards for approval or other resource parent pre-service training curriculum approved by DCFS, as needed; Notify the appropriate DCFS Area Directors, Area Resource Workers, and Adoption Specialists of the resource parent pre-service being offered to prospective resource/adoptive parents when requested by supervisor. \u00a0 Assessment Management: Conduct the contracted home study model on prospective resource and adoptive homes in accordance with the criteria set out in the Minimum Licensing Standards for Child Welfare Agencies, Standards for Approval of Resource and Adoptive Homes, and the contracted home study model protocols; Conduct both of the minimally required visits with the applicants in the applicants' home; Provide original contracted home study model elements ( e.g., completed home study report template, questionnaires, psychosocial rating sheets, etc.) to DCFS at the completion of the home study; Submit a completed home study final report to DCFS within the contracted required days as agreed upon by DCFS; Complete all home visits assigned by the supervisor. These home visits may be assigned statewide. \u00a0 Program Management: \u00a0 Receive weekly supervision and problem-solve issues that may arise; Communicate with program participants (phone, email, mail) between sessions, as needed; Complete program documentation and monthly reporting requirements; Attend required monthly and quarterly meetings with Area Resource staff to provide ongoing feedback regarding training needs, problem-solving, and technical assistance. \u00a0 Other duties as assigned. \u00a0 Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Excellent skills in facilitating groups from diverse backgrounds; Skills in conducting home visits; Ability to use assessment tools/collect data; Ability to travel in-state and out-of-state with overnight stays; Knowledge of teaching principles and methods; Ability to coordinate and conduct training programs, as assigned; Ability to prepare reports, maintain records, and ensure documentation in compliance with program deliverables; The ability to work outside of normal office hours is required; Ability to adapt to organizational change and handle multiple tasks; Must have computer skills, including Microsoft Office, and the ability to operate AV equipment. \u00a0 Additional Information: Salary Information: $52,500 - $55,500 Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume, Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Mary Tillman, Administrative Support Manager, mjtillman@midsouth.ualr.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Child Maltreatment, Criminal Background Check, Motor Vehicle Reports Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Driving, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Standing, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Balancing, Climbing, Crawling, Crouching, Feeling, Grasping, Kneeling, Lifting, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Stooping Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Adjunct-Lecturer---Fall-2027-Artist-in-Residence_R0088035": {"title": "Adjunct Lecturer / Fall 2027 Artist in Residence", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-15\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Adjunct Faculty Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Less than Annual Appointment (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Little Rock The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is a metropolitan research university that provides an accessible, quality education through flexible learning and unparalleled internship opportunities. At UA Little Rock, we prepare our more than 8,900 students to be innovators and responsible leaders in their fields. Committed to its metropolitan research university mission, UA Little Rock is a driving force in Little Rock's thriving cultural community and a major component of the city and state's growing profile as a regional leader in research, technology transfer, economic development, and job creation. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . Department: Art and Design Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Windgate Artist in Residence will work in the Windgate Center of Art + Design at the University of Arkansas at Little Rock for the fall 2027 semester. This residency offers the Windgate Artist in Residence the opportunity to make work and to engage with the community of the UA Little Rock School of Art and Design. While in residence, the artist is expected to make work in the provided studio space and/or the shared studio spaces of the building. In addition, artists will interact with students through weekly open studio hours, studio visits to student workspaces, in-class activities hosted by program faculty, and welcome and farewell community receptions. Participating artists will also donate one work of art to the UA Little Rock Art Collection. This position is governed by state and federal laws, and agency/institution policy. Qualifications: Required Education and/or Experience: High School Diploma Preferred Education and/or Experience: MFA, BFA, BA, or commensurate experience; Evidence of active participation in exhibitions at the national or international level; Teaching and/or mentorship of students at any level. Job Duties and Responsibilities: Being present for the duration of the residency (August 15 - December 15); Making artwork in the Windgate Center of Art + Design M-F (daily); Maintaining open studio hours (weekly); Giving a public artist\u2019s talk (one time); Critiquing students; Participating as a guest artist in relevant classes (1-2 times): examples include giving a talk, participating in critiques, or leading an in-class activity; Attending welcome and farewell receptions; Providing a work to the UA Little Rock Art Collection; Other duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Knowledge of artistic processes and media; Knowledge of studio safety procedures; Strong interpersonal skills; Ability to teach; Ability to effectively communicate and collaborate; Willingness to engage in collaboration with faculty as a guest artist in their classes; Willingness to engage with students and the broader community. Additional Information: Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Curriculum Vitae, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Other (see special instructions for details) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Important note: please upload all of the following files in the field on the application that prompts you to upload your CV. You may submit them individually or as one large PDF. This is the only place on the application that allows file uploads. -Letter of interest specifying qualifications and experience (cover letter) -Curriculum Vitae -PDF Portfolio of artwork or link to online portfolio Additional Information: Housing is provided approximately one block from the Windgate Center for Art + Design. The house is a 2-bedroom, 1-bathroom house with parking. Artists with families are encouraged to apply. One pet is allowed. Recruitment Contact Information: Joli Livaudais, Director, jklivaudais@ualr.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: No Background Check Required The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Sitting, Standing Frequent Physical Activity: Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Crouching, Feeling, Grasping, Lifting, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Adjunct-Lecturer---Spring-2028-Artist-in-Residence_R0088052": {"title": "Adjunct Lecturer / Spring 2028 Artist in Residence", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-15\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Adjunct Faculty Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Less than Annual Appointment (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Little Rock The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is a metropolitan research university that provides an accessible, quality education through flexible learning and unparalleled internship opportunities. At UA Little Rock, we prepare our more than 8,900 students to be innovators and responsible leaders in their fields. Committed to its metropolitan research university mission, UA Little Rock is a driving force in Little Rock's thriving cultural community and a major component of the city and state's growing profile as a regional leader in research, technology transfer, economic development, and job creation. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . Department: Art and Design Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Windgate Artist in Residence provisional position will work in the Windgate Center of Art + Design at the University of Arkansas at Little Rock for the spring 2028 semester. This residency offers the Windgate Artist in Residence the opportunity to make work and to engage with the community of the UA Little Rock School of Art and Design. While in residence, the artist is expected to make work in the provided studio space and/or the shared studio spaces of the building. In addition, artists will interact with students through weekly open studio hours, studio visits to student workspaces, in-class activities hosted by program faculty, and welcome and farewell community receptions. Participating artists will also donate one work of art to the UA Little Rock Art Collection. This position is governed by state and federal laws, and agency/institution policy. Qualifications: Required Education and/or Experience: High School Diploma Preferred Education and/or Experience: MFA, BFA, BA, or commensurate experience; Evidence of active participation in exhibitions at the national or international level; Teaching and/or mentorship of students at any level. Job Duties and Responsibilities: Being present for the duration of the residency (Jan 15 - May 15); Making artwork in the Windgate Center of Art + Design M-F (daily); Maintaining open studio hours (weekly); Giving a public artist\u2019s talk (one time); Critiquing students; Participating as a guest artist in relevant classes (1-2 times): examples include giving a talk, participating in critiques, or leading an in-class activity; Attending welcome and farewell receptions; Providing a work to the UA Little Rock Art Collection; Other duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Knowledge of artistic processes and media; Knowledge of studio safety procedures; Strong interpersonal skills; Ability to teach; Ability to effectively communicate and collaborate; Willingness to engage in collaboration with faculty as a guest artist in their classes; Willingness to engage with students and the broader community. Additional Information: Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Curriculum Vitae, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Other (see special instructions for details) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Important note: please upload all of the following files in the field on the application that prompts you to upload your CV. You may submit them individually or as one large PDF. This is the only place on the application that allows file uploads. -Letter of interest specifying qualifications and experience (cover letter) -Curriculum Vitae -PDF Portfolio of artwork or link to online portfolio Additional Information: Housing is provided approximately one block from the Windgate Center for Art + Design. The house is a 2-bedroom, 1-bathroom house with parking. Artists with families are encouraged to apply. One pet is allowed. Recruitment Contact Information: Joli Livaudais, Director, jklivaudais@ualr.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: No Background Check Required The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Sitting, Standing Frequent Physical Activity: Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Crouching, Feeling, Grasping, Lifting, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/North-Little-Rock/Extra-Help---AHEC_R0087867": {"title": "Extra Help - AHEC", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-14\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 10/31/2026 Type of Position: Clerical Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas Pulaski Technical College University of Arkansas - Pulaski Technical College at North Little Rock is an integral part of the Arkansas Technical and Community College System maintained by the State of Arkansas. The college is governed by the University of Arkansas System Board of Trustees and a seven-member Board of Visitors and derives its support largely from student tuition and fees and legislative appropriations. UA - Pulaski Tech, a comprehensive two-year college, offers associate degree and certificate programs for students who plan to transfer to four-year colleges and universities and/or for career preparation and advancement. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply link/button. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at (501) 812-2839. Department: Dental Assisting Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: This position is to assist faculty members and students in the clinical and laboratory areas. This person would be responsible for setting up and cleaning up materials and instruments that are needed for various lab procedures, making sure that instruments are sterilized and ready to be used in the clinical setting and helping maintain the clinical and laboratory areas. Skills necessary to assist faculty and students would be: manipulation and usage of dental materials, making and trimming temporary crowns, assist with various tray set ups and instruments, assist in all aspects of radiography. Also included would be assisting with competencies for: amalgam and composite procedures, sealant placement, crown preparation, identifying the dental unit components and how they work, applying fluoride varnish, patient education, hand washing, prophylaxis and fluoride treatment to name a few. Qualifications: Must be a graduate of a CODA, Commission on Dental Accreditation, approved college, have a minimum of an associate degree, be a Registered Dental Assistant with the State Board of Dental Examiners of Arkansas and willing to attain national certification within one year. Additional Information: Salary Information: $21.00 hourly Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume, Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants Recruitment Contact Information: Human Resources humanresources@uaptc.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: University of Arkansas - Pulaski Technical College is committed to providing a safe campus community. Title IX protects the college community from sexual harassment in a school's education programs and activities. This means that Title IX protects the college community in connection with all academic, educational, extracurricular, athletic, and other programs of the school, whether those programs take place in a school's facilities, in college transportation, at a class or training program sponsored by the school at another location, or elsewhere. \u00a0 We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/TRIO-Student-Support-Services-Math-and-Science-Tutor_R0081681": {"title": "TRIO Student Support Services Math and Science Tutor", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-14\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 10/31/2026 Type of Position: Staff (Non-Classified) Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Less than Annual Appointment (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas Pulaski Technical College University of Arkansas - Pulaski Technical College at North Little Rock is an integral part of the Arkansas Technical and Community College System maintained by the State of Arkansas. The college is governed by the University of Arkansas System Board of Trustees and a seven-member Board of Visitors and derives its support largely from student tuition and fees and legislative appropriations. UA - Pulaski Tech, a comprehensive two-year college, offers associate degree and certificate programs for students who plan to transfer to four-year colleges and universities and/or for career preparation and advancement. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply link/button. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at (501) 812-2839. Department: TRIO SSS- South Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: \u2022 Possess the ability to work well with students \u2022 Tutor in basic skills math up to college algebra. \u2022 Tutor in science courses including biology and physical science. \u2022 Assist in topics using time management, goalsetting, learning styles, blackboard, Library resources. \u2022 Assist and conduct class pre- and post- assessments. \u2022 Help maintain cleanliness of the tutor lab to meet CDC Guidelines before and after class. \u2022 Document students individual progress maintain student attendance records. \u2022 Contact supervisor in advance when unable to come in for work. \u2022 Perform other Duties as requested. Qualifications: Bachelors degree in education, math or related field-Masters preferred Two or more years teaching on the college level-preferred Experience developing curriculum-preferred Demonstrate the ability to use basic computer programs that are applicable in a college setting. Additional Information: Salary Information: $15-$18 per hour, depending on educational background Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Resume, Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants Recruitment Contact Information: Human Resources humanresources@uaptc.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Motor Vehicle Reports Check, Sex Offender Registry University of Arkansas - Pulaski Technical College is committed to providing a safe campus community. Title IX protects the college community from sexual harassment in a school's education programs and activities. This means that Title IX protects the college community in connection with all academic, educational, extracurricular, athletic, and other programs of the school, whether those programs take place in a school's facilities, in college transportation, at a class or training program sponsored by the school at another location, or elsewhere. \u00a0 We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Repetitive Motion, Sitting, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Feeling, Standing, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Pulling, Pushing, Reaching Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAG--University-of-Arkansas-Grantham/PT-Faculty---Criminal-Justice_R0088387-1": {"title": "PT Faculty - Criminal Justice", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-14\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Adjunct Faculty Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Less than Annual Appointment (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas Grantham As an employer, the University of Arkansas Grantham offers a remote work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 - 10% of employee salary. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions, you should review before applying for the opening. If you need assistance with the application process, or if you are a person with a disability who would like to request a reasonable accommodation related to the application process, please contact the Department of Human Resources at hr@uagrantham.edu. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at recruiting@uagrantham.edu. Department: General Academics Team Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The University of Arkansas Grantham is looking for REMOTE Part Time Faculty in the following states: AL, AR, AZ, DE, FL, GA, KS, IA, ID, IN, KY, LA, MD, MI, MO, MS, NC, NE, NJ, OH, OK, SC, TN, TX, UT, VA, VT, WI and WY. Please only apply if you are able to live and work full-time in one of the states listed above. State locations and specifics are subject to change as our hiring requirements shift. POSITION DESCRIPTION: Part-time Faculty for University of Arkansas Grantham (UAG) have primary responsibility for online instruction and corresponding outreach to an approximate maximum load of 70 students at a given time. Part-time faculty serve in a remote capacity at the University. This position is for the designated college and will report to the Faculty Manager. Part-time faculty teach courses that may begin monthly or quarterly depending on the course and program. Courses are eight weeks in length and utilize the Blackboard Learning Management System. Each course week runs Wednesday through Tuesday midnight of the following week. Faculty are given access one week prior to the course start date to set up the course. KEY JOB RESPONSIBILITIES: \u25cf Follow all University policies as provided in the University Catalog and Faculty Handbook. \u25cf Provide instruction in accordance with the University and within the scope of departmentally-defined courses, programs of study, and degrees. \u25cf Responsibility includes timely interaction with students and quality assessment of student work with substantive feedback. \u25cf Provide weekly \u201coffice hours\u201d support and communicate (e.g., email, posting, live-chat, etc.) in a timely manner with students, other faculty and staff regarding student concerns or issues. \u25cf Faculty may take part in shared governance of curriculum, in some instances participating in curriculum development. \u25cf Participate in training on necessary technologies to facilitate courses. \u25cf Assume responsibility to keep current in the field of study/area of expertise and continue to develop professionally in content, methodologies, and distance-learning strategies. \u25cf Able to make decisions and work independently with exceptional problem solving and analytical skills. \u25cf Maintain accurate electronic records for both the learning management system maintenance as well as the University records system and submit all records when required. \u25cf Participate actively in faculty development opportunities (internally and externally). \u25cf Provide feedback concerning student and faculty issues. \u25cf Utilize the philosophy and objectives of University of Arkansas Grantham to create a positive growth environment for learning. Follow principles of good educational practice: provide ongoing contact between students, develop reciprocity/cooperation among students, use active learning techniques, give prompt feedback, emphasize time on task, communicate high expectations, and respect diverse talents and ways of learning. \u25cf Proactively participate with students within programs through teaching, welcome forums, recorded videos, etc. \u25cf Notify the appropriate University administrator of any course or course administration issues in a timely manner. \u25cf Other duties as assigned Qualifications: EDUCATION/WORK EXPERIENCE REQUIREMENTS AND DESIRED SKILLS: Part-time faculty teaching undergraduate courses are required to hold a Master\u2019s Degree in Juris Doctor, Political Science, Criminal Justice Minimum of 18 credit hours in Government to teach American Government Five years of professional experience Prospective faculty must enroll in and successfully complete the Faculty Orientation Training Course Online teaching experience is preferred All degrees must be conferred from an institution accredited by an accreditation agency recognized by the United States Department of Education or the Council for Higher Education Accreditation (CHEA).\u00a0 For faculty holding degrees awarded by non-U.S. institutions, the institutions must be approved by the appropriate governmental or accreditation agency. A student-centered instructional philosophy is required Curriculum development experience a plus Proficiency in MS Office Suite Products and leveraging the Internet Knowledge of, and use of Blackboard Learning Management System is preferred Able to make decisions and work independently with effective problem solving and analytical skills Strong interpersonal skills and ability to collaborate with technicians and faculty Knowledge of distance learning educational model required Able to gather, analyze, evaluate, and integrate information electronically In-depth knowledge of distance learning educational models, adult learning styles, and technology-assisted instruction. In-depth knowledge of developing curriculum design required Excellent analytical, interpersonal, oral, and written communication skills required High speed Internet and a webcam are required for this role. Able to effectively communicate orally and in writing. A flexible work schedule is required. Able to multi-task yet maintain close attention to detail and timeliness of work production. Able to work in a positive team-oriented manner with a variety of people (students, faculty, staff, administrators, vendors, and members of the general public) Language Skills : Able to read, analyze, and interpret common journals and legal documents. Able to respond to common inquiries or complaints from customers, regulatory agencies, or members of the business community. Able to effectively present information to executive management, faculty, staff, and/or students. Mathematical Skill : Able to apply concepts such as fractions, percentages, ratios, and proportions to practical situations. Reasoning Ability: Able to define problems, collect data, establish facts, and draw valid conclusions. Ability to present facts to faculty for departmental response. Able to deal with a variety of information presented in oral or written formats. Able to deal with non-verbal behavior in assisting with problem resolution. Physical Demands: The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Frequently required to use hand to finger, handle, or feel (including the use of computer keyboards) and talk or hear (including the use of a telephone and computer). Occasionally required to walk, stand, and make presentations. This position may involve sitting at a desk for extended periods of time. Specific vision abilities include close vision and distance vision. University of Arkansas Grantham will seek to reasonably accommodate qualified individuals with a disability. Such reasonable accommodation may take the form of making existing facilities readily accessible to or usable by individuals with a disability, restructuring jobs, modifying schedules, acquiring, or modifying equipment, adjusting training materials, adjusting employment policies, and the like. Additional Information: Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Proof of Veteran Status, Resume, Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: recruiting@uagrantham.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-Arkansas-at-Pine-Bluff/Institutional-Services-Assistant---Student-Union_R0088227": {"title": "Institutional Services Assistant - Student Union", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-14\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Skilled Labor Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff The University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff is an 1890 Land-Grant HBCU with a diverse student population, competitive degree offerings and stellar faculty. For more than 140 years, the University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff has worked to create an environment that inculcates learning, growth and productivity while affording a basic need to its students \u2013 a chance to advance. The 15:1 student to teacher ratio makes it possible to maintain a learning environment with close interaction between students and faculty while challenging curricula encourage our students to seek and fulfill their potential. You can excel in your chosen field of study through a curriculum of \u00a0 Certificate and Associates degree programs,\u00a0 more than thirty\u00a0 Undergraduate programs, Master\u2019s degree programs and a Doctorate program in Aquaculture/Fisheries. You can also develop workplace readiness through internships, co-ops and fellowships in the U.S. and abroad. Out-of-class experiences and student involvement include more than 90 student organizations, an internationally renowned Vesper Choir, Marching Band, Concert Bands, Wind Symphony, nationally recognized debate team, award-winning theater department and accomplished athletic program. Though the main campus is in Pine Bluff, its reach is worldwide. UAPB has an extended campus in North Little Rock and offers as well as online courses. With the addition of the Arkansas Research and Education Optical Network (ARE-ON), students can engage in information exchange with others anywhere in the world. There are also Research and Extension offices in Lonoke, Newport and Lake Village and collaborations with other colleges and universities in the State through the National Science Foundation funded STEM (Science, Technology, Engineering and Mathematics) Academy. As the second oldest land-grant institution in the state of Arkansas, the mission of this No Excuse University remains the same \u2013 to provide a high quality, affordable education with a personal touch. We invite you to Become a Part of the Pride at the University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process and require reasonable accommodations, please contact Human Resources at 870.575.8400 . Department: Student Union Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Institutional Services Assistant is responsible for maintaining a clean, safe, and welcoming environment within the Student Union and associated facilities. This position performs routine and specialized custodial services in offices, classrooms, meeting rooms, auditoriums, dining areas, restrooms, and common spaces to support daily operations, campus events, and student engagement activities. The position is governed by applicable state and federal regulations and institutional policies. Key Responsibilities Custodial & Facility Maintenance \u2022 Remove trash and recyclables from waste receptacles; empty, sanitize, re-line containers, and operate trash compactors as required. \u2022 Clean and sanitize interior spaces including offices, conference rooms, lounges, classrooms, auditoriums, hallways, stairwells, and entryways. \u2022 Sweep, mop, buff, and vacuum floors daily; shampoo carpets and clean baseboards as scheduled. \u2022 Strip, wax, and buff floors according to established maintenance schedules. \u2022 Dust, wipe, and sanitize furniture, desks, tables, cabinets, appliances, fixtures, ceiling fans, and whiteboards/blackboards. \u2022 Clean walls, windows, window sills, doors, and high-touch surfaces to maintain sanitation standards. Restroom & Specialized Cleaning \u2022 Clean and disinfect restroom fixtures; restock soap, paper towels, and toilet tissue. \u2022 Perform specialized cleaning using approved methods, chemicals, and equipment, including proper handling and disposal of contaminated materials when required. Event & Operational Support \u2022 Assist with event setup and breakdown, including furniture arrangement and post-event cleaning for meetings, programs, and special events hosted in the Student Union. \u2022 Support peak usage periods by ensuring spaces remain clean, orderly, and operational throughout the day and during scheduled events. Safety & Compliance \u2022 Follow all safety procedures, chemical handling guidelines, and institutional standards to ensure a safe working environment. \u2022 Report maintenance concerns, safety hazards, or supply needs to supervisors in a timely manner Qualifications: The formal education equivalent of a high school diploma. Must have knowledge of basic techniques and cleaning equipment operation and maintenance; ability to follow instructions and perform repetitive manual work; ability to use cleansers and other agents to clean floors and furniture; ability to work independently without close supervision and to follow oral and or written instructions; ability to perform multiple tasks and prioritize assignments; and the ability to lift up to 50 lbs. Additional Information: List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), and Resume Salary Information: $30,000 Required Documents to Apply: List of three Professional References (name, email, business title) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants (Please upload all required documents in the \"Resume\" attachment section of your application to be considered for this position) : Recruitment Contact Information: Sharron Williams, Employment Manager/Recruiter Human Resources williamssm@uapb.edu 870-575-8403 All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: The University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff may conduct pre-employment background checks on certain positions for applicants being considered for employment. \u00a0 The background checks may include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. \u00a0 Required checks are identified in the position listing. \u00a0 A criminal background check or arrest pending adjudication information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absences of a relationship to the requirements of the position. \u00a0 Background check information will be used in a consistent, non-discriminatory manner consistent with the state and federal law. \u00a0 The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAM--Monticello-Campus/Area-Coordinator-for-Residential-Curriculum-and-Student-Leadership--Live-In-_R0088363-1": {"title": "Area Coordinator for Residential Curriculum and Student Leadership (Live-In)", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-14\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Staff - Management, Supervisory Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Monticello UAM, one of twenty campuses of the University of Arkansas System, is located in southeastern Arkansas in the beautiful timberlands, rich in outdoor recreation activities, and approximately 100 miles south of Little Rock. UAM is a comprehensive, residential and commuter, undergraduate institution also offering selected master\u2019s degree programs. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please submit a request via the OEOC website: \u00a0Applicants are required to submit a request for each position to which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 870-460-1422 . Department: Residence Halls Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Residential Curriculum & Student Learning \u2022Lead the implementation and continuous assessment of the department's Residential Curriculum. \u2022Develop intentional learning outcomes that support student success, wellness, leadership, community engagement, and personal responsibility. \u2022Coordinate educational initiatives aligned with departmental and institutional strategic priorities. \u2022Assess programming effectiveness and prepare annual reports using learning outcomes and assessment data. \u2022Collaborate with campus partners to provide educational opportunities for residential students. \u2022Maintain programming calendars and curriculum timelines. Resident Assistant Program Administration \u2022Provide direct supervision for all Resident Assistants. \u2022Coordinate Resident Assistant recruitment, selection, hiring, and onboarding. \u2022Develop and facilitate comprehensive RA training programs each semester. \u2022Conduct weekly staff meetings and individual supervisory meetings. \u2022Complete performance evaluations and provide coaching and professional development. \u2022Monitor RA duty coverage and accountability. \u2022Provide guidance regarding conflict mediation, community development, and crisis response. \u2022Recognize and celebrate outstanding student staff performance. Graduate Assistant Supervision \u2022Directly supervise all Graduate Assistants within Housing and Residence Life. \u2022Establish work expectations and professional development goals. \u2022Provide mentoring in higher education administration and student engagement. \u2022Conduct regular one-on-one meetings and performance evaluations. \u2022Delegate departmental projects and assess completion. Administrative Responsibilities \u2022Maintain accurate student staff records. \u2022Prepare reports and assessment documents. \u2022Assist with departmental planning and strategic initiatives. \u2022Maintain confidentiality of student records in accordance with FERPA and university policies. \u2022Utilize departmental technology and software, including StarRez, Microsoft Office, and institutional systems. \u2022Maintain working knowledge of StarRez for student staff assignments, occupancy management, reporting, programming documentation, and administrative functions Student Leadership Development \u2022Develop leadership curriculum for Resident Assistants and Graduate Assistants. \u2022Coordinate leadership retreats, workshops, and professional development opportunities. \u2022Foster a culture of accountability, professionalism, and servant leadership. \u2022Mentor student leaders in communication, ethical decision-making, crisis management, and student engagement. Residential Programming \u2022Oversee educational, social, cultural, and wellness programming throughout the residential communities. \u2022Ensure programming aligns with departmental learning outcomes. \u2022Monitor programming budgets. \u2022Assist with campus-wide student engagement initiatives. \u2022Encourage collaboration between Residence Life and Student Engagement. Student Conduct \u2022Address policy violations occurring within the residence halls. \u2022Meet with students regarding behavioral concerns. \u2022Document incidents accurately and promptly. \u2022Participate in the student conduct process as assigned. \u2022Follow up on student welfare concerns and behavioral interventions. Crisis Management \u2022Respond to emergencies and critical incidents within residential communities. \u2022Serve as a member of the professional on-call rotation. \u2022Provide support to students experiencing crises. \u2022Coordinate with University Police, Counseling Services, Facilities Management, Student Health Services, and other campus partners during emergencies. \u2022Complete timely incident documentation. Housing Operations Support \u2022Assist with opening, closing, and transition processes. \u2022Support occupancy management and room assignments as needed. \u2022Assist with room inspections and damage assessments. \u2022Participate in departmental committees and special projects. \u2022Support summer conferences, camps, and special housing operations. Qualifications: Required Qualifications Bachelor's degree from an accredited institution One to three years of progressively responsible experience in Housing and Residence Life or Student Engagement. Experience supervising Resident Assistants and/or Graduate Assistants. Experience planning educational programming and leadership development. Demonstrated crisis management and conflict resolution skills. Strong written and verbal communication skills. Ability to work evenings, weekends, holidays, and respond to emergencies. Preferred Qualifications Experience implementing a residential curriculum model. Working knowledge of StarRez Housing Management Software. Experience with assessment and learning outcomes. Experience with student conduct processes. Experience in crisis intervention and behavioral response. Additional Information: Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Knowledge of student development theory. Knowledge of residence hall operations. Strong organizational and project management skills. Ability to supervise, motivate, and mentor student leaders. Ability to make sound decisions under pressure. Excellent interpersonal and conflict resolution skills. Strong presentation and facilitation abilities. Ability to analyze assessment data and make recommendations. Ability to maintain confidentiality and professionalism. Ability to establish collaborative relationships across campus. Salary Information: $40,000 Required Documents to Apply: List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Jessica Foxworth, Associate VC for Student Affairs and Dean of Students, foxworth@uamont.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Motor Vehicle Reports Check, Sex Offender Registry, Substance Abuse Testing The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting, Standing Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAM--Monticello-Campus/Area-Coordinator-for-Housing-Operations--Live-in-_R0088362-1": {"title": "Area Coordinator for Housing Operations (Live-in)", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-14\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Skilled Labor Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Monticello UAM, one of twenty campuses of the University of Arkansas System, is located in southeastern Arkansas in the beautiful timberlands, rich in outdoor recreation activities, and approximately 100 miles south of Little Rock. UAM is a comprehensive, residential and commuter, undergraduate institution also offering selected master\u2019s degree programs. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please submit a request via the OEOC website: \u00a0Applicants are required to submit a request for each position to which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 870-460-1422 . Department: Residence Halls Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Housing Operations \u2022Coordinate the day-to-day operations of all residence halls and university apartments. \u2022Serve as the departmental functional user for StarRez Housing Management Software, ensuring the accuracy of housing assignments, occupancy records, room inventories, student applications, room changes, check-in/check-out processes, key management, and reporting. \u2022Maintain accurate occupancy records, housing rosters, waitlists, and assignment data utilizing StarRez. \u2022Process housing applications, assignments, room changes, cancellations, and contract updates through StarRez. \u2022Generate occupancy, assignment, utilization, and operational reports using StarRez to support departmental planning and decision-making. \u2022Assist with housing selection, room assignments, and residential occupancy management for new and returning students. \u2022Coordinate opening, closing, break housing, and transition processes. \u2022Conduct routine room inspections and ensure all rooms are prepared for student occupancy, conferences, camps, and special events. \u2022Monitor room readiness, including furniture inventories, cleanliness, maintenance completion, and safety compliance. Administrative Responsibilities \u2022Maintain accurate housing records and operational reports. \u2022Assist with departmental assessment initiatives. \u2022Prepare occupancy, damage, and facilities reports. \u2022Analyze occupancy trends and operational data to support strategic planning. \u2022Assist with budget monitoring for assigned operational areas. \u2022Participate in departmental committees and strategic initiatives. Facilities Management \u2022Serve as the departmental liaison with Facilities Management regarding maintenance and repair projects. \u2022Monitor work orders from submission through completion. \u2022Conduct follow-up inspections to ensure satisfactory completion of repairs. \u2022Identify facility concerns and recommend preventative maintenance initiatives. \u2022Maintain inventories of furniture, appliances, keys, equipment, and operational supplies. \u2022Coordinate furniture replacement, room inventory, and asset management. Custodial and Operational Oversight \u2022Provide daily operational oversight of custodial services within residential facilities. \u2022Develop and monitor cleaning schedules. \u2022Conduct quality assurance inspections. \u2022Ensure compliance with university cleanliness standards. \u2022Assist with summer conference turnover, room preparation, and deep-cleaning schedules. Student Development \u2022Foster a welcoming, engaging, and student-centered residential community. \u2022Respond to student concerns and provide conflict mediation when appropriate. \u2022Support departmental programming initiatives. \u2022Promote student engagement, wellness, and academic success. Conduct and Crisis Response \u2022Participate in the professional staff on-call rotation. \u2022Respond to emergencies, crises, and after-hours incidents. \u2022Document incidents using departmental reporting systems. \u2022Adjudicate student conduct cases in accordance with university policies. \u2022Collaborate with University Police, Counseling Services, Student Conduct, and Title IX personnel as appropriate. Summer Conferences and Camps \u2022Coordinate housing operations for summer camps, conferences, orientation programs, and special events. \u2022Manage check-in and check-out processes using StarRez. \u2022Coordinate staffing and operational logistics to support conference housing. Other Duties \u2022Serve on university committees. \u2022Participate in recruitment and orientation activities. \u2022Perform other duties as assigned. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications Bachelor's degree from an accredited institution. One year of professional experience in Housing & Residence Life, Student Engagement, facilities operations, or a related field. Working knowledge of StarRez Housing Management Software or a comparable higher education housing management system. Strong organizational, interpersonal, and communication skills. Valid driver's license. Preferred Qualifications Master's degree in Higher Education, Student Affairs, Educational Leadership, or a related field. Two or more years of progressively responsible Residence Life experience. Experience supervising student employees. Experience with housing occupancy management and facilities operations. Experience with student conduct administration. Additional Information: Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Thorough knowledge of Housing & Residence Life operations. Working knowledge of StarRez Housing Management Software , including housing applications, assignments, occupancy management, reporting, room inventory, and student records. Proficiency with Microsoft Office Suite, including Word, Excel, Outlook, and Teams. Strong organizational and project management skills. Excellent written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills. Ability to supervise, mentor, and develop student employees. Ability to establish collaborative working relationships across campus. Sound judgment and effective decision-making skills. Ability to analyze housing occupancy and operational data. Commitment to outstanding customer service and student success. Working Conditions Full-time, 12-month, live-in professional position. University-provided apartment required as a condition of employment. Evening, weekend, holiday, and emergency hours required. Participation in an after-hours on-call rotation. Frequent walking throughout residential facilities. Ability to lift and move up to 40 pounds occasionally. Exposure to varying weather conditions while conducting facility inspections. Supervision Exercised Student Workers Operational oversight of custodial staff Reports To Director of Housing & Residence Life Salary Information: $40,000 Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Jessica Foxworth Associate Vice-Chancellor for Student Engagement/ Dean of Students 870-460-1110 All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Motor Vehicle Reports Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Extra-Help-Resident-Assistant--Multiple-Open-Positions-_R0088282": {"title": "Extra Help/Resident Assistant (Multiple Open Positions)", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-13\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Administration - Student Affairs, Clerical Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Little Rock The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is a metropolitan research university that provides an accessible, quality education through flexible learning and unparalleled internship opportunities. At UA Little Rock, we prepare our more than 8,900 students to be innovators and responsible leaders in their fields. Committed to its metropolitan research university mission, UA Little Rock is a driving force in Little Rock's thriving cultural community and a major component of the city and state's growing profile as a regional leader in research, technology transfer, economic development, and job creation. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . Department: Campus Living Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Extra Help/Resident Assistants (RAs) are students selected on the basis of leadership, experience, scholarship, and the desire to help residential students realize their potential for personal development through community living. RAs serve as role models for residential students and are expected to use their best judgment, maturity, and concern for those individuals with whom they live and work. Their responsibilities for the general welfare of the students and facilities extend to all areas of the campus. RAs are responsible for maintaining communication with the appropriate staff members about the concerns and accomplishments of their community members. This position is governed by state and federal laws, and agency/institution policy. Qualifications: Required Education and/or Experience: Must be admitted to the University; A Resident Assistant must maintain a full-time academic course load (12 credits/semester undergraduate, 9 graduate) but is not to exceed 18 credit hours unless approved by their supervisor; Resident Assistants must maintain a minimum 2.5 cumulative grade point average; Student Contact and Leadership experience; A Resident Assistant must have lived on campus for at least a semester. Job Duties and Responsibilities: Be available in the community, especially during the evening hours, maintain frequent contact with all residents, and be a visible member of the community; Recognize and assist students with social, personal, and academic-related concerns/needs; Assist in conflict resolution and mediation; Respond to, document, and report any inappropriate, disruptive, and/or concerning behavior; Maintain professional confidentiality. (i.e. FERPA); Know campus and community resources and refer when appropriate; Community Building and Programming Plan, organize, and facilitate programs based on the needs and interests of the residents; Be involved in your community and encourage the involvement of residents in community and campus activities; Fulfill community building requirements as outlined by Residential Curriculum, their Hall Director (HD), and through training sessions; Attend UA Little Rock-sponsored events throughout the academic year. On Call RAs are required to participate in their community\u2019s on-call rotation.\u00a0 It is up to the community\u2019s HD to set the On-Call schedule with the RAs; Notify the Hall Director or the on-call Hall Director anytime emergency personnel are observed in the building, you are in need of a consultation, or need to report an incident; Rounds and on-call responsibilities are subject to change for holidays, sanctioned University functions, and to meet the needs of the Office of Campus Living. Property Walk all areas of their hall/floor on a regular basis; Report damages, facility repairs, and safety concerns in a timely manner and follow up with residents on the progress of repairs; Assist with move-outs/tours when needed or when there are a large number of prospective students. (i.e. Discover UA Little Rock & Experience UA Little Rock); Conduct health/safety inspections twice a month; Document trash or aesthetic violations observed in the community. Administrative Distribute and collect reports, notices, and forms as requested by the Hall Director(s), Area Coordinator, Assistant Director(s), Campus Living Office, and UA Little Rock; Know, communicate, and enforce Campus Living & University policies and regulations at all times; Complete necessary reports and forms (i.e. duty logs, inventory sheets, programming paperwork, room inspection forms, resident interaction logs, etc.) thoroughly by the appropriate deadline; Attend and participate in all weekly staff meetings and all one-on-one meetings with their Hall Director; Check your assigned mailbox daily; RA\u2019s must utilize and check daily their UA Little Rock email address as an official means of communication with the staff and the Office of Campus Living. \u200b Training Attend all RA Training and In-Service sessions in their entirety, including- Fall, Spring, and Summer sessions; RA\u2019s must complete all payroll paperwork prior to the date specified in their offer letter and may not start training/working until all paperwork is approved; New RA\u2019s are required to attend Title IX and Mandated Reporter Training; Complete all required compliance training. Time Commitment Because of the year-round nature of the living communities, RAs are expected to work during breaks and when the university is closed.\u00a0 Holiday coverage will be rotated among the staff; The RA position is expected to be a top priority after academics and before other non-academic activities, internships, and/or other work; All other non-academic activities (athletics, leadership positions, etc.) and on or off-campus work (including internships) must be approved by your Hall Director; Returning RAs may not work more than 10 hours per week at an off-campus job. Some consideration may be given to exceeding the 10-hour-per-week maximum if the outside employment is at another on-campus location (must be a non-work study position and paid monthly); All employment outside of Campus Living, including the number of hours, worked per week, must be discussed and mutually agreed upon by the RA with her/his supervisor prior to beginning the position; Credit or required academic internships are not considered as part of the 10 hours, but MUST be discussed with his/her supervisor at the beginning of the semester; Exceptions are made on an individual basis considering credit hours, internships, location of employment, and past demonstration of being able to balance multiple roles; Resident Assistants are permitted weeknights as well as weekends away, as long as it does not conflict with the on-call schedule. \u200b Additional Duties Learn the names of and develop a rapport with each resident in their community; Participate in all portions of RA Recruitment, including informational sessions, group process, and interviews; Serve as a tour guide on Discover UA Little Rock days, New Student Orientation, etc.; Attend the End of the Year banquet; Assist with the Campus Living re-application process; Assist with the collection of surveys; Any other responsibilities and expectations as assigned. \u200b Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities:\u00a0\u00a0 Good communication skills; Critical thinking; Working well in a team; Self-motivation; Being flexible; Good time management. Additional Information: Salary Information: $6,800 stipend Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Elizabeth J. Roshell Assistant Director for Residential Life and Education ejroshell@ualr.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Crouching, Lifting, Standing Frequent Physical Activity: Hearing, Reaching, Repetitive Motion, Sitting Occasional Physical Activity: Climbing, Feeling, Lifting Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Senior-Research-Assistant---12-MONTH_R0088250": {"title": "Senior Research Assistant - 12 MONTH", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-13\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Researchers Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Fixed Duration of Project/Grant (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Little Rock The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is a metropolitan research university that provides an accessible, quality education through flexible learning and unparalleled internship opportunities. At UA Little Rock, we prepare our more than 8,900 students to be innovators and responsible leaders in their fields. Committed to its metropolitan research university mission, UA Little Rock is a driving force in Little Rock's thriving cultural community and a major component of the city and state's growing profile as a regional leader in research, technology transfer, economic development, and job creation. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . Department: APAC - Provisional Positions Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Senior Research Assistant serves as the Program Manager for the Arkansas Certified Public Manager\u00ae (CPM) Program which is accredited through the National CPM Consortium (NCPMC). The program is a \u201ccomprehensive leadership and management program committed to developing exceptional public managers.\u201d This position serves as a valuable member of the Arkansas Public Administration Consortium (APAC) which is located in the School of Public Affairs at the University of Arkansas at Little Rock. This is a 12-month grant-funded position. Continued employment is contingent upon the availability of annual grant funding. This position is governed by state and federal laws and agency/institution policy. Qualifications: Required Education and/or Experience: Bachelor\u2019s degree; Experience in training, program management, and/or conference/event planning; Program evaluation experience. Preferred Education and/or Experience: CPM program completion; Master\u2019s degree in a relevant field; Work in or with the public sector in Arkansas; Experience with adult education, teaching, facilitation, creating online learning experiences with significant engagement, implementing learning innovations, marketing programs, online technology required for learning, program strategic planning, and/or mentoring professionals. Job Duties and Responsibilities: Program Management Develop and manage all program logistics, policies, procedures, communication, and record keeping; Develop experiences for participants that maximize management and leadership learning; Mentor and support program participants; Implement a thorough program evaluation process; Actively participate in the National CPM Consortium (NCPMC) and serve as the voting member for the Arkansas program; Oversee the NCPCM continuing accreditation process. \u200bProgram Marketing Develop and implement recruitment and marketing campaigns as well as stakeholder development initiatives. Program Strategic Development Facilitate the CPM Advisory Council; Develop effective working relationships with program stakeholders; Identify and secure resources to support the program; Manage program strategic planning. Program Instruction Instruct trainings that focus on orienting participants to the program and various program requirements; Provide instruction in additional areas of expertise. Supervision Recruit, support, and evaluate program instructors; Assist with hiring, training, supervising, and supporting graduate assistants, program coordinators, and others assisting with program support work. Alumni Engagement Be the APAC liaison to CPM alumni associations; Develop and implement alumni engagement activities. Additional Work Engage in the larger conversation about public sector management and leadership. This includes attending relevant events; giving presentations; and creating relevant social media content; Support other APAC programs, projects, planning, and administration when needed. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Clear, concise, and compelling written and oral communication; Collaboration skills that encourage teamwork, respect, engagement, and buy-in; Ability to work independently and manage multiple, concurrent tasks and projects; Ability to manage conflict effectively; Ability to work effectively with diverse program participants, stakeholders, and alumni; Ability to quickly learn online technology required for learning, data collection and analysis, participation tracking, and program marketing such as Google Products (forms, docs, slides, sheets), Zoom, Canvas Learning Management System, Qualtrics, WordPress, Facebook Ads Manager, etc. Additional Information: Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Please upload all required documents in the specified section of your application (before hitting the submit button), if you want to be considered for this position. Recruitment Contact Information: Derek Slagle, Chair, drslagle@ualr.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting Frequent Physical Activity: Hearing, Talking Occasional Physical Activity: Driving, Grasping, Lifting, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Standing, Walking Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Assistant-Professor-of-Criminal-Justice-and-Criminology---9MONTH_R0087910": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Criminal Justice and Criminology - 9MONTH", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-13\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Faculty - Tenure/Tenure Track Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Academic Term (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Little Rock The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is a metropolitan research university that provides an accessible, quality education through flexible learning and unparalleled internship opportunities. At UA Little Rock, we prepare our more than 8,900 students to be innovators and responsible leaders in their fields. Committed to its metropolitan research university mission, UA Little Rock is a driving force in Little Rock's thriving cultural community and a major component of the city and state's growing profile as a regional leader in research, technology transfer, economic development, and job creation. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . Department: Criminal Justice Department Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The duties of this position include teaching courses in both face-to-face and online formats within the School of Criminal Justice and Criminology. The tenure-track nature of the role would also encompass the standard academic responsibilities of conducting research and scholarship, serving on institutional committees, and providing service to the university. This position is governed by state and federal laws, and agency/institution policy. Qualifications: Required Education and/or Experience Ph.D. or ABD in Criminology, Criminal Justice, or a closely related field; A J.D. (law degree) is not appropriate for this position. Preferred Education and/or Experience Strong expertise in courts and sentencing, juvenile delinquency/justice, or statistics. Job Duties and Responsibilities Teach online or face-to-face formats at the undergraduate, master\u2019s, and doctoral level; Work positively with faculty, staff, students, and the community; Mentor students across the curriculum; Conduct and disseminate scholarly research; Serve the department, the university, and the community; Perform other duties as required. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Commitment to teaching and mentoring students; Willingness to teach in both online and face-to-face formats; Active research agenda in Criminology or Criminal Justice; Additional Information: Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Curriculum Vitae, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Michael Cavanaugh, Director of the School of Criminal Justice and Criminology, mcavanaugh@ualr.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Stuttgart-Campus/Grand-Prairie-Center--Part-time_R0088191": {"title": "Grand Prairie Center, Part-time", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-13\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Staff (Classified) (Inactive) Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: Phillips Community College of the University of Arkansas The first community college established in Arkansas, Phillips Community College of the University of Arkansas (PCCUA) is a multi-campus, two-year college serving Eastern Arkansas. PCCUA has academic, occupational/technical and continuing education programs and offers over 25 associate degree programs with campuses in DeWitt, Helena-W. Helena and Stuttgart. Thank you for your interest, and we hope you\u2019ll be joining our Ridge Runner family soon! Below you will find the details for the position as well as any specific application requirements you should review before applying for this opening. To apply for this position, please click the Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process, please call Human Resources at (870) 338-6474, ext. 1271. Department: Grand Prairie Center Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Extra Help Assistant is responsible for providing unskilled, semi-skilled labor or performing basic tasks in a state agency or institution. Duties include cleaning rooms in the Grand Prairie Center (GPC) as well as assisting with special events. This position is governed by state and federal laws and agency policy. Qualifications: Must be able to follow written and oral instructions; must have a valid drivers\u2019 license; must be able to perform manual labor; must be able to bend and reach without undue physical exertion; must be able to perform general cleaning responsibilities; must have the ability to do required lifting (up to 50 lbs.); and be tolerate solvent and cleaning solution odors. Flexible work schedule to include weekend and weeknights may be required. High school diploma or GED and experience in comparable setting. Additional Information: Salary Information: $12/hour Required Documents to Apply: None Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Renee Robison, RRobison@pccua.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check For general application assistance, or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at (870) 338-6474, ext. 1271. PCCUA is committed to providing a safe campus community. We will conduct criminal background checks and a sex offender registry check for applicants seeking employment. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Climbing, Crouching, Grasping, Kneeling, Lifting, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Repetitive Motion, Sitting, Standing, Stooping, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Women---Infants-In-House-Agency--IHA--RN_R0086360-1": {"title": "Women & Infants In-House Agency (IHA) RN", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-13\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/13/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | WISL Float Pool Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The In-House Agency RN Program offers PRN employment for 13-week intervals in the Perinatal and/or Labor & Delivery inpatient units. Participants are required to work 36 hours/week for 13 weeks and will be paid a competitive hourly rate plus weekend differentials. To qualify, applicants must have a valid RN license issued by the State of Arkansas and 12 months experience in an acute care hospital. Experience in the past 12 months must include 6 months in a direct patient care role in an acute care hospital. Applicants cannot be currently employed by UAMS, and previous UAMS employees must have terminated more than 180 days prior. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Graduate of an accredited Nursing Program with an Associate Degree, Nursing Diploma, Bachelor\u2019s in Nursing, or Master's in Nursing Valid RN License Nursing Experience: minimum of 12 months of experience as an RN in an acute care hospital in Labor & Delivery, Mother/Baby, Perinatal, or Antepartum Experience in the last 12 months may include up to 6 months in a management position, but must include at least 6 months in a direct patient care role in an acute care hospital Excellent communication skills Basic computer skills Strong work ethic and accountability Work one major holiday and one additional holiday if applicable, in addition to every other weekend throughout the duration of the 13-week RN Internal Contract agreement period. Preferred Qualifications:\u00a0 2 or more years of RN experience in Labor & Delivery, Mother/Baby, Perinatal, or Antepartum Additional Information: Responsibilities: The Registered Nurse provides direct patient care in the UAMS Perinatal (E6) and/or Labor & Delivery (E5) units, located in the Harry P. Ward Clinical Tower. These units deliver comprehensive, high-risk obstetrical care to patients from across the state. The Perinatal Unit (E6) features 28 rooms and a newborn procedure area, supporting postpartum, well newborn, high-risk antepartum, and gynecologic patients. The Labor & Delivery Unit (E5) includes 14 LDR suites, triage beds, operating rooms, recovery space, and neonatal stabilization rooms, with approximately 300\u2013330 deliveries per month. Both units emphasize patient- and family-centered care, allowing stable newborns to remain with their mothers to promote bonding. In this professional nursing role, the Registered Nurse is responsible for coordinating and triaging patient care, collaborating with providers, fellows, and interdisciplinary staff, and supporting seamless transitions of care. The RN works closely with patients and their families to develop and implement individualized care plans, coordinates appointments and referrals, and provides education on complex health conditions. Salary Information: Commensurate with education & experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAMS/Physical-Therapist--Warren-Kids-First-_R0083603-1": {"title": "Physical Therapist (Warren Kids First)", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-13\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 08/13/2026 Type of Position: Clinical Staff - Rehabilitation Therapy Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: COM | Peds Kids First Warren Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: This position is located in Warren, Arkansas. KIDS FIRST serves children with special healthcare needs ranging in age from six weeks to five years. In our pediatric day healthcare clinics, children diagnosed as having a medical condition known to place them at risk for developmental delays and disabilities receive intensive intervention. The Physical Therapist works as a member of an interdisciplinary team to provide the evidence-based best practice evaluation and therapy techniques for the birth to 5 population with a variety of gross motor delays/disorders at UAMS Kids First clinic. May provide supervision to physical therapy assistants. Travel to other KIDS FIRST locations may be required. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor\u2019s degree in Physical Therapy if graduated prior to 2002 OR Master\u2019s degree in Physical Therapy if graduated prior to 2016 OR Doctorate degree in Physical Therapy Current Arkansas Physical Therapy License or eligible to obtain license within 1 month of date of hire Intermediate computer skills Candidate must pass state abuse registry checks, drug screen, submit to a TB skin test and required immunizations or provide proof of immunizations. Additional Information: Responsibilities:\u00a0 Provides gross motor assessment and treatment using evidence-based techniques in a naturalistic, developmentally appropriate manner. \u00a0 On receipt of a prescription, evaluates to determine muscle tone, reflexes, strength, balance, range of motion, locomotion delays/disorders and/or potential orthopedic concerns using appropriate diagnostic instruments. \u00a0Also, determines the need for adaptive equipment and referral for orthotics. \u00a0 Reviews results of standardized scores along with informed clinical judgment and observations to make the correct diagnosis.\u00a0 Translates the obtained information into a professional, typed document along with treatment recommendations, developing appropriate goals and objectives as related to patient\u2019s needs. \u00a0Confers with the Medical Director when necessary regarding said results/recommendations. Implements direct therapy for children, based upon findings using evidence-based techniques.\u00a0 Continually monitors progress and makes modifications to treatment plan as needed.\u00a0 Documents services provided in a professional, timely manner. Carefully, prepares and provides billing documents according to KIDS FIRST and Medicaid guidelines on a weekly basis. \u00a0Verifies accuracy billing documents through careful review of progress notes, treatment room sign-out forms, and child\u2019s individual prescription requirements. Collaborates and communicates with families, other therapists, nurses, social workers, director, developmental staff, and contractors to provide the best quality of care and optimal outcomes for each child. Encourage families to take an active role in supporting their child\u2019s development using the principles of Family Centered Care.\u00a0 Supports the academic mission of the Kids First program. This includes participation in the training of students and pre-service professionals, education and outreach to stakeholders, families served, and community partners. May include training and participation in research projects or other duties as assigned. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Proof of Veteran Status, Resume, Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Adult Maltreatment, Child Maltreatment, Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Crawling, Crouching, Feeling, Grasping, Hearing, Kneeling, Lifting, Stooping, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Standing, Talking Occasional Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/North-Little-Rock/Part-Time-Police-Public-Safety-Officer_R0087797": {"title": "Part Time Police/Public Safety Officer", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-12\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/30/2026 Type of Position: Staff - Public Safety Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Less than Annual Appointment (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas Pulaski Technical College University of Arkansas - Pulaski Technical College at North Little Rock is an integral part of the Arkansas Technical and Community College System maintained by the State of Arkansas. The college is governed by the University of Arkansas System Board of Trustees and a seven-member Board of Visitors and derives its support largely from student tuition and fees and legislative appropriations. UA - Pulaski Tech, a comprehensive two-year college, offers associate degree and certificate programs for students who plan to transfer to four-year colleges and universities and/or for career preparation and advancement. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply link/button. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at (501) 812-2839. Department: Police - Asst. Director Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Public Safety Officer is responsible for the enforcement of traffic and criminal laws and parking regulations. This position is governed by law enforcement standards, state and federal laws, and agency policy. Qualifications: A part-time law enforcement officer is required to satisfactorily complete the minimum standards for employment or appointment as authorized in CLEST Rules and have satisfactorily completed not less than 110 hours of Commission approved training. Additional Information: Salary Information: $20/hr Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Resume, Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants Recruitment Contact Information: Human Resources humanresources@uaptc.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Motor Vehicle Reports Check, Sex Offender Registry University of Arkansas - Pulaski Technical College is committed to providing a safe campus community. Title IX protects the college community from sexual harassment in a school's education programs and activities. This means that Title IX protects the college community in connection with all academic, educational, extracurricular, athletic, and other programs of the school, whether those programs take place in a school's facilities, in college transportation, at a class or training program sponsored by the school at another location, or elsewhere. \u00a0 We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Driving, Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Pulling, Pushing, Reaching Occasional Physical Activity: Crouching, Kneeling, Lifting, Stooping Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAPBCAINECaine-Gilleland-Hall/Math-Lab-Advisor_R0087790": {"title": "Math Lab Advisor", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-11\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Staff - Clerical Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Annual Appointment (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff The University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff is an 1890 Land-Grant HBCU with a diverse student population, competitive degree offerings and stellar faculty. For more than 140 years, the University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff has worked to create an environment that inculcates learning, growth and productivity while affording a basic need to its students \u2013 a chance to advance. The 15:1 student to teacher ratio makes it possible to maintain a learning environment with close interaction between students and faculty while challenging curricula encourage our students to seek and fulfill their potential. You can excel in your chosen field of study through a curriculum of \u00a0 Certificate and Associates degree programs,\u00a0 more than thirty\u00a0 Undergraduate programs, Master\u2019s degree programs and a Doctorate program in Aquaculture/Fisheries. You can also develop workplace readiness through internships, co-ops and fellowships in the U.S. and abroad. Out-of-class experiences and student involvement include more than 90 student organizations, an internationally renowned Vesper Choir, Marching Band, Concert Bands, Wind Symphony, nationally recognized debate team, award-winning theater department and accomplished athletic program. Though the main campus is in Pine Bluff, its reach is worldwide. UAPB has an extended campus in North Little Rock and offers as well as online courses. With the addition of the Arkansas Research and Education Optical Network (ARE-ON), students can engage in information exchange with others anywhere in the world. There are also Research and Extension offices in Lonoke, Newport and Lake Village and collaborations with other colleges and universities in the State through the National Science Foundation funded STEM (Science, Technology, Engineering and Mathematics) Academy. As the second oldest land-grant institution in the state of Arkansas, the mission of this No Excuse University remains the same \u2013 to provide a high quality, affordable education with a personal touch. We invite you to Become a Part of the Pride at the University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process and require reasonable accommodations, please contact Human Resources at 870.575.8400 . Department: Math & Computer Science Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Department of Mathematics and Computer Science at the University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff (UAPB ) is seeking qualified candidates to apply for the position of Math Lab Advisor. This position is a 12-month full-time appointment and will serve a key role in leading the design, implementation, and operation of a new Math Tutoring Lab that supports undergraduate academic success in foundational math courses. Qualifications: Candidates must be able to teach and tutor mathematics at the undergraduate level, provide academic advising, develop structured academic support resources, and lead initiatives to improve student outcomes in core math courses. The successful candidate will be expected to work collaboratively with faculty, staff, and institutional research offices to design and deliver data-informed tutoring strategies, implement student engagement tools, and support math education majors preparing for certification exams Additional Information: Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Curriculum Vitae, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants (Please upload all required documents in the \"Resume\" attachment section of your application to be considered for this position) : Recruitment Contact Information: Sharron M. Williams Employment Manager Williamssm@uapb.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: No Background Check Required The University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff may conduct pre-employment background checks on certain positions for applicants being considered for employment. \u00a0 The background checks may include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. \u00a0 Required checks are identified in the position listing. \u00a0 A criminal background check or arrest pending adjudication information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absences of a relationship to the requirements of the position. \u00a0 Background check information will be used in a consistent, non-discriminatory manner consistent with the state and federal law. \u00a0 The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Sitting, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Sitting, Talking Occasional Physical Activity: Talking Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Hot-Springs/Visitor-Services-Cashier---Garvan-Woodland-Gardens_R0087981-1": {"title": "Visitor Services Cashier \u2013 Garvan Woodland Gardens", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-10\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com, then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at all University of Arkansas institutions will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students.\u201d University of Arkansas, Fayetteville students will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Student Jobs at UAF.\u201d All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. Closing Date: 09/06/2026 Type of Position: Staff - Clerical Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas, Fayetteville Founded in 1871, the University of Arkansas is a land grant institution, classified by the Carnegie Foundation among the nation\u2019s top 2 percent of universities with the highest level of research activity. The University of Arkansas works to advance the state and build a better world through education, research, and outreach by providing transformational opportunities and skills, fostering a welcoming climate, and nurturing creativity, discovery, and the spread of new ideas and innovations. The University of Arkansas campus is located in Fayetteville, a welcoming community ranked as one of the best places to live in the U.S. The growing region surrounding Fayetteville is home to numerous Fortune 500 companies and one of the nation\u2019s strongest economies. Northwest Arkansas is also quickly gaining a national reputation for its focus on the arts and overall quality of life. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10% of employee salary. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions, you should review before applying for the opening. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process, please submit a request via the Disability Accommodations | OEOC | University of Arkansas (uark.edu) : Request an Accommodation. Appli\u00adcants are required to submit a request for each position of which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 479.575.5351. Department: Visitor Services Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Garvan Woodland Gardens, one of top attractions in Arkansas is hiring! We are looking for positive, motivated, personable new team members to join our crew. Work outdoors in a setting voted in the top 10 most colorful places on the planet by Trip Advisor. We would love for you to come grow with us! Garvan Woodland Gardens, a 210-acre botanical garden situated on a peninsula surrounded by scenic Lake Hamilton located in Hot Springs, AR is seeking a skilled and dedicated Visitor Services Cashier. The Visitor Services Cashier will be responsible for greeting guests, checking in guests, taking funds, and balancing the point of sale system at closing. This position will also serve as a guest docent by driving golf cart tours and giving a scripted explanation of the garden spaces. This team member will be expected to work well with others and ensure a positive guest experience. Part-time, up to 32 hours a week, including weekends and nights during Holiday Lights (mid-November thru Dec 31). Visitor Services Cashier is a part-time, temporary position limited to the 1250-hour University of Arkansas policy. The campus is a non-smoking facility. This position requires a valid driver\u2019s license. Some night and weekend work will be required seasonally. Regular, reliable, and non-disruptive attendance is an essential job duty, as is the ability to create and maintain collegial, harmonious working relationships with others. Qualifications: \u00a0 Minimum Qualifications: High School Diploma or equivalent Customer Service Experience Valid Driver\u2019s License Background Checks Required: Criminal Background Check, Motor Vehicle Reports Check, Sex Offender Registry, Financial Background Check Preferred Qualifications: Previous experience collecting money for payment Experience taking funds and balancing point of sale systems Additional Information: Salary Information: Hourly pay $12.50-$14.00 based on experience Required Documents to Apply: List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Proof of Veteran Status Recruitment Contact Information: Susan Harper, Director of Visitor Services sah17@uark.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Special Instructions to Applicants: Work schedule up to 24 hours week; Resume can consist of a word document with work history, experience, and dates. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Financial Credit Check, Motor Vehicle Reports Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas seeks to attract, develop and retain high quality faculty, staff and administrators that consistently display practices and behaviors to advance a culture that embeds equal opportunity, educational excellence and unparalleled access for all. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All Application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting, Standing, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Driving Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Director-of-the-Science-Triangle_R0088141": {"title": "Director of the Science Triangle", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-10\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Professional Staff - Project/Program Administration Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Little Rock The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is a metropolitan research university that provides an accessible, quality education through flexible learning and unparalleled internship opportunities. At UA Little Rock, we prepare our more than 8,900 students to be innovators and responsible leaders in their fields. Committed to its metropolitan research university mission, UA Little Rock is a driving force in Little Rock's thriving cultural community and a major component of the city and state's growing profile as a regional leader in research, technology transfer, economic development, and job creation. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . Department: Donaghey College of Science, Technology, Engineering & Mathematics Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: UA Little Rock is seeking to hire a Director of the Science Triangle. The Director will provide visionary leadership, strategic coordination, and administrative oversight for Science Triangle programs and initiatives while collaborating closely with university leadership, academic units, community partners, and Science Triangle stakeholders to advance the mission and strategic goals. The Science Triangle integrates three major public-facing scientific and educational assets of the university: Shellam Flake Planetarium, UA Little Rock Observatory, and the Museum of Natural History. The Director will unify these facilities under a shared mission focused on STEM education, public engagement, science outreach, experiential learning, community partnerships, and interdisciplinary programming. The position will strengthen the university\u2019s role as a regional center for science communication, STEM education, and public scientific literacy while supporting academic initiatives across Arkansas. This position is governed by state and federal laws and agency/institution policy. Qualifications: Required Education and/or Experience: Master\u2019s degree in a STEM field, museum studies, natural sciences, STEM education, public administration, or a related discipline; Demonstrated leadership experience in science outreach and STEM education programming; Strong leadership, organizational, and communication skills; Experience developing partnerships and collaborative programs; Experience managing educational or public-facing scientific facilities, programs, or initiatives. Preferred Education and/or Experience: Earned doctorate in a STEM field, museum studies, natural sciences, STEM education, public administration, or a related discipline; Experience directing or managing a planetarium, observatory, museum, science center, or public outreach program; Experience securing external funding through grants, sponsorships, or philanthropy; Experience working with K\u201312 educational systems and community organizations; Experience supervising multidisciplinary teams and coordinating public programming; Familiarity with STEM outreach technologies, museum exhibits, and experiential STEM learning models. Job Duties and Responsibilities: Strategic Leadership Develop and implement a comprehensive strategic vision for the Science Triangle initiative; Lead the implementation and periodic updating of the Science Triangle strategic plan; Create synergies among the planetarium, observatory, and museum facilities to enhance educational and community impact; Promote interdisciplinary collaboration among faculty, students, educators, and external partners; Position the Science Triangle as a premier regional destination for science outreach and STEM education. Public Engagement & Community Outreach Expand public programming including lectures, exhibitions, astronomy nights, science festivals, workshops, and K\u201312 outreach activities; Develop initiatives that increase community participation and scientific literacy throughout Central Arkansas; Build partnerships with schools, museums, libraries, nonprofits, government agencies, and community organizations; Serve as a public ambassador for the Science Triangle and the university at local, regional, and national events; Develop and manage volunteer engagement programs and advisory groups that support Science Triangle initiatives. Educational Programming Support curriculum-connected educational experiences for K\u201312 students, undergraduate students, and lifelong learners; Coordinate hands-on learning opportunities involving STEM disciplines and emerging technologies; Create opportunities for undergraduate and graduate students to engage in outreach, science communication, informal STEM education, and public programming; Encourage experiential learning opportunities for students through internships, outreach activities, and facility operations; Develop teacher-training programs and educational resources aligned with Arkansas STEM education priorities; Support and participate in scholarly activities related to STEM education, informal science learning, outreach assessment, and public engagement. Operations & Facility Coordination Oversee operational coordination among the planetarium, observatory, and museum-related activities; Assist in scheduling, program development, visitor engagement, and facility utilization strategies; Work collaboratively with technical staff, educators, faculty, and volunteers to ensure high-quality programming and visitor experiences; Support the maintenance and modernization of scientific equipment, exhibits, and educational technologies. Advancement & External Partnerships Work with the University Advancement Office to cultivate donors and secure philanthropic support for Science Triangle initiatives; Pursue external funding opportunities through grants, sponsorships, philanthropy, and public-private partnerships; Develop relationships with donors, scientific organizations, cultural institutions, and industry partners; Collaborate with university advancement and research offices to support long-term sustainability and growth; Support Science Triangle advisory committees and stakeholder groups; Identify opportunities for regional and national visibility through collaborative initiatives and special events. Administration & Assessment Manage budgets, reporting, strategic planning, and performance assessment for the Science Triangle initiative; Establish measurable goals related to visitor engagement, educational impact, outreach effectiveness, and partnership development; Develop and communicate evidence-based assessments of educational, community, and economic impact; Ensure compliance with university policies and safety procedures; Supervise personnel, student workers, and volunteers associated with the initiative. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Ability to communicate scientific concepts effectively to diverse audiences; Strong commitment to public engagement and science literacy; Ability to develop innovative educational and outreach programs; Ability to manage multiple facilities and collaborative initiatives simultaneously; Strong interpersonal and partnership-building skills; Commitment to fostering inclusive and accessible STEM education opportunities. Additional Information: Salary Information: $75,000 Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Curriculum Vitae, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Tansel Karabacka, Ph.D. | Professor and Dean Donaghey College of Science, Technology, Engineering, and Mathematics University of Arkansas at Little Rock txkarabacak@ualr.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Grasping, Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting, Talking Occasional Physical Activity: Grasping, Standing Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Administrative-Analyst---Science-Triangle_R0088143-1": {"title": "Administrative Analyst - Science Triangle", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-10\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Staff - Clerical Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Little Rock The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is a metropolitan research university that provides an accessible, quality education through flexible learning and unparalleled internship opportunities. At UA Little Rock, we prepare our more than 8,900 students to be innovators and responsible leaders in their fields. Committed to its metropolitan research university mission, UA Little Rock is a driving force in Little Rock's thriving cultural community and a major component of the city and state's growing profile as a regional leader in research, technology transfer, economic development, and job creation. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . Department: Donaghey College of Science, Technology, Engineering & Mathematics Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: UA Little Rock is seeking to hire an Administrative Analyst for the Science Triangle. The Administrative Analyst will provide administrative, operational, and organizational support for the Science Triangle initiative at the University of Arkansas at Little Rock. The position supports the daily operations and coordination of activities associated with the Shellam Flake Planetarium, UA Little Rock Observatory, and Museum of Natural History, as part of the Science Triangle initiative. The Administrative Analyst serves as a central point of communication for internal and external stakeholders, university staff, faculty, outreach coordinators, student workers, volunteers, community partners, and assists with scheduling, event coordination, records management, communications, visitor engagement, and office operations. The individual in this role must demonstrate professionalism, discretion, strong organizational skills, and the ability to manage multiple priorities in a dynamic educational and public outreach environment. This position is governed by state and federal laws and agency instituiton/policy. Qualifications: Required Education and/or Experience: Associate degree in business administration, communications, public administration, office administration, or a related field; or equivalent combination of education and experience; Demonstrated administrative or executive support experience; Strong organizational, communication, and interpersonal skills; Proficiency with standard office software, scheduling systems, and digital communication tools; Ability to manage multiple tasks and deadlines effectively. Preferred Education and/or Experience: Bachelor\u2019s degree in business administration, communications, public administration, or a related field; Experience working in higher education, public-facing educational organizations, museums, science centers, outreach programs, or nonprofit organizations; Experience supporting public events or educational programming; Familiarity with university administrative systems and procedures; Experience with website management, social media, or event coordination; Experience using event registration, customer relationship management (CRM), or visitor management systems. Job Duties and Responsibilities: Administrative Support Provide direct administrative support to the Director of the Science Triangle; Manage calendars, appointments, meetings, and travel arrangements; Prepare correspondence, reports, presentations, agendas, and meeting minutes; Maintain organized records, files, databases, and operational documents; Assist with budget tracking, purchasing requests, reimbursements, and financial documentation. Perform other duties as assigned. Program & Event Coordination Maintain and coordinate a unified Science Triangle calendar encompassing educational programs, outreach activities, facility reservations, and special events; Coordinate event logistics, including facility reservations, registrations, communications, catering, transportation, audiovisual support, and post-event follow-up; Support the coordination of public events, workshops, astronomy nights, educational programs, exhibitions, and outreach activities; Assist with scheduling facility use for the planetarium, observatory, and related Science Triangle programs; Coordinate logistics for visiting speakers, school groups, community partners, and special events; Assist with registration and communication activities. Communications & Public Engagement Serve as a primary point of contact for inquiries from students, faculty, schools, community organizations, and the public; Assist with the preparation and distribution of promotional materials, newsletters, announcements, and outreach communications; Support website content updates and coordinate with university marketing personnel regarding social media and promotional activities; Provide professional customer service to visitors and stakeholders; Assist with visitor reception, guest services, and public-facing operations associated with Science Triangle facilities and programs. Office Operations Maintain office supplies, scheduling systems, and operational workflows; Assist in coordinating student workers, volunteers, and temporary staff schedules; Ensure proper handling of confidential information and university records; Support compliance with university administrative procedures and policies. Coordination & Collaboration Facilitate communication among university departments, outreach personnel, faculty, and external partners; Assist with grant administration, documentation, reporting, and recordkeeping activities associated with Science Triangle projects and programs; Support strategic initiatives and special projects led by the Director; Participate in planning meetings and operational coordination activities. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Excellent written and verbal communication skills; Strong attention to detail and organizational abilities; Ability to organize and coordinate multiple events and projects simultaneously; Ability to interact professionally with diverse audiences; Ability to maintain confidentiality and exercise sound judgment; Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a fast-paced environment; Ability to work occasional evenings and weekends in support of Science Triangle programming and special events; Commitment to supporting public engagement and STEM education initiatives. Additional Information: Salary Information: $36,327 Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Tansel Karabacka, Ph.D. | Professor and Dean Donaghey College of Science, Technology, Engineering, and Mathematics University of Arkansas at Little Rock txkarabacak@ualr.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Financial Credit Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Repetitive Motion Frequent Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting Occasional Physical Activity: Kneeling, Standing, Walking Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Program-Manager-for-Planetarium_R0088142": {"title": "Program Manager for Planetarium", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-10\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Project Management Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Little Rock The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is a metropolitan research university that provides an accessible, quality education through flexible learning and unparalleled internship opportunities. At UA Little Rock, we prepare our more than 8,900 students to be innovators and responsible leaders in their fields. Committed to its metropolitan research university mission, UA Little Rock is a driving force in Little Rock's thriving cultural community and a major component of the city and state's growing profile as a regional leader in research, technology transfer, economic development, and job creation. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . Department: Donaghey College of Science, Technology, Engineering & Mathematics Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: UA Little Rock is seeking to hire a Planetarium Program Manager for the Shellam Flake Planetarium. The Program Manager is responsible for the development, coordination, and daily management of educational programming, public outreach activities, visitor engagement, and operational support for the planetarium. The Planetarium Program Manager will play a central role in advancing STEM education and outreach, experiential learning, and community engagement initiatives at the University of Arkansas at Little Rock. The position supports the mission of the Science Triangle by creating innovative and accessible educational experiences for K\u201312 students, university students, educators, and the broader public. The position will collaborate with faculty, staff, schools, community organizations, and external partners to expand the planetarium's impact and visibility as a regional hub for science education and public engagement. The Program Manager will also collaborate with other Science Triangle facilities and initiatives to support interdisciplinary STEM education, outreach, and public engagement activities. This position is governed by state and federal laws and agency/institution policies. Qualifications: Required Education and/or Experience: Bachelor\u2019s degree in astronomy, physics, STEM education, science communication, museum studies, communications, or a related field; Experience in science outreach, education, public programming, or informal STEM learning; Strong organizational, communication, and presentation skills; Ability to work evenings and weekends as required for public events and astronomy programming. Preferred Education and/or Experience: Master's degree in astronomy, physics, science education, STEM education, science communication, museum studies, communications, or a related field; Experience presenting live planetarium programs to public audiences; Experience developing K\u201312 STEM educational programming; Familiarity with planetarium software, astronomical visualization systems, and audiovisual technologies; Experience supervising student employees, interns, or volunteers; Experience with grant-supported educational or outreach programs. Job Duties and Responsibilities: Educational Programming Develop, coordinate, and deliver planetarium shows, educational programs, workshops, and STEM outreach activities; Design programming aligned with Arkansas K\u201312 science standards and university educational objectives; Create engaging educational content related to STEM fields and emerging technologies; Coordinate special programs for schools, summer camps, teacher workshops, and community organizations; Develop, adapt, or curate full-dome content, interactive presentations, and educational resources for diverse audiences; Develop programming that is accessible and engaging for audiences with diverse educational backgrounds, abilities, and interests; Evaluate educational programming and outreach activities to support continuous improvement and reporting. Public Outreach & Community Engagement Organize and support public astronomy events, guest lectures, science festivals, and special presentations; Build partnerships with schools, museums, libraries, nonprofits, and community organizations; Develop and maintain partnerships with K\u201312 educators to enhance classroom integration of planetarium programming and STEM learning resources; Promote scientific literacy and public interest in STEM disciplines; Assist in expanding outreach efforts to underserved and rural communities across Arkansas. Planetarium Operations Coordinate scheduling, facility utilization, and daily operations of the planetarium; Operate and assist with maintenance of planetarium projection systems, audiovisual equipment, and educational technologies; Ensure high-quality visitor experiences during public programs and educational events; Support educational, community, and special-event use of the planetarium facility; Assist with facility management, safety procedures, preventive maintenance, and equipment upgrades. Student & Volunteer Engagement Supervise and train student workers, interns, and volunteers involved in planetarium operations and outreach activities; Support experiential learning opportunities for undergraduate and graduate students; Encourage student participation in science communication and outreach initiatives. Communications & Promotion Assist with marketing and promotion of planetarium programs through digital media, newsletters, and community outreach; Coordinate event announcements, registration activities, and public communications; Support website content updates and coordinate with university marketing personnel regarding promotion of planetarium programming. Administrative & Strategic Support Assist with budget tracking, program assessment, reporting, and operational planning; Collect and analyze participation and visitor engagement metrics; Support grant proposals, sponsorship development, and fundraising activities related to educational programming; Contribute to long-term strategic planning for the planetarium and Science Triangle initiatives. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Ability to communicate scientific concepts to audiences of all ages and backgrounds; Strong public speaking and educational presentation skills; Ability to manage multiple programs and events simultaneously; Ability to work collaboratively with educators, faculty, students, and community partners; Strong technical aptitude related to educational and audiovisual technologies; Commitment to inclusive and accessible STEM education and outreach. Additional Information: Salary Information: $55,000 Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Curriculum Vitae, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Tansel Karabacka, Ph.D. | Professor and Dean Donaghey College of Science, Technology, Engineering, and Mathematics University of Arkansas at Little Rock txkarabacak@ualr.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Feeling, Grasping, Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting Frequent Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting, Talking Occasional Physical Activity: Crouching, Kneeling, Lifting, Walking Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Cossatot-Community-College-of-the-University-of-Arkansas/Agriculture-Instructor-Program-Advancement-Coordinator_R0088210": {"title": "Agriculture Instructor/Program Advancement Coordinator", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-09\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Faculty - Non-Tenure Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: Cossatot Community College of the University of Arkansas Cossatot Community College of the University of Arkansas (UA Cossatot) began in DeQueen, Arkansas in 1975 as an Arkansas Vocational-Technical School, designed to provide relevant workforce training for four counties in southwest Arkansas. Fast forward to now where UA Cossatot has four vibrant campuses and over 1500 students learning in a variety of for-credit disciplines plus a host of area industry employees sharpening their skills through our workforce training programs. UA Cossatot prides itself on a safe work environment, where all employees undergo rigorous background checks and are welcomed to the college with an abundance of hands-on orientations to their positions. UA Cossatot also embraces Continuous Quality Improvement (CQI) where everything we do is measured and analyzed to ensure we are giving students the very best we have to offer. CQI involves all employees and completes a cycle that starts with the strategic plan and ends with an Institutional Effectiveness Evaluation. It's okay to brag a little when you work for UA Cossatot!Cossatot Community College of the University o Arkansas is an NCA-accredited two-year institution affiliated with the University of Arkansas System with Campuses in De Queen, Nashville, Ashdown, and Lockesburg Arkansas. The Colleges designated service area includes Sevier, Little River, Howard and Pike counties.\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please submit a request via the OEOC website: \u00a0Applicants are required to submit a request for each position to which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at (870) 584-1104. Department: Division of Professional and Technical Programs Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Agriculture Instructor/Coordinator of Program Advancement is responsible for providing high-quality instruction while serving as the primary leader for the growth and development of the Agriculture Program at UA Cossatot. This is a full-time, on-campus position requiring 40 hours per week, with occasional travel. The appointment year runs from August 1 through June 30, providing the month of July off each year, and renews annually. Primary Responsibilities \u2022 Teach assigned courses, develop curriculum, assess student learning outcomes, and create engaging, hands-on learning experiences that prepare students for careers in agriculture. \u2022 Aggressively grow the Agriculture Program through student recruitment, community outreach, and strategic partnerships with schools, FFA chapters, industry, and other colleges. \u2022 Help develop and guide a collegiate judging team. \u2022 Advise the Collegiate FFA chapter. \u2022 Plan and expand the annual Colts Classic competition. \u2022 Participate in grant writing and administration. \u2022 Oversee the development of a campus farm. \u2022 Manage the greenhouse. Qualifications: \u00b7 \u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Master's degree in agriculture or closely related field. \u00b7 \u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Relevant experience in agriculture, agribusiness, agricultural education, or related field. \u00b7 \u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Experience with FFA, Extension, judging teams, or similar leadership programs preferred. \u00b7 \u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Previous teaching experience preferred. Additional Information: Annual Compensation Package Includes Annual salary range of $50,000\u2013$55,000, depending on experience, education, and hands-on farming experience. Compensation package includes health, dental, and life insurance; short- and long-term disability insurance; a retirement plan with employer matching; paid sick leave; and educational assistance for employees and their dependents. All applications must include a cover letter, an updated r\u00e9sum\u00e9, and copies of college transcripts. Applications received without the required documents will be considered incomplete and will not be reviewed. Salary Information: Annual salary range of $50,000\u2013$55,000, depending on experience, education, and hands-on farming experience. Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Resume, Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: All applications must include a cover letter, an updated r\u00e9sum\u00e9, and copies of college transcripts. Applications received without the required documents will be considered incomplete and will not be reviewed. Recruitment Contact Information: Kelly Plunk, Director of Human Resources, (870) 584-1104 or kplunk@cccua.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check Cossatot Community College of the University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Fayetteville-AR/Facilities-Management---Custodial-Lead---2nd-Shift_R0088222-1": {"title": "Facilities Management - Custodial Lead - 2nd Shift", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-09\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com, then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at all University of Arkansas institutions will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students.\u201d University of Arkansas, Fayetteville students will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Student Jobs at UAF.\u201d All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. Closing Date: Type of Position: Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Night Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas, Fayetteville Founded in 1871, the University of Arkansas is a land grant institution, classified by the Carnegie Foundation among the nation\u2019s top 2 percent of universities with the highest level of research activity. The University of Arkansas works to advance the state and build a better world through education, research, and outreach by providing transformational opportunities and skills, fostering a welcoming climate, and nurturing creativity, discovery, and the spread of new ideas and innovations. The University of Arkansas campus is located in Fayetteville, a welcoming community ranked as one of the best places to live in the U.S. The growing region surrounding Fayetteville is home to numerous Fortune 500 companies and one of the nation\u2019s strongest economies. Northwest Arkansas is also quickly gaining a national reputation for its focus on the arts and overall quality of life. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10% of employee salary. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions, you should review before applying for the opening. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process, please submit a request via the Disability Accommodations | OEOC | University of Arkansas (uark.edu) : Request an Accommodation. Appli\u00adcants are required to submit a request for each position of which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 479.575.5351. Department: Building Services Department's Website: https://fama.uark.edu/ Summary of Job Duties: The Custodial Lead is responsible for general cleaning of areas in and around office buildings, class rooms, lecture halls, conference rooms, auditoriums, building common areas, and other areas as required (such as, vacuuming, mopping, sweeping, dusting, emptying small office trash cans and large brut trash cans, using carpet extractor, using floor buffer, cleaning commodes, sinks, water fountains, etc.). Snow/ice removal during winter months. Assist Coordinator of Housekeeping leading a team. Regular, reliable, and non-disruptive attendance is an essential job duty, as is the ability to create and maintain collegial, harmonious working relationships with others. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Ability to effectively communicate to be able to perform job duties At least one year of experience in housekeeping Valid Driver\u2019s License in good standings At least one year of leadership experience Preferred Qualifications: Bilingual in English and Spanish, with the ability to communicate effectively in both languages, verbally At least three years of experience in housekeeping At least two years supervisory or leadership experience Knowledge, Skills & Abilities: Knowledge of supervisory practices and procedures Knowledge of custodial and maintenance practices and techniques Knowledge of materials and equipment used in custodial and maintenance work Knowledge of the operation and maintenance requirements of commercial laundry equipment Ability to maintain adequate supplies and inventory records Ability to prepare written documents Ability to conduct inspections to determine compliance with standards Ability to lead a staff of custodial workers and semi-skilled maintenance repairmen Additional Information: 2nd Shift: 3:00 PM - 11:30PM This post is for current and anticipated future openings. Salary Information: $36,300 + 6% Shift Differential Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Recruitment Contact Information: Troy Vela, Strategic Talent Acquisition Specialist, tvela1@uark.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Special Instructions to Applicants: Pre-employment Screening Requirements: The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas seeks to attract, develop and retain high quality faculty, staff and administrators that consistently display practices and behaviors to advance a culture that embeds equal opportunity, educational excellence and unparalleled access for all. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All Application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Fayetteville-AR/Facilities-Management---Custodial-Lead---3rd-Shift_R0077817-1": {"title": "Facilities Management - Custodial Lead - 3rd Shift", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-09\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com, then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at all University of Arkansas institutions will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students.\u201d University of Arkansas, Fayetteville students will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Student Jobs at UAF.\u201d All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. Closing Date: Type of Position: Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Night Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas, Fayetteville Founded in 1871, the University of Arkansas is a land grant institution, classified by the Carnegie Foundation among the nation\u2019s top 2 percent of universities with the highest level of research activity. The University of Arkansas works to advance the state and build a better world through education, research, and outreach by providing transformational opportunities and skills, fostering a welcoming climate, and nurturing creativity, discovery, and the spread of new ideas and innovations. The University of Arkansas campus is located in Fayetteville, a welcoming community ranked as one of the best places to live in the U.S. The growing region surrounding Fayetteville is home to numerous Fortune 500 companies and one of the nation\u2019s strongest economies. Northwest Arkansas is also quickly gaining a national reputation for its focus on the arts and overall quality of life. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10% of employee salary. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions, you should review before applying for the opening. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process, please submit a request via the Disability Accommodations | OEOC | University of Arkansas (uark.edu) : Request an Accommodation. Appli\u00adcants are required to submit a request for each position of which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 479.575.5351. Department: Building Services Department's Website: https://fama.uark.edu/ Summary of Job Duties: The Custodial Lead is responsible for general cleaning of areas in and around office buildings, class rooms, lecture halls, conference rooms, auditoriums, building common areas, and other areas as required (such as, vacuuming, mopping, sweeping, dusting, emptying small office trash cans and large brut trash cans, using carpet extractor, using floor buffer, cleaning commodes, sinks, water fountains, etc.). Snow/ice removal during winter months. Assist Coordinator of Housekeeping leading a team. Regular, reliable, and non-disruptive attendance is an essential job duty, as is the ability to create and maintain collegial, harmonious working relationships with others. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Ability to effectively communicate to be able to perform job duties At least one year of experience in housekeeping Valid Driver\u2019s License in good standings At least one year of leadership experience Preferred Qualifications: Bilingual in English and Spanish, with the ability to communicate effectively in both languages, verbally At least three years of experience in housekeeping At least two years supervisory or leadership experience Knowledge, Skills & Abilities: Knowledge of supervisory practices and procedures Knowledge of custodial and maintenance practices and techniques Knowledge of materials and equipment used in custodial and maintenance work Knowledge of the operation and maintenance requirements of commercial laundry equipment Ability to maintain adequate supplies and inventory records Ability to prepare written documents Ability to conduct inspections to determine compliance with standards Ability to lead a staff of custodial workers and semi-skilled maintenance repairmen Additional Information: 3rd Shift: 10:30PM - 7:00AM, Sunday - Thursday This post is for current and anticipated future openings. Salary Information: $36,300 + 12% Shift Differential Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), Proof of Veteran Status Recruitment Contact Information: Caitlin Hughes, Strategic Talent Acquisition Specialist, cmmitche@uark.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Special Instructions to Applicants: Pre-employment Screening Requirements: The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas seeks to attract, develop and retain high quality faculty, staff and administrators that consistently display practices and behaviors to advance a culture that embeds equal opportunity, educational excellence and unparalleled access for all. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All Application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Fayetteville-AR/Facilities-Management---Custodian-I---3rd-Shift_R0088219-1": {"title": "Facilities Management - Custodian I - 3rd Shift", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-09\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com, then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at all University of Arkansas institutions will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students.\u201d University of Arkansas, Fayetteville students will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Student Jobs at UAF.\u201d All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. Closing Date: Type of Position: Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas, Fayetteville Founded in 1871, the University of Arkansas is a land grant institution, classified by the Carnegie Foundation among the nation\u2019s top 2 percent of universities with the highest level of research activity. The University of Arkansas works to advance the state and build a better world through education, research, and outreach by providing transformational opportunities and skills, fostering a welcoming climate, and nurturing creativity, discovery, and the spread of new ideas and innovations. The University of Arkansas campus is located in Fayetteville, a welcoming community ranked as one of the best places to live in the U.S. The growing region surrounding Fayetteville is home to numerous Fortune 500 companies and one of the nation\u2019s strongest economies. Northwest Arkansas is also quickly gaining a national reputation for its focus on the arts and overall quality of life. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10% of employee salary. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions, you should review before applying for the opening. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process, please submit a request via the Disability Accommodations | OEOC | University of Arkansas (uark.edu) : Request an Accommodation. Appli\u00adcants are required to submit a request for each position of which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 479.575.5351. Department: Building Services Department's Website: https://fama.uark.edu/ Summary of Job Duties: The Custodian I is responsible for general cleaning of areas in and around office buildings, classrooms, lecture halls, conference rooms, auditoriums, building common areas, and other areas on campus as required. This will include vacuuming, mopping, sweeping, dusting, and emptying small office trash cans as well as large Brute trash cans. This position will also be responsible for using a carpet extractor and a floor buffer, cleaning commodes, sinks, water fountains, etc. This position will also be responsible for snow/ice removal during winter months. Other duties as assigned. Regular, reliable, and non-disruptive attendance is an essential job function of this job, as is the ability to create and maintain collegial, harmonious working relationships with others. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Ability to effectively communicate to be able to perform job duties Preferred Qualifications: At least one year of custodial experience in the commercial/corporate industry Knowledge, Skills & Abilities: Knowledge of basic cleaning techniques Knowledge of cleaning equipment operation and maintenance Ability to follow instructions and perform repetitive manual work Ability to use cleansers and other agents to clean floors and furniture Ability to use housekeeping cleaning supplies and equipment Ability to work independently without close supervision Ability to follow oral and/or written instructions Ability to perform multiple tasks and to prioritize assignments Ability to perform repetitive manual work Ability to do required lifting (up to 50 lbs.) Additional Information: 3rd Shift: 10:30PM - 7AM This post is for current and anticipated future openings. Salary Information: $31,200 +12% Shift Differential Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Proof of Veteran Status Recruitment Contact Information: Troy Vela, Strategic Talent Acquisition Specialist, tvela1@uark.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Special Instructions to Applicants: Pre-employment Screening Requirements: The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas seeks to attract, develop and retain high quality faculty, staff and administrators that consistently display practices and behaviors to advance a culture that embeds equal opportunity, educational excellence and unparalleled access for all. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All Application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Fayetteville-AR/Facilities-Management---Custodian-I---2nd-Shift_R0088213-1": {"title": "Facilities Management - Custodian I - 2nd Shift", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-09\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com, then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at all University of Arkansas institutions will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students.\u201d University of Arkansas, Fayetteville students will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Student Jobs at UAF.\u201d All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. Closing Date: Type of Position: Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas, Fayetteville Founded in 1871, the University of Arkansas is a land grant institution, classified by the Carnegie Foundation among the nation\u2019s top 2 percent of universities with the highest level of research activity. The University of Arkansas works to advance the state and build a better world through education, research, and outreach by providing transformational opportunities and skills, fostering a welcoming climate, and nurturing creativity, discovery, and the spread of new ideas and innovations. The University of Arkansas campus is located in Fayetteville, a welcoming community ranked as one of the best places to live in the U.S. The growing region surrounding Fayetteville is home to numerous Fortune 500 companies and one of the nation\u2019s strongest economies. Northwest Arkansas is also quickly gaining a national reputation for its focus on the arts and overall quality of life. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10% of employee salary. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions, you should review before applying for the opening. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process, please submit a request via the Disability Accommodations | OEOC | University of Arkansas (uark.edu) : Request an Accommodation. Appli\u00adcants are required to submit a request for each position of which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 479.575.5351. Department: Building Services Department's Website: https://fama.uark.edu/ Summary of Job Duties: The Custodian I is responsible for general cleaning of areas in and around office buildings, classrooms, lecture halls, conference rooms, auditoriums, building common areas, and other areas on campus as required. This will include vacuuming, mopping, sweeping, dusting, and emptying small office trash cans as well as large Brute trash cans. This position will also be responsible for using a carpet extractor and a floor buffer, cleaning commodes, sinks, water fountains, etc. This position will also be responsible for snow/ice removal during winter months. Other duties as assigned. Regular, reliable, and non-disruptive attendance is an essential job function of this job, as is the ability to create and maintain collegial, harmonious working relationships with others. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Ability to effectively communicate to be able to perform job duties Preferred Qualifications: At least one year of custodial experience in the commercial/corporate industry Knowledge, Skills & Abilities: Knowledge of basic cleaning techniques Knowledge of cleaning equipment operation and maintenance Ability to follow instructions and perform repetitive manual work Ability to use cleansers and other agents to clean floors and furniture Ability to use housekeeping cleaning supplies and equipment Ability to work independently without close supervision Ability to follow oral and/or written instructions Ability to perform multiple tasks and to prioritize assignments Ability to perform repetitive manual work Ability to do required lifting (up to 50 lbs.) Additional Information: 2nd Shift: 3:00 PM - 11:30PM This post is for current and anticipated future openings. Salary Information: $31,200 +6% Shift Differential Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Proof of Veteran Status Recruitment Contact Information: Troy Vela, Strategic Talent Acquisition Specialist, tvela1@uark.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Special Instructions to Applicants: Pre-employment Screening Requirements: The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas seeks to attract, develop and retain high quality faculty, staff and administrators that consistently display practices and behaviors to advance a culture that embeds equal opportunity, educational excellence and unparalleled access for all. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All Application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAM--Monticello-Campus/Extra-Help-Golf_R0085116": {"title": "Graduate Assistant -Men's and Women's Golf", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-09\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Staff (Classified) (Inactive) Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Monticello UAM, one of twenty campuses of the University of Arkansas System, is located in southeastern Arkansas in the beautiful timberlands, rich in outdoor recreation activities, and approximately 100 miles south of Little Rock. UAM is a comprehensive, residential and commuter, undergraduate institution also offering selected master\u2019s degree programs. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please submit a request via the OEOC website: \u00a0Applicants are required to submit a request for each position to which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 870-460-1422 . Department: UAM | Golf Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Attend all meetings as directed by head coach. Daily golf practices. Strength, conditioning and flexibility workout leadership. Nutrition program development. Attend tournaments as assigned. Travel with selected teams to tournaments when dates conflict. Ensure a commitment to the academic success of student athletes. Qualifications: Dependable, on-time, can work whenever needed, and honest. Additional Information: Covers meal plan and housing plus 18 hours of Graduate School. Salary Information: $11.00 / hour Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Alex Spainhouer - Assistant Athletic Director for Internal Affairs & Special Events - 870-460-1157 All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Motor Vehicle Reports Check The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Balancing, Climbing, Crawling, Crouching, Driving, Feeling, Grasping, Hearing, Kneeling, Lifting, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Repetitive Motion, Sharps, Sitting, Standing, Stooping, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Balancing, Climbing, Crawling, Crouching, Driving, Feeling, Grasping, Hearing, Kneeling, Lifting, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Repetitive Motion, Sharps, Sitting, Standing, Stooping, Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Balancing, Climbing, Crawling, Crouching, Driving, Feeling, Grasping, Hearing, Kneeling, Lifting, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Repetitive Motion, Sharps, Sitting, Standing, Stooping, Talking, Walking Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/North-Little-Rock/Maintenance-Supervisor_R0087252": {"title": "Maintenance Supervisor", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-09\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 10/31/2026 Type of Position: Skilled Labor Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas Pulaski Technical College University of Arkansas - Pulaski Technical College at North Little Rock is an integral part of the Arkansas Technical and Community College System maintained by the State of Arkansas. The college is governed by the University of Arkansas System Board of Trustees and a seven-member Board of Visitors and derives its support largely from student tuition and fees and legislative appropriations. UA - Pulaski Tech, a comprehensive two-year college, offers associate degree and certificate programs for students who plan to transfer to four-year colleges and universities and/or for career preparation and advancement. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply link/button. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at (501) 812-2839. Department: Maintenance Operations Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: \u2022 Follows all integrity guidelines and procedures and ensures no manipulation of data. \u2022 Performs repair and preventive maintenance to the facility, grounds and systems. \u2022 Inspects the work of other maintenance personnel. \u2022 Physical requirements include sitting, standing, climbing, walking, lifting, pulling and/or pushing, carrying, reaching, stooping and crouching. \u2022 Researches and recommends purchase of replacement equipment as needed. \u2022 Provides supervision for maintenance personnel. \u2022 Oversee the activities and quality of performance of outside contractors performing repairs and/or replacement of equipment. \u2022 Conducts periodic inspections of building systems and equipment to ensure working quality. \u2022 Conducts inspections and maintains code and safety requirements. \u2022 Produces quality work/assignments in a thorough, timely and accurate manner. \u2022 Maintains appropriate personal attendance, accountability and work productivity standards. \u2022 Understands and applies job knowledge to effectively complete all required job responsibilities. Proactively maintains the skills required to perform job duties. \u2022 Shows respect and courtesy to students and staff. \u2022 Provides quality services for students and staff ensuring that quality is maintained and needs are met. \u2022 Exchanges ideas and information, both orally and in writing, in a clear and concise manner and contributes meaningfully to group efforts by offering relevant ideas and knowledge. \u2022 Effectively articulates thoughts and ideas. Identifies problems, analyzes causes and evaluates appropriate solutions prior to taking or recommending actions. Follows up to ensure prompt/appropriate action is taken and that problems are in fact corrected. \u2022 Works in partnership with staff from all Departments to ensure effective supervision and services are provided. \u2022 Accepts direction and supervision to include assignments to temporarily perform job responsibilities of other positions and time frames. \u2022 Other duties as assigned. Qualifications: Required:\u00a0 High School Diploma or equivalent, HVAC certification with a minimum of 5 years\u2019 experience. \u00a0Minimum 5 years\u2019 experience in building maintenance required with working knowledge of PMs and work order systems. Required: 3 years of previous lead or supervisory experience. Physical requirements include sitting, standing, climbing, walking, lifting, pulling and/or pushing, carrying, reaching, stooping and crouching. Demonstrates the ability to lift 40 pounds and / or the ability to assess the lift load in order to ask for necessary assistance. Additional Information: Salary Information: $47,500 Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants Recruitment Contact Information: Human Resources humanresources@uaptc.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Motor Vehicle Reports Check, Sex Offender Registry University of Arkansas - Pulaski Technical College is committed to providing a safe campus community. Title IX protects the college community from sexual harassment in a school's education programs and activities. This means that Title IX protects the college community in connection with all academic, educational, extracurricular, athletic, and other programs of the school, whether those programs take place in a school's facilities, in college transportation, at a class or training program sponsored by the school at another location, or elsewhere. \u00a0 We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Climbing, Crouching, Lifting, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Sitting, Standing, Stooping, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Crawling, Driving, Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Talking Occasional Physical Activity: Balancing Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAFS--University-of-Arkansas-Fort-Smith/Resident-Director--Lion-s-Den_R0088145": {"title": "Resident Director, Lion's Den", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-09\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Professional Staff - Student Affairs Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Fort Smith University of Arkansas \u2013 Fort Smith The University of Arkansas - Fort Smith is a dynamic, mid-sized public university that\u2019s redefining higher education. We\u2019re on a mission to provide transformative, hands-on learning experiences for students of all backgrounds and aspirations. Our multi-faceted approach to education offers a wealth of opportunities, with over 70 academic programs, including certificates, associate, bachelor\u2019s, and master\u2019s degrees. We\u2019re committed to building a diverse community that mirrors Arkansas\u2019s rich tapestry, reflecting our dedication to serving the state\u2019s varied population while enhancing the quality of our institution. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life, and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10 percent of employee salary. \u00a0 Fort Smith, Arkansas Nestled along the Arkansas River, this vibrant city offers a perfect blend of history, culture, and natural beauty. Immerse yourself in the rich heritage of the Old West at the Fort Smith National Historic Site, explore the eclectic local art scene, or take a scenic stroll along the picturesque riverfront trails. With a welcoming community, diverse dining options, and a thriving downtown, Fort Smith is the ideal destination for history enthusiasts and those seeking modern amenities. Thank you for your interest in joining our university. Below you will find details for the position including any supplementary documentation and/or questions you should review before submitting your application. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at (479) 788-7080. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 479-788-7080. Applicants are required to submit a request for each position to which they have applied. Department: Housing and Residential Life Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Lions\u2019 Den Resident Director is a full-time live-in position that reports directly to the Assistant Dean of Students for Housing & Campus and Community Engagement. As a member of the Student Affairs staff, they are responsible for the general welfare of all students, encouraging them to maximize their intellectual growth and personal development. They are expected to positively influence, contribute to, and improve the quality of life of the residential student through the residential curriculum, implementing college policies and procedures, and by forming relationships with students in their facility. Qualifications: Required Education and/or Work Experience: Minimum requirements include a bachelor's degree with at least one-year significant experience in a student housing employment position or equivalent experience. The position requires knowledge and skills related to human development, programming, conflict resolution, and the fair application of regulations. Other job-related education and/or experience may be substituted for part of these requirements. Preferred Education and/or Work Experience: Candidates with a master's degree in college student personnel, educational administration, or a related field, and previous experience supervising resident assistants, working with a residence hall association, and working with peer student conduct systems are preferred. Excellent verbal and written communication skills, the ability to work with diverse populations effectively, and excellent customer service skills are all expected. Essential Job Duties and Responsibilities: Supervise 14 Resident Assistants through weekly staff meetings, scheduled 1 on 1s, monitoring programming and community development, and semester evaluations Participate in the development, coordination and implementation of Housing & Residential Life procedures and programs Coordinate the assignments, contract, and billing processes for Lion\u2019s Den residents Serve as a University Conduct Administrator. Serve as a conduct officer for assigned residential area. Inform Assistant Dean of Students for Housing & Campus and Community Engagement of any issues. Serve in an on-call capacity with other HRL professional staff. Respond to all situations by answering phone, working with Resident Assistant On Call, and communicating with applicable staff such as the University Police Department, state and local emergency personnel, Assistant Dean of Students for Housing & Campus and Community Engagement, and other chief Student Affairs personnel Supervise front desk/ office operations including supervising RAs and student workers in the office, receiving mail and packages, communicating with residents and visitors, and answering the phone Coordinate all move in and move out times and processes. Includes inspection of each room after the students have vacated and before it is occupied again, distribution and collection of applicable housing forms, and timely communication to residents Ensure that the quality and cleanliness of residential area, including outdoor property, is maintained Work jointly with Assistant Dean of Students for Housing & Campus and Community Engagement and Director of Facilities & Environmental Safety to ensure ongoing upkeep of facilities, custodial needs, maintenance efforts, and timely responses to work order requests Coordinate lock and key changes with maintenance and track all key use, loss, and theft Conduct quarterly Health & Safety Inspections of all rooms with the help of Resident Assistants. Document all work order needs and damage. Address any conduct violations. Implement, interpret, and continually develop HRL policies as stated in the Residential Handbook and Student Code of Conduct Serve as a Campus Security Authority (CSA) by understanding and following FERPA, Title IX, and the Clery Act as they pertain to on campus situations. Serve as a mandatory reporter and be trained in Title IX policy. Serve as first-level contact for parents regarding student housing needs and resident concerns Coordinate room changes and consolidation throughout the year Assist residents with approved ADA accommodations based on need Maintain residential area budget Establish Resident Assistant On Call schedule by ensuring staff availability for evenings, nights, and weekends Advise the Residence Hall Association Serve as coordinator for all Resident Assistant hiring and training Hire, train, and supervisor Lion\u2019s Den desk workers Other Job Duties and Responsibilities: Adhere to the University of Arkansas \u2013 Fort Smith Employee Handbook Requires consistent on-time attendance Responsible for maintaining a positive work atmosphere by acting and communicating in a manner to foster teamwork and to provide leadership to subordinates. Identify student rooms to serve as tour rooms for Admissions and ensure those rooms are ready when needed Attend all University trainings, as required Take part in university and/or departmental committees as required by the department of Student Affairs or for professional development Assist in development and implementation of campus emergency and crisis management procedures, programs, and services Maintain confidentiality of all student information Review and create reports on an as-needed basis Other duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: To perform the job successfully, the following competencies are required for the essential functions of this position: Conflict resolution Knowledge of university structures and governance Budget projections and management Communicate well with very diverse constituents Teaching and facilitating with individuals and groups Ability to apply conduct regulations fairly and consistently Ability to identify and draw on resources across campus Skills in conceiving, designing, and implementing educational programming Knowledge of laws and procedures related to university housing Ability to balance and respect individual rights and community rights Knowledge of learning processes and commitment to foster student learning Adaptability \u2013 adapts to changes in the work environment, manages competing demands and is able to deal with frequent change, delays or unexpected events. Dependability \u2013 is consistently at work and on time, follows instructions, responds to management direction and solicits feedback to improve performance. Knowledge of the principles of computer operations to understand the college\u2019s information systems and services which carry out accounting, budgeting, purchasing, human resources, enrollment, and other or similar centralized institution-wide management information functions.\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Additional Information: Working Relationships: Work in a dynamic team of diverse faculty, staff, and students in a fast paced, growth-oriented environment. Frequent contact with vendors, personnel from other agencies and institutions and the general public, student employees, resident assistants, professional staff in student affairs, housing and residential life professional staff, custodial and grounds workers, maintenance workers, faculty, parents, student residents.\u00a0\u00a0 List Employees Supervised: Fourteen Resident Assistants (RAs) and all Lion\u2019s Den Desk Workers (2). Special Job Dimensions: Modest travel required for professional development and accompanying student groups; modest physical demands and stamina needed in working with resident assistants, programming materials, move-ins, on call, etc.; Required abilities include walking, standing, and sitting for extended periods. Visual demands include close, relatively detailed vision when focusing on a computer screen; hours are traditional office hours with evening meetings and programs and on call responsibilities in the overnight, weekends, and holidays; live-in is required. Background Check Requirements. Criminal Background Check, Financial Background Check, and Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) Check ; Position requires employee complete Arkansas Mandated Reporter training prior to employment. This job description is not designed to contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties, and/or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time with or without notice. Salary Information: $37,745.05 plus additional benefits: Furnished apartment to include utilities, wired and wireless internet, reserved parking space, unlimited meal plan, $1,000 in Lion's Cash Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume, Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Full consideration will be given to applications received by July 16, 2026. Recruitment Contact Information: HR 479-788-7080 All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position may be subject to a pre-employment criminal background check, sex offender registry check, financial history background check, and/or drug screening. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication and/or adverse financial history alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background checks and drug screening information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAPBFACILITIESFacilities-Management/Institutional-Services-Asst_R0087076": {"title": "Institutional Services Asst", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-09\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Skilled Labor Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff The University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff is an 1890 Land-Grant HBCU with a diverse student population, competitive degree offerings and stellar faculty. For more than 140 years, the University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff has worked to create an environment that inculcates learning, growth and productivity while affording a basic need to its students \u2013 a chance to advance. The 15:1 student to teacher ratio makes it possible to maintain a learning environment with close interaction between students and faculty while challenging curricula encourage our students to seek and fulfill their potential. You can excel in your chosen field of study through a curriculum of \u00a0 Certificate and Associates degree programs,\u00a0 more than thirty\u00a0 Undergraduate programs, Master\u2019s degree programs and a Doctorate program in Aquaculture/Fisheries. You can also develop workplace readiness through internships, co-ops and fellowships in the U.S. and abroad. Out-of-class experiences and student involvement include more than 90 student organizations, an internationally renowned Vesper Choir, Marching Band, Concert Bands, Wind Symphony, nationally recognized debate team, award-winning theater department and accomplished athletic program. Though the main campus is in Pine Bluff, its reach is worldwide. UAPB has an extended campus in North Little Rock and offers as well as online courses. With the addition of the Arkansas Research and Education Optical Network (ARE-ON), students can engage in information exchange with others anywhere in the world. There are also Research and Extension offices in Lonoke, Newport and Lake Village and collaborations with other colleges and universities in the State through the National Science Foundation funded STEM (Science, Technology, Engineering and Mathematics) Academy. As the second oldest land-grant institution in the state of Arkansas, the mission of this No Excuse University remains the same \u2013 to provide a high quality, affordable education with a personal touch. We invite you to Become a Part of the Pride at the University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process and require reasonable accommodations, please contact Human Resources at 870.575.8400 . Department: Custodial Services Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Job Profile Summary The Institutional Services Assistant is responsible for general cleaning of areas in and around office buildings, class rooms, lecture halls, conference rooms, auditoriums, resident halls, dining areas, building common areas, and other areas as required. Qualifications: MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS: The formal education equivalent of a high school diploma. Must have knowledge of basic techniques and cleaning equipment operation and maintenance; ability to follow instructions and perform repetitive manual work; ability to use cleansers and other agents to clean floors and furniture; ability to work independently without close supervision and to follow oral and or written instructions; ability to perform multiple tasks and prioritize assignments; and the ability to lift up to 50 lbs. Additional Information: Salary Information: 23,168.00 - 35,568.00 USD Annual Required Documents to Apply: List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Proof of Veteran Status, Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants (Please upload all required documents in the \"Resume\" attachment section of your application to be considered for this position) : Recruitment Contact Information: Sharron Williams, Employment Manager 870-575-8403 All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: The University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff may conduct pre-employment background checks on certain positions for applicants being considered for employment. \u00a0 The background checks may include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. \u00a0 Required checks are identified in the position listing. \u00a0 A criminal background check or arrest pending adjudication information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absences of a relationship to the requirements of the position. \u00a0 Background check information will be used in a consistent, non-discriminatory manner consistent with the state and federal law. \u00a0 The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAPBFACILITIESFacilities-Management/Shipping-and-Receiving-Clerk-1_R0087072": {"title": "Shipping and Receiving Clerk-1", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-09\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Procurement, Inventory Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff The University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff is an 1890 Land-Grant HBCU with a diverse student population, competitive degree offerings and stellar faculty. For more than 140 years, the University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff has worked to create an environment that inculcates learning, growth and productivity while affording a basic need to its students \u2013 a chance to advance. The 15:1 student to teacher ratio makes it possible to maintain a learning environment with close interaction between students and faculty while challenging curricula encourage our students to seek and fulfill their potential. You can excel in your chosen field of study through a curriculum of \u00a0 Certificate and Associates degree programs,\u00a0 more than thirty\u00a0 Undergraduate programs, Master\u2019s degree programs and a Doctorate program in Aquaculture/Fisheries. You can also develop workplace readiness through internships, co-ops and fellowships in the U.S. and abroad. Out-of-class experiences and student involvement include more than 90 student organizations, an internationally renowned Vesper Choir, Marching Band, Concert Bands, Wind Symphony, nationally recognized debate team, award-winning theater department and accomplished athletic program. Though the main campus is in Pine Bluff, its reach is worldwide. UAPB has an extended campus in North Little Rock and offers as well as online courses. With the addition of the Arkansas Research and Education Optical Network (ARE-ON), students can engage in information exchange with others anywhere in the world. There are also Research and Extension offices in Lonoke, Newport and Lake Village and collaborations with other colleges and universities in the State through the National Science Foundation funded STEM (Science, Technology, Engineering and Mathematics) Academy. As the second oldest land-grant institution in the state of Arkansas, the mission of this No Excuse University remains the same \u2013 to provide a high quality, affordable education with a personal touch. We invite you to Become a Part of the Pride at the University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process and require reasonable accommodations, please contact Human Resources at 870.575.8400 . Department: Central Receiving & Stores Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Shipping and Receiving Clerk is responsible for maintaining inventory control of incoming and outgoing supplies and materials. Shipping and receiving clerk is also responsible for organizing, sorting and transferring goods from one location to another. Monitor packages from the start to finish, ensuring proper techniques are carried out. May operate lift truck or use hand truck to move, convey or hoist shipments from shipping platform to other locations. Unloads trucks and delivery receivables. Maintains an accurate log of daily moves along with scanning inventory and counting accurately. Provides additional backup support for shipping and receiving department. This position is governed by state and federal laws and agency policy. Qualifications: Must be able to pull, push, lift a minimum of 30 pounds, strong sense of time organization and urgency, able to work independently and within a team. Must have valid Arkansas driver\u2019s license, high school diploma or equivalent. Additional Information: Salary Information: 23,227.00 - 38,471.00 USD Annual Required Documents to Apply: List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Proof of Veteran Status, Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants (Please upload all required documents in the \"Resume\" attachment section of your application to be considered for this position) : Recruitment Contact Information: Tina L. Parks Admin III (870) 575-8832 All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: The University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff may conduct pre-employment background checks on certain positions for applicants being considered for employment. \u00a0 The background checks may include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. \u00a0 Required checks are identified in the position listing. \u00a0 A criminal background check or arrest pending adjudication information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absences of a relationship to the requirements of the position. \u00a0 Background check information will be used in a consistent, non-discriminatory manner consistent with the state and federal law. \u00a0 The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Sitting Frequent Physical Activity: Driving, Kneeling, Lifting, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Standing, Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Pulling Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAFS--University-of-Arkansas-Fort-Smith/Adjunct-Faculty_R0087775": {"title": "Adjunct Faculty", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-09\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Faculty - Non-Tenure Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Less than Annual Appointment (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Fort Smith University of Arkansas \u2013 Fort Smith The University of Arkansas - Fort Smith is a dynamic, mid-sized public university that\u2019s redefining higher education. We\u2019re on a mission to provide transformative, hands-on learning experiences for students of all backgrounds and aspirations. Our multi-faceted approach to education offers a wealth of opportunities, with over 70 academic programs, including certificates, associate, bachelor\u2019s, and master\u2019s degrees. We\u2019re committed to building a diverse community that mirrors Arkansas\u2019s rich tapestry, reflecting our dedication to serving the state\u2019s varied population while enhancing the quality of our institution. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life, and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10 percent of employee salary. \u00a0 Fort Smith, Arkansas Nestled along the Arkansas River, this vibrant city offers a perfect blend of history, culture, and natural beauty. Immerse yourself in the rich heritage of the Old West at the Fort Smith National Historic Site, explore the eclectic local art scene, or take a scenic stroll along the picturesque riverfront trails. With a welcoming community, diverse dining options, and a thriving downtown, Fort Smith is the ideal destination for history enthusiasts and those seeking modern amenities. Thank you for your interest in joining our university. Below you will find details for the position including any supplementary documentation and/or questions you should review before submitting your application. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at (479) 788-7080. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 479-788-7080. Applicants are required to submit a request for each position to which they have applied. Department: Center for Economic Development Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Adjunct instructors may teach non-credit workforce, technical, business, leadership, and professional development courses offered through the Center for Economic Development. Instructional areas may include, but are not limited to, industrial technology, advanced manufacturing, industrial maintenance, PLCs, robotics, electrical systems, mechanical systems, hydraulics and pneumatics, welding, machining, OSHA/safety, Lean manufacturing, continuous improvement, leadership, supervision, communication, project management, entrepreneurship, and customized training for business and industry. This is a pool position. Applicants will be contacted as positions become available. The position reports to the Associate Vice Chancellor for Economic and Workforce Development who assigns responsibilities regarding student needs and course outcomes. Qualifications: Required Education and/or Work Experience: Qualifications of instructors teaching in the classroom for both lower and/or upper-level courses leading to an associate or bachelor\u2019s degree requires a master\u2019s degree in the discipline or related field with a minimum of 18 graduate credits in the subject area. Courses leading to a master\u2019s require a doctorate degree. Adjunct faculty with a clinical assignment must be prepared at the level required by accreditation. Instructors in occupational and technical areas are generally required to have a minimum of an associate\u2019s degree and related work experience. Other job-related education and/or experience may be substituted for part of these requirements. Preferred Education and/or Work Experience: Prior teaching experience. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: To perform the job successfully, the following competencies are required for the essential functions of this position: \u00b7 Current knowledge of the relevant discipline. \u00b7 Good organizational skills and timeliness in responding to student inquiries. \u00b7 Ability to respond to needs of learners from a variety of educational backgrounds in a multicultural environment. \u00b7 Ability to deliver course outcomes and content through a variety of teaching/learning styles. \u00b7 Ability to use technology effectively in teaching. \u00b7 Ability to communicate effectively both orally and in writing. \u00b7 Ability to establish and maintain effective interpersonal relationships with students and colleagues. This is a pool position. Applicants will be contacted as positions become available. Job Responsibilities \u00b7 Classroom and online instruction \u00b7 Assess and evaluate student learning \u00b7 Responsible for maintaining a positive work atmosphere by acting and communicating in a manner to foster teamwork and by providing leadership to subordinates. \u00b7 Requires consistent on-time attendance. \u00b7 Other duties as assigned. Additional Information: Working Relationships: Work with a dynamic team of faculty, staff, and students in a fast-paced, growth-oriented environment. May possibly have contact with vendors, personnel from other agencies and institutions, and the general public. List Employees Supervised: None Special Job Dimensions: Work performed primarily in an office setting. While performing the duties of this job, the employee regularly exhibits digital dexterity when entering data into computer. The employee frequently sits for extended periods of time, and occasionally stands and walks. Vision demands include close, relatively detailed vision when focusing on a computer screen. Employee regularly talks and hears. Employee occasionally lifts items up to 50 pounds. Routine work schedule Monday through Friday, 8:00am to 5:00pm with occasional overtime and travel required Background Check Requirements. Criminal Background Check and Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) Check. May also include a drug screen, child maltreatment check, and proof of immunizations depending upon area of study. Salary Information: Dependent upon department. Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: HR All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Motor Vehicle Reports Check This position may be subject to a pre-employment criminal background check, sex offender registry check, financial history background check, and/or drug screening. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication and/or adverse financial history alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background checks and drug screening information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Hearing Frequent Physical Activity: Talking Occasional Physical Activity: Sitting Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Magnolia/County-Extension-Agent---Family---Consumer-Science-4-H_R0088051-1": {"title": "County Extension Agent - Family & Consumer Science/4-H", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-09\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Professional Staff - Extension Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: Division of Agriculture of the University of Arkansas The University of Arkansas System Division of Agriculture is a state wide campus, with faculty based on University campuses, at Research and Extension Centers and in every Arkansas county. It consists of the Arkansas Agricultural Experiment Station (AES) and the Arkansas Cooperative Extension Service (CES), and is home to more than 1400 employees.\u00a0 The Division was established in 1959 and is headed by the Vice-President for Agriculture.\u00a0 The Division headquarters is located in Little Rock with the rest of the University of Arkansas System Administration.\u00a0 As an employer, the University of Arkansas System Division of Agriculture offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance.\u00a0 Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process and require reasonable accommodations, please contact the Division's Office of Program & Employment Compliance at compliance@uada.edu . For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-671-2219 or 479-502-9820. Department: CEA * Staff Chair * Columbia County Department's Website: https://uaex.uada.edu/ Summary of Job Duties: The County Extension Agent \u2013 Family & Consumer Science/4-H conducts practical, community-based educational programs to empower individuals, families, and communities in the area of nutrition, family well-being, health, food safety, and economic self-sufficiency. The agent works closely with a broad audience base and local volunteers to solicit support and participation within the county. \u2022 Maintains a thorough knowledge of the social, economic, and political characteristics of the county and will be an effective liaison with local community leaders, agencies and governments. Maintains an up-to-date and working knowledge of Arkansas Extension programs. \u2022 Develops and executes an annual action plan based on issues identified by the programmatic Subcommittee(s) and personal observations. Plans, delivers and teaches educational programs, demonstrations, and activities that address the needs of the county\u2019s clientele. Provides opportunities for program participation at the county, district, and state levels, while also sharing educational information with county government leaders, community organizations and stakeholders to support the overall Extension mission. \u2022 Leverages Extension specialists and research-based information to design, implement and teach educational programs in all Family and Consumer Sciences (FCS) priority areas. Responds to clientele inquiries through phone consultations, e-mails, in-person office and site visits, providing tailored researched based recommendations as required. \u2022 Serve as an advisor to the county (EHC) Extension Homemaker Club officers, board and members if an established EHC program exists in the county. Provides researched and unbiased leader training for EHC clubs. Provide support during and at county, district and state EHC activities. \u2022 Supports the county 4-H program and related activities, including FCS educational programming, training for competitive events, volunteer recruitment and development, and fundraising efforts. Contributes to program delivery at the county, district, and state levels. \u2022 Employs effective evaluation techniques to measure the impact of county FCS and 4-H programs. Compiles and communicates program results to the county advisory committee, Extension Council (if applicable), and county and state government officials on an annual basis. \u2022 Ensures compliance with civil rights requirements and maintains current knowledge of applicable rules and regulations. Promotes inclusivity by ensuring all programs are accessible to the public and maintains accurate records to demonstrate compliance. \u2022 Completes and submits required reports on a monthly basis to ensure accuracy, consistency, and accountability. \u2022 Collaborate with colleagues, partners, and stakeholders to effectively carry out and advance the Extension mission. \u2022 Establish and maintain good working relationships with Extension staff, clientele and general public. \u2022 Build a network of supporters and volunteers to assist in program delivery. \u2022 Maintains a working knowledge of researched based FCS practices and programs by attending in-service trainings offered through Arkansas Extension, professional development associations and other opportunities deemed appropriate by their supervisor. \u2022 Demonstrates knowledge of and adherence to University of Arkansas Division of Agriculture policies and procedures, ensuring alignment with institutional standards in all professional activities. \u2022 Performs additional responsibilities as assigned by the immediate supervisor or district director. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor\u2019s degree in family and consumer sciences, education, youth development, or related field of study; degree must be conferred by date of hire or Bachelor\u2019s degree with relevant work experience. Must have reliable transportation for use on the job with liability insurance in effect. Must successfully complete the standard background check which includes the Arkansas Child Abuse and Neglect Central Registry Check. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities: Knowledge in family and consumer sciences subject matter areas appropriate to the county assigned. Ability to plan and conduct programs and work with all clientele regardless of race, color, national origin, religion, gender, age, disability, marital or veteran status, genetic information, sexual preference, pregnancy, or any other legally protected status. Ability to speak and write clearly and communicate ideas effectively. Ability to work long and irregular hours and travel frequently. Additional Information: Applicants for this position are required to upload a Resume, Cover letter, transcript, and a list of three (3) references including name, phone number and email address (if available) prior to submitting the application. Once an application is submitted, the applicant will not be able to edit the application or upload additional documents. If you have technical issues uploading a document or if you have a need to provide additional documentation after submitting your application, email humanresources@uada.edu Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume, Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Carla Due, Ouachita District Director, 501-671-2036, cdue@uada.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Child Maltreatment, Criminal Background Check, Motor Vehicle Reports Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas System Division of Agriculture may conduct pre-employment background checks on certain positions for applicants being considered for employment. \u00a0 The background checks may include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. \u00a0 Required checks are identified in the position listing. \u00a0 A criminal background check or arrest pending adjudication information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absences of a relationship to the requirements of the position. \u00a0 Background check information will be used in a consistent, non-discriminatory manner consistent with the state and federal law. \u00a0 The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Driving, Feeling, Grasping, Standing, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Kneeling, Lifting, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Repetitive Motion, Sitting Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Murfreesboro/County-Extension-Agent---Family---Consumer-Science_R0088049-1": {"title": "County Extension Agent - Family & Consumer Science", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-09\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Professional Staff - Extension Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: Division of Agriculture of the University of Arkansas The University of Arkansas System Division of Agriculture is a state wide campus, with faculty based on University campuses, at Research and Extension Centers and in every Arkansas county. It consists of the Arkansas Agricultural Experiment Station (AES) and the Arkansas Cooperative Extension Service (CES), and is home to more than 1400 employees.\u00a0 The Division was established in 1959 and is headed by the Vice-President for Agriculture.\u00a0 The Division headquarters is located in Little Rock with the rest of the University of Arkansas System Administration.\u00a0 As an employer, the University of Arkansas System Division of Agriculture offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance.\u00a0 Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process and require reasonable accommodations, please contact the Division's Office of Program & Employment Compliance at compliance@uada.edu . For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-671-2219 or 479-502-9820. Department: District Director * Ouachita (Carla Due, Kris Boulton) Department's Website: https://www.uaex.uada.edu/ Summary of Job Duties: The County Extension Agent \u2013 Family & Consumer Science conducts practical, community-based educational programs to empower individuals, families, and communities in the area of nutrition, family well-being, health, food safety, and economic self-sufficiency. The agent works closely with a broad audience base and local volunteers to solicit support and participation within the county. Job Responsibilities: \u2022 Maintains a thorough knowledge of the social, economic, and political characteristics of the county and will be an effective liaison with local community leaders, agencies and governments. Maintains an up-to-date and working knowledge of Arkansas Extension programs. \u2022 Develops and executes an annual action plan based on issues identified by the programmatic Subcommittee(s) and personal observations. Plans, delivers and teaches educational programs, demonstrations, and activities that address the needs of the county\u2019s clientele. Provides opportunities for program participation at the county, district, and state levels, while also sharing educational information with county government leaders, community organizations and stakeholders to support the overall Extension mission. \u2022 Leverages Extension specialists and research-based information to design, implement and teach educational programs in all Family and Consumer Sciences (FCS) priority areas. Responds to clientele inquiries through phone consultations, e-mails, in-person office and site visits, providing tailored researched based recommendations as required. \u2022 Serve as an advisor to the county (EHC) Extension Homemaker Club officers, board and members if an established EHC program exists in the county. Provides researched and unbiased leader training for EHC clubs. Provide support during and at county, district and state EHC activities. \u2022 Supports the county 4-H program and related activities, including FCS educational programming, training for competitive events, volunteer recruitment and development, and fundraising efforts. Contributes to program delivery at the county, district, and state levels. \u2022 Employs effective evaluation techniques to measure the impact of county FCS and 4-H programs. Compiles and communicates program results to the county advisory committee, Extension Council (if applicable), and county and state government officials on an annual basis. \u2022 Ensures compliance with civil rights requirements and maintains current knowledge of applicable rules and regulations. Promotes inclusivity by ensuring all programs are accessible to the public and maintains accurate records to demonstrate compliance. \u2022 Completes and submits required reports on a monthly basis to ensure accuracy, consistency, and accountability. \u2022 Collaborate with colleagues, partners, and stakeholders to effectively carry out and advance the Extension mission. \u2022 Establish and maintain good working relationships with Extension staff, clientele and general public. \u2022 Build a network of supporters and volunteers to assist in program delivery. \u2022 Maintains a working knowledge of researched based FCS practices and programs by attending in-service trainings offered through Arkansas Extension, professional development associations and other opportunities deemed appropriate by their supervisor. \u2022 Demonstrates knowledge of and adherence to University of Arkansas Division of Agriculture policies and procedures, ensuring alignment with institutional standards in all professional activities. \u2022 Performs additional responsibilities as assigned by the immediate supervisor or district director. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications Bachelor\u2019s degree in family and consumer sciences, education, youth development, or related field of study; degree must be conferred by date of hire or Bachelor\u2019s degree with relevant work experience. Must have reliable transportation for use on the job with liability insurance in effect. Must successfully complete the standard background check which includes the Arkansas Child Abuse and Neglect Central Registry Check. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Knowledge in family and consumer sciences subject matter areas appropriate to the county assigned. Ability to plan and conduct programs and work with all clientele regardless of race, color, national origin, religion, gender, age, disability, marital or veteran status, genetic information, sexual preference, pregnancy, or any other legally protected status. Ability to speak and write clearly and communicate ideas effectively. Ability to work long and irregular hours and travel frequently. Additional Information: Applicants for this position are required to upload a Resume, Cover letter, transcript, and a list of three (3) references including name, phone number and email address (if available) prior to submitting the application. Once an application is submitted, the applicant will not be able to edit the application or upload additional documents. If you have technical issues uploading a document or if you have a need to provide additional documentation after submitting your application, email humanresources@uada.edu Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume, Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Carla Due, Ouachita District Director, 501-671-2036, cdue@uada.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Child Maltreatment, Criminal Background Check, Motor Vehicle Reports Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas System Division of Agriculture may conduct pre-employment background checks on certain positions for applicants being considered for employment. \u00a0 The background checks may include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. \u00a0 Required checks are identified in the position listing. \u00a0 A criminal background check or arrest pending adjudication information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absences of a relationship to the requirements of the position. \u00a0 Background check information will be used in a consistent, non-discriminatory manner consistent with the state and federal law. \u00a0 The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Driving, Feeling, Grasping, Standing, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Kneeling, Lifting, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Repetitive Motion, Sitting Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAPBFACILITIESFacilities-Management/Maintenance-Assistant_R0087092-1": {"title": "Maintenance Assistant", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-08\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Skilled Labor Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff The University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff is an 1890 Land-Grant HBCU with a diverse student population, competitive degree offerings and stellar faculty. For more than 140 years, the University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff has worked to create an environment that inculcates learning, growth and productivity while affording a basic need to its students \u2013 a chance to advance. The 15:1 student to teacher ratio makes it possible to maintain a learning environment with close interaction between students and faculty while challenging curricula encourage our students to seek and fulfill their potential. You can excel in your chosen field of study through a curriculum of \u00a0 Certificate and Associates degree programs,\u00a0 more than thirty\u00a0 Undergraduate programs, Master\u2019s degree programs and a Doctorate program in Aquaculture/Fisheries. You can also develop workplace readiness through internships, co-ops and fellowships in the U.S. and abroad. Out-of-class experiences and student involvement include more than 90 student organizations, an internationally renowned Vesper Choir, Marching Band, Concert Bands, Wind Symphony, nationally recognized debate team, award-winning theater department and accomplished athletic program. Though the main campus is in Pine Bluff, its reach is worldwide. UAPB has an extended campus in North Little Rock and offers as well as online courses. With the addition of the Arkansas Research and Education Optical Network (ARE-ON), students can engage in information exchange with others anywhere in the world. There are also Research and Extension offices in Lonoke, Newport and Lake Village and collaborations with other colleges and universities in the State through the National Science Foundation funded STEM (Science, Technology, Engineering and Mathematics) Academy. As the second oldest land-grant institution in the state of Arkansas, the mission of this No Excuse University remains the same \u2013 to provide a high quality, affordable education with a personal touch. We invite you to Become a Part of the Pride at the University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process and require reasonable accommodations, please contact Human Resources at 870.575.8400 . Department: Building and Grounds Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Maintenance Assistant is responsible for grounds maintenance and general labor activities. This position is governed by state and federal laws and agency/institution policy. The maintenance assistant performs grounds maintenance by mowing, edging, weeding, and trimming lawns and bushes, planting trees, and sodding yards. Collects and removes trash from lawn. Operates light to medium lawn equipment. Assists with work orders for special events and exhibits. Inspects tools and equipment. Performs minor equipment and vehicle repairs. Maintains equipment by oiling, greasing, sharpening blades, and performing other minor repairs and services vehicles which includes: filling with gas, changing oil, tune-ups, and washing. Assists with minor electrical repairs, remodeling of buildings, and performs minor carpentry duties such as fence repair, installing signs, and other carpentry duties Qualifications: Qualifications:\u00a0 Completion of sufficient education or training to read and write; plus two years of experience/on-the-job training, performing grounds keeping and/or the maintenance of lawn-care equipment.\u00a0\u00a0 Must have knowledge of methods and practices in skilled and unskilled trades.\u00a0 Must have ability to operate and perform routine maintenance on various types of grounds keeping tools and equipment and ability to receive, assign, and coordinate work activities. Additional Information: Salary Information: 22,880.00 - 51,129.00 USD Annual Required Documents to Apply: List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Proof of Veteran Status, Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants (Please upload all required documents in the \"Resume\" attachment section of your application to be considered for this position) : Recruitment Contact Information: Tina L. Parks Admin III (870) 575-8832 All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: The University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff may conduct pre-employment background checks on certain positions for applicants being considered for employment. \u00a0 The background checks may include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. \u00a0 Required checks are identified in the position listing. \u00a0 A criminal background check or arrest pending adjudication information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absences of a relationship to the requirements of the position. \u00a0 Background check information will be used in a consistent, non-discriminatory manner consistent with the state and federal law. \u00a0 The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-Arkansas-at-Pine-Bluff/Extra-Help-Skilled-Tradesman---2_R0088150": {"title": "Extra Help Skilled Tradesman - 2", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-08\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Skilled Labor Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff The University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff is an 1890 Land-Grant HBCU with a diverse student population, competitive degree offerings and stellar faculty. For more than 140 years, the University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff has worked to create an environment that inculcates learning, growth and productivity while affording a basic need to its students \u2013 a chance to advance. The 15:1 student to teacher ratio makes it possible to maintain a learning environment with close interaction between students and faculty while challenging curricula encourage our students to seek and fulfill their potential. You can excel in your chosen field of study through a curriculum of \u00a0 Certificate and Associates degree programs,\u00a0 more than thirty\u00a0 Undergraduate programs, Master\u2019s degree programs and a Doctorate program in Aquaculture/Fisheries. You can also develop workplace readiness through internships, co-ops and fellowships in the U.S. and abroad. Out-of-class experiences and student involvement include more than 90 student organizations, an internationally renowned Vesper Choir, Marching Band, Concert Bands, Wind Symphony, nationally recognized debate team, award-winning theater department and accomplished athletic program. Though the main campus is in Pine Bluff, its reach is worldwide. UAPB has an extended campus in North Little Rock and offers as well as online courses. With the addition of the Arkansas Research and Education Optical Network (ARE-ON), students can engage in information exchange with others anywhere in the world. There are also Research and Extension offices in Lonoke, Newport and Lake Village and collaborations with other colleges and universities in the State through the National Science Foundation funded STEM (Science, Technology, Engineering and Mathematics) Academy. As the second oldest land-grant institution in the state of Arkansas, the mission of this No Excuse University remains the same \u2013 to provide a high quality, affordable education with a personal touch. We invite you to Become a Part of the Pride at the University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process and require reasonable accommodations, please contact Human Resources at 870.575.8400 . Department: Agriculture, Fisheries & Human Science Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Performs skilled maintenance and repair of HVAC and plumbing systems Installs, inspects, and services mechanical, piping, and ventilation systems Troubleshoots system malfunctions and performs corrective maintenance Reads and interprets blueprints and technical manuals Ensures compliance with state building codes and safety regulations May assist in other trades (electrical, carpentry) as needed Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications (State-Consistent): High school diploma or GED Formal technical training OR equivalent work experience Knowledge of HVAC, refrigeration, and plumbing systems Ability to operate tools and diagnostic equipment Preferred Enhancements (UAPB-Specific): EPA Section 608 Certification Arkansas Plumbing License Experience in higher education or large institutional facilities Additional Information: Salary Information: $20 - $24 Required Documents to Apply: List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants (Please upload all required documents in the \"Resume\" attachment section of your application to be considered for this position) : Recruitment Contact Information: Sharron Williams All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Motor Vehicle Reports Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff may conduct pre-employment background checks on certain positions for applicants being considered for employment. \u00a0 The background checks may include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. \u00a0 Required checks are identified in the position listing. \u00a0 A criminal background check or arrest pending adjudication information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absences of a relationship to the requirements of the position. \u00a0 Background check information will be used in a consistent, non-discriminatory manner consistent with the state and federal law. \u00a0 The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/RN-Emergency-Department-Night-Shift_R0058136": {"title": "RN Emergency Department Night Shift", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-08\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/08/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Night Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | EMSL Nursing OP C Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Schedule: Fulltime This position will be utilized to fill multiple positions The Registered Nurse provides direct patient care to assigned patients in the Emergency Department and Trauma Center.\u00a0 UAMS provides emergency care to greater than 55,000 patients per year. Medical and nursing coverage is delivered by faculty, residents, registered nurses and technicians from the Emergency Medicine Service Line. \u00a0Educational opportunities exist to obtain ACLS, PALS, and TNCC certifications as well as instructor certifications in these courses. The Emergency Department aims to achieve 100% of nursing staff to become Certified Emergency Nurses (CEN) through the Emergency Nurses Association. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Graduate of an accredited Nursing Program with Associates Degree, Nursing Diploma, Bachelors in Nursing, or Master's in Nursing.\u00a0 Valid RN License, 1 year of Registered Nursing experience, excellent communication skills, basic computer skills, strong work ethics and accountability. BLS, ACLS, TNCC. PALS within 6 months of hire. \u00a0 Preferred Qualifications: 2 years or more nursing experience with current BLS, CEN or TCRN. Additional Information: Additional Information: Collects and documents assessment data. Develops a Plan of Care (POC) per standard. Implements POC including medical order and interdisciplinary approach.\u00a0 Evaluates the progress of patient toward attainment of desired outcomes.\u00a0 Provides effective patient/family education/discharge planning.\u00a0 Administers medication per standard including drug information to patients/families.\u00a0 Acts as a resource/supports others.\u00a0 Delivers patient care using the principles of the defined nursing modality.\u00a0 Delegates care based on UAMS standards, legal and regulatory requirements, specific job description and individual level of education and training.\u00a0 Contributes to a positive work environment that is conducive to clinical education while serving as a resource for student nurses and staff. Registered Nurse delivers nursing care for patients in within the limits of the Nurse Practice Act of the State of Arkansas and adheres to institutional policies, procedures and standards. \u00a0 The\u00a0RN is responsible to adhere to the standard of care defined by UAMS, ANA, and Standards for specialty patient population with support and mentoring by other team members.\u00a0 Employees in this role must be fitted for, capable of donning and performing routine tasks in personal protective equipment to include N95 masks, Powered Air Purifying Respirators (PAPR) or Controlled Air Purifying Respirators (CAPR). Constant Physical Activity : Hear, Read, Concentrate, Think Analytically, Frequent Physical Activity : Stand Occasional Physical Activity : Bend, sit, crawl, crouch, kneel, stoop or reach overhead Lift/Carry Weight: 11 - 25 Lbs. or more Push/Pull Weight: 100 Lbs. or more Physical Environment : Inside medical Facility Noise Level: Moderate Visual Requirements: Color discrimination, Depth perception, Far visual acuity Near visual acuity Hazards : Biological, Dust, Fumes/Gases/Odors, Radiation, Sharp objects/tools #UAMSNurses Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAMS/Clinic-Assistant-Instructor_R0088088-1": {"title": "Clinic Assistant Instructor", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-07\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/08/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: CON | College of Nursing DNP Programs Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) College of Nursing (CON) is seeking a dedicated and experienced Clinic Instructor to provide teaching support for the Fall semester. The Clinic Instructor will deliver course content, engage students in meaningful learning experiences, and support academic instruction as assigned by the department. Responsibilities may include classroom, laboratory, simulation, and/or clinical teaching, student evaluation, and collaboration with faculty to support program objectives. The Clinic Instructor will contribute to the educational mission of the department by promoting student success and maintaining excellence in teaching and professional practice. Qualifications: \u00a0Ba chelor of Science in Nursing (BSN) \u00a0 Additional Information: Responsibilities: Deliver assigned course content for the fall semester in alignment with curriculum standards \u00a0 Prepare and present lectures, instructional materials, and learning activities \u00a0 Facilitate classroom and/or clinical instruction as applicable \u00a0 Evaluate student performance and provide\u00a0 timely \u00a0feedback \u00a0 Maintain\u00a0 accurate \u00a0records of attendance, grades, and student progress \u00a0 Support student engagement and promote a positive learning environment \u00a0 Collaborate with faculty and department leadership on course delivery \u00a0 Adhere to university policies, procedures, and academic standards \u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: \u00a0 Hearing, Standing, Talking \u00a0 Frequent Physical Activity: \u00a0 Feeling, Sitting, Walking \u00a0 Occasional Physical Activity: \u00a0 Driving, Pulling, Pushing \u00a0 \u00a0 Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Curriculum Vitae, Resume, Writing Sample Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAMS/Early-Childhood-Development-Specialist--Mountain-View-_R0085656-1": {"title": "Early Childhood Development Specialist (Mountain View)", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-07\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/05/2026 Type of Position: Clinical Staff - Medical Ancillary Support Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: COM | Peds Kids First Mountain View Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: This position is in Mountain View, AR We\u2019re looking for an Early Childhood Development Specialist (ECDS) to join our Kids First team in Mountain View, AR. Kids First is dynamic and growing organization that is committed to providing the best possible care and developmental intervention for young children. Our ideal candidate is someone who is passionate about working with children and families, is knowledgeable about early childhood development, and is committed to providing high-quality, individualized care to young children with special healthcare needs. Qualifications: Bachelor's degree plus at least one of the following: \u00a01) Early Childhood or Early Childhood Special Education Certificate, 2) A Child Development Associate Certificate, 3) Birth to Pre-K Credential WITH documentation that 12 hours of experience working with children with special needs and 12 hours of coursework in early childhood, child development, special education, elementary education, or child and family studies PLUS six (6) months documented experience working with children. \u00a0 Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Excellent communication, organization, and interpersonal skills Ability to work independently and as a team Ability to administer standardized developmental testing instruments Ability to build relationships with children, parents, and colleagues \u00a0\u00a0 Knowledge of developmental milestones in the birth-five population Additional Information: Responsibilities: Ensures quality of individualized developmental services provided at KIDS FIRST. Supports the academic mission of the Kids First program. Demonstrates professionalism, continued development of skills, and job related interest and concern. Other duties assigned. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Adult Maltreatment, Child Maltreatment, Criminal Background Check, FBI Background Check, Sex Offender Registry This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Hearing Frequent Physical Activity: Crawling, Crouching, Feeling, Kneeling, Standing, Stooping, Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Sitting Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Extra-Help-Trojan-Works-Graphic-Designer-Assistant_R0087543-1": {"title": "Extra Help/Trojan Works Graphic Designer Assistant", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-06\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Clerical Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Little Rock The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is a metropolitan research university that provides an accessible, quality education through flexible learning and unparalleled internship opportunities. At UA Little Rock, we prepare our more than 8,900 students to be innovators and responsible leaders in their fields. Committed to its metropolitan research university mission, UA Little Rock is a driving force in Little Rock's thriving cultural community and a major component of the city and state's growing profile as a regional leader in research, technology transfer, economic development, and job creation. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . Department: Trojan Works Program Department's Website: ualr.edu/trojanworks ualr.edu/communications Summary of Job Duties: Trojan Works Student Workers serve in various roles across campus as Institutional Work-Study (IWS) student workers. Specific duties are designated by the department hiring manager to include but are not limited to customer service, answering phones, and clerical work. This position is governed by state and federal laws, and agency/institution policy. Qualifications: Required Education and/or Experience: Degree-seeking UA Little Rock students enrolled in classes at the time of application; Eligible to legally work 20 hours per week in the United States; The formal education equivalent of a high school diploma\u00a0; Must be ineligible for Federal Work-Study (FWS); Required to major in Graphic Design at UA Little Rock; Have taken classes: Intro to Visual Arts, 3D Design, and Comp II Job Duties and Responsibilities: Marq templates; Logos work; Training in Adobe suite programs; Help assist our photographer on photoshoots; Grab photos of events for social media/story posts; Create plasma screens and marquee slides; Other duties as assigned to assist employees in the Office of Communications and Marketing; Have basic knowledge of design; Staff the Communications and Marketing front desk. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Understanding of Microsoft Word; Have a passion for design; Be creative; Be organized; Complete projects in a timely manner; Ability to work up to 20 hours per week, concentrated M-F during regular business hours, with the potential for some nights and weekends to cover special events; Staff the Communications and Marketing front desk; Able to follow directions & take critique. Additional Information: Cover letter/letter of application is required for consideration. Salary Information: $11.00 per hour Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Optional Documents: List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Special Instructions to Applicants: Cover letter/letter of application required for consideration. Recruitment Contact Information: Nancy Mallett Hyde, Trojan Works Coordinator, trojanworks@ualr.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: No Background Check Required The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding Frequent Physical Activity: Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Lifting, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Sitting, Standing, Walking Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Extra-Help-Trojan-Works-Trojan-Forge-Attendant_R0087598-1": {"title": "Extra Help/Trojan Works Trojan Forge Attendant", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-06\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Staff - Clerical Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Shift Vary (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Little Rock The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is a metropolitan research university that provides an accessible, quality education through flexible learning and unparalleled internship opportunities. At UA Little Rock, we prepare our more than 8,900 students to be innovators and responsible leaders in their fields. Committed to its metropolitan research university mission, UA Little Rock is a driving force in Little Rock's thriving cultural community and a major component of the city and state's growing profile as a regional leader in research, technology transfer, economic development, and job creation. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . Department: Trojan Works Program Department's Website: ualr.edu/trojanworks Summary of Job Duties: Extra Help/Trojan Works Student Workers serve in various roles across campus as Institutional Work-Study (IWS) student workers. Specific duties are designated by the department hiring manager to include but are not limited to customer service, answering phones, and clerical work. This position is governed by state and federal laws, and agency/institution policy. This position is a provisional appointment with UA Little Rock and is funded through a grant or contract. Annual position renewal is contingent upon continued grant funding and satisfactory job performance. The Trojan Works/Trojan Forge Attendant is an hourly extra help assistant position available for students who do not qualify for Federal Work Study. It will serve as a front-line customer service representative and technical support to the Trojan Forge, including managing student reservations, managing physical supplies/inventory, and assisting in the coordination of assigned office activities. The incumbent will work with students utilizing the Trojan Forge\u2019s resources. This position will manage inventory, equipment, scheduling reservations, community engagement, usage data, and other clerical duties as assigned. This position reports directly to the Director of Academic Affairs Retention Office. This position is governed by state and federal laws and agency/institution policy. Qualifications: Required Education and/or Experience Degree-seeking UA Little Rock students enrolled in classes at the time of application; Eligible to legally work 20 hours per week in the United States; Flexible availability M-F 9am to 5pm; Must be ineligible for Federal Work-Study (FWS). Maintain good standing with the UA Little Rock Job Duties and Responsibilities Provide assistance and clarification to potential students, current students, graduates, and/or program affiliates; Answer incoming calls/emails and forward them to the appropriate staff member if necessary and/or document all messages; Assist students in scheduling reservations for equipment; Assist with overall customer service departmental goals by supporting staff, faculty, students and other Forge staff when needed; Provide technical assistance to students utilizing specialized forge equipment and resources; Manage and track physical supplies and inventory levels for the Trojan Forge; Ensure all equipment is maintained, organized, and ready for student use; Maintain cleanliness of the Trojan Forge; Oversee and manage the student reservation system for forge space and equipment; Collect and report usage data; Perform general clerical duties and assist in community engagement activities; Attend and actively participate in scheduled training sessions and staff meetings; Performs other work-related duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills, & Abilities Strong Communication skills - both orally and in writing; Excellent organizational skills; Problem-solving skills; Ability to work independently when appropriate, as part of a team, and to follow instructions; Ability to prioritize and organize multiple tasks; Ability to interpret and explain instructional manuals; Ability to demonstrate patience and accuracy in resolving student concerns; Ability to develop, interpret, and apply policies and procedures; Willingness to learn how to use equipment in the Trojan Forge, including 3D Printers, sewing machines, sublimation printers, and more; \u00a0 Additional Information: Cover letter/letter of application is required for consideration for Trojan Works positions. Salary Information: $11.00 per hour Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Resume Optional Documents: List of three Professional References (name, email, business title) Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Nancy Mallett, Trojan Works Coordinator, njmallett@ualr.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: No Background Check Required The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding Frequent Physical Activity: Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Lifting, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Sitting, Standing, Walking Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Assistant-Professor---Law---9-MONTH_R0087778": {"title": "Assistant Professor - Law - 9 MONTH", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-06\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Faculty - Tenure/Tenure Track Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Academic Term (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Little Rock The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is a metropolitan research university that provides an accessible, quality education through flexible learning and unparalleled internship opportunities. At UA Little Rock, we prepare our more than 8,900 students to be innovators and responsible leaders in their fields. Committed to its metropolitan research university mission, UA Little Rock is a driving force in Little Rock's thriving cultural community and a major component of the city and state's growing profile as a regional leader in research, technology transfer, economic development, and job creation. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . Department: Bowen School of Law Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The University of Arkansas at Little Rock William H. Bowen School of Law seeks applicants for an assistant professor of the Veterans Legal Services Clinic to teach and direct one clinical program. This is a nine-month, full-time, tenure-track position. This position is governed by state and federal laws, and agency/institution policy. Qualifications: Required Education and/or Experience: J.D. from an ABA-accredited law school; Admission to the practice of law and good standing in at least one state or the District of Columbia; Admission to the Arkansas bar or capable of admission within one year of hiring; Veterans Affairs (VA) - accreditation or eligibility for accreditation and prepared to apply upon hiring; Strong writing and interpersonal skills. Preferred Education and/or Experience: Outstanding academic credentials; Prior experience in either clinical teaching of law students or supervision of other attorneys; Experience with the legal representation of veterans and/or military personnel; Interest in and efforts to develop a record as a legal scholar. Job Duties: Design and teach a rigorous clinical course, including clinic seminar, and an additional doctrinal course, as needed; Achieve teaching goals; Screen and select clients for clinic representation; Represent clients and manage clinic operations; Supervise clinical students in work on client matters; Collaborate with the director of the VLSC Pro Bono Program; Collaborate with other supervising attorneys in the Bowen legal clinic; Develop and maintain relationships with community partners; Produce high-quality legal scholarship; Support the university through internal and external service; Perform other duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Demonstrated ability to teach and practice law; Demonstrated ability to effectively communicate in person, in writing, and through electronic means of communication; Demonstrated ability to analyze and utilize data in decision making; Demonstrated ability to work with a diverse group of students; Demonstrated ability to advise students; Demonstrated ability to work as a team player and collaborate with colleagues; Excellent interpersonal, motivational, and management skills; Proficiency in using electronic case-management systems. Additional Information: Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Curriculum Vitae, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Statement of Research Philosophy, Statement of Teaching Philosophy Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Shanna Fitzgerald, Director of Finance, semorris@ualr.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Sitting, Standing Occasional Physical Activity: Walking Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAPBNLRNorth-Little-Rock/Extra-Help-Research-Assistant_R0086706": {"title": "Extra Help Research Assistant", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-06\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Research Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff The University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff is an 1890 Land-Grant HBCU with a diverse student population, competitive degree offerings and stellar faculty. For more than 140 years, the University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff has worked to create an environment that inculcates learning, growth and productivity while affording a basic need to its students \u2013 a chance to advance. The 15:1 student to teacher ratio makes it possible to maintain a learning environment with close interaction between students and faculty while challenging curricula encourage our students to seek and fulfill their potential. You can excel in your chosen field of study through a curriculum of \u00a0 Certificate and Associates degree programs,\u00a0 more than thirty\u00a0 Undergraduate programs, Master\u2019s degree programs and a Doctorate program in Aquaculture/Fisheries. You can also develop workplace readiness through internships, co-ops and fellowships in the U.S. and abroad. Out-of-class experiences and student involvement include more than 90 student organizations, an internationally renowned Vesper Choir, Marching Band, Concert Bands, Wind Symphony, nationally recognized debate team, award-winning theater department and accomplished athletic program. Though the main campus is in Pine Bluff, its reach is worldwide. UAPB has an extended campus in North Little Rock and offers as well as online courses. With the addition of the Arkansas Research and Education Optical Network (ARE-ON), students can engage in information exchange with others anywhere in the world. There are also Research and Extension offices in Lonoke, Newport and Lake Village and collaborations with other colleges and universities in the State through the National Science Foundation funded STEM (Science, Technology, Engineering and Mathematics) Academy. As the second oldest land-grant institution in the state of Arkansas, the mission of this No Excuse University remains the same \u2013 to provide a high quality, affordable education with a personal touch. We invite you to Become a Part of the Pride at the University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process and require reasonable accommodations, please contact Human Resources at 870.575.8400 . Department: Extra Help Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Research Assistant is responsible: Assisting with the planning and scheduling of demonstrations for the Food insecurity project community gardens project. \u2022 Provide leadership for the Crump Garden project in Little Rock. \u2022 Assist in maintaining demonstrations in the high tunnel at Crump garden. \u2022 Assist in the implementation of the demonstrations for the National American Association of Community Gardens Associations annual conference in June. \u2022 Collecting research data & Maintain records and documentation of the demonstrations and distribution of the vegetables to the seniors and members of the community Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications Excellent verbal and written communication skills. Ability to communicate effectively with diverse audiences and stakeholders. Additional Information: Salary Information: $20-$25 Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants (Please upload all required documents in the \"Resume\" attachment section of your application to be considered for this position) : Recruitment Contact Information: Sharron Williams All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Motor Vehicle Reports Check The University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff may conduct pre-employment background checks on certain positions for applicants being considered for employment. \u00a0 The background checks may include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. \u00a0 Required checks are identified in the position listing. \u00a0 A criminal background check or arrest pending adjudication information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absences of a relationship to the requirements of the position. \u00a0 Background check information will be used in a consistent, non-discriminatory manner consistent with the state and federal law. \u00a0 The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Assistant-Professor---STEM---9-Month_R0087139": {"title": "Assistant Professor - STEM - 9 Month", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-06\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Faculty - Tenure/Tenure Track Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Academic Term (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Little Rock The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is a metropolitan research university that provides an accessible, quality education through flexible learning and unparalleled internship opportunities. At UA Little Rock, we prepare our more than 8,900 students to be innovators and responsible leaders in their fields. Committed to its metropolitan research university mission, UA Little Rock is a driving force in Little Rock's thriving cultural community and a major component of the city and state's growing profile as a regional leader in research, technology transfer, economic development, and job creation. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . Department: Computer Science Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: UA Little Rock is seeking to hire an Assistant Professor - 9-Month. The Assistant Professor is responsible for teaching, research, and service in the School of Computer and Information Sciences. This position is governed by state and federal laws, and agency/institution policy. Qualifications: Required Education and/or Experience: Ph.D. in Computer Science or a related field from an accredited institution; At least five years of academic experience, including teaching, research, and administrative responsibilities; Proven ability to build and sustain collaborative relationships with faculty, staff, students, and external stakeholders; A track record of research, teaching, and service that aligns with the mission and goals of the school and the university. Preferred Education and/or Experience: Experience in securing research funding and fostering industry partnerships; Strong understanding of the rapidly evolving technology landscape and the future of Computer and Information Science education. Job Duties and Responsibilities: Promote an inclusive learning environment and actively work to improve student retention and graduation rates; Support academic advising efforts and student engagement with school-sponsored extracurricular activities such as clubs, hackathons, and internships; Monitor and evaluate student satisfaction with academic programs and implement strategies for continuous improvement; Assist in the development and execution of the department\u2019s strategic plan, aligning it with the broader vision of the university and college; Represent the department in university meetings, faculty councils, and other academic forums; Develop partnerships with local industries, government agencies, and other academic institutions to enhance research, internships, and employment opportunities for students. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Commitment to inclusive teaching; Ability to provide effective mentorship; Excellent communication, interpersonal, and organizational skills. Additional Information: Salary Information: $105,000.00 Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Curriculum Vitae, Statement of Research Philosophy, Statement of Teaching Philosophy Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Ahmed Halimeh, Director of the School of Computer and Information Science aaabuhalime@ualr.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting Frequent Physical Activity: Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Lifting Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Assistant-Professor---9-MONTH_R0087717": {"title": "Assistant Professor - 9 MONTH", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-02\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Faculty - Tenure/Tenure Track Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Little Rock The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is a metropolitan research university that provides an accessible, quality education through flexible learning and unparalleled internship opportunities. At UA Little Rock, we prepare our more than 8,900 students to be innovators and responsible leaders in their fields. Committed to its metropolitan research university mission, UA Little Rock is a driving force in Little Rock's thriving cultural community and a major component of the city and state's growing profile as a regional leader in research, technology transfer, economic development, and job creation. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . Department: School of Mass Communication Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Assistant Professor - 9 MONTH includes teaching primarily in the area of public relations in face-to-face, hybrid, online, and weekend formats. Faculty will be expected to work collaboratively with faculty, staff, students, and the community, teach courses as assigned, have an active research/creative work agenda, and participate in university and community service. This position is governed by state and federal laws, and agency/institution policy. Qualifications: Required Education and/or Experience: Terminal degree (PhD, EDD, JD, MFA) in public relations or a related field. ABD or AB thesis considered. Preferred Education and/or Experience: College teaching experience in public relations and/or related field; Industry experience (public relations and/or related field); Student supervisory experience;\u00a0 Research/creative activity related to the discipline and consistent with departmental focus and needs; Experience with industry-standard software and equipment; APR accreditation and PRSA membership.\u00a0\u00a0 Job Duties and/or Responsibilities: Teach undergraduate and graduate courses in face-to-face, online, and hybrid formats; Serve as faculty advisor for student organizations; Advise and mentor graduate and undergraduate students; Have an active research agenda; Participate in university and community service;\u00a0 Work collaboratively with faculty, staff, students, and the community. Collaborate to strengthen public relations program; Teach core mass communication courses;\u00a0 Other duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Knowledge of public relations; A program of research consistent with departmental focus; Ability to teach a variety of courses within our curriculum in traditional and online formats; Desire to engage in professional service activities in the community. Additional Information: Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Curriculum Vitae, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Please upload all required documents in the \"Resume\" attachment section of your application (before hitting the submit button), if you want to be considered for this position. Recruitment Contact Information: Kiel Thorlton, Chair, kthirlton@ualr.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Standing, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Sitting, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAMS---NWA/Faculty-Member--Department-of-Family-and-Preventive_R0083820-1": {"title": "Faculty Member- Department of Family and Preventive", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-02\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: COM | DFPM Community Research Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Join the Department of Family and Preventive Medicine at UAMS Family Medical Center in Northwest Arkansas as an Assistant/Associate Professor. In this dynamic role, you will deliver exceptional, evidence-based, patient-centered care while fostering a positive learning environment for residents and students. Your responsibilities will include providing high-quality patient care, mentoring residents in outpatient and inpatient settings, and contributing to continuous improvement initiatives. You will also collaborate on scholarly activities, engage in research, and uphold the mission and academic goals of the department. Additionally, you will be required to spend approximately 12 weeks in the hospital setting precepting residents. If you are passionate about advancing clinical medicine, promoting health and wellness, and shaping the next generation of healthcare providers, we invite you to bring your expertise to our team and make a difference in Northwest Arkansas! Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Medical Degree and/or PhD/DO Board Certified in Family Medicine Arkansas State Medical License DEA Knowledge, Skills, & Abilities (KSAs): Strong clinical expertise and commitment to evidence-based, patient-centered care. Proficiency in medical teaching and mentoring residents. Ability to collaborate effectively with interdisciplinary teams. Knowledge of quality metrics and performance standards. Strong communication and organizational skills. Commitment to advancing clinical medicine through education and research. Additional Information: Key Responsibilities: Patient Care: Provide coordination, continuity, and consistency in patient care. Serve as an attending physician in the hospital and precept residents in outpatient settings. Dedicate four hours weekly to private clinic time. Engage in direct patient care, medical teaching, and research collaborations. Education: Provide instruction using various methodologies, including didactic, bedside, and clinical experiences. Promote academic excellence and the health and wellness of Arkansans. Engage in clinical care and scholarly activities that advance clinical medicine. Research: Collaborate on research initiatives that promote health and wellness. Participate in scholarly activities that advance clinical medicine. Additional Duties: Serve in roles such as fellowship director, division director, service line leader, resident preceptor, or mentor. Interact professionally with diverse groups, including co-workers, management, and external stakeholders. Provide exceptional customer service and maintain strict confidentiality. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Curriculum Vitae, License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions) Optional Documents: List of five Professional References (name, email, business title), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Extra-Help-Assistant-Learning-Assistant_R0087082-2": {"title": "Extra Help Assistant/Learning Assistant", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-01\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Clerical Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Little Rock The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is a metropolitan research university that provides an accessible, quality education through flexible learning and unparalleled internship opportunities. At UA Little Rock, we prepare our more than 8,900 students to be innovators and responsible leaders in their fields. Committed to its metropolitan research university mission, UA Little Rock is a driving force in Little Rock's thriving cultural community and a major component of the city and state's growing profile as a regional leader in research, technology transfer, economic development, and job creation. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . Department: UALR | STEM Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: UA Little Rock is seeking to hire an Extra Help Assistant/Learning Assistant. Learning Assistant duties include assisting course instructors with designing, implementing, disseminating, and revising evidence-based teaching practices in their courses. This position is governed by state and federal laws, and agency/institution policy. Qualifications: Required Education and/or Experience: Some college experience. Preferred Education and/or Experience: They must have successfully completed qualifying STEM courses for which they are applying to be Learning Assistants, unless otherwise approved by the course instructor. Job Duties and Responsibilities: Assist course instructors in designing evidence-based teaching practices for the course instructors\u2019 classes; Assist course instructors in implementing evidence-based teaching practices in the course instructor\u2019s class (either in class, workshop, or lab); Meet with the course instructor at least once a week to provide feedback and plan for the next week\u2019s tasks; Guide students in the course instructor\u2019s class as they learn course material. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Ability to communicate clearly and effectively; Ability to creatively solve problems; Ability to work as part of a team; Ability to receive, apply, and provide constructive feedback. Additional Information: Salary Information: $780-$975 Required Documents to Apply: Resume, Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Dr. Michael Moore Director of Undergraduate Research and Mentoring memoore5@ualr.edu 501-916-6039 All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: No Background Check Required The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting, Standing, Stooping, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Lifting, Pulling, Pushing Occasional Physical Activity: Balancing, Climbing Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Extra-Help-Registered-Nurse_R0087523": {"title": "Extra Help/Registered Nurse", "description": "Start date: 2026-07-01\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Clerical Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Little Rock The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is a metropolitan research university that provides an accessible, quality education through flexible learning and unparalleled internship opportunities. At UA Little Rock, we prepare our more than 8,900 students to be innovators and responsible leaders in their fields. Committed to its metropolitan research university mission, UA Little Rock is a driving force in Little Rock's thriving cultural community and a major component of the city and state's growing profile as a regional leader in research, technology transfer, economic development, and job creation. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . Department: Health Services Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: This position provides the services of an Extra Help/Registered Nurse to the operations of UA Little Rock Health Services. This position is governed by state and federal laws, and agency/institution policy. Qualifications: Required Education and/or Experience Successful completion of an accredited nursing degree \u00a0 program. \u00a0 Current licensure as a Registered Nurse by the Arkansas State Board of Nursing or current multistate license from a Nurse Licensure Compact (NLC) member state; Current CPR certification. Job Duties and Responsibilities Provide triage assessments, by telephone and in person, and appropriately direct patients to urgent care, same day, future appointments, and referrals to off-site services as indicated; Urgent care, same day, future appointments, and referrals to off-site services as indicated; Administer medications & immunizations within scope of practice, as ordered by APRNs and MDs, and in accordance with the Arkansas Department of Health (ADH) and Center for Disease Control and Prevention (CDCP) recommendations and standards; Assist receptionist as needed with check-in procedures, making appointments, insurance verification, responding to patient inquiries, and answering the telephone; Provide appropriate and effective health education to patients regarding their health problems, behavioral risk assessment, interventions, and medications; Document all findings and patient care interventions accurately and legibly and according to professional and legal standards; in Medicat (Electronic Health Record); Appropriately refer patients to Advanced Practice Registered Nurses (APRNs), Physicians, and off-site services; Follow client confidentiality policies and procedures for UA Little Rock Health Services and according to HIPAA guidelines; Comply with OSHA and clinic protocols regarding infectious disease prevention and control, including proper handling and disposal of infectious waste, gloving and sharps management/disposal, and proper disinfection of exam rooms and equipment; Maintain and document proper storage of vaccines as per ADH protocols, including completion of daily temperature log for refrigerator and freezer and regular inspection of expiration dates and proper disposal of expired vaccines; Participate and contribute to the development and implementation of campus health outreach programs; Perform CLIA waived tests and collect, package, route, and track lab specimens to off-site reference laboratory as directed; Perform tuberculosis screening and follow-up; including documentation of results in the Arkansas Department of Health tuberculosis database; Participate in regular staff meetings and contribute to progress toward developing and addressing Health Services\u2019 goals and objectives; Participate and contribute to quality improvement programs for Health Services; Participate and contribute to staff in-services and educational programs; Other duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills, And Abilities Knowledge of computers and software applications (Microsoft, Internet, e-mail); Knowledge or ability to learn appropriate use of the Medicat Electronic Health Record system; Strong communication skills to provide effective education to clients and accurately relate client concerns to consulting professionals; Strong ability to work with diverse constituencies including persons with disabilities. Additional Information: Salary Information: Required Documents to Apply: Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Adult Maltreatment, Annual TB Screening, Child Maltreatment, Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry, Substance Abuse Testing The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting, Standing, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Feeling, Reaching, Repetitive Motion, Sharps Occasional Physical Activity: Kneeling, Lifting, Pulling, Pushing Benefits Eligible:"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-Arkansas-at-Pine-Bluff/Research-Associate_R0087734": {"title": "Research Associate", "description": "Start date: 2026-06-29\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Researchers Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff The University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff is an 1890 Land-Grant HBCU with a diverse student population, competitive degree offerings and stellar faculty. For more than 140 years, the University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff has worked to create an environment that inculcates learning, growth and productivity while affording a basic need to its students \u2013 a chance to advance. The 15:1 student to teacher ratio makes it possible to maintain a learning environment with close interaction between students and faculty while challenging curricula encourage our students to seek and fulfill their potential. You can excel in your chosen field of study through a curriculum of \u00a0 Certificate and Associates degree programs,\u00a0 more than thirty\u00a0 Undergraduate programs, Master\u2019s degree programs and a Doctorate program in Aquaculture/Fisheries. You can also develop workplace readiness through internships, co-ops and fellowships in the U.S. and abroad. Out-of-class experiences and student involvement include more than 90 student organizations, an internationally renowned Vesper Choir, Marching Band, Concert Bands, Wind Symphony, nationally recognized debate team, award-winning theater department and accomplished athletic program. Though the main campus is in Pine Bluff, its reach is worldwide. UAPB has an extended campus in North Little Rock and offers as well as online courses. With the addition of the Arkansas Research and Education Optical Network (ARE-ON), students can engage in information exchange with others anywhere in the world. There are also Research and Extension offices in Lonoke, Newport and Lake Village and collaborations with other colleges and universities in the State through the National Science Foundation funded STEM (Science, Technology, Engineering and Mathematics) Academy. As the second oldest land-grant institution in the state of Arkansas, the mission of this No Excuse University remains the same \u2013 to provide a high quality, affordable education with a personal touch. We invite you to Become a Part of the Pride at the University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process and require reasonable accommodations, please contact Human Resources at 870.575.8400 . Department: Center of Excellence (Aquaculture & Fisheries) Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Location: UAPB Fish Station and Research Facilities (Pine Bluff, Lonoke, and Eudora) Reports To: Director, Center of Excellence, Dept. of Aquaculture and Fisheries ________________________________________ Position Overview The Research Associate will oversee computer networking, data connectivity, and system performance across UAPB's aquaculture research facilities located in Pine Bluff, Lonoke, and Eudora. This position combines advanced IT management with artificial intelligence applications in aquaculture research. The specialist will play a key role in building and maintaining computing infrastructure, including a high-performance supercomputer, and developing AI-driven monitoring systems for aquatic species. The successful candidate will support ongoing AI-based projects focused on analyzing shrimp and fish feeding behavior, growth metrics (length, weight), health assessment, and environmental conditions, contributing directly to precision aquaculture initiatives. ________________________________________ Key Responsibilities IT Infrastructure and Networking \u2022 Manage and maintain network systems, servers, and computer workstations across UAPB, Lonoke, and Eudora facilities \u2022 Ensure seamless connectivity between research laboratories, sensors, and field monitoring stations \u2022 Troubleshoot software, hardware, and networking issues to maintain system reliability \u2022 Coordinate data flow between field stations and the main research hub for real-time monitoring and analysis AI Research and Development \u2022 Collaborate with faculty and research teams to design and deploy AI-based monitoring systems for shrimp and fish culture \u2022 Develop machine learning models for automated detection of feeding behavior, growth metrics (size, length, weight), and health indicators using imaging and sensor data \u2022 Support AI-assisted environmental monitoring and predictive modeling for aquaculture systems \u2022 Manage large datasets and assist in developing cloud and local data storage frameworks High-Performance Computing \u2022 Lead the assembly, configuration, and maintenance of a high-performance computing (HPC) system or supercomputer for AI research applications \u2022 Optimize computational workflows for data-intensive aquaculture projects \u2022 Ensure integration of computing resources across all UAPB aquaculture facilities for collaborative AI research Facility and Research Support \u2022 Maintain IT connectivity and digital infrastructure for research stations at Lonoke, Eudora, and UAPB \u2022 Provide technical support for smart sensors, monitoring cameras, and laboratory equipment \u2022 Assist researchers and students with data access, backup, and computational analysis \u2022 Support workshops, training, and outreach programs related to AI and aquaculture technology ________________________________________ Skills and Competencies \u2022 Strong problem-solving, analytical, and troubleshooting abilities \u2022 Ability to manage IT systems across multiple research facilities \u2022 Excellent communication and teamwork skills \u2022 Proficiency in managing large datasets and computational workflows \u2022 Commitment to innovation in applying AI to aquaculture systems Qualifications: \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0BS or MS in Information Technology, Computer Science, Artificial Intelligence, Data Science, or related field \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Proven experience with networking systems, computer maintenance, and IT troubleshooting \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Knowledge of Python, R, MATLAB, or other programming languages used in AI research \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Familiarity with Linux environments and server management Additional Information: Preferred Qualifications \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Master's degree or equivalent experience in AI, Computational Biology, or a related discipline \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Experience with machine learning, image processing, or computer vision systems \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Background in aquaculture, fisheries, or environmental data analysis \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Experience building or maintaining high-performance computing systems or clusters Salary Information: $55,000 - $63,541 Required Documents to Apply: Letters of Recommendation, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume, Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants (Please upload all required documents in the \"Resume\" attachment section of your application to be considered for this position) : Recruitment Contact Information: Sharron Williams All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: The University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff may conduct pre-employment background checks on certain positions for applicants being considered for employment. \u00a0 The background checks may include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. \u00a0 Required checks are identified in the position listing. \u00a0 A criminal background check or arrest pending adjudication information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absences of a relationship to the requirements of the position. \u00a0 Background check information will be used in a consistent, non-discriminatory manner consistent with the state and federal law. \u00a0 The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Administrative-Analyst---Biology_R0086935": {"title": "Administrative Analyst - Biology", "description": "Start date: 2026-06-26\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Staff - Clerical Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Little Rock The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is a metropolitan research university that provides an accessible, quality education through flexible learning and unparalleled internship opportunities. At UA Little Rock, we prepare our more than 8,900 students to be innovators and responsible leaders in their fields. Committed to its metropolitan research university mission, UA Little Rock is a driving force in Little Rock's thriving cultural community and a major component of the city and state's growing profile as a regional leader in research, technology transfer, economic development, and job creation. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . Department: Biology Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: UA Little Rock is seeking to hire an Administrative Analyst. The incumbent reports directly to the Department Chair and assists the Chair in supporting students, faculty, and staff with the flow of information and documents. Job duties also include assisting the Chair with monitoring the department budget and preparing and processing documents related to hiring, payroll, faculty travel, purchasing, and departmental events. This individual also provides registration assistance to students and faculty, and inputs course schedule information throughout the year. This position is governed by state and federal laws and agency/institution policy. Qualifications: Required Education and/or Experience: The formal education equivalent of a high school diploma; One year (minimum) of specialized training in business management, business education, or a related field; Three years (minimum) of experience in specialized, or a related field applicable to work performed; Other job-related education and/or experience may be substituted for all or part of these basic requirements. Job Duties and Responsibilities: Process purchasing requisitions, reconciliation and authorization for payments of invoices, travel authorizations, and TR-1 forms, Electronic Personnel Action forms, and leave reports; Manage and balance the departmental budget; Collect necessary information and prepare/process documents relating to hiring, payroll, travel, purchasing, and departmental events; Input and update the course listing and manage E-updates; Manage the Biology office, prepare department meeting minutes, and manage inventory; Direct the activities of subordinate employees, monitor and review work regularly, and prepare annual performance evaluations; Delegate tasks and organize assignments for work-study students and manage their time clock; Provide registration assistance (clear advising flags when requested, course overrides, and related tasks); Provide information to students and faculty and assist as needed/requested by students and/or faculty; Maintain and develop new office policy and procedures as needed; Answer the telephone and greet visitors professionally; Perform other duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Knowledge of the principles and practices of mathematics and statistics; Knowledge of policy and procedures concerning the day-to-day operations of UA Little Rock; Knowledge of policy and procedures concerning UA Little Rock Admissions, Academic Advising, and Registration; Strong knowledge of computers and Microsoft Office. Ability to plan, organize, and coordinate activities, resources, and materials associated with the needs of the department or program; Ability to communicate effectively with others; Knowledge of computers and software applications; Ability to prepare, present, review oral and written information and reports; Ability to research and analyze related work program information; Ability to develop, recommend, interpret, and apply policy and procedures; Ability to analyze financial records and prepare reports; Ability to plan, organize, and direct the work of others; Ability to learn Workday. Additional Information: Salary Information: $36,327.00 Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Sinead Ni Chadhain, Department Chair snichadhain@ualr.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Financial Credit Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Sitting Frequent Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Repetitive Motion Occasional Physical Activity: Hearing, Lifting, Standing, Talking Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-Arkansas-at-Pine-Bluff/Vice-Chancellor-for-Institutional-Advancement_R0084657": {"title": "Vice Chancellor for Institutional Advancement", "description": "Start date: 2026-06-25\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Leadership - Institutional Officer Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff The University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff is an 1890 Land-Grant HBCU with a diverse student population, competitive degree offerings and stellar faculty. For more than 140 years, the University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff has worked to create an environment that inculcates learning, growth and productivity while affording a basic need to its students \u2013 a chance to advance. The 15:1 student to teacher ratio makes it possible to maintain a learning environment with close interaction between students and faculty while challenging curricula encourage our students to seek and fulfill their potential. You can excel in your chosen field of study through a curriculum of \u00a0 Certificate and Associates degree programs,\u00a0 more than thirty\u00a0 Undergraduate programs, Master\u2019s degree programs and a Doctorate program in Aquaculture/Fisheries. You can also develop workplace readiness through internships, co-ops and fellowships in the U.S. and abroad. Out-of-class experiences and student involvement include more than 90 student organizations, an internationally renowned Vesper Choir, Marching Band, Concert Bands, Wind Symphony, nationally recognized debate team, award-winning theater department and accomplished athletic program. Though the main campus is in Pine Bluff, its reach is worldwide. UAPB has an extended campus in North Little Rock and offers as well as online courses. With the addition of the Arkansas Research and Education Optical Network (ARE-ON), students can engage in information exchange with others anywhere in the world. There are also Research and Extension offices in Lonoke, Newport and Lake Village and collaborations with other colleges and universities in the State through the National Science Foundation funded STEM (Science, Technology, Engineering and Mathematics) Academy. As the second oldest land-grant institution in the state of Arkansas, the mission of this No Excuse University remains the same \u2013 to provide a high quality, affordable education with a personal touch. We invite you to Become a Part of the Pride at the University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process and require reasonable accommodations, please contact Human Resources at 870.575.8400 . Department: University of Arkansas Pine Bluff Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Primary Purpose of the Position Building upon a sustained philanthropic growth rate exceeding 25% annually over the past three years, the Vice Chancellor for Institutional Advancement offers a unique opportunity for a creative and innovative advancement leader to transform the institutional culture and significantly grow operational revenue. Reporting directly to the Chancellor and serving as a member of the Chancellor\u2019s Executive Cabinet, the Vice Chancellor for Institutional Advancement is the university\u2019s chief fundraising officer and senior advancement strategist. This executive leader is responsible for the comprehensive direction, execution, and evaluation of all development and alumni engagement functions at UAPB. The Vice Chancellor also works in close partnership with the University of Arkansas System Foundation to align philanthropic strategies, steward donor intent, and maximize long-term fundraising success on behalf of UAPB. The Vice Chancellor leads efforts to cultivate individual, corporate, and foundation support, spearheads major campaigns, and partners with internal stakeholders to align philanthropic strategy with institutional priorities outlined in Preeminence 2030: Advancing the Pride. The role also serves as a key ambassador to alumni, friends, and external partners, promoting a shared sense of pride, ownership, and investment in UAPB\u2019s future. Key Responsibilities The successful candidate will perform the following key duties and responsibilities within the Division of Institutional Advancement: Strategic Fundraising Leadership \u2022 Develop and implement a multi-year strategic fundraising plan that supports institutional priorities including student scholarships, endowed faculty positions, academic programs, facilities, and research. \u2022 Personally manage a portfolio of high-capacity major gift prospects and donors, providing strategic cultivation, solicitation, and stewardship. \u2022 Oversee all aspects of the giving pipeline, including annual giving, major gifts, planned giving, corporate and foundation relations, and capital campaigns. \u2022 Collaborate with the Chancellor, deans, and faculty to develop compelling cases for support and strategic fundraising priorities. \u2022 Engage directly in donor cultivation and solicitation activities, modeling best practices and reinforcing a high-performance, team-oriented culture. \u2022 Ensure all fundraising strategies are aligned with measurable outcomes, including increased student retention, degree completion, and institutional return on investment. Alumni Engagement and Constituent Relations \u2022 Lead and strengthen the Office of Alumni Affairs to build lifelong relationships with alumni through targeted communications, class reunions, regional events, affinity groups, homecoming activities, and volunteer engagement. \u2022 Develop segmented engagement strategies that connect alumni across generations, majors, industries, and regions. \u2022 Expand alumni participation in mentorship programs, student recruitment, career support, and annual giving. Campaign Planning and Execution \u2022 Build institutional readiness for a future comprehensive fundraising campaign by developing campaign infrastructure, donor pipeline, volunteer leadership, and internal systems. \u2022 Work closely with Institutional Advancement staff and academic leadership to establish campaign goals, timelines, and campaign marketing materials. \u2022 Leverage predictive analytics and donor segmentation tools to identify and prioritize high-impact prospects and campaign strategies. \u2022 Monitor campaign progress through performance metrics and report regularly to the Chancellor and Executive Cabinet. Donor Relations and Stewardship \u2022 Establish a comprehensive stewardship program to recognize, retain, and deepen donor relationships. \u2022 Ensure gift acknowledgement and reporting processes are timely, personalized, and aligned with donor intent. Use data visualization and AI-enhanced platforms to generate impact reports and donor communications that demonstrate transparency and long-term value. Foundation and Corporate Relations \u2022 Demonstrate an established portfolio of productive corporate, foundation, and business relationships and leverage those networks to expand philanthropic investment and strategic partnerships on behalf of UAPB. \u2022 Cultivate partnerships with private foundations and corporations to support scholarships, research, student internships, workforce development, and academic programming. \u2022 Write or contribute to the preparation of grant proposals in collaboration with academic units or the Office of Sponsored Programs. \u2022 Build external networks with employers, philanthropic organizations, and civic groups that align with UAPB\u2019s strategic and economic development goals. \u2022 Serve as a key strategist for Foundation-initiated proposals and joint funding ventures with industry-aligned academic programs. \u2022 Serve as a visible and active presence in the Pine Bluff community and broader Delta region, strengthening relationships that enhance institutional reputation and philanthropic support. Operational Management and Team Leadership \u2022 Recruit, mentor, and manage a high-performing Institutional Advancement team with expertise in donor relations, data analytics, alumni affairs, and campaign planning. \u2022 Develop and implement a structured professional development framework to support staff growth, succession planning, and advancement career pathways. \u2022 Oversee advancement operations including budget management, CRM systems (e.g., Raiser\u2019s Edge or equivalent), gift processing, prospect research, and reporting. \u2022 Implement AI-informed tools and digital engagement platforms to automate donor communications, personalize outreach, and improve giving conversion rates. \u2022 Establish clear KPIs, performance benchmarks, and assessment tools to track progress toward fundraising and engagement goals. \u2022 Foster a culture of innovation and continuous improvement by integrating data analytics into all decision-making and performance tracking processes. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications Baccalaureate degree from a regionally accredited four-year institution of higher education required. Minimum of five years of progressive advancement leadership experience, preferably at a four-year institution of higher education. Demonstrated, quantifiable record of securing and closing six- and seven-figure major gifts along with sustained donor stewardship and campaign leadership success. Evidence of fundraising and leveraging funds raised to support student success, including measurable improvements in retention, persistence, and 4-year degree completion. Experience managing fundraising teams and cross-functional advancement operations. Exceptional communication, collaboration, and interpersonal leadership skills. Preferred Qualifications An advanced degree from a regionally accredited four-year institution of higher education. Advancement experience at a public four-year institution, preferably a public land-grant or research-focused institution. Experience working across diverse institutional types, with an understanding of and appreciation for the mission and legacy of historically Black colleges and universities (HBCUs). Experience with alumni engagement, planned giving, foundation relations, and capital fundraising. Experience leading multi-million-dollar capital campaigns for four-year institutions of higher education. Experience directing, managing, and guiding multi-million dollar institutional and concept proposals to success. Understanding of advancement analytics, donor management systems (e.g., Affinaquest Advancement RM, Raiser\u2019s Edge, Slate, Scholarship Universe), and performance metrics. Commitment to expanding access, opportunity and impact through philanthropy. Additional Information: The University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff (UAPB), a proud 1890 land-grant institution, the only public historically Black university in Arkansas, and a Carnegie-classified Research College and University, seeks an accomplished, forward-thinking leader to serve as Vice Chancellor for Institutional Advancement. This defining moment in UAPB\u2019s history is marked by bold vision, accelerating institutional momentum, and expanding regional and national impact. The Vice Chancellor will serve as a strategist and chief fundraising officer, helping position UAPB as a beacon of opportunity and a catalyst for transformation across Arkansas and beyond. As UAPB accelerates its pursuit of national preeminence and Research 2 (R2) designation, the Vice Chancellor will lead efforts to grow philanthropic support, deepen alumni engagement, and foster a culture of giving that advances the university\u2019s most critical priorities from student success and faculty excellence to academic innovation and capital development. Why Join UAPB? At the University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff, you will join a leadership team committed to transformation, equity, and excellence. As UAPB expands its impact across the Arkansas Delta and beyond, the Vice Chancellor for Institutional Advancement will be empowered to build an advancement infrastructure that attracts new investment, engages alumni, and tells the compelling story of a university on the rise. This is more than a fundraising role\u2014it\u2019s a leadership opportunity to shape UAPB\u2019s future and ensure the continued legacy of one of America\u2019s most historic and promising HBCUs. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume, Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants (Please upload all required documents in the \"Resume\" attachment section of your application to be considered for this position) : Recruitment Contact Information: Sharron Williams Employment Manager 870 575-8403 All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: The University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff may conduct pre-employment background checks on certain positions for applicants being considered for employment. \u00a0 The background checks may include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. \u00a0 Required checks are identified in the position listing. \u00a0 A criminal background check or arrest pending adjudication information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absences of a relationship to the requirements of the position. \u00a0 Background check information will be used in a consistent, non-discriminatory manner consistent with the state and federal law. \u00a0 The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Stuttgart-Campus/Welding-Instructor--Career---Tech-Center_R0004840": {"title": "Welding Instructor, Career & Tech Center (Stuttgart)", "description": "Start date: 2026-06-24\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Academic (Non-Classified) Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: Phillips Community College of the University of Arkansas The first community college established in Arkansas, Phillips Community College of the University of Arkansas (PCCUA) is a multi-campus, two-year college serving Eastern Arkansas. PCCUA has academic, occupational/technical and continuing education programs and offers over 25 associate degree programs with campuses in DeWitt, Helena-W. Helena and Stuttgart. Thank you for your interest, and we hope you\u2019ll be joining our Ridge Runner family soon! Below you will find the details for the position as well as any specific application requirements you should review before applying for this opening. To apply for this position, please click the Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process, please call Human Resources at (870) 338-6474, ext. 1271. Department: Career and Technical Center Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Teach, develop and update welding and related courses for the Career and Technical Center. Teach all applicable regulations, policies and procedures for health, safety, and environmental compliance. Instruct and prepare students to take and pass NCCER certification. Assist with program recruiting. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications Associates of Applied Science degree in welding or related filed. Applicants with teaching experience or work experience will be given preference. Experience with welding or HVAC desired. Preferred Qualifications Master Welding Certification. Additional Information: Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Demetric Johnson, DJohnson@pccua.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry For general application assistance, or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at (870) 338-6474, ext. 1271. PCCUA is committed to providing a safe campus community. We will conduct criminal background checks and a sex offender registry check for applicants seeking employment. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Standing, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Sitting Occasional Physical Activity: Driving, Kneeling, Lifting, Pulling, Pushing Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAM--Monticello-Campus/Assistant-Professor-of-Accounting_R0079793-1": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Accounting", "description": "Start date: 2026-06-23\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Faculty - Tenure/Tenure Track Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Monticello UAM, one of twenty campuses of the University of Arkansas System, is located in southeastern Arkansas in the beautiful timberlands, rich in outdoor recreation activities, and approximately 100 miles south of Little Rock. UAM is a comprehensive, residential and commuter, undergraduate institution also offering selected master\u2019s degree programs. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please submit a request via the OEOC website: \u00a0Applicants are required to submit a request for each position to which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 870-460-1422 . Department: Business Department's Website: www.uamont.edu Summary of Job Duties: The University of Arkansas at Monticello invites applications for an assistant/instructor faculty position in accounting. Primary duties consist of teaching Principles of Managerial Accounting and upper-level courses in the major such as Cost Accounting, Auditing, Governmental/Nonprofit and Accounting Information Systems. Other responsibilities include advising students and service to the University and the School of Business. Expectations for promotion and tenure include research/scholarly activities appropriate to a teaching-centered School of Business. Collegiality, professionalism, effective communication skills, and a strong commitment to teaching excellence are necessary. As a member of the business faculty the successful candidate will be an integral part of the School and have the opportunity to shape the accounting and business programs. Qualifications: For appointment at the assistant professor level a Ph.D. or D.B.A. is strongly preferred. \u00a0 Applicants with CPA licensure and a Master\u2019s degree in business, accounting, or a related field may be considered for appointment at the assistant level. Applicants with a Master\u2019s degree in business, accounting, or a related field may be considered for appointment at the instructor level. \u00a0 Preference will be given to candidates with previous higher education teaching experience, both online and in-person. \u00a0 Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Additional Information: Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience. Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Curriculum Vitae, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Marsha Clayton, Dean, School of Business, clayton@uamont.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Accountant---Accounting---Compliance-Specialist_R0086551-1": {"title": "Accountant - Accounting & Compliance Specialist", "description": "Start date: 2026-06-23\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Staff - Accounting, Finance, Business Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: Division of Agriculture of the University of Arkansas The University of Arkansas System Division of Agriculture is a state wide campus, with faculty based on University campuses, at Research and Extension Centers and in every Arkansas county. It consists of the Arkansas Agricultural Experiment Station (AES) and the Arkansas Cooperative Extension Service (CES), and is home to more than 1400 employees.\u00a0 The Division was established in 1959 and is headed by the Vice-President for Agriculture.\u00a0 The Division headquarters is located in Little Rock with the rest of the University of Arkansas System Administration.\u00a0 As an employer, the University of Arkansas System Division of Agriculture offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance.\u00a0 Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process and require reasonable accommodations, please contact the Division's Office of Program & Employment Compliance at compliance@uada.edu . For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-671-2219 or 479-502-9820. Department: Division | Asst. VP for Finance & Administration Department's Website: uada.edu Summary of Job Duties: The Accounting & Compliance Specialist is an accounting position responsible for the processing, analysis, interpretation, and management of financial accounting data. Typical Functions: \u2022 Review and process Workday transactions for compliance and accuracy. \u2022 Prepare and process data files using mass data upload tools. \u2022 Prepare and post accounting journals and budget amendments. \u2022 Prepare various financial reports, including state, federal, and ad-hoc reports. \u2022 Assist with year-end processes \u2022 Perform general ledger account reconciliations \u2022 Assist in gathering and reviewing data for preparation of fiscal year budget \u2022 Assist other departments within the Business Office when needed in various accounting duties. \u2022 Participate in the development and implementation of new processes and procedures \u2022 Perform other duties as assigned. This position is governed by Generally Accepted Accounting Principles (GAAP), state and federal laws, and institution policy. Regular, reliable, and non-disruptive attendance is an essential job duty, as is the ability to create and maintain collegial, harmonious working relationships with others. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications The formal education equivalent of a bachelor\u2019s degree in accounting, business administration, or related field. Preferred Qualifications: \u00b7 2 years of relevant professional experience \u00b7 Workday financials experience \u00b7 Higher Education or State Government experience \u00b7 Proficient in Microsoft Office, especially Excel Knowledge, Skills & Abilities: \u00b7 Knowledge of accounting principles, financial statements, and ledgers \u00b7 Knowledge of Microsoft Office and computer technology related to accounting systems. \u00b7 Ability to establish, maintain, and reconcile accounting records and reports. \u00b7 Ability to interpret and apply provisions of laws, rules, or policies to specific situations. \u00b7 Ability to analyze financial data and prepare financial reports. \u00b7 Ability to provide guidance and technical assistance to end users. \u00b7 Ability to scrutinize transactions for accuracy. \u00b7 Ability to organize, plan, & prioritize work. Additional Information: Salary Information: $50,000 - $55,000 Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Jan Sampson, jsampson@uada.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check The University of Arkansas System Division of Agriculture may conduct pre-employment background checks on certain positions for applicants being considered for employment. \u00a0 The background checks may include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. \u00a0 Required checks are identified in the position listing. \u00a0 A criminal background check or arrest pending adjudication information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absences of a relationship to the requirements of the position. \u00a0 Background check information will be used in a consistent, non-discriminatory manner consistent with the state and federal law. \u00a0 The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding Frequent Physical Activity: Repetitive Motion, Talking Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Harrisburg/Director--Northeast-Rice-Research---Extension-Center_R0087158-1": {"title": "Director, Northeast Rice Research & Extension Center", "description": "Start date: 2026-06-22\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Faculty - Non-Tenure Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: Yes Institution Name: Division of Agriculture of the University of Arkansas The University of Arkansas System Division of Agriculture is a state wide campus, with faculty based on University campuses, at Research and Extension Centers and in every Arkansas county. It consists of the Arkansas Agricultural Experiment Station (AES) and the Arkansas Cooperative Extension Service (CES), and is home to more than 1400 employees.\u00a0 The Division was established in 1959 and is headed by the Vice-President for Agriculture.\u00a0 The Division headquarters is located in Little Rock with the rest of the University of Arkansas System Administration.\u00a0 As an employer, the University of Arkansas System Division of Agriculture offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance.\u00a0 Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process and require reasonable accommodations, please contact the Division's Office of Program & Employment Compliance at compliance@uada.edu . For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-671-2219 or 479-502-9820. Department: Admin Department's Website: https://aaes.uada.edu/research-locations/northeast-rice-research-and-extension-center/ Summary of Job Duties: The University of Arkansas System Division of Agriculture seeks an energetic and visionary leader to serve as Director of the Northeast Rice Research & Extension Center (NERREC), located near Jonesboro, Arkansas. The Director will lead a multidisciplinary team of approximately five research and extension faculty and 30 full time and hourly support staff. The Director is responsible for guiding, fostering, and advancing strong, collaborative research and Extension programs addressing applied and basic research needs relevant to Arkansas and the mid-South rice industry. The successful candidate will provide comprehensive leadership in planning, integration, and implementation of all research and Extension activities conducted at NERREC. Key responsibilities include: \u2022 Administrative and fiscal leadership for NERREC personnel, programs, and physical resources. \u2022 Program planning, faculty development, and pursuit of extramural funding. \u2022 Coordination with other university programs, professional organizations, governmental agencies, and agricultural industry groups. \u2022 Active engagement with industry stakeholders, including but not limited to the Arkansas Rice Research & Promotion Board, Rice Technical Working Group, Arkansas Farm Bureau, USA Rice, and Arkansas Rice Federation. \u2022 Establishing research and Extension priorities related to rice production, processing, and marketing. \u2022 Providing overall leadership for planning and execution of the annual NE Rice Field Day. More information about NERREC is available at: https://aaes.uada.edu/research-locations/northeast-rice-research-and-extension-center/ This is a full time, twelve-month, non-tenure track appointment. Salary is commensurate with qualifications and experience. Qualifications: Required Qualifications Earned Ph.D. in Agriculture or a closely related discipline. Outstanding record of professional accomplishments that merit appointment at the rank of Professor . Demonstrated ability to communicate effectively and persuasively with both scientific and stakeholder audiences. Evidence of administrative leadership skills and the ability to guide a dynamic research and Extension program. Demonstrated ability to collaborate and communicate with diverse clientele. \u00a0 Preferred Qualifications Experience in the Land-Grant University System, including research, Extension, or both. Experience conducting field research at research stations or Research & Extension Centers. Demonstrated success managing fiscal, human, and infrastructure resources. Proven ability to attract and manage extramural funding. Experience leading or coordinating multidisciplinary research teams . Excellence in written and oral communication. \u00a0 Additional Information: Applicants should submit: 1. Letter of interest describing relevant experience and vision for the role. 2. Curriculum vitae . 3. Names and contact information for five references who may be asked to provide letters of reference. 4. A one\u2011page statement addressing: (1) Professional goals (2) Key challenges facing row\u2011crop agriculture and the mid\u2011South rice industry (3) Approaches to addressing these challenges, including the applicant\u2019s philosophy of administrative leadership The position will remain open until a suitable candidate is identified. Screening of applicants is expected to begin in August. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Curriculum Vitae, List of five Professional References (name, email, business title), Other (see special instructions for details) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: A one-page statement addressing: o (1) Professional goals o (2) Key challenges facing row crop agriculture and the mid-South rice industry o (3) Approaches to addressing these challenges, including the applicant\u2019s philosophy of administrative leadership Recruitment Contact Information: Dr. Jean-Fran\u00e7ois Meullenet Senior Associate Vice President for Agriculture-Research and Director of the AAES jfmeull@uark.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Motor Vehicle Reports Check The University of Arkansas System Division of Agriculture may conduct pre-employment background checks on certain positions for applicants being considered for employment. \u00a0 The background checks may include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. \u00a0 Required checks are identified in the position listing. \u00a0 A criminal background check or arrest pending adjudication information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absences of a relationship to the requirements of the position. \u00a0 Background check information will be used in a consistent, non-discriminatory manner consistent with the state and federal law. \u00a0 The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting, Talking Occasional Physical Activity: Kneeling, Lifting, Reaching Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-Arkansas-Community-College-at-Batesville/Faculty-Mathematics_R0087191": {"title": "Faculty-Mathematics", "description": "Start date: 2026-06-22\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. Closing Date: Type of Position: Faculty - Non-Tenure Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Academic Term (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas Community College at Batesville The University of Arkansas Community College at Batesville (UACCB) is a comprehensive community college committed to providing learning experiences that improve the lives of those we serve. UACCB provides affordable access to technical education and college transfer programs that meet the diverse higher education needs of the citizens of north central Arkansas. \u00a0 These programs are provided to the traditional college student as well as to high school students through a state approved Secondary Area Career Center. \u00a0 The College also promotes economic development and an enhanced quality of life for the community through adult education, developmental education, customized business and industry training, and continuing education programs. UACCB's mission is to provide quality educational opportunities within a supportive learning environment. We promote success through community partnerships, responsive programs, and an enduring commitment to improvement. Thank you for your interest. \u00a0 We hope you will be joining us soon! After reviewing the Job Duties and Qualifications listed below, click the Apply button at the top of the page to begin the application process. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process or for general application assistance, please contact the Human Resource Office at (870) 612-2045. Department: Dean of General Education Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Basic Functions Under the direction of the Dean of General Education and Transfer, this full-time, 9-month faculty position is responsible for delivering high-quality instruction in the assigned General Education teaching area across on-ground, hybrid, and online formats. Beyond instruction, this position is essential for curriculum development, student learning assessment, and engagement with industry and/or academic partners to align educational programs with current academic, transfer, and workforce trends. Position Duties 75% Classroom and Laboratory Instruction Focus on delivering high-quality instruction in the assigned teaching area. This includes the development and assessment of student learning outcomes to ensure competency in both credit and non-credit coursework depending on program and assigned teaching area needs. The instructor utilizes the college\u2019s student and learning management systems as well as other college identified instructional technology to deliver content effectively across multiple platforms while maintaining a safe and productive learning environment. 15% Student Retention and Recruitment Directs efforts toward student success by implementing retention and completion strategies designed to identify and support students. This includes engaging with students regularly in both curricular and co-curricular settings. The instructor maintains regular office hours to provide a consistent point of contact for academic support and intervention. Additionally, this position actively leads and participates in recruitment activities to promote the General Education degree programs within the community and local high schools, ensuring a steady pipeline of qualified applicants. 5% Industry/Academic Alignment Focus on building and maintaining relationships with industry and/or academic partners to ensure that degree program and course curriculum remain aligned with current academic/transfer requirements and workforce needs. 5% Professional Development and College Service Maintains professional expertise by staying current with regulatory, policy, or academic requirements, best practices, and teaching methodologies through ongoing professional development and faculty workshops. This duty includes participating in shared institutional governance through campus, division/department, and faculty senate meetings. The instructor also serves on committees and engages in service activities that support the institution and the local community. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Knowledge Subject Matter: Comprehensive understanding of subject matter in the identified teaching area. Instructional Design: Knowledge of curriculum development and alignment, including the creation of syllabi, instructional materials, and assessments. Pedagogical Methodology: Understanding of student-centered learning and critical thinking strategies appropriate for both high school and adult learners. Educational Technology: Knowledge of online, hybrid, and on-ground instructional delivery methods and the utilization of learning management systems (LMS). Skills Instructional Delivery: Skilled in delivering high-quality instruction and conducting assessments of student learning. Technology Utilization: Competent in utilizing technology effectively in a teaching environment to enhance student learning. Communication: Excellent oral and written communication skills necessary for student engagement and collaborating with diverse stakeholders. Strategic Assessment: Ability to facilitate planning, assessment, and evaluation activities in support of institutional, program, and student learning outcomes. Abilities Adaptability: Ability to teach across various formats (online, hybrid, on-ground) and handle both credit and non-credit coursework. Student-Centered Support: Ability to perform duties that support student retention and completion goals. Governance Participation: Ability to effectively participate in shared institutional governance such as faculty senate and committees. Collaborative Partnership: Ability to work effectively and collegially with internal and external stakeholders to support success of current and future students. Qualifications: Qualifications\u00a0 Master\u2019s Degree from an accredited college or university in Mathematics or related field. Applicable Licenses, Certifications, and/or Credentials may also be considered when relevant.\u00a0 Ability to communicate effectively and utilize technology in teaching.\u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Preferred Qualifications\u00a0 Doctorate Degree from an accredited college or university in Mathematics or related field.\u00a0\u00a0 Teaching experience in higher education, specifically in a community college setting or corporate training experience.\u00a0 Additional Information: Salary Information: Salary determined by UACCB scale and commensurate with education and experience. Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume, Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Human Resources hr@uaccb.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Child Maltreatment, Criminal Background Check, Motor Vehicle Reports Check, Sex Offender Registry UACCB is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check for all applicants.\u00a0 Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Driving, Grasping, Reaching, Repetitive Motion Occasional Physical Activity: Balancing, Climbing, Crawling, Crouching, Feeling, Kneeling, Lifting, Pulling, Pushing, Stooping Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-Arkansas-at-Pine-Bluff/Assistant-Professor-1_R0087193": {"title": "Assistant Professor-1", "description": "Start date: 2026-06-18\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Faculty - Tenure/Tenure Track Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Academic Term (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff The University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff is an 1890 Land-Grant HBCU with a diverse student population, competitive degree offerings and stellar faculty. For more than 140 years, the University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff has worked to create an environment that inculcates learning, growth and productivity while affording a basic need to its students \u2013 a chance to advance. The 15:1 student to teacher ratio makes it possible to maintain a learning environment with close interaction between students and faculty while challenging curricula encourage our students to seek and fulfill their potential. You can excel in your chosen field of study through a curriculum of \u00a0 Certificate and Associates degree programs,\u00a0 more than thirty\u00a0 Undergraduate programs, Master\u2019s degree programs and a Doctorate program in Aquaculture/Fisheries. You can also develop workplace readiness through internships, co-ops and fellowships in the U.S. and abroad. Out-of-class experiences and student involvement include more than 90 student organizations, an internationally renowned Vesper Choir, Marching Band, Concert Bands, Wind Symphony, nationally recognized debate team, award-winning theater department and accomplished athletic program. Though the main campus is in Pine Bluff, its reach is worldwide. UAPB has an extended campus in North Little Rock and offers as well as online courses. With the addition of the Arkansas Research and Education Optical Network (ARE-ON), students can engage in information exchange with others anywhere in the world. There are also Research and Extension offices in Lonoke, Newport and Lake Village and collaborations with other colleges and universities in the State through the National Science Foundation funded STEM (Science, Technology, Engineering and Mathematics) Academy. As the second oldest land-grant institution in the state of Arkansas, the mission of this No Excuse University remains the same \u2013 to provide a high quality, affordable education with a personal touch. We invite you to Become a Part of the Pride at the University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process and require reasonable accommodations, please contact Human Resources at 870.575.8400 . Department: Curriculum and Instruction Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Position Summary The Assistant Professor is a tenure-track faculty position that integrates teaching, scholarship, service, and coordination of the EPP program. The faculty member provides high-quality undergraduate and graduate instruction while serving as the academic lead for the reading instruction. The position supports educator preparation by ensuring alignment with state licensure requirements, CAEP accreditation standards, and institutional priorities. The faculty member reports to the Department Chair of Curriculum and Instruction and collaborates with the Dean, advisors, certification staff, and PK\u201312 partners. Appointment Details \u2022 Appointment Type: Tenure-track faculty appointment \u2022 Rank: Assistant Professor \u2022 Reports To: Department Chair, Curriculum and Instruction \u2022 Appointment Length: Nine (9) months (with possible summer assignment) \u2022 Teaching Assignment: Twelve (12) semester credit hours per term, including undergraduate and graduate coursework, adjusted as appropriate for program coordination responsibilities Primary Role Allocation Category Percentage Teaching & Advising 50% Scholarship & Research 25% Service, Leadership & Program Coordination 25% Teaching and Advising (50%) \u2022 Teach a combined load of undergraduate and graduate courses totaling twelve (12) semester credit hours per term in areas such as curriculum, instruction, assessment, methods, and professional practice. \u2022 Deliver instruction aligned with CAEP standards, state licensure competencies, and institutional learning outcomes. \u2022 Incorporate evidence-based instructional strategies, technology, and inclusive pedagogical practices. \u2022 Advise undergraduate and graduate students on coursework, program milestones, licensure requirements, and degree completion. \u2022 Supervise field-based, clinical, internship, residency, and capstone experiences as assigned. \u2022 Model excellence in teaching and contribute to curriculum coherence across undergraduate and graduate programs. \u2022 Coordinate curriculum planning, course sequencing, scheduling, and cohort management. \u2022 Ensure program alignment with Arkansas licensure requirements, CAEP standards, and institutional policies. \u2022 Lead admissions review, student progression monitoring, and candidate support systems. \u2022 Collaborate with advisors, certification officers, clinical coordinators, and district partners. \u2022 Lead data collection, assessment reporting, and continuous improvement efforts for reading instruction. \u2022 Prepare required reports for accreditation, state approval, and internal review. Scholarship and Research (25%) \u2022 Maintain an active scholarly agenda in curriculum and instruction, teacher education, assessment, or related fields. \u2022 Publish in peer-reviewed journals and present at regional, state, or national conferences. \u2022 Engage in collaborative research and, where appropriate, involve undergraduate and graduate students. \u2022 Seek external funding and contribute to grant initiatives supporting educator preparation. Service and Institutional Engagement (Within 25% Service/Leadership Allocation) \u2022 Serve on departmental, college, and university committees. \u2022 Contribute to accreditation, assessment, and quality assurance activities. \u2022 Support recruitment, orientation, and retention of undergraduate and graduate students. \u2022 Build and sustain partnerships with PK\u201312 schools and districts. \u2022 Participate in professional service related to educator preparation. Required Education and Experience Education \u2022 Earned doctoral degree (PhD or EdD) in Curriculum and Instruction, Teacher Education, or a closely related field from an accredited institution. o ABD candidates may be considered if degree completion is imminent. Teaching Experience \u2022 Demonstrated effectiveness teaching undergraduate and/or graduate coursework in education-related fields. Program or Leadership Experience \u2022 Experience in program coordination, curriculum leadership, assessment, advising, or accreditation-related work is required or expected by the time of tenure consideration. Preferred Qualifications \u2022 Experience teaching in both undergraduate and graduate educator preparation programs. \u2022 Familiarity with CAEP accreditation, state licensure systems, and educator preparation accountability. \u2022 Knowledge of edTPA, Praxis, or clinical supervision models. \u2022 Evidence of or potential for grant writing and funded initiatives. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Knowledge \u2022 Knowledge of curriculum design, instructional theory, and pedagogy across P\u201312 settings. \u2022 Knowledge of educator preparation standards, licensure requirements, and accreditation processes. \u2022 Knowledge of assessment, data use, and continuous improvement practices. Skills \u2022 Strong teaching and course design skills for undergraduate and graduate instruction. \u2022 Effective written and oral communication skills. \u2022 Advising, mentoring, and organizational skills. \u2022 Ability to analyze program and student data for improvement. Abilities \u2022 Ability to manage a 12-credit-hour teaching load while coordinating a graduate program. \u2022 Ability to collaborate with faculty, staff, students, and school partners. \u2022 Ability to meet multiple deadlines and manage administrative and instructional responsibilities. \u2022 Ability to model professionalism, equity-centered practice, and instructional excellence. Additional Information \u2022 Summer teaching or coordination assignments may be available subject to funding and program needs. \u2022 Teaching assignments may be adjusted in accordance with coordination responsibilities and departmental workload policy. Qualifications: Required Education and Experience Education Required Qualifications Earned \u00a0 doctorate (Ph.D. or Ed.D.) \u00a0in Reading, Literacy Education, Curriculum & Instruction with a Literacy emphasis, or a closely related field from an accredited institution. At least \u00a0 18 graduate credit hours in Reading/Literacy . Minimum of \u00a0 3 years of P\u201312 teaching experience . Valid teaching license/certification in Reading, Literacy, Elementary Education, or a related area. Evidence of successful teaching at the P\u201312 and/or higher education level. Knowledge of the \u00a0 Science of Reading \u00a0and evidence-based literacy practices. Ability to teach undergraduate and graduate reading/literacy courses. Demonstrated potential for scholarship, research, and service. Preferred Qualifications Reading Specialist endorsement and/or National Board Certification. Experience preparing teacher candidates for state licensure examinations, including Foundations of Reading. Experience with CAEP accreditation, assessment, and program evaluation. Online teaching experience using learning management systems. Record of scholarly publications, presentations, and/or grant activity. Experience supervising teacher candidates during clinical practice or residency experiences. Expertise in the \u00a0 Science of Reading and Foundations of Reading competencies . Experience working with diverse and high-needs school districts. Ability to support \u00a0 Praxis and Foundations of Reading preparation initiatives . Commitment to the mission of an HBCU and the 1890 land-grant tradition. Typical Responsibilities Teach undergraduate and graduate literacy/reading courses. Supervise field experiences, internships, and residencies. Advise and mentor students. Engage in scholarship, research, and grant development. Participate in departmental, college, university, and community service. Support accreditation and continuous improvement efforts Teaching Experience Demonstrated effectiveness teaching undergraduate and/or graduate coursework in education-related fields. Program or Leadership Experience Experience in program coordination, curriculum leadership, assessment, advising, or accreditation-related work is required or expected by the time of tenure consideration. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Knowledge Knowledge of curriculum design, instructional theory, and pedagogy across P\u201312 settings. Knowledge of educator preparation standards, licensure requirements, and accreditation processes. Knowledge of assessment, data use, and continuous improvement practices. Skills Strong teaching and course design skills for undergraduate and graduate instruction. Effective written and oral communication skills. Advising, mentoring, and organizational skills. Ability to analyze program and student data for improvement. Abilities Ability to manage a 12-credit-hour teaching load while coordinating a graduate program. Ability to collaborate with faculty, staff, students, and school partners. Ability to meet multiple deadlines and manage administrative and instructional responsibilities. Ability to model professionalism, equity-centered practice, and instructional excellence. Additional Information Summer teaching or coordination assignments may be available subject to funding and program needs. Teaching assignments may be adjusted in accordance with coordination responsibilities and departmental workload policy. \u00a0 Additional Information: Salary Information: 55,000-60,000 Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume, Statement of Teaching Philosophy, Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants (Please upload all required documents in the \"Resume\" attachment section of your application to be considered for this position) : Recruitment Contact Information: Sharron Williams Employment Manager 870-575-8402 All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check The University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff may conduct pre-employment background checks on certain positions for applicants being considered for employment. \u00a0 The background checks may include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. \u00a0 Required checks are identified in the position listing. \u00a0 A criminal background check or arrest pending adjudication information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absences of a relationship to the requirements of the position. \u00a0 Background check information will be used in a consistent, non-discriminatory manner consistent with the state and federal law. \u00a0 The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAMS/APRN-PA---WISL_R0087236-1": {"title": "APRN/PA - WISL", "description": "Start date: 2026-06-18\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/18/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: ICE | WISL APRN A OP C Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Summary Of Job Duties The APRN/PA will extend the patient care and administrative services for the UAMS Women and Infants Service Line (WISL) physicians in the outpatient settings. APRN/PA will be expected to provide comprehensive health assessments, determine diagnoses, implement treatment plans, perform procedures, and prescribe medicines and treatments. The APRN/PA will also manage health issues for patients, independently or in collaboration with the designated physicians. The APRN/PA will work autonomously as well as in collaboration with a variety of individuals to diagnose and manage patient's health care problems; and will serve as a health care resource, interdisciplinary consultant, and patient advocate. The APRN/PA will also coordinate the multidisciplinary care of patients, facilitating all necessary consults, assuring that care is timely and appropriate. Qualifications: Minimum Qualification: Master\u2019s Degree Two (2) years nursing experience Licensed Registered Nurse in Arkansas; APRN/CPN License, or PA with State Medical Board. Current BLS certification or must successfully obtain certification within the first 30 days of employment. Must be able to operate all typical nursing equipment essential to performing the job (i.e., scales, procedure equipment, needles, blood pressure equipment, and EKG machines).\u00a0 Must have normal communication sensory requirement. Ability to comply with CDC Universal Precautions when indicated.\u00a0 \u00a0 Preferred Qualifications : Preferred nursing experience in endocrine or women\u2019s health. Prescriptive authority and DEA license must be obtained after hire. Additional Information: Responsibilities: Delivers prenatal, intrapartum, and postpartum care to women, including routine assessments, screenings, and management of complications. \u200b Collaborates with maternal-fetal medicine specialists to care for patients with conditions such as diabetes, hypertension, and placental abnormalities. \u200b Supports laboring patients, assist with deliveries, and respond to obstetric emergencies in the labor and delivery unit. \u200b Conducts newborn assessments, manage common neonatal conditions, and collaborate with the Neonatal Intensive Care Unit (NICU) team for more complex cases. \u200b Provides education on breastfeeding, safe sleep practices, infant care, and postpartum mental health to families. \u200b Engages in telehealth consultations to extend care to underserved populations, ensuring access to specialized services. \u200b Collaborates with obstetricians, pediatricians, lactation consultants, and social workers to deliver holistic care to mothers and infants. \u200b Engages in quality assurance and improvement activities to enhance patient outcomes and care delivery processes. \u200b Delivers care through mobile health units and community outreach programs, ensuring access to services for women in rural areas. \u200b Contributes to clinical research and provide education to medical students, residents, and other healthcare professionals. May perform other duties assigned. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAFS--University-of-Arkansas-Fort-Smith/Assistant-to-the-Dean---College-of-Business-and-Industry_R0087220": {"title": "Assistant to the Dean - College of Business and Industry", "description": "Start date: 2026-06-17\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Professional Staff - Institutional Affairs Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Fort Smith University of Arkansas \u2013 Fort Smith The University of Arkansas - Fort Smith is a dynamic, mid-sized public university that\u2019s redefining higher education. We\u2019re on a mission to provide transformative, hands-on learning experiences for students of all backgrounds and aspirations. Our multi-faceted approach to education offers a wealth of opportunities, with over 70 academic programs, including certificates, associate, bachelor\u2019s, and master\u2019s degrees. We\u2019re committed to building a diverse community that mirrors Arkansas\u2019s rich tapestry, reflecting our dedication to serving the state\u2019s varied population while enhancing the quality of our institution. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life, and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10 percent of employee salary. \u00a0 Fort Smith, Arkansas Nestled along the Arkansas River, this vibrant city offers a perfect blend of history, culture, and natural beauty. Immerse yourself in the rich heritage of the Old West at the Fort Smith National Historic Site, explore the eclectic local art scene, or take a scenic stroll along the picturesque riverfront trails. With a welcoming community, diverse dining options, and a thriving downtown, Fort Smith is the ideal destination for history enthusiasts and those seeking modern amenities. Thank you for your interest in joining our university. Below you will find details for the position including any supplementary documentation and/or questions you should review before submitting your application. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at (479) 788-7080. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 479-788-7080. Applicants are required to submit a request for each position to which they have applied. Department: College of Business and Industry Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Provide executive-level administrative support for the Office of the Dean. Will coordinate and screen the dean\u2019s schedule, anticipate and resolve issues, track budgets, help with faculty schedule and workloads, coordinate special events and other metrics to ensure the success of the College of Business & Industry. The position reports to the Dean of the College of Business and Industry. Qualifications: Required Education and/or Work Experience: Associates degree and four years\u2019 experience in an administrative/secretarial position or related field or a bachelor\u2019s degree and two years\u2019 experience in an administrative/secretarial position or related field.\u00a0 Other job-related education and/or experience may be substituted for part of these requirements. Preferred Education and/or Work Experience: Previous experience in an executive assistant role or in an administrative/secretarial position in higher education is preferred. Essential Job Duties and Responsibilities: Oversee daily office activities and provide administrative support for the dean, to include screening and handling telephone communications, greeting and directing visitors, and assisting with administrative problems and inquiries. Serves as a primary point of contact and liaison between the office, various internal stakeholders including the Provost, departmental leadership, faculty, students, as well as external constituencies on a range of day-to-day issues. Schedule and coordinate the dean's appointments and/or travel arrangements. Work collaboratively with department heads and faculty to coordinate purchasing. Organize meetings and special events; schedule and coordinate dates and times, venues, participant attendance, agendas, and facilities; record minutes and follow-up on matters arising from meetings. Compose and prepare written documentation and correspondence for the office; screen and evaluate incoming and outgoing correspondence and prepare responses as appropriate. Provide general oversight of student assistants and work collaboratively with other administrative assistants in the College and across campus. Assist with administrative activities associated with academic affairs, such as contracts, teaching schedules, workload, and promotion. Enhances professional growth and development through participation in educational programs, current literature, college and university meetings, and workshops. Other Job Duties and Responsibilities: Establish and maintain files and retrieve information as needed for reference or reports. Prepare PowerPoint presentations. Perform duplication and copying as needed. Coordinates security and maintenance requests to building. Other duties as assigned. Responsible for maintaining a positive work atmosphere by acting and communicating in a manner to foster teamwork and by providing leadership to subordinates. Requires consistent on-time attendance. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: To perform the job successfully, the following competencies are required for the essential functions of this position: Knowledge of general office management principles and procedures, including the operation of standard office equipment. Excellent technical skills, including working knowledge of Workday, Microsoft Office Suite, and/or a willingness to learn new programs. Excellent customer service, interpersonal, and communication skills. Ability to coordinate and organize meetings and/or special events. High attention for details. Ability to extract and organize information. Ability to multitask and prioritize. Ability to work collaboratively with others.\u00a0 Additional Information: Working Relationships: Regular contact with Business, Engineering & Industry staff, students, other campus departments, organizations, and the public. List Employees Supervised: Student workers. Special Job Dimensions: Work performed primarily in an office setting. Occasional travel and extended hours required. While performing the duties of this job, the employee regularly exhibits digital dexterity when entering data into computer. Required abilities include walking, standing, and sitting for extended periods. Visual demands include close, relatively detailed vision when focusing on a computer screen. Employee regularly talks and hears. Office hours 8 a.m. until 5 p.m., Monday through Friday. Employee occasionally lifts items up to 10 pounds Background Check Requirements. Criminal Background Check and Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) Check. This job description is not designed to contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties, and/or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time with or without notice. Salary Information: $36,000 Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume, Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Candidates are encouraged to apply by June 24th for full consideration. Recruitment Contact Information: HR 479-788-7080 All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Motor Vehicle Reports Check This position may be subject to a pre-employment criminal background check, sex offender registry check, financial history background check, and/or drug screening. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication and/or adverse financial history alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background checks and drug screening information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting Occasional Physical Activity: Talking Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Operations-Coordinator_R0087073": {"title": "Operations Coordinator", "description": "Start date: 2026-06-15\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Administration - Operations Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Little Rock The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is a metropolitan research university that provides an accessible, quality education through flexible learning and unparalleled internship opportunities. At UA Little Rock, we prepare our more than 8,900 students to be innovators and responsible leaders in their fields. Committed to its metropolitan research university mission, UA Little Rock is a driving force in Little Rock's thriving cultural community and a major component of the city and state's growing profile as a regional leader in research, technology transfer, economic development, and job creation. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . Department: Office-Government Relations Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Operations Coordinator is responsible for taking a support role in the daily administrative operations of the University Affairs Division, which is responsible for local, state, and federal government affairs. The Operations Coordinator also provides project support for the Chancellor\u2019s Office as needed. The Operations Coordinator works closely with the Vice Chancellor for University Affairs to design and implement systems to efficiently manage departmental needs including supplies, equipment, phone coverage, events, and planning for key stakeholders visiting campus. Responsibilities also include procurement purchases with P-card; processing purchase requisitions and fund transfers through Workday, and Foundation Fund Tracking and Administration (FFTA); submitting orders and payments to campus catering for University Affairs and other units as assigned. The Operations Coordinator also provides support for meetings, receptions, and special events organized and coordinated by University Affairs. The Operations Coordinator will be accountable for delivering excellent customer service. This position is governed by state and federal laws, and agency/institution policy. Qualifications: Required Education and/or Experience: High School Diploma; Administrative Support experience in a professional setting.\u00a0 Preferred Education and/or Experience: Event experience. Experience with Workday. Job Duties and Responsibilities: Customer Service and Support Provide quality customer support service to internal and external guests; Act as liaison for managing contacts from within and outside of campus as needed to support the work of University Affairs, such as IT Services, Finance and Administration, catering services, Marketing and Communications, Student Affairs, and Facilities Management; Assist with planning and executing events and campus visits with key stakeholders coordinated by University Affairs. Office Management Support Provide professional administrative support for the Chancellor's Office and University Affairs, including assisting with management of the Vice Chancellor for University Affairs' calendar by ensuring key legislative and campus events are included and scheduling meetings with stakeholders and relevant personnel as requested; Assist with campus visits and tours for elected officials and key stakeholders by coordinating invitations, securing space, obtaining and returning golf carts, maintaining materials, and communicating visitor parking needs to campus police; Handle routine printing, photocopying, scanning of documents, and processing of packages for express delivery; Assist Vice Chancellor for University Affairs in meeting preparation by providing supporting documents for monthly Arkansas Legislative Council meetings and other public meetings; Assist with daily bill review during legislative sessions, including printing bills and amendments, assigning bills for review, tracking legislation, and generating reports; Review agendas for local governing bodies regularly and identify any items of possible interest to the University and provide those to VCUA; Maintain office supplies; Carryout annual inventory tracking for University Affairs; Prepare email, mail, and text message invitations for events or programs; Prepare agendas for campus visits; Organize filing system and maintain all University Affairs files; Ensure accurate contact database management through quarterly reviews and updates of stakeholder information; Add contact information to database as necessary; Perform other duties as assigned. Finance and Purchasing Handle routine purchasing and transfers for University Affairs; Maintain P-Card for purchasing; Responsible for record-keeping and transaction verifications; Process accounts payable tasks and payment requests in FFTA and Workday; Perform other support duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Ability to multitask, prioritize, and manage multiple projects, including assisting with special events; Demonstrated skill at collaborating with various internal and external roles serving different organizational missions; Aptitude for internalizing policies and procedures concerning day-to-day operations of UA Little Rock; Proficient in use of technology and software applications, including Microsoft Office and Gmail; Familiarity with Workday, or similar enterprise-level planning solution; Ability to represent University Affairs with a high degree of professionalism over the phone and in-person; Ability to plan, organize, and coordinate activities, resources, and materials associated with the needs of University Affairs; Ability to work well with individuals at all levels of the university and with external constituents; Ability to operate a motor vehicle. Additional Information: Salary Information: $35,568 Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Emily Cox Vice Chancellor for University Affairs ecox@ualr.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Financial Credit Check, Motor Vehicle Reports Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Repetitive Motion, Standing Occasional Physical Activity: Walking Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Extra-Help--Programming-Support_R0086731": {"title": "Extra Help/ Programming Support", "description": "Start date: 2026-06-15\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Staff - Clerical Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Little Rock The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is a metropolitan research university that provides an accessible, quality education through flexible learning and unparalleled internship opportunities. At UA Little Rock, we prepare our more than 8,900 students to be innovators and responsible leaders in their fields. Committed to its metropolitan research university mission, UA Little Rock is a driving force in Little Rock's thriving cultural community and a major component of the city and state's growing profile as a regional leader in research, technology transfer, economic development, and job creation. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . Department: English Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: This position will provide extra help for School of Literary and Performing Arts programming and events. This position is governed by state and federal law and agency/institution policy. Qualifications: Required Education and/or Experience: High School Diploma Job Duties and Responsibilities: Work with the School directors or their delegates to provide support for programming and events Other duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Adequate computer skills; Knowledge of basic grammar. Knowledge of computers & software applications. Ability to communicate both orally & in writing. Additional Information: Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: None Optional Documents: Resume Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Kris McAbee, Director, kxmcabee@ualr.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: No Background Check Required The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Sitting, Standing, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Grasping, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding Occasional Physical Activity: Lifting, Repetitive Motion Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Extra-Help-Police-Officer_R0086937": {"title": "Extra Help/Police Officer", "description": "Start date: 2026-06-15\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: DNU - Public Safety (Inactive) Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Little Rock The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is a metropolitan research university that provides an accessible, quality education through flexible learning and unparalleled internship opportunities. At UA Little Rock, we prepare our more than 8,900 students to be innovators and responsible leaders in their fields. Committed to its metropolitan research university mission, UA Little Rock is a driving force in Little Rock's thriving cultural community and a major component of the city and state's growing profile as a regional leader in research, technology transfer, economic development, and job creation. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . Department: Public Safety Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Extra Help/Police Officer is responsible for the enforcement of traffic, criminal laws and parking regulations. This position is governed by law enforcement standards, state and federal laws, and agency/institution policy. Qualifications: Required Education and experience The formal education equivalent of a high school diploma; Must possess a valid drivers license; Muse be certified by the Arkansas Law Enforcement Certification Training in accordance with ACA 12-9-106, an approved law enforcement training academy. Job Duties and Responsibilities Patrol assigned areas to detect and prevent crimes, enforce traffic laws, recognize parking violations, issue traffic citations, and identify safety hazards and violators; Perform security checks of campus buildings; Conduct investigations of crimes, accidents, and reports incidents committed on campus; Monitor security and fire panel for security and fire detection, assist with checking the alarm systems and emergency power supply, and inspect and maintain fire extinguishers; Arrest violators write incident reports, and testify in court, as required; Direct traffic during periods of high density to facilitate smooth flow; Respond to alarm, call for assistance, check for locked or unlocked buildings and offices, as necessary, and assist stranded motorists and others in need of assistance; Performs other duties as assigned.\u2002 Must maintain ACIC (Arkansas Crime Information Center) class one certification. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Knowledge of general law enforcement methods and techniques; Ability to direct traffic and to maintain order; Ability to prepare reports of incidents and accidents; Ability to communicate orally and in writing; Ability to operate motor vehicles used in patrol duties. Additional Information: Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Physical, Criminal Background Check, Motor Vehicle Reports Check, Sex Offender Registry, and Substance Abuse Testing Salary Information: 15.00 an hour Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Andrea Robinson Police Services Manager 501-916-5308 All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Driving, Hearing Frequent Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Climbing, Lifting, Pulling, Reaching Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Cossatot-Community-College-of-the-University-of-Arkansas/Cybersecurity-Artificial-Intelligence-Instructor_R0087023": {"title": "Cybersecurity/Artificial Intelligence Instructor", "description": "Start date: 2026-06-11\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Faculty - Non-Tenure Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: Cossatot Community College of the University of Arkansas Cossatot Community College of the University of Arkansas (UA Cossatot) began in DeQueen, Arkansas in 1975 as an Arkansas Vocational-Technical School, designed to provide relevant workforce training for four counties in southwest Arkansas. Fast forward to now where UA Cossatot has four vibrant campuses and over 1500 students learning in a variety of for-credit disciplines plus a host of area industry employees sharpening their skills through our workforce training programs. UA Cossatot prides itself on a safe work environment, where all employees undergo rigorous background checks and are welcomed to the college with an abundance of hands-on orientations to their positions. UA Cossatot also embraces Continuous Quality Improvement (CQI) where everything we do is measured and analyzed to ensure we are giving students the very best we have to offer. CQI involves all employees and completes a cycle that starts with the strategic plan and ends with an Institutional Effectiveness Evaluation. It's okay to brag a little when you work for UA Cossatot!Cossatot Community College of the University o Arkansas is an NCA-accredited two-year institution affiliated with the University of Arkansas System with Campuses in De Queen, Nashville, Ashdown, and Lockesburg Arkansas. The Colleges designated service area includes Sevier, Little River, Howard and Pike counties.\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please submit a request via the OEOC website: \u00a0Applicants are required to submit a request for each position to which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at (870) 584-1104. Department: General Education Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Cybersecurity/Artificial Intelligence Instructor will teach a combination of at least five in-person and/or online courses per semester to both secondary and/or post-secondary students; develop curriculum and instructional materials for courses as needed; evaluate student performance by following UAC\u2019s assessment plan; engage with business and industry representatives; facilitate and maintain relationships with other colleges within the CyberLearn consortium; participate in grant writing and administration; advise program students; and attend recruiting events. This is a full-time, on-campus position requiring 30 hours per week, typically Monday through Thursday, with occasional Friday meetings. Some travel is required. Qualifications: \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Bachelor\u2019s degree in cybersecurity, computer science, or related field with at least 5 years of in-field experience OR Master's degree in cybersecurity, computer science, or related field. \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Previous teaching experience preferred. Additional Information: All applications must include a cover letter, an updated resume, copies of certifications held (if any), and unofficial transcripts.\u00a0 Applications received without the required documents will be incomplete and will not be considered for the position. Salary Information: $58,000 to $68,000 annual salary; plus an excellent benefits package Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Resume, Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: All applications must include a cover letter, an updated resume, copies of certifications held (if any), and unofficial transcripts. Applications received without the required documents will be incomplete and will not be considered for the position. Recruitment Contact Information: Kelly Plunk, Director of Human Resources, (870) 584-1104 or kplunk@cccua.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Child Maltreatment, Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry Cossatot Community College of the University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Reaching, Repetitive Motion Frequent Physical Activity: Standing, Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAM--McGehee-Campus/Associate-Vice-Chancellor-of-Student-Services_R0086667-1": {"title": "Associate Vice Chancellor of Student Services", "description": "Start date: 2026-06-11\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Management - Student Affairs Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Monticello UAM, one of twenty campuses of the University of Arkansas System, is located in southeastern Arkansas in the beautiful timberlands, rich in outdoor recreation activities, and approximately 100 miles south of Little Rock. UAM is a comprehensive, residential and commuter, undergraduate institution also offering selected master\u2019s degree programs. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please submit a request via the OEOC website: \u00a0Applicants are required to submit a request for each position to which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 870-460-1422 . Department: College of Technology-McGehee Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Director of Student Services will provide strategic leadership and operational oversight of student-facing functions at UAM\u2013CTM. Specific duties include, but are not limited to: \u2022 Recruit and retain students for technical programs and Associate of Applied Science degree offerings, with emphasis on underrepresented and non-traditional populations \u2022 Guide students through admissions and financial aid processes, including the development and processing of student contracts with TAA, WIA, HDC, and other financial assistance providers \u2022 Assist students with course registration, including evening and night registrations; establish and maintain accurate student records in accordance with institutional and regulatory requirements \u2022 Enforce and monitor student services policies and procedures; support and monitor established retention activities \u2022 Compile and analyze data for student services reports; assist with conducting completer/graduate and employer follow-up surveys to inform program effectiveness \u2022 Coordinate and assist with activities and events of student organizations; support scheduling and administering of admissions-related testing \u2022 Serve on institutional committees as assigned; develop and disseminate news articles and promotional/recruitment materials \u2022 Participate in ongoing professional development activities aligned with best practices in community and technical college student services \u2022 Supervise bookstore operations and employees; perform other duties as assigned by the Vice Chancellor This is a full-time administrative position responsible for overseeing comprehensive student services operations across UAM\u2013CTM\u2019s technical education programs. The Director plays a pivotal role in advancing student access, persistence, and success while supporting institutional compliance, accreditation, and workforce development goals. Qualifications: A master\u2019s degree in education, higher education administration, student affairs, or a closely related field is required. Relevant work experience in a post-secondary or technical education environment is strongly preferred. Successful candidates will demonstrate: Proficient computer skills, including student information systems and data management platforms Strong interpersonal and written communication skills with the ability to engage diverse stakeholder groups Demonstrated ability to work collaboratively with staff, faculty, administrators, and students Willingness and availability to work evenings and weekends as required for promotional, recruitment, and college events Experience managing Perkins V federal funds and navigating related compliance, reporting, and audit processes is highly preferred Additional Information: Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience. Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Mr. Steven Jossell, Vice Chancellor UAM COT-McGehee 1609 East Ash Street McGehee, AR 71664 Phone{870)-460-2101 email: JossellS@uamont.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Assistant-Professor-of-Social-Work_R0086778": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Social Work", "description": "Start date: 2026-06-11\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Faculty - Tenure/Tenure Track Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Academic Term (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Little Rock The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is a metropolitan research university that provides an accessible, quality education through flexible learning and unparalleled internship opportunities. At UA Little Rock, we prepare our more than 8,900 students to be innovators and responsible leaders in their fields. Committed to its metropolitan research university mission, UA Little Rock is a driving force in Little Rock's thriving cultural community and a major component of the city and state's growing profile as a regional leader in research, technology transfer, economic development, and job creation. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . Department: School of Social Work Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Assistant Professor of Social Work teaches in both the graduate and undergraduate social work programs, advises BSW and MSW students, and maintains an active agenda of scholarship and or research, which includes social work-based research/training projects and ongoing scholarly publications. Additionally, value is placed on participation in community service at the local, state, and national levels. Grant-funded research is encouraged and supported by the university. This position is governed by state and federal laws, and agency/institution policy. Qualifications: Required Education and/or Experience: MSW from a CSWE-accredited School of Social Work; Doctoral degree in Social Work or a closely related field (ABD considered). Preferred Education and/or Experience:\u00a0 At least two (2) years of social work practice experience; Prior teaching experience in higher education with the ability to teach across the curriculum; Online teaching experience; LMSW or LCSW (or LCSW eligible if not currently licensed in Arkansas). Job Duties and Responsibilities: Teach BSW and/or MSW classes each semester; Provide service to the School; Keep course content timely and in line with accreditation standards; Engage in scholarship sufficient to meet requirements for promotion, tenure, or other advancements, as appropriate for the rank; Engage in service at the university, community, and professional levels sufficient to meet requirements for promotion, tenure, or other advancements, as appropriate for the rank; Respond to inquiries regarding the designated program(s); Monitor student progress through the program(s) and adjust degree plans as necessary; Performs other duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Computer literacy and practical knowledge of current technology;\u00a0 Strong commitment to effective teaching;\u00a0 Ability to teach introductory and advanced-level classes; Knowledge of social work history, theory, and practice concepts. Additional Information: Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Curriculum Vitae, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Statement of Research Philosophy, Statement of Teaching Philosophy Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Please also include a Service Philosophy. Recruitment Contact Information: Jacqueline Burse - jrburse@ualr.edu Lindsay Ruhr - lrruhr@ualr.edu Theresa Flowers - tdflowers@ualr.edu Latisha Young - llyoung@ualr.edu Esaa Samarah - esamarahsama@ualr.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting, Standing, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Fayetteville/Investigations---Differential-Response-Practice-Coach--Based-in-Fayetteville-_R0086737-1": {"title": "Investigations & Differential Response Practice Coach (Based in Fayetteville)", "description": "Start date: 2026-06-10\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Professional Staff - Support Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Little Rock The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is a metropolitan research university that provides an accessible, quality education through flexible learning and unparalleled internship opportunities. At UA Little Rock, we prepare our more than 8,900 students to be innovators and responsible leaders in their fields. Committed to its metropolitan research university mission, UA Little Rock is a driving force in Little Rock's thriving cultural community and a major component of the city and state's growing profile as a regional leader in research, technology transfer, economic development, and job creation. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . Department: MidSouth Department's Website: midsouth.ualr.edu Summary of Job Duties: THIS POSITION IS BASED IN FAYETTEVILLE. The Investigations Practice Coach will provide coaching to all newly hired Social Services Specialists and Social Services Supervisors/Experts assigned to an Investigations or Differential Response Unit of the Division of Children and Family Services. The Investigations Practice Coach will provide coaching focused on the Division of Children and Family Services Policy and Internal Procedures and aligned with the Division\u2019s practice model. The Investigations Practice Coach will work with the Investigations Coaching Coordinator, MidSOUTH training staff, DCFS staff, University Partnership staff, and other stakeholders to coordinate and facilitate the statewide training and professional development as outlined in the Investigations Practice Coach Guidebook. This position is directly responsible to the Investigations Coaching Coordinator. This is a full-time, annually renewed grant-funded position. Extensive travel is required. This position is governed by state and federal laws, and agency/institution policy. Qualifications: Required Education and/or Experience: Bachelor\u2019s Degree plus one (1) year of professional experience with children and families; Professional Experience in mentoring, teaching, or training. Preferred Education and/or Experience: Master\u2019s Degree in Social Work or related field; Professional Experience with child maltreatment assessments; Experience and training in curriculum development and training delivery; Professional experience with\u00a0the Arkansas Division of Children and Family Services. Job Duties and Responsibilities: Coaching of Division of Children and Family Services Staff: Provide coaching of newly hired Social Services Specialists and Social Services Supervisors/Experts assigned to an Investigations or Differential Response Unit in the applicable DCFS area; Responsible for field coordination of all training activities in their assigned regional training area, including shadowing home visits and investigations; Attend Training of Trainers, DCFS mandatory training, and continuing education workshops when relevant to the position; Provide training or assistance with new staff training or continuing education as requested; Provide additional training as requested in designated areas. Collaboration: \u00a0 Work collaboratively with MidSOUTH training staff, DCFS staff, University Partnership staff, and other stakeholders; Coordinate and facilitate communication with assigned DCFS area; Attend quarterly academic partnership meetings; Participate in DCFS workgroups when requested. Record Keeping and Maintenance: Maintain a monthly record of coaching activities and staff/university partnership contacts; Responsible for the timely completion of coaching-related assessments and surveys; Maintain entry of timely documentation within two working days of any coaching activities; Perform other duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills, & Abilities: Ability to travel extensively in the state, which will include overnight stays; Ability to work a flexible schedule, which may include nights and weekends; Possess exemplary public speaking and interpersonal skills; Ability to use customer service initiatives for clients and the campus community; Ability to work independently; Ability to meet multiple program deadlines, and manage multiple tasks; Experience using Microsoft Office Suite, Google Applications, and Teams; Possess a valid driver\u2019s license and dependable transportation; Ability to maintain a monthly record of contacts; Knowledge of the Arkansas Child Welfare System; Ability to train others. Additional Information: Salary Information: $52,500-$55,500 Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume, Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Mary Tillman, Admin Support Manager, mjtillman@midsouth.ualr.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Child Maltreatment, Criminal Background Check, Motor Vehicle Reports Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting, Standing Frequent Physical Activity: Driving, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Standing, Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Lifting, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Repetitive Motion Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAM--Monticello-Campus/Non-Student-Extra-Help--Kids--University-_R0086812-2": {"title": "Non-Student Extra Help (Kids' University)", "description": "Start date: 2026-06-09\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Staff - Clerical Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Monticello UAM, one of twenty campuses of the University of Arkansas System, is located in southeastern Arkansas in the beautiful timberlands, rich in outdoor recreation activities, and approximately 100 miles south of Little Rock. UAM is a comprehensive, residential and commuter, undergraduate institution also offering selected master\u2019s degree programs. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please submit a request via the OEOC website: \u00a0Applicants are required to submit a request for each position to which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 870-460-1422 . Department: Education Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: TBD Qualifications: TBD Additional Information: Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: None Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Rebecca Newton, Director of Kids' University newtonr@uamont.edu 870-460-1596 All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Crouching, Feeling, Kneeling, Lifting, Reaching, Repetitive Motion, Standing, Stooping, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Crouching, Feeling, Lifting, Reaching, Standing, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Climbing Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/CORE-Research-Assistant---Extra-Help-Assistant-1_R0085871-2": {"title": "CORE Research Assistant / Extra Help Assistant-1", "description": "Start date: 2026-06-09\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Clerical Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Little Rock The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is a metropolitan research university that provides an accessible, quality education through flexible learning and unparalleled internship opportunities. At UA Little Rock, we prepare our more than 8,900 students to be innovators and responsible leaders in their fields. Committed to its metropolitan research university mission, UA Little Rock is a driving force in Little Rock's thriving cultural community and a major component of the city and state's growing profile as a regional leader in research, technology transfer, economic development, and job creation. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . Department: CORE Center - Undergraduates and Graduates Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Cyberspace Operations Research and Education (CORE) Center at the University of Arkansas at Little Rock is seeking Cybersecurity Research Assistant candidates to support ongoing research and educational initiatives in cybersecurity. The primary responsibility of an Cybersecurity Researcher is to provide professional-level support related to research and creative activities under the direct supervision of a faculty member, including data collection, cybersecurity initiatives, and other tasks as assigned. Students are expected to have an adequate background in foundational IT knowledge, hands-on technical skills, basic security principles or digital workflows. The position can be extended to future semesters. This position is governed by state and federal laws, and agency/institution policy. Qualifications: Qualifications: \u00a0 Required Education and/or Experience:\u00a0 High School Diploma\u00a0 Preferred Education and/or Experience: \u00a0 If a current student, overall GPA 3.0 or higher;\u00a0 Bachelor's Degree in Cybersecurity, Computer Science, or a related field;\u00a0 At least 1 year of work experience in a computer science or cybersecurity field;\u00a0 Completion of a comprehensive cybersecurity course or equivalent experience.\u00a0 Job Duties and Responsibilities: \u00a0 Participate in and contribute to cybersecurity research projects, including threat hunting and application development;\u00a0 Participate in Cybersecurity Clinic initiatives, projects, and other related tasks;\u00a0 Familiarity with resources pertaining to area of expertise;\u00a0 This position will also be responsible for other duties as assigned by supervising faculty, including but not limited to the preparation of research materials, providing editing assistance, and reviewing materials for errors or inconsistencies;\u00a0 During work hours an employee should be reachable by work channels (email, phone, text) and responsible for timely response;\u00a0 Assist with peer learning and collaborative student projects in cybersecurity practices and research techniques;\u00a0 Assist in the development and presentation of research findings at academic or industry events;\u00a0\u00a0 Must notify supervising faculty when circumstances prevent the employee from carrying out job responsibilities.\u00a0 This is an in-person role. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: \u00a0 Excellent verbal and written communication skills;\u00a0 Ability to work effectively both independently and as part of a team;\u00a0 Foundational knowledge of cybersecurity principles, basic computer systems, common cyber threat awareness, and security controls.\u00a0\u00a0 Follow instructions well and assiduously;\u00a0 Ability to use critical thinking and problem solving skills;\u00a0 Ability to adapt to stay current as threats, technology, and defenses evolve.\u00a0\u00a0 Understand situational awareness of environment and system interdependencies.\u00a0\u00a0 Ability to analyze data to identify trends, anomalies, or potential threats.\u00a0 Ability to approach security holistically, understanding how people, processes, and technology interact.\u00a0\u00a0 Accept constructive feedback and implement it effectively.\u00a0\u00a0 Additional Information: Salary Information: $15.00 Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Raney Anderson, CORE Operations Manager, 501-916-3983, randerson@ualr.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: No Background Check Required The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Sitting, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Sitting, Talking Occasional Physical Activity: Lifting, Sitting, Walking Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/North-Little-Rock/Non-Credit-Adjunct--Business-and-Industry-Center_R0086719": {"title": "Non-Credit Adjunct- Business and Industry Center", "description": "Start date: 2026-06-08\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/30/2026 Type of Position: Adjunct Faculty Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Less than Annual Appointment (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas Pulaski Technical College University of Arkansas - Pulaski Technical College at North Little Rock is an integral part of the Arkansas Technical and Community College System maintained by the State of Arkansas. The college is governed by the University of Arkansas System Board of Trustees and a seven-member Board of Visitors and derives its support largely from student tuition and fees and legislative appropriations. UA - Pulaski Tech, a comprehensive two-year college, offers associate degree and certificate programs for students who plan to transfer to four-year colleges and universities and/or for career preparation and advancement. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply link/button. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at (501) 812-2839. Department: BIC Instructors Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The available part time adjunct faculty position will effectively teach non-credit courses in their designated field of expertise. Daily tasks may include but not limited to: \u2022 Teach non-credit classes \u2022 Adhere to safety standards in the lab area \u2022 Attend virtual and/or face-to-face meetings as needed. \u2022 Assist with completing required student documents including sign-in sheets, etc. \u2022 Other duties as assigned Qualifications: Required Qualifications: \u00a0 Minimum 2 years experience in field of expertise Preferred Qualifications: \u00a0 Teaching experience preferred. Additional Information: Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume, Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants Recruitment Contact Information: Human Resources humanresources@uaptc.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Motor Vehicle Reports Check, Sex Offender Registry University of Arkansas - Pulaski Technical College is committed to providing a safe campus community. Title IX protects the college community from sexual harassment in a school's education programs and activities. This means that Title IX protects the college community in connection with all academic, educational, extracurricular, athletic, and other programs of the school, whether those programs take place in a school's facilities, in college transportation, at a class or training program sponsored by the school at another location, or elsewhere. \u00a0 We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Feeling, Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Repetitive Motion, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Balancing, Crawling, Crouching, Kneeling Occasional Physical Activity: Stooping Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Fayetteville-AR/Extra-Help-Assistant--Child-Care-Aide_R0052745": {"title": "Extra Help Assistant- Child Care Aide (Current and Anticipated Future Openings)", "description": "Start date: 2026-06-03\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com, then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at all University of Arkansas institutions will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students.\u201d University of Arkansas, Fayetteville students will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Student Jobs at UAF.\u201d All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. Closing Date: Type of Position: Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas, Fayetteville Founded in 1871, the University of Arkansas is a land grant institution, classified by the Carnegie Foundation among the nation\u2019s top 2 percent of universities with the highest level of research activity. The University of Arkansas works to advance the state and build a better world through education, research, and outreach by providing transformational opportunities and skills, fostering a welcoming climate, and nurturing creativity, discovery, and the spread of new ideas and innovations. The University of Arkansas campus is located in Fayetteville, a welcoming community ranked as one of the best places to live in the U.S. The growing region surrounding Fayetteville is home to numerous Fortune 500 companies and one of the nation\u2019s strongest economies. Northwest Arkansas is also quickly gaining a national reputation for its focus on the arts and overall quality of life. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10% of employee salary. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions, you should review before applying for the opening. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process, please submit a request via the Disability Accommodations | OEOC | University of Arkansas (uark.edu) : Request an Accommodation. Appli\u00adcants are required to submit a request for each position of which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 479.575.5351. Department: Jean Tyson Child Development Study Center Operations B Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The role of the childcare aide/substitute is to supplement the quality of the child care program by assisting in the classroom, kitchen, and administrative offices when needed. The childcare aide/substitute will assist the lead and assistant educators in all tasks related to managing the classroom which include but are not limited to: providing positive and effective guidance to children; comforting children; redirecting unsafe activities to more productive activities; actively engaging with children by talking, listening, and playing with children; assisting teachers in supervision of children during indoor and outdoor play; assisting with all classroom routines including cleaning classroom areas and materials, toileting/diapering, hand washing, and serving meals; conducting activities with children that are prepared by educators; following all Center's policies and standards. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications:\u00a0 The formal education equivalent of a high school diploma At least one year of experience working with young children between the ages of 8 weeks and 5 years Available for regularly scheduled shifts between the hours of 7:30 a.m. and 5:30 p.m. Monday through Friday Available for on-call shifts to meet the\u00a0needs of unexpected absences or illnesses Must commit to a minimum of 10 hours a week Preferred Qualifications: Higher education or training\u00a0in Early Childhood Education or closely related field At least two or more years working with young children Experience working in a licensed and/or accredited child care center Additional Information: Salary Information: $11.00 Required Documents to Apply: List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Recruitment Contact Information: Shelley McNally, smcnally@uark.edu; Executive Director of Education Programs All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Special Instructions to Applicants: Please provide 3 professional references and 2 personal. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas seeks to attract, develop and retain high quality faculty, staff and administrators that consistently display practices and behaviors to advance a culture that embeds equal opportunity, educational excellence and unparalleled access for all. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All Application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Helena-Campus/Dance--part-time_R0086599": {"title": "Dance, part-time", "description": "Start date: 2026-06-03\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Staff (Non-Classified) Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Evening Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: Phillips Community College of the University of Arkansas The first community college established in Arkansas, Phillips Community College of the University of Arkansas (PCCUA) is a multi-campus, two-year college serving Eastern Arkansas. PCCUA has academic, occupational/technical and continuing education programs and offers over 25 associate degree programs with campuses in DeWitt, Helena-W. Helena and Stuttgart. Thank you for your interest, and we hope you\u2019ll be joining our Ridge Runner family soon! Below you will find the details for the position as well as any specific application requirements you should review before applying for this opening. To apply for this position, please click the Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process, please call Human Resources at (870) 338-6474, ext. 1271. Department: Community Service Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Extra Help Assistant is responsible for assisting dance students (preschool, elementary, etc.) This position is governed by state and federal laws and agency policy. Qualifications: Dance background. Excellent interpersonal communication skills. Must be punctual. Able to work a flexible schedule Additional Information: Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: None Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Wandra Williams All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check For general application assistance, or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at (870) 338-6474, ext. 1271. PCCUA is committed to providing a safe campus community. We will conduct criminal background checks and a sex offender registry check for applicants seeking employment. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Balancing, Feeling, Hearing, Kneeling, Lifting, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Repetitive Motion, Sitting, Standing, Stooping, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Room-Service-Ambassador_R0055496": {"title": "Room Service Ambassador", "description": "Start date: 2026-06-02\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/30/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: OPS | NUTRI Patient Food Call Center Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Room Service Ambassador is responsible for assisting patients with menu selections, and ensuring the patients receive meals and nourishments in accordance with physician prescribed diets, food allergies, and preferences. The Room Service Ambassador provides excellent customer service to ensure the department\u2019s goals are met. Qualifications: Minimum: High School diploma/GED plus computer. Basic keyboard skills and telephone etiquette skills. Preferred: Experience in a food service, customer services or patient care setting. Responsibilities: Provides an excellent customer service experience when the patients are making menu selections. Take food orders over the phone. Make selections into the electronic meal selection, and updating and recording patient information. Corrects menu choices based on meal patterns, allergies and patient preferences. Trouble-shoots issues at the point of service affecting patient satisfaction with the food service. May perform other duties as assigned . Additional Information: Stand Occasionally Sit Continuously Walk Occasionally Bend, crawl, crouch, kneel, stoop or reach overhead Occasionally Lift and carry weight 10 lbs or less Push and pull weight 10 lbs or less Use hands to touch, handle or feel Occasionally Talk Continuously Hear Continuously Taste or smell Never Read, concentrate, think analytically Continuously Physical Environment Inside Medical Facility Environment Noise Level Moderate Visual Requirements Color discrimination Depth perception Far visual acuity Near visual acuity Hazards None Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience. Required Documents to Apply: List of three Professional References (name, email, business title) Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Dietetic-Technician_R0055497-1": {"title": "Dietetic Technician", "description": "Start date: 2026-06-02\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/30/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: OPS | NUTRI Patient Food PRI Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: **Position is considered Essential Personnel** The Dietetic Technician is responsible for daily routines and functions in order to see that all patients receive meals in a timely fashion and the meals meet the Physician order and patient preferences.\u00a0 The Dietetic Technician Level I is responsible for assisting in planning and implementing nutritional programs and services in the hospital.\u00a0 Qualifications: Minimum: High School diploma/GED plus 2 years of experience in customer service. Ideal candidate is team-oriented and has great customer service skills. Must be able to work during Inclement Weather. Must be able to work rotating Weekends and Holidays. Preferred:\u00a0 Experience in a food service or patient care setting. Responsibilities: Assisting patients and ensures that patients receive meals and nourishments in accordance to current diet orders and food allergens. Proactively seeks patients\u2019 food orders for those who did not call the call center, may have difficulty speaking, hearing or seeing, and those that may need language assistance. Takes food orders, promptly and accurately within the constraints of the diet order, at the bedside with IPads. Makes selections into the electronic meal selection on room service assist and house selection criteria. Updates and records patient information from the electronic medical record, correct menu choices based on meal patterns, allergies and patient preferences while alerting the Lead Room Service Ambassadors or Supervisors to any issues. Serves trays in a timely manner according to the departmental policies and procedures. Accurately identifies patient and appropriate tray by using two patient identifiers. Assesses and trouble-shoots issues at the point of service that may impact patient satisfaction. Responds to patient requests by communicating with appropriate staff. Retrieves trays from assigned patient units after the patients have finished their meals. Prepares beverages following thickened policies when required. Stocks coolers, freezers and dry storage items in the patient food area. Stores supplies and food according to department standards. Ensures FIFO, proper temperatures, and properly labeling standards are applied Follows cleaning checklist and maintains a clean and organized work area Greets customers in a courteous manner, identifying themselves by name and department, maintains eye contact and offers assistance. Serves as a role model for other employees by modeling appropriate behaviors including taking initiative to cross-train and assist others, exhibiting flexibility, and maintaining a focus on customer service.\u00a0 Demonstrates integrity, compassion, respect, and a positive attitude to co- workers, patients, visitors, and UAMS staff regardless of race, gender, sexual orientation, ethnicity, religious belief, age and/or disability. Completes other duties as assigned by management. Additional Information: Stand Continuously Sit Never Walk Frequently Bend, crawl, crouch, kneel, stoop or reach overhead Frequently Lift and carry weight 26 - 50 lbs Push and pull weight 26 - 50 lbs Use hands to touch, handle or feel Continuously Talk Continuously Hear Continuously Taste or smell Occasionally Read, concentrate, think analytically Continuously Physical Environment Inside Medical Environment Noise Level Loud Hazards \u00a0 Chemicals Electrical Fumes/Gases/Odors Heavy Machinery Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience. Required Documents to Apply: List of three Professional References (name, email, business title) Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Fort-Smith/Occupational-Therapist--Kids-First-Fort-Smith_R0083500-1": {"title": "Occupational Therapist- Kids First Fort Smith", "description": "Start date: 2026-06-01\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 08/01/2026 Type of Position: Other Health Care - Rehabilitation Therapy Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: COM | Peds Kids First Fort Smith Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: *This position is located in Fort Smith, Arkansas* KIDS FIRST serves children with special healthcare needs ranging in age from six weeks to five years. In our pediatric day healthcare clinics, children diagnosed as having a medical condition known to place them at risk for developmental delays and disabilities receive intensive intervention. The Occupational Therapist works as a member of an interdisciplinary team to provide the evidence-based best practice evaluation and therapy techniques for the birth to 5 population with a variety of fine motor delays/disorders at UAMS Kids First clinic. May provide supervision to occupational therapy assistants. Travel to other KIDS FIRST locations may be required. Qualifications: Master's degree in Occupational Therapy or \u00a0Bachelor's degree in Occupational Therapy plus two (2)\u00a0years of experience in Occupational Therapy required. Certified by the National Board for Certification of Occupational Therapy (NBCOT) or eligible to apply for the examination. Current Arkansas Occupational Therapy License or eligible to obtain license within one (1) month of date of hire. Knowledge, Skills &Abilities: Excellent communication skills with adults and children. Must have the ability to function as a health care team member and operate within an interprofessional team. Intermediate computer skills\u00a0(MS Office preferred). Additional Information: Responsibilities: Provides fine motor assessment and treatment using evidence-based techniques in a naturalistic, developmentally appropriate manner.\u00a0 Evaluates to determine fine motor skills, visual perceptual motor skills, sensory processing and self-help skills in addition to upper extremity strength, range of motion, muscle tone, dynamic sitting/standing balance for functional task and trunk stability using appropriate diagnostic instruments. \u00a0Also, determines the need for adaptive equipment and splinting needs. Reviews results of standardized scores along with informed clinical judgment and observations to make the correct diagnosis. Translates the obtained information into a professional, typed document along with treatment recommendations, developing appropriate goals and objectives as related to patient\u2019s needs. \u00a0 Confers with the Medical Director when necessary regarding said results/recommendations. Implements direct therapy for children, based upon findings using evidence-based techniques. Monitors progress and makes modifications to treatment plan as needed. Documents services provided in a professional, timely manner. Prepares and provides billing documents according to KIDS FIRST and Medicaid guidelines on a weekly basis. \u00a0 Verifies accuracy billing documents through careful review of progress notes, treatment room sign-out forms, and child\u2019s individual prescription requirements. Collaborates and communicates with families, other therapists, nurses, social workers, director, developmental staff, and contractors to provide the best quality of care and optimal outcomes for each child. Encourage families to take an active role in supporting their child\u2019s development using the principles of Family Centered Care. Supports the academic mission of the Kids First program. This includes participation in the training of students and pre-service professionals, education and outreach to stakeholders, families served, and community partners. \u00a0May include training and participation in research projects. Performs other duties as assigned. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: None Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status, Resume Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Adult Maltreatment, Child Maltreatment, Criminal Background Check, FBI Background Check This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Climbing, Crawling, Crouching, Feeling, Grasping, Reaching, Standing, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Lifting, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Talking Occasional Physical Activity: Sitting Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Occupational-Therapist--Kids-First-Little-Rock_R0083501-1": {"title": "Occupational Therapist- Kids First Little Rock", "description": "Start date: 2026-06-01\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 08/01/2026 Type of Position: Other Health Care - Rehabilitation Therapy Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: COM | Peds Kids First Little Rock Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: *This position is located in Little Rock, Arkansas* KIDS FIRST serves children with special healthcare needs ranging in age from six weeks to five years. In our pediatric day healthcare clinics, children diagnosed as having a medical condition known to place them at risk for developmental delays and disabilities receive intensive intervention. The Occupational Therapist works as a member of an interdisciplinary team to provide the evidence-based best practice evaluation and therapy techniques for the birth to 5 population with a variety of fine motor delays/disorders at UAMS Kids First clinic. May provide supervision to occupational therapy assistants. Travel to other KIDS FIRST locations may be required. Qualifications: Master's degree in Occupational Therapy or \u00a0Bachelor's degree in Occupational Therapy plus two (2)\u00a0years of experience in Occupational Therapy required. Certified by the National Board for Certification of Occupational Therapy (NBCOT) or eligible to apply for the examination. Current Arkansas Occupational Therapy License or eligible to obtain license within one (1) month of date of hire. Knowledge, Skills &Abilities: Excellent communication skills with adults and children. Must have the ability to function as a health care team member and operate within an interprofessional team. Intermediate computer skills\u00a0(MS Office preferred). Additional Information: Responsibilities: Provides fine motor assessment and treatment using evidence-based techniques in a naturalistic, developmentally appropriate manner.\u00a0 Evaluates to determine fine motor skills, visual perceptual motor skills, sensory processing and self-help skills in addition to upper extremity strength, range of motion, muscle tone, dynamic sitting/standing balance for functional task and trunk stability using appropriate diagnostic instruments. \u00a0Also, determines the need for adaptive equipment and splinting needs. Reviews results of standardized scores along with informed clinical judgment and observations to make the correct diagnosis. Translates the obtained information into a professional, typed document along with treatment recommendations, developing appropriate goals and objectives as related to patient\u2019s needs. \u00a0 Confers with the Medical Director when necessary regarding said results/recommendations. Implements direct therapy for children, based upon findings using evidence-based techniques. Monitors progress and makes modifications to treatment plan as needed. Documents services provided in a professional, timely manner. Prepares and provides billing documents according to KIDS FIRST and Medicaid guidelines on a weekly basis. \u00a0 Verifies accuracy billing documents through careful review of progress notes, treatment room sign-out forms, and child\u2019s individual prescription requirements. Collaborates and communicates with families, other therapists, nurses, social workers, director, developmental staff, and contractors to provide the best quality of care and optimal outcomes for each child. Encourage families to take an active role in supporting their child\u2019s development using the principles of Family Centered Care. Supports the academic mission of the Kids First program. This includes participation in the training of students and pre-service professionals, education and outreach to stakeholders, families served, and community partners. \u00a0May include training and participation in research projects. Performs other duties as assigned. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: None Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status, Resume Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Adult Maltreatment, Annual TB Screening, Child Maltreatment, Criminal Background Check, FBI Background Check, Sex Offender Registry, Substance Abuse Testing This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Climbing, Crawling, Crouching, Feeling, Grasping, Reaching, Standing, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Lifting, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding Occasional Physical Activity: Sitting Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Security-and-Safety-Officer_R0078779-1": {"title": "Security and Safety Officer", "description": "Start date: 2026-05-28\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 09/28/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: OPS | Hospitality Svc PA Health Screeners Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Safety and Security Officer reports directly to the Supervisor of Safety and Security. This position is responsible for customer service, service recovery, security screening, weapon detection, and video surveillance systems monitoring. This position is also responsible for maintaining standards in accordance with all regulatory agencies. The Safety Security Officer will monitor for any safety issues while on foot patrol, responding to alarms, and assisting visitors and patients with guidance and requests. This position may assist Safety and Security Ambassadors' assignments as needed or assigned. Assignments may vary with increased security concerns within the UAMS system. Qualifications: Minimum: High school diploma / GED. Preferred: Associate or bachelor\u2019s degree in hospitality, Education, General Education, Management, Technical, Communication, Finance, Business. Additional Information: Performs safety screenings at the metal detector in the ED and weapon detection systems at various locations at entrances of UAMS. Safety and Security Officers will help with the effort to assure proper and efficient flow of visitors, patients and staff while monitoring the weapon detection equipment and persons entering UAMS at areas monitored by the weapon detection systems. Patrols on foot inside buildings while performing property checks on secure and high-risk areas of UAMS and having a visual presence of a security team throughout the facility, helping create a safer environment for staff, patients, and visitors. Assist with monitoring camera systems for safety and security concerns and reporting any suspicious activity to the UAMS Police Department. Fills in at the Information Desk in the main hospital during evening hours. Upon request, escorts employees and members of the campus population to their desired location. Escorts patients from the Outpatient Clinics (OPC) holding area to appointments. Responds to alarms as needed. Unlock buildings and offices as requested. Rotate areas of responsibility throughout each shift or as needed with other team members. Assist Safety and Security Ambassadors with assignments as needed or assigned. Crosstrain to work in all positions assigned. Perform other duties as assigned. Salary Information: Commensurate with experience Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAPBADMIAdministration-Building/MAINTENANCE-SPECIALIST-DRIVER-Extra-Help_R0085242": {"title": "MAINTENANCE SPECIALIST/DRIVER Extra Help", "description": "Start date: 2026-05-28\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Skilled Labor Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff The University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff is an 1890 Land-Grant HBCU with a diverse student population, competitive degree offerings and stellar faculty. For more than 140 years, the University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff has worked to create an environment that inculcates learning, growth and productivity while affording a basic need to its students \u2013 a chance to advance. The 15:1 student to teacher ratio makes it possible to maintain a learning environment with close interaction between students and faculty while challenging curricula encourage our students to seek and fulfill their potential. You can excel in your chosen field of study through a curriculum of \u00a0 Certificate and Associates degree programs,\u00a0 more than thirty\u00a0 Undergraduate programs, Master\u2019s degree programs and a Doctorate program in Aquaculture/Fisheries. You can also develop workplace readiness through internships, co-ops and fellowships in the U.S. and abroad. Out-of-class experiences and student involvement include more than 90 student organizations, an internationally renowned Vesper Choir, Marching Band, Concert Bands, Wind Symphony, nationally recognized debate team, award-winning theater department and accomplished athletic program. Though the main campus is in Pine Bluff, its reach is worldwide. UAPB has an extended campus in North Little Rock and offers as well as online courses. With the addition of the Arkansas Research and Education Optical Network (ARE-ON), students can engage in information exchange with others anywhere in the world. There are also Research and Extension offices in Lonoke, Newport and Lake Village and collaborations with other colleges and universities in the State through the National Science Foundation funded STEM (Science, Technology, Engineering and Mathematics) Academy. As the second oldest land-grant institution in the state of Arkansas, the mission of this No Excuse University remains the same \u2013 to provide a high quality, affordable education with a personal touch. We invite you to Become a Part of the Pride at the University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process and require reasonable accommodations, please contact Human Resources at 870.575.8400 . Department: Motor Pool Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Motor Coach Operator is responsible for operating UAPB Motor Coaches and driving cross-country (southeast region) to transport UAPB students faculty and staff. This position is governed by state and federal laws and UAPB policy. Qualifications: TYPICAL FUNCTIONS An Operator drives the motor coach safely, arrives at pickup location at assigned times, drives to the point of destination in a safe manner according to the schedule, adheres to traffic laws and DOT regulations, follows proper procedures when arriving at a location, maintains awareness of driving conditions and scans environment for possible safety hazards. \u00b7 Reviews the prior day\u2019s Driver Vehicle Inspection Report and conducts a comprehensive pre-trip inspection and post-trip inspection of the motor coach to ensure safe operating conditions. \u00b7 Inspects the inside and outside of the motor coach and brake system following a checklist, documents mechanical malfunctions or other motor coach problems on the proper form, verbally notifies the mechanic or supervisor of mechanical malfunctions if unable to safely operate the vehicle, receives notification from mechanic of action to take, and determines if the motor coach is safe for operation. \u00b7 Boards and deboards passengers, provide passenger pretrip safety announcements, and load passenger baggage into baggage compartment using proper lifting techniques. \u00b7 Responsible for enforcing the rules of the motor coach; make determination of whether incidents on the motor coach require unscheduled stops or the notification of law enforcement and consider welfare of all passengers. \u00b7 Passenger questions and respond to requests for assistance. \u00b7 Must provide positive customer service to passengers, act in a friendly and courteous manner and follow correct routes. \u00b7 Completes all required documentation and maintains driver logs according to DOT regulations and UAPB Policies. \u00b7 Coordinates any special requirements or considerations necessary for making the trip with appropriate personnel. \u00b7 Maintains records of bus use and travel logs, and prepares reports of operations. \u00b7 Attends driving courses as needed and/or required. \u00b7 Performs other duties as assigned. \u00b7 Maintains professional dress and grooming (uniforms will be provided). Additional Information: KNOWLEDGES, ABILITIES, AND SKILLS Ability to drive for periods up to 10 hours at a time. Ability to communicate in oral and written form. Skill in commercial bus or truck driving. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS The formal education equivalent of a high school diploma; plus 3-5 years of experience in cross-country commercial driving. \u00b7 CDL Class B or Class A \u00b7 Passenger Endorsement \u00b7 Must provide valid documentation of a Department of Transportation (DOT) medical examination. Salary Information: 12.39 - 24.34 USD Hourly Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Proof of Veteran Status, Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants (Please upload all required documents in the \"Resume\" attachment section of your application to be considered for this position) : Recruitment Contact Information: Sharron Williams, Employment Manager, 870-575-8403, williamssm@uapb.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: The University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff may conduct pre-employment background checks on certain positions for applicants being considered for employment. \u00a0 The background checks may include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. \u00a0 Required checks are identified in the position listing. \u00a0 A criminal background check or arrest pending adjudication information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absences of a relationship to the requirements of the position. \u00a0 Background check information will be used in a consistent, non-discriminatory manner consistent with the state and federal law. \u00a0 The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-Arkansas-at-Pine-Bluff/Transfer-Articulation-Specialist-1_R0086290-1": {"title": "Transfer Articulation Specialist-1", "description": "Start date: 2026-05-27\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Recruitment and Admissions Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff The University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff is an 1890 Land-Grant HBCU with a diverse student population, competitive degree offerings and stellar faculty. For more than 140 years, the University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff has worked to create an environment that inculcates learning, growth and productivity while affording a basic need to its students \u2013 a chance to advance. The 15:1 student to teacher ratio makes it possible to maintain a learning environment with close interaction between students and faculty while challenging curricula encourage our students to seek and fulfill their potential. You can excel in your chosen field of study through a curriculum of \u00a0 Certificate and Associates degree programs,\u00a0 more than thirty\u00a0 Undergraduate programs, Master\u2019s degree programs and a Doctorate program in Aquaculture/Fisheries. You can also develop workplace readiness through internships, co-ops and fellowships in the U.S. and abroad. Out-of-class experiences and student involvement include more than 90 student organizations, an internationally renowned Vesper Choir, Marching Band, Concert Bands, Wind Symphony, nationally recognized debate team, award-winning theater department and accomplished athletic program. Though the main campus is in Pine Bluff, its reach is worldwide. UAPB has an extended campus in North Little Rock and offers as well as online courses. With the addition of the Arkansas Research and Education Optical Network (ARE-ON), students can engage in information exchange with others anywhere in the world. There are also Research and Extension offices in Lonoke, Newport and Lake Village and collaborations with other colleges and universities in the State through the National Science Foundation funded STEM (Science, Technology, Engineering and Mathematics) Academy. As the second oldest land-grant institution in the state of Arkansas, the mission of this No Excuse University remains the same \u2013 to provide a high quality, affordable education with a personal touch. We invite you to Become a Part of the Pride at the University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process and require reasonable accommodations, please contact Human Resources at 870.575.8400 . Department: Registrar/Academic Records Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Transfer Articulation Specialist plays a critical role in the enrollment and retention of transfer students by evaluating and articulating incoming coursework for college transfer applicants. This position serves as a key liaison between Enrollment Management, Registrar\u2019s Office, Academic Departments, and Institutional partners to ensure accurate and timely evaluation of transcripts, maintenance of articulation agreements, and implementation of best practices in transfer credit equivalency. The specialist supports institutional efforts to build seamless pathways for transfer students and contributes to the institution\u2019s enrollment growth, student success, and degree completion goals. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Bachelor\u2019s degree from an accredited institution. \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 At least 2-3 years of experience in higher education, preferably in admissions, transfer evaluation, articulation, or student services. \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Demonstrated experience working with student information systems (e.g., Ellucians, Workday Student, Banner, PeopleSoft) and transfer credit systems (e.g., TES, DegreeWorks, CollegeSource, Workday Student). \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Knowledge of FERPA, accreditation standards, and articulation practices and policies. \u00a0 Preferred Qualifications: \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Master\u2019s degree in Higher Education, Student Affairs, Counseling, or related field. \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Experience working with community colleges or developing articulation agreements. \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Familiarity with statewide transfer frameworks. \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Strong analytical skills and attention to detail in reviewing curricula and transcripts. \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Demonstrated commitment to supporting diverse student populations, particularly first-generation and non-traditional transfer students. Additional Information: Salary Information: $45,000 - $52,000 Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants (Please upload all required documents in the \"Resume\" attachment section of your application to be considered for this position) : Recruitment Contact Information: Sharron Williams williamssm@uapb.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check The University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff may conduct pre-employment background checks on certain positions for applicants being considered for employment. \u00a0 The background checks may include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. \u00a0 Required checks are identified in the position listing. \u00a0 A criminal background check or arrest pending adjudication information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absences of a relationship to the requirements of the position. \u00a0 Background check information will be used in a consistent, non-discriminatory manner consistent with the state and federal law. \u00a0 The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Director-of-Counseling--Human-Performance--and-Rehabilitation_R0086237": {"title": "Director of Counseling, Human Performance, and Rehabilitation", "description": "Start date: 2026-05-27\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Chair Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Little Rock The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is a metropolitan research university that provides an accessible, quality education through flexible learning and unparalleled internship opportunities. At UA Little Rock, we prepare our more than 8,900 students to be innovators and responsible leaders in their fields. Committed to its metropolitan research university mission, UA Little Rock is a driving force in Little Rock's thriving cultural community and a major component of the city and state's growing profile as a regional leader in research, technology transfer, economic development, and job creation. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . Department: College of Business, Health, & Human Services Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: This position is a 12-month, tenured Associate or Full Professor position with qualifications and professional background in one of the programs that comprise the School of Counseling, Human Performance, and Rehabilitation. The Director is responsible for ensuring adherence to accreditation/assessment standards for all School programs. The Director will provide comprehensive management for the School, collaborate with College and University offices as necessary, and complete all necessary reporting. This is an in-person position that requires residency in the greater Little Rock area during employment. This position is governed by state and federal laws, and agency/institution policy. Qualifications: Required Education and or Experience: Terminal degree in one of the disciplines that comprises the School of Counseling, Human Performance, and Rehabilitation (Counseling, Health Education and Promotion, Interpretation/ASL, Communication Sciences and Disorders, Sports Management); Experience at the college/university-level in the teaching of a field of study that comprises the School of Counseling, Human Performance, and Rehabilitation; Experience with a learning management system (e.g., Blackboard Ultra). Preferred\u00a0Education and or Experience: Experience teaching across various modalities (e.g., face-to-face, online, and/or hybrid); Evidence of a commitment to working collegially;\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Training in specialty areas and teaching competency in areas that complement current faculty specialties in the School of Counseling, Human Performance, and Rehabilitation; Related professional memberships and evidence of active involvement in those organizations;\u00a0 Established record of conference presentations and publishing in peer-reviewed journals and/or books. Job Duties: Effectively managing and providing oversight of the unit and grant budget and ongoing reporting of unit financial status; Scheduling of all classes and confirmation that scheduled class times meet university minimum enrollment expectations and expected credit hour timeframes. This is to be done at the level of the director, not at the level of the coordinators or faculty;\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Planning equitable and full workloads for all full-time faculty in a manner that reflects fiscal responsibility, strategic planning, and the established workload policy. This is to be done at the level of the director, not at the level of the coordinators or faculty;\u00a0 Completing and submitting all university reports including, but not limited to: Instructional Unit Report, graduation/retention reports, annual reports; Establishing and maintaining of a systematic method of monitoring, evaluating and submitting required reports that meet college, state, and national accreditation and approval expectations and deadlines;\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Ensuring consistent availability and participation of full-time faculty in order to meet college, school, and student needs;\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Actively participate and assess student recruitment and retention initiatives, developing improvement plans as necessary; Establishing and maintaining a systematic program assessment that includes use of data (achievement of student learning outcomes, graduate and employer satisfaction, timely completion of dissertation and degree completions and other data needed to ensure program viability) for program improvement, viability, and streamlining needs; Annual reviewing of part- and full-time faculty in a manner that reflects objective analysis and consistency with rank expectations in the areas of teaching, research, and service;\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Perform other duties as required. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Exceptional skills in problem-solving, decision-making, time management, writing, as well as program planning, implementation, and evaluation; Knowledge of classroom instruction, curriculum development, and program evaluation;\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Effective in leading a team of faculty, support staff, and students; Collegial and cordial attitude toward interaction with colleagues, students, and staff;\u00a0 Ability to manage, motivate, and evaluate a diverse population of students; Demonstrable content knowledge of CACREP, CAEP, HLC, and other specialty accreditations; Self-motivated, responsible, and able to work with minimal direct supervision; Ability to serve effectively on committees;\u00a0 Ability to conduct research in a specialty area; Ability to engage with the local community. Additional Information: Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Curriculum Vitae, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Statement of Teaching Philosophy Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Matt Matusiak, Associate Dean, mmatusiak@ualr.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Financial Credit Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting, Talking Occasional Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting, Talking Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Stuttgart-Campus/Industrial-Technology-Instructor_R0086261": {"title": "Industrial Technology Instructor", "description": "Start date: 2026-05-27\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Faculty (Non-Classified) Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: Phillips Community College of the University of Arkansas The first community college established in Arkansas, Phillips Community College of the University of Arkansas (PCCUA) is a multi-campus, two-year college serving Eastern Arkansas. PCCUA has academic, occupational/technical and continuing education programs and offers over 25 associate degree programs with campuses in DeWitt, Helena-W. Helena and Stuttgart. Thank you for your interest, and we hope you\u2019ll be joining our Ridge Runner family soon! Below you will find the details for the position as well as any specific application requirements you should review before applying for this opening. To apply for this position, please click the Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process, please call Human Resources at (870) 338-6474, ext. 1271. Department: Workforce Training Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Development and delivery of manufacturing/processing credit and non-credit training programs that may include plant automation, mechanical systems maintenance, industrial safety, pump maintenance, hydraulics/pneumatics, welding, industrial electricity, industrial supervision, programmable logic controllers, etc. Performs other related responsibilities as required Qualifications: Able to work a flexible schedule that may include evening and weekends. Bachelor\u2019s degree in industrial technology or engineering technology is preferred.\u00a0 Strong organizational, computer, and interpersonal skills are a must.\u00a0 Prior teaching or training experience preferred.\u00a0 Industry maintenance certification a plus. Additional Information: Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Resume, Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Joe St. Columbia, Jr., JSColumbia@pccua.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Motor Vehicle Reports Check For general application assistance, or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at (870) 338-6474, ext. 1271. PCCUA is committed to providing a safe campus community. We will conduct criminal background checks and a sex offender registry check for applicants seeking employment. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Balancing, Climbing, Crawling, Crouching, Driving, Grasping, Hearing, Kneeling, Lifting, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Sharps, Sitting, Standing, Stooping, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Skilled-Tradesman--Locksmith_R0086149": {"title": "Skilled Tradesman -Locksmith", "description": "Start date: 2026-05-22\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Skilled Labor Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Little Rock The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is a metropolitan research university that provides an accessible, quality education through flexible learning and unparalleled internship opportunities. At UA Little Rock, we prepare our more than 8,900 students to be innovators and responsible leaders in their fields. Committed to its metropolitan research university mission, UA Little Rock is a driving force in Little Rock's thriving cultural community and a major component of the city and state's growing profile as a regional leader in research, technology transfer, economic development, and job creation. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . Department: Structural Services Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Locksmith is responsible for maintaining the University\u2019s campus-wide lock systems for all buildings to include inspection, installations, operations, and repairs of door hardware and locking systems. This position may also assist concerning issues with locking cabinet doors and file cabinets. All departments depend on the Locksmith to maintain the security of all campus buildings. In addition, because Facilities Management personnel interact with virtually every area of campus life, a pleasant relationship that is supportive of the Facilities Management objective is essential. To accomplish this objective, workers are occasionally required to perform work not related to their specific trade. This position is governed by state and federal laws and agency/institution policy. Qualifications: Required Education &/or Experience: The formal education equivalent of a high school diploma; Experience and/or training with repair and maintenance of locking devices shop maintenance, inventory, key production, re-keying, core replacement, etc., Possess a valid driver\u2019s license and have the ability to drive a vehicle. Other job-related education and/or experience may be substituted for all or part of these basic requirements, except for certification or license requirements. Preferred Education &/or Experience: Vocational locksmith training; Experience with Keystone, key management software; experience with OnGuard, access control management software; Experience with Workday; Experience working in Facilities Management. Job Duties & Responsibilities: Make recommendations as to the effectiveness and appropriateness of various types of locking devices, including researching new technologies; Work with the departments and assigned personnel to determine the best access and security needs for entry into buildings, offices, and other assigned areas; Maintain detailed records of the staff and locks they have access to; Track and distribute keys accurately; Verify all keys and other devices are returned to the University when staff terminates; Prepare locks as needed, including key locks, electronic locking systems, locking cabinets and file cabinets, and dial combinations locks; Code lock cores, operate key reproducing equipment, make keys, re-key locks for security purposes; Maintain records of keys and matching locks; Install new locks and door hardware as needed.\u00a0 This would include new constructions, remodel projects, breakage, etc.; Perform maintenance work on lock systems and door hardware as required; Repair and disassemble locks, and replace worn tumblers, springs, and other parts, as needed, including repairing and adjusting door-mounted closers and floor closers; Maintain the security and software updates of the computer systems, including floor plans, lock and key assignments, and electronic access control systems. Determine schedule of lock inspections and maintenance to ensure timely care of all locking systems campus-wide; Maintain log of inspections performed and corrective work; Manage outsourcing repair and maintenance work to vendors including receiving quotes, overseeing work, and processing invoices; Inspect for and report any tampering with locking devices. Maintain the inventory of parts and replacements for locking devices; orders through purchasing as necessary; Perform other duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities : Knowledge of Locksmith methods, practices, and safety precautions; Knowledge of Locksmith laws and regulations; Ability to operate machinery or equipment necessary for key making; Ability to use the key cutter, portable drills, welder, computer, and miscellaneous hand tools necessary in the locksmith trade; Ability to maintain inventory of needed parts and tools; Ability to read, interpret, and apply lock maintenance and repair manuals, policies, and procedures; Ability to prepare, present, and review oral and written information and reports; Knowledge of computers and software applications, specifically MS Word, Excel, Google Docs, Google Sheets, and key management software and access control management software; Must be able to operate a motor vehicle. Additional Information: Salary Information: $40,568.00 Required Documents to Apply: List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Emily Mills, Director of Construction, Planning, and Design Email: egmills@ualr.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Motor Vehicle Reports Check, Sex Offender Registry, Substance Abuse Testing The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Lifting, Standing, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Climbing, Crawling, Driving, Kneeling, Pulling, Pushing, Sitting Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAPBCAINECaine-Gilleland-Hall/Student-Research-Assistant-2_R0085815": {"title": "Student Research Assistant-2", "description": "Start date: 2026-05-15\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Staff (Non-Classified) Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Non-Employee Student Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff The University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff is an 1890 Land-Grant HBCU with a diverse student population, competitive degree offerings and stellar faculty. For more than 140 years, the University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff has worked to create an environment that inculcates learning, growth and productivity while affording a basic need to its students \u2013 a chance to advance. The 15:1 student to teacher ratio makes it possible to maintain a learning environment with close interaction between students and faculty while challenging curricula encourage our students to seek and fulfill their potential. You can excel in your chosen field of study through a curriculum of \u00a0 Certificate and Associates degree programs,\u00a0 more than thirty\u00a0 Undergraduate programs, Master\u2019s degree programs and a Doctorate program in Aquaculture/Fisheries. You can also develop workplace readiness through internships, co-ops and fellowships in the U.S. and abroad. Out-of-class experiences and student involvement include more than 90 student organizations, an internationally renowned Vesper Choir, Marching Band, Concert Bands, Wind Symphony, nationally recognized debate team, award-winning theater department and accomplished athletic program. Though the main campus is in Pine Bluff, its reach is worldwide. UAPB has an extended campus in North Little Rock and offers as well as online courses. With the addition of the Arkansas Research and Education Optical Network (ARE-ON), students can engage in information exchange with others anywhere in the world. There are also Research and Extension offices in Lonoke, Newport and Lake Village and collaborations with other colleges and universities in the State through the National Science Foundation funded STEM (Science, Technology, Engineering and Mathematics) Academy. As the second oldest land-grant institution in the state of Arkansas, the mission of this No Excuse University remains the same \u2013 to provide a high quality, affordable education with a personal touch. We invite you to Become a Part of the Pride at the University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process and require reasonable accommodations, please contact Human Resources at 870.575.8400 . Department: Chemistry and Physics Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Work with perovskite material and twisted 2D materials to design and fabricate the sensor and emitters, materials and device characterization, data analysis, present their work in conferences and journals. Qualifications: Should be doing undergraduate at UAPB.\u00a0 Additional Information: Salary Information: Required Documents to Apply: Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants (Please upload all required documents in the \"Resume\" attachment section of your application to be considered for this position) : Recruitment Contact Information: All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: No Background Check Required The University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff may conduct pre-employment background checks on certain positions for applicants being considered for employment. \u00a0 The background checks may include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. \u00a0 Required checks are identified in the position listing. \u00a0 A criminal background check or arrest pending adjudication information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absences of a relationship to the requirements of the position. \u00a0 Background check information will be used in a consistent, non-discriminatory manner consistent with the state and federal law. \u00a0 The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible:"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Mountain-View/RN-PRN---Kids-First---Mountainview--AR_R0085662": {"title": "RN PRN - Kids First - Mountainview, AR", "description": "Start date: 2026-05-15\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 06/15/2026 Type of Position: Clinical Staff - Nursing Job Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: COM | Peds Kids First Mountain View Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: *The position in in Mountainview, AR* The Registered Nurse (PRN), provides clinical nursing care for children enrolled in local KIDS FIRST clinics. Acts as a clinical resource for clinic staff. Qualifications: Graduate of an accredited Nursing Program with an Associate's degree, Nursing diploma, Bachelor's in Nursing, or Master's in Nursing Valid RN License Minimum of 2 years of Registered Nursing experience or 2 years of clinical nursing experience Knowledge, Skills & Abilities: Excellent communication skills. Basic computer skills. Strong work ethics and accountability. Preferred Qualifications: BSN or MSN with three (3) or more years of nursing experience. Pediatric Care experience. Current BLS. Responsibilities: Implements the nursing process to manage patient care problems of a complex and changing nature as demonstrated by documentation and observation. Assumes accountability and responsibility for all aspects of care for the assigned group of patients, with respect for developmental level and age-specific issues. Administers medications and treatments and performs procedures according to UAMS and KIDS FIRST policies. Evaluates children to identify signs of illness or injury and intervenes appropriately. Maintains current and accurate records and ensures confidentiality. Teaching/learning needs of patients and families are identified, addressed, and documented.\u00a0 Acts as a resource for staff in the areas of health, safety, and infection control.\u00a0 Assumes responsibility for acquiring knowledge and experience to meet professional goals. Develops and maintains close working relationships with the clinic director, the Medical Director, nursing managers, the clinic nurse, and other team members.\u00a0 Actively works with contacts to coordinate care and promote referrals to the program.\u00a0\u00a0 Collaborates with KIDS FIRST staff, PCPs, UAMS resources, and others to implement and revise plan of care as needed.\u00a0\u00a0 Provides employment documentation such as annual TB screening, CPR /nursing license renewal verification, etc., promptly. Performs other duties as assigned. Additional Information: Salary Information: $38.00/hour Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), Proof of Veteran Status, Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Adult Maltreatment, Child Maltreatment, Criminal Background Check, FBI Background Check, Sex Offender Registry This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Feeling, Hearing, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Crawling, Crouching, Grasping, Kneeling, Lifting, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Standing, Stooping, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Sitting Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Extra-Help-Assistant--EHS-Tech_R0085618": {"title": "Extra Help Assistant- EHS Tech", "description": "Start date: 2026-05-13\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Clerical Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Little Rock The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is a metropolitan research university that provides an accessible, quality education through flexible learning and unparalleled internship opportunities. At UA Little Rock, we prepare our more than 8,900 students to be innovators and responsible leaders in their fields. Committed to its metropolitan research university mission, UA Little Rock is a driving force in Little Rock's thriving cultural community and a major component of the city and state's growing profile as a regional leader in research, technology transfer, economic development, and job creation. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . Department: Operations & Services Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Extra Help Assistant- EHS Tech will assist the Director of Environmental Health and Safety (EHS) in maintaining campus compliance in general safety, fire safety, lab safety, recycling, and animal control. This position is governed by government regulations and agency/institution policy. Qualifications: Required Education and/or Experience: The formal education equivalent of a high school diploma; Must have basic computer skills and some experience with MS Word, Excel, and Access. Job Duties and Responsibilities: Routine Safety Systems Inspection and Repair to include but not limited to: \u00a0Fire Extinguishers, Emergency Lighting, Exit Signs, Smoke/Heat Detectors, UST Monitoring Wells, Eyewashes, Safety Showers, and other Building Devices; Fire Systems Maintenance and Inspection; Lamp Recycling; Safety/General Equipment Inspection; Animal Control; Miscellaneous Trouble Calls/Fire Alarm Responses; and Performs other duties as assigned. \u00a0 Preferred Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities : Two years of specialized training in electronics or related field; Knowledge of operation, maintenance, and repair of electrical and mechanical equipment; Ability to localize and repair mechanical or electrical problems; Ability to test and monitor equipment functions; \u00a0 Additional Information: Salary Information: $11.00 - $19.00 hourly - Commensurate with education and experience. Required Documents to Apply: List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Shawn Bayouth, Director of Environmental, Health, and Safety Email: sbayouth@ualr.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Substance Abuse Testing The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Kneeling, Lifting, Pulling, Pushing, Standing, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Climbing, Crawling, Sitting Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Adjunct-Lecturer-of-Interpreter-Education-1_R0079103": {"title": "Adjunct Lecturer of Interpreter Education-1", "description": "Start date: 2026-05-12\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Adjunct Faculty Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Less than Annual Appointment (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Little Rock The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is a metropolitan research university that provides an accessible, quality education through flexible learning and unparalleled internship opportunities. At UA Little Rock, we prepare our more than 8,900 students to be innovators and responsible leaders in their fields. Committed to its metropolitan research university mission, UA Little Rock is a driving force in Little Rock's thriving cultural community and a major component of the city and state's growing profile as a regional leader in research, technology transfer, economic development, and job creation. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . Department: Counseling, Adult, & Rehabilitation Education Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Adjunct Faculty to teach American Sign Language or interpreter training courses at the post-secondary level for the University of Arkansas at Little Rock. This position will be responsible for teaching course(s) in-class, assessing student-submitted work, and following the course objectives and syllabus prepared for the course. This position is governed by state and federal laws, and agency/institution policy. Qualifications: Required Education and/or Experience: Master\u2019s degree in ASL, Interpreting, or other related fields; Native or native-like competency in ASL. Preferred Education and/or Experience:\u00a0 \u00a0 Experience teaching in-class and online. Job Duties and Responsibilities: Teach assigned courses; Assess student-submitted work; Follow course objectives and syllabus; Commit to teaching the entire university semester; Participate as a part of the IEP faculty team. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Knowledge of classroom instruction; Ability to manage, motivate, and evaluate a diverse population of students; Collegial and cordial attitude toward interaction with colleagues, students, and staff; Demonstrable content knowledge of American Sign Language and Deaf Culture and closely related fields and the ties between the field and various allied disciplines; Excellent problem-solving and decision-making skills; Self-motivated, responsible, and able to work with minimal direct supervision. Additional Information: Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Curriculum Vitae, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume, Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Meagan Beaty, Assistant Professor/Coordinator Interpreter Education Program, mrbeaty@ualr.edu - David R. Montague, Ph.D. Associate Vice Chancellor for Academic Affairs & Professor of Criminal Justice and Criminology; Interim Director of CHPR, drmontague@ualr.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: No Background Check Required The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Cashier_R0055493-1": {"title": "Cashier", "description": "Start date: 2026-05-12\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 06/12/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: OPS | NUTRI Hospital Cafes Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Cashier handles register transactions with customers at retail food outlets, including operating cash register to receive money for sales of food service items and making change. The position may also prepare and/or serve food items for customers. Qualifications: Minimum: High School diploma/GED plus 6 months customer service and cashier experience required. Knowledge of Point of Sales Systems (POS). Preferred: Food service experience preferred. ServSafe certified. Responsibilities: Performs all transactions involving forms of payment including cash, cards, meal tickets and payroll deduct, etc. Preparing and producing specialty drinks. Cleans immediate work area around register as well as work unit including walls, chairs, tables, cabinets, etc.\u00a0 Stocks paper goods, food items and beverages as needed. May perform other duties as assigned. Additional Information: Physical Requirements: Frequent Physical Activity : Stand Continuously Bend, crawl, crouch, kneel, stoop or reach overhead Use hands to touch, handle or feel Talk Occasional Physical Activity : Taste or smell Lift/Carry Weight:\u00a0 26 - 50 Lbs. Push/Pull Weight: \u00a0 26 - 50 Lbs. Physical Environment : Inside medical Facility Noise Level: \u00a0 Loud Visual Requirements: \u00a0 Color discrimination, Depth perception, Far visual acuity Near visual acuity Hazards : Chemical, Electrical, Fumes/Gases/Odors, Sharp objects/tools Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience. Required Documents to Apply: None Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Fayetteville/Early-Childhood-Educator--Classroom-Teacher--Current-and-Anticipated-Future-Openings-_R0085379-1": {"title": "Early Childhood Educator: Classroom Teacher (Current and Anticipated Future Openings)", "description": "Start date: 2026-05-08\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com, then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at all University of Arkansas institutions will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students.\u201d University of Arkansas, Fayetteville students will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Student Jobs at UAF.\u201d All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. Closing Date: 05/06/2028 Type of Position: Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas, Fayetteville Founded in 1871, the University of Arkansas is a land grant institution, classified by the Carnegie Foundation among the nation\u2019s top 2 percent of universities with the highest level of research activity. The University of Arkansas works to advance the state and build a better world through education, research, and outreach by providing transformational opportunities and skills, fostering a welcoming climate, and nurturing creativity, discovery, and the spread of new ideas and innovations. The University of Arkansas campus is located in Fayetteville, a welcoming community ranked as one of the best places to live in the U.S. The growing region surrounding Fayetteville is home to numerous Fortune 500 companies and one of the nation\u2019s strongest economies. Northwest Arkansas is also quickly gaining a national reputation for its focus on the arts and overall quality of life. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10% of employee salary. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions, you should review before applying for the opening. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process, please submit a request via the Disability Accommodations | OEOC | University of Arkansas (uark.edu) : Request an Accommodation. Appli\u00adcants are required to submit a request for each position of which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 479.575.5351. Department: Jean Tyson Child Development Study Center Operations B Department's Website: https://jean-tyson-child-development-study-center.uark.edu/ Summary of Job Duties: The Early Childhood Educator - Classroom Teacher (teaching associate) will work as a team member to develop predictable, yet flexible, routines and rituals that support children and families. The teaching associate, who may work with children 8 weeks to 5 years, will collaboratively design and implement developmentally appropriate, emergent, and play-based curriculum for children. The teaching associate will follow all licensing requirements and model nationally recommended practices for children, colleagues, university students, families, and other school visitors. The teaching associate will document and communicate the development of children by engaging in activities that include but are not limited to: completing program-adopted assessment practices, collecting artifacts of learning, preparing weekly journals of classroom experiences, conducting parent-teacher conference, and maintaining classroom and children\u2019s portfolios. The teaching associate will also model for and mentor new teaching staff including part-time employees, undergraduate students and aides. Regular, reliable, and non-disruptive attendance is an essential job duty, as is the ability to create and maintain collegial, harmonious working relationships with others. Duties \u2022 Ability to design and implement developmentally appropriate curriculum \u2022 Ability to understand the NAEYC accreditation process \u2022 Ability to model for and mentor undergraduate students and hourly aides Qualifications: Minimum Requirements An associate\u2019s degree in early childhood education, child development, elementary education, human development/family studies, early childhood special education or a closely related field from an accredited institution of higher education OR Candidates may also be considered with an equivalency to an associate\u2019s degree (AA) in early childhood education, which is defined by NAEYC as at least 60 college/university credits with at least 30 college credits in early childhood education, early childhood education, child development, elementary education, human development/family studies, or early childhood special education or a closely related field from an accredited institution of higher education At least two years experience working with young children and/or directing early childhood programs Demonstrated participation in professional development and/or professional organizations Preferred Requirements Bachelor degree (BA/BS) in early childhood education, child development, elementary education, human development/family studies, early childhood special education or a closely related field from an accredited institution of higher education OR An equivalency of a BA/BS or higher in early childhood education, which is defined by NAEYC as a baccalaureate degree in any discipline with at least 36 college credits in early childhood education, child development, elementary education, human development/family studies, or early childhood special education from an accredited institution of higher education Knowledge, Skills & Abilities (KSAs): Ability to design and implement developmentally appropriate curriculum Ability to understand the NAEYC accreditation process Ability to model for and mentor undergraduate students and hourly aides Additional Information: When applying, for \"other\" document, please provide the names and contact information for two personal references. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Child Maltreatment, Criminal Background Check, FBI Background Check, Sex Offender Registry, Substance Abuse Testing Please Note: This posting will be used to collect applications to fill current openings as well as anticipated future openings. Future openings are anticipated but not guaranteed. This posting will expire on the posting end date indicated. Applicants wishing to be considered after this date must reapply. Salary Information: Salary is commensurate with education and experience. The starting salary for individuals meeting minimum requirements is $39,930. Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Recruitment Contact Information: Annie Kohanek, Administrative Specialist III, akohanek@uark.edu, 479-575-7482 Shelley McNally, Executive Director, smcnally@uark.edu, 479-575-6288 All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Special Instructions to Applicants: Pre-employment Screening Requirements: The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas seeks to attract, develop and retain high quality faculty, staff and administrators that consistently display practices and behaviors to advance a culture that embeds equal opportunity, educational excellence and unparalleled access for all. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All Application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Cook_R0055495-1": {"title": "Cook", "description": "Start date: 2026-05-08\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 06/08/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: OPS | NUTRI Cafeteria Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Cook collaborates with other cooks and food prep techs under the direction of a supervisor to requisition, prepare, season, and cook a wide range of foods, including soups, salads, bakery and entrees for patients, employees, or patrons. Qualifications: Minimum: High School diploma/GED plus 1 year experience in institutional or commercial cooking. Must be able to work during Inclement Weather. Must be able to work rotating Weekends and Holidays. Preferred: Formal Culinary Education and ServSafe Certified. Responsibilities Cleans, cut, and cook food items according to menus, special dietary or nutritional restrictions, or numbers of portions to be served. \u00a0\u00a0 Clean and inspect gallery equipment, kitchen appliances, and work areas to ensure cleanliness and functional operation.\u00a0 Apportion and serve food to patients, employees, and patrons. Other duties as assigned.\u00a0 Additional Information: Constant Physical Activity : Read, Concentrate, Think Analytically, Frequent Physical Activity : Stand Walk Bend, crawl, crouch, kneel, stoop or reach overhead Hear Taste or Smell Use hands to touch, handle or feel Lift/Carry Weight: 26 - 50 Lbs. Push/Pull Weight: 26 - 50 Lbs. Physical Environment : Inside Medical Facility Noise Level: Loud Visual Requirements: Color discrimination, Depth perception, Far visual acuity Near visual acuity Hazards : Biological, Fumes/Gases/Odors, Sharp objects/tools, Chemical Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience. Required Documents to Apply: List of three Professional References (name, email, business title) Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/North-Little-Rock/Biology-Adjunct-Faculty_R0085374": {"title": "Biology Adjunct Faculty", "description": "Start date: 2026-05-05\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Less than Annual Appointment (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas Pulaski Technical College University of Arkansas - Pulaski Technical College at North Little Rock is an integral part of the Arkansas Technical and Community College System maintained by the State of Arkansas. The college is governed by the University of Arkansas System Board of Trustees and a seven-member Board of Visitors and derives its support largely from student tuition and fees and legislative appropriations. UA - Pulaski Tech, a comprehensive two-year college, offers associate degree and certificate programs for students who plan to transfer to four-year colleges and universities and/or for career preparation and advancement. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply link/button. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at (501) 812-2839. Department: Natural Sciences Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The University of Arkansas - Pulaski Technical College in North Little Rock, Arkansas, is accepting applications for a part-time faculty position in Biology. This position requires a commitment to teaching in a dynamic community college setting and the ability to successfully interact and respond to the broad ranging needs of an academically and culturally diverse campus setting. Courses may be online or in person dependent upon campus need. Qualifications: A master\u2019s degree in biology with at least 18 graduate hours in the discipline (preferably an Anatomy and Physiology preparation) is required. A minimum of two years of teaching experience, preferably in a community college setting involving a diverse student body, is preferred.\u00a0 The successful candidate will possess competence and experience to develop, revise, implement and assess the curriculum to ensure that students are acquiring current knowledge, including familiarity with technology used in classroom settings.\u00a0 The ability to utilize web-based educational technology is expected. Candidates must have flexibility to teach day, evening, and weekend classes.\u00a0 Teaching assignments may include off-campus sites and involve alternative delivery methods. Additional Information: Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants Recruitment Contact Information: Human Resources humanresources@uaptc.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: University of Arkansas - Pulaski Technical College is committed to providing a safe campus community. Title IX protects the college community from sexual harassment in a school's education programs and activities. This means that Title IX protects the college community in connection with all academic, educational, extracurricular, athletic, and other programs of the school, whether those programs take place in a school's facilities, in college transportation, at a class or training program sponsored by the school at another location, or elsewhere. \u00a0 We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-Arkansas-Community-College-at-Batesville/Cosmetology-Part-Time-Instructor_R0084962-1": {"title": "Cosmetology Part-Time Instructor", "description": "Start date: 2026-04-29\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. Closing Date: Type of Position: Adjunct Faculty Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Less than Annual Appointment (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas Community College at Batesville The University of Arkansas Community College at Batesville (UACCB) is a comprehensive community college committed to providing learning experiences that improve the lives of those we serve. UACCB provides affordable access to technical education and college transfer programs that meet the diverse higher education needs of the citizens of north central Arkansas. \u00a0 These programs are provided to the traditional college student as well as to high school students through a state approved Secondary Area Career Center. \u00a0 The College also promotes economic development and an enhanced quality of life for the community through adult education, developmental education, customized business and industry training, and continuing education programs. UACCB's mission is to provide quality educational opportunities within a supportive learning environment. We promote success through community partnerships, responsive programs, and an enduring commitment to improvement. Thank you for your interest. \u00a0 We hope you will be joining us soon! After reviewing the Job Duties and Qualifications listed below, click the Apply button at the top of the page to begin the application process. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process or for general application assistance, please contact the Human Resource Office at (870) 612-2045. Department: Dean of Career Education Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Cosmetology Part-Time Instructor will work assigned hours to assist the full time faculty in working directly with students to ensure compliance with local, state, and federal regulatory and certifying agencies and deliver theoretical and practical instruction in the field of cosmetology services. The ideal applicant will be one who can demonstrate the ability to work with the Cosmetology faculty to promote and maintain a positive learning environment; teach courses as assigned; assess student performance; ensure safe and sanitary practices by students when practicing cosmetology; ensure client satisfaction by effectively managing clinic floor; counseling and guiding students; assisting in resolving student issues; and, perform other duties as assigned. Qualifications: Licensed as a cosmetology instructor by the Arkansas Department of Health Cosmetology Section with two years experience in the licensed practice of cosmetology in a licensed cosmetological establishment or in the teaching of cosmetology in a licensed school of cosmetology or any combination of experience thereof. \u00a0 Additional Information: Salary Information: Hourly rate commensurate with education and experience. Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume, Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Human Resources hr@uaccb.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Child Maltreatment, Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry, Substance Abuse Testing UACCB is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check for all applicants.\u00a0 Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Feeling, Grasping, Hearing, Lifting, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Pulling, Reaching, Repetitive Motion, Sharps, Standing, Stooping, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Balancing, Crouching, Pushing Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Maintenance-Assistant_R0084987-1": {"title": "Maintenance Assistant", "description": "Start date: 2026-04-29\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Skilled Labor Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: Division of Agriculture of the University of Arkansas The University of Arkansas System Division of Agriculture is a state wide campus, with faculty based on University campuses, at Research and Extension Centers and in every Arkansas county. It consists of the Arkansas Agricultural Experiment Station (AES) and the Arkansas Cooperative Extension Service (CES), and is home to more than 1400 employees.\u00a0 The Division was established in 1959 and is headed by the Vice-President for Agriculture.\u00a0 The Division headquarters is located in Little Rock with the rest of the University of Arkansas System Administration.\u00a0 As an employer, the University of Arkansas System Division of Agriculture offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance.\u00a0 Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process and require reasonable accommodations, please contact the Division's Office of Program & Employment Compliance at compliance@uada.edu . For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-671-2219 or 479-502-9820. Department: Assistant Facilities Manager * Department's Website: uada.edu Summary of Job Duties: The Maintenance Assistant is responsible for facilities & grounds maintenance, construction, general labor demands, and other maintenance related job duties in support of the Little Rock State Office. Job Duties: Building and facilities maintenance. Assist the facility management department with minor electrical, plumbing, HVAC, etc. repair. Assist with construction projects with minor carpentry, painting, etc. Assist the Landscape Specialist with grounds-keeping on an as needed basis. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications\nThe formal education equivalent of a high school diploma; plus one year of experience or training in the building construction trades, general building maintenance, or in the repair or maintenance of mechanical equipment.\n\nKnowledge, Skills & Abilities\nKnowledge of basic carpentry, electrical systems, plumbing, painting, & heating & air conditioning. Knowledge of the operation, maintenance, & safety requirements of motorized vehicles & equipment. Ability to operate & perform routine maintenance & minor repairs on motorized vehicles & equipment. Ability to perform routine building & grounds maintenance work. Ability to use, operate, & maintain electrical tools & machinery. Additional Information: For technical assistance with the application process, please email humanresources@uada.edu \u00a0or call 501-671-2219. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Kirby Owens, kowens@uada.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Motor Vehicle Reports Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas System Division of Agriculture may conduct pre-employment background checks on certain positions for applicants being considered for employment. \u00a0 The background checks may include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. \u00a0 Required checks are identified in the position listing. \u00a0 A criminal background check or arrest pending adjudication information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absences of a relationship to the requirements of the position. \u00a0 Background check information will be used in a consistent, non-discriminatory manner consistent with the state and federal law. \u00a0 The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Talking Occasional Physical Activity: Talking Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Fayetteville-AR/Academic-Tutor--Current-and-Anticipated-Future-Openings-_R0049835": {"title": "Academic Tutor (Current and Anticipated Future Openings)", "description": "Start date: 2026-04-28\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com, then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at all University of Arkansas institutions will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students.\u201d University of Arkansas, Fayetteville students will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Student Jobs at UAF.\u201d All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. Closing Date: 12/31/2026 Type of Position: Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas, Fayetteville Founded in 1871, the University of Arkansas is a land grant institution, classified by the Carnegie Foundation among the nation\u2019s top 2 percent of universities with the highest level of research activity. The University of Arkansas works to advance the state and build a better world through education, research, and outreach by providing transformational opportunities and skills, fostering a welcoming climate, and nurturing creativity, discovery, and the spread of new ideas and innovations. The University of Arkansas campus is located in Fayetteville, a welcoming community ranked as one of the best places to live in the U.S. The growing region surrounding Fayetteville is home to numerous Fortune 500 companies and one of the nation\u2019s strongest economies. Northwest Arkansas is also quickly gaining a national reputation for its focus on the arts and overall quality of life. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10% of employee salary. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions, you should review before applying for the opening. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process, please submit a request via the Disability Accommodations | OEOC | University of Arkansas (uark.edu) : Request an Accommodation. Appli\u00adcants are required to submit a request for each position of which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 479.575.5351. Department: Educational Enrichment Services Hourly Support Department's Website: https://arkansasrazorbacks.com/ Summary of Job Duties: Academic tutors provide instructional support to students in specific academic content areas and help students develop successful study skills. Primary job duties include: \u2022 Planning and implementing weekly sessions with students to promote independent learning \u2022 Communicating effectively with students and staff \u2022 Identifying and addressing study skill needs for students in the context of their tutoring sessions \u2022 Preparing and submitting accurate records of sessions with students. \u2022 Maintaining a high level of knowledge in their academic content area. \u2022 Knowing and complying with University FERPA, Sexual Harassment, and confidentiality guidelines \u2022 Knowing and complying with policies governing the tutoring of student-athletes in the NCAA \u2022 Attending training exercises designed to develop instructional skills and compliance with University and NCAA policies regarding the tutoring of student-athletes \u2022 Additional duties as assigned Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Have earned at least 30 credit hours Have at least a 3.0 cumulative GPA Earned a B (A preferred) in the classes you wish to tutor Available at least two evenings each week to tutor (Sunday \u2013 Thursday) Can provide two letters of recommendation, one of which must be a University Faculty/Staff reference who can speak to knowledge and capacity to tutor Additional Information: \u200b Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry. Graduate students are subject to background checks. Please Note: This posting will be used to collect applications to fill current openings as well as anticipated future openings. Future openings are anticipated but not guaranteed. This posting will expire on the posting end date indicated. Applicants wishing to be considered after this date must reapply. Salary Information: $15.00 per hour Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Letters of Recommendation, Proof of Veteran Status Recruitment Contact Information: Trevor Williamson, Tutor Coordinator, 479-575-5691, tpwillia@uark.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Special Instructions to Applicants: Pre-employment Screening Requirements: The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas seeks to attract, develop and retain high quality faculty, staff and administrators that consistently display practices and behaviors to advance a culture that embeds equal opportunity, educational excellence and unparalleled access for all. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All Application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Fayetteville-AR/Ticket-Center-Assistant--Current-and-Anticipated-Future-Openings-_R0049846": {"title": "Ticket Center Assistant (Current and Anticipated Future Openings)", "description": "Start date: 2026-04-28\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com, then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at all University of Arkansas institutions will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students.\u201d University of Arkansas, Fayetteville students will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Student Jobs at UAF.\u201d All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. Closing Date: 12/31/2026 Type of Position: Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas, Fayetteville Founded in 1871, the University of Arkansas is a land grant institution, classified by the Carnegie Foundation among the nation\u2019s top 2 percent of universities with the highest level of research activity. The University of Arkansas works to advance the state and build a better world through education, research, and outreach by providing transformational opportunities and skills, fostering a welcoming climate, and nurturing creativity, discovery, and the spread of new ideas and innovations. The University of Arkansas campus is located in Fayetteville, a welcoming community ranked as one of the best places to live in the U.S. The growing region surrounding Fayetteville is home to numerous Fortune 500 companies and one of the nation\u2019s strongest economies. Northwest Arkansas is also quickly gaining a national reputation for its focus on the arts and overall quality of life. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10% of employee salary. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions, you should review before applying for the opening. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process, please submit a request via the Disability Accommodations | OEOC | University of Arkansas (uark.edu) : Request an Accommodation. Appli\u00adcants are required to submit a request for each position of which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 479.575.5351. Department: Ticket Office Hourly Support Department's Website: https://arkansasrazorbacks.com/ Summary of Job Duties: The Ticket Center Assistant will provide ticket center staff with assistance in the Razorback Ticket Center. The Ticket Center Assistant will provide ticket center staff with assistance during athletic events, including events held on weeknights, weekends, and over University of Arkansas designated breaks. The Ticket Center Assistant must be able to work all home football games, most home men\u2019s and women\u2019s basketball games and baseball games. Other select events will include Volleyball, Soccer, Indoor/Outdoor Track and Field, Gymnastics and Softball, as well as other events held in University of Arkansas athletic facilities. Regular, reliable, and non-disruptive attendance is an essential job duty, as is the ability to create and maintain collegial, harmonious working relationships with others. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: The formal equivalent of a high school diploma Must be 18 years of age or older Preferred Qualifications: Cash handling experience Basic computer skills Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities (KSAs): Ability to communicate with customers Ability to multi-task while providing excellent customer service Ability to be detail-oriented Additional Information: Please Note: This posting will be used to collect applications to fill current openings as well as anticipated future openings. Future openings are anticipated but not guaranteed. This posting will expire on the posting end date indicated. Applicants wishing to be considered after this date must reapply. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Financial Credit Check, Sex Offender Registry Salary Information: $11.00 per hour Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Recruitment Contact Information: Pete Heim, Associate Athletic Director of Ticket Operations & Sales - peteheim@uark.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Special Instructions to Applicants: Pre-employment Screening Requirements: The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas seeks to attract, develop and retain high quality faculty, staff and administrators that consistently display practices and behaviors to advance a culture that embeds equal opportunity, educational excellence and unparalleled access for all. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All Application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAMS/Food-Preparation-Supervisor_R0055500-1": {"title": "Food Preparation Supervisor", "description": "Start date: 2026-04-28\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: 07/31/2026 Type of Position: Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences The University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS) has a unique combination of education, research, and clinical programs that encourages and supports teamwork and diversity. We champion being a collaborative health care organization, focused on improving patient care and the lives of Arkansans. \u00a0 UAMS offers amazing benefits and perks ( available for benefits eligible positions only ): Health: Medical, Dental and Vision plans available for qualifying staff and family Holiday, Vacation and Sick Leave Education discount for staff and dependents (undergraduate only) Retirement: Up to 10% matched contribution from UAMS Basic Life Insurance up to $50,000 Career Training and Educational Opportunities Merchant Discounts Concierge prescription delivery on the main campus when using UAMS pharmacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. \u00a0 For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at askrecruitment@uams.edu . Department: OPS | NUTRI Lobby Cafe Team 1 Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Food Preparation Supervisor is responsible for the supervision of food service personnel, directing food service activities, monitoring security and safety practices, coordinating the production and serving of food, ordering supplies, and the preparation of reports. This position is governed by state and federal laws and agency policy. Qualifications: Minimum: High School Diploma or GED. 2 years of experience in institutional or commercial food service operations, including 1 year supervisory experience. Self-directed, flexible and innovative. Good leadership and organizational skills. Preferred: Bachelors degree in dietetics or a related field, ServSafe Certified, Certified Dietary Manager. Responsibilities: Perform all task of the cashier and the food preparation technician with proficiency. Helps staff prepare food, make coffee drinks, cleaning, cashiering, and any other tasks that are necessary while providing outstanding customer service. Ensures that the staff are following recipes that are designed by management. Handles questions, concerns and complaints. Trains and supervise all staff while following UAMS policies and procedure. Performs all register counting duties while following the policies and procedures, as well as, holds the staff accountable for the policies and procedures. Completes all documentation daily. Accurately records the temperatures of the coolers and food to ensure customer safety. Audit staff duties and completes daily cleaning checklists for inspection.\u00a0 Performs other duties assigned. Additional Information: PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS: Stand Continuously Sit Occasionally Walk Frequently Bend, crawl, crouch, kneel, stoop or reach overhead Frequently Lift and carry weight 26 - 50 lbs Push and pull weight 26 - 50 lbs Use hands to touch, handle or feel Continuously Talk Continuously Hear Continuously Taste or smell Occasionally Read, concentrate, think analytically Continuously Physical Environment Inside Medical Facility Environment Noise Level Loud Visual Requirements Color discrimination Depth perception Far visual acuity Near visual acuity Hazards Chemical Electrical Heavy machinery Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: License or Certificate (see special instructions for submission instructions), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Please contact askrecruitment@uams.edu\u00a0 for any recruiting related\u00a0questions. All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: This position is subject to pre-employment screening (criminal background, drug testing, and/or education verification). A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication alone shall not disqualify an applicant except as provided by law. Any criminal history will be evaluated in relationship to job responsibilities and business necessity.\u00a0 The information obtained in these reports will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law.\u00a0 Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAM--Monticello-Campus/Non-Student-Extra-Help--Residence-Life-Furnishing-Assistant-_R0083868-2": {"title": "Non-Student Extra Help (Residence Life Furnishing Assistant)", "description": "Start date: 2026-04-24\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Clerical Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Monticello UAM, one of twenty campuses of the University of Arkansas System, is located in southeastern Arkansas in the beautiful timberlands, rich in outdoor recreation activities, and approximately 100 miles south of Little Rock. UAM is a comprehensive, residential and commuter, undergraduate institution also offering selected master\u2019s degree programs. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please submit a request via the OEOC website: \u00a0Applicants are required to submit a request for each position to which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 870-460-1422 . Department: Residence Halls Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Residence Life Furnishing Assistant helps our Residence Services team prepare our residences for the next academic year. This part-time summer position might require work outside of regular business hours. Qualifications: Must be at least 18 years of age Must have a High School Diploma or GED equivalent Additional Information: Salary Information: $11.00/hourly Required Documents to Apply: None Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Jessica L. Foxworth Associate Vice Chancellor for Student Engagement and Dean of Students University of Arkansas at Monticello Student Success Center 201D Monticello, Arkansas Foxworth@uamont.edu 870.460.1110 All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: No Background Check Required The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Adjunct-Part-time-Lecturer_R0084833": {"title": "Adjunct/Part-time Lecturer", "description": "Start date: 2026-04-24\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Adjunct Faculty Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Less than Annual Appointment (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Little Rock The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is a metropolitan research university that provides an accessible, quality education through flexible learning and unparalleled internship opportunities. At UA Little Rock, we prepare our more than 8,900 students to be innovators and responsible leaders in their fields. Committed to its metropolitan research university mission, UA Little Rock is a driving force in Little Rock's thriving cultural community and a major component of the city and state's growing profile as a regional leader in research, technology transfer, economic development, and job creation. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . Department: Budget Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The UA Little Rock Bowen School of Law is seeking an Adjunct Lecturer to teach during the Fall 2026 semester. This position is governed by state and federal laws, and agency/institution policy. Qualifications: Required Education and/or Experience: Juris Doctorate Degree from an accredited law school. Job Duties and Responsibilities: Prepare for and teach the assigned course. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Good organizational skills and timeliness in responding to student inquiries; Ability to respond to the needs of students from a variety of educational backgrounds in a multicultural environment; Ability to deliver course instruction and content through a variety of teaching/learning styles; Ability to use technology effectively in teaching; Ability to communicate effectively; Ability to establish and maintain effective interpersonal relationships with students and Additional Information: The Adjuncts need to be able to teach one of the following courses: Adv. Appellate Advocacy Lawyering Skills Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Jennifer Jones, Assistant Finance Director, jljones27@ualr.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: No Background Check Required The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Sitting, Standing, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Grasping, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding Occasional Physical Activity: Lifting, Repetitive Motion Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAM--Monticello-Campus/Director-of-Library-and-Assistant-Professor_R0084802": {"title": "Director of Library and Assistant Professor", "description": "Start date: 2026-04-24\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Library Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Monticello UAM, one of twenty campuses of the University of Arkansas System, is located in southeastern Arkansas in the beautiful timberlands, rich in outdoor recreation activities, and approximately 100 miles south of Little Rock. UAM is a comprehensive, residential and commuter, undergraduate institution also offering selected master\u2019s degree programs. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please submit a request via the OEOC website: \u00a0Applicants are required to submit a request for each position to which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 870-460-1422 . Department: VC Academic Affairs Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Director of Library will provide leadership in developing and expanding the library services program at UAM; develop, present, and implement the budget to accomplish planned goals; coordinate the Library activities with academic programs in UAM\u2019s schools; hire, supervise and encourage the professional development of library professionals and staff; plan for and establish priorities and policies for the development of collections, and public and technical services. The Library Director is a member of the Academic Council and reports to the Vice Chancellor for Academic Affairs. Qualifications: A doctorate degree in library or library information sciences or in a cognate area pertinent to UAM\u2019s program offerings is preferred.\u00a0 An earned master\u2019s degree in library or library informational sciences from an accredited program; three years of higher education library experience is required.\u00a0 The candidate must have highly effective interpersonal skills, a consultative leadership style, and a commitment to working effectively with faculty, staff, administration, and students. Additional Information: Curriculum Vitae, Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Curriculum Vitae, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Ms. Crystal Halley, Vice Chancellor for Academic Affairs halleyc@uamont.edu 870-460-1032 All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Financial Credit Check, Sex Offender Registry, Substance Abuse Testing The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAM--Monticello-Campus/Graduate-Assistant---CFANR_R0015820": {"title": "Graduate Assistant - CFANR", "description": "Start date: 2026-04-20\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Monticello UAM, one of twenty campuses of the University of Arkansas System, is located in southeastern Arkansas in the beautiful timberlands, rich in outdoor recreation activities, and approximately 100 miles south of Little Rock. UAM is a comprehensive, residential and commuter, undergraduate institution also offering selected master\u2019s degree programs. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please submit a request via the OEOC website: \u00a0Applicants are required to submit a request for each position to which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 870-460-1422 . Department: Forestry / Agri / Nat. Resourc Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: Attend graduate classes and perform research duties related to assigned project. Qualifications: High school diplpma Additional Information: Salary Information: $15,000 - $18,000 annually Required Documents to Apply: None Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Valerie Harvey, harvey@uamont.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: No"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Fayetteville-AR/Parking-Services-Partner---Current-and-Anticipated-Future-Openings---Evergreen-_R0072552-1": {"title": "Parking Services Partner", "description": "Start date: 2026-04-17\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com, then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at all University of Arkansas institutions will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students.\u201d University of Arkansas, Fayetteville students will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Student Jobs at UAF.\u201d All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. Closing Date: Type of Position: Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas, Fayetteville Founded in 1871, the University of Arkansas is a land grant institution, classified by the Carnegie Foundation among the nation\u2019s top 2 percent of universities with the highest level of research activity. The University of Arkansas works to advance the state and build a better world through education, research, and outreach by providing transformational opportunities and skills, fostering a welcoming climate, and nurturing creativity, discovery, and the spread of new ideas and innovations. The University of Arkansas campus is located in Fayetteville, a welcoming community ranked as one of the best places to live in the U.S. The growing region surrounding Fayetteville is home to numerous Fortune 500 companies and one of the nation\u2019s strongest economies. Northwest Arkansas is also quickly gaining a national reputation for its focus on the arts and overall quality of life. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10% of employee salary. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions, you should review before applying for the opening. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process, please submit a request via the Disability Accommodations | OEOC | University of Arkansas (uark.edu) : Request an Accommodation. Appli\u00adcants are required to submit a request for each position of which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 479.575.5351. Department: Patrol, IT and Special Events Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Parking Services Partner is a critical member of the University\u2019s Campus Services Team ensuring the safe and smooth flow of vehicles and our campus community; while responding to real-time opportunities to support campus access, safety, and parking operations. As a frontline university representative, this position will have opportunities to interact with students, staff, and visitors across campus, providing exceptional customer service, communicating parking and transit options, and resolving parking concerns and infractions across campus. The role also involves providing guidance to students, employees, and visitors; collaborating with other parking personnel; and reporting safety or maintenance issues. This position may require work outside of normal business hours. Regular, reliable, and non-disruptive attendance is an essential job duty, as is the ability to create and maintain collegial, harmonious working relationships with others. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: The formal education equivalent of a high school diploma Valid Driver\u2019s License Preferred Qualifications: Associate\u2019s degree or advanced specialized or technical training Experience in customer service, security, campus operations, or parking services Knowledge, Skills & Abilities: Knowledge of campus parking rules and regulations Knowledge of handheld computers and radio procedures Knowledge of basic rules of conflict resolution Knowledge of parking and building locations and parking enforcement procedures Ability to oversee the activities Ability to provide parking assistance for the campus and proper enforcement Ability to communicate effectively both orally and in writing Additional Information: PSP hours: Day shift: 6:30a to 2:30p, M-F Evening shift: 2p to 10p., M-F \u00a0 Summer shifts: Day: 6:30a to 2:30p, M-F Evening: 10a-6p, M-F \u00a0 Work special events such as: concerts, men\u2019s and women\u2019s basketball games, football games, commencement, baseball games, etc. This post is for current and anticipated future openings. Salary Information: $40,000 Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Recruitment Contact Information: Caitlin Hughes, Strategic Talent Acquisition Specialist, cmmitche@uark.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Special Instructions to Applicants: Pre-employment Screening Requirements: The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas seeks to attract, develop and retain high quality faculty, staff and administrators that consistently display practices and behaviors to advance a culture that embeds equal opportunity, educational excellence and unparalleled access for all. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All Application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Frequent Physical Activity: Occasional Physical Activity: Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Little-Rock/Assistant-Professor-of-Communication-Disorders-and-Sciences---9-MONTH_R0084337": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Communication Disorders and Sciences - 9 MONTH", "description": "Start date: 2026-04-13\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \u201cMy Draft Applications\u201d located on your Candidate Home page. \u00a0 Closing Date: Type of Position: Faculty - Tenure/Tenure Track Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Little Rock The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is a metropolitan research university that provides an accessible, quality education through flexible learning and unparalleled internship opportunities. At UA Little Rock, we prepare our more than 8,900 students to be innovators and responsible leaders in their fields. Committed to its metropolitan research university mission, UA Little Rock is a driving force in Little Rock's thriving cultural community and a major component of the city and state's growing profile as a regional leader in research, technology transfer, economic development, and job creation. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the \u00a0 Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . Department: Counseling, Adult, & Rehabilitation Education Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: This position is for a full-time, 9-month, tenure-track Assistant Professor of Communication Disorders and Sciences with qualifications and professional background sufficient to teach courses in Communication Sciences and Disorders. An ideal candidate will be able to teach any courses in our undergraduate curriculum. This position is governed by state and federal laws and agency/institution policy. Qualifications: Required Education and/or Experience: Ph.D. in Communication Sciences and Disorders, Audiology, or a very closely related field. Preferred Education and/or Experience:\u00a0 Professional experience in the Communication Sciences and Disorders field; Teaching experience in multiple modalities (in person, hybrid, online); Experience mentoring or supervising students; A research agenda that allows for publication and funding; Experience working on and preparing funded research projects. \u00a0 Job Duties and Responsibilities: Responsible for teaching Communication Sciences and Disorders courses in face-to-face, hybrid, and online formats; Work positively with faculty, staff, students, and the community; Mentor students across the curriculum; Conduct and disseminate scholarly research; Serve the school, college, university, and community; Help with recruitment, retention, and program initiatives; Perform other duties as required.\u00a0 Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Commitment to teaching and mentoring students; Committed to remaining current in the area of expertise and instruction; Active research agenda in field of expertise; Collegial and establish good relationships with our external constituency. Additional Information: Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Curriculum Vitae, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Matt Matusiak, Associate Dean, mmatusiak@ualr.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site\u00a0 https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS \u00a0 Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University\u2019s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting, Standing Occasional Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Repetitive Motion Benefits Eligible: Yes"}, "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UAM--Monticello-Campus/University-Forest-Assistant---Non-Student_R0084334-1": {"title": "University Forest Assistant - Non Student", "description": "Start date: 2026-04-10\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for \u201cFind Jobs for Students\u201d. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through \